{"job":{"id":19939063,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"PetDesk","title":"VoIP Install: YeaLink devices ","description":{"html":"<br><ol><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Equipment &amp; Conduct Requirements</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Contractor shall provide all <strong>necessary tools and materials</strong>, including:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tools for mounting hardware</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Wiring/cables</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">PPE/safety equipment</li><li>Contractor agents must:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Be friendly, professional, and minimize disruption to operations</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Leave the site clean and free of debris</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Be skilled, knowledgeable, and capable of fulfilling all duties</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Be comfortable working in an <strong>active veterinary environment</strong> during business hour</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">No allergies, fear of animals, or other limiting conditions</span></li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> Unpacking the Phone Boxes</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Assemble devices </li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Phone Removal </strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Contractor will </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">properly box up old </strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">phones and set aside for Hospital Manager to store </span></li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> Installing the Phones /&nbsp;Setting Up Yealink Desktop Phones</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Answer site contact’s basic questions about phone use or </li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Review Key phone system features available on devices </li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Extensions </li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Call Park </li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Call Hold </li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Toggles </li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Voicemail</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Intercom/Paging</li><li class=\"ql-indent-3\"><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><em>If customer has additional questions escalate questions to PetDesk. </em></strong></li><li><strong>Progress Tracking &amp; Communication</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Installation progress</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Photos and key dates</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Access to a device (preferably a laptop) where the Contractor is able to join a zoom call with PetDesk team is necessary</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Call Forwarding Assistance</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Contractor shall assist the on-site POC with <strong>forwarding phone numbers</strong> to the temporary number provided by PetDesk. (See installation guide below)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Test Calls</strong> (post-installation):</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>Outbound call</strong> to a live external number (cell or local business)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>Inbound call</strong> from an external source answered on-site (for call quality check)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>Call to *933</strong> to verify E911 service address (do not call 911 directly)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Device Support</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Support for additional connected devices (if applicable):</li><li class=\"ql-indent-3\">Doorbells, Intercom/PA systems, Fax Adapters</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Basic Network Troubleshooting</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Contractor may need to run <strong>new Ethernet cabling</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">If poor call quality is identified:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-3\">Confirm there are no firewall blocks</li><li class=\"ql-indent-3\">Disable SIP ALG if needed</li><li class=\"ql-indent-3\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Check for packet filtering issues</span></li></ol>","markdown":"1. **Equipment & Conduct Requirements**\n2. Contractor shall provide all **necessary tools and materials**, including:\n3. Tools for mounting hardware\n4. Wiring/cables\n5. PPE/safety equipment\n6. Contractor agents must:\n7. Be friendly, professional, and minimize disruption to operations\n8. Leave the site clean and free of debris\n9. Be skilled, knowledgeable, and capable of fulfilling all duties\n10. Be comfortable working in an **active veterinary environment** during business hour\n11. No allergies, fear of animals, or other limiting conditions\n12. **Unpacking the Phone Boxes**\n13. Assemble devices\n14. **Phone Removal**\n15. Contractor will **properly box up old** phones and set aside for Hospital Manager to store\n16. **Installing the Phones / Setting Up Yealink Desktop Phones**\n17. Answer site contact’s basic questions about phone use or\n18. Review Key phone system features available on devices\n19. Extensions\n20. Call Park\n21. Call Hold\n22. Toggles\n23. Voicemail\n24. Intercom/Paging\n25. ***If customer has additional questions escalate questions to PetDesk.***\n26. **Progress Tracking & Communication**\n27. Installation progress\n28. Photos and key dates\n29. Access to a device (preferably a laptop) where the Contractor is able to join a zoom call with PetDesk team is necessary\n30. **Call Forwarding Assistance**\n31. Contractor shall assist the on-site POC with **forwarding phone numbers** to the temporary number provided by PetDesk. (See installation guide below)\n32. **Test Calls** (post-installation):\n33. **Outbound call** to a live external number (cell or local business)\n34. **Inbound call** from an external source answered on-site (for call quality check)\n35. **Call to \\*933** to verify E911 service address (do not call 911 directly)\n36. **Device Support**\n37. Support for additional connected devices (if applicable):\n38. Doorbells, Intercom/PA systems, Fax Adapters\n39. **Basic Network Troubleshooting**\n40. Contractor may need to run **new Ethernet cabling**\n41. If poor call quality is identified:\n42. Confirm there are no firewall blocks\n43. Disable SIP ALG if needed\n44. Check for packet filtering issues","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-18T10:30","end":"2026-09-18T13:30"},"payRange":{"min":70,"max":210},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":70,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":51},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $210 (countered: $210) is below minimum threshold $250"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-21T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-09-18T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"},{"start":"2026-09-11T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-11T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"SMALL BACKBOARD/ DATA REMOTE INSTALL/ MUST HAVE BUTT-SET/MULTIMETER-DIS148477"},{"start":"2026-09-10T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-10T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Maintenance Kit Swap - Apex, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-04T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-05T13:30:00.000Z","summary":"DSS 9223 - Install (1) QNAP + UPS + Switch, I