{"job":{"id":19939035,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"Troubleshooting - Damage Assessment","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Job Details:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Work Summary:</strong> Troubleshooting/Damage Assessment for Electronics/Appliances</li><li><strong>Location:</strong> Nelson, VA 24580</li><li><strong>Client Contact:</strong> <del>****** **** * *************</del></li><li><strong>Required Materials:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Reference \"Client Documents\" section for all relevant and necessary documentation.</li><li><strong>Technician is needed to inspect, test, photograph, and document findings for the following claimed items:</strong></li></ul><p><strong>***You are REQUIRED to request and document any and all invoices ***</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>-</strong>Range</p><p>-Range Hood</p><p>-Ceiling Fan (Big Ass Fan)</p><p>-Projector</p><p><br></p><p>*** <strong>YOU ARE </strong>authorized to inspect any additional electronics/appliances the owner may present to you. ***</p><p>*** Should any of the aforementioned items be unavailable for inspection and documentation, notate reason in spreadsheet. ***</p><ul><li><strong>Special Instructions:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>*** NEW *** Access 24/7 Real Time AI Technician Support:</u></strong> <del>**************************************************************</del></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Photos must be uploaded in JPEG/JPG format.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Photo Labeling is <strong>REQUIRED</strong>.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Photos of the electrical panel and power meter/meter box are <strong>REQUIRED</strong>.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Online spreadsheet for inspection findings will be accessible once the work order is assigned.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************** ********* </del></span><del>***************************************</del><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>******</del></span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>****** ******** </del></span><em style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><u><del>**** ******** ********</del></u></em><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><em><u><del> </del></u></em></strong><del>****************************************</del></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Claimed loss type is&nbsp;</strong><em>POWER SURGE</em>.&nbsp;<strong><u>TECHNICIAN SHOULD MAKE AN INDEPENDENT DAMAGE CAUSATION ASSESSMENT BASED ON HIS/HER ONSITE TESTING.</u></strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><u>﻿</u>&gt;&gt; Check breaker panel &gt;&gt; Test power supply line(s) for continuity w/ Multimeter, or for voltage with Voltage Tester &gt;&gt; Test for proper voltage at the applicable source &gt;&gt; Run Device &gt;&gt; Document all performance observations &gt;&gt; Photograph all testing results</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>You&nbsp;must</strong>&nbsp;complete all the tasks listed and submit fully completed work order with labeled photos within 24 hours of appointment time. If more time is needed due to scope and/or number of items, discuss with our office <strong>PRIOR TO</strong> inspection.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>All items must be listed individually on the spreadsheet</strong>. Cannot put 2 or more items on one line of the spreadsheet (Examples:&nbsp;5 Speakers listed in the work order require 5 individual entries in the spreadsheet or 10 light fixtures require 10 individual entries in the spreadsheet)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Please be discrete and confidential with your findings – though your opinions will influence our reporting, only the insurance company can make the ultimate determination of coverage or payout. *** Reference the&nbsp;<u>Keeping Findings Discreet</u>&nbsp;document for suggestions on what to say if asked about findings. ***</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>If you feel there is anything that is urgent or that is mentioned by the owner as urgent to them, call and let us know.</u></strong></li></ul><p><strong>Required Tools and Equipment:</strong></p><ul><li>Multimeter</li><li>Camera (or camera phone that takes quality photos)</li><li>Laptop</li><li>Tape measure</li><li>Ladder (4'6')</li><li>Basic toolkit</li><li>Standard 25 50' Edison 120 VAC extension cord</li><li>IEC to Edison (10A, 2-slot &amp; 3-slot) 120 VAC power supply cords</li><li>Temperature gauge (infrared thermometer or temp. adapter for a multimeter)</li><li>Non-contact Voltage Tester</li></ul><p><strong>Dress Code:</strong></p><ul><li>Casual professional attire (<strong>no logos</strong>)</li></ul><p><strong>Work Overview:</strong></p><p><strong>Pre-Work:</strong></p><ol><li>Set start time.</li><li>Read the entire work order, including scope of work, standard instructions, and confidential information instructions.</li><li>Check all required tools and equipment.</li><li>Ensure a face covering is available.</li><li>Review the CLAIMED LOSS TYPE (<em>POWER SURGE</em>) and be prepared to assess causation.</li></ol><p><strong>On-Site:</strong></p><ol><li>Provide a courtesy call to the insured 30 minutes prior to arrival. If call is not answered, <strong>PROCEED TO SITE.</strong></li><li>Check-in with the insured upon site arrival.</li><li>Obtain the insured's signature on the PROPERTY INSPECTION AGREEMENT.</li><li>Take at least (2) clear quality photos of EACH claimed item.</li><li>Test EVERY claimed item for functionality or continuity with a multimeter.</li><li>Document all performance observations.</li><li>Photograph all testing results.</li><li>Inquire with the insured about replacement or repair invoices.</li><li>Take and upload photos of the power meter/meter box <strong>-AND-</strong> electrical panel.</li><li>Be discreet and confidential with findings.</li><li>In case of any urgent occurrence, contact the <strong>our office</strong> immediately. If afterhours, contact <strong>Emergency After-Hours Tech Line</strong>.</li></ol><p><strong>Post-Work:</strong></p><ol><li>Upload a completed Excel spreadsheet with detailed notes on item information and testing procedures (each item must be listed individually).</li><li>Rename each JPEG photo file with a description of the inspected item.</li><li>Upload photos of all inspected items.</li><li>Upload photos of all relevant invoices/estimates/receipts.</li><li>Upload the signed PROPERTY INSPECTION AGREEMENT.</li><li>Upload the signed CONTRACTOR AGREEMENT.</li><li>Enter detailed Close Out Notes summarizing the assessment, explaining the cause of damage (if any), and including information provided by the insured.</li></ol><p><strong>Required Deliverables:</strong></p><ul><li>Completed Excel spreadsheet with detailed notes or online spreadsheet with detailed testing notes</li><li>Renamed JPEG photos of claimed items</li><li>Photos of power meter/meter box <strong>-AND-</strong> electrical panel</li><li>Photos of all relevant invoices/estimates/receipts</li><li>Signed PROPERTY INSPECTION AGREEMENT</li><li>Signed CONTRACTOR AGREEMENT</li><li>Detailed Close Out Notes</li></ul><p><strong>*** Failure to complete all of the above will result in non-payment for order. We are not paid by our client for late or incomplete work. ***</strong></p><p><strong>Please review and confirm your understanding of the work order details. If you have any questions or require further information, contact our office prior to proceeding with the work. Thank you for your attention to detail and commitment to completing this job efficiently and professionally.</strong></p>","markdown":"**Job Details:**\n\n- **Work Summary:** Troubleshooting/Damage Assessment for Electronics/Appliances\n- **Location:** Nelson, VA 24580\n- **Client Contact:** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- **Required Materials:**\n- Reference \"Client Documents\" section for all relevant and necessary documentation.\n- **Technician is needed to inspect, test, photograph, and document findings for the following claimed items:**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*You are REQUIRED to request and document any and all invoices \\*\\*\\***\n\n**-**Range\n\n-Range Hood\n\n-Ceiling Fan (Big Ass Fan)\n\n-Projector\n\n\\*\\*\\* **YOU ARE** authorized to inspect any additional electronics/appliances the owner may present to you. \\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\* Should any of the aforementioned items be unavailable for inspection and documentation, notate reason in spreadsheet. \\*\\*\\*\n\n- **Special Instructions:**\n- **\\*\\*\\* NEW \\*\\*\\* Access 24/7 Real Time AI Technician Support:** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- Photos must be uploaded in JPEG/JPG format.\n- Photo Labeling is **REQUIRED**.\n- Photos of the electrical panel and power meter/meter box are **REQUIRED**.\n- Online spreadsheet for inspection findings will be accessible once the work order is assigned.\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* *\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- **Claimed loss type is** *POWER SURGE*. **TECHNICIAN SHOULD MAKE AN INDEPENDENT DAMAGE CAUSATION ASSESSMENT BASED ON HIS/HER ONSITE TESTING.**\n- ﻿>> Check breaker panel >> Test power supply line(s) for continuity w/ Multimeter, or for voltage with Voltage Tester >> Test for proper voltage at the applicable source >> Run Device >> Document all performance observations >> Photograph all testing results\n- **You must** complete all the tasks listed and submit fully completed work order with labeled photos within 24 hours of appointment time. If more time is needed due to scope and/or number of items, discuss with our office **PRIOR TO** inspection.\n- **All items must be listed individually on the spreadsheet**. Cannot put 2 or more items on one line of the spreadsheet (Examples: 5 Speakers listed in the work order require 5 individual entries in the spreadsheet or 10 light fixtures require 10 individual entries in the spreadsheet)\n- **Please be discrete and confidential with your findings – though your opinions will influence our reporting, only the insurance company can make the ultimate determination of coverage or payout. \\*\\*\\* Reference the Keeping Findings Discreet document for suggestions on what to say if asked about findings. \\*\\*\\***\n- **If you feel there is anything that is urgent or that is mentioned by the owner as urgent to them, call and let us know.**\n\n**Required Tools and Equipment:**\n\n- Multimeter\n- Camera (or camera phone that takes quality photos)\n- Laptop\n- Tape measure\n- Ladder (4'6')\n- Basic toolkit\n- Standard 25 50' Edison 120 VAC extension cord\n- IEC to Edison (10A, 2-slot & 3-slot) 120 VAC power supply cords\n- Temperature gauge (infrared thermometer or temp. adapter for a multimeter)\n- Non-contact Voltage Tester\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n- Casual professional attire (**no logos**)\n\n**Work Overview:**\n\n**Pre-Work:**\n\n1. Set start time.\n2. Read the entire work order, including scope of work, standard instructions, and confidential information instructions.\n3. Check all required tools and equipment.\n4. Ensure a face covering is available.\n5. Review the CLAIMED LOSS TYPE (*POWER SURGE*) and be prepared to assess causation.\n\n**On-Site:**\n\n1. Provide a courtesy call to the insured 30 minutes prior to arrival. If call is not answered, **PROCEED TO SITE.**\n2. Check-in with the insured upon site arrival.\n3. Obtain the insured's signature on the PROPERTY INSPECTION AGREEMENT.\n4. Take at least (2) clear quality photos of EACH claimed item.\n5. Test EVERY claimed item for functionality or continuity with a multimeter.\n6. Document all performance observations.\n7. Photograph all testing results.\n8. Inquire with the insured about replacement or repair invoices.\n9. Take and upload photos of the power meter/meter box **-AND-** electrical panel.\n10. Be discreet and confidential with findings.\n11. In case of any urgent occurrence, contact the **our office** immediately. If afterhours, contact **Emergency After-Hours Tech Line**.\n\n**Post-Work:**\n\n1. Upload a completed Excel spreadsheet with detailed notes on item information and testing procedures (each item must be listed individually).\n2. Rename each JPEG photo file with a description of the inspected item.\n3. Upload photos of all inspected items.\n4. Upload photos of all relevant invoices/estimates/receipts.\n5. Upload the signed PROPERTY INSPECTION AGREEMENT.\n6. Upload the signed CONTRACTOR AGREEMENT.\n7. Enter detailed Close Out Notes summarizing the assessment, explaining the cause of damage (if any), and including information provided by the insured.\n\n**Required Deliverables:**\n\n- Completed Excel spreadsheet with detailed notes or online spreadsheet with detailed testing notes\n- Renamed JPEG photos of claimed items\n- Photos of power meter/meter box **-AND-** electrical panel\n- Photos of all relevant invoices/estimates/receipts\n- Signed PROPERTY INSPECTION AGREEMENT\n- Signed CONTRACTOR AGREEMENT\n- Detailed Close Out Notes\n\n**\\*\\*\\* Failure to complete all of the above will result in non-payment for order. We are not paid by our client for late or incomplete work. \\*\\*\\***\n\n**Please review and confirm your understanding of the work order details. If you have any questions or require further information, contact our office prior to proceeding with the work. Thank you for your attention to detail and commitment to completing this job efficiently and professionally.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-14T10:00","end":"2026-09-14T12:00","latestStart":"2026-09-14T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":184,"max":184},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":49},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $184 is below minimum threshold $250"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-15T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-17T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-18T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"},{"start":"2026-09-11T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-11T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"SMALL BACKBOARD/ DATA REMOTE INSTALL/ MUST HAVE BUTT-SET/MULTIMETER-DIS148477"},{"start":"2026-09-10T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-10T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Maintenance Kit Swap - Apex, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-04T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-05T13:30:00.000Z","summary":"DSS 9223 - Install (1) QNAP + UPS + Switch, Install (3) TP-Link Wireless Bridge, Install (3) 8 Port PoE Switch, Replace (15) Analog Cameras w/ (15) IP Cameras + Cable Runs - Lead Tech"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789161341492}
{"job":{"id":19939003,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"ESP Global Services Inc.","title":"WEEKLY DESKTOP SUPPORT- KT","description":{"html":"<p>Genpact Kymera Ticket Reference: CS0951170/WOT0886318</p>\n<p><strong>Please send resume to Cherise.cadiz@espglobalservices.com</strong></p>\n<p>SOW: DESKTOP SUPPORT</p>\n<p>LOCATION: NC</p>\n<p>HOURS: 32- (Monday to Wednesday)</p>\n<p><strong>L1 Desktop Support Engineer – ESP Standard</strong></p>\n<p>1-3 years’ experience in IT infrastructure support, troubleshooting hardware, software, and operating system issues. As a Level 1 engineer, you will resolve issues while adhering to hardware warranty and customer security compliance standards.</p>\n<p>Hardware Support &amp; Troubleshooting:</p>\n<p>• Hands-on experience in installing, troubleshooting, and repairing desktops, printers, laptops, and other computer peripherals. (Monitors, keyboards, mice, printers, fax machines, scanners)</p>\n<p>• Ability to lift and move equipment weighing up to 50 lbs.</p>\n<p>• Provide Smart Hands support for peripheral and networking hardware, including routers, switches, firewalls, racks, and cabinets. Smart Hands activities involve performing physical tasks on-site while following instructions from senior engineers or remote technical teams, or by adhering to predefined procedures. Level 1 deskside engineers are expected to execute these tasks as directed but do not engage in configuring or troubleshooting complex network infrastructure, which is escalated to Level 2 engineers as needed.</p>\n<p>Software &amp; OS Support:</p>\n<p>• Experience to follow instructions for installing and troubleshooting desktop applications.</p>\n<p>• Skilled in desk-side support and PC break/fix, with basic administration of Windows operating systems.</p>\n<p>• Assist with anti-spyware and anti-virus software, including troubleshooting installation issues.</p>\n<p>• Basic support for iOS/Android tablets, assisting with configuration and troubleshooting.</p>\n<p>• Assist with software and operating system deployments using tools such as MSCM, WDS, or MDM solutions to install Microsoft Office, antivirus software, and company-specific applications. Level 1 deskside engineers support these deployments by following established procedures but do not take ownership of or troubleshoot enterprise deployment failures, which are escalated to Level 2 engineers when necessary.</p>\n<p>Active Directory &amp; Identity Management:</p>\n<p>• Assist with basic user account management tasks in Active Directory, including password resets, account unlocks, and adding users to existing groups. Level 1 deskside engineers perform these routine tasks but do not engage in more complex</p>\n<p>account management or troubleshooting, which is escalated to Level 2 engineers as required.</p>\n<p>• Assist with access permissions and escalate issues as needed to senior teams for complex Active Directory problems.</p>\n<p>• Level 1 deskside engineers are not expected to troubleshoot complex security, firewall, or enterprise software issues Network &amp; Connectivity Support:</p>\n<p>• Basic knowledge of enterprise LAN and WAN setups, with the ability to troubleshoot simple connectivity issues.</p>\n<p>• Familiarity with TCP/IP, DNS, DHCP, VPN, and RDP.</p>\n<p>• Basic wireless network troubleshooting, including using diagnostic tools (ping, ipconfig, Wi-Fi analyser).</p>\n<p>Certifications:</p>\n<p>• CompTIA A+ or equivalent entry-level IT certification (or acquired during employment). • Basic awareness of ITIL processes, including Incident, Change, and Problem Management, Service Requests, and spare/buffer stock management.</p>\n<p>• Customer site-specific certification may be introduced during induction.</p>\n<p>Competency Requirements:</p>\n<p>• Strong written and oral communication skills with clients and management.</p>\n<p>• Excellent people skills for effective interaction with users and teams. • Ability to meet deadlines and manage tasks efficiently.</p>\n<p>• Strong deductive reasoning skills for troubleshooting issues.</p>\n<p>• Capability to work independently with minimal supervision.</p>\n<p>• Support of computer networks, as directed by senior technicians or service desk support.</p>\n<p>• Proficient in ticket handling, adhering to client requirements.</p>\n<p>Languages:</p>\n<p>The Desktop Engineer must demonstrate B2-level proficiency in both English and the relevant local language, as certified by the Common European Framework of Reference for Languages (CEFR), to ensure effective communication with end users and stakeholders. Higher proficiency levels, including mastery or native fluency, may warrant a rate adjustment.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>","markdown":"Genpact Kymera Ticket Reference: CS0951170/WOT0886318\n\n**Please send resume to Cherise.cadiz@espglobalservices.com**\n\nSOW: DESKTOP SUPPORT\n\nLOCATION: NC\n\nHOURS: 32- (Monday to Wednesday)\n\n**L1 Desktop Support Engineer – ESP Standard**\n\n1-3 years’ experience in IT infrastructure support, troubleshooting hardware, software, and operating system issues. As a Level 1 engineer, you will resolve issues while adhering to hardware warranty and customer security compliance standards.\n\nHardware Support & Troubleshooting:\n\n• Hands-on experience in installing, troubleshooting, and repairing desktops, printers, laptops, and other computer peripherals. (Monitors, keyboards, mice, printers, fax machines, scanners)\n\n• Ability to lift and move equipment weighing up to 50 lbs.\n\n• Provide Smart Hands support for peripheral and networking hardware, including routers, switches, firewalls, racks, and cabinets. Smart Hands activities involve performing physical tasks on-site while following instructions from senior engineers or remote technical teams, or by adhering to predefined procedures. Level 1 deskside engineers are expected to execute these tasks as directed but do not engage in configuring or troubleshooting complex network infrastructure, which is escalated to Level 2 engineers as needed.\n\nSoftware & OS Support:\n\n• Experience to follow instructions for installing and troubleshooting desktop applications.\n\n• Skilled in desk-side support and PC break/fix, with basic administration of Windows operating systems.\n\n• Assist with anti-spyware and anti-virus software, including troubleshooting installation issues.\n\n• Basic support for iOS/Android tablets, assisting with configuration and troubleshooting.\n\n• Assist with software and operating system deployments using tools such as MSCM, WDS, or MDM solutions to install Microsoft Office, antivirus software, and company-specific applications. Level 1 deskside engineers support these deployments by following established procedures but do not take ownership of or troubleshoot enterprise deployment failures, which are escalated to Level 2 engineers when necessary.\n\nActive Directory & Identity Management:\n\n• Assist with basic user account management tasks in Active Directory, including password resets, account unlocks, and adding users to existing groups. Level 1 deskside engineers perform these routine tasks but do not engage in more complex\n\naccount management or troubleshooting, which is escalated to Level 2 engineers as required.\n\n• Assist with access permissions and escalate issues as needed to senior teams for complex Active Directory problems.\n\n• Level 1 deskside engineers are not expected to troubleshoot complex security, firewall, or enterprise software issues Network & Connectivity Support:\n\n• Basic knowledge of enterprise LAN and WAN setups, with the ability to troubleshoot simple connectivity issues.\n\n• Familiarity with TCP/IP, DNS, DHCP, VPN, and RDP.\n\n• Basic wireless network troubleshooting, including using diagnostic tools (ping, ipconfig, Wi-Fi analyser).\n\nCertifications:\n\n• CompTIA A+ or equivalent entry-level IT certification (or acquired during employment). • Basic awareness of ITIL processes, including Incident, Change, and Problem Management, Service Requests, and spare/buffer stock management.\n\n• Customer site-specific certification may be introduced during induction.\n\nCompetency Requirements:\n\n• Strong written and oral communication skills with clients and management.\n\n• Excellent people skills for effective interaction with users and teams. • Ability to meet deadlines and manage tasks efficiently.\n\n• Strong deductive reasoning skills for troubleshooting issues.\n\n• Capability to work independently with minimal supervision.\n\n• Support of computer networks, as directed by senior technicians or service desk support.\n\n• Proficient in ticket handling, adhering to client requirements.\n\nLanguages:\n\nThe Desktop Engineer must demonstrate B2-level proficiency in both English and the relevant local language, as certified by the Common European Framework of Reference for Languages (CEFR), to ensure effective communication with end users and stakeholders. Higher proficiency levels, including mastery or native fluency, may warrant a rate adjustment.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-14T08:00","end":"2026-09-16T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":400},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":8,"distance":6},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":60,"baseAmount":480,"estHours":8,"travelExpense":0,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T15:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":60,"mode":"hours","reason":"arrival_window"}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-15T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-17T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-18T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"},{"start":"2026-09-11T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-11T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"SMALL BACKBOARD/ DATA REMOTE INSTALL/ MUST HAVE BUTT-SET/MULTIMETER-DIS148477"},{"start":"2026-09-10T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-10T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Maintenance Kit Swap - Apex, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-04T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-05T13:30:00.000Z","summary":"DSS 9223 - Install (1) QNAP + UPS + Switch, Install (3) TP-Link Wireless Bridge, Install (3) 8 Port PoE Switch, Replace (15) Analog Cameras w/ (15) IP Cameras + Cable Runs - Lead Tech"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1789161351362}
{"job":{"id":19938807,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Abacus Hardware","title":"Tech Needed for DC84 Raleigh NC","description":{"html":"<p><em>The purpose of this document is to provide the scope to internal or external Smart Hands resources that will be supporting the O&amp;M PHS MIST Migration project.</em></p><p><strong>Note: </strong><em>Failure to follow instructions may result in penalty.</em><strong> </strong></p><ul><li>Field Engineer to follow instructions from the O&amp;M Engineer.</li><li>Pictures to be taken before and after moving any cables or devices</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Smart Hands Equipment:</strong></p><ul><li>&nbsp;Smart Hands needs to bring for the PHS MIST Migration</li><li>&nbsp;Laptop to use with console cable</li><li>&nbsp;Laptop&nbsp;Applications</li><li>&nbsp;HOT SPOT (access to remotely connect to the internet )</li><li>&nbsp;PuTTY installed on the local contact’s laptop (with required drivers)&nbsp;</li><li>MS Teams Meeting&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Screwdrivers (3mm Allen wrench, Phillips &amp; flathead)&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Detailed Scope: </strong></p><p><strong><span class=\"ql-cursor\">﻿</span>﻿Call into the Teams bridge follow instruction from the oncall engineer to install a follow Circuit upgrade Scope&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>********** ** *** ****** ***** ***** ***</del></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>******</del></strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><u><del>*********** ******* ***** *** ***** ******* *** ****** * ** ** * *** ******** ***** * * *** **** *** ******** *** ******* ***** *** *********** **** ******** ********* ********** * ***********</del></u></strong></p><p><strong>Scope of Smart Hands Services:</strong></p><ul><li>&nbsp;&nbsp;Initial assessment &amp; planning.&nbsp;</li><li>&nbsp;Owens &amp; Minor using the Work Order Request form to provide details about location, site contact, on-site visit timing, and hardware.&nbsp;·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>&nbsp;&nbsp;Console Cable to login into the Juniper SSR130 as a backup plan along with PuTTY installed on the local contact’s laptop (with required drivers)&nbsp;·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>&nbsp;&nbsp;Join the MS Teams Technical Bridge and wait for instructions from the O&amp;M Lead Engineer</li></ul><p><strong>Action to be taken&nbsp;</strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Smart Hands arriving onsite to access Comms or Server room locate Juniper Node 0&nbsp;</li><li>Bring up your Laptop log into Teams Technical Meeting</li><li>Log into your HOT SPOT (access to remotely connect to the internet )</li><li>Bring up PuTTY installed on the local contact’s laptop (with required drivers)</li><li>Connect the Console cable to your laptop</li><li>Wait for instructions from the assigned engineer&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong> Action to be taken if the VPN Router is required&nbsp;: </strong> ·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><ol><li>&nbsp;Smart Hands need to configure the TP-Link ER605 V2 Wired Gigabit VPN Router</li></ol><ul><li>Bring up your Laptop log into TP-Link ER605 V2 Wired Gigabit VPN Router</li><li>Log into&nbsp;</li><li>Bring up&nbsp;</li><li>&nbsp;Connect&nbsp;</li><li>Wait for instructions&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Dress Code Policy:</strong></p><p>To maintain a clean, professional, and respectful environment, the following dress code must be observed:</p><p><strong>Permitted Attire:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pants:</strong> Clean slacks, khakis, or jeans are acceptable. Jeans must be in good condition, free of holes, excessive wear, or distressing. When in doubt about an item’s appropriateness, please choose an alternative.</li><li><strong>Footwear:</strong> Clean, closed-toe shoes such as sneakers are permitted, provided they are in good condition and free of holes or damage.</li><li><strong>Grooming &amp; Hygiene:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Hair must be neatly groomed and maintained.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Facial hair, including beards, must be clean and properly trimmed.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Good personal hygiene is required at all times.</li></ul><p><strong>Prohibited Attire:</strong></p><ul><li>Shirts with <strong>graphics, logos, slogans, or advertisements</strong> of any kind.</li><li><strong>Sandals</strong>, open-toed shoes, or any footwear with holes.</li><li><strong>Dresses or skirts</strong> of any style or length.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Professionalism</strong>:</p><p>We adhere to the highest standards of professionalism for our organization. You are representing an organization that stands for integrity, expertise, promptness, common courtesy, respectful conversations &amp; timeliness to compete projects. Refrain from any conversations regarding pay rate or finances of any kind, political conversations, profanity, religious views and conversations that could be posted on social media and bring a negative light to any or all involved.&nbsp;</p>","markdown":"*The purpose of this document is to provide the scope to internal or external Smart Hands resources that will be supporting the O&M PHS MIST Migration project.*\n\n**Note:** *Failure to follow instructions may result in penalty.*\n\n- Field Engineer to follow instructions from the O&M Engineer.\n- Pictures to be taken before and after moving any cables or devices\n\n**Smart Hands Equipment:**\n\n- Smart Hands needs to bring for the PHS MIST Migration\n- Laptop to use with console cable\n- Laptop Applications\n- HOT SPOT (access to remotely connect to the internet )\n- PuTTY installed on the local contact’s laptop (with required drivers)\n- MS Teams Meeting\n- Screwdrivers (3mm Allen wrench, Phillips & flathead)\n\n**Detailed Scope:**\n\n**﻿﻿Call into the Teams bridge follow instruction from the oncall engineer to install a follow Circuit upgrade Scope**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\***\n\n**\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\* \\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**Scope of Smart Hands Services:**\n\n- Initial assessment & planning.\n- Owens & Minor using the Work Order Request form to provide details about location, site contact, on-site visit timing, and hardware. ·\n- Console Cable to login into the Juniper SSR130 as a backup plan along with PuTTY installed on the local contact’s laptop (with required drivers) ·\n- Join the MS Teams Technical Bridge and wait for instructions from the O&M Lead Engineer\n\n**Action to be taken** ·\n\n- Smart Hands arriving onsite to access Comms or Server room locate Juniper Node 0\n- Bring up your Laptop log into Teams Technical Meeting\n- Log into your HOT SPOT (access to remotely connect to the internet )\n- Bring up PuTTY installed on the local contact’s laptop (with required drivers)\n- Connect the Console cable to your laptop\n- Wait for instructions from the assigned engineer\n\n **Action to be taken if the VPN Router is required :**  ·\n\n1. Smart Hands need to configure the TP-Link ER605 V2 Wired Gigabit VPN Router\n\n- Bring up your Laptop log into TP-Link ER605 V2 Wired Gigabit VPN Router\n- Log into\n- Bring up\n- Connect\n- Wait for instructions\n\n**Dress Code Policy:**\n\nTo maintain a clean, professional, and respectful environment, the following dress code must be observed:\n\n**Permitted Attire:**\n\n- **Pants:** Clean slacks, khakis, or jeans are acceptable. Jeans must be in good condition, free of holes, excessive wear, or distressing. When in doubt about an item’s appropriateness, please choose an alternative.\n- **Footwear:** Clean, closed-toe shoes such as sneakers are permitted, provided they are in good condition and free of holes or damage.\n- **Grooming & Hygiene:**\n- Hair must be neatly groomed and maintained.\n- Facial hair, including beards, must be clean and properly trimmed.\n- Good personal hygiene is required at all times.\n\n**Prohibited Attire:**\n\n- Shirts with **graphics, logos, slogans, or advertisements** of any kind.\n- **Sandals**, open-toed shoes, or any footwear with holes.\n- **Dresses or skirts** of any style or length.\n\n**Professionalism**:\n\nWe adhere to the highest standards of professionalism for our organization. You are representing an organization that stands for integrity, expertise, promptness, common courtesy, respectful conversations & timeliness to compete projects. Refrain from any conversations regarding pay rate or finances of any kind, political conversations, profanity, religious views and conversations that could be posted on social media and bring a negative light to any or all involved.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-11T04:00","end":"2026-10-11T07:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":150},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":12},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $150 (countered: $180) is below minimum threshold $350"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-13T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-14T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-15T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-13T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Columbus Day"},{"start":"2026-10-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-12T22:00:00.000