{"job":{"id":"7269886749","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"MG21 Gateway SIM Swap & Connection Verification","description":"Hilton SIM Swap SOW<br><br>Required Materials:<br>Laptop w/ Admin Rights and Ethernet Port<br>RJ45-RJ45 Ethernet Cable<br><br>Required Deliverables:<br>NEW SIM Number<br>MG21 with visible Purple status light<br>MG21 before and after pictures<br><br>SIM Card UPS Tracking: TBD<br><br>Please review the SIM Installation section of the attached PDF prior to dispatch.<br><br>Technician must be able to access and actively use Microsoft Teams, including Teams chat, for communication, coordination, and support during the installation<br>Upon arrival, the Granite Technician checks in with the Front Desk and asks for the Granite package containing the SIM card<br>For any access issues, please reach out to the Granite PM Jonathon at (401) 955-9477<br><br>When you have the SIM and locate the MG21, please call into the below bridge to work with Granite technical support:<br><br>Dial-In: +1 929-229-2436<br>Passcode: 355013377#<br><br>General Directions:<br>Validate the existing MG21 Gateway is fully operational with the local manager<br>Power down the existing MG21 Gateway<br>Record the serial number for Hilton Worldwide records<br>Disconnect the MG from power<br>Remove the existing SIM by unscrewing the back panel<br>Insert the new SIM and replace the back plate<br>Power on the unit and confirm a solid purple LED indicating proper configuration, active SIM, and cellular connectivity<br>If status light remains Amber (Orange): utilize laptop, console cable, and mobile phone for any required Hilton Worldwide APN configuration (see steps below)<br>Verify the MG21 router is online and all network services are operational<br>Before leaving site, confirm system functionality with the technical coordinator on the Teams meeting<br>Record the store manager’s name as confirmation of successful SIM migration<br><br>How to Manually Change APN<br><br>Step 1 — Physically Connect to the MG<br>Power on the Meraki MG.<br>Connect your laptop directly to the MG LAN port using an Ethernet cable.<br>Wait about 1–2 minutes for your computer to receive an IP address automatically via DHCP.<br><br>Step 2 — Open the Local Status Page (may need to use an incognito browser window)<br>Open a web browser and go to: mg.meraki.com  <br>If that does not work, try:<br>• setup.meraki.com<br>• my.meraki.com<br>If that still does not work, try:<br>Open the Command Prompt and perform an IPCONFIG<br>Get the Gateway IP<br>Copy or Type the Gateway IP in the Web Browser tab<br>Click Enter<br><br>Step 3 — Log Into the MG<br>For newer firmware:<br>Username: admin<br>Password:  (please include the dashes)<br>The serial number is located on the sticker on the bottom or back of the MG.<br><br>Step 4 — Navigate to the Configure Page<br>Select the Configure tab.<br>Locate the Bearer Settings or Cellular Configuration section.<br><br>Step 5 — Override the SIM APN Settings<br>Find the option labeled Cellular Override or Override SIM Settings.<br>Enable Override SIM Settings to manually configure the APN.<br>Step 6 — Enter the APN<br>In the APN field, enter: wbdata<br><br>Step 6: Leave Username and Password blank unless your carrier specifically requires them.<br>Example:<br>APN: wbdata<br>Username: blank<br>Password: blank<br> <br>Step 7 — Confirm/update the next fields<br>Cellular authorization:  None<br>Cellular IP type:  IPv4v6<br> <br>Step 8 — Save the Configuration<br>Scroll to the bottom of the page.<br>Click Save.<br>The MG may briefly reconnect to the cellular network while applying the new APN.<br><br>Step 9 — Verify Connectivity<br>Go to the Connection or Cellular Status page and verify:<br>Carrier is detected<br>APN shows wbdata<br>Signal strength is present<br>Internet connectivity is connected<br>Meraki cloud connectivity is connected<br><br>Troubleshooting<br>Cannot Reach mg.meraki.com:<br>Disconnect and reconnect Ethernet<br>Use another browser<br>Try incognito browser<br>Confirm Wi-Fi is off<br>Browse directly to the MG gateway IP<br>Try setup.meraki.com<br><br>APN Does Not Save:<br>Ensure you clicked Save<br>Reboot the MG<br>Recheck the APN spelling: wbdata<br><br>No Cellular Connectivity:<br>Verify SIM card is active<br>Verify SIM is fully inserted<br>Confirm carrier supports the device<br>Confirm APN is correct<br>Verify signal strength is adequate<br><br>Optional — Factory Reset<br>Press and hold the Reset button for at least 10 seconds.<br>Allow 5–10 minutes for reboot and reconfiguration.<br>Factory reset clears Local Status Page settings including APN configuration.<br><br>Document and provide any returned equipment to the hotel MOD","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-23T08:45","end":"2026-09-23T10:15"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":75},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":1.5,"distance":9.3},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $75 (countered: $98) is below minimum threshold $350"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-18T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"},{"start":"2026-09-11T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-11T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"SMALL BACKBOARD/ DATA REMOTE INSTALL/ MUST HAVE BUTT-SET/MULTIMETER-DIS148477"},{"start":"2026-09-10T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-10T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Maintenance Kit Swap - Apex, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-04T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-05T13:30:00.000Z","summary":"DSS 9223 - Install (1) QNAP + UPS + Switch, Install (3) TP-Link Wireless Bridge, Install (3) 8 Port PoE Switch, Replace (15) Analog Cameras w/ (15) IP Cameras + Cable Runs - Lead Tech"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789161373770}
{"job":{"id":19938455,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Integrated Business Applications","title":"Troubleshoot 13x IP cameras down","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Troubleshoot 13x IP Cameras</strong></p><p>Only an experienced&nbsp;<strong>IP Camera and Networking Technician</strong>&nbsp;is needed to troubleshoot&nbsp;Thirteen<strong>&nbsp;(13) offline IP cameras (1, 4, 13-23)</strong>. Technician must be proficient in diagnosing issues involving&nbsp;<strong>PoE switches, network connections, access points, and CAT cabling</strong>.</p><p>Please&nbsp;<strong>do not request this work order</strong>&nbsp;if you are not equipped or skilled to perform IP camera diagnostics.</p><p><strong>Photos are required</strong>&nbsp;before and after troubleshooting, including:</p><ul><li>The manager’s camera view or NVR screen</li><li>Camera model and serial number labels</li><li>Any exposed cable runs or conduit conditions (installed, damaged, or missing)</li></ul><p>Thorough notes must be included for all findings and actions taken.</p><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><p>Upon arrival, the Technician must&nbsp;<strong>check in with the General Manager</strong>&nbsp;and inform them they are with&nbsp;<strong>IBA</strong>&nbsp;to troubleshoot the offline camera.</p><p>The Manager will identify the camera location and assist with access as needed.</p><p>The affected camera will be connected via&nbsp;<strong>CAT5 or CAT6 cabling</strong>&nbsp;to a&nbsp;<strong>PoE switch</strong>&nbsp;located in either the&nbsp;<strong>Main Building</strong>,&nbsp;<strong>Shop Building</strong>, or&nbsp;<strong>Pole-mounted cabinet</strong>.</p><p>Some outdoor cameras may require an extension ladder or lift for access.</p><p>If applicable, a&nbsp;<strong>40’ articulating boom lift will be available on-site</strong>&nbsp;for this task.</p><p>Technician must be&nbsp;<strong>trained and authorized to operate a boom lift</strong>&nbsp;— otherwise, this work order cannot be accepted.</p><p><strong>Troubleshooting Steps:</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Visually inspect</strong>&nbsp;camera, cabling, and mounting area for damage or loose connections.</li><li><strong>Test the PoE connection</strong>&nbsp;using an IP camera tester with built-in PoE.</li><li><strong>Check the network link</strong>&nbsp;between the camera and the PoE switch.</li><li>If the camera is offline,&nbsp;<strong>verify link lights</strong>&nbsp;and test the cable for continuity or damage.</li><li>If the camera has been reset to defaults,&nbsp;<strong>reconfigure network settings</strong>&nbsp;with assistance from remote support.</li><li><strong>Confirm camera visibility</strong>&nbsp;on the NVR or management software once restored.</li></ol><p><br></p><p>Contact&nbsp;<strong>Joshua Myers (918-813-1569)</strong>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<strong>Drew Dimatos (214-773-6902)</strong>&nbsp;for remote configuration support as needed.</p><p>Support may be provided through&nbsp;<strong>TeamViewer</strong>,&nbsp;<strong>AnyDesk</strong>, or&nbsp;<strong>Quick Assist</strong>&nbsp;as needed.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Documentation Requirements:</strong></p><ul><li>Before and after photos of the camera and manager’s screen</li><li>Photo of camera model/serial number label</li><li>Notes detailing the issue, diagnostic steps, and final outcome</li><li>Photos of any damaged or exposed cables/conduit</li></ul><p><strong>Required Equipment and Tools:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Tall Extension Ladder</strong>&nbsp;(up to 22’ if needed)</li><li><strong>Laptop and Hotspot</strong>&nbsp;(with&nbsp;<em>Advanced IP Scanner</em>&nbsp;installed)</li><li><strong>Monitor, Keyboard, and Mouse</strong>&nbsp;(for NVR access if necessary)</li><li><strong>IP Camera Tester with built-in PoE</strong>&nbsp;(NOT an analog tester)</li><li><strong>Cable Tester</strong></li><li>Standard networking tools and materials:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">RJ-45 connectors, CAT6 cable, termination/crimp tools</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Screwdrivers, drill, snips, labeler, pull string</li></ul><p>Technician is responsible for providing all required tools and materials to complete this troubleshooting work order.</p>","markdown":"**Troubleshoot 13x IP Cameras**\n\nOnly an experienced **IP Camera and Networking Technician** is needed to troubleshoot Thirteen **(13) offline IP cameras (1, 4, 13-23)**. Technician must be proficient in diagnosing issues involving **PoE switches, network connections, access points, and CAT cabling**.\n\nPlease **do not request this work order** if you are not equipped or skilled to perform IP camera diagnostics.\n\n**Photos are required** before and after troubleshooting, including:\n\n- The manager’s camera view or NVR screen\n- Camera model and serial number labels\n- Any exposed cable runs or conduit conditions (installed, damaged, or missing)\n\nThorough notes must be included for all findings and actions taken.\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\nUpon arrival, the Technician must **check in with the General Manager** and inform them they are with **IBA** to troubleshoot the offline camera.\n\nThe Manager will identify the camera location and assist with access as needed.\n\nThe affected camera will be connected via **CAT5 or CAT6 cabling** to a **PoE switch** located in either the **Main Building**, **Shop Building**, or **Pole-mounted cabinet**.\n\nSome outdoor cameras may require an extension ladder or lift for access.\n\nIf applicable, a **40’ articulating boom lift will be available on-site** for this task.\n\nTechnician must be **trained and authorized to operate a boom lift** — otherwise, this work order cannot be accepted.\n\n**Troubleshooting Steps:**\n\n1. **Visually inspect** camera, cabling, and mounting area for damage or loose connections.\n2. **Test the PoE connection** using an IP camera tester with built-in PoE.\n3. **Check the network link** between the camera and the PoE switch.\n4. If the camera is offline, **verify link lights** and test the cable for continuity or damage.\n5. If the camera has been reset to defaults, **reconfigure network settings** with assistance from remote support.\n6. **Confirm camera visibility** on the NVR or management software once restored.\n\nContact **Joshua Myers (918-813-1569)** or **Drew Dimatos (214-773-6902)** for remote configuration support as needed.\n\nSupport may be provided through **TeamViewer**, **AnyDesk**, or **Quick Assist** as needed.\n\n**Documentation Requirements:**\n\n- Before and after photos of the camera and manager’s screen\n- Photo of camera model/serial number label\n- Notes detailing the issue, diagnostic steps, and final outcome\n- Photos of any damaged or exposed cables/conduit\n\n**Required Equipment and Tools:**\n\n- **Tall Extension Ladder** (up to 22’ if needed)\n- **Laptop and Hotspot** (with *Advanced IP Scanner* installed)\n- **Monitor, Keyboard, and Mouse** (for NVR access if necessary)\n- **IP Camera Tester with built-in PoE** (NOT an analog tester)\n- **Cable Tester**\n- Standard networking tools and materials:\n- RJ-45 connectors, CAT6 cable, termination/crimp tools\n- Screwdrivers, drill, snips, labeler, pull string\n\nTechnician is responsible for providing all required tools and materials to complete this troubleshooting work order.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-16T13:00","end":"2026-09-16T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":300,"max":300},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":35},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"fixed","counterRate":100,"baseAmount":300,"estHours":3,"travelExpense":60,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T18:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":60,"mode":"hours","reason":"arrival_window"}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-16T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start"