{"job":{"id":19769277,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"LITnetworking LLC","title":"SMALL BACKBOARD/ DATA REMOTE INSTALL/ MUST HAVE BUTT-SET/MULTIMETER-DIS148477","description":{"html":"<p>PLEASE CALL METTEL SUPPORT UPON ARRIVAL 3852623457 Ticket 11745077</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Call Travis Newkirk @ 3852623457 when on site.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>**PIAB Install**</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Tech will need: butt-set, bridge clips, toner, multi-meter, label maker, screw driver.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>This is for a PIAB install. CROSS CONNECT REQUIRED.</p>\n<p>Install/mount equipment (CDS-9090, Pano MIMO antenna, hydra cable and 66 block) on the backboard near the network rack. Connect WAN port to store switch 01 port 14 or port 15 if port 14 is unavailable, confirm WAN and LTE connectivity, test line (inbound and outbound) off the CDS-9090 and the 66 block.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Cross connect new line from 66 block to the stores downtime phone. This new line will replace the existing line on the phone. Tech may have to tone existing jack. Have store manager confirm downtime phone is working on the new line.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Label the following and take pictures of each item:</p>\n<p>Label CDS-9090 with 'METTEL'</p>\n<p>Label 66 block cover with 'METTEL xx/xx/xxxx (date of install)'</p>\n<p>Label inside 66 block with each phone number</p>\n<p>Take photo of WAN cable connection on the CDS-9090</p>\n<p>Take photo of WAN cable connection on the switch port</p>\n<p>Take photo of downtime phone, wall jack, switch port</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>LCON: Dominique Brown 919-200-6460</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Once install is complete, please contact the GAP Network Voice Team at 800-333-7899 Extn: 66645 to checkout and provide a status</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>-Data Remote CDS-9090</p>\n<p>-MiMo Antenna &amp; Bracket Kit</p>\n<p>-Tech to locate equipment.</p>\n<p>-Locate customer network switch in room switch/router.</p>\n<p>-Install MetTel Board and CDS-9090.</p>\n<p>-Attach antennas and power on.</p>\n<p>-MetTel will validate configurations.</p>\n<p>-Connect laptop and run speed tests over LTE. Do not use speedtest.net</p>\n<p>-Verify dial tone and in/outbound calling on all provisioned CDS9090 RJ11 ports.</p>\n<p>-Validate e911 address on one each line.</p>\n<p>-Use multimeter to verify each existing pair has a voltage of 0 on customer side of the demark.</p>\n<p>If voltage is found, locate the short/bridge and repair.</p>\n<p>-Work with customer to contact the alarms monitoring vendor and have the Fire Panel placed into test mode.</p>\n<p>-Locate/tag Elevator, Fire and Burglar lines.</p>\n<p>-Cross-connect to Fire Panel, Burglar Panel, and test.</p>\n<p>-Contact the fire monitoring vendor to confirm that they are receiving the faults, restoral, low battery and battery restore signals.</p>\n<p>-Confirm monitoring vendor sees the correct service address.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Please review the following requirements and protocols for your upcoming assignment with Lit Networking:</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>To ensure the successful completion of this site visit, you must arrive with the following tools and materials: - A fully charged laptop with an Ethernet port and a cellphone with a hotspot device. - Cabling tools: Multimeter wire tester, butt set, punch down tool, crimpers, and wire cutters. - Hardware: RJ11 and RJ45 connectors, biscuit jacks, and 100 feet of Cat 5e/6 cable for potential device relocation. - Standard mounting kit: Drill, level, hammer, screwdrivers, screws, and anchors. - General supplies: Adjustable or open-end wrenches, a 4–6 ft ladder, and a 100 ft extension cord.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Work Order and Payment Procedures All work orders must be signed by the onsite Point of Contact and must clearly list your arrival and departure times. Please upload the signed Lit Networking work order directly to Field Nation. Please be advised that any forged signatures will be reported to Field Nation and will result in non-payment. Adhering to these documentation requirements is essential to avoid any delays in your payment processing. If you encounter any issues while onsite, please leave a detailed message through the Field Nation platform.</p>","markdown":"PLEASE CALL METTEL SUPPORT UPON ARRIVAL 3852623457 Ticket 11745077\n\nCall Travis Newkirk @ 3852623457 when on site.\n\n\\*\\*PIAB Install\\*\\*\n\nTech will need: butt-set, bridge clips, toner, multi-meter, label maker, screw driver.\n\nThis is for a PIAB install. CROSS CONNECT REQUIRED.\n\nInstall/mount equipment (CDS-9090, Pano MIMO antenna, hydra cable and 66 block) on the backboard near the network rack. Connect WAN port to store switch 01 port 14 or port 15 if port 14 is unavailable, confirm WAN and LTE connectivity, test line (inbound and outbound) off the CDS-9090 and the 66 block.\n\nCross connect new line from 66 block to the stores downtime phone. This new line will replace the existing line on the phone. Tech may have to tone existing jack. Have store manager confirm downtime phone is working on the new line.\n\nLabel the following and take pictures of each item:\n\nLabel CDS-9090 with 'METTEL'\n\nLabel 66 block cover with 'METTEL xx/xx/xxxx (date of install)'\n\nLabel inside 66 block with each phone number\n\nTake photo of WAN cable connection on the CDS-9090\n\nTake photo of WAN cable connection on the switch port\n\nTake photo of downtime phone, wall jack, switch port\n\nLCON: Dominique Brown 919-200-6460\n\nOnce install is complete, please contact the GAP Network Voice Team at 800-333-7899 Extn: 66645 to checkout and provide a status\n\n-Data Remote CDS-9090\n\n-MiMo Antenna & Bracket Kit\n\n-Tech to locate equipment.\n\n-Locate customer network switch in room switch/router.\n\n-Install MetTel Board and CDS-9090.\n\n-Attach antennas and power on.\n\n-MetTel will validate configurations.\n\n-Connect laptop and run speed tests over LTE. Do not use speedtest.net\n\n-Verify dial tone and in/outbound calling on all provisioned CDS9090 RJ11 ports.\n\n-Validate e911 address on one each line.\n\n-Use multimeter to verify each existing pair has a voltage of 0 on customer side of the demark.\n\nIf voltage is found, locate the short/bridge and repair.\n\n-Work with customer to contact the alarms monitoring vendor and have the Fire Panel placed into test mode.\n\n-Locate/tag Elevator, Fire and Burglar lines.\n\n-Cross-connect to Fire Panel, Burglar Panel, and test.\n\n-Contact the fire monitoring vendor to confirm that they are receiving the faults, restoral, low battery and battery restore signals.\n\n-Confirm monitoring vendor sees the correct service address.\n\n.\n\nPlease review the following requirements and protocols for your upcoming assignment with Lit Networking:\n\nTo ensure the successful completion of this site visit, you must arrive with the following tools and materials: - A fully charged laptop with an Ethernet port and a cellphone with a hotspot device. - Cabling tools: Multimeter wire tester, butt set, punch down tool, crimpers, and wire cutters. - Hardware: RJ11 and RJ45 connectors, biscuit jacks, and 100 feet of Cat 5e/6 cable for potential device relocation. - Standard mounting kit: Drill, level, hammer, screwdrivers, screws, and anchors. - General supplies: Adjustable or open-end wrenches, a 4–6 ft ladder, and a 100 ft extension cord.\n\nWork Order and Payment Procedures All work orders must be signed by the onsite Point of Contact and must clearly list your arrival and departure times. Please upload the signed Lit Networking work order directly to Field Nation. Please be advised that any forged signatures will be reported to Field Nation and will result in non-payment. Adhering to these documentation requirements is essential to avoid any delays in your payment processing. If you encounter any issues while onsite, please leave a detailed message through the Field Nation platform.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-11T10:00","end":"2026-09-11T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":120,"max":170},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":120},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":8},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 9/11/2026, 10:00:00 AM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-11T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-11T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-12T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-12T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-15T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-11T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-12T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-09-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-12T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-09-18T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"},{"start":"2026-09-11T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-11T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"SMALL BACKBOARD/ DATA REMOTE INSTALL/ MUST HAVE BUTT-SET/MULTIMETER-DIS148477"},{"start":"2026-09-10T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-10T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Maintenance Kit Swap - Apex, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-04T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-05T13:30:00.000Z","summary":"DSS 9223 - Install (1) QNAP + UPS + Switch, Install (3) TP-Link Wireless Bridge, Install (3) 8 Port PoE Switch, Replace (15) Analog Cameras w/ (15) IP Cameras + Cable Runs - Lead Tech"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789161462343}
{"job":{"id":19938000,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Connext","title":"BAT| FortiGate, rXg, PMS & Onity Network Discovery and Connectivity Validation| Work with Remote Engineer","description":{"html":"<p><strong>PLEASE ADD YOUR NAME ON THE BADGE UNDER DOCUMENTS AND PRINT OUT FOR USE ON SITE. PLEASE PUT IN A CLEAR BADGE HOLDER AND ON A LANYARD IF POSSIBLE.</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>IF YOU DO NOT READ THIS WORK ORDER IN ITS ENTIRETY, YOU WILL NOT BE PREPARED FOR THIS JOB AND WILL NOT BE PAID IF THE JOB IS NOT COMPLETED.</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>PLEASE NOTE -</u></strong> <strong><u>IF YOU ARE TAKING A LUNCH BREAK</u>,</strong> YOU MUST SIGN IN AND OUT OF THIS WORK ORDER. <strong>YOU MUST SIGN OUT OF THE TEAMS BRIDGE WHEN YOU ARE LEAVING AND SIGN BACK INTO THE TEAMS BRIDGE WHEN YOU RETURN</strong>. THESE BRIDGELINES ARE RECORDED AND THE CUSTOMER KEEPS TRACK OF EXTENDED AWAY TIMES UNLESS THEY KNOW WHAT YOU ARE WORKING ON. <strong>THESE TIMES WILL BE COMPARED AGAINST THE TEAM BRIDGELINE CHAT, SO BE ACCURATE.</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>﻿<u>Must Have Windows OS or Mac OS based laptop</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Your check-in and check-out numbers</strong> are located under the confidential section of this work order.</p>\n<p><strong>Travel expenses</strong>must be pre-approved prior to scheduling and must be requested as an expense when you apply.&nbsp;Tolls &amp; Parking will be reimbursed with a receipt.</p>\n<p><strong>Reminder:</strong> If the dispatch will take longer than the allotted time to complete or there are any Out-of-Scope issues that arise, <strong>YOU MUST</strong>call the Connext escalation line (located under Confidential Information section) to notify Connext. Any extra time on site needs pre-approval by the PM and you will need good notes when you close out your work order to justify the additional time.</p>\n<p><strong><u>Important Instructions:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><del>** *** ***** ** ****** **** *** *** **** ***** *******</del></strong></li>\n<li><strong>Technicians must identify themselves as representatives of</strong> <del>****************</del><u>&nbsp;u</u>pon arrival and provide the GM passcode/security passcode. This ensures the GM/POC recognizes that the technician is a legitimate participant in the project and authorized to access the property and networking rooms.</li>\n<li><strong>PASSCODE TO BE ALLOWED TO WORK</strong>:<strong><del>** *** *** ****</del></strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Please have the following password recovery tool downloaded before you get to the site.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>https://www.hirensbootcd.org/files/HBCD_PE_x64.iso</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>SCOPE OF WORK</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Please make sure to we have your correct email address for the bridge-line you may have with the engineer.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>AS SOON AS YOU GET ON THE SITE, EVEN BEFORE REACHING OUT TO THE GM OR POC, PLEASE LOG INTO THE BRIDGE-LINE, IF YOU HAVE BEEN SENT ONE, AND LET THE ENGINEER KNOW THAT YOU ARE ONSITE. THIS IS MANDATORY.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>IF THERE IS NO BRIDGE-LINE, CALL THE ENGINEER BELOW.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>You will work directly with Customer's Engineer</strong>. Your engineer is *<strong><del>******* ******** ************</del></strong></li>\n<li><strong>YOU WILL HAVE TO GET A RELEASE CODE FROM THE ENGINEER WHEN YOU ARE CHECKING OUT OF THE SITE.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Perform an on-site network discovery and connectivity validation to identify the physical and logical network topology supporting the FortiGate, rXg, core/access switches, PMS, Onity/key-system equipment, and related Aimbridge and guest networks. Document the existing configuration, identify DHCP responsibilities, and verify Layer 2/Layer 3 connectivity between systems.</p>\nScope of Work\n<p>During dispatch, the technician will:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Locate and identify the FortiGate, rXg, core/access switches, FD/Key Server, Onity/PMS-related network equipment, and associated network infrastructure.</li>\n<li>Identify and document the physical network connections between the above devices.</li>\n<li>Trace the FortiGate port1 connection and determine where the 192.168.220.0/24 network is being switched.</li>\n<li>Locate and document the physical network connection and interface associated with the rXg (192.168.220.9).</li>\n<li>Document applicable switch names, manufacturers/models, port numbers, VLAN assignments, tagged/untagged configurations, and uplinks relevant to the systems being investigated.</li>\n<li>Determine which network/VLAN is intended for Aimbridge devices and which network/VLAN is intended for guest traffic.</li>\n<li>Determine whether the rXg is functioning as the guest-network gateway/DHCP platform and document how it connects to the FortiGate.</li>\n<li>Investigate why both the FortiGate and rXg appear to be providing DHCP services associated with 192.168.220.0/24.</li>\n<li>Document the intended DHCP authority, scope, gateway, and network design for the 192.168.220.0/24 network.</li>\n<li>Trace the network connection for AS-HP-35 and the Onity/key-system equipment, including associated switch and port information.</li>\n<li>Record, where available, the following information for relevant devices:</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">IP address</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Subnet mask</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Default gateway</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">DNS servers</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">VLAN ID/name</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Switch name/model</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Switch port</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Physical/uplink connection</li>\n<li>Verify Layer 2 and Layer 3 connectivity between the systems involved in PMS/Onity communication.</li>\n<li>Identify any apparent VLAN, switching, DHCP, cabling, or connectivity discrepancies discovered during the investigation.</li>\n<li>Photograph and document relevant equipment, rack layouts, cabling, labels, switch ports, and unidentified connections as needed.</li>\n<li>Provide documented findings and identify any configuration or connectivity issues requiring further remediation.</li>\n</ul>\nEquipment Needed — Technician (TReX)\n<ul>\n<li>Network cables</li>\n<li>Patch cables</li>\n<li>Rollover cable</li>\n<li>Cable toner</li>\n<li>Monitor</li>\n<li>VGA cable</li>\n<li>HDMI cable</li>\n<li>Laptop</li>\n<li>USB-to-Serial/console adapter with appropriate console drivers</li>\n<li>Ethernet/USB Ethernet adapter</li>\n<li>Basic network cable tester</li>\n<li>Label maker/tape and marker for documenting unidentified connections</li>\n<li>Phone/camera for clear photos of equipment, cabling, port assignments, labels, and rack layout</li>\n<li>Power extension cord/charger as needed for technician equipment</li>\n</ul>\nDeliverables\n<p>At completion of the dispatch, provide:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Physical network connection/topology documentation</li>\n<li>Relevant switch and port assignments</li>\n<li>VLAN and tagged/untagged configuration findings</li>\n<li>192.168.220.0/24 network path and DHCP findings</li>\n<li>FortiGate-to-rXg connectivity details</li>\n<li>AS-HP-35 and Onity/key-system connection details</li>\n<li>IP addressing information for relevant systems</li>\n<li>PMS/Onity Layer 2/Layer 3 connectivity findings</li>\n<li>Photos of relevant equipment, cabling, and rack/port assignments</li>\n<li>Identification of any discrepancies or issues requiring follow-up remediation</li>\n<li><br /></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Required Deliverables</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Take pictures of your work area before and after you complete your work.</li>\n<li>Deliverables must be submitted in real-time, while onsite. Do not leave the site until Connext has approved your deliverables.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>MUST DO FOR PAYMENT</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>You must get a signoff from the General Manager or the Customer Site Contact each day you are on site. Have either GM or the Assistant GM verify and confirm your work, and get a signature of completion before submitting for payment.</strong>&nbsp;<strong>You need a legible FIRST and LAST name printed/typed</strong>, a signature, and the date/time needs to be the same date as your work date.&nbsp;<strong>FN already pushes the date and time, so don't forget to get a signoff. This is mandatory for all work orders.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Please note that if you are taking a lunch break, you must sign in and out of this work order. You must drop in the Teams bridge when you are leaving and then again when you are back. These will be compared against the Teams bridge, so be accurate. We can't invoice our Customer for a lunch break.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Reminder:</strong>&nbsp;If the dispatch will take longer than the allotted time to complete or there are any Out-of-Scope issues that arise,&nbsp;<strong>YOU MUST</strong>&nbsp;call the Connext escalation line (<strong>located under Confidential Information section</strong>) to notify Connext. Any extra time on site needs pre-approval by the PM and you will need good notes when you close out your work order to justify the additional time.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>MANDATORY TOOLS</u></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>8+ Port Managed Switch</strong></li>\n<li><strong>VARIOUS TYPE OF CONSOLE CABLES (RJ45, USB, C-PORT, ETC.)</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Network cable toner and probe kit</strong></li>\n<li><strong>USB to RJ45</strong></li>\n<li><strong>USB Cables</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Serial Cables</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Crossover cables</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Windows OS or Mac OS based laptop.</strong>Laptop/tablet that can take photos and has internet access (required as the survey is completed using a weblink)</li>\n<li>Laptop/tablet power cable/charger</li>\n<li>Mobile phone with camera</li>\n<li>Mobile phone charger</li>\n<li>Cat5e and Cat6 PVC UTP cable</li>\n<li>Cat5e and Cat6 modular tips and keystone jacks</li>\n<li>Cable crimper</li>\n<li>Cable supports (zip ties, Velcro straps, etc.)</li>\n<li>Surface mount boxes and flush mount plates</li>\n<li>6’ ladder</li>\n<li>Cordless Drill</li>\n<li>Voltmeter</li>\n<li>Electric Stud Finder</li>\n</ol>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Requirements/Expectations</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>This work order has all the necessary information to complete the scope. If anything is unclear, please reach out to Tech Support Number listed under Confidential Information.&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></li>\n<li>For this assignment, you will be representing CONNEXT. Please follow our standard procedures on site and be fully prepared to complete the scope.</li>\n<li>As a technician, maintain a professional and courteous attitude while working. Once onsite, greet the customer and let them know who you are working with and show them your ID and/or Work Order.</li>\n<li><strong>Be professional even under stressful situations.</strong></li>\n<li>Communicate often with the customer and Helpdesk as your work proceeds.</li>\n<li><strong>Dress Code</strong> - <strong>Long pants (jeans, khakis or work pants), collared shirt (button up or polo), closed toed shoes. No t-shirts, shorts, sandals, graphic, or offensive clothing of any kind.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Times and MOD signed Work Orders</strong> <strong>are used for payment NOT worker platform times.</strong></li>\n<li>I<strong>F APPLICABLE, RETURN DEFECTIVE EQUIPMENT USING RETURN LABEL IN BOX THAT IS STAPLED TO THE PACKING SLIP.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Reimbursement Rates</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Cat5e PVC $0.16 ft</li>\n<li>Cat5 Plenum $0.25 ft</li>\n<li>Cat6 PVC $0.25 ft</li>\n<li>Cat6 Plenum $0.46 ft</li>\n<li>Biscuit Jack $5.00</li>\n<li>Surface Mount Box $5.31</li>\n<li>Face Plate $3.00</li>\n<li>RJ45 jack Cat 6 $9.98</li>\n<li>RJ48 jack $5.00</li>\n<li>66 Block $15.72</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**PLEASE ADD YOUR NAME ON THE BADGE UNDER DOCUMENTS AND PRINT OUT FOR USE ON SITE. PLEASE PUT IN A CLEAR BADGE HOLDER AND ON A LANYARD IF POSSIBLE.**\n\n**IF YOU DO NOT READ THIS WORK ORDER IN ITS ENTIRETY, YOU WILL NOT BE PREPARED FOR THIS JOB AND WILL NOT BE PAID IF THE JOB IS NOT COMPLETED.**\n\n**PLEASE NOTE -** **IF YOU ARE TAKING A LUNCH BREAK,** YOU MUST SIGN IN AND OUT OF THIS WORK ORDER. **YOU MUST SIGN OUT OF THE TEAMS BRIDGE WHEN YOU ARE LEAVING AND SIGN BACK INTO THE TEAMS BRIDGE WHEN YOU RETURN**. THESE BRIDGELINES ARE RECORDED AND THE CUSTOMER KEEPS TRACK OF EXTENDED AWAY TIMES UNLESS THEY KNOW WHAT YOU ARE WORKING ON. **THESE TIMES WILL BE COMPARED AGAINST THE TEAM BRIDGELINE CHAT, SO BE ACCURATE.**\n\n**﻿Must Have Windows OS or Mac OS based laptop**\n\n**Your check-in and check-out numbers** are located under the confidential section of this work order.\n\n**Travel expenses**must be pre-approved prior to scheduling and must be requested as an expense when you apply. Tolls & Parking will be reimbursed with a receipt.\n\n**Reminder:** If the dispatch will take longer than the allotted time to complete or there are any Out-of-Scope issues that arise, **YOU MUST**call the Connext escalation line (located under Confidential Information section) to notify Connext. Any extra time on site needs pre-approval by the PM and you will need good notes when you close out your work order to justify the additional time.\n\n**Important Instructions:**\n\n- **\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n- **Technicians must identify themselves as representatives of** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* upon arrival and provide the GM passcode/security passcode. This ensures the GM/POC recognizes that the technician is a legitimate participant in the project and authorized to access the property and networking rooms.\n- **PASSCODE TO BE ALLOWED TO WORK**:**\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**Please have the following password recovery tool downloaded before you get to the site.**\n\n- https://www.hirensbootcd.org/files/HBCD_PE_x64.iso\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK**\n\n**Please make sure to we have your correct email address for the bridge-line you may have with the engineer.**\n\n**AS SOON AS YOU GET ON THE SITE, EVEN BEFORE REACHING OUT TO THE GM OR POC, PLEASE LOG INTO THE BRIDGE-LINE, IF YOU HAVE BEEN SENT ONE, AND LET THE ENGINEER KNOW THAT YOU ARE ONSITE. THIS IS MANDATORY.**\n\n**IF THERE IS NO BRIDGE-LINE, CALL THE ENGINEER BELOW.**\n\n- **You will work directly with Customer's Engineer**. Your engineer is \\***\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n- **YOU WILL HAVE TO GET A RELEASE CODE FROM THE ENGINEER WHEN YOU ARE CHECKING OUT OF THE SITE.**\n\nPerform an on-site network discovery and connectivity validation to identify the physical and logical network topology supporting the FortiGate, rXg, core/access switches, PMS, Onity/key-system equipment, and related Aimbridge and guest networks. Document the existing configuration, identify DHCP responsibilities, and verify Layer 2/Layer 3 connectivity between systems.\n\nScope of Work During dispatch, the technician will:\n\n- Locate and identify the FortiGate, rXg, core/access switches, FD/Key Server, Onity/PMS-related network equipment, and associated network infrastructure.\n- Identify and document the physical network connections between the above devices.\n- Trace the FortiGate port1 connection and determine where the 192.168.220.0/24 network is being switched.\n- Locate and document the physical network connection and interface associated with the rXg (192.168.220.9).\n- Document applicable switch names, manufacturers/models, port numbers, VLAN assignments, tagged/untagged configurations, and uplinks relevant to the systems being investigated.\n- Determine which network/VLAN is intended for Aimbridge devices and which network/VLAN is intended for guest traffic.\n- Determine whether the rXg is functioning as the guest-network gateway/DHCP platform and document how it connects to the FortiGate.\n- Investigate why both the FortiGate and rXg appear to be providing DHCP services associated with 192.168.220.0/24.\n- Document the intended DHCP authority, scope, gateway, and network design for the 192.168.220.0/24 network.\n- Trace the network connection for AS-HP-35 and the Onity/key-system equipment, including associated switch and port information.\n- Record, where available, the following information for relevant devices:\n- IP address\n- Subnet mask\n- Default gateway\n- DNS servers\n- VLAN ID/name\n- Switch name/model\n- Switch port\n- Physical/uplink connection\n- Verify Layer 2 and Layer 3 connectivity between the systems involved in PMS/Onity communication.\n- Identify any apparent VLAN, switching, DHCP, cabling, or connectivity discrepancies discovered during the investigation.\n- Photograph and document relevant equipment, rack layouts, cabling, labels, switch ports, and unidentified connections as needed.\n- Provide documented findings and identify any configuration or connectivity issues requiring further remediation.\n\nEquipment Needed — Technician (TReX) - Network cables\n- Patch cables\n- Rollover cable\n- Cable toner\n- Monitor\n- VGA cable\n- HDMI cable\n- Laptop\n- USB-to-Serial/console adapter with appropriate console drivers\n- Ethernet/USB Ethernet adapter\n- Basic network cable tester\n- Label maker/tape and marker for documenting unidentified connections\n- Phone/camera for clear photos of equipment, cabling, port assignments, labels, and rack layout\n- Power extension cord/charger as needed for technician equipment\n\nDeliverables At completion of the dispatch, provide:\n\n- Physical network connection/topology documentation\n- Relevant switch and port assignments\n- VLAN and tagged/untagged configuration findings\n- 192.168.220.0/24 network path and DHCP findings\n- FortiGate-to-rXg connectivity details\n- AS-HP-35 and Onity/key-system connection details\n- IP addressing information for relevant systems\n- PMS/Onity Layer 2/Layer 3 connectivity findings\n- Photos of relevant equipment, cabling, and rack/port assignments\n- Identification of any discrepancies or issues requiring follow-up remediation\n- \n\n**Required Deliverables**\n\n- Take pictures of your work area before and after you complete your work.\n- Deliverables must be submitted in real-time, while onsite. Do not leave the site until Connext has approved your deliverables.\n\n**MUST DO FOR PAYMENT**\n\n- **You must get a signoff from the General Manager or the Customer Site Contact each day you are on site. Have either GM or the Assistant GM verify and confirm your work, and get a signature of completion before submitting for payment.** **You need a legible FIRST and LAST name printed/typed**, a signature, and the date/time needs to be the same date as your work date. **FN already pushes the date and time, so don't forget to get a signoff. This is mandatory for all work orders.**\n- **Please note that if you are taking a lunch break, you must sign in and out of this work order. You must drop in the Teams bridge when you are leaving and then again when you are back. These will be compared against the Teams bridge, so be accurate. We can't invoice our Customer for a lunch break.**\n- **Reminder:** If the dispatch will take longer than the allotted time to complete or there are any Out-of-Scope issues that arise, **YOU MUST** call the Connext escalation line (**located under Confidential Information section**) to notify Connext. Any extra time on site needs pre-approval by the PM and you will need good notes when you close out your work order to justify the additional time.\n\n**MANDATORY TOOLS**\n\n1. **8+ Port Managed Switch**\n2. **VARIOUS TYPE OF CONSOLE CABLES (RJ45, USB, C-PORT, ETC.)**\n3. **Network cable toner and probe kit**\n4. **USB to RJ45**\n5. **USB Cables**\n6. **Serial Cables**\n7. **Crossover cables**\n8. **Windows OS or Mac OS based laptop.**Laptop/tablet that can take photos and has internet access (required as the survey is completed using a weblink)\n9. Laptop/tablet power cable/charger\n10. Mobile phone with camera\n11. Mobile phone charger\n12. Cat5e and Cat6 PVC UTP cable\n13. Cat5e and Cat6 modular tips and keystone jacks\n14. Cable crimper\n15. Cable supports (zip ties, Velcro straps, etc.)\n16. Surface mount boxes and flush mount plates\n17. 6’ ladder\n18. Cordless Drill\n19. Voltmeter\n20. Electric Stud Finder\n\n**Requirements/Expectations**\n\n- **This work order has all the necessary information to complete the scope. If anything is unclear, please reach out to Tech Support Number listed under Confidential Information.**\n- For this assignment, you will be representing CONNEXT. Please follow our standard procedures on site and be fully prepared to complete the scope.\n- As a technician, maintain a professional and courteous attitude while working. Once onsite, greet the customer and let them know who you are working with and show them your ID and/or Work Order.\n- **Be professional even under stressful situations.**\n- Communicate often with the customer and Helpdesk as your work proceeds.\n- **Dress Code** - **Long pants (jeans, khakis or work pants), collared shirt (button up or polo), closed toed shoes. No t-shirts, shorts, sandals, graphic, or offensive clothing of any kind.**\n- **Times and MOD signed Work Orders** **are used for payment NOT worker platform times.**\n- I**F APPLICABLE, RETURN DEFECTIVE EQUIPMENT USING RETURN LABEL IN BOX THAT IS STAPLED TO THE PACKING SLIP.**\n\n**Reimbursement Rates**\n\n- Cat5e PVC $0.16 ft\n- Cat5 Plenum $0.25 ft\n- Cat6 PVC $0.25 ft\n- Cat6 Plenum $0.46 ft\n- Biscuit Jack $5.00\n- Surface Mount Box $5.31\n- Face Plate $3.00\n- RJ45 jack Cat 6 $9.98\n- RJ48 jack $5.00\n- 66 Block $15.72","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-16T09:00","end":"2026-09-16T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":300},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":6,"distance":56},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":60,"baseAmount":360,"estHours":6,"travelExpense":85,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T18:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":60,"mode":"hours","reason":"arrival_window"}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-16T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-17T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-18T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"},{"start":"2026-09-11T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-11T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"SMALL BACKBOARD/ DATA REMOTE INSTALL/ MUST HAVE BUTT-SET/MULTIMETER-DIS148477"},{"start":"2026-09-10T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-10T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Maintenance Kit Swap - Apex, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-04T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-05T13:30:00.000Z","summary":"DSS 9223 - Install (1) QNAP + UPS + Switch, Install (3) TP-Link Wireless Bridge, Install (3) 8 Port PoE Switch, Replace (15) Analog Cameras w/ (15) IP Cameras + Cable Runs - Lead Tech"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1789161468841}
{"job":{"id":19937739,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Essintial","title":"FIRM START | Access Point installation","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Important:</strong> Technicians MUST read the entire work order and all provided documentation before arriving on-site. All guides and plans must be printed and/or available on a laptop or tablet (not a phone) for review onsite.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>REQUIRED SKILLS:</u></strong> Mid-level to advanced-level network tech. Must be able to run cable neatly through various ceiling types, terminate cables with RJ45 plugs and or Keystone jacks. Must be able to Operate a Lift.</p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>OVERVIEW:</u></strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li><strong><u>Scope Of Work</u></strong>: Technician needed onsite to <strong>install X new customer provided APs</strong> (pictures provided in attachments), run cable as necessary, and provide additional troubleshooting. While onsite and after completing the install and cable run, tech MUST complete capture various photos and complete the Essintial Online Deliverable Survey using the provided link. Once all tasks are completed, the technician will contact the<strong>Essintial Technical Support @ 717-516-3009</strong> to validate that the data capture is completed, review the completed online deliverable and obtain approval prior to leaving the site.</li><li><strong>CHECK IN with Onsite POC / Manager and Call TA Contact (440-808-9110 ext 0)</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>TA will provide support and patching information</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Post install validation</strong></li><li>Technicians will need to complete multiple wifi surveys onsite - one in the Service Bay(s) and one in the Service Plaza</li><li><strong>Estimated Duration: 2 hrs per cable run</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tech <strong>MUST</strong> report <strong>ANY/ALL DELAYS</strong> (whether you exceeded the Estimated Hours or not): You <strong>MUST</strong> report why and who/what caused the delay(s) and for how long.</li><li><strong><u>You MUST represent yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of Travel Centers while onsite</u></strong></li><li><strong>Techs will install or move APs and run cable based on provided floor plans</strong></li><li><strong>Techs will be REQUIRED</strong> to capture various photos of each AP</li><li>Tech is <strong>REQUIRED</strong> to complete an Online Deliverable Survey PRIOR to leaving the site &ndash; link provided in your work order</li><li>Tech <strong>MUST</strong> contact the <strong>Essintial Technical Support @ 717-516-3009</strong> to validate that the data captured is completed, review the completed online deliverable and obtain approval prior to leaving the site.</li><li>Tech is required to follow instructions and work with <strong>Essintial Technical Support @ 717-516-3009</strong> during the process / while onsite / escalations</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>IMPORTANT Requirements &amp; Call Outs:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong><u>You MUST represent yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of Travel Centers</u></strong></li><li><strong>Dress Code: Professional work dress code</strong> is mandatory: Technicians should present a clean, professional appearance. A plain polo / collared / or button-down shirt, slacks / durable work pants (no shorts), and nice shoes / steel- or composite-toe slip-resistant shoes or boots. <strong>Not allowed</strong>: T‑shirts, hoodies, graphics, holes, or stained clothing.</li><li><strong>These are live environments, and technician must act in a professional manner, taking care not to disrupt business.</strong> <strong>Be Respectful</strong> and limit any disruptions while on site.</li><li><strong>This WO only covers ONE visit to site. If a customer requires a return visit, you MUST be assigned another WO by Essintial. Time logged for additional days onsite will be rejected for not following process.&nbsp;</strong></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Site Badging / Onsite Access Information:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Government Issued ID</li><li>Essintial Badge</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Required Tools / Material:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Basic / Standard Hand Tools</li><li>Cell Phone or other device that has phone, camera, and internet ability (for online deliverable)</li><li>Punch down tools</li><li>Cable testers</li><li>Cable strippers</li><li>RJ45 crimpers</li><li>Tone and probe kit</li><li>Cordless drill</li><li>Masonry Bits</li><li>Tapcons</li><li>Fish tape/rods</li><li>Cable ties</li><li>Labels/Label Maker</li><li>Headlamp / Flashlight</li><li>Ladder &ndash; 10 FT</li><li>PPE (safety glasses, gloves)</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Pre-Site Requirements:</strong></p><ul><li><strong><u>Download and then Print</u> all relevant attachments (guides and checklists) in color to bring to the site.</strong>Please review all attachments prior to arriving onsite.<strong><em><u>Important Note:</u></em></strong> These Links will take you to / show you a<strong><u>PREVIEW</u></strong> of the document, <strong><em>IT IS VERY IMPORTANT</em></strong> that you<strong><em>DOWNLOAD</em></strong> the files from this view and then <strong>PRINT</strong> (<em>DO NOT PRINT FROM PREVIEW MODE</em>)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Essintial Badge Template</strong>: <a href=\"https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004o0CD/e1LDRzExSIcVt31Ck.33xXfswccpVccuJRYzTs0Tt6M\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004o0CD/e1LDRzExSIcVt31Ck.33xXfswccpVccuJRYzTs0Tt6M</a></li><li>Confirm the start date and time. You will receive pre-calls at 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will not be granted.</li><li>Bring the Required Tools &amp; Material with you to the site</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>ARRIVAL:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>CHECK IN TO YOUR WORK ORDER</strong>&ndash;if you are unable to do so then you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.</li><li><strong>CHECK IN with Onsite POC / Manager and Call TA Contact (440-808-9110 ext 0)-</strong> Introduce yourself to the site contact immediately. Collaborate on an installation plan that ensures minimal disruption to ongoing operations.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>ONSITE:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>Refer to the provided onsite technical documents for onsite actions needing completed</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Technicians may be required to install a new APs and run cable</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Technicians may be required to relocate an existing AP to maximize coverage</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Technicains may be required to perform other trouble shooting as identified during the previous survey.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Capture Required Photos</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Any issues or questions please reach out to the Essintial Technical Support Team @ 717-516-3009</strong></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>CLOSING OUT | COMPLETE BEFORE LEAVING SITE:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>Complete and Submit Online Deliverable</strong>(Due back to Essintial PRIOR TO LEAVING SITE):</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tech will be asked to confirm site/location details</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tech will be asked to upload requested photos</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">You will be asked to enter closing/completion notes</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">You will be asked to obtain Manager/POC Signature</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tech will be asked to provide the confirmation code received upon completion of your online deliverables.</li><li><strong>CHECK OUT with TA Contact (440-808-9110 ext 6)</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>TA will provide support and patching information</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Post install validation</strong></li><li><strong>Call and Check Out with Essintial Technical Support @ 717-516-3009 to perform your final check out - You MUST review your deliverables BEFORE you LEAVE SITE and have them approved by Project Tech Support</strong></li><li><strong>Check-Out on your WO</strong> - if you are unable to do so then you <strong>MUST </strong>call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in. <strong>NOTE</strong>: Your Check In and Check Out times must all match <em>(Work Order Platform and Final Check Out with Essintial)</em></li><li><strong>NOTE</strong>: Your Check In and Check Out times must all match (Work Order Platform, and Final Check Out with Essintial.</li><li><strong>If this is your only site / last site to complete a survey</strong> &ndash; please drop equipment off at local FedEx using the provided Return Shipping Label (check your work order attachments for label) - Any questions please escalate to the<strong>Essintial Technical Support @ 717-516-3009</strong></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Closing / Completion Notes:</strong></p><ul><li>Did you complete the online deliverable? If so, please provide confirmation code</li><li>Detailed Description of the Work that took Place, including any issues.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>ESCALATION:</u>&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>Support Related Questions / Onsite Issues / Issues Related to your scope of work should be escalated directly to the Essintial Project Tech Support @ 717-516-3009&nbsp;&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><u>PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS:</u></strong> Must be able to bend, kneel, stand and lift, carry 50lbs repeatedly for extended periods of time.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:</u></strong></p><ul><li>All expenses such as tolls, parking, materials must be pre-approved and accompanied by a receipt. Reimbursements will not be increased to cover markups of any kind.</li><li>Technicians must contact Essintial for any deviations from the scheduled service date or time. No payment will be granted for work performed prior to the scheduled start time.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>SCHEDULE:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>Start Times:</strong> Varies</li><li><strong>Estimated Duration:</strong> approx 2 hours per cable run</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tech <strong>MUST</strong> report <strong>ANY/ALL DELAYS</strong> (whether you exceeded the Estimated Hours or not): You <strong>MUST</strong> report why and who/what caused the delay(s) and for how long.</li><li>You will receive pre-calls 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will not be granted.</li><li>You will not be paid for work performed prior to your work order's scheduled start time. Please contact Essintial if the customer is asking you to deviate from this service date or time.</li><li>If you must remove yourself from this project, you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to be <strong>REMOVED </strong>and <strong><em>REMOVE YOURSELF </em></strong>from the work order.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Attachments - All guides/plans MUST be available either printed or on a laptop/tablet, something other than your mobile device as you will be on the phone a lot and will need to refer to your document at the same time:</strong></p>","markdown":"**Important:** Technicians MUST read the entire work order and all provided documentation before arriving on-site. All guides and plans must be printed and/or available on a laptop or tablet (not a phone) for review onsite.\n\n**REQUIRED SKILLS:** Mid-level to advanced-level network tech. Must be able to run cable neatly through various ceiling types, terminate cables with RJ45 plugs and or Keystone jacks. Must be able to Operate a Lift.\n\n**OVERVIEW:**\n\n- **Scope Of Work**: Technician needed onsite to **install X new customer provided APs** (pictures provided in attachments), run cable as necessary, and provide additional troubleshooting. While onsite and after completing the install and cable run, tech MUST complete capture various photos and complete the Essintial Online Deliverable Survey using the provided link. Once all tasks are completed, the technician will contact the**Essintial Technical Support @ 717-516-3009** to validate that the data capture is completed, review the completed online deliverable and obtain approval prior to leaving the site.\n- **CHECK IN with Onsite POC / Manager and Call TA Contact (440-808-9110 ext 0)**\n- **TA will provide support and patching information**\n- **Post install validation**\n- Technicians will need to complete multiple wifi surveys onsite - one in the Service Bay(s) and one in the Service Plaza\n- **Estimated Duration: 2 hrs per cable run**\n- Tech **MUST** report **ANY/ALL DELAYS** (whether you exceeded the Estimated Hours or not): You **MUST** report why and who/what caused the delay(s) and for how long.\n- **You MUST represent yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of Travel Centers while onsite**\n- **Techs will install or move APs and run cable based on provided floor plans**\n- **Techs will be REQUIRED** to capture various photos of each AP\n- Tech is **REQUIRED** to complete an Online Deliverable Survey PRIOR to leaving the site – link provided in your work order\n- Tech **MUST** contact the **Essintial Technical Support @ 717-516-3009** to validate that the data captured is completed, review the completed online deliverable and obtain approval prior to leaving the site.\n- Tech is required to follow instructions and work with **Essintial Technical Support @ 717-516-3009** during the process / while onsite / escalations\n\n**IMPORTANT Requirements & Call Outs:**\n\n- **You MUST represent yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of Travel Centers**\n- **Dress Code: Professional work dress code** is mandatory: Technicians should present a clean, professional appearance. A plain polo / collared / or button-down shirt, slacks / durable work pants (no shorts), and nice shoes / steel- or composite-toe slip-resistant shoes or boots. **Not allowed**: T‑shirts, hoodies, graphics, holes, or stained clothing.\n- **These are live environments, and technician must act in a professional manner, taking care not to disrupt business.** **Be Respectful** and limit any disruptions while on site.\n- **This WO only covers ONE visit to site. If a customer requires a return visit, you MUST be assigned another WO by Essintial. Time logged for additional days onsite will be rejected for not following process.**\n\n**Site Badging / Onsite Access Information:**\n\n- Government Issued ID\n- Essintial Badge\n\n**Required Tools / Material:**\n\n- Basic / Standard Hand Tools\n- Cell Phone or other device that has phone, camera, and internet ability (for online deliverable)\n- Punch down tools\n- Cable testers\n- Cable strippers\n- RJ45 crimpers\n- Tone and probe kit\n- Cordless drill\n- Masonry Bits\n- Tapcons\n- Fish tape/rods\n- Cable ties\n- Labels/Label Maker\n- Headlamp / Flashlight\n- Ladder – 10 FT\n- PPE (safety glasses, gloves)\n\n**Pre-Site Requirements:**\n\n- **Download and then Print all relevant attachments (guides and checklists) in color to bring to the site.**Please review all attachments prior to arriving onsite.***Important Note:*** These Links will take you to / show you a**PREVIEW** of the document, ***IT IS VERY IMPORTANT*** that you***DOWNLOAD*** the files from this view and then **PRINT** (*DO NOT PRINT FROM PREVIEW MODE*)\n- **Essintial Badge Template**: [](https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004o0CD/e1LDRzExSIcVt31Ck.33xXfswccpVccuJRYzTs0Tt6M)<https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004o0CD/e1LDRzExSIcVt31Ck.33xXfswccpVccuJRYzTs0Tt6M>\n- Confirm the start date and time. You will receive pre-calls at 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will not be granted.\n- Bring the Required Tools & Material with you to the site\n\n**ARRIVAL:**\n\n- **CHECK IN TO YOUR WORK ORDER**–if you are unable to do so then you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.\n- **CHECK IN with Onsite POC / Manager and Call TA Contact (440-808-9110 ext 0)-** Introduce yourself to the site contact immediately. Collaborate on an installation plan that ensures minimal disruption to ongoing operations.\n\n**ONSITE:**\n\n- **Refer to the provided onsite technical documents for onsite actions needing completed**\n- **Technicians may be required to install a new APs and run cable**\n- **Technicians may be required to relocate an existing AP to maximize coverage**\n- **Technicains may be required to perform other trouble shooting as identified during the previous survey.**\n- **Capture Required Photos**\n- **Any issues or questions please reach out to the Essintial Technical Support Team @ 717-516-3009**\n\n**CLOSING OUT | COMPLETE BEFORE LEAVING SITE:**\n\n- **Complete and Submit Online Deliverable**(Due back to Essintial PRIOR TO LEAVING SITE):\n- Tech will be asked to confirm site/location details\n- Tech will be asked to upload requested photos\n- You will be asked to enter closing/completion notes\n- You will be asked to obtain Manager/POC Signature\n- Tech will be asked to provide the confirmation code received upon completion of your online deliverables.\n- **CHECK OUT with TA Contact (440-808-9110 ext 6)**\n- **TA will provide support and patching information**\n- **Post install validation**\n- **Call and Check Out with Essintial Technical Support @ 717-516-3009 to perform your final check out - You MUST review your deliverables BEFORE you LEAVE SITE and have them approved by Project Tech Support**\n- **Check-Out on your WO** - if you are unable to do so then you **MUST** call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in. **NOTE**: Your Check In and Check Out times must all match *(Work Order Platform and Final Check Out with Essintial)*\n- **NOTE**: Your Check In and Check Out times must all match (Work Order Platform, and Final Check Out with Essintial.\n- **If this is your only site / last site to complete a survey** – please drop equipment off at local FedEx using the provided Return Shipping Label (check your work order attachments for label) - Any questions please escalate to the**Essintial Technical Support @ 717-516-3009**\n\n**Closing / Completion Notes:**\n\n- Did you complete the online deliverable? If so, please provide confirmation code\n- Detailed Description of the Work that took Place, including any issues.\n\n**ESCALATION:**\n\n- Support Related Questions / Onsite Issues / Issues Related to your scope of work should be escalated directly to the Essintial Project Tech Support @ 717-516-3009\n\n**PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS:** Must be able to bend, kneel, stand and lift, carry 50lbs repeatedly for extended periods of time.\n\n**Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy:**\n\n- All expenses such as tolls, parking, materials must be pre-approved and accompanied by a receipt. Reimbursements will not be increased to cover markups of any kind.\n- Technicians must contact Essintial for any deviations from the scheduled service date or time. No payment will be granted for work performed prior to the scheduled start time.\n\n**SCHEDULE:**\n\n- **Start Times:** Varies\n- **Estimated Duration:** approx 2 hours per cable run\n- Tech **MUST** report **ANY/ALL DELAYS** (whether you exceeded the Estimated Hours or not): You **MUST** report why and who/what caused the delay(s) and for how long.\n- You will receive pre-calls 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will not be granted.\n- You will not be paid for work performed prior to your work order's scheduled start time. Please contact Essintial if the customer is asking you to deviate from this service date or time.\n- If you must remove yourself from this project, you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to be **REMOVED** and ***REMOVE YOURSELF*** from the work order.\n\n**Attachments - All guides/plans MUST be available either printed or on a laptop/tablet, something other than your mobile device as you will be on the phone a lot and will need to refer to your document at the same time:**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-22T08:45","end":"2026-09-22T12:45"},"payRange":{"min":40,"max":160},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":40,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":30},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $160 (countered: $240) is below minimum threshold $350"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-18T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-