{"job":{"id":"2307980903","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"MG21 Gateway SIM Swap & Connection Verification","description":"Hilton SIM Swap SOW<br><br>Required Materials:<br>Laptop w/ Admin Rights and Ethernet Port<br>RJ45-RJ45 Ethernet Cable<br><br>Required Deliverables:<br>NEW SIM Number<br>MG21 with visible Purple status light<br>MG21 before and after pictures<br><br>SIM Card UPS Tracking: TBD<br><br>Please review the SIM Installation section of the attached PDF prior to dispatch.<br><br>Technician must be able to access and actively use Microsoft Teams, including Teams chat, for communication, coordination, and support during the installation<br>Upon arrival, the Granite Technician checks in with the Front Desk and asks for the Granite package containing the SIM card<br>For any access issues, please reach out to the Granite PM Jonathon at (401) 955-9477<br><br>When you have the SIM and locate the MG21, please call into the below bridge to work with Granite technical support:<br><br>Dial-In: +1 929-229-2436<br>Passcode: 355013377#<br><br>General Directions:<br>Validate the existing MG21 Gateway is fully operational with the local manager<br>Power down the existing MG21 Gateway<br>Record the serial number for Hilton Worldwide records<br>Disconnect the MG from power<br>Remove the existing SIM by unscrewing the back panel<br>Insert the new SIM and replace the back plate<br>Power on the unit and confirm a solid purple LED indicating proper configuration, active SIM, and cellular connectivity<br>If status light remains Amber (Orange): utilize laptop, console cable, and mobile phone for any required Hilton Worldwide APN configuration (see steps below)<br>Verify the MG21 router is online and all network services are operational<br>Before leaving site, confirm system functionality with the technical coordinator on the Teams meeting<br>Record the store manager’s name as confirmation of successful SIM migration<br><br>How to Manually Change APN<br><br>Step 1 — Physically Connect to the MG<br>Power on the Meraki MG.<br>Connect your laptop directly to the MG LAN port using an Ethernet cable.<br>Wait about 1–2 minutes for your computer to receive an IP address automatically via DHCP.<br><br>Step 2 — Open the Local Status Page (may need to use an incognito browser window)<br>Open a web browser and go to: mg.meraki.com  <br>If that does not work, try:<br>• setup.meraki.com<br>• my.meraki.com<br>If that still does not work, try:<br>Open the Command Prompt and perform an IPCONFIG<br>Get the Gateway IP<br>Copy or Type the Gateway IP in the Web Browser tab<br>Click Enter<br><br>Step 3 — Log Into the MG<br>For newer firmware:<br>Username: admin<br>Password:  (please include the dashes)<br>The serial number is located on the sticker on the bottom or back of the MG.<br><br>Step 4 — Navigate to the Configure Page<br>Select the Configure tab.<br>Locate the Bearer Settings or Cellular Configuration section.<br><br>Step 5 — Override the SIM APN Settings<br>Find the option labeled Cellular Override or Override SIM Settings.<br>Enable Override SIM Settings to manually configure the APN.<br>Step 6 — Enter the APN<br>In the APN field, enter: wbdata<br><br>Step 6: Leave Username and Password blank unless your carrier specifically requires them.<br>Example:<br>APN: wbdata<br>Username: blank<br>Password: blank<br> <br>Step 7 — Confirm/update the next fields<br>Cellular authorization:  None<br>Cellular IP type:  IPv4v6<br> <br>Step 8 — Save the Configuration<br>Scroll to the bottom of the page.<br>Click Save.<br>The MG may briefly reconnect to the cellular network while applying the new APN.<br><br>Step 9 — Verify Connectivity<br>Go to the Connection or Cellular Status page and verify:<br>Carrier is detected<br>APN shows wbdata<br>Signal strength is present<br>Internet connectivity is connected<br>Meraki cloud connectivity is connected<br><br>Troubleshooting<br>Cannot Reach mg.meraki.com:<br>Disconnect and reconnect Ethernet<br>Use another browser<br>Try incognito browser<br>Confirm Wi-Fi is off<br>Browse directly to the MG gateway IP<br>Try setup.meraki.com<br><br>APN Does Not Save:<br>Ensure you clicked Save<br>Reboot the MG<br>Recheck the APN spelling: wbdata<br><br>No Cellular Connectivity:<br>Verify SIM card is active<br>Verify SIM is fully inserted<br>Confirm carrier supports the device<br>Confirm APN is correct<br>Verify signal strength is adequate<br><br>Optional — Factory Reset<br>Press and hold the Reset button for at least 10 seconds.<br>Allow 5–10 minutes for reboot and reconfiguration.<br>Factory reset clears Local Status Page settings including APN configuration.<br><br>Document and provide any returned equipment to the hotel MOD","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-21T10:45","end":"2026-09-21T12:15"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":75},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":1.5,"distance":12},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $75 (countered: $98) is below minimum threshold $350"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-18T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"},{"start":"2026-09-11T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-11T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"SMALL BACKBOARD/ DATA REMOTE INSTALL/ MUST HAVE BUTT-SET/MULTIMETER-DIS148477"},{"start":"2026-09-10T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-10T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Maintenance Kit Swap - Apex, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-04T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-05T13:30:00.000Z","summary":"DSS 9223 - Install (1) QNAP + UPS + Switch, Install (3) TP-Link Wireless Bridge, Install (3) 8 Port PoE Switch, Replace (15) Analog Cameras w/ (15) IP Cameras + Cable Runs - Lead Tech"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789161546751}
{"job":{"id":19936647,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Robotic Assistance Devices","title":"Technician Needed to Power Cycle a Solar Powered CCTV Trailer","description":{"html":"<p>The Solar Powered CCTV Trailer at this site is currently offline / not reporting to remote monitoring. Technician is needed on site to work with a remote RAD Support team member (by phone) to locate the trailer and perform a power cycle.</p><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><ol><li>On arrival, call RAD Support program manager. A RAD Support team member will stay on the line to help locate the Solar Powered CCTV Trailer and guide you through the power cycle.</li><li>Locate the Solar Powered CCTV Trailer on site (RAD Support can assist by phone if needed).</li><li>Open the trailer's electrical cabinet and turn the load power OFF.</li><li>Wait 60 seconds.</li><li>Turn the load power back ON.</li><li>Observe and note the indicator light behavior during boot-up.</li><li>Wait 15–30 minutes for the unit to fully boot and reconnect to the network.</li><li>Confirm with the RAD Support team member that the unit is back online and reporting correctly before leaving site. Do not close out the work order or leave site until RAD confirms the unit is back up.</li></ol><p><strong>If the unit does not come back online:</strong></p><ul><li>Stay on the line with RAD Support for further troubleshooting guidance.</li><li>Do not attempt disassembly, wiring changes, or configuration changes without direct instruction from RAD Support.</li></ul><p><strong>Deliverables (required before completing work order):</strong></p><ul><li>Photo of the cabinet/load switch before the power cycle</li><li>Photo of the unit powered on / indicator lights after the power cycle</li><li>Confirmation (verbal, from RAD Support on the call) that the unit is back online</li></ul><p><strong>Estimated time on site:</strong> 30–45 minutes, including the RAD Support call and boot wait time.</p>","markdown":"The Solar Powered CCTV Trailer at this site is currently offline / not reporting to remote monitoring. Technician is needed on site to work with a remote RAD Support team member (by phone) to locate the trailer and perform a power cycle.\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n1. On arrival, call RAD Support program manager. A RAD Support team member will stay on the line to help locate the Solar Powered CCTV Trailer and guide you through the power cycle.\n2. Locate the Solar Powered CCTV Trailer on site (RAD Support can assist by phone if needed).\n3. Open the trailer's electrical cabinet and turn the load power OFF.\n4. Wait 60 seconds.\n5. Turn the load power back ON.\n6. Observe and note the indicator light behavior during boot-up.\n7. Wait 15–30 minutes for the unit to fully boot and reconnect to the network.\n8. Confirm with the RAD Support team member that the unit is back online and reporting correctly before leaving site. Do not close out the work order or leave site until RAD confirms the unit is back up.\n\n**If the unit does not come back online:**\n\n- Stay on the line with RAD Support for further troubleshooting guidance.\n- Do not attempt disassembly, wiring changes, or configuration changes without direct instruction from RAD Support.\n\n**Deliverables (required before completing work order):**\n\n- Photo of the cabinet/load switch before the power cycle\n- Photo of the unit powered on / indicator lights after the power cycle\n- Confirmation (verbal, from RAD Support on the call) that the unit is back online\n\n**Estimated time on site:** 30–45 minutes, including the RAD Support call and boot wait time.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-14T09:00","end":"2026-09-14T10:00","latestStart":"2026-09-14T13:30"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":5},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 is below minimum threshold $250"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-15T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-17T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-18T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"},{"start":"2026-09-11T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-11T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"SMALL BACKBOARD/ DATA REMOTE INSTALL/ MUST HAVE BUTT-SET/MULTIMETER-DIS148477"},{"start":"2026-09-10T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-10T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Maintenance Kit Swap - Apex, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-04T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-05T13:30:00.000Z","summary":"DSS 9223 - Install (1) QNAP + UPS + Switch, Install (3) TP-Link Wireless Bridge, Install (3) 8 Port PoE Switch, Replace (15) Analog Cameras w/ (15) IP Cameras + Cable Runs - Lead Tech"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789161559650}
{"job":{"id":"2019797969","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"9AM Hard Start: Staples Cutover-Install Order 2_1743","description":"***IMPORTANT***<br>Tech MUST READ the Broadband Circuit Replacement Guide attached to ticket.<br>Tech MUST PRINT LOA attached to ticket.<br><br>**REQUIRED TOOLS**<br>Laptop (10/100 network card or better) with Ethernet port (or adapter)<br>Console Cable<br>Velcro Straps<br>Phillips, Slotted and Torx bits<br>Label maker<br>Charger<br>Assorted patch cables<br>Cat5/6 Cable - In case extension is needed<br>Printed files on Workmarket Ticket<br><br>Overview:<br>STEP 1: Arrival - Present LOA (attached to ticket)<br>STEP 2: Locate Rack, Cisco Router and New Broadband NID/Cable Modem<br>STEP 3: Identify Cisco Router (ISR 1100-4G) - Guide attached to ticket<br>STEP 4: Call Staples IT @ 508-253-7570<br>STEP 5: Move to new Cable Modem/Broadband NID<br>STEP 6: Gather Deliverables<br><br>STEP 1: Arrival &amp; Site Verification<br>-Introduce yourself to the Staples Store Manager prior to beginning work. Present LOA - attached to ticket.<br>-The Store Manager will escort you to the Tel/Elec/Data room.<br><br>STEP 2: Locate Rack, Cisco Router and New Broadband NID/Cable Modem<br>-Document the current condition of the network equipment rack or equipment backboard by taking pictures before beginning any work on the site.<br><br>STEP 3: Identify Cisco Router (ISR 1100-4G) in the data rack.<br>-Identify Port 1 and trace the network cable from Port 1. This will lead to an ISPs Fiber to Ethernet NID.<br>-Refer to the attached guide for sample pictures.<br>***Please do not unplug any cables from the router.***<br><br>STEP 4: Call Staples IT @ 508-253-7570<br>-Identify yourself and the store you’re in.<br>-Inform Staples IT you are replacing the store’s existing fiber service with broadband.<br>-Request permission to move the network cable over to the new Cable Modem/Broadband NID.<br><br>STEP 5: Move to new Cable Modem/Broadband NID<br>-Disconnect cable from the ISP NID.<br>-Move the network cable to the appropriate network port/jack on the newly installed Cable Modem/Broadband NID.  <br>-Confirm you see a green link light on Cisco router port 1. It should take a few seconds before you see link indication. <br>-Confirm that there is a network cable running from the Cisco router port 1 to the appropriate network port/jack on the CM/ND. <br>-Inform Staples IT that the broadband circuit is now interconnected and that you see (or do not see) link. <br>-Staples IT will notify you that the new circuit is being seen by the router.  You will then either be released or work to further troubleshoot any connectivity issue(s).<br><br>STEP 6: Gather Deliverables<br>Required Deliverables:<br>-Picture of cabinet/backboard (close up and wide)<br>-Pictures of connection on both ends (before and after)<br>-MUST get a signature prior to leaving the site that all items are tested and completed.","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-21T09:00","end":"2026-09-21T10:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":50},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":13.1},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $50 (countered: $65) is below minimum threshold $350"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-18T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 