{"job":{"id":19935819,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Momentara","title":"Install Gas Pump Advertising at Truckstops 10mins/site-Amazon Relay -C316874","description":{"html":"<p><strong>SCOPE OF WORK: <u>PUMP TOP AD INSTALL ON DIESEL PUMPS ONLY. WHERE SEMIS FUEL UP</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>I will need to ship you the advertising. Please provide your MAILING and EMAIL addresses so I can ship you the ads and send you some info on the install.</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Provider is to arrive and contact owner or manager on duty to alert them that you are there to install the advertising campaign assigned to you. If they have any questions, they can call 1-800-525-8762.</strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>Pump Tops:</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>INSTALL ONLY ON DIESEL PUMPS FOR SEMIS</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>This campaign is truck stops only - please check around for install of <u>DIESEL PUMPS for semis</u> - will be different than average pumps ex: taller roof over pumps.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>If station is unbranded and needs frames – install them (we supply them).</strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>Pump Top Photos:</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Take at least two pics at every pump that you install (from 10'-15' away).</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Station perspective photos: Take 2 perspective photos showing ALL pumps with the station in the background.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>&nbsp;*<u>DO NOT INSTALL ON \"OUT OF ORDER\" PUMPS.</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>*<u>DO NOT INSTALL ON PUMPS BLOCKED BY CARD HOLDERS OR OTHER SIGNAGE.</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>*MAKE SURE ALL ADS ARE FULLY TUCKED DOWN INTO THE BOTTOM OF THE FRAME.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>*NOTIFY ALLOVER MEDIA INSTALLATION REP WITH ALL ISSUES WHILE AT STATION.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Other Elements: (May not be apart of this program - your install rep will let you know if there are clings or not)</strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>Front Door/Window Cling</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Clean and dry glass on front door or window (see directions on which place, door or window, as directed)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Photos</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Take a close up shot - (10' away)</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Required Tools:</u></strong></p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Smart Phone</strong></p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Step Stool</strong></p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Frames (we can supply with ad shipment)</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>We appreciate providers who provide good communication and documentation, especially when the \"expected unexpected\" things happen.</strong></p>","markdown":"**SCOPE OF WORK: PUMP TOP AD INSTALL ON DIESEL PUMPS ONLY. WHERE SEMIS FUEL UP**\n\n**I will need to ship you the advertising. Please provide your MAILING and EMAIL addresses so I can ship you the ads and send you some info on the install.**\n\n**Provider is to arrive and contact owner or manager on duty to alert them that you are there to install the advertising campaign assigned to you. If they have any questions, they can call 1-800-525-8762.**\n\n**Pump Tops:**\n\n**INSTALL ONLY ON DIESEL PUMPS FOR SEMIS**\n\n**This campaign is truck stops only - please check around for install of DIESEL PUMPS for semis - will be different than average pumps ex: taller roof over pumps.**\n\n**If station is unbranded and needs frames – install them (we supply them).**\n\n**Pump Top Photos:**\n\n**Take at least two pics at every pump that you install (from 10'-15' away).**\n\n**Station perspective photos: Take 2 perspective photos showing ALL pumps with the station in the background.**\n\n **\\*DO NOT INSTALL ON \"OUT OF ORDER\" PUMPS.**\n\n**\\*DO NOT INSTALL ON PUMPS BLOCKED BY CARD HOLDERS OR OTHER SIGNAGE.**\n\n**\\*MAKE SURE ALL ADS ARE FULLY TUCKED DOWN INTO THE BOTTOM OF THE FRAME.**\n\n**\\*NOTIFY ALLOVER MEDIA INSTALLATION REP WITH ALL ISSUES WHILE AT STATION.**\n\n**Other Elements: (May not be apart of this program - your install rep will let you know if there are clings or not)**\n\n**Front Door/Window Cling**\n\n**Clean and dry glass on front door or window (see directions on which place, door or window, as directed)**\n\n**Photos**\n\n**Take a close up shot - (10' away)**\n\n**Required Tools:**\n\n· **Smart Phone**\n\n· **Step Stool**\n\n· **Frames (we can supply with ad shipment)**\n\n**We appreciate providers who provide good communication and documentation, especially when the \"expected unexpected\" things happen.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-16T00:00","end":"2026-09-16T02:00","latestStart":"2026-09-16T23:59"},"payRange":{"min":30,"max":30},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":49},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $30 is below minimum threshold $250"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-16T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-17T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-18T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"},{"start":"2026-09-11T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-11T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"SMALL BACKBOARD/ DATA REMOTE INSTALL/ MUST HAVE BUTT-SET/MULTIMETER-DIS148477"},{"start":"2026-09-10T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-10T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Maintenance Kit Swap - Apex, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-04T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-05T13:30:00.000Z","summary":"DSS 9223 - Install (1) QNAP + UPS + Switch, Install (3) TP-Link Wireless Bridge, Install (3) 8 Port PoE Switch, Replace (15) Analog Cameras w/ (15) IP Cameras + Cable Runs - Lead Tech"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789161660431}
{"job":{"id":"3930498497","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Retail Technology Group","title":"Panera Bread - De-Install / Inventory / Pack / Return POS equipment","description":"<p>**DO NOT CONTACT CAFÉ** </p><p><br></p><p>Tech shall drop equipment off at a local UPS ship center**, need a van or truck to transport equipment**, need to pack POS equipment in a professional manner, so it is not damaged in shipping** </p><p>**Failure to properly pack equipment for safe transport back to RTG will result in loss of pay equal to the cost of the damaged equipment** </p><p><br></p><p>Escalation Path: </p><p>Panera Onsite Contact: </p><p>RTG Project Manager: Scott 314-347-7573</p><p><br></p><p>Check-IN / OUT on WM. </p><p><br></p><p>Attached files: </p><p>RTG Sign-Off sheet.pdf </p><p>Panera De-Install Checklist.pdf </p><p>UPS return labels </p><p><br></p><p>Tools and supplies you will need. All packing material is Billable. </p><p>7 - 18x18x18 BOXES </p><p>4 - 18x24x18 BOXES </p><p>Bubble Wrap and Packing Material (Newspaper is fine to fill in the empty spaces in the box. Monitors need to be covered with bubble wrap. </p><p>Packing Tape </p><p>Various screw drivers </p><p>Various Nut Drivers *3/8\" is commonly used to hold the brackets to the wall. </p><p>Socket Set </p><p>Cordless Drill </p><p>6-8' Ladder </p><p><br></p><p>Scope of Work: </p><p>**YOU WILL NEED VEHICLE TO TAKE BOXES TO THE NEAREST UPS SHIPPING LOCATION** </p><p>**UPS drop off locations will not accept a box over 50lbs.** </p><p>**Return labels are attached to WO** </p><p><br></p><p>We do not want any equipment destroyed or broken during shipment, so you will need to provide bubble wrap to cover all monitors. Use the bubble wrap as well to wrap POS registers, controllers, printers, bumpbars, Verifone Credit Card machines, Server, Routers, Switches, WAP's, Etc. </p><p>We understand that equipment can get damaged in shipping, but not using bubble wrap is not acceptable. </p><p>It is up to you to neatly pack equipment in boxes for return to RTG. </p><p>Be sure to fill the boxes with crumbled up newspaper, packing peanuts, or other packing material, so they do not collapse in transit from UPS. </p><p><br></p><p>1. Print out the attached De-Installed Equipment Checklists attached to this WO. </p><p><br></p><p>2. Start with the POS registers. POS registers should have a printer, cash drawer, and maybe a Verifone Credit card machine. Throw away the cash drawers. We do want all the LRS pagers and paging systems as well.</p><p><br></p><p>3. Kitchen Display Systems (KDS). These will be mounted in the kitchen on brackets. Brackets can be thrown away. </p><p>Controllers, Monitors, and Bumpbars will need to be neatly boxed up. Note on checklist. Pack for return.</p><p>Be sure to remove the Catering WS as well. The MFC printer can be thrown away. We do not want it back. </p><p><br></p><p>4. Office Equipment should include a Server, Network equipment (Including racks), Phone system, and network switch. The MFC printer can be thrown away. We do not want it back. </p><p>There is a C240 Server in the network rack. To remove it from the rails, you have to push in the two white buttons on the side rails. </p><p>You should have this professionally boxed up by UPS. Bill me for the cost.</p><p>There are 3 AP's in the ceiling. One will be near the Kiosks, One will be centered in the dining room, and One will be back by the office and walkin coolers.</p><p><br></p><p>DO NOT TOUCH </p><p>*Leave Cafe Music System </p><p>*Leave ISP’s modem, and\\or T1 equipment </p><p>*Leave Security System and Camera’s. </p><p>*Leave Fire and Alarm Panels. </p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>6. iPADS, &amp; Kiosks</p><p><br></p><p>7. If café has a drive thru, there will be equipment listed on the DeInstall Checklist to be removed. </p><p><br></p><p>8. If there is any equipment you are unsure of, contact Project Manager. </p><p><br></p><p>9. Take a picture of inside each box before sealing so we can make sure it is properly packed. Upload as a deliverable </p><p><br></p><p>10. Be sure to number each Box, attach a return label &amp; Include De-Installed Checklist in BOX1. Upload it ASAP. </p><p><br></p><p>Deliverables: </p><p>RTG Signoff sheet </p><p>De-Installed Equipment Checklist </p><p>Packing Material Receipts *Be sure to add your expenses to WO. </p><p>Pic of each box before being sealed to verify that it is properl</p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-16T09:00","end":"2026-09-16T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":0,"max":497.70557729},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":3},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"fixed","counterRate":124,"baseAmount":497.70557729,"estHours":4,"travelExpense":0,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T18:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":60,"mode":"hours","reason":"arrival_window"}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-16T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-17T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-18T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"},{"start":"2026-09-11T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-11T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"SMALL BACKBOARD/ DATA REMOTE INSTALL/ MUST HAVE BUTT-SET/MULTIMETER-DIS148477"},{"start":"2026-09-10T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-10T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Maintenance Kit Swap - Apex, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-04T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-05T13:30:00.000Z","summary":"DSS 9223 - Install (1) QNAP + UPS + Switch, Install (3) TP-Link Wireless Bridge, Install (3) 8 Port PoE Switch, Replace (15) Analog Cameras w/ (15) IP Cameras + Cable Runs - Lead Tech"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1789161667842}
{"job":{"id":19934728,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"DiverseNet","title":"Troubleshoot - Media Player(s) - SC-054304","description":{"html":"<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>───────────────────────────────────────</p>\n<p><strong>IMPORTANT NOTES</strong></p>\n<p>───────────────────────────────────────</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Technician must upload all deliverables before calling DiverseNet to check out or leaving site</li>\n<li>Technician must call to check in and out with DiverseNet to receive full payment</li>\n<li>Technician must arrive during the given time frame to receive full payment</li>\n<li>Any out of scope work, or time logged past the not to exceed amount, must be approved by DiverseNet to receive payment</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>───────────────────────────────────────</p>\n<p><strong>SKILLS, TOOLS, MATERIALS AND DRESS CODE</strong></p>\n<p>───────────────────────────────────────</p>\n<p><strong>Skills</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>General AV Knowledge (screens, media players, etc.)</li>\n<li>Networking</li>\n<li>Low voltage cabling</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Tools/Materials</strong></p>\n<p><strong><em>***All materials bill backs must be pre-approved by DiverseNet***</em></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Laptop &amp; DB9 Console Cable</li>\n<li>Test-set</li>\n<li>Tone and probe</li>\n<li>Punch down tools</li>\n<li>Modular crimp tool</li>\n<li>In-house wire</li>\n<li>Cross connect</li>\n<li>RJ11 Jacks</li>\n<li>CAT5 Cable / Keystones / Ends</li>\n<li>Standard hand tools (screwdriver, etc.)</li>\n<li>Mouse and Keyboard</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Dress Code</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Close toed shoes</li>\n<li>Long pants</li>\n<li>Collared shirt</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>───────────────────────────────────────</p>\n<p><strong>CHECK IN INSTRUCTIONS AND ESCALATION</strong></p>\n<p>───────────────────────────────────────</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Must check in</strong> with DiverseNet at 317-536-6000 x 7 and reference case number 00051307\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Ask for&nbsp;check in code - (Required for Payment)</strong></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Must check in</strong> with&nbsp;<del>********** *** * ************** ****** *</del>&nbsp;and reference ticket #&nbsp;<del>*********</del></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>For Jewelry Locations, technicians are expected to:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Sign in at the front desk.</li>\n<li>Speak with store staff and explain the purpose of the visit before beginning work.</li>\n<li>Present the applicable work order and a state-issued ID upon request.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Use the following escalation path for all issues on site:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><del>********** *** * ************** ****** *</del></li>\n<li>DiverseNet -&nbsp;317-536-6000 x2</li>\n</ol>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>───────────────────────────────────────</p>\n<p><strong>DESCRIPTION OF WORK</strong></p>\n<p>───────────────────────────────────────</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Print off sign off form before going on site.﻿</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Please make sure to be in contact with the NOC every hour to keep them updated.</strong></li>\n<li>Notes: Dispatch to send tech to investigate all offline players.</li>\n<li>Tech must have cable tester/toner.</li>\n<li>Tech must schedule appointment with MOD before arriving onsite or risk being turned away.</li>\n<li>Tech must contact Convergent NOC @ 800.877.7802 Opt 3.</li>\n<li><del>********** ** **** **** ** ****** *** ******* ******* * ************ ****************************</del></li>\n<li>Tech must get completion code from NOC to ensure no issues with invoicing.</li>\n<li>Case Items: ({Case Items: Name: =SAM-PC-BRIGHTSIGN-XD1033, Mac=null, SN=R4J7D8002189, desc=STJ_1534_BridalWall_Zales_}, {Case Items: Name: =SAM-PC-BRIGHTSIGN-XD1033, Mac=null, SN=R4J7DJ002156, desc=STJ_1534_ExteriorWall_Zales_}, {Case Items: Name: =SAM-PC-BRIGHTSIGN-XD1033, Mac=null, SN=R4J7DG002157, desc=STJ_1534_PromoWall_Zales_})</li>\n<li><strong>If equipment is being replaced, old equipment must be dropped off at FedEx for return and receipt uploaded.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Please clean area entirely when finished.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>───────────────────────────────────────</p>\n<p><strong>DELIVERABLE REQUIREMENTS</strong></p>\n<p>───────────────────────────────────────</p>\n<p><strong>All deliverables need to be submitted on the platform before checking out with DiverseNet</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Before pictures of nonfunctioning Media Player(s)</li>\n<li>After pictures of functioning Media Player(s)</li>\n<li>Serial numbers of worked on equipment</li>\n<li>Drop off receipt (if applicable)</li>\n<li>Work order&nbsp;<em>signed by the Manager on Duty</em>&nbsp;with dates and times</li>\n<li><strong>Upload all deliverables before calling to check out</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>**If parts are required to be delivered the technician MUST take a clear photo of the tracking label, drop off receipt, and the equipment properly packaged inside the box. If technician fails to provide the following DiverseNet reserves the right to not pay the work order in full**</strong></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>───────────────────────────────────────</p>\n<p><strong>CHECK OUT INSTRUCTIONS</strong></p>\n<p>───────────────────────────────────────</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Must check ou</strong>t with <del>********** *** * ************** ****** *</del>&nbsp;and reference ticket #<del>*********</del>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Obtain NOC agents Name and check out code (Must be included in closing notes)</strong></li>\n<li><strong>When checking out, verify with the<del>**********</del> NOC agent if any equipment will be need to be returned. If so, request a return label for this equipment.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Must check out</strong> with Diversenet at 317-536-6000 x 7&nbsp;and reference case number 00051307\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Ask for check out code - (Required for Payment)</strong></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"───────────────────────────────────────\n\n**IMPORTANT NOTES**\n\n───────────────────────────────────────\n\n- Technician must upload all deliverables before calling DiverseNet to check out or leaving site\n- Technician must call to check in and out with DiverseNet to receive full payment\n- Technician must arrive during the given time frame to receive full payment\n- Any out of scope work, or time logged past the not to exceed amount, must be approved by DiverseNet to receive payment\n\n───────────────────────────────────────\n\n**SKILLS, TOOLS, MATERIALS AND DRESS CODE**\n\n───────────────────────────────────────\n\n**Skills**\n\n- General AV Knowledge (screens, media players, etc.)\n- Networking\n- Low voltage cabling\n\n**Tools/Materials**\n\n***\\*\\*\\*All materials bill backs must be pre-approved by DiverseNet\\*\\*\\****\n\n- Laptop & DB9 Console Cable\n- Test-set\n- Tone and probe\n- Punch down tools\n- Modular crimp tool\n- In-house wire\n- Cross connect\n- RJ11 Jacks\n- CAT5 Cable / Keystones / Ends\n- Standard hand tools (screwdriver, etc.)\n- Mouse and Keyboard\n\n**Dress Code**\n\n- Close toed shoes\n- Long pants\n- Collared shirt\n\n───────────────────────────────────────\n\n**CHECK IN INSTRUCTIONS AND ESCALATION**\n\n───────────────────────────────────────\n\n- **Must check in** with DiverseNet at 317-536-6000 x 7 and reference case number 00051307 \n  - **Ask for check in code - (Required for Payment)**\n- **Must check in** with \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* and reference ticket # \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**For Jewelry Locations, technicians are expected to:**\n\n- Sign in at the front desk.\n- Speak with store staff and explain the purpose of the visit before beginning work.\n- Present the applicable work order and a state-issued ID upon request.\n\nUse the following escalation path for all issues on site:\n\n1. \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\