{"job":{"id":19763414,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"NEC Corporation of America","title":"SCO (Self Checkout) Removal, Install Hand Scanners and Bag Holder POS Units 3","description":{"html":"<p><strong>The estimated duration will be 2 hours</strong></p><p><strong>Overview: Remove ALL SCO equipment, signage, and return the equipment, also install and configure hand scanners and install a bag holder for all POS Units on site.</strong></p><p>Seeking a technician with experience in POS deinstallation. Prefer Retail Point-of-Sale/kiosk experience.</p><p><strong>Tech is required to deinstall and package SCO tablet and peripherals for return shipping. Packing materials will be sent to the store. Use all the bubble wrap to ensure the parts are safely packed. Tech is to deinstall the SCO advertising displays and dispose of the marketing materials in the store dumpster</strong>.  <strong>You will also be installing an additional hand scanner on each POS as well as a bag holder on the front counter (customer facing)</strong></p><ol><li>You will also have to perform the steps to factory reset the unit. (Attached Document has the steps for this process)</li><li>The return waybill will be attached to the work order and will need to be printed before going to the store.</li><li>You will install a hand scanner for each POS unit as well as a Bag Holder per POS unit mounted on the front of the customer counter</li></ol><p>A detailed deinstallation guide is provided to the assigned provider</p><p>ALL PHOTOS must be <strong>uploaded to the work order</strong>, BEFORE checkout code will be given.</p><p>Estimated duration is 2 hours</p><p>Tools Required:</p><ul><li>Camera or phone for clear pictures on deliverables</li><li>Scrapper tool w/goo-be gone to remove the residue from the stickers or glue pads</li><li>Basic tool kit</li></ul><p><strong>Pre-Site Requirements:</strong></p><p>Check that you are at the store number situated on your work request. The store number can be found on the front window of the store. If you don't see it posted, ask store staff.</p><p><strong>On-Site Tasks (Overview- Step-by-step process attached in the document section of the work order)</strong></p><p>Introduction to store personnel and purpose of visit.</p><p>Remove and pack SCO tablet and peripherals (ELO tablet and power assembly, 7-11 pin pad and cable, printer and cable, scanner and cable, scanner stand). Remove SCO signs and base plate for store to dispose of.</p><p>Please note any delays or issues in your close-out notes.</p><p><strong>Required On-Site Deliverables</strong>:</p><p>1) TaBaSCO (SCO) equipment upon arrival</p><p>2) Connections under Tablet</p><p>3) Bubble wrap Tablet screens (front &amp; back screens)</p><p>4) Equipment in box securely packaged (box opened, unsealed)</p><p>5) Box sealed with return label</p><p>6) Return label (MUST DROP BOXED SCO UNIT OFF AT UPS STORE)</p><p>7) Front counter (before &amp; after)</p><p>&nbsp;Additional Contacts:&nbsp;</p><p>NEC Deployment Support team</p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************ *** *</del></span></p><p><strong>Escalation Process:</strong></p><p><strong>Work order questions- contact work order manager Brian Simpson</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************</del></span></p><ul><li><strong>&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;<strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************** *** *</del></strong></li></ul><p><strong>﻿Please read below.</strong></p><p><strong>Call Before Starting Work:</strong>&nbsp;Ensure you call the provided number,&nbsp;<strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************** *** *</del></strong><strong>, before commencing any work. Hours of operation are 7:00 am - 7:00 pm </strong>CST. There will be no support outside of these hours; therefore, you will not be able to check in<strong> prior to 7am CST.</strong></p><p><strong>Check-In for Time Tracking:</strong>&nbsp;The agent will provide a&nbsp;<strong>check-in number, marking the official start of your work for timekeeping purposes.</strong></p><p><strong>Check-Out to End Time Tracking:</strong>&nbsp;When your work is&nbsp;<strong>finished, contact the agent again to obtain a check-out number, signifying the official end of your work.</strong></p><p><strong>*********** MAKE SURE ALL WORK IS COMPLETE (INCLUDING SITE CLEANUP) BEFORE CHECKING OUT WITH DST AS THAT WILL BE TIME OF RECORD - WE WANT TO AVOID TIME DISCREPANCIES FOR PAYMENT APPROVAL. **********</strong></p><p><strong>Record Based on Agent Timestamps:</strong>&nbsp;The agent will record the&nbsp;<strong>timestamps for both check-in and check-out, serving as the official record of your work duration.</strong></p><p><strong>Include Codes in Work Order:</strong>&nbsp;Remember to incorporate these check-in and check-out codes into your work order to ensure approval for payment.</p><p>By following these guidelines, you'll guarantee accurate timekeeping and a smooth approval process for your work order.</p><p><strong><u>Turn away fee:</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>In the event of a site turn away</u></strong>&nbsp;(Something wrong when arriving at store that prevents our install - some examples: network down, equipment lost, store refusing install, no power) provider will be paid a $50 cancellation fee, and will be given first rite of refusal for the return trip in the future.&nbsp;Contact DST immediately and notify of issue, and take guidance to see if we can first resolve issue.&nbsp;DST will work with customer to resolve situation/approve your release.&nbsp;Will need to allow 20 minutes for issue resolution and contact DST if no update in that time frame to request release and reschedule.</p><p><strong>Readiness Policy:&nbsp;</strong>The provider is expected to arrive on-site with all the required skills, tools and materials to complete the scope of work they accepted.&nbsp;Failure to meet these requirements may result in pay not being approved.</p><p><strong>On My Way:&nbsp;</strong>When traveling to the site, place yourself on the work order as On My Way\" This will update the Support team that you are to the site.</p><p><strong>Arriving Late:</strong>&nbsp;All work orders are HARD start work orders. This means you are expected to be on-site on or before the start of the work order.&nbsp;Failure to check in on time may result in a reduction of your approved pay.</p><p><strong>Changing Resources:</strong>&nbsp;By accepting this work order, you are the resource expected to show up on-site to perform work. Swapping out resources on a work order MUST be PRE-APPROVED before arrival at the location. Sending someone else to perform this work order without getting prior written approval may result in pay not being approved.</p><p><strong>Dress Code:</strong>&nbsp;Your professional appearance reflects our company. Always look clean, presentable, and professional. Wear a non-logo collared shirt and pants (jeans are OK with NO holes), no shorts, flip-flops, or open-toed shoes.</p><p><strong>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy</strong></p><p><strong>Expense Approval:</strong>&nbsp;Any travel or material expenses must be negotiated before the WO assignment's acceptance. These MUST be negotiated via counteroffer in the work order.</p><p><strong>Additional Time On-site:</strong>&nbsp;If there are any delays beyond the authorized work order time, you must contact the Support team and explain what has caused the delay(s) so this can be documented for payment purposes. Failure to get PRE-APPROVAL may result in additional pay not being approved. You will be paid <span style=\"color: black;\">$45 per hour</span> after the initial hour, which covers the work order.</p><p><strong>Out-of-Scope Work:&nbsp;</strong>If you are asked to perform work beyond the scope stated above, please direct the end user to contact the support desk to open another incident.&nbsp;Do NOT perform Out-of-Scope work without authorization.&nbsp;Failure to get PRE-APPROVAL may result in out-of-scope pay not being approved. You will be paid at <span style=\"color: black;\">$45 per hour</span> after the initial hour that covers the work order. You will be paid <span style=\"color: black;\">$45 per hour</span> after the initial hour, which covers the work order.</p><p><strong>Returning Parts:</strong>&nbsp;Return Waybills will be found in the original package the part was shipped to you in. You must enter the UPS Tracking number into the TASK Field on the work order and drop the part off at a UPS Store. We must see that the returned part is being tracked in the UPS System before we approve payment for your work order.</p>","markdown":"**The estimated duration will be 2 hours**\n\n**Overview: Remove ALL SCO equipment, signage, and return the equipment, also install and configure hand scanners and install a bag holder for all POS Units on site.**\n\nSeeking a technician with experience in POS deinstallation. Prefer Retail Point-of-Sale/kiosk experience.\n\n**Tech is required to deinstall and package SCO tablet and peripherals for return shipping. Packing materials will be sent to the store. Use all the bubble wrap to ensure the parts are safely packed. Tech is to deinstall the SCO advertising displays and dispose of the marketing materials in the store dumpster**. **You will also be installing an additional hand scanner on each POS as well as a bag holder on the front counter (customer facing)**\n\n1. You will also have to perform the steps to factory reset the unit. (Attached Document has the steps for this process)\n2. The return waybill will be attached to the work order and will need to be printed before going to the store.\n3. You will install a hand scanner for each POS unit as well as a Bag Holder per POS unit mounted on the front of the customer counter\n\nA detailed deinstallation guide is provided to the assigned provider\n\nALL PHOTOS must be **uploaded to the work order**, BEFORE checkout code will be given.\n\nEsti