{"job":{"id":19934282,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"National Video Monitoring Corp","title":"Troubleshoot Offline Camera*24ft Ladder Needed*","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Specific SOW Below: Refer to Summary for additional Information</strong></p><p>Upon arrival technician will need to call-in to EyeQ for Check-in and out: 727-437-3586</p><p>Remote Support. 678-846-9271&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>SCOPE OF WORK</strong></p><p><strong>Site Name:</strong> Trinity Building Corp - Trinity Gardens Apartments [465-505]</p><p><strong>SOW Type:</strong> Camera Offline - Single Device</p><p><strong>Estimated Time Onsite:</strong> 2 hours</p><p><strong>Ladder Requirement:</strong> 24ft ladder required</p><p><strong>Lift Requirement:</strong> No lift</p><p><strong>Parts Required:</strong> No parts</p><p><strong>Standard Requirements</strong></p><ul><li>Network tools</li><li>Laptop</li><li>Basic hand tools</li><li>Cable tester/toner if cabling needs to be validated</li></ul><p><strong>Issue to Address Onsite</strong></p><p>Camera 7 (IP: 172.17.31.156) is currently down and not responding. Remote Support was unable to bring the camera back online remotely. Field technician needs to validate power, cabling, PoE, switch port/link lights, and physical camera condition onsite.</p><p><strong>Device Details</strong></p><p>1. Camera 7 | Camera | Axis | AXISP3225LVEMkII | IP: 172.17.31.156 | MAC: AC-CC-8E-A6-B3-43 | Status/Issue: DOWN</p><p><strong>Remote Troubleshooting Already Attempted</strong></p><ul><li>Remote Support rebooted available switches/network equipment and adjusted wireless settings, but the issue remained unresolved.</li></ul><p><strong>Actions Required Onsite</strong></p><ul><li>Locate the affected camera onsite.</li><li>Validate camera power/PoE and confirm link lights at the camera and switch.</li><li>Inspect camera cabling, terminations, patch cable, and any exposed connectors for damage or water intrusion.</li><li>Test with a known-good patch cable where possible.</li><li>Confirm whether the camera can be reached locally.</li><li>Work with Remote Support to confirm the camera is online and streaming before leaving site.</li></ul><p><strong>Deliverables / What to Report Back</strong></p><ul><li>Photo of the affected camera.</li><li>Photo of camera cabling/connector condition.</li><li>Photo of switch port/link lights if accessible.</li><li>Confirmation of power/PoE status.</li><li>Root cause of the camera being offline.</li><li>Confirmation whether the camera is online and streaming before leaving site.</li></ul><p><strong>Required Remote Support Coordination</strong></p><ul><li>Technician must contact Field Coordination upon arrival before beginning work.</li><li>Technician must provide photos of the affected equipment, cabling, power, link lights, and surrounding area where applicable.</li><li>Technician must contact Remote Support before replacing, factory resetting, relocating, or removing any equipment unless specifically instructed in this SOW.</li><li>Technician must contact Remote Support before leaving site to confirm final device status and verify whether any additional action is required.</li><li>If the issue cannot be resolved onsite, technician must provide clear findings, suspected root cause, photos, and what is needed for a return visit.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Time Management:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Approval:</strong> Call for additional time if the job exceeds 2 hours. Extra time without prior approval will not be compensated.</li><li><strong>Contact:</strong> Contact the Work Order Manager immediately if the onsite contact does not allow you to work.</li><li><strong>Work Hours:</strong> Complete the work during the specified timeframe and normal business hours unless otherwise stated.</li><li><strong>Completion:</strong> Do not leave without discussing unresolved issues with the Work Order Manager.</li></ul><p><strong>Required Equipment:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Ladders:</strong> 8/16' Little Giant Ladder or 8' A-frame and a 24' Extension Ladder.</li><li><strong>Cabling:</strong> Cat5 Cable (reimbursed at $0.18 per foot) and RJ-45 Cable Termination Ends.</li><li><strong>Tools:</strong> Network testing tools, toner, installation tools, voltmeter, smartphone with Field Nation app, laptop with RJ-45 and Wi-Fi, and a basic technician tool kit.</li><li><strong>Additional Instructions:</strong> Refer to the Standard Instructions section for standardized equipment reimbursement rates.</li></ul><p><strong>Important Policies:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Check-in/Out:</strong> Call 678-846-9271 before starting and after completing the work. Provide details if the Scope of Work cannot be completed.</li><li><strong>Technical Support:</strong> Available M-F, 9 AM-4:30 PM EST. Provide details on your work progress when contacting technical support.</li><li><strong>Equipment Return:</strong> Return unused equipment to EyeQ (NVMC) with original packaging. Contact the Work Order Manager for a return shipping label.</li><li><strong>Rescheduling Policy:</strong> If rescheduling is necessary due to EyeQ’s error (e.g., missing equipment), a $30 travel fee will be paid.</li><li><strong>Issue Diagnosis:</strong> For issues requiring a return trip, the ticket remains open with additional expenses. Misdiagnoses will not be compensated for a second trip.</li><li><strong>NTE (Not To Exceed) Hours:</strong> Additional time beyond the initial approved period requires prior approval from the Work Order Manager.</li></ul>","markdown":"**Specific SOW Below: Refer to Summary for additional Information**\n\nUpon arrival technician will need to call-in to EyeQ for Check-in and out: 727-437-3586\n\nRemote Support. 678-846-9271\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK**\n\n**Site Name:** Trinity Building Corp - Trinity Gardens Apartments \\[465-505\\]\n\n**SOW Type:** Camera Offline - Single Device\n\n**Estimated Time Onsite:** 2 hours\n\n**Ladder Requirement:** 24ft ladder required\n\n**Lift Requirement:** No lift\n\n**Parts Required:** No parts\n\n**Standard Requirements**\n\n- Network tools\n- Laptop\n- Basic hand tools\n- Cable tester/toner if cabling needs to be validated\n\n**Issue to Address Onsite**\n\nCamera 7 (IP: 172.17.31.156) is currently down and not responding. Remote Support was unable to bring the camera back online remotely. Field technician needs to validate power, cabling, PoE, switch port/link lights, and physical camera condition onsite.\n\n**Device Details**\n\n1\\. Camera 7 | Camera | Axis | AXISP3225LVEMkII | IP: 172.17.31.156 | MAC: AC-CC-8E-A6-B3-43 | Status/Issue: DOWN\n\n**Remote Troubleshooting Already Attempted**\n\n- Remote Support rebooted available switches/network equipment and adjusted wireless settings, but the issue remained unresolved.\n\n**Actions Required Onsite**\n\n- Locate the affected camera onsite.\n- Validate camera power/PoE and confirm link lights at the camera and switch.\n- Inspect camera cabling, terminations, patch cable, and any exposed connectors for damage or water intrusion.\n- Test with a known-good patch cable where possible.\n- Confirm whether the camera can be reached locally.\n- Work with Remote Support to confirm the camera is online and streaming before leaving site.\n\n**Deliverables / What to Report Back**\n\n- Photo of the affected camera.\n- Photo of camera cabling/connector condition.\n- Photo of switch port/link lights if accessible.\n- Confirmation of power/PoE status.\n- Root cause of the camera being offline.\n- Confirmation whether the camera is online and streaming before leaving site.\n\n**Required Remote Support Coordination**\n\n- Technician must contact Field Coordination upon arrival before beginning work.\n- Technician must provide photos of the affected equipment, cabling, power, link lights, and surrounding area where applicable.\n- Technician must contact Remote Support before replacing, factory resetting, relocating, or removing any equipment unless specifically instructed in this SOW.\n- Technician must contact Remote Support before leaving site to confirm final device status and verify whether any additional action is required.\n- If the issue cannot be resolved onsite, technician must provide clear findings, suspected root cause, photos, and what is needed for a return visit.\n\n**Time Management:**\n\n- **Approval:** Call for additional time if the job exceeds 2 hours. Extra time without prior approval will not be compensated.\n- **Contact:** Contact the Work Order Manager immediately if the onsite contact does not allow you to work.\n- **Work Hours:** Complete the work during the specified timeframe and normal business hours unless otherwise stated.\n- **Completion:** Do not leave without discussing unresolved issues with the Work Order Manager.\n\n**Required Equipment:**\n\n- **Ladders:** 8/16' Little Giant Ladder or 8' A-frame and a 24' Extension Ladder.\n- **Cabling:** Cat5 Cable (reimbursed at $0.18 per foot) and RJ-45 Cable Termination Ends.\n- **Tools:** Network testing tools, toner, installation tools, voltmeter, smartphone with Field Nation app, laptop with RJ-45 and Wi-Fi, and a basic technician tool kit.\n- **Additional Instructions:** Refer to the Standard Instructions section for standardized equipment reimbursement rates.\n\n**Important Policies:**\n\n- **Check-in/Out:** Call 678-846-9271 before starting and after completing the work. Provide details if the Scope of Work cannot be completed.\n- **Technical Support:** Available M-F, 9 AM-4:30 PM EST. Provide details on your work progress when contacting technical support.\n- **Equipment Return:** Return unused equipment to EyeQ (NVMC) with original packaging. Contact the Work Order Manager for a return shipping label.\n- **Rescheduling Policy:** If rescheduling is necessary due to EyeQ’s error (e.g., missing equipment), a $30 travel fee will be paid.\n- **Issue Diagnosis:** For issues requiring a return trip, the ticket remains open with additional expenses. Misdiagnoses will not be compensated for a second trip.\n- **NTE (Not To Exceed) Hours:** Additional time beyond the initial approved period requires prior approval from the Work Order Manager.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-14T09:00","end":"2026-09-14T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":70,"max":140},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":70,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":58},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $140 (countered: $140) is below minimum threshold $250"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-15T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-17T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-18T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"},{"start":"2026-09-11T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-11T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"SMALL BACKBOARD/ DATA REMOTE INSTALL