{"job":{"id":19864759,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"PIVITAL","title":"Handheld Scanner upgrade - Tech 1","description":{"html":"<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>2026 POS Handheld Devices</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Overview:</strong> Replace older Honeywell scanners with new Zebra handheld scanners.</p>\n<p><strong><u>The handheld scanners are NOT HOT SWAPPABLE.</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>The registers must be shut down</u>,</strong> then the Honeywell scanners can be removed and the zebras installed,<strong><u>THEN</u></strong> reboot the register.</p>\n<p>This is in the doc., page 6</p>\n<p>This should help avoid the issues with the supplemental tests failing and save the troubleshooting time</p>\n<p>Shift : Dayside</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Preparation:</strong> Tools include drill, putty knife, screwdrivers, wire cutters, and cut-resistive gloves. Video install training available</li>\n<li><strong>Installation Tasks:</strong> Remove old scanner, install Zebra scanner, install 12ft USB cable, and install mounting cup (if applicable).</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Non-SCO Registers – Zebra scanner, 12ft USB cable, mounting cup</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">NCR SCO Registers – Zebra scanner, 12ft USB cable, mounting cup</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">ELO SCO Registers - Only need the zebra hand scanner and 12 ft USB cable installed. The mounting cup is not needed.</li>\n<li><strong>&nbsp;Deliverables:</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Changes to ATR process:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Only send hand scanners back to HQ Depot if returning with a palletized ATR (POS Refresh or Control Room Clean Up)</strong></li>\n<li>If this is the only scope to ATR, please CRC hardware</li>\n<li><strong>Package old scanners/cables for HQ Depot. Contact Deployment Support for ATR process</strong></li>\n<li>Old scanner cup holders need to place them in the CRC pallet</li>\n<li>No photos required. Deployment Support validation that everything has been completed accordingly to customer requirements.<em>﻿</em></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>General Tool Requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Windows 10 Laptop + Charger</li>\n<li>Smartphone with Camera + Charger</li>\n<li>#1 &amp; #2 Phillips, M3/M4 Allen Keys</li>\n<li>Velcro Strips (no zip ties/twist ties)</li>\n<li>Standard Tool Kit, Black Ink Pens, Scotch Tape</li>\n<li>Printed Register Labels (if provided)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>General Daily Process &amp; Smartsheet Requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Check In/Out in Smartsheet <strong>while onsite</strong>.</li>\n<li>Meet with Store MOD/Lead upon arrival.</li>\n<li>Maintain professionalism with all store staff; assist in resolving reported issues.</li>\n<li>Submit required photos daily in <strong>Smartsheet Photo Form</strong> and attach to Work Order.</li>\n<li><strong>Deployment Support must release you before leaving site.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Obtain MOD/Lead sign-off prior to departure.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Call Pivital to confirm deliverables/photos before leaving site.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Deployment Support Contact Information</strong></p>\n<p><del>************</del></p>\n<ul>\n<li><del>****** * *** ********* ******* *********** *******</del></li>\n<li><del>****** * *** ****** *******</del></li>\n<li><del>****** * *** ****** ****** ********</del></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Compliance &amp; Penalties</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Deliverables, photos, cleanup, and timeliness are mandatory.</li>\n<li>Expense Documentation: If materials, parking, or toll expenses are added to the Work Order, a valid receipt or invoice must be submitted for each individual expense. Expenses submitted without supporting documentation will not be approved.</li>\n<li>Missing or incomplete deliverables may result in penalties or hours not approved.</li>\n<li>Pay Change Requests are not accepted. Work reflects agreed rate + verified hours.</li>\n<li>GPS check-in/out is required for onsite presence.</li>\n<li>If GPS is disabled or shows offsite, proof of onsite work is required. Proof of onsite and offsite presence must be provided if GPS is disabled. Failure to have GPS enabled or offsite time entries will result in the additional time being logged to not be approved</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Work Order Requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Technicians must check in and out in Field Nation while onsite. No exceptions.</li>\n<li>Do not log multiple site visits on this work order.</li>\n<li>Each site visit will require its own work order.</li>\n<li>If a revisit is needed, close out this work order and contact Pivital ASAP to notify that a revisit will be required.</li>\n<li>Technicians must call and/or text Pivital upon arrival and departure.</li>\n<li>All tasks and deliverables outlined in the Work Order must be fully completed.</li>\n<li>Technicians must log time only for the duration physically onsite.</li>\n<li>Time entries are verified by GPS.</li>\n<li>Any issues encountered onsite must be reported to Pivital immediately.</li>\n<li>Technicians must not mention Field Nation to store staff or customers..</li>\n<li>All standard policies and procedures must be followed.</li>\n<li>If there is a conflict between policies and the Service Description/Confidential Section, the Service Description/Confidential Section takes precedence.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Site Requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Closing notes must be completed onsite.</li>\n<li>Government-issued photo ID required for entry.</li>\n<li>All technician names must be submitted in advance.</li>\n<li>Check in with site contacts as a<del>********</del>representative.</li>\n<li>Technicians must be fully equipped; no use of customer tools/equipment.</li>\n<li>Business casual attire and professional conduct required.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>","markdown":"**2026 POS Handheld Devices**\n\n**Overview:** Replace older Honeywell scanners with new Zebra handheld scanners.\n\n**The handheld scanners are NOT HOT SWAPPABLE.**\n\n**The registers must be shut down,** then the Honeywell scanners can be removed and the zebras installed,**THEN** reboot the register.\n\nThis is in the doc., page 6\n\nThis should help avoid the issues with the supplemental tests failing and save the troubleshooting time\n\nShift : Dayside\n\n- **Preparation:** Tools include drill, putty knife, screwdrivers, wire cutters, and cut-resistive gloves. Video install training available\n- **Installation Tasks:** Remove old scanner, install Zebra scanner, install 12ft USB cable, and install mounting cup (if applicable).\n- Non-SCO Registers – Zebra scanner, 12ft USB cable, mounting cup\n- NCR SCO Registers – Zebra scanner, 12ft USB cable, mounting cup\n- ELO SCO Registers - Only need the zebra hand scanner and 12 ft USB cable installed. The mounting cup is not needed.\n- **Deliverables:**\n\nChanges to ATR process:\n\n- **Only send hand scanners back to HQ Depot if returning with a palletized ATR (POS Refresh or Control Room Clean Up)**\n- If this is the only scope to ATR, please CRC hardware\n- **Package old scanners/cables for HQ Depot. Contact Deployment Support for ATR process**\n- Old scanner cup holders need to place them in the CRC pallet\n- No photos required. Deployment Support validation that everything has been completed accordingly to customer requirements.*﻿*\n\n**General Tool Requirements**\n\n- Windows 10 Laptop + Charger\n- Smartphone with Camera + Charger\n- \\#1 & #2 Phillips, M3/M4 Allen Keys\n- Velcro Strips (no zip ties/twist ties)\n- Standard Tool Kit, Black Ink Pens, Scotch Tape\n- Printed Register Labels (if provided)\n\n**General Daily Process & Smartsheet Requirements**\n\n- Check In/Out in Smartsheet **while onsite**.\n- Meet with Store MOD/Lead upon arrival.\n- Maintain professionalism with all store staff; assist in resolving reported issues.\n- Submit required photos daily in **Smartsheet Photo Form** and attach to Work Order.\n- **Deployment Support must release you before leaving site.**\n- **Obtain MOD/Lead sign-off prior to departure.**\n- **Call Pivital to confirm deliverables/photos before leaving site.**\n\n**Deployment Support Contact Information**\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Compliance & Penalties**\n\n- Deliverables, photos, cleanup, and timeliness are mandatory.\n- Expense Documentation: If materials, parking, or toll expenses are added to the Work Order, a valid receipt or invoice must be submitted for each individual expense. Expenses submitted without supporting documentation will not be approved.\n- Missing or incomplete deliverables may result in penalties or hours not approved.\n- Pay Change Requests are not accepted. Work reflects agreed rate + verified hours.\n- GPS check-in/out is required for onsite presence.\n- If GPS is disabled or shows offsite, proof of onsite work is required. Proof of onsite and offsite presence must be provided if GPS is disabled. Failure to have GPS enabled or offsite time entries will result in the additional time being logged to not be approved\n\n**Work Order Requirements**\n\n- Technicians must check in and out in Field Nation while onsite. No exceptions.\n- Do not log multiple site visits on this work order.\n- Each site visit will require its own work order.\n- If a revisit is needed, close out this work order and contact Pivital ASAP to notify that a revisit will be required.\n- Technicians must call and/or text Pivital upon arrival and departure.\n- All tasks and deliverables outlined in the Work Order must be fully completed.\n- Technicians must log time only for the duration physically onsite.\n- Time entries are verified by GPS.\n- Any issues encountered onsite must be reported to Pivital immediately.\n- Technicians must not mention Field Nation to store staff or customers..\n- All standard policies and procedures must be followed.\n- If there is a conflict between policies and the Service Description/Confidential Section, the Service Description/Confidential Section takes precedence.\n\n**Site Requirements**\n\n- Closing notes must be completed onsite.\n- Government-issued photo ID required for entry.\n- All technician names must be submitted in advance.\n- Check in with site contacts as a\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*representative.\n- Technicians must be fully equipped; no use of customer tools/equipment.\n- Business casual attire and professional conduct required.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-28T08:00","end":"2026-09-28T13:45"},"payRange":{"min":35,"max":201},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":35,"estLaborHours":5.75,"distance":44},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $201 (countered: $345) is below minimum threshold $350"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-18T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3