{"job":{"id":19873134,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Network Engineering Technologies","title":"ShopperTrak - Upgrade to Orbit AI devices –    Lids Locker Room - The Streets At Southpoint -     Technician should arrive onsit","description":{"html":"<p style=&quot;margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in&quot;><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px; font-family: Helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;>ShopperTrak - Upgrade to Orbit AI devices –&nbsp;</span><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>Lids Locker Room - The Streets At Southpoint -&nbsp;</span><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px; font-family: Helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;>&nbsp;Technician should arrive onsite at the time designated on the Work Order.&nbsp;</span>Do not discuss or comment on the Orbit AI technology with store managers.</p><p style=&quot;margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in&quot;><span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt; font-family: Helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>______________________________________________________________________________________</span><br><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>1) Login with NET Helpdesk 608-827-2271 option 3, and then follow the scope of\nwork and Orbit </span><span style=&quot;text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 14px;&quot;>AI</span><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;> or Video AI Installation\nGuide</span><br><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>TECH SHOULD BRING SMARTPHONE. Tech will need to send photos of installed Orbit(s) and back office equipment FROM SITE.</span><br><br><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>2) Locate the Equipment for replacement with NEW AI Devices. The replacement equipment is generally in the manager’s office or cash wrap area. Look for a white box from ShopperTrak. Bracket and screw are in a separate box taped to the box with the Orbit AI. If replacement equipment cannot be located STOP and immediately call NET.</span><br><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>Be sure to remove existing Orbit(s) and any ST600 or PoE devices unless otherwise directed by NET/ShopperTrak.</span><br><br><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>3) Tech to work with NET to replace Orbit 5 or 8 with Orbit AI device and call ShopperTrak to test. Orbit AI light should be pointing inside the store. Cabling should already be in place. Use existing port(s). Tech must also route the existing cable at the Orbit so that no cable is exposed. IF a GPU device is included with the ShopperTrak equipment, you'll need to install that using a patch cable in port 12. If port 12 is occupied, use port 13. See GPU Connections doc for reference.</span><br><br><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>4) If removing an Orbit 8 device, it will need to be boxed up for return using the ShopperTrak box with included return shipping label, packing slip, and tape. This ready to ship box should then be given to the store manager to return.</span><br><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>-Report to NET the contact information (Name and Phone #; Store number is acceptable) of who was given the equipment to return.</span></span></p><p style=&quot;margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in&quot;><span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt; font-family: Helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;><br></span></span></p><p style=&quot;margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in&quot;><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>Description: Shipped replacement equip Upgrade Orbit V or Orbit 8 to Orbit AI. No GPUs. One for One swap. Tech should be prepared to run cable if cable is bad. Have tech provide MOD with LOI</span></p><p style=&quot;margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in&quot;><br></p><p style=&quot;margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in&quot;><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>Pre-Cabled: No</span></p><p style=&quot;margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in&quot;><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;># of Orbits: 1</span></p><p style=&quot;margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in&quot;><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>Special Instructions: Mount on the white stripe in-line with the red box, angle bracket</span></p><p style=&quot;margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:7.5pt;margin-left:0in&quot;><span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt; font-family: Helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;><br><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>*Required Materials:**</span><br><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>Tech should bring patching compound to fill any holes left when mounting orbit/s.</span><br><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>**Cat5e or cat6 cable</span><br><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>Minimum 10ft ladder</span><br><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>Misc Cat5 materials: jacks, surface mount boxes, patch cords, etcetera…</span><br><br><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>*Required Tools:</span><br><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>Digital camera or smartphone</span><br><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>Cat5e/Cat6 tester</span><br><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>Butt set</span><br><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>Toner</span><br><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>Punch tool</span><br><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>Standard cabling tools</span><br><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>Standard hand tools and power tools</span><br><br><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>5) Photos needed:</span><br><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>1. Orbit/Video AI devices close up</span><br><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>2. Orbit/Video AI devices farther back to include the bottom of the doorway and mounted device</span><br><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>3. Back office switch/network area</span><br><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>4. Wide-shot showing the location of the GPU units (if applicable)</span><br><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>5. Photos of what was done before and after</span><br><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>6. Photo of the Serial Number/Mac Addresses address on new devices</span><br><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>7. Photo of the Serial Number/Mac Addresses of the old device(s)</span><br><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>8. Please be prepared to take additional photos that the NET support may ask for (situational)</span><br><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>9. Label the cable ends with the included red “ShopperTrak”, labels and submit photos.</span><br><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>Remove the lens covers.</span><br><br><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>6) Send pictures in ASAP, so NET has them when you are ready to log out.</span><br><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>Photos should be sent to dss@nettechnology.com with the work order number in square brackets [XXXXXX] in the subject line. To send photos to DSS please create a new email with the in the format shown. The To Line should be the dss email address and the subject should be the WO by itself with no other numbers symbols or text inside of square brackets. The WO number is the 7 digit ID for this assignment</span><br><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>To: dss@nettechnology.com</span><br><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>Subject: [WO#]</span><br><br><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>7) **Call ShopperTrak 1-312-529-5304 when ready to test. Hold times are to be expected please remain on the line.***You will need to provide the names of any and all ShopperTrak tech support that you talk to while onsite.</span><br><br><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>8) Logout with NET Helpdesk 608-827-2271 option 3, upon departure.&nbsp; Contact NET Project Manager at 608-827-7949 ext XXXX for out of scope changes or afterhours support. Be respectful to the store managers</span><br><span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;>.*FAILURE TO COMPLY WITH ANY PORTION OF THIS WORK ORDER WILL RESULT IN NON-PAYMENT</span></span></p>","markdown":"ShopperTrak - Upgrade to Orbit AI devices – Lids Locker Room - The Streets At Southpoint -  Technician should arrive onsite at the time designated on the Work Order. Do not discuss or comment on the Orbit AI technology with store managers.\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_  \n1\\) Login with NET Helpdesk 608-827-2271 option 3, and then follow the scope of work and Orbit AI or Video AI Installation Guide  \nTECH SHOULD BRING SMARTPHONE. Tech will need to send photos of installed Orbit(s) and back office equipment FROM SITE.  \n  \n2\\) Locate the Equipment for replacement with NEW AI Devices. The replacement equipment is generally in the manager’s office or cash wrap area. Look for a white box from ShopperTrak. Bracket and screw are in a separate box taped to the box with the Orbit AI. If replacement equipment cannot be located STOP and immediately call NET.  \nBe sure to remove existing Orbit(s) and any ST600 or PoE devices unless otherwise directed by NET/ShopperTrak.  \n  \n3\\) Tech to work with NET to replace Orbit 5 or 8 with Orbit AI device and call ShopperTrak to test. Orbit AI light should be pointing inside the store. Cabling should already be in place. Use existing port(s). Tech must also route the existing cable at the Orbit so that no cable is exposed. IF a GPU device is included with the ShopperTrak equipment, you'll need to install that using a patch cable in port 12. If port 12 is occupied, use port 13. See GPU Connections doc for reference.  \n  \n4\\) If removing an Orbit 8 device, it will need to be boxed up for return using the ShopperTrak box with included return shipping label, packing slip, and tape. This ready to ship box should then be given to the store manager to return.  \n-Report to NET the contact information (Name and Phone #; Store number is acceptable) of who was given the equipment to return.\n\nDescription: Shipped replacement equip Upgrade Orbit V or Orbit 8 to Orbit AI. No GPUs. One for One swap. Tech should be prepared to run cable if cable is bad. Have tech provide MOD with LOI\n\nPre-Cabled: No\n\n\\# of Orbits: 1\n\nSpecial Instructions: Mount on the white stripe in-line with the red box, angle bracket\n\n  \n\\*Required Materials:\\*\\*  \nTech should bring patching compound to fill any holes left when mounting orbit/s.  \n\\*\\*Cat5e or cat6 cable  \nMinimum 10ft ladder  \nMisc Cat5 materials: jacks, surface mount boxes, patch cords, etcetera…  \n  \n\\*Required Tools:  \nDigital camera or smartphone  \nCat5e/Cat6 tester  \nButt set  \nToner  \nPunch tool  \nStandard cabling tools  \nStandard hand tools and power tools  \n  \n5\\) Photos needed:  \n1\\. Orbit/Video AI devices close up  \n2\\. Orbit/Video AI devices farther back to include the bottom of the doorway and mounted device  \n3\\. Back office switch/network area  \n4\\. Wide-shot showing the location of the GPU units (if applicable)  \n5\\. Photos of what was done before and after  \n6\\. Photo of the Serial Number/Mac Addresses address on new devices  \n7\\. Photo of the Serial Number/Mac Addresses of the old device(s)  \n8\\. Please be prepared to take additional photos that the NET support may ask for (situational)  \n9\\. Label the cable ends with the included red “ShopperTrak”, labels and submit photos.  \nRemove the lens covers.  \n  \n6\\) Send pictures in ASAP, so NET has them when you are ready to log out.  \nPhotos should be sent to dss@nettechnology.com with the work order number in square brackets \\[XXXXXX\\] in the subject line. To send photos to DSS please create a new email with the in the format shown. The To Line should be the dss email address and the subject should be the WO by itself with no other numbers symbols or text inside of square brackets. The WO number is the 7 digit ID for this assignment  \nTo: dss@nettechnology.com  \nSubject: \\[WO#\\]  \n  \n7\\) \\*\\*Call ShopperTrak 1-312-529-5304 when ready to test. Hold times are to be expected please remain on the line.\\*\\*\\*You will need to provide the names of any and all ShopperTrak tech support that you talk to while onsite.  \n  \n8\\) Logout with NET Helpdesk 608-827-2271 option 3, upon departure. Contact NET Project Manager at 608-827-7949 ext XXXX for out of scope changes or afterhours support. Be respectful to the store managers  \n.\\*FAILURE TO COMPLY WITH ANY PORTION OF THIS WORK ORDER WILL RESULT IN NON-PAYMENT","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-03T14:30","end":"2026-09-03T15:30"},"payRange":{"min":120,"max":480},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":1,"amount":120},"additional":{"units":3,"amount":120}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":11},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 9/3/2026, 2:30:00 PM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-03T18:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-04T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-04T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-04T13:30:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-07T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-08T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Labor Day"},{"start":"2026-09-03T12:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-03T18:30:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-09-18T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"},{"start":"2026-09-11T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-11T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"SMALL BACKBOARD/ DATA REMOTE INSTALL/ MUST HAVE BUTT-SET/MULTIMETER-DIS148477"},{"start":"2026-09-10T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-10T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Maintenance Kit Swap - Apex, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-04T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-05T13:30:00.000Z","summary":"DSS 9223 - Install (1) QNAP + UPS + Switch, Install (3) TP-Link Wireless Bridge, Install (3) 8 Port PoE Switch, Replace (15) Analog Cameras w/ (15) IP Cameras + Cable Runs - Lead Tech"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789161988289}
{"job":{"id":19923918,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Core Technology Solutions","title":"Technician Needed - Install of a vertical mounted 55” TV","description":{"html":"<p>SITE SCOPE- ONE (1)PANEL INSTALLATION.</p><p>Main listed activities:</p><p>• Upon arrival the local technician will secure the inventory and transport from storage area to lobby</p><p>• Unbox and stage (at this time confirm power is available and live prior to installation)</p><p>• Mount bracket and TV in a vertical position per Customer provided installation guide</p><ul><li>Bottom of TV must be mounted between 39-41inches from floor</li></ul><p><br></p><p>o Note: each site may have a slight variance to height and location based on site floorplan. Local technician will have mounting components to accommodate masonry, wood, or metal stud attachments to support installation.</p><p>If for any reason there is concern for structure integrity of the chosen location an escalation path will be</p><p>created between remote, site, and Provider contacts to secure an alternate location at time of installation.</p><p>• After physical mounting the TV will be powered on and connected to local WIFI or wired connection where available</p><p>o WIFI passwords will be provided to onsite Technician</p><p>o Assumed WIFI is installed and validated working prior to onsite arrival</p><p>o Technician will change input to Magic Info and enter the server name for Magic Info as provided by Customer in the TV settings. - You are good when you get the magic screensaver</p><p>▪ Remote support will validate connection and software updates and media flow to device - client will push images themselves</p><p>• Remove all packaging and trash to local dumpster or recycling bin as instructed by site contact. Note, no hardware will be disposed</p><p>Customer has indicated that an installation runbook of instructions will be provided as developed from previous installations to Provider’s team to allow repeatable and consistent installations across all franchise locations</p><p><br></p><p><strong>TOOLS REQUIRED:</strong></p><p>• Valid photo ID</p><p>• Fully-charged smartphone</p><p>• Toolkit , Drill, Level, Stud finder , Wall anchors</p><p>• Any tools required to complete the scope above</p><p><br></p><p><strong>ADDITIONAL INFORMATION:</strong></p><p>• Deliverables must be attached to WO before leaving site</p><p>• Work order must be marked complete before leaving site</p>","markdown":"SITE SCOPE- ONE (1)PANEL INSTALLATION.\n\nMain listed activities:\n\n• Upon arrival the local technician will secure the inventory and transport from storage area to lobby\n\n• Unbox and stage (at this time confirm power is available and live prior to installation)\n\n• Mount bracket and TV in a vertical position per Customer provided installation guide\n\n- Bottom of TV must be mounted between 39-41inches from floor\n\no Note: each site may have a slight variance to height and location based on site floorplan. Local technician will have mounting components to accommodate masonry, wood, or metal stud attachments to support installation.\n\nIf for any reason there is concern for structure integrity of the chosen location an escalation path will be\n\ncreated between remote, site, and Provider contacts to secure an alternate location at time of installation.\n\n• After physical mounting the TV will be powered on and connected to local WIFI or wired connection where available\n\no WIFI passwords will be provided to onsite Technician\n\no Assumed WIFI is installed and validated working prior to onsite arrival\n\no Technician will change input to Magic Info and enter the server name for Magic Info as provided by Customer in the TV settings. - You are good when you get the magic screensaver\n\n▪ Remote support will validate connection and software updates and media flow to device - client will push images themselves\n\n• Remove all packaging and trash to local dumpster or recycling bin as instructed by site contact. Note, no hardware will be disposed\n\nCustomer has indicated that an installation runbook of instructions will be provided as developed from previous installations to Provider’s team to allow repeatable and consistent installations across all franchise locations\n\n**TOOLS REQUIRED:**\n\n• Valid photo ID\n\n• Fully-charged smartphone\n\n• Toolkit , Drill, Level, Stud finder , Wall anchors\n\n• Any tools required to complete the scope above\n\n**ADDITIONAL INFORMATION:**\n\n• Deliverables must be attached to WO before leaving site\n\n• Work order must be marked complete before leaving site","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-10T10:00","end":"2026-09-10T12:00","latestStart":"2026-09-10T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":150},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":100},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":15},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"TV\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-10T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-10T17:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-10T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-11T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-11T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-11T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-12T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-12T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-10T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-10T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-09-11T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-12T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-09-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-12T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-09-18T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.