{"job":{"id":19940421,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"StrikeCheck","title":"Express Damage Assessment - StrikeCheck Appointment A-2712746","description":{"html":"<p>*Please make sure to read through all instructions to avoid a second visit to the property and/or non-payment*</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The following items need to be <strong><em>documented</em></strong>, <strong><em>inspected</em></strong>, <strong><em>tested</em></strong> and <strong><em>photographed, even if they are found to be non-damaged</em></strong>:</p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(32, 33, 36);\"><b><ul><li>TV : Brand Unknown : 5</li><li>DVD Player : Brand Unknown : 1</li><li>Gaming Console : Brand Unknown : 3</li><li>Computer : Brand Unknown : 3</li><li>Monitor : Brand Unknown : 1</li><li>Speaker : Brand Unknown : 2</li><li>Audio System : Brand Unknown : 1</li><li>Soundbar : Brand Unknown : 1</li><li>Subwoofer : Brand Unknown : 1</li></ul></b></span></p><p><br></p><p><strong>ATTENTION: Every technician must use the CCG IQ Inspection Wizard to submit their findings. We cannot complete our payment to you if the findings are submitted to the Field Nation platform or via email. All findings, including non-damaged items on your list, must be sent directly to StrikeCheck using our CCG IQ Inspection Wizard via our Android app or web portal. If any item cannot be documented you must include a statement in your notes explaining those circumstances.</strong></p><p><strong>If you are unsure of how to use our Android app or web portal, or are having issues while you are onsite, please call (888) 980-8544 and a live representative will talk you through the submission process. Android users will need to download the \"CCG IQ Inspection Wizard\" in the app store on your device. Our office hours are 8am-8pm EST Monday-Friday and 8am-5pm on Saturdays. If no one is available to take your call please leave a message and we will return your call ASAP!</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>Testing and Documentation Requirements:</strong></p><ol><li>Full testing and documentation procedures on a per-item type basis can be found under the “Resources” tab in our web app. Select “StrikeCheck” in the “Libraries” folder to review the requirements before every inspection to ensure all required data is being captured.</li><li>Basic continuity/ohm testing is required using a digital multimeter. Verify a functional power source or outlet with your meter and document those readings. If needed, reset any associated circuit breakers but do not otherwise alter the electrical panel.&nbsp;</li><li>Apply power and operationally test ALL FUNCTIONS of every item. Notate any connected items (speakers to receiver, cameras to DVR, etc.) and advise if further testing is necessary due to the failure of one of those components (\"Can't test speakers due to damaged receiver\").&nbsp;</li><li>Document and photograph all obtainable readings/testing. <strong>If the item is not damaged or has already been replaced with new equipment, we still need the same amount of evidence (photos and test results) to support your findings.</strong> If the item is not operating properly, determine the causation of damage.&nbsp;</li><li>In addition to photos of the loss location and your meter readings, we require that you provide a minimum of 3 pictures per item. These pictures should illustrate where/how the item is installed, the overall condition of the item, any visual damages, and <strong><em>most importantly, </em></strong>the data plate. Also photograph any associated components connected to the item you are inspecting. Additional photographs and documentation are always encouraged.</li></ol><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Inspection Requirements:</strong></p><ul><li>A smart phone with access to our Android app or web app portal for Apple iOS users is the preferred method to document and upload your findings in real time. Access the app or portal before the inspection begins and it will walk you through all steps required for each item you enter.</li><li>Use of a camera and our Technician Worksheets is an alternate option that will require a computer to access the web app portal in order to upload photos as well as transcribing your detailed technical documentation from the worksheets into our system.</li><li>Multimeter/VOM and a basic toolkit</li><li>Must be professionally dressed (wear a clean collared shirt and pants; No shorts, no t-shirts, no flip-flops, and no ripped jeans). Avoid wearing anything that will identify your personal employer/company name or contact info to prevent insureds from calling you directly after you complete your assignment. This is an independent inspection on behalf of StrikeCheck, an insurance consulting company. <strong>You</strong> <strong>must represent yourself as being with StrikeCheck</strong> <strong>when you arrive onsite</strong>.</li><li>Must be willing to display contractor photo identification (if issued) and must have appropriate background and skills to perform the listed work order requirements</li><li>Must have passed a background check and drug test.&nbsp;</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Submission Requirements:</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>iPhone/iPad users: Upload required information via our <strong>web portal</strong> the same day as the inspection using a secure password. Click the \"Login\" link below or use this web address to access the portal:&nbsp;https://consolidatedclaims.my.site.com/ccginspector/&nbsp;</li><li>All findings, pictures, and determinations should be submitted on the same day as the inspection. <strong>Your deadline to submit is 24 hours from the scheduled appointment start time. Failure to do so may result in non-payment and could affect your rating.</strong></li><li>Your work order is not considered complete and payable until findings are submitted through the Android app or web portal and is approved by our Processing Department. Please make yourself available for follow-up calls if we have any questions regarding your findings.</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">Scheduling Requirements:</strong></p><ul><li>These work orders most likely take place in a residential property, and therefore requires the ETA to be approved by the client.</li><li>When you are assigned this work order, please submit an ETA as soon as possible.</li><li>We will reach out to the client to confirm that they are able to be onsite during your proposed ETA. <strong><u>The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.</u></strong></li><li>A project manager will message you via the Field Nation App when the ETA has been confirmed with the insured. If you go to the loss location before we confirm the appointment is set, you will not be afforded a trip fee in the event that the insured is not present when you arrive.</li><li><strong>You must update our project managers and dispatch coordinators regularly on work order progress, any service delays, or schedule conflicts. If you cannot make an appointment CALL OUR OFFICE IMMEDIATELY TO RESCHEDULE. Field Nation messages are not an accepted medium for rescheduling or canceling appointments!</strong></li><li>If you go to the property, but the client does not show for the appointment, call us immediately so we can follow up with the client and determine if they will be arriving soon. <strong>If the client misses the appointment, you must take a clear photo of the house/property, showing the address so we can confirm you were there.</strong></li><li>StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the insured cannot make the appointment.&nbsp;</li><li>StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the scope of work cannot be completed for any reason</li><li>StrikeCheck will <em>not </em>provide a trip fee if you arrive at an appointment that has <em>not </em>been confirmed with the client and the project manager. <strong><u>The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.</u></strong></li></ul>","markdown":"\\*Please make sure to read through all instructions to avoid a second visit to the property and/or non-payment\\*\n\nThe following items need to be ***documented***, ***inspected***, ***tested*** and ***photographed, even if they are found to be non-damaged***:\n\n**- TV : Brand Unknown : 5\n\\- DVD Player : Brand Unknown : 1\n\\- Gaming Console : Brand Unknown : 3\n\\- Computer : Brand Unknown : 3\n\\- Monitor : Brand Unknown : 1\n\\- Speaker : Brand Unknown : 2\n\\- Audio System : Brand Unknown : 1\n\\- Soundbar : Brand Unknown : 1\n\\- Subwoofer : Brand Unknown : 1**\n\n**ATTENTION: Every technician must use the CCG IQ Inspection Wizard to submit their findings. We cannot complete our payment to you if the findings are submitted to the Field Nation platform or via email. All findings, including non-damaged items on your list, must be sent directly to StrikeCheck using our CCG IQ Inspection Wizard via our Android app or web portal. If any item cannot be documented you must include a statement in your notes explaining those circumstances.**\n\n**If you are unsure of how to use our Android app or web portal, or are having issues while you are onsite, please call (888) 980-8544 and a live representative will talk you through the submission process. Android users will need to download the \"CCG IQ Inspection Wizard\" in the app store on your device. Our office hours are 8am-8pm EST Monday-Friday and 8am-5pm on Saturdays. If no one is available to take your call please leave a message and we will return your call ASAP!**\n\n**Testing and Documentation Requirements:**\n\n1. Full testing and documentation procedures on a per-item type basis can be found under the “Resources” tab in our web app. Select “StrikeCheck” in the “Libraries” folder to review the requirements before every inspection to ensure all required data is being captured.\n2. Basic continuity/ohm testing is required using a digital multimeter. Verify a functional power source or outlet with your meter and document those readings. If needed, reset any associated circuit breakers but do not otherwise alter the electrical panel.\n3. Apply power and operationally test ALL FUNCTIONS of every item. Notate any connected items (speakers to receiver, cameras to DVR, etc.) and advise if further testing is necessary due to the failure of one of those components (\"Can't test speakers due to damaged receiver\").\n4. Document and photograph all obtainable readings/testing. **If the item is not damaged or has already been replaced with new equipment, we still need the same amount of evidence (photos and test results) to support your findings.** If the item is not operating properly, determine the causation of damage.\n5. In addition to photos of the loss location and your meter readings, we require that you provide a minimum of 3 pictures per item. These pictures should illustrate where/how the item is installed, the overall condition of the item, any visual damages, and ***most importantly,*** the data plate. Also photograph any associated components connected to the item you are inspecting. Additional photographs and documentation are always encouraged.\n\n**Inspection Requirements:**\n\n- A smart phone with access to our Android app or web app portal for Apple iOS users is the preferred method to document and upload your findings in real time. Access the app or portal before the inspection begins and it will walk you through all steps required for each item you enter.\n- Use of a camera and our Technician Worksheets is an alternate option that will require a computer to access the web app portal in order to upload photos as well as transcribing your detailed technical documentation from the worksheets into our system.\n- Multimeter/VOM and a basic toolkit\n- Must be professionally dressed (wear a clean collared shirt and pants; No shorts, no t-shirts, no flip-flops, and no ripped jeans). Avoid wearing anything that will identify your personal employer/company name or contact info to prevent insureds from calling you directly after you complete your assignment. This is an independent inspection on behalf of StrikeCheck, an insurance consulting company. **You** **must represent yourself as being with StrikeCheck** **when you arrive onsite**.\n- Must be willing to display contractor photo identification (if issued) and must have appropriate background and skills to perform the listed work order requirements\n- Must have passed a background check and drug test.\n\n**Submission Requirements:**\n\n- iPhone/iPad users: Upload required information via our **web portal** the same day as the inspection using a secure password. Click the \"Login\" link below or use this web address to access the portal: <https://consolidatedclaims.my.site.com/ccginspector/&nbsp;>\n- All findings, pictures, and determinations should be submitted on the same day as the inspection. **Your deadline to submit is 24 hours from the scheduled appointment start time. Failure to do so may result in non-payment and could affect your rating.**\n- Your work order is not considered complete and payable until findings are submitted through the Android app or web portal and is approved by our Processing Department. Please make yourself available for follow-up calls if we have any questions regarding your findings.\n\n**Scheduling Requirements:**\n\n- These work orders most likely take place in a residential property, and therefore requires the ETA to be approved by the client.\n- When you are assigned this work order, please submit an ETA as soon as possible.\n- We will reach out to the client to confirm that they are able to be onsite during your proposed ETA. **The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.**\n- A project manager will message you via the Field Nation App when the ETA has been confirmed with the insured. If you go to the loss location before we confirm the appointment is set, you will not be afforded a trip fee in the event that the insured is not present when you arrive.\n- **You must update our project managers and dispatch coordinators regularly on work order progress, any service delays, or schedule conflicts. If you cannot make an appointment CALL OUR OFFICE IMMEDIATELY TO RESCHEDULE. Field Nation messages are not an accepted medium for rescheduling or canceling appointments!**\n- If you go to the property, but the client does not show for the appointment, call us immediately so we can follow up with the client and determine if they will be arriving soon. **If the client misses the appointment, you must take a clear photo of the house/property, showing the address so we can confirm you were there.**\n- StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the insured cannot make the appointment.\n- StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the scope of work cannot be completed for any reason\n- StrikeCheck will *not* provide a trip fee if you arrive at an appointment that has *not* been confirmed with the client and the project manager. **The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-11T08:00","end":"2026-09-11T10:00","latestStart":"2026-09-11T20:00"},"payRange":{"min":140,"max":140},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":58},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 9/11/2026, 8:00:00 AM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-11T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-11T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-12T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-12T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-15T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-11T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-12T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-09-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-12T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"},{"start":"2026-09-11T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-11T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"SMALL BACKBOARD/ DATA REMOTE INSTALL/ MUST HAVE BUTT-SET/MULTIMETER-DIS148477"},{"start":"2026-09-10T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-10T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Maintenance Kit Swap - Apex, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-04T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-05T13:30:00.000Z","summary":"DSS 9223 - Install (1) QNAP + UPS + Switch, Install (3) TP-Link Wireless Bridge, Install (3) 8 Port PoE Switch, Replace (15) Analog Cameras w/ (15) IP Cameras + Cable Runs - Lead Tech"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789163495588}
{"job":{"id":19940562,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Zayo Group","title":"Network Equipment and Cable Troubleshooting / Repair - Work with NOC","description":{"html":"<p><strong><em>NOTE: If travel/gas is required, it must be requested as a counter-offer BEFORE the ticket is assigned. Any requests made after ticket assignment may be denied.</em></strong></p><p><strong>DISPATCH OVERVIEW</strong></p><p>The objective of this dispatch is to perform onsite troubleshooting of the site’s WattBox, network equipment (CradlePoint and/or VeloCloud), and associated cabling. The technician is responsible for identifying and addressing the root cause of the issue in order to restore full network connectivity.</p><p>Please follow the troubleshooting steps outlined below in coordination with the NOC. The technician is expected to assist in diagnosing the issue and work with the NOC to confirm that connectivity has been successfully restored before leaving the site. Additional troubleshooting and/or repair steps may be requested by the NOC analyst during the dispatch, in addition to what is listed below.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>See \"Confidential Information\" section for device specific troubleshooting steps (if needed).</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Site Specific Information</strong></p><p>Ticket (INC) Reference Number (Number for tech to reference when calling into the NOC): INC1800465<br/><br/><br/>Equipment to Troubleshoot (make and model of equipment to ensure tech brings proper console cables if/when they are needed) and Port Assignments (if possible):<br/>Velocloud GE1<br/>Spectrum modem<br/><br/>ISP (Internet Service Provider) Name and Equipment (make/model):<br/>Spectrum modem<br/><br/>Special Tools and/or Materials Required (other than what is listed in the tech minimum tool list - if not needed, leave blank):<br/><br/><br/>Tracking Number of Equipment Sent To Site (If not available or needed, leave blank):<br/><br/><br/>Special Tech Instructions (access requirements, etc. - if not needed, leave blank):<br/>Passphrase: Harvest Panda<br/>Work order is for the DISTRICT OFFICE</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Site Check-In and Initial Activities</strong></p><p><strong>-1-</strong> Upon arrival, call and check in with the NOC to review and confirm the scope of work to be performed before beginning any tasks.</p><p>--- NOC Phone Number: <del>**************</del></p><p><strong>-2-</strong> Check in with the site contact or manager (refer to the custom field “Site Contact Name &amp; Number” for contact information)</p><p><strong>-3-</strong> Capture all required before pictures as outlined in the photo documentation list below.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Cable Inspection, Testing, and Replacement</strong></p><p>The technician shall perform inspections and testing on any necessary patch cords (between networking equipment) and/or demarcation extensions. All findings, including any cable replacements, must be relayed to the assigned NOC analyst.</p><p><strong>-1-</strong> Visually inspect all cabling between the network equipment. Document any issues (damaged cable or MOD ends, broken clips, etc.)</p><p><strong>-2-</strong> Test any suspect cables and document the results</p><p><strong>-3-</strong> Replace any faulty cables that are identified and confirm functionality with the NOC analyst</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Network Equipment Power Inspection</strong></p><p>The technician shall perform an initial power inspection of all onsite network equipment, including but not limited to routers, switches, Cradlepoints, VeloCloud devices, and ISP-provided modems.</p><p><strong>-1-</strong> Inspect all power outlets / strips for signs of failure or loose power cords</p><p><strong>-2-</strong> Inspect any UPSs (uninterrupted power supplies or battery back-ups) for any signs of failure or loose power cords</p><p><strong>-3-</strong> Check for tripped circuit breakers - switch back on if they have been tripped</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Device Reboots and Link (Status) Light Verification on Network Equipment</strong></p><p>The technician shall perform a controlled reboot on all network equipment in coordination with the NOC analyst.</p><p><strong>-1-</strong> Reboot network devices one at a time to minimize disruption as directed by the NOC (Do NOT reboot any equipment without NOC approval first)</p><p><strong>-2-</strong> Document any observed changes in network behavior and/or status light indicators during and after each reboot</p><p><strong>-3-</strong> Collaborate with the NOC analyst to identify any ports that should display a green (active/good) status indicator but instead show red (fault/bad) or no status light at all</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Connectivity Testing</strong></p><p>The technician shall perform connectivity testing as directed by the NOC once all other steps have been completed and devices confirmed up.</p><p><strong>-1-</strong> Attempt to access an external website (such as google.com, yahoo.com, etc.) and document results</p><p><strong>-2-</strong> Perform a speed test (using google or speedtest.net) and document results</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Site Wrap-Up and Check-Out</strong></p><p><strong>-1-</strong> Confirm with the site manager or designated site contact that all systems are functioning properly on their end and that services have been fully restored. Document confirmation in your closing notes.</p><p><strong>-2-</strong> Clean up the work area to ensure it is left in a neat and orderly condition. Gather all tools, equipment, and materials brought onsite before departing.</p><p><strong>-3-</strong> Take all required after pictures (see pictures list below)</p><p><strong>-4-</strong> Upload all pictures to this work order and/or email to the NOC analyst as requested (NOC Email if/when needed: <del>**************</del>)</p><p><strong>-5-</strong> Please fill in the \"Reason For Outage\" custom field with a brief description, such as power outage, UPS failure, etc.</p><p><strong>-6-</strong> Check-out and get released from site by the NOC analyst</p><p>--- NOC Phone Number: <del>**************</del></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>****************************************************************************************************************************************</p><p><strong>Technician Minimum Required Tools/Materials</strong></p><p><strong>-1-</strong> Network cable tester/toner</p><p><strong>-2-</strong> Laptop w/charger and various console cables</p><p><strong>-3-</strong> Full charged cell phone w/camera and mobile hotspot</p><p><strong>-4-</strong> Various console cables</p><p><strong>-5-</strong> Various length of patch cables (or the ability to make while onsite)</p><p><strong>-6-</strong> Box of Cat5 or Cat6 cable with a minimum of 300' (foot)</p><p><strong>-7-</strong> Spare RJ-45 keystone jacks and mod ends</p><p><strong>-8-</strong> Basic hand tools (screwdrivers, star/hex head drivers, wrenches, pliers, etc.)</p><p><strong>-9-</strong> Minimum 6’ A-Frame ladder</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>****************************************************************************************************************************************</p><p><strong>Technician Required Photos (Additional may be requested/required by the NOC analyst)</strong></p><p><strong>-1-</strong> Existing equipment (close up) / equipment location (wide angle of network area/room) prior to starting work</p><p><strong>-2-</strong> Existing equipment (close up) / equipment location (wide angle of network area/room) after work is completed</p><p><strong>-3-</strong> Capture any additional photographs as requested by the NOC analyst during the course of the work</p><p><br></p><p>****************************************************************************************************************************************</p><p><strong>Equipment Shipment Instructions (If Needed)</strong></p><p>The removed equipment must be prepared for return. In most cases, this will require dropping it off at the nearest UPS Store. If the site manager prefers to handle the return, the technician must provide the old equipment securely boxed with the return label attached.</p><p><strong>-1-</strong> Return shipping label will be included inside the package containing the new equipment</p><p><strong>-2-</strong> The removed equipment shall be packaged using the original box and packing materials from the newly delivered device</p><p><strong>-3-</strong> Affix the return shipping label to the box, ensuring the original shipping label is fully covered or obscured (e.g., by placing the new label directly over it or blacking it out with a permanent marker)</p><p><strong>-4-</strong> Capture clear photographs of the packaged equipment with the return label securely attached</p><p><strong>-5-</strong> The packaged equipment may either be dropped off at the nearest UPS location or left with the designated site manager/contact for return</p><p><strong>-6-</strong> Capture a clear photograph of the drop off receipt from UPS (or other carrier) and upload to confirm date/time package dropped for shipping</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>****************************************************************************************************************************************</p><p><strong>Tech Requirements and Expectations</strong></p><p><strong>-1-</strong> Technicians are expected to adhere to a business casual dress code, which includes pants without holes and closed-toe shoes. Shorts, tank tops, and sleeveless shirts are not permitted</p><p><strong>-2-</strong> The technician must arrive onsite with the minimum required tools and materials as outlined in the Tool/Material List</p><p><strong>-3-</strong> Please note that only one site visit can be processed per work order. If a revisit is required, a new work order will be issued. Do not return to a site without explicit authorization and a new active work order</p>","markdown":"***NOTE: If travel/gas is required, it must be requested as a counter-offer BEFORE the ticket is assigned. Any requests made after ticket assignment may be denied.***\n\n**DISPATCH OVERVIEW**\n\nThe objective of this dispatch is to perform onsite troubleshooting of the site’s WattBox, network equipment (CradlePoint and/or VeloCloud), and associated cabling. The technician is responsible for identifying and addressing the root cause of the issue in order to restore full network connectivity.\n\nPlease follow the troubleshooting steps outlined below in coordination with the NOC. The technician is expected to assist in diagnosing the issue and work with the NOC to confirm that connectivity has been successfully restored before leaving the site. Additional troubleshooting and/or repair steps may be requested by the NOC analyst during the dispatch, in addition to what is listed below.\n\nSee \"Confidential Information\" section for device specific troubleshooting steps (if needed).\n\n**Site Specific Information**\n\nTicket (INC) Reference Number (Number for tech to reference when calling into the NOC): INC1800465  \n  \n  \nEquipment to Troubleshoot (make and model of equipment to ensure tech brings proper console cables if/when they are needed) and Port Assignments (if possible):  \nVelocloud GE1  \nSpectrum modem  \n  \nISP (Internet Service Provider) Name and Equipment (make/model):  \nSpectrum modem  \n  \nSpecial Tools and/or Materials Required (other than what is listed in the tech minimum tool list - if not needed, leave blank):  \n  \n  \nTracking Number of Equipment Sent To Site (If not available or needed, leave blank):  \n  \n  \nSpecial Tech Instructions (access requirements, etc. - if not needed, leave blank):  \nPassphrase: Harvest Panda  \nWork order is for the DISTRICT OFFICE\n\n**Site Check-In and Initial Activities**\n\n**-1-** Upon arrival, call and check in with the NOC to review and confirm the scope of work to be performed before beginning any tasks.\n\n\\--- NOC Phone Number: \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**-2-** Check in with the site contact or manager (refer to the custom field “Site Contact Name & Number” for contact information)\n\n**-3-** Capture all required before pictures as outlined in the photo documentation list below.\n\n**Cable Inspection, Testing, and Replacement**\n\nThe technician shall perform inspections and testing on any necessary patch cords (between networking equipment) and/or demarcation extensions. All findings, including any cable replacements, must be relayed to the assigned NOC analyst.\n\n**-1-** Visually inspect all cabling between the network equipment. Document any issues (damaged cable or MOD ends, broken clips, etc.)\n\n**-2-** Test any suspect cables and document the results\n\n**-3-** Replace any faulty cables that are identified and confirm functionality with the NOC analyst\n\n**Network Equipment Power Inspection**\n\nThe technician shall perform an initial power inspection of all onsite network equipment, including but not limited to routers, switches, Cradlepoints, VeloCloud devices, and ISP-provided modems.\n\n**-1-** Inspect all power outlets / strips for signs of failure or loose power cords\n\n**-2-** Inspect any UPSs (uninterrupted power supplies or battery back-ups) for any signs of failure or loose power cords\n\n**-3-** Check for tripped circuit breakers - switch back on if they have been tripped\n\n**Device Reboots and Link (Status) Light Verification on Network Equipment**\n\nThe technician shall perform a controlled reboot on all network equipment in coordination with the NOC analyst.\n\n**-1-** Reboot network devices one at a time to minimize disruption as directed by the NOC (Do NOT reboot any equipment without NOC approval first)\n\n**-2-** Document any observed changes in network behavior and/or status light indicators during and after each reboot\n\n**-3-** Collaborate with the NOC analyst to identify any ports that should display a green (active/good) status indicator but instead show red (fault/bad) or no status light at all\n\n**Connectivity Testing**\n\nThe technician shall perform connectivity testing as directed by the NOC once all other steps have been completed and devices confirmed up.\n\n**-1-** Attempt to access an external website (such as google.com, yahoo.com, etc.) and document results\n\n**-2-** Perform a speed test (using google or speedtest.net) and document results\n\n**Site Wrap-Up and Check-Out**\n\n**-1-** Confirm with the site manager or designated site contact that all systems are functioning properly on their end and that services have been fully restored. Document confirmation in your closing notes.\n\n**-2-** Clean up the work area to ensure it is left in a neat and orderly condition. Gather all tools, equipment, and materials brought onsite before departing.\n\n**-3-** Take all required after pictures (see pictures list below)\n\n**-4-** Upload all pictures to this work order and/or email to the NOC analyst as requested (NOC Email if/when needed: \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*)\n\n**-5-** Please fill in the \"Reason For Outage\" custom field with a brief description, such as power outage, UPS failure, etc.\n\n**-6-** Check-out and get released from site by the NOC analyst\n\n\\--- NOC Phone Number: \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Technician Minimum Required Tools/Materials**\n\n**-1-** Network cable tester/toner\n\n**-2-** Laptop w/charger and various console cables\n\n**-3-** Full charged cell phone w/camera and mobile hotspot\n\n**-4-** Various console cables\n\n**-5-** Various length of patch cables (or the ability to make while onsite)\n\n**-6-** Box of Cat5 or Cat6 cable with a minimum of 300' (foot)\n\n**-7-** Spare RJ-45 keystone jacks and mod ends\n\n**-8-** Basic hand tools (screwdrivers, star/hex head drivers, wrenches, pliers, etc.)\n\n**-9-** Minimum 6’ A-Frame ladder\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Technician Required Photos (Additional may be requested/required by the NOC analyst)**\n\n**-1-** Existing equipment (close up) / equipment location (wide angle of network area/room) prior to starting work\n\n**-2-** Existing equipment (close up) / equipment location (wide angle of network area/room) after work is completed\n\n**-3-** Capture any additional photographs as requested by the NOC analyst during the course of the work\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Equipment Shipment Instructions (If Needed)**\n\nThe removed equipment must be prepared for return. In most cases, this will require dropping it off at the nearest UPS Store. If the site manager prefers to handle the return, the technician must provide the old equipment securely boxed with the return label attached.\n\n**-1-** Return shipping label will be included inside the package containing the new equipment\n\n**-2-** The removed equipment shall be packaged using the original box and packing materials from the newly delivered device\n\n**-3-** Affix the return shipping label to the box, ensuring the original shipping label is fully covered or obscured (e.g., by placing the new label directly over it or blacking it out with a permanent marker)\n\n**-4-** Capture clear photographs of the packaged equipment with the return label securely attached\n\n**-5-** The packaged equipment may either be dropped off at the nearest UPS location or left with the designated site manager/contact for return\n\n**-6-** Capture a clear photograph of the drop off receipt from UPS (or other carrier) and upload to confirm date/time package dropped for shipping\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Tech Requirements and Expectations**\n\n**-1-** Technicians are expected to adhere to a business casual dress code, which includes pants without holes and closed-toe shoes. Shorts, tank tops, and sleeveless shirts are not permitted\n\n**-2-** The technician must arrive onsite with the minimum required tools and materials as outlined in the Tool/Material List\n\n**-3-** Please note that only one site visit can be processed per work order. If a revisit is required, a new work order will be issued. Do not return to a site without explicit authorization and a new active work order","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-15T10:00","end":"2026-09-15T11:00","latestStart":"2026-09-15T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":85,"max":145},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":1,"amount":85},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":60}},"hourlyRate":0,"es