{"job":{"id":19944932,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Spencer Technologies","title":"Primo® Brands - WB1F Raleigh, NC Camera Installation - Assist","description":{"html":"For all technical troubleshooting or field support needs, call the Field Tech Support Team at 508.321.4060 for live assistance and guidance.<br/>For non-technical issues including site access, scheduling, store readiness, or scope clarification outside of technical execution, contact your assigned Project Team directly.<br/>Do not mark yourself as “Arrived” until you have physically entered and checked in at the client site.<br/><br/>SOW: <br/>Check in and out with Spencer APM Sam Marion 508-744-9634<br/><br/>Tech must be prepared with:<br/>PPE (Hard hat, safety glasses, gloves & vests)<br/>Label maker and labels!<br/><br/>DS/Primo IT contacts (if needed): <br/>   - Senthil Kumar Gangadharan 602-245-2238  <br/>   - David Hollis 727-418-4650 <br/>   - Robert Chambers 203-509-6467<br/>   - Rod Waldrop (770)937-7318<br/>   - Serhii Aladov 514-956-2615<br/>Onsite contact:<br/>  - Kristina Smith Region Coordinator<br/>503-803-5823<br/>   - Ray Anonuevo District Ops manager  <br/>661-445-9180<br/>   - Darrell Bowie District Ops manager<br/>910-689-4061<br/><br/><br/>Site Specific Details:<br/>Rough-In, Terminate, and Test (6) CAT6 Cables for Cameras<br/>Install (6) Cameras<br/>Test & Adjust FOV for Cameras<br/><br/>Here are the results of the camera installation survey:<br/>1.           Interior Office / Corridor Camera<br/>a.            Location: General Manager and main hallway junction area.<br/>b.            Scope: Install one interior vandal-resistant turret camera on the ceiling/wall junction. Run CAT6 cable through drop ceilings/walls back to the central network rack.<br/>c.             Estimated Cable Length: 75 ft.<br/><br/>2.            Front Elevation – Upper Roofline<br/>a.             Location: Upper right corner of the main office front facade.<br/>b.            Scope: Install an exterior bullet camera with wide-angle coverage for the front parking/approach area. Run exterior-rated CAT6 cable, utilizing conduit where exposed along the exterior wall.<br/>c.             Estimated Cable Length: 120 ft.<br/><br/>3.            Front Elevation – Main Entrance<br/>a.             Location: Directly above the primary office entrance doors and windows.<br/>b.            Scope: Install a low-profile dome/turret camera for visitor identification and entry monitoring. Seal all wall penetrations with weatherproof silicone.<br/>c.             Estimated Cable Length: 90 ft.<br/><br/>4.            Loading Dock Elevation – Upper Perimeter<br/>a.             Location: Upper section of the right-side loading dock elevation.<br/>b.            Scope: Install a high-resolution security bullet camera to monitor the upper exterior yard and roofline approach. Run CAT6 cable through protective outdoor conduit.<br/>c.             Estimated Cable Length: 150 ft.<br/><br/>5.            Loading Dock Elevation – Bay Doors<br/>a.             Location: Centered above the active loading dock bay doors.<br/>b.            Scope: Install a varifocal bullet camera optimized for tracking loading activity, trailers, and personnel movement around the docks.<br/>c.             Estimated Cable Length: 140 ft.<br/><br/>6.            Loading Dock Elevation – Lower Corner<br/>a.             Location: Lower left corner / side yard area of the loading dock elevation.<br/>b.            Scope: Install an exterior-rated bullet camera to cover the blind spot near the building corner and egress paths.<br/>c.             Estimated Cable Length: 160 ft.<br/><br/><br/>Deliverables:<br/>- Before & after pictures of all work done<br/>- Summary of work completed, including site times<br/><br/>Send deliverables to primowater@spencertech.com BEFORE leaving site.<br/><br/>Check out with APM Sam Marion 508-744-9634<br/><br/>**Technician may need to provide materials to complete scope of work. Reimbursement will be made after work complete.","markdown":"For all technical troubleshooting or field support needs, call the Field Tech Support Team at 508.321.4060 for live assistance and guidance.  \nFor non-technical issues including site access, scheduling, store readiness, or scope clarification outside of technical execution, contact your assigned Project Team directly.  \nDo not mark yourself as “Arrived” until you have physically entered and checked in at the client site.  \n  \nSOW:   \nCheck in and out with Spencer APM Sam Marion 508-744-9634  \n  \nTech must be prepared with:  \nPPE (Hard hat, safety glasses, gloves & vests)  \nLabel maker and labels!  \n  \nDS/Primo IT contacts (if needed):   \n\\- Senthil Kumar Gangadharan 602-245-2238   \n\\- David Hollis 727-418-4650   \n\\- Robert Chambers 203-509-6467  \n\\- Rod Waldrop (770)937-7318  \n\\- Serhii Aladov 514-956-2615  \nOnsite contact:  \n\\- Kristina Smith Region Coordinator  \n503-803-5823  \n\\- Ray Anonuevo District Ops manager   \n661-445-9180  \n\\- Darrell Bowie District Ops manager  \n910-689-4061  \n  \n  \nSite Specific Details:  \nRough-In, Terminate, and Test (6) CAT6 Cables for Cameras  \nInstall (6) Cameras  \nTest & Adjust FOV for Cameras  \n  \nHere are the results of the camera installation survey:  \n1\\. Interior Office / Corridor Camera  \na. Location: General Manager and main hallway junction area.  \nb. Scope: Install one interior vandal-resistant turret camera on the ceiling/wall junction. Run CAT6 cable through drop ceilings/walls back to the central network rack.  \nc. Estimated Cable Length: 75 ft.  \n  \n2\\. Front Elevation – Upper Roofline  \na. Location: Upper right corner of the main office front facade.  \nb. Scope: Install an exterior bullet camera with wide-angle coverage for the front parking/approach area. Run exterior-rated CAT6 cable, utilizing conduit where exposed along the exterior wall.  \nc. Estimated Cable Length: 120 ft.  \n  \n3\\. Front Elevation – Main Entrance  \na. Location: Directly above the primary office entrance doors and windows.  \nb. Scope: Install a low-profile dome/turret camera for visitor identification and entry monitoring. Seal all wall penetrations with weatherproof silicone.  \nc. Estimated Cable Length: 90 ft.  \n  \n4\\. Loading Dock Elevation – Upper Perimeter  \na. Location: Upper section of the right-side loading dock elevation.  \nb. Scope: Install a high-resolution security bullet camera to monitor the upper exterior yard and roofline approach. Run CAT6 cable through protective outdoor conduit.  \nc. Estimated Cable Length: 150 ft.  \n  \n5\\. Loading Dock Elevation – Bay Doors  \na. Location: Centered above the active loading dock bay doors.  \nb. Scope: Install a varifocal bullet camera optimized for tracking loading activity, trailers, and personnel movement around the docks.  \nc. Estimated Cable Length: 140 ft.  \n  \n6\\. Loading Dock Elevation – Lower Corner  \na. Location: Lower left corner / side yard area of the loading dock elevation.  \nb. Scope: Install an exterior-rated bullet camera to cover the blind spot near the building corner and egress paths.  \nc. Estimated Cable Length: 160 ft.  \n  \n  \nDeliverables:  \n\\- Before & after pictures of all work done  \n\\- Summary of work completed, including site times  \n  \nSend deliverables to primowater@spencertech.com BEFORE leaving site.  \n  \nCheck out with APM Sam Marion 508-744-9634  \n  \n\\*\\*Technician may need to provide materials to complete scope of work. Reimbursement will be made after work complete.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-23T09:00","end":"2026-09-23T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":480},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":60,"estLaborHours":8,"distance":11},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":60,"baseAmount":480,"estHours":8,"travelExpense":30,"payStructure":null},"reason":"TRAVEL_REQUIRED","rejectDetails":"Travel required (11mi reported + 10mi padding = 21mi > 20mi)"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"},{"start":"2026-09-11T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-11T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"SMALL BACKBOARD/ DATA REMOTE INSTALL/ MUST HAVE BUTT-SET/MULTIMETER-DIS148477"},{"start":"2026-09-10T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-10T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Maintenance Kit Swap - Apex, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-04T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-05T13:30:00.000Z","summary":"DSS 9223 - Install (1) QNAP + UPS + Switch, Install (3) TP-Link Wireless Bridge, Install (3) 8 Port PoE Switch, Replace (15) Analog Cameras w/ (15) IP Cameras + Cable Runs - Lead Tech"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1789384671896}
{"job":{"id":19944931,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Spencer Technologies","title":"Primo® Brands - WB1F Raleigh, NC Camera Installation - Lead","description":{"html":"For all technical troubleshooting or field support needs, call the Field Tech Support Team at 508.321.4060 for live assistance and guidance.<br/>For non-technical issues including site access, scheduling, store readiness, or scope clarification outside of technical execution, contact your assigned Project Team directly.<br/>Do not mark yourself as “Arrived” until you have physically entered and checked in at the client site.<br/><br/>SOW: <br/>Check in and out with Spencer APM Sam Marion 508-744-9634<br/><br/>Tech must be prepared with:<br/>PPE (Hard hat, safety glasses, gloves & vests)<br/>Label maker and labels!<br/><br/>DS/Primo IT contacts (if needed): <br/>   - Senthil Kumar Gangadharan 602-245-2238  <br/>   - David Hollis 727-418-4650 <br/>   - Robert Chambers 203-509-6467<br/>   - Rod Waldrop (770)937-7318<br/>   - Serhii Aladov 514-956-2615<br/>Onsite contact:<br/>  - Kristina Smith Region Coordinator<br/>503-803-5823<br/>   - Ray Anonuevo District Ops manager  <br/>661-445-9180<br/>   - Darrell Bowie District Ops manager<br/>910-689-4061<br/><br/><br/>Site Specific Details:<br/>Rough-In, Terminate, and Test (6) CAT6 Cables for Cameras<br/>Install (6) Cameras<br/>Test & Adjust FOV for Cameras<br/><br/>Here are the results of the camera installation survey:<br/>1.           Interior Office / Corridor Camera<br/>a.            Location: General Manager and main hallway junction area.<br/>b.            Scope: Install one interior vandal-resistant turret camera on the ceiling/wall junction. Run CAT6 cable through drop ceilings/walls back to the central network rack.<br/>c.             Estimated Cable Length: 75 ft.<br/><br/>2.            Front Elevation – Upper Roofline<br/>a.             Location: Upper right corner of the main office front facade.<br/>b.            Scope: Install an exterior bullet camera with wide-angle coverage for the front parking/approach area. Run exterior-rated CAT6 cable, utilizing conduit where exposed along the exterior wall.<br/>c.             Estimated Cable Length: 120 ft.<br/><br/>3.            Front Elevation – Main Entrance<br/>a.             Location: Directly above the primary office entrance doors and windows.<br/>b.            Scope: Install a low-profile dome/turret camera for visitor identification and entry monitoring. Seal all wall penetrations with weatherproof silicone.<br/>c.             Estimated Cable Length: 90 ft.<br/><br/>4.            Loading Dock Elevation – Upper Perimeter<br/>a.             Location: Upper section of the right-side loading dock elevation.<br/>b.            Scope: Install a high-resolution security bullet camera to monitor the upper exterior yard and roofline approach. Run CAT6 cable through protective outdoor conduit.<br/>c.             Estimated Cable Length: 150 ft.<br/><br/>5.            Loading Dock Elevation – Bay Doors<br/>a.             Location: Centered above the active loading dock bay doors.<br/>b.            Scope: Install a varifocal bullet camera optimized for tracking loading activity, trailers, and personnel movement around the docks.<br/>c.             Estimated Cable Length: 140 ft.<br/><br/>6.            Loading Dock Elevation – Lower Corner<br/>a.             Location: Lower left corner / side yard area of the loading dock elevation.<br/>b.            Scope: Install an exterior-rated bullet camera to cover the blind spot near the building corner and egress paths.<br/>c.             Estimated Cable Length: 160 ft.<br/><br/><br/>Deliverables:<br/>- Before & after pictures of all work done<br/>- Summary of work completed, including site times<br/><br/>Send deliverables to primowater@spencertech.com BEFORE leaving site.<br/><br/>Check out with APM Sam Marion 508-744-9634<br/><br/>**Technician may need to provide materials to complete scope of work. Reimbursement will be made after work complete.","markdown":"For all technical troubleshooting or field support needs, call the Field Tech Support Team at 508.321.4060 for live assistance and guidance.  \nFor non-technical issues including site access, scheduling, store readiness, or scope clarification outside of technical execution, contact your assigned Project Team directly.  \nDo not mark yourself as “Arrived” until you have physically entered and checked in at the client site.  \n  \nSOW:   \nCheck in and out with Spencer APM Sam Marion 508-744-9634  \n  \nTech must be prepared with:  \nPPE (Hard hat, safety glasses, gloves & vests)  \nLabel maker and labels!  \n  \nDS/Primo IT contacts (if needed):   \n\\- Senthil Kumar Gangadharan 602-245-2238   \n\\- David Hollis 727-418-4650   \n\\- Robert Chambers 203-509-6467  \n\\- Rod Waldrop (770)937-7318  \n\\- Serhii Aladov 514-956-2615  \nOnsite contact:  \n\\- Kristina Smith Region Coordinator  \n503-803-5823  \n\\- Ray Anonuevo District Ops manager   \n661-445-9180  \n\\- Darrell Bowie District Ops manager  \n910-689-4061  \n  \n  \nSite Specific Details:  \nRough-In, Terminate, and Test (6) CAT6 Cables for Cameras  \nInstall (6) Cameras  \nTest & Adjust FOV for Cameras  \n  \nHere are the results of the camera installation survey:  \n1\\. Interior Office / Corridor Camera  \na. Location: General Manager and main hallway junction area.  \nb. Scope: Install one interior vandal-resistant turret camera on the ceiling/wall junction. Run CAT6 cable through drop ceilings/walls back to the central network rack.  \nc. Estimated Cable Length: 75 ft.  \n  \n2\\. Front Elevation – Upper Roofline  \na. Location: Upper right corner of the main office front facade.  \nb. Scope: Install an exterior bullet camera with wide-angle coverage for the front parking/approach area. Run exterior-rated CAT6 cable, utilizing conduit where exposed along the exterior wall.  \nc. Estimated Cable Length: 120 ft.  \n  \n3\\. Front Elevation – Main Entrance  \na. Location: Directly above the primary office entrance doors and windows.  \nb. Scope: Install a low-profile dome/turret camera for visitor identification and entry monitoring. Seal all wall penetrations with weatherproof silicone.  \nc. Estimated Cable Length: 90 ft.  \n  \n4\\. Loading Dock Elevation – Upper Perimeter  \na. Location: Upper section of the right-side loading dock elevation.  \nb. Scope: Install a high-resolution security bullet camera to monitor the upper exterior yard and roofline approach. Run CAT6 cable through protective outdoor conduit.  \nc. Estimated Cable Length: 150 ft.  \n  \n5\\. Loading Dock Elevation – Bay Doors  \na. Location: Centered above the active loading dock bay doors.  \nb. Scope: Install a varifocal bullet camera optimized for tracking loading activity, trailers, and personnel movement around the docks.  \nc. Estimated Cable Length: 140 ft.  \n  \n6\\. Loading Dock Elevation – Lower Corner  \na. Location: Lower left corner / side yard area of the loading dock elevation.  \nb. Scope: Install an exterior-rated bullet camera to cover the blind spot near the building corner and egress paths.  \nc. Estimated Cable Length: 160 ft.  \n  \n  \nDeliverables:  \n\\- Before & after pictures of all work done  \n\\- Summary of work completed, including site times  \n  \nSend deliverables to primowater@spencertech.com BEFORE leaving site.  \n  \nCheck out with APM Sam Marion 508-744-9634  \n  \n\\*\\*Technician may need to provide materials to complete scope of work. Reimbursement will be made after work complete.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-23T09:00","end":"2026-09-23T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":480},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":60,"estLaborHours":8,"distance":11},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":60,"baseAmount":480,"estHours":8,"travelExpense":30,"payStructure":null},"reason":"TRAVEL_REQUIRED","rejectDetai