{"job":{"id":19944652,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"PNC - Network Upgrade - Low Voltage Technician (LVT)","description":{"html":"<p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><u>IMPORTANT:</u></strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> REVIEW ALL EQUIPMENT LISTED IN THIS SCOPE,&nbsp;IN ITS ENTIRETY BEFORE REQUESTING THIS WORK ORDER!</span></p><p><strong>Low Voltage Technician</strong></p><p>WWT has been contracted to assist in the deployment of new standardized network stacks at PNC Bank facilities in North America. The overall solution includes two separated processes: (a) LVV and (b) the Installation Cut-Over.&nbsp;&nbsp;The first process includes (i) updating network cabling, (ii) a new wall-mount cabinet and backer board, (iii) terminating new cabling, (iv) moving cabling from an existing patch panel over to new patch panel, (v) clean up, and (vi) deliverables.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>You are part of a 3-person team, with 1 lead and 2 technicians.&nbsp;Each LVV site will be 3 nights (approx. 4pm to 2am).&nbsp;&nbsp;Perform low voltage technician work in accordance with onsite lead technician, PMO direction, and the Deployment Guide.</strong></p><p>Technicians must have demonstrated knowledge, skills, and abilities in the activities outlined above.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;This is not just a cabling or a rack and stack project, the <strong>technician must have direct experience in terminating CAT6a cables, moving cables from an existing patch panel to a new patch panel, and complex cabling.</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><strong> Technicians will be selected with the following criteria:</strong></p><ul><li>Demonstrated work experience in your FN work history (including cabling, termination, patch panel relocation)</li><li>Field Nation score specifically timeliness, back-out ranking, and marketplace score.</li><li>Availability of working all sites on the route (could be up to 6 months)</li><li>Ability to work with other technicians.</li><li>Distance from sites (no travel provided).</li></ul><p><strong>Technician Expectations:</strong></p><ul><li>Attend required training.</li><li>On the bridge at all times.</li><li>Have reliable transportation.</li><li>Have the required tools identified in the Run-Book/Deployment Guide.</li><li>Follow the directions from the bridge and</li></ul><p><strong>A fixed rate is a fixed rate, WE DO NOT accept counter offers, and WE DO NOT allow substitutions.</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><u>Technician's Required Toolkit</u></strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Technicians are </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">REQUIRED</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> to have in their possession and be familiar with the safe and proper</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">use of each of the following tools</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> PRIOR TO ARRIVING ON SITE</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">:</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;Smartphone (with charger and battery pack)</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Download and install the current </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Microsoft Teams</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> application</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Download, install and login to the </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">TrueContext</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> application</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Working camera/smartphone (deliverables) </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">with charger</strong></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Cellular hotspot (optional)</span></li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Tech tools, equipment, and supplies</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">8' Step Ladder</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Hook and Loop (\"Velcro\") strips / roll (for cable management)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Zip ties, black (NOT for cable management)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Packing Tape (to seal box for unused parts/legacy gear)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Philips screwdrivers (#0, #1, and #2 tips)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Slotted screwdriver</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Other screwdrivers (various sizes) (optional)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Cordless drill with various bits</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Needle nose pliers / dykes</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Scissors</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Label printer (such as Brady, Brother or Dymo)</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">with ~1/2 (12mm) white tape (black print)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Mechanic gloves/latex gloves</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">(to prevent handprints when touching ceiling tiles)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Wired/wireless headset</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Box cutter</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Telescoping magnetic pickup</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Tape measure (12' minimum)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Socket set(s)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Screw extractor kit</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Torpedo level (wall brackets)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Head Lamp (optional)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Cat 6a cable tools/crimper with</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">PASSTHROUGH Cat 6a RJ-45 connectors</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Ethernet Cable tester (both continuity and tone tracing tools)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Fish tape or cable pull string (to get cables through millwork)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Crossover cable &ndash; Specifically required; techs were reminded to bring one, and pink patch cables in PNC branches were identified as crossover cables</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Rollover cable &ndash; Explicitly called out alongside crossover cables as required inventory</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">RJ45 crossover adapter (male&ndash;female red adapterPNC - LVT Template Update: ) &ndash; Mentioned as a small adapter that comes with switches/routers and should be available if included in care packs</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Power over Ethernet (PoE) switch &ndash; Required to power access points during testing and wipe activities</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">PoE injector &ndash; Identified as an alternative if a PoE switch is not available</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Windows laptop computer &ndash; Required software including PuTTY</span></li></ul><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">﻿</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Lead Technician per-site equipment and supplies</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">2' x 4' fire-rated plywood for wall cabinet backer board</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Mounting hardware such as</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">2\" wood screws for mounting on wood studs</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">3/16\" or 1/4\" toggle bolts or \"zip-its\" for mounting the board on a hollow wall</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Masonry screw kit for mounting on block walls</span></li></ul>","markdown":"**IMPORTANT:** REVIEW ALL EQUIPMENT LISTED IN THIS SCOPE, IN ITS ENTIRETY BEFORE REQUESTING THIS WORK ORDER!\n\n**Low Voltage Technician**\n\nWWT has been contracted to assist in the deployment of new standardized network stacks at PNC Bank facilities in North America. The overall solution includes two separated processes: (a) LVV and (b) the Installation Cut-Over. The first process includes (i) updating network cabling, (ii) a new wall-mount cabinet and backer board, (iii) terminating new cabling, (iv) moving cabling from an existing patch panel over to new patch panel, (v) clean up, and (vi) deliverables.\n\n**You are part of a 3-person team, with 1 lead and 2 technicians. Each LVV site will be 3 nights (approx. 4pm to 2am). Perform low voltage technician work in accordance with onsite lead technician, PMO direction, and the Deployment Guide.**\n\nTechnicians must have demonstrated knowledge, skills, and abilities in the activities outlined above. This is not just a cabling or a rack and stack project, the **technician must have direct experience in terminating CAT6a cables, moving cables from an existing patch panel to a new patch panel, and complex cabling.**\n\n **Technicians will be selected with the following criteria:**\n\n- Demonstrated work experience in your FN work history (including cabling, termination, patch panel relocation)\n- Field Nation score specifically timeliness, back-out ranking, and marketplace score.\n- Availability of working all sites on the route (could be up to 6 months)\n- Ability to work with other technicians.\n- Distance from sites (no travel provided).\n\n**Technician Expectations:**\n\n- Attend required training.\n- On the bridge at all times.\n- Have reliable transportation.\n- Have the required tools identified in the Run-Book/Deployment Guide.\n- Follow the directions from the bridge and\n\n**A fixed rate is a fixed rate, WE DO NOT accept counter offers, and WE DO NOT allow substitutions.**\n\n**Technician's Required Toolkit**\n\nTechnicians are **REQUIRED** to have in their possession and be familiar with the safe and proper\n\nuse of each of the following tools **PRIOR TO ARRIVING ON SITE**:\n\n **Smartphone (with charger and battery pack)**\n\n- Download and install the current **Microsoft Teams** application\n- Download, install and login to the **TrueContext** application\n- Working camera/smartphone (deliverables) **with charger**\n- Cellular hotspot (optional)\n\n**Tech tools, equipment, and supplies**\n\n- 8' Step Ladder\n- Hook and Loop (\"Velcro\") strips / roll (for cable management)\n- Zip ties, black (NOT for cable management)\n- Packing Tape (to seal box for unused parts/legacy gear)\n- Philips screwdrivers (#0, #1, and #2 tips)\n- Slotted screwdriver\n- Other screwdrivers (various sizes) (optional)\n- Cordless drill with various bits\n- Needle nose pliers / dykes\n- Scissors\n- Label printer (such as Brady, Brother or Dymo)\n- with ~1/2 (12mm) white tape (black print)\n- Mechanic gloves/latex gloves\n- (to prevent handprints when touching ceiling tiles)\n- Wired/wireless headset\n- Box cutter\n- Telescoping magnetic pickup\n- Tape measure (12' minimum)\n- Socket set(s)\n- Screw extractor kit\n- Torpedo level (wall brackets)\n- Head Lamp (optional)\n- Cat 6a cable tools/crimper with\n- PASSTHROUGH Cat 6a RJ-45 connectors\n- Ethernet Cable tester (both continuity and tone tracing tools)\n- Fish tape or cable pull string (to get cables through millwork)\n- Crossover cable – Specifically required; techs were reminded to bring one, and pink patch cables in PNC branches were identified as crossover cables\n- Rollover cable – Explicitly called out alongside crossover cables as required inventory\n- RJ45 crossover adapter (male–female red adapterPNC - LVT Template Update: ) – Mentioned as a small adapter that comes with switches/routers and should be available if included in care packs\n- Power over Ethernet (PoE) switch – Required to power access points during testing and wipe activities\n- PoE injector – Identified as an alternative if a PoE switch is not available\n- Windows laptop computer – Required software including PuTTY\n\n﻿\n\n **Lead Technician per-site equipment and supplies**\n\n- 2' x 4' fire-rated plywood for wall cabinet backer board\n- Mounting hardware such as\n- 2\" wood screws for mounting on wood studs\n- 3/16\" or 1/4\" toggle bolts or \"zip-its\" for mounting the board on a hollow wall\n- Masonry screw kit for mounting on block walls","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-29T16:30","end":"2026-09-29T26:30"},"payRange":{"min":500,"max":500},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":10,"distance":8},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"fixed","counterRate":60,"baseAmount":600,"estHours":10,"travelExpense":0,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":0}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"},{"start":"2026-09-11T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-11T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"SMALL BACKBOARD/ DATA REMOTE INSTALL/ MUST HAVE BUTT-SET/MULTIMETER-DIS148477"},{"start":"2026-09-10T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-10T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Maintenance Kit Swap - Apex, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-04T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-05T13:30:00.000Z","summary":"DSS 9223 - Install (1) QNAP + UPS + Switch, Install (3) TP-Link Wireless Bridge, Install (3) 8 Port PoE Switch, Replace (15) Analog Cameras w/ (15) IP Cameras + Cable Runs - Lead Tech"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1789384705293}
