{"job":{"id":19944135,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"DataLink Group Inc","title":"PRE RUNS Low Voltage | Installing Devices","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Read all instructions below before applying. Do not accept this call if you do not have the necessary tools, equipment, or skill set to install the cabling and devices.</strong></p><p><strong>Technician Requirements:</strong></p><ul><li>PPE (Personal Protective Equipment)</li><li>Basic cable tools</li><li>110 punch down tool</li><li>8-foot ladder</li><li>Brother P-Touch labeler with cable wrap capability</li></ul><p><em><u>This site work includes a total of </u></em><strong><em><u>03 CAT6A cable runs, terminations</u></em></strong><em><u> and </u></em><strong><em><u>AP devices</u></em></strong><em><u>. </u></em></p><p><u>Due to restricted site access, the workday begins at 07:45 and ends at 17:45 each day.</u></p><p><strong>*No running cables*</strong></p><p><strong>*No running cables*</strong></p><p><strong>*No running cables*</strong></p><p><strong>*No running cables*</strong></p><p><strong>*No running cables*</strong></p><p><strong><span class=\"ql-cursor\">﻿</span>*No running cables*</strong></p><p>This site has three (3) existing pre-run CAT6A cables. Scope includes installation of three (3) access point (AP) devices.</p><p><strong><u>Carefully read and follow all instructions below for cable installation.</u></strong></p><p><strong>Scope of work:</strong></p><ol><li>Meet with the POC and conduct a site walkthrough to verify the accuracy of the prints. Immediately report any discrepancies. Take photos of any visible damage to ceiling tiles, walls, or other areas. Any new damages identified will be the responsibility of the installers for repair.</li><li>Verify material count and complete inventory by cross-referencing the provided order sheet for accuracy. Report any shortages</li><li>Label the APs according to the naming convention in the OSAR Excel sheet. For each AP, enter the corresponding MAC address into the Excel sheet. Plug the AP into the switch temporary and record the switch port number for that AP. Juniper APs can't be stacked on each other*. Be aware that the POC may either handle the AP connection themselves or permit you to do it. Submit the completed Excel sheet within 1-2 hours while still on site. In addition, ensure that the biscuit jacks, patch cables, and patch panel are also properly labeled according to the specified conventions.</li><li>Run cables to the designated locations, referencing the provided site prints for accuracy.</li><li>Terminate cables, conduct cable testing, and hang APs**.</li></ol><p>*Juniper Access Points (APs) should not be physically stacked. Stacking can cause signal interference, limit airflow, and lead to overheating, negatively impacting performance and device longevity. Ensure proper spacing for adequate ventilation and optimal wireless coverage.</p><p><strong>**</strong>Wait for the \"ready to hang\" confirmation before disconnecting the AP from the switch and proceeding to mount it.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>The technician must follow these instructions precisely to successfully complete the work.</strong></p><p><strong>Daily Report</strong></p><p>If you have multiple days to complete work at this site, you must submit a daily report. Below is the required format. The number inside the parentheses indicates the work completed that day, while the number on the left shows the cumulative total. Update the cumulative total daily.</p><p><strong>DAILY REPORT FORMAT</strong></p><p>APs Mounted – 0 (0) of 00</p><p>Cables Pulled – 0 (0) of 00</p><p>AP Swaps – 0 (0) of 00</p><p>Cables Tested – 0 (0) of 00</p><p>APs Plugged In – 0 (0) of 00</p><p>Number of Penetrations – (0)</p><p>Channel Adapters Installed – (0)</p><p>Angle Brackets Installed – (0)</p><p>Quantity of Cable Installers Onsite – 00</p><p><strong>Comments / Issues / Installation Notes</strong></p><p>On-Site:</p><p>Off-Site:</p><p><br></p><p><strong><em><u>Labeling is crucial (see specific requirements below). All labeling and naming requirements for cables and AP devices at this site are outlined in the OSAR.</u></em></strong></p><strong>Labeling Requirements:</strong><ul><li><strong>APs and Biscuit Jacks:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Label APs and biscuit jacks using the AP Label section in the OSAR Excel sheet.</li><li><strong>Patch Cables:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Patch Cables:</strong> Label both ends using the AP Label section in the OSAR.</li><li><strong>Patch Panel Labeling:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Tape Size:</strong> 12mm</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Font Size:</strong> Auto</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Label Type:</strong> Patch Panel</li><li><strong>AP Labeling:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Tape Size:</strong> 12mm</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Font Size:</strong> Auto</li><li><strong>Biscuit Labeling:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Tape Size:</strong> 12mm</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Font Size:</strong> 18</li><li><strong>Cable Labeling:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Tape Size:</strong> 12mm</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Font Size:</strong> Auto</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Label Type:</strong> Cable wrap</li></ul><p><br></p><strong>Photos are Critical and Required for This Site: </strong><ul><li><strong>AP Photos (Ground Level):</strong> Capture each AP from the ground, ensuring the label and green light are clearly visible.</li><li><strong>AP Photos (Above Ceiling):</strong> Take photos of each AP above the ceiling, showing the J-hook, cable, and biscuit jack labels.</li><li><strong>Patch Panel Photos:</strong> Ensure to take clear photos of the front and back of each patch panel, with all labels visible.</li><li><strong>Switch Photos:</strong> Photograph each switch, focusing on the labeled patched cables (only for switches worked on, not every switch in the room).</li><li><strong>Cable Pathway Photos:</strong> Take clear photos of the entire cable pathway, ensuring all J-hooks, supports, and cable routing are documented.</li></ul><br><strong>Cabling and Installation Standards: </strong><ul><li>Install cabling according to site and industry standards.</li><li><strong>Do not use tie-wraps</strong> for cable management. <strong>Only Velcro must be used</strong>.</li></ul><strong>AP Installation Requirements:</strong><ul><li>APs must be installed at least 12 inches away from walls.</li><li>Maintain a minimum distance of 24 inches between APs and lights, sprinkler heads, or other ceiling devices.</li><li>Install bat-wing J-hooks above each AP for a service loop.</li><li>Ensure service loops do not exceed 5 feet of slack.</li></ul><strong>Fire-Stop Requirements:</strong><ul><li>All new penetrations must be properly fire-stopped.</li><li>Re-fire stop any existing penetrations that are used.</li></ul><strong>Ceiling Tile and Cable Management:</strong><ul><li>Notch ceiling tiles to lay flat with no visible cables or notches.</li><li>Ensure no exposed or visible cabling around the AP.</li></ul><strong>AP Mounting Brackets:</strong><ul><li>Tighten the set screw on AP mounting brackets to prevent sliding on the grid.</li></ul><p><br></p><strong>Cable Test:</strong><ol><li><strong>Power On</strong>: Turn on the Fluke tester.</li><li><strong>Attach Adapters</strong>: Connect the appropriate adapters (Channel) to both the main and remote units.</li><li><strong>Connect the Cable</strong>: Plug the Ethernet cable into both the main and remote units.</li><li><strong>Name the Cable ID</strong>: Input the cable ID(from the OSAR) into the Fluke tester.</li><li><strong>Select Test Standard</strong>: Choose the correct cable type (CAT6a) and standard (TIA)</li><li><strong>Start the Test</strong>: Press the <strong>Test</strong> button to initiate diagnostics.</li><li><strong>Review Results</strong>: Check if the test passes or fails and review details on the screen.</li><li><strong>Save Results</strong>: Save the test results for documentation.</li><li><strong>Troubleshoot</strong>: If the test fails, use the provided details to fix issues.</li><li><strong>Turn Off and Store</strong>: Power off the tester and store it properly.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><em><u>All materials and equipment are provided and available on-site.</u></em></p><p><strong><u><del>**** ********* *********</del></u></strong></p><p><del>***** *** ****** ****</del></p><p><del>**** ***** ***** **</del></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>**** ***** ***** **</del></span></p><p><del>****** ***** *******</del></p><p><del>***** ** ***** **** ****</del></p><p><del>***** ** ***** **** ****</del></p><p><del>***** ***** ****** *******</del></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>***** ***** ****** *******</del>A CH PANEL, 12-PORTAT6A PATCH PANEL, 12-</span></p><p><del>**** ****** ***** ****</del></p><p><del>**** **** ******* ***** * *************</del></p><p><del>****** **** **** ***** ***</del></p>","markdown":"**Read all instructions below before applying. Do not accept this call if you do not have the necessary tools, equipment, or skill set to install the cabling and devices.**\n\n**Technician Requirements:**\n\n- PPE (Personal Protective Equipment)\n- Basic cable tools\n- 110 punch down tool\n- 8-foot ladder\n- Brother P-Touch labeler with cable wrap capability\n\n*This site work includes a total of* ***03 CAT6A cable runs, terminations*** *and* ***AP devices****.*\n\nDue to restricted site access, the workday begins at 07:45 and ends at 17:45 each day.\n\n**\\*No running cables\\***\n\n**\\*No running cables\\***\n\n**\\*No running cables\\***\n\n**\\*No running cables\\***\n\n**\\*No running cables\\***\n\n**﻿\\*No running cables\\***\n\nThis site has three (3) existing pre-run CAT6A cables. Scope includes installation of three (3) access point (AP) devices.\n\n**Carefully read and follow all instructions below for cable installation.**\n\n**Scope of work:**\n\n1. Meet with the POC and conduct a site walkthrough to verify the accuracy of the prints. Immediately report any discrepancies. Take photos of any visible damage to ceiling tiles, walls, or other areas. Any new damages identified will be the responsibility of the installers for repair.\n2. Verify material count and complete inventory by cross-referencing the provided order sheet for accuracy. Report any shortages\n3. Label the APs according to the naming convention in the OSAR Excel sheet. For each AP, enter the corresponding MAC address into the Excel sheet. Plug the AP into the switch temporary and record the switch port number for that AP. Juniper APs can't be stacked on each other\\*. Be aware that the POC may either handle the AP connection themselves or permit you to do it. Submit the completed Excel sheet within 1-2 hours while still on site. In addition, ensure that the biscuit jacks, patch cables, and patch panel are also properly labeled according to the specified conventions.\n4. Run cables to the designated locations, referencing the provided site prints for accuracy.\n5. Terminate cables, conduct cable testing, and hang APs\\*\\*.\n\n\\*Juniper Access Points (APs) should not be physically stacked. Stacking can cause signal interference, limit airflow, and lead to overheating, negatively impacting performance and device longevity. Ensure proper spacing for adequate ventilation and optimal wireless coverage.\n\n**\\*\\***Wait for the \"ready to hang\" confirmation before disconnecting the AP from the switch and proceeding to mount it.\n\n**The technician must follow these instructions precisely to successfully complete the work.**\n\n**Daily Report**\n\nIf you have multiple days to complete work at this site, you must submit a daily report. Below is the required format. The number inside the parentheses indicates the work completed that day, while the number on the left shows the cumulative total. Update the cumulative total daily.\n\n**DAILY REPORT FORMAT**\n\nAPs Mounted – 0 (0) of 00\n\nCables Pulled – 0 (0) of 00\n\nAP Swaps – 0 (0) of 00\n\nCables Tested – 0 (0) of 00\n\nAPs Plugged In – 0 (0) of 00\n\nNumber of Penetrations – (0)\n\nChannel Adapters Installed – (0)\n\nAngle Brackets Installed – (0)\n\nQuantity of Cable Installers Onsite – 00\n\n**Comments / Issues / Installation Notes**\n\nOn-Site:\n\nOff-Site:\n\n***Labeling is crucial (see specific requirements below). All labeling and naming requirements for cables and AP devices at this site are outlined in the OSAR.***\n\n**Labeling Requirements:**- **APs and Biscuit Jacks:**\n- Label APs and biscuit jacks using the AP Label section in the OSAR Excel sheet.\n- **Patch Cables:**\n- **Patch Cables:** Label both ends using the AP Label section in the OSAR.\n- **Patch Panel Labeling:**\n- **Tape Size:** 12mm\n- **Font Size:** Auto\n- **Label Type:** Patch Panel\n- **AP Labeling:**\n- **Tape Size:** 12mm\n- **Font Size:** Auto\n- **Biscuit Labeling:**\n- **Tape Size:** 12mm\n- **Font Size:** 18\n- **Cable Labeling:**\n- **Tape Size:** 12mm\n- **Font Size:** Auto\n- **Label Type:** Cable wrap\n\n**Photos are Critical and Required for This Site:** - **AP Photos (Ground Level):** Capture each AP from the ground, ensuring the label and green light are clearly visible.\n- **AP Photos (Above Ceiling):** Take photos of each AP above the ceiling, showing the J-hook, cable, and biscuit jack labels.\n- **Patch Panel Photos:** Ensure to take clear photos of the front and back of each patch panel, with all labels visible.\n- **Switch Photos:** Photograph each switch, focusing on the labeled patched cables (only for switches worked on, not every switch in the room).\n- **Cable Pathway Photos:** Take clear photos of the entire cable pathway, ensuring all J-hooks, supports, and cable routing are documented.\n\n  \n**Cabling and Installation Standards:** - Install cabling according to site and industry standards.\n- **Do not use tie-wraps** for cable management. **Only Velcro must be used**.\n\n**AP Installation Requirements:**- APs must be installed at least 12 inches away from walls.\n- Maintain a minimum distance of 24 inches between APs and lights, sprinkler heads, or other ceiling devices.\n- Install bat-wing J-hooks above each AP for a service loop.\n- Ensure service loops do not exceed 5 feet of slack.\n\n**Fire-Stop Requirements:**- All new penetrations must be properly fire-stopped.\n- Re-fire stop any existing penetrations that are used.\n\n**Ceiling Tile and Cable Management:**- Notch ceiling tiles to lay flat with no visible cables or notches.\n- Ensure no exposed or visible cabling around the AP.\n\n**AP Mounting Brackets:**- Tighten the set screw on AP mounting brackets to prevent sliding on the grid.\n\n**Cable Test:**1. **Power On**: Turn on the Fluke tester.\n2. **Attach Adapters**: Connect the appropriate adapters (Channel) to both the main and remote units.\n3. **Connect the Cable**: Plug the Ethernet cable into both the main and remote units.\n4. **Name the Cable ID**: Input the cable ID(from the OSAR) into the Fluke tester.\n5. **Select Test Standard**: Choose the correct cable type (CAT6a) and standard (TIA)\n6. **Start the Test**: Press the **Test** button to initiate diagnostics.\n7. **Review Results**: Check if the test passes or fails and review details on the screen.\n8. **Save Results**: Save the test results for documentation.\n9. **Troubleshoot**: If the test fails, use the provided details to fix issues.\n10. **Turn Off and Store**: Power off the tester and store it properly.\n\n*All materials and equipment are provided and available on-site.*\n\n**\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*A CH PANEL, 12-PORTAT6A PATCH PANEL, 12-\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-21T07:45","end":"2026-09-21T14:45"},"payRange":{"min":250,"max":250},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":7,"distance":13},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $250 is below minimum threshold $350"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"},{"start":"2026-09-11T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-11T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"SMALL BACKBOARD/ DATA REMOTE INSTALL/ MUST HAVE BUTT-SET/MULTIMETER-DIS148477"},{"start":"2026-09-10T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-10T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Maintenance Kit Swap - Apex, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-04T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-05T13:30:00.000Z","summary":"DSS 9223 - Install (1) QNAP + UPS + Switch, Install (3) TP-Link Wireless Bridge, Install (3) 8 Port PoE Switch, Replace (15) Analog Cameras w/ (15) IP Cameras + Cable Runs - Lead Tech"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789384752501}
{"job":{"id":19944122,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"PNC - Network Upgrade - Workstation Technician (WRK)","description":{"html":"<p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">IMPORTANT:</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> REVIEW ALL EQUIPMENT LISTED IN THIS SCOPE, IN ITS ENTIRETY BEFORE REQUESTING THIS WORK ORDER!</span></p><ul><li><strong>As part of the PNC Branch Refresh / Unification project, WWT</strong> has been contracted to assist in the deployment of several <strong>Workstation(s). </strong> This process includes the replacement and installation of PCs, power up and test, cable management at the device (as good or better than original configuration), de-installation and staging of legacy equipment, cleanup of trash/debris and submission of deliverable photographs/documentation.</li><li>A 1 hour training is required prior to your first workstation project. Although you only have to take this training once, it is recommended to have a refresher if you have not performed this installation in several months.</li><li>You will be required to use both the <strong>Deployment Guide</strong> (attached to this Work Order) for each deployment and accomplishment of As-Built / Deliverable documentation.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">(Not implemented yet) This project requires the use of the <strong>True Context (TC) </strong>application (Google/Apple store). The <strong>TC </strong>application will require the creation of an account via the WWT Project team.</li></ul><p><strong>Tools/materials required:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0); --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-ee0000, #ff2525);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Printed Deployment Guide</strong></li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0); --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-ee0000, #ff2525);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Printed Acceptance Test Plan / Site Acceptance Acknowledgement form </strong><strong>(requires liquid signatures)</strong></li><li><strong>Current U.S. Photo ID</strong></li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0); --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-ee0000, #ff2525);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Printed Letter of Authorization</strong></li><li><strong>Smartphone </strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0); --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-ee0000, #ff2525);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">(with charger)</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Download and install the current <strong>Microsoft Teams</strong> application</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Download install and login to the <strong>TrueContext</strong> application</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Working</strong> camera/smartphone (deliverables) <strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0); --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-ee0000, #ff2525);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">with charger</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Cellular hotspot</strong></li><li><strong>Tech tools, equipment, and supplies</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Hook and Loop (\"Velcro\") strips / roll (for cable management)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">3/16\" or 1/8\" toggle bolts or \"zip-its\" (for wall mount devices)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Zip ties, black</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Packing Tape (to seal box for unused parts/legacy gear)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">P0 and P1 screwdrivers</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Slotted screwdriver</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Cat 6 cable tools/crimper with Cat 6 RJ-45 connectors</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Ethernet Cable tester (both continuity and tone tracing tools)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Other screwdrivers (various sizes) (optional)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Cordless drill with various bits</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Needle nose pliers / dykes</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Scissors</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Fish tape or cable pull string (to get cables through millwork)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Label printer (such as Brady, Brother or Dymo) with ~1/2 (12mm) white tape (black print)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Mechanic gloves/latex gloves (to prevent handprints when installing phones)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Wired/wireless headset</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Box cutter</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Telescoping magnetic pickup</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tape measure (6' minimum) (wall brackets)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Socket set(s)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Screw extractor kit</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Torpedo level (wall brackets)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Head Lamp (optional)</li><li>Work orders will be paid <strong>within 5 working days</strong>.</li></ul><p><strong>Parking Reimbursement Policy</strong></p><ul><li>Parking costs will only be reimbursed if proof is provided.</li><li><strong>Proof must be uploaded and saved to the Work Order (WO) when the WO is marked \"Complete.\"</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Acceptable proof includes:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Clear picture of the parking receipt (or digital receipt).</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Receipt must show date, time, amount, and location.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Parking costs submitted after the WO is paid will not be reimbursed.</strong></li></ul><p><br></p>","markdown":"**IMPORTANT:** REVIEW ALL EQUIPMENT LISTED IN THIS SCOPE, IN ITS ENTIRETY BEFORE REQUESTING THIS WORK ORDER!\n\n- **As part of the PNC Branch Refresh / Unification project, WWT** has been contracted to assist in the deployment of several **Workstation(s).**  This process includes the replacement and installation of PCs, power up and test, cable management at the device (as good or better than original configuration), de-installation and staging of legacy equipment, cleanup of trash/debris and submission of deliverable photographs/documentation.\n- A 1 hour training is required prior to your first workstation project. Although you only have to take this training once, it is recommended to have a refresher if you have not performed this installation in several months.\n- You will be required to use both the **Deployment Guide** (attached to this Work Order) for each deployment and accomplishment of As-Built / Deliverable documentation.\n- (Not implemented yet) This project requires the use of the **True Context (TC)** application (Google/Apple store). The **TC** application will require the creation of an account via the WWT Project team.\n\n**Tools/materials required:**\n\n- **Printed Deployment Guide**\n- **Printed Acceptance Test Plan / Site Acceptance Acknowledgement form** **(requires liquid signatures)**\n- **Current U.S. Photo ID**\n- **Printed Letter of Authorization**\n- **Smartphone** **(with charger)**\n- Download and install the current **Microsoft Teams** application\n- Download install and login to the **TrueContext** application\n- **Working** camera/smartphone (deliverables) **with charger**\n- **Cellular hotspot**\n- **Tech tools, equipment, and supplies**\n- Hook and Loop (\"Velcro\") strips / roll (for cable management)\n- 3/16\" or 1/8\" toggle bolts or \"zip-its\" (for wall mount devices)\n- Zip ties, black\n- Packing Tape (to seal box for unused parts/legacy gear)\n- P0 and P1 screwdrivers\n- Slotted screwdriver\n- Cat 6 cable tools/crimper with Cat 6 RJ-45 connectors\n- Ethernet Cable tester (both continuity and tone tracing tools)\n- Other screwdrivers (various sizes) (optional)\n- Cordless drill with various bits\n- Needle nose pliers / dykes\n- Scissors\n- Fish tape or cable pull string (to get cables through millwork)\n- Label printer (such as Brady, Brother or Dymo) with ~1/2 (12mm) white tape (black print)\n- Mechanic gloves/latex gloves (to prevent handprints when installing phones)\n- Wired/wireless headset\n- Box cutter\n- Telescoping magnetic pickup\n- Tape measure (6' minimum) (wall brackets)\n- Socket set(s)\n- Screw extractor kit\n- Torpedo level (wall brackets)\n- Head Lamp (optional)\n- Work orders will be paid **within 5 working days**.\n\n**Parking Reimbursement Policy**\n\n- Parking costs will only be reimbursed if proof is provided.\n- **Proof must be uploaded and saved to the Work Order (WO) when the WO is marked \"Complete.\"**\n- Acceptable proof includes:\n- Clear picture of the parking receipt (or digital receipt).\n- Receipt must show date, time, amount, and location.\n- **Parking costs submitted after the WO is paid will not be reimbursed.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-30T09:30","end":"2026-09-30T14:30"},"payRange":{"min":250,"max":250},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":5,"distance":6},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $250 is below minimum threshold $350"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"},{"start":"2026-09-11T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-11T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"SMALL BACKBOARD/ DATA REMOTE INSTALL/ MUST HAVE BUTT-SET/MULTIMETER-DIS148477"},{"start":"2026-09-10T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-10T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Maintenance Kit Swap - Apex, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-04T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-05T13:30:00.000Z","summary":"DSS 9223 - Install (1) QNAP + UPS + Switch, Install (3) TP-Link Wireless Bridge, Install (3) 8 Port PoE Switch, Replace (15) Analog Cameras w/ (15) IP Cameras + Cable Runs - Lead Tech"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789384758734}
{"job":{"id":19944042,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"PNC - Network Upgrade - Delivery Receipt","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Pre Installation and Delivery Technician</u></strong></p><p>WWT has been contracted to assist in the deployment of new standardized network stacks at PNC Bank facilities in North America. The overall solution includes two separated processes: (a) LVV and (b) the Installation Cut-Over.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>There is a material delivery that takes place on the day of installation.</p><p><strong><u>Please be onsite the entire time of the visit, due to multiple deliveries.</u></strong></p><p>You are required to be onsite from 1pm to 4pm to supervise any delivery, document what was delivered, and take pictures of the existing network room.</p><p><strong><u>There will NOT be a bridge, instead we will have to answer some questions in Field Nation.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Be onsite for the delivery and collect basic information from the site.</strong> Including detailed photos of the network room.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>IMPORTANT / CRITICAL: NO NETWORK OUTAGES ARE ALLOWED. </strong></p><p>DO NOT touch the rack or step on any cables. Do not move cables, this is just a picture survey</p><p><strong><u>Technicians Expectations:</u></strong></p><ul><li>·Photos of completed delivery showing all boxes neatly stacked</li><li>MIN of 8<strong> WIDE ANGLE pictures </strong>of the network room, showing walls, plugs, and network rack. Go to 4 corners and take pictures toward the rack, and 4 pictures from the rack to the walls showing ceiling to floor. If this cannot be accomplished, please take multiple pictures.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Upload these picture to this work order.</strong></p><p><strong>A fixed rate is a fixed rate, we do not accept counteroffers, and we do not allow substitutions.</strong></p>","markdown":"**Pre Installation and Delivery Technician**\n\nWWT has been contracted to assist in the deployment of new standardized network stacks at PNC Bank facilities in North America. The overall solution includes two separated processes: (a) LVV and (b) the Installation Cut-Over.\n\nThere is a material delivery that takes place on the day of installation.\n\n**Please be onsite the entire time of the visit, due to multiple deliveries.**\n\nYou are required to be onsite from 1pm to 4pm to supervise any delivery, document what was delivered, and take pictures of the existing network room.\n\n**There will NOT be a bridge, instead we will have to answer some questions in Field Nation.**\n\n**Be onsite for the delivery and collect basic information from the site.** Including detailed photos of the network room.\n\n**IMPORTANT / CRITICAL: NO NETWORK OUTAGES ARE ALLOWED.**\n\nDO NOT touch the rack or step on any cables. Do not move cables, this is just a picture survey\n\n**Technicians Expectations:**\n\n- ·Photos of completed delivery showing all boxes neatly stacked\n- MIN of 8 **WIDE ANGLE pictures** of the network room, showing walls, plugs, and network rack. Go to 4 corners and take pictures toward the rack, and 4 pictures from the rack to the walls showing ceiling to floor. If this cannot be accomplished, please take multiple pictures.\n\n**Upload these picture to this work order.**\n\n**A fixed rate is a fixed rate, we do not accept counteroffers, and we do not allow substitutions.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00","end":"2026-09-28T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":150,"max":150},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":6},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $150 is below minimum threshold $350"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"},{"start":"2026-09-11T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-11T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"SMALL BACKBOARD/ DATA REMOTE INSTALL/ MUST HAVE BUTT-SET/MULTIMETER-DIS148477"},{"start":"2026-09-10T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-10T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Maintenance Kit Swap - Apex, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-04T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-05T13:30:00.000Z","summary":"DSS 9223 - Install (1) QNAP + UPS + Switch, Install (3) TP-Link Wireless Bridge, Install (3) 8 Port PoE Switch, Replace (15) Analog Cameras w/ (15) IP Cameras + Cable Runs - Lead Tech"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789384764858}
{"job":{"id":19943972,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"PNC - Network Upgrade - Installation Technician (INT)","description":{"html":"<p><strong style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\"><u>IMPORTANT:</u></strong><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\"> REVIEW ALL EQUIPMENT LISTED IN THIS SCOPE,&nbsp;IN ITS ENTIRETY BEFORE REQUESTING THIS WORK ORDER!</span></p><p><strong>Installation Technician (INT):</strong></p><p>WWT has been contracted to assist in the deployment of new standardized network stacks at PNC Bank facilities in North America.</p><p><strong>There are two parts to the installation</strong>; the pre-work (LVV) and the installation of the active devices that connect to the LVV infrastructure. This connection occurs during the installation/cut-over phase (this work order) or the second part (the Installation).</p><p><strong>The LVV includes; </strong>(i) a new network cabinet and back board, (ii) new cabling for access points, (iii) a UXI sensor, (iv) security devices (if in scope), and ((v) moving the existing cables from the existing rack to the new wall mount rack.</p><p><strong>The INT: Installation Technician: the second part (this work order) includes; </strong>(i) installation of a new network stack (in a rolling cabinet), (ii) installation and configuration of new end devices (AP's &amp; UXI), (iii) installation of new workstations, (iv) the migration of the old routers and circuits, (v) decommissioning of the old equipment, (vi) connection of new security devices, (vii) removal of the old rack, and (viii) clean up, deliverables, and site checkout.</p><p>Your responsibility is to assist the Lead in the activities associated with the attached deployment guide and to report to the bridge any abnormalities associated with these activities.</p><p><strong>This is NOT a basic technician job. </strong>Technicians are expected to bring to site the tools and equipment identified in the Run-Book/Deployment Guide and possess advanced termination and troubleshooting skills.</p><p>Perform network upgrade in accordance with PMO direction, the Deployment Guide.</p><p><strong style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\"><u>Technician's Required Toolkit</u></strong></p><p><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Technicians are </span><strong style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">REQUIRED</strong><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\"> to have in their possession and be familiar with the safe and proper</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">use of each of the following tools</span><strong style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\"> PRIOR TO ARRIVING ON SITE</strong><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">:</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">&nbsp;Smartphone (with charger and battery pack)</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Download and install the current </span><strong style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Microsoft Teams</strong><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\"> application</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Download, install and login to the </span><strong style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">TrueContext</strong><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\"> application</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Working camera/smartphone (deliverables) </span><strong style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">with charger</strong></li><li><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Cellular hotspot (optional)</span></li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Tech tools, equipment, and supplies</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">8' Step Ladder</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Hook and Loop (\"Velcro\") strips / roll (for cable management)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Zip ties, black (NOT for cable management)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Packing Tape (to seal box for unused parts/legacy gear)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Philips screwdrivers (#0, #1, and #2 tips)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Slotted screwdriver</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Other screwdrivers (various sizes) (optional)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Cordless drill with various bits</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Needle nose pliers / dykes</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Scissors</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Label printer (such as Brady, Brother or Dymo)</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">with ~1/2 (12mm) white tape (black print)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Mechanic gloves/latex gloves</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">(to prevent handprints when touching ceiling tiles)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Wired/wireless headset</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Box cutter</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Telescoping magnetic pickup</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Tape measure (12' minimum)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Socket set(s)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Screw extractor kit</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Torpedo level (wall brackets)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Head Lamp (optional)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Cat 6a cable tools/crimper with</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">PASSTHROUGH Cat 6a RJ-45 connectors</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Ethernet Cable tester (both continuity and tone tracing tools)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Fish tape or cable pull string (to get cables through millwork)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Crossover cable &ndash; Specifically required; techs were reminded to bring one, and pink patch cables in PNC branches were identified as crossover cables</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Rollover cable &ndash; Explicitly called out alongside crossover cables as required inventory</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">RJ45 crossover adapter (male&ndash;female red adapterPNC - LVT Template Update: ) &ndash; Mentioned as a small adapter that comes with switches/routers and should be available if included in care packs</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Power over Ethernet (PoE) switch &ndash; Required to power access points during testing and wipe activities</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">PoE injector &ndash; Identified as an alternative if a PoE switch is not available</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Windows laptop computer &ndash; Required software including PuTTY</span></li></ul><p><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">﻿</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Lead Technician per-site equipment and supplies</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">2' x 4' fire-rated plywood for wall cabinet backer board</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Mounting hardware such as</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">2\" wood screws for mounting on wood studs</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">3/16\" or 1/4\" toggle bolts or \"zip-its\" for mounting the board on a hollow wall</span></li><li><span style=\"color: black; --darkreader-inline-color: var(--darkreader-text-000000, #e8e6e3);\" data-darkreader-inline-color=\"\">Masonry screw kit for mounting on block walls</span></li></ul>","markdown":"**IMPORTANT:** REVIEW ALL EQUIPMENT LISTED IN THIS SCOPE, IN ITS ENTIRETY BEFORE REQUESTING THIS WORK ORDER!\n\n**Installation Technician (INT):**\n\nWWT has been contracted to assist in the deployment of new standardized network stacks at PNC Bank facilities in North America.\n\n**There are two parts to the installation**; the pre-work (LVV) and the installation of the active devices that connect to the LVV infrastructure. This connection occurs during the installation/cut-over phase (this work order) or the second part (the Installation).\n\n**The LVV includes;** (i) a new network cabinet and back board, (ii) new cabling for access points, (iii) a UXI sensor, (iv) security devices (if in scope), and ((v) moving the existing cables from the existing rack to the new wall mount rack.\n\n**The INT: Installation Technician: the second part (this work order) includes;** (i) installation of a new network stack (in a rolling cabinet), (ii) installation and configuration of new end devices (AP's & UXI), (iii) installation of new workstations, (iv) the migration of the old routers and circuits, (v) decommissioning of the old equipment, (vi) connection of new security devices, (vii) removal of the old rack, and (viii) clean up, deliverables, and site checkout.\n\nYour responsibility is to assist the Lead in the activities associated with the attached deployment guide and to report to the bridge any abnormalities associated with these activities.\n\n**This is NOT a basic technician job.** Technicians are expected to bring to site the tools and equipment identified in the Run-Book/Deployment Guide and possess advanced termination and troubleshooting skills.\n\nPerform network upgrade in accordance with PMO direction, the Deployment Guide.\n\n**Technician's Required Toolkit**\n\nTechnicians are **REQUIRED** to have in their possession and be familiar with the safe and proper\n\nuse of each of the following tools **PRIOR TO ARRIVING ON SITE**:\n\n **Smartphone (with charger and battery pack)**\n\n- Download and install the current **Microsoft Teams** application\n- Download, install and login to the **TrueContext** application\n- Working camera/smartphone (deliverables) **with charger**\n- Cellular hotspot (optional)\n\n**Tech tools, equipment, and supplies**\n\n- 8' Step Ladder\n- Hook and Loop (\"Velcro\") strips / roll (for cable management)\n- Zip ties, black (NOT for cable management)\n- Packing Tape (to seal box for unused parts/legacy gear)\n- Philips screwdrivers (#0, #1, and #2 tips)\n- Slotted screwdriver\n- Other screwdrivers (various sizes) (optional)\n- Cordless drill with various bits\n- Needle nose pliers / dykes\n- Scissors\n- Label printer (such as Brady, Brother or Dymo)\n- with ~1/2 (12mm) white tape (black print)\n- Mechanic gloves/latex gloves\n- (to prevent handprints when touching ceiling tiles)\n- Wired/wireless headset\n- Box cutter\n- Telescoping magnetic pickup\n- Tape measure (12' minimum)\n- Socket set(s)\n- Screw extractor kit\n- Torpedo level (wall brackets)\n- Head Lamp (optional)\n- Cat 6a cable tools/crimper with\n- PASSTHROUGH Cat 6a RJ-45 connectors\n- Ethernet Cable tester (both continuity and tone tracing tools)\n- Fish tape or cable pull string (to get cables through millwork)\n- Crossover cable – Specifically required; techs were reminded to bring one, and pink patch cables in PNC branches were identified as crossover cables\n- Rollover cable – Explicitly called out alongside crossover cables as required inventory\n- RJ45 crossover adapter (male–female red adapterPNC - LVT Template Update: ) – Mentioned as a small adapter that comes with switches/routers and should be available if included in care packs\n- Power over Ethernet (PoE) switch – Required to power access points during testing and wipe activities\n- PoE injector – Identified as an alternative if a PoE switch is not available\n- Windows laptop computer – Required software including PuTTY\n\n﻿\n\n **Lead Technician per-site equipment and supplies**\n\n- 2' x 4' fire-rated plywood for wall cabinet backer board\n- Mounting hardware such as\n- 2\" wood screws for mounting on wood studs\n- 3/16\" or 1/4\" toggle bolts or \"zip-its\" for mounting the board on a hollow wall\n- Masonry screw kit for mounting on block walls","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-01T16:00","end":"2026-10-01T26:00"},"payRange":{"min":501,"max":501},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":10,"distance":6},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"fixed","counterRate":60,"baseAmount":600,"estHours":10,"travelExpense":0,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":0}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"},{"start":"2026-09-11T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-11T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"SMALL BACKBOARD/ DATA REMOTE INSTALL/ MUST HAVE BUTT-SET/MULTIMETER-DIS148477"},{"start":"2026-09-10T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-10T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Maintenance Kit Swap - Apex, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-04T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-05T13:30:00.000Z","summary":"DSS 9223 - Install (1) QNAP + UPS + Switch, Install (3) TP-Link Wireless Bridge, Install (3) 8 Port PoE Switch, Replace (15) Analog Cameras w/ (15) IP Cameras + Cable Runs - Lead Tech"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1789384770904}
