ing rack to the new wall mount rack.\n\n**The INT: Installation Technician: the second part (this work order) includes;** (i) installation of a new network stack (in a rolling cabinet), (ii) installation and configuration of new end devices (AP's & UXI), (iii) installation of new workstations, (iv) the migration of the old routers and circuits, (v) decommissioning of the old equipment, (vi) connection of new security devices, (vii) removal of the old rack, and (viii) clean up, deliverables, and site checkout.\n\nYour responsibility is to assist the Lead in the activities associated with the attached deployment guide and to report to the bridge any abnormalities associated with these activities.\n\n**This is NOT a basic technician job.** Technicians are expected to bring to site the tools and equipment identified in the Run-Book/Deployment Guide and possess advanced termination and troubleshooting skills.\n\nPerform network upgrade in accordance with PMO direction, the Deployment Guide.\n\n**Technician's Required Toolkit**\n\nTechnicians are **REQUIRED** to have in their possession and be familiar with the safe and proper\n\nuse of each of the following tools **PRIOR TO ARRIVING ON SITE**:\n\n **Smartphone (with charger and battery pack)**\n\n- Download and install the current **Microsoft Teams** application\n- Download, install and login to the **TrueContext** application\n- Working camera/smartphone (deliverables) **with charger**\n- Cellular hotspot (optional)\n\n**Tech tools, equipment, and supplies**\n\n- 8' Step Ladder\n- Hook and Loop (\"Velcro\") strips / roll (for cable management)\n- Zip ties, black (NOT for cable management)\n- Packing Tape (to seal box for unused parts/legacy gear)\n- Philips screwdrivers (#0, #1, and #2 tips)\n- Slotted screwdriver\n- Other screwdrivers (various sizes) (optional)\n- Cordless drill with various bits\n- Needle nose pliers / dykes\n- Scissors\n- Label printer (such as Brady, Brother or Dymo)\n- with ~1/2 (12mm) white tape (black print)\n- Mechanic gloves/latex gloves\n- (to prevent handprints when touching ceiling tiles)\n- Wired/wireless headset\n- Box cutter\n- Telescoping magnetic pickup\n- Tape measure (12' minimum)\n- Socket set(s)\n- Screw extractor kit\n- Torpedo level (wall brackets)\n- Head Lamp (optional)\n- Cat 6a cable tools/crimper with\n- PASSTHROUGH Cat 6a RJ-45 connectors\n- Ethernet Cable tester (both continuity and tone tracing tools)\n- Fish tape or cable pull string (to get cables through millwork)\n- Crossover cable – Specifically required; techs were reminded to bring one, and pink patch cables in PNC branches were identified as crossover cables\n- Rollover cable – Explicitly called out alongside crossover cables as required inventory\n- RJ45 crossover adapter (male–female red adapterPNC - LVT Template Update: ) – Mentioned as a small adapter that comes with switches/routers and should be available if included in care packs\n- Power over Ethernet (PoE) switch – Required to power access points during testing and wipe activities\n- PoE injector – Identified as an alternative if a PoE switch is not available\n- Windows laptop computer – Required software including PuTTY\n\n﻿\n\n **Lead Technician per-site equipment and supplies**\n\n- 2' x 4' fire-rated plywood for wall cabinet backer board\n- Mounting hardware such as\n- 2\" wood screws for mounting on wood studs\n- 3/16\" or 1/4\" toggle bolts or \"zip-its\" for mounting the board on a hollow wall\n- Masonry screw kit for mounting on block walls","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-30T16:00","end":"2026-09-30T26:00"},"payRange":{"min":501,"max":501},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":10,"distance":6},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"fixed","counterRate":60,"baseAmount":600,"estHours":10,"travelExpense":0,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":0}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"},{"start":"2026-09-11T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-11T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"SMALL BACKBOARD/ DATA REMOTE INSTALL/ MUST HAVE BUTT-SET/MULTIMETER-DIS148477"},{"start":"2026-09-10T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-10T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Maintenance Kit Swap - Apex, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-04T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-05T13:30:00.000Z","summary":"DSS 9223 - Install (1) QNAP + UPS + Switch, Install (3) TP-Link Wireless Bridge, Install (3) 8 Port PoE Switch, Replace (15) Analog Cameras w/ (15) IP Cameras + Cable Runs - Lead Tech"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1789384782907}
