agement)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Zip ties, black (NOT for cable management)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Packing Tape (to seal box for unused parts/legacy gear)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Philips screwdrivers (#0, #1, and #2 tips)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Slotted screwdriver</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Other screwdrivers (various sizes) (optional)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Cordless drill with various bits</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Needle nose pliers / dykes</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Scissors</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Label printer (such as Brady, Brother or Dymo)</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">with ~1/2 (12mm) white tape (black print)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Mechanic gloves/latex gloves</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">(to prevent handprints when touching ceiling tiles)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Wired/wireless headset</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Box cutter</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Telescoping magnetic pickup</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Tape measure (12' minimum)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Socket set(s)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Screw extractor kit</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Torpedo level (wall brackets)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Head Lamp (optional)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Cat 6a cable tools/crimper with</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">PASSTHROUGH Cat 6a RJ-45 connectors</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Ethernet Cable tester (both continuity and tone tracing tools)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Fish tape or cable pull string (to get cables through millwork)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Crossover cable &ndash; Specifically required; techs were reminded to bring one, and pink patch cables in PNC branches were identified as crossover cables</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Rollover cable &ndash; Explicitly called out alongside crossover cables as required inventory</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">RJ45 crossover adapter (male&ndash;female red adapterPNC - LVT Template Update: ) &ndash; Mentioned as a small adapter that comes with switches/routers and should be available if included in care packs</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Power over Ethernet (PoE) switch &ndash; Required to power access points during testing and wipe activities</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">PoE injector &ndash; Identified as an alternative if a PoE switch is not available</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Windows laptop computer &ndash; Required software including PuTTY</span></li></ul><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">﻿</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Lead Technician per-site equipment and supplies</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">2' x 4' fire-rated plywood for wall cabinet backer board</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Mounting hardware such as</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">2\" wood screws for mounting on wood studs</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">3/16\" or 1/4\" toggle bolts or \"zip-its\" for mounting the board on a hollow wall</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Masonry screw kit for mounting on block walls</span></li></ul>","markdown":"**IMPORTANT:** REVIEW ALL EQUIPMENT LISTED IN THIS SCOPE, IN ITS ENTIRETY BEFORE REQUESTING THIS WORK ORDER!\n\n**Low Voltage Technician**\n\nWWT has been contracted to assist in the deployment of new standardized network stacks at PNC Bank facilities in North America. The overall solution includes two separated processes: (a) LVV and (b) the Installation Cut-Over. The first process includes (i) updating network cabling, (ii) a new wall-mount cabinet and backer board, (iii) terminating new cabling, (iv) moving cabling from an existing patch panel over to new patch panel, (v) clean up, and (vi) deliverables.\n\n**You are part of a 3-person team, with 1 lead and 2 technicians. Each LVV site will be 3 nights (approx. 4pm to 2am). Perform low voltage technician work in accordance with onsite lead technician, PMO direction, and the Deployment Guide.**\n\nTechnicians must have demonstrated knowledge, skills, and abilities in the activities outlined above. This is not just a cabling or a rack and stack project, the **technician must have direct experience in terminating CAT6a cables, moving cables from an existing patch panel to a new patch panel, and complex cabling.**\n\n **Technicians will be selected with the following criteria:**\n\n- Demonstrated work experience in your FN work history (including cabling, termination, patch panel relocation)\n- Field Nation score specifically timeliness, back-out ranking, and marketplace score.\n- Availability of working all sites on the route (could be up to 6 months)\n- Ability to work with other technicians.\n- Distance from sites (no travel provided).\n\n**Technician Expectations:**\n\n- Attend required training.\n- On the bridge at all times.\n- Have reliable transportation.\n- Have the required tools identified in the Run-Book/Deployment Guide.\n- Follow the directions from the bridge and\n\n**A fixed rate is a fixed rate, WE DO NOT accept counter offers, and WE DO NOT allow substitutions.**\n\n**Technician's Required Toolkit**\n\nTechnicians are **REQUIRED** to have in their possession and be familiar with the safe and proper\n\nuse of each of the following tools **PRIOR TO ARRIVING ON SITE**:\n\n **Smartphone (with charger and battery pack)**\n\n- Download and install the current **Microsoft Teams** application\n- Download, install and login to the **TrueContext** application\n- Working camera/smartphone (deliverables) **with charger**\n- Cellular hotspot (optional)\n\n**Tech tools, equipment, and supplies**\n\n- 8' Step Ladder\n- Hook and Loop (\"Velcro\") strips / roll (for cable management)\n- Zip ties, black (NOT for cable management)\n- Packing Tape (to seal box for unused parts/legacy gear)\n- Philips screwdrivers (#0, #1, and #2 tips)\n- Slotted screwdriver\n- Other screwdrivers (various sizes) (optional)\n- Cordless drill with various bits\n- Needle nose pliers / dykes\n- Scissors\n- Label printer (such as Brady, Brother or Dymo)\n- with ~1/2 (12mm) white tape (black print)\n- Mechanic gloves/latex gloves\n- (to prevent handprints when touching ceiling tiles)\n- Wired/wireless headset\n- Box cutter\n- Telescoping magnetic pickup\n- Tape measure (12' minimum)\n- Socket set(s)\n- Screw extractor kit\n- Torpedo level (wall brackets)\n- Head Lamp (optional)\n- Cat 6a cable tools/crimper with\n- PASSTHROUGH Cat 6a RJ-45 connectors\n- Ethernet Cable tester (both continuity and tone tracing tools)\n- Fish tape or cable pull string (to get cables through millwork)\n- Crossover cable – Specifically required; techs were reminded to bring one, and pink patch cables in PNC branches were identified as crossover cables\n- Rollover cable – Explicitly called out alongside crossover cables as required inventory\n- RJ45 crossover adapter (male–female red adapterPNC - LVT Template Update: ) – Mentioned as a small adapter that comes with switches/routers and should be available if included in care packs\n- Power over Ethernet (PoE) switch – Required to power access points during testing and wipe activities\n- PoE injector – Identified as an alternative if a PoE switch is not available\n- Windows laptop computer – Required software including PuTTY\n\n﻿\n\n **Lead Technician per-site equipment and supplies**\n\n- 2' x 4' fire-rated plywood for wall cabinet backer board\n- Mounting hardware such as\n- 2\" wood screws for mounting on wood studs\n- 3/16\" or 1/4\" toggle bolts or \"zip-its\" for mounting the board on a hollow wall\n- Masonry screw kit for mounting on block walls","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-29T16:00","end":"2026-09-29T26:00"},"payRange":{"min":501,"max":501},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":10,"distance":15},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"fixed","counterRate":60,"baseAmount":600,"estHours":10,"travelExpense":35,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":0}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"},{"start":"2026-09-11T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-11T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"SMALL BACKBOARD/ DATA REMOTE INSTALL/ MUST HAVE BUTT-SET/MULTIMETER-DIS148477"},{"start":"2026-09-10T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-10T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Maintenance Kit Swap - Apex, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-04T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-05T13:30:00.000Z","summary":"DSS 9223 - Install (1) QNAP + UPS + Switch, Install (3) TP-Link Wireless Bridge, Install (3) 8 Port PoE Switch, Replace (15) Analog Cameras w/ (15) IP Cameras + Cable Runs - Lead Tech"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1789384805407}
{"job":{"id":19943675,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"REF #568671 - Wall Tablet Trouble shoot -  Chapel Hill, NC","description":{"html":"<strong><u>It is required that the technician performing the on-site service is the same individual who was initially assigned to the job.</u></strong><br><p><br></p><strong>Scope of work:</strong><p><br></p><p>In the Downstairs Ballroom, there are 3 Extron wall tablet panels. One of them no longer powers on. This has happened before with the other 2 Extron panels, and was resolved by servicing the wires connected to the panel through the wall.&nbsp;</p><p>1. Objective: Restore power to the Extron wall panel in the ballroom&nbsp;</p><p>2. Arrive on time wearing work appropriate attire&nbsp;</p><p>3. Check in with AVIT upon arriving on site REQUIRED&nbsp;</p><p>4. locate av room where tablets are getting POE from&nbsp;</p><p>5. reseat POE connections and verify that tablets are getting POE&nbsp;</p><p>6. remove tablets if needed and check for power button&nbsp;</p><p>check behind mount for POE device&nbsp;</p><p>8. check with management for any other issues&nbsp;</p><p>9.&nbsp;Collaborate with AVIT to resolve the issue as needed&nbsp;</p><p>10. Clean up work area of tools or debris caused by the job 11. Check out with AVIT upon leaving site&nbsp;</p><p>Tools:&nbsp;</p><p>Laptop with NIC and patch cable&nbsp;</p><p>line tester/toner/probe&nbsp;</p><p>charged smartphone with camera&nbsp;</p><p>FLASHLIGHT (NOT YOUR PHONE)&nbsp;</p><p>cat5 and Coax termination tools&nbsp;</p><p>ladders 16' (working over shrubs on outside speakers) basic hand tools&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><ul><li>Complete all tasks listed in the WO.</li><li>Represent the CLIENT professionally and keep the site clean. Dress code: Professional attire.</li><li>Work closely with our remote support.</li></ul><p><br></p><strong>Date of Visit:</strong><p><strong>[Insert Date]</strong></p><p><br></p><strong>Required Tools:</strong><p>Cat6 cable, 6 ft ladder, screwdrivers, pliers, cutters/strippers, crimper, punch-down tool, multimeter, cable tester, tone/probe, loopback plugs, Ethernet cables, RJ45 connectors, label maker, ESD strap, flashlight, laptop, USB drive, rack screws/brackets, Velcro/zip ties, and basic hand tools.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><strong>1. Pre-Site Preparation</strong><ul><li><strong>Review:</strong>&nbsp;Study the WO and all attachments.</li><li><strong>Inventory:</strong>&nbsp;Verify all shipped equipment and ensure you have all necessary tools/parts.</li><li><strong>Support:</strong>&nbsp;Contact Support Tech with any pre-trip questions.</li></ul><strong>2. On-Site Procedures</strong><ul><li><strong>Check-In:</strong>&nbsp;Log into the WO, call&nbsp;<strong>Support Tech (470-470-7757)</strong>, and introduce yourself to the On-site Contact/Manager.</li><li><strong>Execution:</strong>&nbsp;Complete work, record the Manager on Duty’s name, and keep the work area clean.</li><li><strong>Professionalism:</strong>&nbsp;Do&nbsp;<strong>not</strong>&nbsp;discuss Field Nation with the client; Support Tech handles all reporting.</li></ul><strong>3. Required Deliverables</strong><ul><li><strong>Documentation:</strong>&nbsp;Detailed work notes and the Manager on Duty’s name.</li><li><strong>Photos:</strong>&nbsp;Clear Before/During/After photos of the work.</li><li><strong>Hardware:</strong>&nbsp;Serial and Model numbers (as applicable).</li><li><strong>Completion:</strong>&nbsp;Confirm full functionality with remote support before check-out.</li></ul><strong>4. Check-Out &amp; Submission</strong><ul><li><strong>Final Call:</strong>&nbsp;Contact&nbsp;<strong>Support Tech (470-470-7757)</strong>&nbsp;before leaving to review deliverables and obtain release code.</li><li><strong>Deadline:</strong>&nbsp;Upload all deliverables and submit the WO within&nbsp;<strong>24 hours</strong>.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>⚠️Payment &amp; Expense Policy</strong></p><p><strong>1. Flat Rate &amp; Travel Agreement</strong></p><p>This is a <strong>fixed-budget assignment</strong>. By accepting this Work Order without a prior counteroffer, the Service Provider agrees the listed rate is <strong>all-inclusive</strong> of labor, tools, and travel.</p><ul><li><strong>Trip Charges:</strong> No \"Trip Charges,\" \"Fuel Surcharges,\" or \"Travel Fees\" will be approved if added after the work is completed.</li><li><strong>Prior Approval:</strong> Any travel adjustments must have been submitted via counteroffer and approved by the Project/WO Manager <strong>prior to assignment</strong>.</li></ul><p><strong>2. Onsite Hours &amp; Completion</strong></p><p>All onsite hours will be compensated provided they are reasonable and the scope is fully completed.</p><ul><li><strong>Documentation:</strong> You must document any onsite delays or issues in the work order notes, clearly stating the reason for the delay.</li></ul><p><strong>3. Unauthorized Expenses</strong></p><p>Any expenses added to the final invoice that were not pre-authorized in writing via the platform's messaging system will be <strong>automatically rejected</strong>.</p><p><br></p><strong>⚠️ Compliance Alert</strong><p>Reductions in pay or penalties may apply for:</p><ul><li>Leaving site without posting deliverables or obtaining a release code.</li><li>Failing to submit the WO within the 24-hour window.</li><li><br></li></ul>","markdown":"**It is required that the technician performing the on-site service is the same individual who was initially assigned to the job.**  \n**Scope of work:**In the Downstairs Ballroom, there are 3 Extron wall tablet panels. One of them no longer powers on. This has happened before with the other 2 Extron panels, and was resolved by servicing the wires connected to the panel through the wall.\n\n1\\. Objective: Restore power to the Extron wall panel in the ballroom\n\n2\\. Arrive on time wearing work appropriate attire\n\n3\\. Check in with AVIT upon arriving on site REQUIRED\n\n4\\. locate av room where tablets are getting POE from\n\n5\\. reseat POE connections and verify that tablets are getting POE\n\n6\\. remove tablets if needed and check for power button\n\ncheck behind mount for POE device\n\n8\\. check with management for any other issues\n\n9\\. Collaborate with AVIT to resolve the issue as needed\n\n10\\. Clean up work area of tools or debris caused by the job 11. Check out with AVIT upon leaving site\n\nTools:\n\nLaptop with NIC and patch cable\n\nline tester/toner/probe\n\ncharged smartphone with camera\n\nFLASHLIGHT (NOT YOUR PHONE)\n\ncat5 and Coax termination tools\n\nladders 16' (working over shrubs on outside speakers) basic hand tools\n\n- Complete all tasks listed in the WO.\n- Represent the CLIENT professionally and keep the site clean. Dress code: Professional attire.\n- Work closely with our remote support.\n\n**Date of Visit:****\\[Insert Date\\]**\n\n**Required Tools:**Cat6 cable, 6 ft ladder, screwdrivers, pliers, cutters/strippers, crimper, punch-down tool, multimeter, cable tester, tone/probe, loopback plugs, Ethernet cables, RJ45 connectors, label maker, ESD strap, flashlight, laptop, USB drive, rack screws/brackets, Velcro/zip ties, and basic hand tools.\n\n**1. Pre-Site Preparation**- **Review:** Study the WO and all attachments.\n- **Inventory:** Verify all shipped equipment and ensure you have all necessary tools/parts.\n- **Support:** Contact Support Tech with any pre-trip questions.\n\n**2. On-Site Procedures**- **Check-In:** Log into the WO, call **Support Tech (470-470-7757)**, and introduce yourself to the On-site Contact/Manager.\n- **Execution:** Complete work, record the Manager on Duty’s name, and keep the work area clean.\n- **Professionalism:** Do **not** discuss Field Nation with the client; Support Tech handles all reporting.\n\n**3. Required Deliverables**- **Documentation:** Detailed work notes and the Manager on Duty’s name.\n- **Photos:** Clear Before/During/After photos of the work.\n- **Hardware:** Serial and Model numbers (as applicable).\n- **Completion:** Confirm full functionality with remote support before check-out.\n\n**4. Check-Out & Submission**- **Final Call:** Contact **Support Tech (470-470-7757)** before leaving to review deliverables and obtain release code.\n- **Deadline:** Upload all deliverables and submit the WO within **24 hours**.\n\n**⚠️Payment & Expense Policy**\n\n**1. Flat Rate & Travel Agreement**\n\nThis is a **fixed-budget assignment**. By accepting this Work Order without a prior counteroffer, the Service Provider agrees the listed rate is **all-inclusive** of labor, tools, and travel.\n\n- **Trip Charges:** No \"Trip Charges,\" \"Fuel Surcharges,\" or \"Travel Fees\" will be approved if added after the work is completed.\n- **Prior Approval:** Any travel adjustments must have been submitted via counteroffer and approved by the Project/WO Manager **prior to assignment**.\n\n**2. Onsite Hours & Completion**\n\nAll onsite hours will be compensated provided they are reasonable and the scope is fully completed.\n\n- **Documentation:** You must document any onsite delays or issues in the work order notes, clearly stating the reason for the delay.\n\n**3. Unauthorized Expenses**\n\nAny expenses added to the final invoice that were not pre-authorized in writing via the platform's messaging system will be **automatically rejected**.\n\n**⚠️ Compliance Alert**Reductions in pay or penalties may apply for:\n\n- Leaving site without posting deliverables or obtaining a release code.\n- Failing to submit the WO within the 24-hour window.\n-","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-15T09:00","end":"2026-09-15T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":200},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":15},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":60,"baseAmount":240,"estHours":4,"travelExpense":35,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"s