{"job":{"id":19943227,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TailWind Voice & Data, Inc.","title":"Warehouse AP Replacement","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Objective Statement: </strong></p><p>Remove old Meraki (MR46E) wireless AP located in warehouse ceiling&nbsp;</p><p>Using the existing AP mount, click new AP in place</p><p>Contact TCON to confirm its online</p><p>*Will require 2 technicians: one will be operating the lift &amp; the other will serve as the OSHA ground guide</p><p>*A scissor lift will be provided</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p><p>&nbsp;Fully charge Windows Laptop, Console cable, mifi/wifi capable device.</p><p>• Standard technician tools &amp; materials based on the SOW</p><p>• Additional patch panel cabling in various lengths</p><p>• Bulk cabling and termination ends to create new cables as needed to resolve issues</p><p>• Cable certifier/tester</p><p>• 6-8’ ladder</p><p>•<strong>&nbsp;T8 Torx Screwdriver &amp; Phillips Screwdriver</strong></p><p>• TailWind to provide the lift (must reach 36')</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Required Deliverable Format: Technician will be asked to complete a specific JotForm to collect the appropriate deliverables. This is a required task.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>TailWind Requirements: </strong></p><ul><li>Tailwind will only approve the work authorized in the SOW uploaded by Tailwind in the attachments of the Field Nation order.</li><li>Technician must verify that all materials/lifts in the SOW are on-site upon arrival and report any issues to Tailwind immediately via Field Nation messages.</li><li>Any delays on-site need to be reported to Tailwind via Field Nation messages OR by calling in and speaking with someone at TailWind within 1 hour of the delay. (Document who you spoke to and gave you approval)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tailwind will not approve additional time beyond 1 hour for delays that are not reported and responded to by a Tailwind via Field Nation Messages OR phone call.</li><li>Any additional Out of Scope work needs to be requested in the Field Nation messages OR the technician calls into TailWind and gets approval to proceed.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Any verbal agreements will be be followed up with a written confirmation of next steps and approval via Field Nation messages.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Only Tailwind can approve Out of Scope work.</li></ul>","markdown":"**Objective Statement:**\n\nRemove old Meraki (MR46E) wireless AP located in warehouse ceiling\n\nUsing the existing AP mount, click new AP in place\n\nContact TCON to confirm its online\n\n\\*Will require 2 technicians: one will be operating the lift & the other will serve as the OSHA ground guide\n\n\\*A scissor lift will be provided\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n Fully charge Windows Laptop, Console cable, mifi/wifi capable device.\n\n• Standard technician tools & materials based on the SOW\n\n• Additional patch panel cabling in various lengths\n\n• Bulk cabling and termination ends to create new cables as needed to resolve issues\n\n• Cable certifier/tester\n\n• 6-8’ ladder\n\n• **T8 Torx Screwdriver & Phillips Screwdriver**\n\n• TailWind to provide the lift (must reach 36')\n\n**Required Deliverable Format: Technician will be asked to complete a specific JotForm to collect the appropriate deliverables. This is a required task.**\n\n**TailWind Requirements:**\n\n- Tailwind will only approve the work authorized in the SOW uploaded by Tailwind in the attachments of the Field Nation order.\n- Technician must verify that all materials/lifts in the SOW are on-site upon arrival and report any issues to Tailwind immediately via Field Nation messages.\n- Any delays on-site need to be reported to Tailwind via Field Nation messages OR by calling in and speaking with someone at TailWind within 1 hour of the delay. (Document who you spoke to and gave you approval)\n- Tailwind will not approve additional time beyond 1 hour for delays that are not reported and responded to by a Tailwind via Field Nation Messages OR phone call.\n- Any additional Out of Scope work needs to be requested in the Field Nation messages OR the technician calls into TailWind and gets approval to proceed.\n- Any verbal agreements will be be followed up with a written confirmation of next steps and approval via Field Nation messages.\n- Only Tailwind can approve Out of Scope work.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-15T08:00","end":"2026-09-15T14:00","latestStart":"2026-09-15T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":375,"max":375},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":6,"distance":54},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"fixed","counterRate":63,"baseAmount":375,"estHours":6,"travelExpense":80,"payStructure":null},"reason":"TRAVEL_REQUIRED","rejectDetails":"Travel required (54mi reported + 10mi padding = 64mi > 20mi)"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-15T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-17T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-1