{"job":{"id":19943020,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Wachter - Nationwide Service","title":"Troubleshoot Intermittent Spectrum Broadband Disconnects","description":{"html":"<p>IMPORTANT NOTE:</p><p>To receive full payment for this ticket, you MUST follow all instructions while onsite: checking in/out with both Wachter and any site contacts listed on workorder. You must also input detailed closeout notes and upload deliverables before leaving site.&nbsp;</p><p>If you are unable to agree to these terms, please do not accept this work order. More specific details of how to complete this can be found below.</p><p>Provider must introduce themselves as a representative of Wachter while onsite. Do not mention Field Nation.</p><p>______________________________________________________________________</p><p><strong>Check-In / Check-Out</strong></p><p>Call <strong><del>************ ****** ** *****</del>)</strong> upon arrival and before leaving to coordinate dashboard monitoring.</p><p><strong>Scope of Work</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"color: inherit;\">The Spectrum primary broadband is currently connected to port 1 of the Cisco Meraki MX68 router and it looks like it’s disconnecting every now and then. Please help us troubleshoot.</strong></li><li><strong style=\"color: inherit;\">Test cable going between Spectrum modem and Cisco MX68 router. Bring spare cables to replace as necessary.</strong></li><li><strong style=\"color: inherit;\">Check if physically anything strange with hardware going to router and modem.</strong></li><li><strong style=\"color: inherit;\">Connect laptop to Spectrum modem to check speed and see if it provides access to internet as necessary.</strong></li><li><strong style=\"color: inherit;\">Make sure store and all devices are online before leaving.</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Equipment Information</strong></p><ul><li>Spectrum Modem</li><li>Cisco Meraki MX68</li></ul><p><strong>Technician Requirements</strong></p><ul><li>Spare Ethernet cables: 3', 5', 6', 8', and 10'</li><li>Ladder for access to wall cabinet</li><li>Laptop for connectivity testing</li><li><strong>Before-and-after photos of the network rack, with the patch panel, network devices, and UPS visible</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Escalation</strong></p><p>If the scope cannot be completed or an additional trip is required, contact <strong><del>** ****** ********** ** ************</del></strong><del>*</del></p><p>______________________________________________________________________</p><p>The customer <strong>REQUIRES </strong>Techs to be <strong>ON TIME </strong>or <strong>EARLY </strong>for each ticket.&nbsp;</p><p>Please head to the site early to avoid any potential Traffic issues, as this will <strong><u>NOT</u></strong> be a valid excuse for the customer. Contact Wachter dispatch if any concerns.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Deliverables Needed</u></strong></p><p>Pictures are required of all work areas before, during and after doing work. Detailed pics are required of any specific work performed.</p><p>TAKE A WIDE-ANGLE PIC OF THE BACKBOARD. IT MUST SHOW ALL COMPONENTS/WIRING/POWER SOURCES</p><p>WO must include a detailed description of the work completed including the troubleshooting process and steps taken to resolve the issue.</p><p>If hardware was replaced, notate the serial number of both old and new equipment</p><p>If cable was tested, take a picture of pass/fail results for each cable.</p><p>**Disclaimer**</p><p>To ensure full payment for this ticket, the technician must check out with Support and obtain the name of the support personnel spoken with. The technician must also follow all instructions outlined in the Scope of Work and complete checkout with the Project Manager or Dispatch team.</p>","markdown":"IMPORTANT NOTE:\n\nTo receive full payment for this ticket, you MUST follow all instructions while onsite: checking in/out with both Wachter and any site contacts listed on workorder. You must also input detailed closeout notes and upload deliverables before leaving site.\n\nIf you are unable to agree to these terms, please do not accept this work order. More specific details of how to complete this can be found below.\n\nProvider must introduce themselves as a representative of Wachter while onsite. Do not mention Field Nation.\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\n**Check-In / Check-Out**\n\nCall **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*)** upon arrival and before leaving to coordinate dashboard monitoring.\n\n**Scope of Work**\n\n- **The Spectrum primary broadband is currently connected to port 1 of the Cisco Meraki MX68 router and it looks like it’s disconnecting every now and then. Please help us troubleshoot.**\n- **Test cable going between Spectrum modem and Cisco MX68 router. Bring spare cables to replace as necessary.**\n- **Check if physically anything strange with hardware going to router and modem.**\n- **Connect laptop to Spectrum modem to check speed and see if it provides access to internet as necessary.**\n- **Make sure store and all devices are online before leaving.**\n\n**Equipment Information**\n\n- Spectrum Modem\n- Cisco Meraki MX68\n\n**Technician Requirements**\n\n- Spare Ethernet cables: 3', 5', 6', 8', and 10'\n- Ladder for access to wall cabinet\n- Laptop for connectivity testing\n- **Before-and-after photos of the network rack, with the patch panel, network devices, and UPS visible**\n\n**Escalation**\n\nIf the scope cannot be completed or an additional trip is required, contact **\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\\*\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\nThe customer **REQUIRES** Techs to be **ON TIME** or **EARLY** for each ticket.\n\nPlease head to the site early to avoid any potential Traffic issues, as this will **NOT** be a valid excuse for the customer. Contact Wachter dispatch if any concerns.\n\n**Deliverables Needed**\n\nPictures are required of all work areas before, during and after doing work. Detailed pics are required of any specific work performed.\n\nTAKE A WIDE-ANGLE PIC OF THE BACKBOARD. IT MUST SHOW ALL COMPONENTS/WIRING/POWER SOURCES\n\nWO must include a detailed description of the work completed including the troubleshooting process and steps taken to resolve the issue.\n\nIf hardware was replaced, notate the serial number of both old and new equipment\n\nIf cable was tested, take a picture of pass/fail results for each cable.\n\n\\*\\*Disclaimer\\*\\*\n\nTo ensure full payment for this ticket, the technician must check out with Support and obtain the name of the support personnel spoken with. The technician must also follow all instructions outlined in the Scope of Work and complete checkout with the Project Manager or Dispatch team.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-15T09:30","end":"2026-09-15T11:30"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":120},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":60,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":16},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $120 (countered: $120) is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-15T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-17T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"},{"start":"2026-09-11T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-11T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"SMALL BACKBOARD/ DATA REMOTE INSTALL/ MUST HAVE BUTT-SET/MULTIMETER-DIS148477"},{"start":"2026-09-10T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-10T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Maintenance Kit Swap - Apex, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-04T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-05T13:30:00.000Z","summary":"DSS 9223 - Install (1) QNAP + UPS + Switch, Install (3) TP-Link Wireless Bridge, Install (3) 8 Port PoE Switch, Replace (15) Analog Cameras w/ (15) IP Cameras + Cable Runs - Lead Tech"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789384851388}
{"job":{"id":"3627705715","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard","description":"\"If the survey runs over 2 hours you need to get permission from the Property Manager to continue and please let them know about how much longer would be needed<br>Please survey for all fire alarms, burg alarms, elevators, pool phones\\(voice\\), fax<br>If there are different building on the property there are probably fire alarms in each one<br>Please work with Property Manager to make sure we get the correct information<br>If you have any issues please reach out to Hilal 9194246791 or 919-870-5080<br>Survey SOW: SOS must match dates and times that are in WorkMarket and MUST BE SIGNED BY THE CUSTOMER \\(LCON\\)<br>1\\. TECH MUST CALL LCON, 30 MINUTES BEFORE ARRIVAL\\.<br>2\\. Check in and out through Work Market\\. For any questions during the survey, please call the EPIK Technical Coordination \\(TC\\) Team at: 833-479-4768<br>3\\. Upon arrival, departure, and for questions about your scope of work or if you are unclear on instructions before starting the installation, check in with the EPIK Technical Coordination \\(TC\\) Team at 833-479-4768, otherwise Login to EPIK Wizard at https://wizard\\.epik\\.io to begin the Survey process\\. When you enter the Granite ticket number it will be recognized as a survey, and you will be taken to the Survey Wizard\\.  \\(Note: If you have completed a Wizard survey or install before, please be sure to refresh your browser window to ensure the current version is being used\\.\\)<br>4\\. Follow all instructions presented by the Survey Wizard\\.  If you run into any issues or have questions you may call the TC Team\\.  All sections of the survey are required and will require final sign off by Granite Technical Coordinator before you will be cleared to leave the site\\.  The Survey Wizard will guide you through this process\\.<br>5\\. Before departure call the EPIK Technical Coordination \\(TC\\) Team at 833-479- 4768 to review deliverables and receive approval on survey results\\.<br>6\\. Once your survey results have been approved by the TC Team, a TC Team representative will give you a checkout code to enter into WorkMarket which you will use to check out upon completion of the survey\\. Failure to checkout will result in delay or nonpayment for services\\. <br> <br>Materials/Tools Required: Laptop with ability to create hotspot, Smart Phone, Tone Generator and Wand, Punch Tool \\(66 &amp; 110\\) Electrician Scissors, Step Ladder, Flashlight and/or Headlamp, RJ11&amp;RJ45 Crimper, Ethernet Cable Tester, Masonry Bits, Impact Drill, Pencil and/or Marker, Level, Philips Driver Bits and Screwdriver Cordless Drill, Needle-Nose Pliers, Label-Maker, All-Purpose Screws \\(drywall, masonry, wood\\), Cable-Ties and Mountings, Cat3 or Better Cable \\(for analog devices\\), Cat6 Ethernet Cable \\(for data connections\\), CrossConnect Wire, Gel-Crimp Connecters, Label-Tape, RJ11 &amp; Cat6 Ethernet Keystone Jacks, RJ11 &amp; RJ45 Modular Plugs, Lineman’s Telephony Handset/Butt-Set, Infrared Temperature Gun\"","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-15T10:00","end":"2026-09-15T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":195},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":6.8},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":65,"baseAmount":195,"estHours":3,"travelExpense":0,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T18:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":60,"mode":"hours","reason":"arrival_window"}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-15T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-17T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"},{"start":"2026-09-11T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-11T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"SMALL BACKBOARD/ DATA REMOTE INSTALL/ MUST HAVE BUTT-SET/MULTIMETER-DIS148477"},{"start":"2026-09-10T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-10T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Maintenance Kit Swap - Apex, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-04T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-05T13:30:00.000Z","summary":"DSS 9223 - Install (1) QNAP + UPS + Switch, Install (3) TP-Link Wireless Bridge, Install (3) 8 Port PoE Switch, Replace (15) Analog Cameras w/ (15) IP Cameras + Cable Runs - Lead Tech"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1789384864371}
{"job":{"id":19769277,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"LITnetworking LLC","title":"SMALL BACKBOARD/ DATA REMOTE INSTALL/ MUST HAVE BUTT-SET/MULTIMETER-DIS148477","description":{"html":"<p>PLEASE CALL METTEL SUPPORT UPON ARRIVAL 3852623457 Ticket 11745077</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Call Travis Newkirk @ 3852623457 when on site.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>**PIAB Install**</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Tech will need: butt-set, bridge clips, toner, multi-meter, label maker, screw driver.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>This is for a PIAB install. CROSS CONNECT REQUIRED.</p>\n<p>Install/mount equipment (CDS-9090, Pano MIMO antenna, hydra cable and 66 block) on the backboard near the network rack. Connect WAN port to store switch 01 port 14 or port 15 if port 14 is unavailable, confirm WAN and LTE connectivity, test line (inbound and outbound) off the CDS-9090 and the 66 block.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Cross connect new line from 66 block to the stores downtime phone. This new line will replace the existing line on the phone. Tech may have to tone existing jack. Have store manager confirm downtime phone is working on the new line.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Label the following and take pictures of each item:</p>\n<p>Label CDS-9090 with 'METTEL'</p>\n<p>Label 66 block cover with 'METTEL xx/xx/xxxx (date of install)'</p>\n<p>Label inside 66 block with each phone number</p>\n<p>Take photo of WAN cable connection on the CDS-9090</p>\n<p>Take photo of WAN cable connection on the switch port</p>\n<p>Take photo of downtime phone, wall jack, switch port</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>LCON: Dominique Brown 919-200-6460</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Once install is complete, please contact the GAP Network Voice Team at 800-333-7899 Extn: 66645 to checkout and provide a status</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>-Data Remote CDS-9090</p>\n<p>-MiMo Antenna &amp; Bracket Kit</p>\n<p>-Tech to locate equipment.</p>\n<p>-Locate customer network switch in room switch/router.</p>\n<p>-Install MetTel Board and CDS-9090.</p>\n<p>-Attach antennas and power on.</p>\n<p>-MetTel will validate configurations.</p>\n<p>-Connect laptop and run speed tests over LTE. Do not use speedtest.net</p>\n<p>-Verify dial tone and in/outbound calling on all provisioned CDS9090 RJ11 ports.</p>\n<p>-Validate e911 address on one each line.</p>\n<p>-Use multimeter to verify each existing pair has a voltage of 0 on customer side of the demark.</p>\n<p>If voltage is found, locate the short/bridge and repair.</p>\n<p>-Work with customer to contact the alarms monitoring vendor and have the Fire Panel placed into test mode.</p>\n<p>-Locate/tag Elevator, Fire and Burglar lines.</p>\n<p>-Cross-connect to Fire Panel, Burglar Panel, and test.</p>\n<p>-Contact the fire monitoring vendor to confirm that they are receiving the faults, restoral, low battery and battery restore signals.</p>\n<p>-Confirm monitoring vendor sees the correct service address.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Please review the following requirements and protocols for your upcoming assignment with Lit Networking:</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>To ensure the successful completion of this site visit, you must arrive with the following tools and materials: - A fully charged laptop with an Ethernet port and a cellphone with a hotspot device. - Cabling tools: Multimeter wire tester, butt set, punch down tool, crimpers, and wire cutters. - Hardware: RJ11 and RJ45 connectors, biscuit jacks, and 100 feet of Cat 5e/6 cable for potential device relocation. - Standard mounting kit: Drill, level, hammer, screwdrivers, screws, and anchors. - General supplies: Adjustable or open-end wrenches, a 4–6 ft ladder, and a 100 ft extension cord.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Work Order and Payment Procedures All work orders must be signed by the onsite Point of Contact and must clearly list your arrival and departure times. Please upload the signed Lit Networking work order directly to Field Nation. Please be advised that any forged signatures will be reported to Field Nation and will result in non-payment. Adhering to these documentation requirements is essential to avoid any delays in your payment processing. If you encounter any issues while onsite, please leave a detailed message through the Field Nation platform.</p>","markdown":"PLEASE CALL METTEL SUPPORT UPON ARRIVAL 3852623457 Ticket 11745077\n\nCall Travis Newkirk @ 3852623457 when on site.\n\n\\*\\*PIAB Install\\*\\*\n\nTech will need: butt-set, bridge clips, toner, multi-meter, label maker, screw driver.\n\nThis is for a PIAB install. CROSS CONNECT REQUIRED.\n\nInstall/mount equipment (CDS-9090, Pano MIMO antenna, hydra cable and 66 block) on the backboard near the network rack. Connect WAN port to store switch 01 port 14 or port 15 if port 14 is unavailable, confirm WAN and LTE connectivity, test line (inbound and outbound) off the CDS-9090 and the 66 block.\n\nCross connect new line from 66 block to the stores downtime phone. This new line will replace the existing line on the phone. Tech may have to tone existing jack. Have store manager confirm downtime phone is working on the new line.\n\nLabel the following and take pictures of each item:\n\nLabel CDS-9090 with 'METTEL'\n\nLabel 66 block cover with 'METTEL xx/xx/xxxx (date of install)'\n\nLabel inside 66 block with each phone number\n\nTake photo of WAN cable connection on the CDS-9090\n\nTake photo of WAN cable connection on the switch port\n\nTake photo of downtime phone, wall jack, switch port\n\nLCON: Dominique Brown 919-200-6460\n\nOnce install is complete, please contact the GAP Network Voice Team at 800-333-7899 Extn: 66645 to checkout and provide a status\n\n-Data Remote CDS-9090\n\n-MiMo Antenna & Bracket Kit\n\n-Tech to locate equipment.\n\n-Locate customer network switch in room switch/router.\n\n-Install MetTel Board and CDS-9090.\n\n-Attach antennas and power on.\n\n-MetTel will validate configurations.\n\n-Connect laptop and run speed tests over LTE. Do not use speedtest.net\n\n-Verify dial tone and in/outbound calling on all provisioned CDS9090 RJ11 ports.\n\n-Validate e911 address on one each line.\n\n-Use multimeter to verify each existing pair has a voltage of 0 on customer side of the demark.\n\nIf voltage is found, locate the short/bridge and repair.\n\n-Work with customer to contact the alarms monitoring vendor and have the Fire Panel placed into test mode.\n\n-Locate/tag Elevator, Fire and Burglar lines.\n\n-Cross-connect to Fire Panel, Burglar Panel, and test.\n\n-Contact the fire monitoring vendor to confirm that they are receiving the faults, restoral, low battery and battery restore signals.\n\n-Confirm monitoring vendor sees the correct service address.\n\n.\n\nPlease review the following requirements and protocols for your upcoming assignment with Lit Networking:\n\nTo ensure the successful completion of this site visit, you must arrive with the following tools and materials: - A fully charged laptop with an Ethernet port and a cellphone with a hotspot device. - Cabling tools: Multimeter wire tester, butt set, punch down tool, crimpers, and wire cutters. - Hardware: RJ11 and RJ45 connectors, biscuit jacks, and 100 feet of Cat 5e/6 cable for potential device relocation. - Standard mounting kit: Drill, level, hammer, screwdrivers, screws, and anchors. - General supplies: Adjustable or open-end wrenches, a 4–6 ft ladder, and a 100 ft extension cord.\n\nWork Order and Payment Procedures All work orders must be signed by the onsite Point of Contact and must clearly list your arrival and departure times. Please upload the signed Lit Networking work order directly to Field Nation. Please be advised that any forged signatures will be reported to Field Nation and will result in non-payment. Adhering to these documentation requirements is essential to avoid any delays in your payment processing. If you encounter any issues while onsite, please leave a detailed message through the Field Nation platform.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-11T10:00","end":"2026-09-11T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":141.5,"max":141.5},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":120},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":8},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 9/11/2026, 10:00:00 AM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-11T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-11T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-12T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-12T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-15T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-11T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-12T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-09-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-12T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"FN"},{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"},{"start":"2026-09-11T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-11T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"SMALL BACKBOARD/ DATA REMOTE INSTALL/ MUST HAVE BUTT-SET/MULTIMETER-DIS148477"},{"start":"2026-09-10T19:00:00.000Z","end":"20