{"job":{"id":19941919,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"StrikeCheck","title":"Express Damage Assessment - StrikeCheck Appointment A-2712941","description":{"html":"<p>*Please make sure to read through all instructions to avoid a second visit to the property and/or non-payment*</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The following items need to be <strong><em>documented</em></strong>, <strong><em>inspected</em></strong>, <strong><em>tested</em></strong> and <strong><em>photographed, even if they are found to be non-damaged</em></strong>:</p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(32, 33, 36);\"><b><ul><li>Garage Door Opener : Brand Unknown : 1</li></ul></b></span></p><p><br></p><p><strong>ATTENTION: Every technician must use the CCG IQ Inspection Wizard to submit their findings. We cannot complete our payment to you if the findings are submitted to the Field Nation platform or via email. All findings, including non-damaged items on your list, must be sent directly to StrikeCheck using our CCG IQ Inspection Wizard via our Android app or web portal. If any item cannot be documented you must include a statement in your notes explaining those circumstances.</strong></p><p><strong>If you are unsure of how to use our Android app or web portal, or are having issues while you are onsite, please call (888) 980-8544 and a live representative will talk you through the submission process. Android users will need to download the \"CCG IQ Inspection Wizard\" in the app store on your device. Our office hours are 8am-8pm EST Monday-Friday and 8am-5pm on Saturdays. If no one is available to take your call please leave a message and we will return your call ASAP!</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>Testing and Documentation Requirements:</strong></p><ol><li>Full testing and documentation procedures on a per-item type basis can be found under the “Resources” tab in our web app. Select “StrikeCheck” in the “Libraries” folder to review the requirements before every inspection to ensure all required data is being captured.</li><li>Basic continuity/ohm testing is required using a digital multimeter. Verify a functional power source or outlet with your meter and document those readings. If needed, reset any associated circuit breakers but do not otherwise alter the electrical panel.&nbsp;</li><li>Apply power and operationally test ALL FUNCTIONS of every item. Notate any connected items (speakers to receiver, cameras to DVR, etc.) and advise if further testing is necessary due to the failure of one of those components (\"Can't test speakers due to damaged receiver\").&nbsp;</li><li>Document and photograph all obtainable readings/testing. <strong>If the item is not damaged or has already been replaced with new equipment, we still need the same amount of evidence (photos and test results) to support your findings.</strong> If the item is not operating properly, determine the causation of damage.&nbsp;</li><li>In addition to photos of the loss location and your meter readings, we require that you provide a minimum of 3 pictures per item. These pictures should illustrate where/how the item is installed, the overall condition of the item, any visual damages, and <strong><em>most importantly, </em></strong>the data plate. Also photograph any associated components connected to the item you are inspecting. Additional photographs and documentation are always encouraged.</li></ol><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Inspection Requirements:</strong></p><ul><li>A smart phone with access to our Android app or web app portal for Apple iOS users is the preferred method to document and upload your findings in real time. Access the app or portal before the inspection begins and it will walk you through all steps required for each item you enter.</li><li>Use of a camera and our Technician Worksheets is an alternate option that will require a computer to access the web app portal in order to upload photos as well as transcribing your detailed technical documentation from the worksheets into our system.</li><li>Multimeter/VOM and a basic toolkit</li><li>Must be professionally dressed (wear a clean collared shirt and pants; No shorts, no t-shirts, no flip-flops, and no ripped jeans). Avoid wearing anything that will identify your personal employer/company name or contact info to prevent insureds from calling you directly after you complete your assignment. This is an independent inspection on behalf of StrikeCheck, an insurance consulting company. <strong>You</strong> <strong>must represent yourself as being with StrikeCheck</strong> <strong>when you arrive onsite</strong>.</li><li>Must be willing to display contractor photo identification (if issued) and must have appropriate background and skills to perform the listed work order requirements</li><li>Must have passed a background check and drug test.&nbsp;</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Submission Requirements:</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>iPhone/iPad users: Upload required information via our <strong>web portal</strong> the same day as the inspection using a secure password. Click the \"Login\" link below or use this web address to access the portal:&nbsp;https://consolidatedclaims.my.site.com/ccginspector/&nbsp;</li><li>All findings, pictures, and determinations should be submitted on the same day as the inspection. <strong>Your deadline to submit is 24 hours from the scheduled appointment start time. Failure to do so may result in non-payment and could affect your rating.</strong></li><li>Your work order is not considered complete and payable until findings are submitted through the Android app or web portal and is approved by our Processing Department. Please make yourself available for follow-up calls if we have any questions regarding your findings.</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">Scheduling Requirements:</strong></p><ul><li>These work orders most likely take place in a residential property, and therefore requires the ETA to be approved by the client.</li><li>When you are assigned this work order, please submit an ETA as soon as possible.</li><li>We will reach out to the client to confirm that they are able to be onsite during your proposed ETA. <strong><u>The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.</u></strong></li><li>A project manager will message you via the Field Nation App when the ETA has been confirmed with the insured. If you go to the loss location before we confirm the appointment is set, you will not be afforded a trip fee in the event that the insured is not present when you arrive.</li><li><strong>You must update our project managers and dispatch coordinators regularly on work order progress, any service delays, or schedule conflicts. If you cannot make an appointment CALL OUR OFFICE IMMEDIATELY TO RESCHEDULE. Field Nation messages are not an accepted medium for rescheduling or canceling appointments!</strong></li><li>If you go to the property, but the client does not show for the appointment, call us immediately so we can follow up with the client and determine if they will be arriving soon. <strong>If the client misses the appointment, you must take a clear photo of the house/property, showing the address so we can confirm you were there.</strong></li><li>StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the insured cannot make the appointment.&nbsp;</li><li>StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the scope of work cannot be completed for any reason</li><li>StrikeCheck will <em>not </em>provide a trip fee if you arrive at an appointment that has <em>not </em>been confirmed with the client and the project manager. <strong><u>The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.</u></strong></li></ul>","markdown":"\\*Please make sure to read through all instructions to avoid a second visit to the property and/or non-payment\\*\n\nThe following items need to be ***documented***, ***inspected***, ***tested*** and ***photographed, even if they are found to be non-damaged***:\n\n**- Garage Door Opener : Brand Unknown : 1**\n\n**ATTENTION: Every technician must use the CCG IQ Inspection Wizard to submit their findings. We cannot complete our payment to you if the findings are submitted to the Field Nation platform or via email. All findings, including non-damaged items on your list, must be sent directly to StrikeCheck using our CCG IQ Inspection Wizard via our Android app or web portal. If any item cannot be documented you must include a statement in your notes explaining those circumstances.**\n\n**If you are unsure of how to use our Android app or web portal, or are having issues while you are onsite, please call (888) 980-8544 and a live representative will talk you through the submission process. Android users will need to download the \"CCG IQ Inspection Wizard\" in the app store on your device. Our office hours are 8am-8pm EST Monday-Friday and 8am-5pm on Saturdays. If no one is available to take your call please leave a message and we will return your call ASAP!**\n\n**Testing and Documentation Requirements:**\n\n1. Full testing and documentation procedures on a per-item type basis can be found under the “Resources” tab in our web app. Select “StrikeCheck” in the “Libraries” folder to review the requirements before every inspection to ensure all required data is being captured.\n2. Basic continuity/ohm testing is required using a digital multimeter. Verify a functional power source or outlet with your meter and document those readings. If needed, reset any associated circuit breakers but do not otherwise alter the electrical panel.\n3. Apply power and operationally test ALL FUNCTIONS of every item. Notate any connected items (speakers to receiver, cameras to DVR, etc.) and advise if further testing is necessary due to the failure of one of those components (\"Can't test speakers due to damaged receiver\").\n4. Document and photograph all obtainable readings/testing. **If the item is not damaged or has already been replaced with new equipment, we still need the same amount of evidence (photos and test results) to support your findings.** If the item is not operating properly, determine the causation of damage.\n5. In addition to photos of the loss location and your meter readings, we require that you provide a minimum of 3 pictures per item. These pictures should illustrate where/how the item is installed, the overall condition of the item, any visual damages, and ***most importantly,*** the data plate. Also photograph any associated components connected to the item you are inspecting. Additional photographs and documentation are always encouraged.\n\n**Inspection Requirements:**\n\n- A smart phone with access to our Android app or web app portal for Apple iOS users is the preferred method to document and upload your findings in real time. Access the app or portal before the inspection begins and it will walk you through all steps required for each item you enter.\n- Use of a camera and our Technician Worksheets is an alternate option that will require a computer to access the web app portal in order to upload photos as well as transcribing your detailed technical documentation from the worksheets into our system.\n- Multimeter/VOM and a basic toolkit\n- Must be professionally dressed (wear a clean collared shirt and pants; No shorts, no t-shirts, no flip-flops, and no ripped jeans). Avoid wearing anything that will identify your personal employer/company name or contact info to prevent insureds from calling you directly after you complete your assignment. This is an independent inspection on behalf of StrikeCheck, an insurance consulting company. **You** **must represent yourself as being with StrikeCheck** **when you arrive onsite**.\n- Must be willing to display contractor photo identification (if issued) and must have appropriate background and skills to perform the listed work order requirements\n- Must have passed a background check and drug test.\n\n**Submission Requirements:**\n\n- iPhone/iPad users: Upload required information via our **web portal** the same day as the inspection using a secure password. Click the \"Login\" link below or use this web address to access the portal: <https://consolidatedclaims.my.site.com/ccginspector/&nbsp;>\n- All findings, pictures, and determinations should be submitted on the same day as the inspection. **Your deadline to submit is 24 hours from the scheduled appointment start time. Failure to do so may result in non-payment and could affect your rating.**\n- Your work order is not considered complete and payable until findings are submitted through the Android app or web portal and is approved by our Processing Department. Please make yourself available for follow-up calls if we have any questions regarding your findings.\n\n**Scheduling Requirements:**\n\n- These work orders most likely take place in a residential property, and therefore requires the ETA to be approved by the client.\n- When you are assigned this work order, please submit an ETA as soon as possible.\n- We will reach out to the client to confirm that they are able to be onsite during your proposed ETA. **The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.**\n- A project manager will message you via the Field Nation App when the ETA has been confirmed with the insured. If you go to the loss location before we confirm the appointment is set, you will not be afforded a trip fee in the event that the insured is not present when you arrive.\n- **You must update our project managers and dispatch coordinators regularly on work order progress, any service delays, or schedule conflicts. If you cannot make an appointment CALL OUR OFFICE IMMEDIATELY TO RESCHEDULE. Field Nation messages are not an accepted medium for rescheduling or canceling appointments!**\n- If you go to the property, but the client does not show for the appointment, call us immediately so we can follow up with the client and determine if they will be arriving soon. **If the client misses the appointment, you must take a clear photo of the house/property, showing the address so we can confirm you were there.**\n- StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the insured cannot make the appointment.\n- StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the scope of work cannot be completed for any reason\n- StrikeCheck will *not* provide a trip fee if you arrive at an appointment that has *not* been confirmed with the client and the project manager. **The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-12T12:00","end":"2026-09-12T14:00","latestStart":"2026-09-12T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":21},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 9/12/2026, 12:00:00 PM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-15T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-12T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"FN"},{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"},{"start":"2026-09-11T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-11T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"SMALL BACKBOARD/ DATA REMOTE INSTALL/ MUST HAVE BUTT-SET/MULTIMETER-DIS148477"},{"start":"2026-09-10T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-10T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Maintenance Kit Swap - Apex, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-04T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-05T13:30:00.000Z","summary":"DSS 9223 - Install (1) QNAP + UPS + Switch, Install (3) TP-Link Wireless Bridge, Install (3) 8 Port PoE Switch, Replace (15) Analog Cameras w/ (15) IP Cameras + Cable Runs - Lead Tech"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789385003243}
{"job":{"id":19941870,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Loopdrive LLC","title":"Smart Home - Door Lock Swap","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Summary:</u></strong><u>&nbsp;</u></p><p>Follow the instructions &amp; guidelines below to replace a smart home door lock, . <u>Do not attempt pairing on your own.</u> Contact the support line for pairing/configuration. Occasionally, Sensors may need to be paired or installed and paired. If needed, this typically adds only about 5 minutes. Sensors are applied with doubled sticky tape and pulling a battery tab. DO NOT DISCUSS OR DEMAND PAY CHANGE WITH SUPPORT TEAM.</p><p>------------------------------</p><p><strong><u>Smart Home Job Requirements &amp; Guidelines</u></strong></p><p><strong>﻿</strong><em>By accepting this order, you agree to follow all outlined requirements and guidelines. </em><strong><em>Failure to comply may result in the order being closed without compensation.</em></strong></p><ul><li><strong>Help Line Availability</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">The Smart Home Help Line is available <strong>only between 9:00 AM and 5:00 PM EST</strong>.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If you arrive onsite too late for them to complete pairing on their end, the visit will need to be <strong>rescheduled—without additional compensation.</strong></li><li><strong>Professional Conduct</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Treat the Resident &amp; Smart Home Help Line staff with respect—they are a small team handling a high volume of repairs and are also our client. <strong>Disrespectful behavior may result in removal from the site without pay.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Orders are not considered complete until the Smart Home team has confirmed that all functional devices are properly paired and online.<strong>Completion Requirement</strong></li><li><strong>Help Line Availability</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If you can’t reach support right away, keep trying for at least 15 minutes. If there’s still no answer, contact the site manager for next steps.</li><li><strong>Scope Changes &amp; Compensation</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If the scope changes during the visit (e.g., another device is accidentally knocked offline), <strong>we may approve additional pay</strong>.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">To qualify, you must provide the following:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Photos of any <strong>additional devices</strong> serviced</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>Timestamped arrival and departure</strong> photos</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">A clear <strong>written closing statement</strong> detailing the added work</li><li><strong>Unable to Complete – Eligible Trip Fee Scenarios</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">You may request a <strong>$35 trip fee</strong>, but <strong>full payment will not be approved</strong> since the order was not completed.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>Resident no-show or refusal of access</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>Unrestrained dogs present</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>Inhospitable or unsafe environment</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>Power outage</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>Missing or incorrect parts</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Before leaving the site</strong>, you must:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>Call the site manager</strong> so we can attempt to resolve the issue.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Provide a <strong>timestamped photo of the front of the home</strong>, and if applicable, document the issue with additional photos or notes.</li><li><strong>Late Arrival Fee</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Arrival times are coordinated with the Smart Home team. If you arrive late, a <strong>$10 fee will be deducted</strong> from your pay. Please plan accordingly and arrive on time.</li><li><strong>Authorized Personnel</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Only the technician assigned to the work order is allowed on site. Do not bring children, friends, coworkers, employees, or assistants.</li></ul><p>------------------------------</p><p><strong><u>Instructions:</u></strong></p><ol><li>For this repair&nbsp;<strong>please identify yourself as a contractor working for Diamond Property Services,&nbsp;</strong>rather than Field Nation or your own company.</li><li><strong>Confirm Start Time in FN.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If you cannot keep your appointment, contact the site manager at 865-776-2593 immediately.</li><li><strong>Upon arrival</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Take a&nbsp;<strong>time-stamped</strong>&nbsp;<strong>photo</strong>&nbsp;of the home.&nbsp;<u>This is required to receive any additional allowances.</u></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Introduce yourself to the tenant and let them know you are there on behalf of&nbsp;<strong>Diamond Property Services</strong>&nbsp;to perform a smart home repair.</li><li><strong>Replace Device(s):</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>(1) Yale Pro 2 Smart Lock</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Likely removing this lock:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-3\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ciHoxeXDJjE</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Likely installing this lock:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-3\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e1Z0J-ZwmQc</li><li><strong>Prepare Doorlock for Pairing</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>If batteries are Horizontal (left to right), follow these steps:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Press and hold black button on back of unit</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">While holding the black button, press the gear button on the front (Gear &amp; 1 key should light up)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Release black button on back of unit.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Press these buttons: 1, gear, 1,8,6,5 (1865 is now the master code)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">The unit should light up and lock. The unit is now ready for pairing.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>If batteries are Vertical (up &amp; down)</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Press gear, 1, gear, 1,8,6,5</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">1865 is now the master code</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>If you cannot get the door lock into pairing mode, call the site manager before calling support.</u></strong></li><li><strong>Do not attempt to pair these devices on your own.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Pairing must be done through the property manager's smart home app.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><u>Call the Support Hotline at&nbsp;</u><strong><u>330-970-2020</u></strong>. Identify yourself as calling on behalf of&nbsp;<strong>Diamond Property Services</strong>, and have the property address ready.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If the hotline is busy, keep trying for 10 minutes.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If you are unable to reach the Support Hotline, contact the site manager at 865-776-2593 and explain the issue.</li><li><strong>Once you're cleared by the support hotline</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Gather all required documentation listed below.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Upload everything to Field Nation to complete the work order.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>Required Deliverables:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Time stamped arrival</strong>&nbsp;<strong>photo</strong>&nbsp;of the front of residence showing the address.</li><li>Photos of all devices you installed/paired</li><li>Screenshot of your call log with support.</li><li>Photo of the tenants app showing the device(s) paired</li><li><strong>Time stamped departure</strong>&nbsp;<strong>photo</strong>&nbsp;of the front of residence showing the address.</li><li>A resolution statement:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Arrival time:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">What you did:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Who you speak with:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">What happened:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">What they said:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Departure time:</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Estimated Time:&nbsp;</strong>Less than 1 hour.</p>","markdown":"**Summary:**\n\nFollow the instructions & guidelines below to replace a smart home door lock, . Do not attempt pairing on your own. Contact the support line for pairing/configuration. Occasionally, Sensors may need to be paired or installed and paired. If needed, this typically adds only about 5 minutes. Sensors are applied with doubled sticky tape and pulling a battery tab. DO NOT DISCUSS OR DEMAND PAY CHANGE WITH SUPPORT TEAM.\n\n\\------------------------------\n\n**Smart Home Job Requirements & Guidelines**\n\n**﻿***By accepting this order, you agree to follow all outlined requirements and guidelines.* ***Failure to comply may result in the order being closed without compensation.***\n\n- **Help Line Availability**\n- The Smart Home Help Line is available **only between 9:00 AM and 5:00 PM EST**.\n- If you arrive onsite too late for them to complete pairing on their end, the visit will need to be **rescheduled—without additional compensation.**\n- **Professional Conduct**\n- Treat the Resident & Smart Home Help Line staff with respect—they are a small team handling a high volume of repairs and are also our client. **Disrespectful behavior may result in removal from the site without pay.**\n- Orders are not considered complete until the Smart Home team has confirmed that all functional devices are properly paired and online.**Completion Requirement**\n- **Help Line Availability**\n- If you can’t reach support right away, keep trying for at least 15 minutes. If there’s still no answer, contact the site manager for next steps.\n- **Scope Changes & Compensation**\n- If the scope changes during the visit (e.g., another device is accidentally knocked offline), **we may approve additional pay**.\n- To qualify, you must provide the following:\n- Photos of any **additional devices** serviced\n- **Timestamped arrival and departure** photos\n- A clear **written closing statement** detailing the added work\n- **Unable to Complete – Eligible Trip Fee Scenarios**\n- You may request a **$35 trip fee**, but **full payment will not be approved** since the order was not completed.\n- **Resident no-show or refusal of access**\n- **Unrestrained dogs present**\n- **Inhospitable or unsafe environment**\n- **Power outage**\n- **Missing or incorrect parts**\n- **Before leaving the site**, you must:\n- **Call the site manager** so we can attempt to resolve the issue.\n- Provide a **timestamped photo of the front of the home**, and if applicable, document the issue with additional photos or notes.\n- **Late Arrival Fee**\n- Arrival times are coordinated with the Smart Home team. If you arrive late, a **$10 fee will be deducted** from your pay. Please plan accordingly and arrive on time.\n- **Authorized Personnel**\n- Only the technician assigned to the work order is allowed on site. Do not bring children, friends, coworkers, employees, or assistants.\n\n\\------------------------------\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. For this repair **please identify yourself as a contractor working for Diamond Property Services,** rather than Field Nation or your own company.\n2. **Confirm Start Time in FN.**\n3. If you cannot keep your appointment, contact the site manager at 865-776-2593 immediately.\n4. **Upon arrival**\n5. Take a **time-stamped** **photo** of the home. This is required to receive any additional allowances.\n6. Introduce yourself to the tenant and let them know you are there on behalf of **Diamond Property Services** to perform a smart home repair.\n7. **Replace Device(s):**\n8. **(1) Yale Pro 2 Smart Lock**\n9. Likely removing this lock:\n10. <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ciHoxeXDJjE>\n11. Likely installing this lock:\n12. <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e1Z0J-ZwmQc>\n13. **Prepare Doorlock for Pairing**\n14. **If batteries are Horizontal (left to right), follow these steps:**\n15. Press and hold black button on back of unit\n16. While holding the black button, press the gear button on the front (Gear & 1 key should light up)\n17. Release black button on back of unit.\n18. Press these buttons: 1, gear, 1,8,6,5 (1865 is now the master code)\n19. The unit should light up and lock. The unit is now ready for pairing.\n20. **If batteries are Vertical (up & down)**\n21. Press gear, 1, gear, 1,8,6,5\n22. 1865 is now the master code\n23. **If you cannot get the door lock into pairing mode, call the site manager before calling support.**\n24. **Do not attempt to pair these devices on your own.**\n25. Pairing must be done through the property manager's smart home app.\n26. Call the Support Hotline at **330-970-2020**. Identify yourself as calling on behalf of **Diamond Property Services**, and have the property address ready.\n27. If the hotline is busy, keep trying for 10 minutes.\n28. If you are unable to reach the Support Hotline, contact the site manager at 865-776-2593 and explain the issue.\n29. **Once you're cleared by the support hotline**\n30. Gather all required documentation listed below.\n31. Upload everything to Field Nation to complete the work order.\n\n**Required Deliverables:**\n\n- **Time stamped arrival** **photo** of the front of residence showing the address.\n- Photos of all devices you installed/paired\n- Screenshot of your call log with support.\n- Photo of the tenants app showing the device(s) paired\n- **Time stamped departure** **photo** of the front of residence showing the address.\n- A resolution statement:\n- Arrival time:\n- What you did:\n- Who you speak with:\n- What happened:\n- What they said:\n- Departure time:\n\n**Estimated Time:** Less than 1 hour.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-22T09:00","end":"2026-09-22T10:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":60},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":37},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $60 is below minimum threshold $350"