ntroduce yourself. Inform them that you are onsite to conduct Front End Preventative Maintenance.\n3. Validate inventory and give the return labels to the Manager in Charge. Ask them to keep the labels at the bridge.\n\n**INSTALLATION PROCEDURE**\n\n**NOTE: DO NOT PROCEED WITH ANY STEPS UNTIL INSTRUCTED BY REMOTE SUPPORT**\n\n1. For each lane:\n2. Vacuum the top and inside of the check stand including removing the scanner and vacuuming out the well. Remove any equipment, papers etc. before vacuuming according to the provided instructions.\n3. Reroute the cash drawer cable to the POS according to the provided instructions.\n4. Wipe down all technology surfaces, removing all dust or grime.\n5. For customer service area (Bridge)\n6. Vacuum the top and inside cubbies of the bridge. Remove any equipment, papers etc. before vacuuming according to the provided instructions.\n7. Wipe down all technology both inside and on top of the bridge removing all dust and grime. Canned air and cleaning supplies provided.\n8. For laptop carts\n9. Vacuum the top and shelves of the cart.\n10. Wipe down all surfaces, removing all dust or grime.\n11. Securely box all unused equipment, attach the provided return label, and hand the box to the Mate in Charge.\n\n**CLEANUP & DEPARTURE INSTRUCTIONS**\n\n1. Using your camera, take pictures of the completed work (details in the attached installation documentation) and upload them to your work order\n2. Give the return shipping boxes to the Manager in Charge.\n3. Gather your tools and checkout with remote support.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-15T21:30","end":"2026-09-15T23:30"},"payRange":{"min":105,"max":205},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":105},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":3},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"📅 Requested schedule unavailable; a later date was considered.\nAlternative: Sep 16, 1:00 PM (Eastern)\n💸 Alternative-date minimum: $250 · listed maximum: $205\nRejected: pay does not meet the alternative-date minimum."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-15T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-17T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"},{"start":"2026-09-11T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-11T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"SMALL BACKBOARD/ DATA REMOTE INSTALL/ MUST HAVE BUTT-SET/MULTIMETER-DIS148477"},{"start":"2026-09-10T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-10T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Maintenance Kit Swap - Apex, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-04T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-05T13:30:00.000Z","summary":"DSS 9223 - Install (1) QNAP + UPS + Switch, Install (3) TP-Link Wireless Bridge, Install (3) 8 Port PoE Switch, Replace (15) Analog Cameras w/ (15) IP Cameras + Cable Runs - Lead Tech"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789395466010}
{"job":{"id":19897210,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"BlueSky IT Partners","title":"Maintenance Kit Swap - Apex, NC","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>SOW Summary:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>target printer is at Apex NC not Brier NC, both had Host 2 printers jamming with paper stuck in -INC3737642 showed Brier as location but this ticket is actually for Apex NC branch Host 2. Requesting (1) technician arrive on site to service using the maintenance kit provided already at the branch. Instructions for swap can also be sent from myself.</li>\n<li><strong>See the confidential section for additional information</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Onsite Steps</u></strong>:&nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Step 1: Call BlueSky Work Order Manager by phone to check in BEFORE going inside or contacting customer!&nbsp;Get a CHECK-IN CODE.&nbsp;Review the CONFIDENTIAL INFO section for any added info for this job.</li>\n<li>Step 2: Meet local contact. Get their name.&nbsp;Call technical support to complete work as outlined below.&nbsp;Get name of main Tech Support rep(s) you work with.</li>\n<li>Step 3: Complete any required documents/pictures.</li>\n<li>Step 4: Verify full operation with the local customer and support team before leaving the site</li>\n<li>Step 5; Upload all required pictures and deliverables to this work order and enter your closing notes WHILE STILL ONSITE.&nbsp;The BlueSky WO Mgr will review site pictures and may ask for a few more if needed.</li>\n<li>Step 6: After your site pictures are uploaded to this job, CALL the Bluesky Work Order Manager by phone to check out BEFORE LEAVING SITE!&nbsp;Get a CHECK-OUT CODE!.&nbsp;<strong>THIS IS REQUIRED FOR FULL PAYMENT.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Note to the technician(s) - BlueSky does show numerous penalties, these are due to the 1% of technicians who cause issues onsite. With proper communication before, during, and after the dispatch BlueSky can waive penalties and add bonuses. Please do not assume this will automatically apply to the work order you are working for us.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Overview</u></strong><u>:</u></p>\n<p>As we navigate the never-ending changes due to the worldwide pandemic, we are all faced with new work and safety obstacles. BlueSky is committed to providing a safe work environment for everyone without having to cut costs for our technicians. Please refer to the changes in our pay structure outlined below.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Field Nation fees are a cost associated with the technicians and are deductible on your taxes. BlueSky is assessed taxes on work orders separately. In an attempt to keep costs down, BlueSky does not pass the taxes onto the technicians and will not reimburse technicians for their fees.</li>\n<li>Flat rate offers are not accepted, They must be broken down to itemize hourly pay.</li>\n<li>All technicians/providers MUST have their own Field Nation profile. If you are a service company, the work order must be reassigned to servicing technician/provider PRIOR to arrival - no exceptions</li>\n<li>It is<strong>&nbsp;IMPERATIVE THAT YOU ARRIVE AT THE SCHEDULED TIME. This cannot be stressed enough</strong></li>\n<li>If you have any issues on site,&nbsp;<strong>contact Blue Sky work order contact immediately</strong></li>\n<li>Onsite contact is limited to MOD/LCON only.&nbsp;<strong>Do not socialize with support staff</strong></li>\n<li>All required deliverables and close-out notes must be provided while the technician is still onsite. This is to ensure all necessary data is received and the technician is paid for his/her time</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Required tools:</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>REQUIRED LAPTOP</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Internet Connectivity (WIFI Hotspot)</li>\n<li>Windows 7 or 10 Laptop with 1Gb Ethernet port</li>\n<li>Active Email Address</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>REQUIRED SOFTWARE</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Teamviewer 12; HyperTerminal, Putty or TeraTerm</li>\n<li>Microsoft Word, Excel</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>REQUIRED CABLES</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Ethernet Patch Cables</li>\n<li>Cisco Console Cable</li>\n<li>USB to DB9</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>REQUIRED TELECOM TOOLS</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Buttset</li>\n<li>RJ11/RJ45 Crimper (crimper ends and bulk cable)</li>\n<li>Snips/Diagonal cutter</li>\n<li>66/110 Punchdown Tool</li>\n<li>Probe/Toner</li>\n<li>Zipties or Velcro (PREFERRED)</li>\n<li>Screwdrivers or Cordless Drill with assorted bits and screws for mounting equipment</li>\n<li>Stepladder</li>\n<li>Cell Phone with camera</li>\n<li>Label Maker</li>\n<li>Proper PPE Gear (Facemasks, hand sanitizer, gloves)</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong><u>Required pictures/deliverables TO BE UPLOADED WHILE STILL ON SITE:</u></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Pictures of the work area before starting.</li>\n<li>Pictures of the server room, network rack, and equipment.</li>\n<li>Pictures of the equipment worked on installed and operating properly.</li>\n<li>List all Conference Call Personnel and their Departments in your Close Out Notes</li>\n<li>Provide info and Upload pictures of all installed, removed, and or existing equipment Serial Numbers</li>\n<li>Any speed tests results</li>\n<li>Pictures of the work area after clean-up.</li>\n</ol>","markdown":"**SOW Summary:**\n\n- target printer is at Apex NC not Brier NC, both had Host 2 printers jamming with paper stuck in -INC3737642 showed Brier as location but this ticket is actually for Apex NC branch Host 2. Requesting (1) technician arrive on site to service using the maintenance kit provided already at the branch. Instructions for swap can also be sent from myself.\n- **See the confidential section for additional information**\n\n**Onsite Steps**:\n\n- Step 1: Call BlueSky Work Order Manager by phone to check in BEFORE going inside or contacting customer! Get a CHECK-IN CODE. Review the CONFIDENTIAL INFO section for any added info for this job.\n- Step 2: Meet local contact. Get their name. Call technical support to complete work as outlined below. Get name of main Tech Support rep(s) you work with.\n- Step 3: Complete any required documents/pictures.\n- Step 4: Verify full operation with the local customer and support team before leaving the site\n- Step 5; Upload all required pictures and deliverables to this work order and enter your closing notes WHILE STILL ONSITE. The BlueSky WO Mgr will review site pictures and may ask for a few more if needed.\n- Step 6: After your site pictures are uploaded to this job, CALL the Bluesky Work Order Manager by phone to check out BEFORE LEAVING SITE! Get a CHECK-OUT CODE!. **THIS IS REQUIRED FOR FULL PAYMENT.**\n- **Note to the technician(s) - BlueSky does show numerous penalties, these are due to the 1% of technicians who cause issues onsite. With proper communication before, during, and after the dispatch BlueSky can waive penalties and add bonuses. Please do not assume this will automatically apply to the work order you are working for us.**\n\n**Overview**:\n\nAs we navigate the never-ending changes due to the worldwide pandemic, we are all faced with new work and safety obstacles. BlueSky is committed to providing a safe work environment for everyone without having to cut costs for our technicians. Please refer to the changes in our pay structure outlined below.\n\n- Field Nation fees are a cost associated with the technicians and are deductible on your taxes. BlueSky is assessed taxes on work orders separately. In an attempt to keep costs down, BlueSky does not pass the taxes onto the technicians and will not reimburse technicians for their fees.\n- Flat rate offers are not accepted, They must be broken down to itemize hourly pay.\n- All technicians/providers MUST have their own Field Nation profile. If you are a service company, the work order must be reassigned to servicing technician/provider PRIOR to arrival - no exceptions\n- It is **IMPERATIVE THAT YOU ARRIVE AT THE SCHEDULED TIME. This cannot be stressed enough**\n- If you have any issues on site, **contact Blue Sky work order contact immediately**\n- Onsite contact is limited to MOD/LCON only. **Do not socialize with support staff**\n- All required deliverables and close-out notes must be provided while the technician is still onsite. This is to ensure all necessary data is received and the technician is paid for his/her time\n\n**Required tools:**\n\n**REQUIRED LAPTOP**\n\n1. Internet Connectivity (WIFI Hotspot)\n2. Windows 7 or 10 Laptop with 1Gb Ethernet port\n3. Active Email Address\n\n**REQUIRED SOFTWARE**\n\n1. Teamviewer 12; HyperTerminal, Putty or TeraTerm\n2. Microsoft Word, Excel\n\n**REQUIRED CABLES**\n\n1. Ethernet Patch Cables\n2. Cisco Console Cable\n3. USB to DB9\n\n**REQUIRED TELECOM TOOLS**\n\n1. Buttset\n2. RJ11/RJ45 Crimper (crimper ends and bulk cable)\n3. Snips/Diagonal cutter\n4. 66/110 Punchdown Tool\n5. Probe/Toner\n6. Zipties or Velcro (PREFERRED)\n7. Screwdrivers or Cordless Drill with assorted bits and screws for mounting equipment\n8. Stepladder\n9. Cell Phone with camera\n10. Label Maker\n11. Proper PPE Gear (Facemasks, hand sanitizer, gloves)\n\n**Required pictures/deliverables TO BE UPLOADED WHILE STILL ON SITE:**\n\n1. Pictures of the work area before starting.\n2. Pictures of the server room, network rack, and equipment.\n3. Pictures of the equipment worked on installed and operating properly.\n4. List all Conference Call Personnel and their Departments in your Close Out Notes\n5. Provide info and Upload pictures of all installed, removed, and or existing equipment Serial Numbers\n6. Any speed tests results\n7. Pictures of the work area after clean-up.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-10T15:00","end":"2026-09-10T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":97,"max":486},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":97.2,"estLaborHours":5,"distance":10},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 9/10/2026, 3:00:00 PM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-10T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-10T17:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-10T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-11T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-11T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-11T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-12T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-12T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-10T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-10T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-09-11T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-12T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-09-12T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-12T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay bills BoA + Amex"},{"start":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"FN"},{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"},{"start":"2026-09-11T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-11T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"SMALL BACKBOARD/ DATA REMOTE INSTALL/ MUST HAVE BUTT-SET/MULTIMETER-DIS148477"},{"start":"2026-09-04T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-05T13:30:00.000Z","summary":"DSS 9223 - Install (1) QNAP + UPS + Switch, Install (3) TP-Link Wireless Bridge, Install (3) 8 Port PoE Switch, Replace (15) Analog Cameras w/ (15) IP Cameras + Cable Runs - Lead Tech"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789395552272}
{"job":{"id":19946306,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Essintial","title":"Device Courier -  Pick Up and Drop Off | 2 DATES/TIMES REQUIRED FROM TECH","description":{"html":"<p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">**</span><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">Tech needs to provide 2 dates/times they are available**</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">YOUR WORK ORDER ONLY COVERS ONE VISIT TO SITE. IF CUSTOMER REQUIRES A RETURN VISIT YOU **MUST** HAVE ANOTHER WORK ORDER. TIME LOGGED FOR ADDITIONAL DAYS ONSITE WILL BE REJECTED FOR NOT FOLLOWING PROCESSES. </span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs97C2AA46\">Important: Onsite Time is measured from arrival time at FedEx, transit time from FedEx to Site, restock, and then drop-off at Fedex for Return.]</span></p><ul style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;\">\n\t\t\t<li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">Technicians Labor Times&nbsp;Start Time</span><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;- is when they&nbsp;</span><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">ARRIVE</span><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;at&nbsp;</span><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">local FEDEX HOLD&nbsp;[ not when they arrive onsite ]</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">Check-In upon arrival at FEDEX&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">Technicians Labor&nbsp;End Time</span><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;-&nbsp;is</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">If technicians&nbsp;</span><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">HAS defective equipment to return</span><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;- their labor ends when they drop equipment off at FedEx</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">Check-Out upon leaving FedEx&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">If Technicians&nbsp;</span><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">DOES NOT have defective equipment to return</span><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;- their labor ends when they are finished at site.&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">Check-Out upon leaving the site&nbsp;</span></li></ul>\n\t\t<p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">Required On-site time/window:</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">Equipment:</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">Make/Model: OTH</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">Serial Number: {SRM_FN.SERIAL}</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">Problem Description:</span><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\"> For Essinsial: This is a refill request for 6 devices. Please collect the Package from Fed-Ex and assist with placing the laptops in the lockers and taking out the defective laptops. Please prepare additional time if we need to rearrange the lockers. The Refill ticket will be logged after we have agreed on a date for the visit, as Fed-Ex will only hold a package for up to 5 days. Once you reach BASF, please call us from Talkative by clicking on &quot;Click to support&quot;</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9AD462FD\">***Scope of Work Instructions***</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs3232DC9D\">General </span><span class=\"csEFAFD4EB\">Scope of Work</span><span class=\"cs97C2AA46\">:&nbsp;</span><span class=\"csC2DDC91E\">Technician to go and pick up equipment up at local fedex hold, drive to customers site location,&nbsp;work with the HCL VITP - Virtual IT Point via onsite&nbsp;&nbsp;&quot;Talkative Video Calling System&quot; to drop equipment off in customers onsite VITP storage lockers, and if applicable take defective equipment out of lockers and drop off a local FedEx Hold for return to customer.&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs3232DC9D\">Scope of Work Step by Step Instructions:</span></p><ul style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;\">\n\t\t\t<li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">Pick up the laptops from FedEx.</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">Arrive at the BASF office</span><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\"> and use the Talkative machine by selecting </span><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">&ldquo;Click to Support.&rdquo;</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">One of our agents [ </span><span class=\"csC2DDC91E\">HCL VITP - Virtual IT Point Agents ]</span><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\"> will answer the call and guide the technician step‑by‑step.</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"csC2DDC91E\">&quot;Talkative Video Calling System&quot; Process -</span><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\"> </span><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">Refer to the&nbsp;HCL BASF Onsite VITP Process - Return and Replenishment Process:&nbsp;<span class=\"csC1D8CEBD\">https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000003uH9J/cEucV0buMb0kEy.aD.huNaNut7UUrDFEb5FO7Un976U</span></span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">Open the package:</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">Every package contains a </span><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">return label</span><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\"> &mdash; keep this aside for return shipping.</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">There will be an inner box containing the </span><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">new laptop</span><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">.</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">Our agent [ </span><span class=\"csC2DDC91E\">HCL VITP - Virtual IT Point Agents ]</span><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\"> will provide the </span><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">admin PIN</span><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\"> and guide the technician to open the locker.</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">Remove the defective laptop</span><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\"> from the locker.</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">Place the new laptop inside the locker</span><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">, share the </span><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">serial number</span><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">, and close the locker.</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">Ship the defective laptop back to FedEx:</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">Pack the old laptop back into the box.</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">Stick the </span><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">return label</span><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\"> onto the box.</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">Return it at the FedEx location.</span></li></ul>\n\t\t<p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs97C2AA46\">Onsite Virtual IT Point via Onsite &quot;Talkative Video Calling System&quot; Process</span></p><ul style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;\">\n\t\t\t<li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs97C2AA46\">Refer to the&nbsp;HCL BASF Onsite VITP Process - Return and Replenishment Process</span><span class=\"csC2DDC91E\">:&nbsp;</span><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\"><span class=\"csC1D8CEBD\">https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000003uH9J/cEucV0buMb0kEy.aD.huNaNut7UUrDFEb5FO7Un976U</span></span></li></ul>\n\t\t<p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"csB54904E9\">Important Tech Information &amp; Requirements</span></p><ul style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;\">\n\t\t\t<li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">Technicians&nbsp;</span><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">ARE NOT</span><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;to go to site unless equipment is ready for pickup at local FedEx&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">Technicians&nbsp;</span><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">MUST</span><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;Represent themselves as an Essintial Technician on behalf of HCL/BASF</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">Technicians&nbsp;</span><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">MUST</span><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;carry/present BASF Badge while onsite</span></li></ul>\n\t\t<p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">Important Information on Site:</span></p><ul style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;\">\n\t\t\t<li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs7D58027A\">You must represent themselves as an Essintial technician on behalf of HCL/BASF while on site.</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">Technicians&nbsp;</span><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">MUST</span><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;carry/present BASF Badge while onsite</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">Onsite -&nbsp;DO NOT GO ANYWHERE ELSE IN THE BUILDING except to the storage locker and back</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs7D58027A\">These are live environments, and technician must act in a professional manner, taking care not to disrupt business. </span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs7D58027A\">Dress code is business casual; no jeans or holes. Collared or button down shirt, slacks, and nice shoes required.</span></li></ul>\n\t\t<p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">Important Scope/Customer Information:</span></p><ul style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;\">\n\t\t\t<li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">Any changes to ETA&rsquo;s MUST be relayed to the End User and Essintial via phone.</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">If you are unfamiliar with the equipment or a particular repair needed, do not tell the customer this. Call Essintial Support for assistance.&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">If additional parts are needed there will be another trip&nbsp;REQUIRED.&nbsp;You MUST CALL Essintial @ 800-326-6999 to advise. This ticket should be closed and a new work order will be opened.&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">All times provided to Essintial MUST MATCH what is listed in your work order as well as any required sign off forms.&nbsp;</span></li></ul>\n\t\t<p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">Required Tools:</span></p><ul style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;\">\n\t\t\t<li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">Cell Phone or other device that has a phone, camera, and internet ability&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">Standard hand tools</span></li></ul>\n\t\t<p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">Upon Arrival at FedEx:</span></p><ul style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;\">\n\t\t\t<li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs5AB00083\">CHECK IN TO YOUR WORK ORDER&nbsp;</span><span class=\"cs7D58027A\">&ndash;&nbsp;if you are unable to do so then you MUST call Essintial @&nbsp;</span><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">855-612-2183</span><span class=\"cs7D58027A\">&nbsp;to check in.&nbsp;</span></li></ul>\n\t\t<p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs5AB00083\">Upon Arrival at the Site:&nbsp;</span></p><ul style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;\">\n\t\t\t<li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">Enter the site with Badge and&nbsp;</span><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">Introduce yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of HCL/BASF&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">Go to Virtual ID Area -</span><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;DO NOT GO ANYWHERE ELSE IN THE BUILDING except to the storage locker and back.</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">Ref to the</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&quot;</span><span class=\"cs3232DC9D\">Scope of Work Step by Step Instructions&quot;</span><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\"> - posted above in your Work Order</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">Once at the VITP Point, there is a device that the techs will use to call the VITP Team - Refer to the&nbsp;HCL BASF Onsite VITP Process - Return and Replenishment Process</span><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">:&nbsp;<span class=\"csC1D8CEBD\">https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000003uH9J/cEucV0buMb0kEy.aD.huNaNut7UUrDFEb5FO7Un976U</span></span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">Work with the HCL VITP Team&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">HCL VITP Agent will Advise what locker the devices will go into and advise which lock to pull the defective from.</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">The team will guide and open lockers for tech and provide support, techs will provide new and old device serials to the team.</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">HCL VITP Agent will provide </span><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">admin PIN</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">VITP Agent will release the tech, once call has ended tech will leave and exit</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">Technician to take any defective equipment with them and drop off at FedEx Immediately after leaving the site</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">Techs DO NOT GO ANYWHERE ELSE IN THE BUILDING except to the storage locker and back.&nbsp;</span></li></ul>\n\t\t<p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">&nbsp;Upon Completion/Closeout Requirements</span></p><ul style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;\">\n\t\t\t<li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">Get Released from the site by the VITP Agent - obtain agents Name</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">Take Defective Equipment and drop off at local FedEx</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs7D58027A\">Call the Essintial Project Team @&nbsp;</span><span class=\"cs8B49C83F\">855-612-2183</span><span class=\"cs7D58027A\">&nbsp;opt 2 to perform your final check out</span><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;</span></li></ul>\n\t\t<p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">Important Note about Check-Out:</span></p><ul style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;\">\n\t\t\t<li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">Technicians Labor&nbsp;End Time</span><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;-&nbsp;is</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">If technicians&nbsp;</span><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">HAS defective equipment to return</span><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;- their labor ends when they drop equipment off at FedEx</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">Check-Out upon leaving FedEx&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">If Technicians&nbsp;</span><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">DOES NOT have defective equipment to return</span><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;- their labor ends when they are finished at site.&nbsp;</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">Check-Out upon leaving the site&nbsp;</span></li></ul>\n\t\t<p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;</span></p><p class=\"csC583D0C8\"><span class=\"cs72F7C9C5\">Closing / Completion Notes:</span><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">&nbsp;</span></p><ul style=\"margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;\">\n\t\t\t<li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">Detailed Description of the Work that took Place, including any issues and delays</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">Name of the HCL VITP Agent who released you from the site?</span></li><li class=\"cs4FC7BF42\"><span class=\"cs9D249CCB\">Return Tracking Numbers (if applicable)</span></li></ul>","markdown":"\\*\\*Tech needs to provide 2 dates/times they are available\\*\\*\n\nYOUR WORK ORDER ONLY COVERS ONE VISIT TO SITE. IF CUSTOMER REQUIRES A RETURN VISIT YOU \\*\\*MUST\\*\\* HAVE ANOTHER WORK ORDER. TIME LOGGED FOR ADDITIONAL DAYS ONSITE WILL BE REJECTED FOR NOT FOLLOWING PROCESSES.\n\nImportant: Onsite Time is measured from arrival time at FedEx, transit time from FedEx to Site, restock, and then drop-off at Fedex for Return.\\]\n\n- Technicians Labor Times Start Time - is when they ARRIVE at local FEDEX HOLD \\[ not when they arrive onsite \\]\n- Check-In upon arrival at FEDEX\n- Technicians Labor End Time - is\n- If technicians HAS defective equipment to return - their labor ends when they drop equipment off at FedEx\n- Check-Out upon leaving FedEx\n- If Technicians DOES NOT have defective equipment to return - their labor ends when they are finished at site.\n- Check-Out upon leaving the site\n\nRequired On-site time/window:\n\nEquipment:\n\nMake/Model: OTH\n\nSerial Number: {SRM\\_FN.SERIAL}\n\nProblem Description: For Essinsial: This is a refill request for 6 devices. Please collect the Package from Fed-Ex and assist with placing the laptops in the lockers and taking out the defective laptops. Please prepare additional time if we need to rearrange the lockers. The Refill ticket will be logged after we have agreed on a date for the visit, as Fed-Ex will only hold a package for up to 5 days. Once you reach BASF, please call us from Talkative by clicking on \"Click to support\"\n\n\\*\\*\\*Scope of Work Instructions\\*\\*\\*\n\nGeneral Scope of Work: Technician to go and pick up equipment up at local fedex hold, drive to customers site location, work with the HCL VITP - Virtual IT Point via onsite \"Talkative Video Calling System\" to drop equipment off in customers onsite VITP storage lockers, and if applicable take defective equipment out of lockers and drop off a local FedEx Hold for return to customer.\n\nScope of Work Step by Step Instructions:\n\n- Pick up the laptops from FedEx.\n- Arrive at the BASF office and use the Talkative machine by selecting “Click to Support.”\n- One of our agents \\[ HCL VITP - Virtual IT Point Agents \\] will answer the call and guide the technician step‑by‑step.\n- \"Talkative Video Calling System\" Process - Refer to the HCL BASF Onsite VITP Process - Return and Replenishment Process: <https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000003uH9J/cEucV0buMb0kEy.aD.huNaNut7UUrDFEb5FO7Un976U>\n- Open the package:\n- Every package contains a return label — keep this aside for return shipping.\n- There will be an inner box containing the new laptop.\n- Our agent \\[ HCL VITP - Virtual IT Point Agents \\] will provide the admin PIN and guide the technician to open the locker.\n- Remove the defective laptop from the locker.\n- Place the new laptop inside the locker, share the serial number, and close the locker.\n- Ship the defective laptop back to FedEx:\n- Pack the old laptop back into the box.\n- Stick the return label onto the box.\n- Return it at the FedEx location.\n\nOnsite Virtual IT Point via Onsite \"Talkative Video Calling System\" Process\n\n- Refer to the HCL BASF Onsite VITP Process - Return and Replenishment Process: <https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000003uH9J/cEucV0buMb0kEy.aD.huNaNut7UUrDFEb5FO7Un976U>\n\nImportant Tech Information & Requirements\n\n- Technicians ARE NOT to go to site unless equipment is ready for pickup at local FedEx\n- Technicians MUST Represent themselves as an Essintial Technician on behalf of HCL/BASF\n- Technicians MUST carry/present BASF Badge while onsite\n\nImportant Information on Site:\n\n- You must represent themselves as an Essintial technician on behalf of HCL/BASF while on site.\n- Technicians MUST carry/present BASF Badge while onsite\n- Onsite - DO NOT GO ANYWHERE ELSE IN THE BUILDING except to the storage locker and back\n- These are live environments, and technician must act in a professional manner, taking care not to disrupt business.\n- Dress code is business casual; no jeans or holes. Collared or button down shirt, slacks, and nice shoes required.\n\nImportant Scope/Customer Information:\n\n- Any changes to ETA’s MUST be relayed to the End User and Essintial via phone.\n- If you are unfamiliar with the equipment or a particular repair needed, do not tell the customer this. Call Essintial Support for assistance.\n- If additional parts are needed there will be another trip REQUIRED. You MUST CALL Essintial @ 800-326-6999 to advise. This ticket should be closed and a new work order will be opened.\n- All times provided to Essintial MUST MATCH what is listed in your work order as well as any required sign off forms.\n\nRequired Tools:\n\n- Cell Phone or other device that has a phone, camera, and internet ability\n- Standard hand tools\n\nUpon Arrival at FedEx:\n\n- CHECK IN TO YOUR WORK ORDER – if you are unable to do so then you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.\n\nUpon Arrival at the Site:\n\n- Enter the site with Badge and Introduce yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of HCL/BASF\n- Go to Virtual ID Area - DO NOT GO ANYWHERE ELSE IN THE BUILDING except to the storage locker and back.\n- Ref to the\n- \"Scope of Work Step by Step Instructions\" - posted above in your Work Order\n- Once at the VITP Point, there is a device that the techs will use to call the VITP Team - Refer to the HCL BASF Onsite VITP Process - Return and Replenishment Process: <https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000003uH9J/cEucV0buMb0kEy.aD.huNaNut7UUrDFEb5FO7Un976U>\n- Work with the HCL VITP Team\n- HCL VITP Agent will Advise what locker the devices will go into and advise which lock to pull the defective from.\n- The team will guide and open lockers for tech and provide support, techs will provide new and old device serials to the team.\n- HCL VITP Agent will provide admin PIN\n- VITP Agent will release the tech, once call has ended tech will leave and exit\n- Technician to take any defective equipment with them and drop off at FedEx Immediately after leaving the site\n- Techs DO NOT GO ANYWHERE ELSE IN THE BUILDING except to the storage locker and back.\n\n Upon Completion/Closeout Requirements\n\n- Get Released from the site by the VITP Agent - obtain agents Name\n- Take Defective Equipment and drop off at local FedEx\n- Call the Essintial Project Team @ 855-612-2183 opt 2 to perform your final check out\n\nImportant Note about Check-Out:\n\n- Technicians Labor End Time - is\n- If technicians HAS defective equipment to return - their labor ends when they drop equipment off at FedEx\n- Check-Out upon leaving FedEx\n- If Technicians DOES NOT have defective equipment to return - their labor ends when they are finished at site.\n- Check-Out upon leaving the site\n\nClosing / Completion Notes:\n\n- Detailed Description of the Work that took Place, including any issues and delays\n- Name of the HCL VITP Agent who released you from the site?\n- Return Tracking Numbers (if applicable)","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-16T09:00","end":"2026-09-16T12:00","latestStart":"2026-09-16T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":30,"max":90},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":30,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":7},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $90 (countered: $180) is below minimum threshold $250"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-16T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-17T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"},{"start":"2026-09-11T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-11T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"SMALL BACKBOARD/ DATA REMOTE INSTALL/ MUST HAVE BUTT-SET/MULTIMETER-DIS148477"},{"start":"2026-09-04T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-05T13:30:00.000Z","summary":"DSS 9223 - Install (1) QNAP + UPS + Switch, Install (3) TP-Link Wireless Bridge, Install (3) 8 Port PoE Switch, Replace (15) Analog Cameras w/ (15) IP Cameras + Cable Runs - Lead Tech"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789395621197}
{"job":{"id":19694168,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Pomeroy","title":"Front End Preventitive Maintenance                    S791L9RALET3","description":{"html":"<p><strong>If this work order&nbsp;is part of a bundle, the bundle must be accepted in whole.&nbsp;This bundle may be for multiple locations on multiple nights.</strong></p><p><strong><u>Tools will be paid with receipt. Other expenses must be requested and approved before arriving on site.</u></strong></p><p><strong>During this visit, your team will perform cleaning, vacuuming</strong>, and cable rerouting on all POS systems, customer service PCs, printers, and the two laptop carts.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>PRE-ARRIVAL INSTRUCTIONS: </u></strong></p><ul><li>Review the scope of work in the work order prior to arrival</li><li>Review and print Installation Instructions and Installation Checklist. Other documents do not need to be printed as long as you have a device that will present them legibly while on-site.</li><li>Validate that you have all the required tools and batteries are charged</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>TOOL LIST</u></strong></p><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Except for the shop vac, all cleaning solutions, canned air, and shop towels will be provided.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>You must bring a Shop vac</u></strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>PHONE - </strong>Mobile with camera, internet access, and charger cable. Camera must have sufficient room to take approximately 60 photos.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Internet access will be required to upload photos to your work order prior to being released from the site.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">DRILL - Cordless Rechargeable Drill Charger and spare battery</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">HAND-TOOLS - Standard technician toolkit to include: Phillips #2 Screwdriver</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Flat-Blade Screwdriver</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Wire Cutters&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Box Cutter</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Pen / Marker and Blue Painters Tape</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>ARRIVAL INSTRUCTIONS</u></strong></p><ol><li>Upon arriving at the store, contact the Pomeroy Remote Support Bridge and check in. The bridge information is located in the confidential section of this work order.</li><li>Please locate the Store Captain (or the next person in charge) and introduce yourself. Inform them that you are onsite to conduct Front End Preventative Maintenance.</li><li>Validate inventory and give the return labels to the Manager in Charge. Ask them to keep the labels at the bridge.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong><u>INSTALLATION PROCEDURE</u></strong></p><p><strong>NOTE: DO NOT PROCEED WITH ANY STEPS UNTIL INSTRUCTED BY REMOTE SUPPORT</strong></p><ol><li>For each lane:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Vacuum the top and inside of the check stand including removing the scanner and vacuuming out the well. Remove any equipment, papers etc. before vacuuming according to the provided instructions.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Reroute the cash drawer cable to the POS according to the provided instructions.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Wipe down all technology surfaces, removing all dust or grime.</li><li>For customer service area (Bridge)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Vacuum the top and inside cubbies of the bridge. Remove any equipment, papers etc. before vacuuming according to the provided instructions.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Wipe down all technology both inside and on top of the bridge removing all dust and grime. Canned air and cleaning supplies provided.</li><li>For laptop carts</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Vacuum the top and shelves of the cart.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Wipe down all surfaces, removing all dust or grime.</li><li>Securely box all unused equipment, attach the provided return label,&nbsp;and hand the box to the Mate in Charge.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong><u>CLEANUP &amp; DEPARTURE INSTRUCTIONS</u></strong></p><ol><li>Using your camera, take pictures of the completed work (details in the attached installation documentation) and upload them to your work order</li><li>Give the return shipping boxes to the Manager in Charge.</li><li>Gather your tools and checkout with remote support.</li></ol>","markdown":"**If this work order is part of a bundle, the bundle must be accepted in whole. This bundle may be for multiple locations on multiple nights.**\n\n**Tools will be paid with receipt. Other expenses must be requested and approved before arriving on site.**\n\n**During this visit, your team will perform cleaning, vacuuming**, and cable rerouting on all POS systems, customer service PCs, printers, and the two laptop carts.\n\n**PRE-ARRIVAL INSTRUCTIONS:**\n\n- Review the scope of work in the work order prior to arrival\n- Review and print Installation Instructions and Installation Checklist. Other documents do not need to be printed as long as you have a device that will present them legibly while on-site.\n- Validate that you have all the required tools and batteries are charged\n\n**TOOL LIST**\n\n- Except for the shop vac, all cleaning solutions, canned air, and shop towels will be provided.\n- **You must bring a Shop vac**\n- **PHONE -** Mobile with camera, internet access, and charger cable. Camera must have sufficient room to take approximately 60 photos.\n- Internet access will be required to upload photos to your work order prior to being released from the site.\n- DRILL - Cordless Rechargeable Drill Charger and spare battery\n- HAND-TOOLS - Standard technician toolkit to include: Phillips #2 Screwdriver\n- Flat-Blade Screwdriver\n- Wire Cutters\n- Box Cutter\n- **Pen / Marker and Blue Painters Tape**\n\n**ARRIVAL INSTRUCTIONS**\n\n1. Upon arriving at the store, contact the Pomeroy Remote Support Bridge and check in. The bridge information is located in the confidential section of this work order.\n2. Please locate the Store Captain (or the next person in charge) and introduce yourself. Inform them that you are onsite to conduct Front End Preventative Maintenance.\n3. Validate inventory and give the return labels to the Manager in Charge. Ask them to keep the labels at the bridge.\n\n**INSTALLATION PROCEDURE**\n\n**NOTE: DO NOT PROCEED WITH ANY STEPS UNTIL INSTRUCTED BY REMOTE SUPPORT**\n\n1. For each lane:\n2. Vacuum the top and inside of the check stand including removing the scanner and vacuuming out the well. Remove any equipment, papers etc. before vacuuming according to the provided instructions.\n3. Reroute the cash drawer cable to the POS according to the provided instructions.\n4. Wipe down all technology surfaces, removing all dust or grime.\n5. For customer service area (Bridge)\n6. Vacuum the top and inside cubbies of the bridge. Remove any equipment, papers etc. before vacuuming according to the provided instructions.\n7. Wipe down all technology both inside and on top of the bridge removing all dust and grime. Canned air and cleaning supplies provided.\n8. For laptop carts\n9. Vacuum the top and shelves of the cart.\n10. Wipe down all surfaces, removing all dust or grime.\n11. Securely box all unused equipment, attach the provided return label, and hand the box to the Mate in Charge.\n\n**CLEANUP & DEPARTURE INSTRUCTIONS**\n\n1. Using your camera, take pictures of the completed work (details in the attached installation documentation) and upload them to your work order\n2. Give the return shipping boxes to the Manager in Charge.\n3. Gather your tools and checkout with remote support.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-16T21:30","end":"2026-09-16T23:30"},"payRange":{"min":105,"max":205},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":105},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":6},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $205 is below minimum threshold $250"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-16T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-17T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"},{"start":"2026-09-11T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-11T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"SMALL BACKBOARD/ DATA REMOTE INSTALL/ MUST HAVE BUTT-SET/MULTIMETER-DIS148477"},{"start":"2026-09-04T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-05T13:30:00.000Z","summary":"DSS 9223 - Install (1) QNAP + UPS + Switch, Install (3) TP-Link Wireless Bridge, Install (3) 8 Port PoE Switch, Replace (15) Analog Cameras w/ (15) IP Cameras + Cable Runs - Lead Tech"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789395656737}
