{"job":{"id":19948945,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Gigstreem","title":"Novel Morrisville - Internet troubleshooting Ruckus AP - #320076","description":{"html":"<p>GiGstreem is a national Internet Service Provider delivering high-quality service to residential and commercial properties across the country.</p>\n<p><strong><u>We will need to﻿ retrieve equipment from a Local UPS store before heading to site.</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Work Order Location:</strong></p>\n<p>Residential Property – Morrisville NC</p>\n<p><em>Refer to confidential notes for exact address and customer contact information.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Scope of Work (SOW): <u>AP Troubleshooting. Need to check on the cable run from idf to wallport.&nbsp;Make sure the customer gets fully connected over wifi and hardwired. Confirm that you have all the tools before requesting the work order.</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Technician Expectations:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Place a courtesy call at least 30 minutes prior to arrival</strong> to inform the customer of your estimated time of arrival (ETA).</li>\n<li>Upon arriving on site, all Field Nation technicians are required to <strong><u>check in at the leasing office or front desk before proceeding to any unit.</u></strong> Contractors must announce their arrival and present their Field Nation ID and credentials for verification. <strong><u>Entry into any resident’s unit is not permitted until this check‑in process is completed and approved by onsite staff.</u></strong></li>\n<li><strong>Represent the brand</strong>&nbsp;with professionalism. Appearance, communication, and the quality of your work must reflect high standards.</li>\n<li><strong>Do not overshare</strong> internal processes or technical details with the customer. Communication should be simple, courteous, and focused on resolving the issue.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>⚠️ <em>If the technician arrives unprepared, misinforms the customer, demonstrates poor presentation, or delivers substandard work, GiGstreem reserves the right to withhold payment for the work order.</em></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>If equipment replacement is determined to be necessary during the visit</strong>, the technician must:</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Take a clear photo of the equipment needing replacement.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Provide a separate photo clearly showing the <strong>equipment label with the MAC address and model/type</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Required Experience</strong></p>\n<p><em>Includes but is not limited to</em></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Telecommunications/networking experience, including troubleshooting of routers and switches</li>\n<li>Installation and troubleshooting of routers, including Cat6 jumper connection</li>\n<li>Copper cabling experience, including Cat5e/Cat6 testing, troubleshooting, and RJ45 termination</li>\n<li>Troubleshooting customer device connectivity (TVs, tablets, computers, etc.)</li>\n<li>Familiarity with Ruckus Access Points, including resetting and wall-mount handling</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Required Equipment</strong></p>\n<p><em>Includes but is not limited to:</em></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Ethernet cable tester</li>\n<li>Wireless-enabled device such as a laptop, phone, or tablet (for WiFi testing)</li>\n<li>Cat5/6 patch cables (jumpers)</li>\n<li>RJ45 connectors</li>\n<li>Laptop (for diagnostics and troubleshooting)</li>\n<li>Ladder</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Coordination:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Work in collaboration with GiGstreem’s Network Operations Team</li>\n<li>Refer to confidential notes for customer and NOC (Network Operations Center) contact information</li>\n</ul>\n<p>At Gigstreem, delivering reliable, high-performance internet service is our top priority. To maintain the integrity of our network and ensure consistent customer experiences, we follow strict guidelines regarding the equipment and solutions we support. This includes a clear stance on the use of Wi-Fi extenders.</p>\n<p><strong><u>Policy on Wi-Fi Extenders - Gigstreem Policy Reminder:</u></strong></p>\n<p>It is strictly against Gigstreem policy to utilize, install, or recommend Wi-Fi extenders as a solution for speed, coverage, or connectivity issues within a unit.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Why This Matters:</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Wi-Fi extenders are not part of our approved network architecture.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">They can introduce interference, degrade performance, and complicate troubleshooting.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Recommending or installing extenders may lead to inconsistent service and customer dissatisfaction.</li>\n<li>Approved Resolution Methods:</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Thorough troubleshooting of the existing AP and network configuration</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Collaboration with engineering to assess AP configuration</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">All technicians and support staff must adhere to this policy without exception. Any deviation should be escalated to management for review.</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"GiGstreem is a national Internet Service Provider delivering high-quality service to residential and commercial properties across the country.\n\n**We will need to﻿ retrieve equipment from a Local UPS store before heading to site.**\n\n**Work Order Location:**\n\nResidential Property – Morrisville NC\n\n*Refer to confidential notes for exact address and customer contact information.*\n\n**Scope of Work (SOW): AP Troubleshooting. Need to check on the cable run from idf to wallport. Make sure the customer gets fully connected over wifi and hardwired. Confirm that you have all the tools before requesting the work order.**\n\n**Technician Expectations:**\n\n- **Place a courtesy call at least 30 minutes prior to arrival** to inform the customer of your estimated time of arrival (ETA).\n- Upon arriving on site, all Field Nation technicians are required to **check in at the leasing office or front desk before proceeding to any unit.** Contractors must announce their arrival and present their Field Nation ID and credentials for verification. **Entry into any resident’s unit is not permitted until this check‑in process is completed and approved by onsite staff.**\n- **Represent the brand** with professionalism. Appearance, communication, and the quality of your work must reflect high standards.\n- **Do not overshare** internal processes or technical details with the customer. Communication should be simple, courteous, and focused on resolving the issue.\n\n⚠️ *If the technician arrives unprepared, misinforms the customer, demonstrates poor presentation, or delivers substandard work, GiGstreem reserves the right to withhold payment for the work order.*\n\n- **If equipment replacement is determined to be necessary during the visit**, the technician must:\n- Take a clear photo of the equipment needing replacement.\n- Provide a separate photo clearly showing the **equipment label with the MAC address and model/type**.\n\n**Required Experience**\n\n*Includes but is not limited to*\n\n- Telecommunications/networking experience, including troubleshooting of routers and switches\n- Installation and troubleshooting of routers, including Cat6 jumper connection\n- Copper cabling experience, including Cat5e/Cat6 testing, troubleshooting, and RJ45 termination\n- Troubleshooting customer device connectivity (TVs, tablets, computers, etc.)\n- Familiarity with Ruckus Access Points, including resetting and wall-mount handling\n\n**Required Equipment**\n\n*Includes but is not limited to:*\n\n- Ethernet cable tester\n- Wireless-enabled device such as a laptop, phone, or tablet (for WiFi testing)\n- Cat5/6 patch cables (jumpers)\n- RJ45 connectors\n- Laptop (for diagnostics and troubleshooting)\n- Ladder\n\n**Coordination:**\n\n- Work in collaboration with GiGstreem’s Network Operations Team\n- Refer to confidential notes for customer and NOC (Network Operations Center) contact information\n\nAt Gigstreem, delivering reliable, high-performance internet service is our top priority. To maintain the integrity of our network and ensure consistent customer experiences, we follow strict guidelines regarding the equipment and solutions we support. This includes a clear stance on the use of Wi-Fi extenders.\n\n**Policy on Wi-Fi Extenders - Gigstreem Policy Reminder:**\n\nIt is strictly against Gigstreem policy to utilize, install, or recommend Wi-Fi extenders as a solution for speed, coverage, or connectivity issues within a unit.\n\n- Why This Matters:\n- Wi-Fi extenders are not part of our approved network architecture.\n- They can introduce interference, degrade performance, and complicate troubleshooting.\n- Recommending or installing extenders may lead to inconsistent service and customer dissatisfaction.\n- Approved Resolution Methods:\n- Thorough troubleshooting of the existing AP and network configuration\n- Collaboration with engineering to assess AP configuration\n- All technicians and support staff must adhere to this policy without exception. Any deviation should be escalated to management for review.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-15T09:00","end":"2026-09-15T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":160,"max":225},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":160},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":65}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":5},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"blended","counterRate":80,"baseAmount":240,"estHours":2,"travelExpense":0,"payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":160},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":80}},"counterDate":{"start":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T18:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":60,"mode":"hours","reason":"arrival_window"}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-15T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-17T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"},{"start":"2026-09-04T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-05T13:30:00.000Z","summary":"DSS 9223 - Install (1) QNAP + UPS + Switch, Install (3) TP-Link Wireless Bridge, Install (3) 8 Port PoE Switch, Replace (15) Analog Cameras w/ (15) IP Cameras + Cable Runs - Lead Tech"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1789407786635}
{"job":{"id":19908569,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"VEHTECH, INC","title":"WASHER REPAIR","description":{"html":"<ol>\n<li>TECHNICIAN NEEDED TO REPAIR WASHER <strong>{PARTS ONSITE WITH CUSTOMER. NOTE: TECHNICIAN MUST INSTALL ALL PARTS ON SITE SHIPPED BY VENDOR.}</strong></li>\n<li><strong>&nbsp;<u>TECH MUST CHECK IN ARRIVAL NO CHECK IN NO PAY 7707882032. TAKE PICTURES OF THE UNIT BEFORE AND AFTER THE REPAIRS AND THE WORK SPACE THESE PICTURES ARE MANDATORY. THE SIGN OFF SHEET MUST BE SIGNED AND UPLOADED TO MARK WORK ORDER COMPLETE FOR PAYMENT TO BE APPROVED.</u></strong></li>\n<li><strong><em>MUST REPRESENT YOURSELF AS A VEHTECH, INC. TECHNICIAN. CALL AND INTRODUCE YOURSELF AS A VEHTECH TECHNICIAN CONFIRM THE APPOINTMENT TIME AND DATE. ESPECIALLY IF YOU HAVE REQUESTED TO COUNTER WITH A DIFFERENT DATE. THIS IS MANDATORY AS PART OF YOUR CHECK IN TASK.</em></strong></li>\n<li><strong>Effective today July 20, 2021 new policy mandatory for all Vehtechnology technicians. Technicians must call the customer one hour before arriving on site, this is and has always been our policy. If you arrive at a customer's home and did not provide a courtesy call before arriving and the customer is not home you WILL NOT BE PAID FOR TRAVEL for this ticket. If you have an instance where you have contacted the customer and no response immediately contact myself or Vincent via text message or phone call, no exceptions.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>﻿<em>Technicians please check in via ext 1005, with your check in time and check out time. If I am unavailable leave me a voicemail with your check in and check out time and any other pertinent information related to your work order. I will return your voicemail at my earliest convenience. If the work order is completed over the weekend you will be contacted on the next business day.</em></strong> <em><u>Please be sure to take all parts with you the customer is not responsible for returning the parts it is part of your work order completion to receive payment approval NO EXCEPTIONS.</u></em></li>\n<li><u>﻿</u><strong>No technician will be permitted to work while under the influence of any legal or illegal substance (i.e. marijuana, alcohol, stimulants or narcotic substances) see additional information below:</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Prohibited Conduct</strong></p>\n<p>Technicians or subcontractors may not:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Report to assignments/ work or remain on duty while impaired by alcohol or drugs</li>\n<li>Possess, use, sell, or distribute illegal drugs on Company property or while conducting Vehtechnology business.</li>\n<li>Misuse legally prescribed or over-the-counter medication in a way that impairs job performance or safety.</li>\n<li>Consume alcohol during work hours.</li>\n<li>This policy applies to all employees, contractors, temporary workers, and interns, while on working on Vehtechnology Assignments or contracted work through Field Nation any premises, conducting Vehtechnology business residential or commercial sites.</li>\n<li>Technicians taking medication that may impair job performance, alertness, or coordination should inform work order Manager to determine if you are permitted to proceed with work order.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Testing</p>\n<p>The Company may conduct drug and/or alcohol testing under the following circumstances, in accordance with applicable state law:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Reasonable suspicion:</strong> When a Customer or Vendor reports or documents specific, objective signs of impairment. If you a customer believes that you are under the influence of drugs or alcohol you will be asked to leave the site and you will not be paid for this assignment. Field Nation will be notified and an investigation immediately will determine if you will be compensated for travel or work.</li>\n<li><strong>Post-accident:</strong> Following a workplace accident meeting the threshold defined by the Company (e.g., resulting in injury requiring medical treatment or significant property damage)</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li><br /></li>\n<li><br /></li>\n</ol>\n<p><br /></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>WASHER REPAIR</strong></li>\n<li><strong>MAKE:</strong> Maytag</li>\n<li><strong>MODEL:</strong>MVW4505MW</li>\n<li><strong>PROBLEM DESCRIPTION:</strong>CX STATED THAT SHE START A CYCLE THEN NOW SHE IS UNABLE TO OPEN THE WASHER DOOR AND ALL THE LIGHTS ARE BLINKING.</li>\n<li><strong>PARTS SENT:</strong>Part Number: W11626074 Part Description: CNTRL-ELEC Quantity: 1 If used during repair, requires return: Yes Part Number: W11399437 Part Description: WASHER DRAIN PUMP Quantity: 1 If used during repair, requires return: DURING REPAIR: 1. Only replace parts needed for the repair. 2. Diagnose issue &amp; if parts sent don''t resolve the issue, please put the original parts back in the unit and back in original condition. 3. Take all parts sent to the customer with you upon leaving. Do not leave ANYTHING with the customer.</li>\n<li><strong>﻿<u>IF THE PARTS ARE NOT ON SITE PLEASE RUN THE CALL AS A TROUBLE SHOOTING AND DIAGNOSTICS. TAKE PICS OF THE MODEL AND SERIAL AND WRITE A SUMMARY OF THE PROBLEM DESCRIPTION AND THE POSSIBLE PARTS NEEDED TO REPAIR THE UNIT.</u></strong></li>\n<li><strong>PICTURES</strong>: <strong>TAKE PICTURES OF THE HOUSE, AND THE UNIT IN THIS INSTANCE FOR VERIFICATION OF YOUR ARRIVAL AND DEPARTURE.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>TAKE PICTURES OF THE UNIT BEFORE THE REPAIRS AND AFTER TO COVER YOURSELF AND THE COMPANY FROM ANY LIABILITY!</strong></li>\n<li><strong>PARTS&nbsp;WILL BE&nbsp;ONSITE FOR REPAIRS AND INSTALLATIONS.&nbsp;</strong></li>\n<li><strong>PLEASE PRESENT YOURSELF AS A VEHTECH,INC REP. &amp; PLEASE PRESENT YOURSELF IN&nbsp;A PROFESSIONAL MANNER.</strong></li>\n<li>&nbsp;<strong>CALL 770-788-2032 - UPON SITE Arrival for check in.</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;IF NO ANSWER LEAVE VOICEMAIL WITH CHECK IN TIME AND CHECK OUT.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp