{"job":{"id":19948877,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Staley Technologies","title":"Tech is needed to Troubleshoot/Repair/Replace Data Cable to AP14 and replace faulty unit if needed. LIFT WILL BE ONSITE","description":{"html":"<p><u>DELIVERABLES ARE REQUIRED BEFORE LEAVING THE SITE</u></p>\n<p><em>&nbsp;</em></p>\n<p><em>&nbsp;</em></p>\n<p><strong>Tech is needed to Troubleshoot/Repair/Replace Data Cable to AP14 and replace faulty unit if needed. LIFT WILL BE ONSITE</strong></p>\n<p><strong>.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Device With Issue: AP14</strong></p>\n<p><strong>.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Location of Device: Floor plan attached</strong></p>\n<p><strong>.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Customer notes: Club 177 - AP 14 is down</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Replacement unit is stored in the computer room</strong></p>\n<p>Tech needs to TRR the data cable, ports, switch and run new data line, if needed. Replace the faulty AP unit</p>\n<p>Tech should capture the location, switch number, and port assignment before departing the club</p>\n<p>Tech should take pictures before and after working in the IDF/MDF</p>\n<p>Tech upon arrival and after repairs should work with the NOC for verification and validation</p>\n<p><strong>NOC: 833-722-3102.</strong></p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p><strong>Access related issues</strong>: Make sure you go to the back of the store and ring the door buzzer after hours. If you still cannot gain access, Call Staley Support 501-320-4738</p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p><strong>Closeout Notes:</strong> Make sure everything that occurred during the visit is called out in the closeout notes</p>\n<p>Phone calls and texts will not be used in lieu of providing detailed and concise closeout notes.</p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p>Tech should send pictures of IDF1, IDF2 and MDF cabinets - multiple pictures of each cabinet. (Doors opened, door closed, sideways, full view. If any of the cabinets are supported by anything for standing or holding onto the wall or anything unusual, please take pictures and let BJ’s NOC know and include it in your notes.</p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p>Pictures of IDF1, IDF2 and MDF cabinets must be labeled</p>\n<p>Example: Club211IDF1 front, Club211IDF1 side and so on</p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p>If any of the cabinets are supported by anything for standing or holding onto the wall or anything unusual, please take pictures and let BJ’s NOC know and include it in your notes.</p>\n<p>Usually, they will be in the following places:</p>\n<p>IDFs – Membership / Break room / Upstairs / Receiving / Upstairs Club Manager’s office</p>\n<p>MDFs – Computer room or Server room at the back of the club</p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p>Failure to do so will result in a penalty.</p>\n<p><strong>.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Incomplete Sites:</strong> If you cannot complete your site for any reason, call Staley Support 501-320-4738</p>\n<p><strong>.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Important Information: Anytime you are bringing a lift into or out of a customer facility, whether through a doorway or overhead door, you must bring the lift to a complete stop before going through the entry.&nbsp;You must walk around the entire lift looking for any obstacles.&nbsp;Be sure to check the height of the cage vs the height of the entry.&nbsp;&nbsp;Be sure to check the width of the lift vs the width of the entry.&nbsp;Only when that has been completed and you are sure there are no potential contact points may you continue forward with the lift.&nbsp;<u>If there is trouble with the lift, please call the number on the side of the equipment for support and let Staley Technologies know of the issues.</u></strong></p>\n<p>-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</p>\n<p><strong>Switch Port range available for AP's</strong></p>\n<p>MDF&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Switch Ports 0-18</p>\n<p>IDF&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Switch Ports 0-19</p>\n<p>-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</p>\n<p><strong>MATERIALS</strong></p>\n<p>QTY&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;DESCRIPTION</p>\n<p>======================================</p>\n<p>300’&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CAT6, WH, Plenum</p>\n<p>1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;1 Port Faceplate</p>\n<p>1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;CAT6 Jack Insert</p>\n<p>1&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;5’ CAT6 Patch Cables Blue</p>\n<p><strong>TOOLS</strong></p>\n<p>---------</p>\n<p>Tech MUST have required tools to perform service job including, but not limited to:</p>\n<p>BUTTSET</p>\n<p>LAPTOP WITH CONSOLE CABLE</p>\n<p>USB TO SERIAL CONVERTOR</p>\n<p>USB KEYBOARD AND MOUSE</p>\n<p>PRECISE SCREWDRIVERS</p>\n<p>PUNCH TOOL W 66/110 BLADES</p>\n<p>WIRE STRIPPERS</p>\n<p>CRIMPER</p>\n<p>TONER</p>\n<p>LABELMAKER</p>\n<p>CABLE TESTER</p>\n<p>STANDARD TOOL KIT (Screw/nut driver, tape, sharpie, pliers, etc.)</p>\n<p>8’ to 10’ LADDER</p>\n<p>-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</p>\n<p><strong>NOTES</strong></p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p>* White, Plenum CAT6 cable is required for all permanent cable runs.</p>\n<p>** Velcro on ALL non-permanent wire management. Including power cords and AC Adapters.</p>\n<p>** DO NOT install any surface mount boxes in the MDF or any IDF's.</p>\n<p>** If ports don’t exist, you will need to install a new 24-port patch panel.</p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p>ATTENTION: Any IDF's in the Club with surface mount boxes must be corrected.</p>\n<p>-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</p>\n<p><strong>TASKS</strong></p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p><strong>1)</strong> Meet with store personnel/management and introduce yourself.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;a) Review details of service request with store personnel/management.</p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p><strong>2) Troubleshoot/Repair/Replace Data Cable for Access Point and replace (AP14).</strong></p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;a) Capture before pictures of the equipment and work area.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;b) If AP does not come online, troubleshoot with BJ’s Support</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;c) Test network cables and determine faults. Repair as needed.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;- Test the cable.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;- Repair as needed.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;- Test the cable again to verify it has been repaired.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;d) If cable is damaged beyond repair, we will need to run a new drop.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;- Run 1 new data cable from network rack to AP location</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;- Terminate/Test/Label new data cable</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;- Patch in the newly installed data cable per site guidelines.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;e) If cable is confirmed to be good, install replacement AP.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;f) Make sure AP is connected to a switch port between 0-18 on the switch.</p>\n<p><strong>Call BJ’s Support (833-722-3102 option 1) to verify that everything is working correctly.</strong></p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p><strong>3) Required Pictures:</strong></p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;a) AP14</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;b) Patch Panel ports</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;c) Switch ports</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;d) Biscuit and Jack</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;e) Cable test results before and after work</p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;f) IDF1, IDF2 and MDF cabinets</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Tech should send pictures of IDF1, IDF2 and MDF cabinets - multiple pictures of each cabinet. (Doors opened, door closed, sideways, full view. If any of the cabinets are supported by anything for standing or holding onto the wall or anything unusual, please take pictures and let BJ’s NOC know and include it in your notes.</p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p>Pictures of IDF1, IDF2 and MDF cabinets must be labeled</p>\n<p>Example: Club211IDF1 Front, Club211IDF1 side and so on</p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p>If any of the cabinets are supported by anything for standing or holding onto the wall or anything unusual, please take pictures and let BJ’s NOC know and include it in your notes.</p>\n<p>Usually, they will be in the following places:</p>\n<p>IDFs – Membership / Break room / Upstairs / Receiving / Upstairs Club Manager’s office</p>\n<p>MDFs – Computer room or Server room at the back of the club</p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p>Failure to do so will result in a penalty.</p>\n<p>.</p>\n<p><strong>Pictures of IDF1, IDF2 and MDF cabinets must be labeled</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong> - Club143_MDF_front, Club143_MDF_side, and so on</p>","markdown":"DELIVERABLES ARE REQUIRED BEFORE LEAVING THE SITE\n\n**Tech is needed to Troubleshoot/Repair/Replace Data Cable to AP14 and replace faulty unit if needed. LIFT WILL BE ONSITE**\n\n**.**\n\n**Device With Issue: AP14**\n\n**.**\n\n**Location of Device: Floor plan attached**\n\n**.**\n\n**Customer notes: Club 177 - AP 14 is down**\n\n**Replacement unit is stored in the computer room**\n\nTech needs to TRR the data cable, ports, switch and run new data line, if needed. Replace the faulty AP unit\n\nTech should capture the location, switch number, and port assignment before departing the club\n\nTech should take pictures before and after working in the IDF/MDF\n\nTech upon arrival and after repairs should work with the NOC for verification and validation\n\n**NOC: 833-722-3102.**\n\n.\n\n**Access related issues**: Make sure you go to the back of the store and ring the door buzzer after hours. If you still cannot gain access, Call Staley Support 501-320-4738\n\n.\n\n**Closeout Notes:** Make sure everything that occurred during the visit is called out in the closeout notes\n\nPhone calls and texts will not be used in lieu of providing detailed and concise closeout notes.\n\n.\n\nTech should send pictures of IDF1, IDF2 and MDF cabinets - multiple pictures of each cabinet. (Doors opened, door closed, sideways, full view. If any of the cabinets are supported by anything for standing or holding onto the wall or anything unusual, please take pictures and let BJ’s NOC know and include it in your notes.\n\n.\n\nPictures of IDF1, IDF2 and MDF cabinets must be labeled\n\nExample: Club211IDF1 front, Club211IDF1 side and so on\n\n.\n\nIf any of the cabinets are supported by anything for standing or holding onto the wall or anything unusual, please take pictures and let BJ’s NOC know and include it in your notes.\n\nUsually, they will be in the following places:\n\nIDFs – Membership / Break room / Upstairs / Receiving / Upstairs Club Manager’s office\n\nMDFs – Computer room or Server room at the back of the club\n\n.\n\nFailure to do so will result in a penalty.\n\n**.**\n\n**Incomplete Sites:** If you cannot complete your site for any reason, call Staley Support 501-320-4738\n\n**.**\n\n**Important Information: Anytime you are bringing a lift into or out of a customer facility, whether through a doorway or overhead door, you must bring the lift to a complete stop before going through the entry. You must walk around the entire lift looking for any obstacles. Be sure to check the height of the cage vs the height of the entry. Be sure to check the width of the lift vs the width of the entry. Only when that has been completed and you are sure there are no potential contact points may you continue forward with the lift. If there is trouble with the lift, please call the number on the side of the equipment for support and let Staley Technologies know of the issues.**\n\n\\-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n**Switch Port range available for AP's**\n\nMDF Switch Ports 0-18\n\nIDF Switch Ports 0-19\n\n\\-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n**MATERIALS**\n\nQTY DESCRIPTION\n\n======================================\n\n300’ CAT6, WH, Plenum\n\n1 1 Port Faceplate\n\n1 CAT6 Jack Insert\n\n1 5’ CAT6 Patch Cables Blue\n\n**TOOLS**\n\n\\---------\n\nTech MUST have required tools to perform service job including, but not limited to:\n\nBUTTSET\n\nLAPTOP WITH CONSOLE CABLE\n\nUSB TO SERIAL CONVERTOR\n\nUSB KEYBOARD AND MOUSE\n\nPRECISE SCREWDRIVERS\n\nPUNCH TOOL W 66/110 BLADES\n\nWIRE STRIPPERS\n\nCRIMPER\n\nTONER\n\nLABELMAKER\n\nCABLE TESTER\n\nSTANDARD TOOL KIT (Screw/nut driver, tape, sharpie, pliers, etc.)\n\n8’ to 10’ LADDER\n\n\\-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n**NOTES**\n\n.\n\n\\* White, Plenum CAT6 cable is required for all permanent cable runs.\n\n\\*\\* Velcro on ALL non-permanent wire management. Including power cords and AC Adapters.\n\n\\*\\* DO NOT install any surface mount boxes in the MDF or any IDF's.\n\n\\*\\* If ports don’t exist, you will need to install a new 24-port patch panel.\n\n.\n\nATTENTION: Any IDF's in the Club with surface mount boxes must be corrected.\n\n\\-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n**TASKS**\n\n.\n\n**1)** Meet with store personnel/management and introduce yourself.\n\n a) Review details of service request with store personnel/management.\n\n.\n\n**2) Troubleshoot/Repair/Replace Data Cable for Access Point and replace (AP14).**\n\n a) Capture before pictures of the equipment and work area.\n\n b) If AP does not come online, troubleshoot with BJ’s Support\n\n c) Test network cables and determine faults. Repair as needed.\n\n\\- Test the cable.\n\n\\- Repair as needed.\n\n\\- Test the cable again to verify it has been repaired.\n\n d) If cable is damaged beyond repair, we will need to run a new drop.\n\n\\- Run 1 new data cable from network rack to AP location\n\n\\- Terminate/Test/Label new data cable\n\n\\- Patch in the newly installed data cable per site guidelines.\n\n e) If cable is confirmed to be good, install replacement AP.\n\n f) Make sure AP is connected to a switch port between 0-18 on the switch.\n\n**Call BJ’s Support (833-722-3102 option 1) to verify that everything is working correctly.**\n\n.\n\n**3) Required Pictures:**\n\n a) AP14\n\n b) Patch Panel ports\n\n c) Switch ports\n\n d) Biscuit and Jack\n\n e) Cable test results before and after work\n\n f) IDF1, IDF2 and MDF cabinets\n\nTech should send pictures of IDF1, IDF2 and MDF cabinets - multiple pictures of each cabinet. (Doors opened, door closed, sideways, full view. If any of the cabinets are supported by anything for standing or holding onto the wall or anything unusual, please take pictures and let BJ’s NOC know and include it in your notes.\n\n.\n\nPictures of IDF1, IDF2 and MDF cabinets must be labeled\n\nExample: Club211IDF1 Front, Club211IDF1 side and so on\n\n.\n\nIf any of the cabinets are supported by anything for standing or holding onto the wall or anything unusual, please take pictures and let BJ’s NOC know and include it in your notes.\n\nUsually, they will be in the following places:\n\nIDFs – Membership / Break room / Upstairs / Receiving / Upstairs Club Manager’s office\n\nMDFs – Computer room or Server room at the back of the club\n\n.\n\nFailure to do so will result in a penalty.\n\n.\n\n**Pictures of IDF1, IDF2 and MDF cabinets must be labeled**\n\n**Example** - Club143\\_MDF\\_front, Club143\\_MDF\\_side, and so on","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-16T21:45","end":"2026-09-16T25:45"},"payRange":{"min":70,"max":280},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":70,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":8},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":70,"baseAmount":280,"estHours":4,"travelExpense":0,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-09-17T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T13:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":0}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-16T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-17T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"},{"start":"2026-09-04T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-05T13:30:00.000Z","summary":"DSS 9223 - Install (1) QNAP + UPS + Switch, Install (3) TP-Link Wireless Bridge, Install (3) 8 Port PoE Switch, Replace (15) Analog Cameras w/ (15) IP Cameras + Cable Runs - Lead Tech"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1789407803100}
{"job":{"id":19948560,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Innover Digital","title":"30 min job - Zebra Scanning Device Replacement & Pairing with RDF40 (201412597-1, 201412597-2 & 201412597-3)","description":{"html":"<p>\n  <strong><u>OVERVIEW</u></strong>\n</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>Swapping the old Zebra scanning device with the new one,\n  replace the battery from the old device to the new one.\n  </li>\n  <li>Turn on the device and pairing the new VC83 / MC93 device\n  with the RFD40 scanner (if any).\n  </li>\n  <li>Request a functionality validation to the Chick-Fil-A\n  representative and get the work order form signed.\n  </li>\n  <li>Returning the old scanning device using the UPS return label\n  to the UPS store\n  </li>\n  <li>DO NOT VISIT THE SITE DURING LUNCH HOURS.\n  </li>\n</ul>\n<p>\n  <strong><u>DELIVERABLES</u></strong>\n</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>Picture of the old device serial #\n  </li>\n  <li>Picture of the new device serial #\n  </li>\n  <li>Picture of the packaging slip\n  </li>\n  <li>Picture of the UPS receipt post drop off\n  </li>\n  <li>Attach the work order acknowledgement form with the signature\n  of the manager on duty or by on-site contact. Please print the\n  form before you go on-site.\n  </li>\n</ul>\n<p>\n  <strong><u>REQUIREMENTS</u></strong>\n</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>DRESS CODE: Polo or button-up, clean and unripped jeans,\n  close toed-shoes\n  </li>\n  <li>Face mask is&nbsp;REQUIRED. Please follow social distancing\n  guidelines while onsite.\n  </li>\n  <li>Timely arrival to site\n  </li>\n  <li>Zebra Scanning Device picked up from the specified UPS RAP\n  location.\n  </li>\n  <li>Remain onsite &amp; put the battery in the new device taken\n  from the faulty one\n  </li>\n  <li>Check the equipment to ensure it is working fine\n  </li>\n  <li>Drop the collected defective device to the specified UPS\n  location.\n  </li>\n  <li>All manuals attached below\n  </li>\n  <li>Chick-Fil-A will enroll you in their visitor log, you will\n  receive an email to enroll by filling in basic details. Once\n  completed you will receive a QR code which you need to save or\n  print and presents the&nbsp;<strong>QR code</strong>&nbsp;to\n  security. Security scans/validates the QR code and confirms the\n  visit&nbsp;\n  </li>\n</ul>\n<p>\n  <strong><u>PRESITE</u></strong>\n</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>Arrive at the specified UPS Location and collect the new\n  replacement spares.\n  </li>\n</ul>\n<p>\n  <strong><u>&nbsp;ONSITE</u></strong>\n</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>Arrive to site introduce yourself to onsite contact as Zebra\n  Fasttrack Smart Hand.\n  </li>\n  <li>Check if the serial number of the defective device matches\n  (not more than 3 digits can be allowed for a mismatch) as per\n  what is mentioned in the work order (In case of incorrect serial\n  number, follow special instructions)\n  </li>\n  <li>Open the box and check the contents, take out the new device\n  in front of the customer\n  </li>\n  <li>Replace the battery from the old device to the new one, turn\n  on the new device.\n  </li>\n  <li>Carry out the instructions\n  </li>\n  <li>Hand the device to the customer to perform a thorough check\n  of the new device to ensure it is working fine\n  </li>\n  <li>Take pictures of the defective device’s serial number and the\n  replacement device\n  </li>\n  <li>Take the old device, place it in the box and paste the return\n  label on the box\n  </li>\n  <li>Call Zebra Helpdesk (+1-302-446-3094) to provide swap update\n  (In case of unsuccessful swap, follow special instructions) &amp;\n  collect the completion code while still on site\n  </li>\n</ul>\n<p>\n  &nbsp;\n</p>\n<p>\n  <strong><u>POST SITE</u></strong>\n</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>Return the defective device to the UPS RAP store from where\n  the good part was picked up\n  </li>\n  <li>Once the return package is delivered to the UPS RAP, call\n  Zebra helpdesk (+1-302-446-3094)&nbsp;to provide status\n  </li>\n</ul>\n<p>\n  <br />\n</p>\n<p>\n  <strong><u>SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS :</u></strong>\n</p>\n<p>\n  1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Unit to be collected does\n  not match the defective SN in RMA?\n</p>\n<p>\n  a.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If unit is a different\n  model and/or has a different serial number than what is mentioned\n  in the RMA, the faulty unit should be a Zebra VC83 or MC93 and\n  the serial number should match to complete the swap with the new\n  device.\n</p>\n<p>\n  b.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Customer should be informed\n  that their unit does not match that of the RMA then the swap\n  cannot be completed and the new device will be returned back\n</p>\n<p>\n  c. If Dead on Arrival - Use the return label and return the\n  device to the UPS store.\n</p>\n<p>\n  d. These devices should not have accessories on them but if for\n  some reason a device does, they should be moved to the\n  replacement unit.\n</p>\n<p>\n  Note1: Not all sites have RFD 40 Scanner.\n</p>\n<p>\n  e. The scope of the onsite activity only covers the VC83 or MC93\n  unit; therefore, any problem or issue associated with the RFD8500\n  must be reported separately to the help desk for\n  troubleshooting.&nbsp;\n</p>\n<p>\n  f. Battery should be pulled from old unit and swapped to the\n  replacement unit.\n</p>\n<p>\n  No action is required for the SIM Card.\n</p>\n<p>\n  Pair the VC83 or MC93 unit to the RFD40.\n</p>\n<p>\n  Request functionality validation from the customer\n  representative.\n</p>\n<p>\n  <strong>c.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If the damage has\n  caused the battery to leak and become dangerous Smart Hands\n  should not leave the replacement unit and request that the\n  customer calls the Zebra helpdesk for advice.</strong>\n</p>","markdown":"**OVERVIEW**\n\n- Swapping the old Zebra scanning device with the new one, replace the battery from the old device to the new one.\n- Turn on the device and pairing the new VC83 / MC93 device with the RFD40 scanner (if any).\n- Request a functionality validation to the Chick-Fil-A representative and get the work order form signed.\n- Returning the old scanning device using the UPS return label to the UPS store\n- DO NOT VISIT THE SITE DURING LUNCH HOURS.\n\n **DELIVERABLES**\n\n- Picture of the old device serial #\n- Picture of the new device serial #\n- Picture of the packaging slip\n- Picture of the UPS receipt post drop off\n- Attach the work order acknowledgement form with the signature of the manager on duty or by on-site contact. Please print the form before you go on-site.\n\n **REQUIREMENTS**\n\n- DRESS CODE: Polo or button-up, clean and unripped jeans, close toed-shoes\n- Face mask is REQUIRED. Please follow social distancing guidelines while onsite.\n- Timely arrival to site\n- Zebra Scanning Device picked up from the specified UPS RAP location.\n- Remain onsite & put the battery in the new device taken from the faulty one\n- Check the equipment to ensure it is working fine\n- Drop the collected defective device to the specified UPS location.\n- All manuals attached below\n- Chick-Fil-A will enroll you in their visitor log, you will receive an email to enroll by filling in basic details. Once completed you will receive a QR code which you need to save or print and presents the **QR code** to security. Security scans/validates the QR code and confirms the visit\n\n **PRESITE**\n\n- Arrive at the specified UPS Location and collect the new replacement spares.\n\n  **ONSITE**\n\n- Arrive to site introduce yourself to onsite contact as Zebra Fasttrack Smart Hand.\n- Check if the serial number of the defective device matches (not more than 3 digits can be allowed for a mismatch) as per what is mentioned in the work order (In case of incorrect serial number, follow special instructions)\n- Open the box and check the contents, take out the new device in front of the customer\n- Replace the battery from the old device to the new one, turn on the new device.\n- Carry out the instructions\n- Hand the device to the customer to perform a thorough check of the new device to ensure it is working fine\n- Take pictures of the defective device’s serial number and the replacement device\n- Take the old device, place it in the box and paste the return label on the box\n- Call Zebra Helpdesk (+1-302-446-3094) to provide swap update (In case of unsuccessful swap, follow special instructions) & collect the completion code while still on site\n\n **POST SITE**\n\n- Return the defective device to the UPS RAP store from where the good part was picked up\n- Once the return package is delivered to the UPS RAP, call Zebra helpdesk (+1-302-446-3094) to provide status\n\n **SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS :**\n\n 1. Unit to be collected does not match the defective SN in RMA?\n\n a. If unit is a different model and/or has a different serial number than what is mentioned in the RMA, the faulty unit should be a Zebra VC83 or MC93 and the serial number should match to complete the swap with the new device.\n\n b. Customer should be informed that their unit does not match that of the RMA then the swap cannot be completed and the new device will be returned back\n\n c. If Dead on Arrival - Use the return label and return the device to the UPS store.\n\n d. These devices should not have accessories on them but if for some reason a device does, they should be moved to the replacement unit.\n\n Note1: Not all sites have RFD 40 Scanner.\n\n e. The scope of the onsite activity only covers the VC83 or MC93 unit; therefore, any problem or issue associated with the RFD8500 must be reported separately to the help desk for troubleshooting.\n\n f. Battery should be pulled from old unit and swapped to the replacement unit.\n\n No action is required for the SIM Card.\n\n Pair the VC83 or MC93 unit to the RFD40.\n\n Request functionality validation from the customer representative.\n\n **c. If the damage has caused the battery to leak and become dangerous Smart Hands should not leave the replacement unit and request that the customer calls the Zebra helpdesk for advice.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-15T11:00","end":"2026-09-15T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":80,"max":80},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":34},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $80 is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-15T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-17T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"},{"start":"2026-09-04T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-05T13:30:00.000Z","summary":"DSS 9223 - Install (1) QNAP + UPS + Switch, Install (3) TP-Link Wireless Bridge, Install (3) 8 Port PoE Switch, Replace (15) Analog Cameras w/ (15) IP Cameras + Cable Runs - Lead Tech"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789407810960}
{"job":{"id":19948552,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"StrikeCheck","title":"Express Damage Assessment - StrikeCheck Appointment A-2713794","description":{"html":"<p>*Please make sure to read through all instructions to avoid a second visit to the property and/or non-payment*</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The following items need to be <strong><em>documented</em></strong>, <strong><em>inspected</em></strong>, <strong><em>tested</em></strong> and <strong><em>photographed, even if they are found to be non-damaged</em></strong>:</p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(32, 33, 36);\"><b><ul><li>Router : Brand Unknown : 1</li><li>Modem : Brand Unknown : 1</li><li>Garage Door Opener : Brand Unknown : 1</li></ul></b></span></p><p><br></p><p><strong>ATTENTION: Every technician must use the CCG IQ Inspection Wizard to submit their findings. We cannot complete our payment to you if the findings are submitted to the Field Nation platform or via email. All findings, including non-damaged items on your list, must be sent directly to StrikeCheck using our CCG IQ Inspection Wizard via our Android app or web portal. If any item cannot be documented you must include a statement in your notes explaining those circumstances.</strong></p><p><strong>If you are unsure of how to use our Android app or web portal, or are having issues while you are onsite, please call (888) 980-8544 and a live representative will talk you through the submission process. Android users will need to download the \"CCG IQ Inspection Wizard\" in the app store on your device. Our office hours are 8am-8pm EST Monday-Friday and 8am-5pm on Saturdays. If no one is available to take your call please leave a message and we will return your call ASAP!</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>Testing and Documentation Requirements:</strong></p><ol><li>Full testing and documentation procedures on a per-item type basis can be found under the “Resources” tab in our web app. Select “StrikeCheck” in the “Libraries” folder to review the requirements before every inspection to ensure all required data is being captured.</li><li>Basic continuity/ohm testing is required using a digital multimeter. Verify a functional power source or outlet with your meter and document those readings. If needed, reset any associated circuit breakers but do not otherwise alter the electrical panel.&nbsp;</li><li>Apply power and operationally test ALL FUNCTIONS of every item. Notate any connected items (speakers to receiver, cameras to DVR, etc.) and advise if further testing is necessary due to the failure of one of those components (\"Can't test speakers due to damaged receiver\").&nbsp;</li><li>Document and photograph all obtainable readings/testing. <strong>If the item is not damaged or has already been replaced with new equipment, we still need the same amount of evidence (photos and test results) to support your findings.</strong> If the item is not operating properly, determine the causation of damage.&nbsp;</li><li>In addition to photos of the loss location and your meter readings, we require that you provide a minimum of 3 pictures per item. These pictures should illustrate where/how the item is installed, the overall condition of the item, any visual damages, and <strong><em>most importantly, </em></strong>the data plate. Also photograph any associated components connected to the item you are inspecting. Additional photographs and documentation are always encouraged.</li></ol><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Inspection Requirements:</strong></p><ul><li>A smart phone with access to our Android app or web app portal for Apple iOS users is the preferred method to document and upload your findings in real time. Access the app or portal before the inspection begins and it will walk you through all steps required for each item you enter.</li><li>Use of a camera and our Technician Worksheets is an alternate option that will require a computer to access the web app portal in order to upload photos as well as transcribing your detailed technical documentation from the worksheets into our system.</li><li>Multimeter/VOM and a basic toolkit</li><li>Must be professionally dressed (wear a clean collared shirt and pants; No shorts, no t-shirts, no flip-flops, and no ripped jeans). Avoid wearing anything that will identify your personal employer/company name or contact info to prevent insureds from calling you directly after you complete your assignment. This is an independent inspection on behalf of StrikeCheck, an insurance consulting company. <strong>You</strong> <strong>must represent yourself as being with StrikeCheck</strong> <strong>when you arrive onsite</strong>.</li><li>Must be willing to display contractor photo identification (if issued) and must have appropriate background and skills to perform the listed work order requirements</li><li>Must have passed a background check and drug test.&nbsp;</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Submission Requirements:</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>iPhone/iPad users: Upload required information via our <strong>web portal</strong> the same day as the inspection using a secure password. Click the \"Login\" link below or use this web address to access the portal:&nbsp;https://consolidatedclaims.my.site.com/ccginspector/&nbsp;</li><li>All findings, pictures, and determinations should be submitted on the same day as the inspection. <strong>Your deadline to submit is 24 hours from the scheduled appointment start time. Failure to do so may result in non-payment and could affect your rating.</strong></li><li>Your work order is not considered complete and payable until findings are submitted through the Android app or web portal and is approved by our Processing Department. Please make yourself available for follow-up calls if we have any questions regarding your findings.</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">Scheduling Requirements:</strong></p><ul><li>These work orders most likely take place in a residential property, and therefore requires the ETA to be approved by the client.</li><li>When you are assigned this work order, please submit an ETA as soon as possible.</li><li>We will reach out to the client to confirm that they are able to be onsite during your proposed ETA. <strong><u>The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.</u></strong></li><li>A project manager will message you via the Field Nation App when the ETA has been confirmed with the insured. If you go to the loss location before we confirm the appointment is set, you will not be afforded a trip fee in the event that the insured is not present when you arrive.</li><li><strong>You must update our project managers and dispatch coordinators regularly on work order progress, any service delays, or schedule conflicts. If you cannot make an appointment CALL OUR OFFICE IMMEDIATELY TO RESCHEDULE. Field Nation messages are not an accepted medium for rescheduling or canceling appointments!</strong></li><li>If you go to the property, but the client does not show for the appointment, call us immediately so we can follow up with the client and determine if they will be arriving soon. <strong>If the client misses the appointment, you must take a clear photo of the house/property, showing the address so we can confirm you were there.</strong></li><li>StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the insured cannot make the appointment.&nbsp;</li><li>StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the scope of work cannot be completed for any reason</li><li>StrikeCheck will <em>not </em>provide a trip fee if you arrive at an appointment that has <em>not </em>been confirmed with the client and the project manager. <strong><u>The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.</u></strong></li></ul>","markdown":"\\*Please make sure to read through all instructions to avoid a second visit to the property and/or non-payment\\*\n\nThe following items need to be ***documented***, ***inspected***, ***tested*** and ***photographed, even if they are found to be non-damaged***:\n\n**- Router : Brand Unknown : 1\n\\- Modem : Brand Unknown : 1\n\\- Garage Door Opener : Brand Unknown : 1**\n\n**ATTENTION: Every technician must use the CCG IQ Inspection Wizard to submit their findings. We cannot complete our payment to you if the findings are submitted to the Field Nation platform or via email. All findings, including non-damaged items on your list, must be sent directly to StrikeCheck using our CCG IQ Inspection Wizard via our Android app or web portal. If any item cannot be documented you must include a statement in your notes explaining those circumstances.**\n\n**If you are unsure of how to use our Android app or web portal, or are having issues while you are onsite, please call (888) 980-8544 and a live representative will talk you through the submission process. Android users will need to download the \"CCG IQ Inspection Wizard\" in the app store on your device. Our office hours are 8am-8pm EST Monday-Friday and 8am-5pm on Saturdays. If no one is available to take your call please leave a message and we will return your call ASAP!**\n\n**Testing and Documentation Requirements:**\n\n1. Full testing and documentation procedures on a per-item type basis can be found under the “Resources” tab in our web app. Select “StrikeCheck” in the “Libraries” folder to review the requirements before every inspection to ensure all required data is being captured.\n2. Basic continuity/ohm testing is required using a digital multimeter. Verify a functional power source or outlet with your meter and document those readings. If needed, reset any associated circuit breakers but do not otherwise alter the electrical panel.\n3. Apply power and operationally test ALL FUNCTIONS of every item. Notate any connected items (speakers to receiver, cameras to DVR, etc.) and advise if further testing is necessary due to the failure of one of those components (\"Can't test speakers due to damaged receiver\").\n4. Document and photograph all obtainable readings/testing. **If the item is not damaged or has already been replaced with new equipment, we still need the same amount of evidence (photos and test results) to support your findings.** If the item is not operating properly, determine the causation of damage.\n5. In addition to photos of the loss location and your meter readings, we require that you provide a minimum of 3 pictures per item. These pictures should illustrate where/how the item is installed, the overall condition of the item, any visual damages, and ***most importantly,*** the data plate. Also photograph any associated components connected to the item you are inspecting. Additional photographs and documentation are always encouraged.\n\n**Inspection Requirements:**\n\n- A smart phone with access to our Android app or web app portal for Apple iOS users is the preferred method to document and upload your findings in real time. Access the app or portal before the inspection begins and it will walk you through all steps required for each item you enter.\n- Use of a camera and our Technician Worksheets is an alternate option that will require a computer to access the web app portal in order to upload photos as well as transcribing your detailed technical documentation from the worksheets into our system.\n- Multimeter/VOM and a basic toolkit\n- Must be professionally dressed (wear a clean collared shirt and pants; No shorts, no t-shirts, no flip-flops, and no ripped jeans). Avoid wearing anything that will identify your personal employer/company name or contact info to prevent insureds from calling you directly after you complete your assignment. This is an independent inspection on behalf of StrikeCheck, an insurance consulting company. **You** **must represent yourself as being with StrikeCheck** **when you arrive onsite**.\n- Must be willing to display contractor photo identification (if issued) and must have appropriate background and skills to perform the listed work order requirements\n- Must have passed a background check and drug test.\n\n**Submission Requirements:**\n\n- iPhone/iPad users: Upload required information via our **web portal** the same day as the inspection using a secure password. Click the \"Login\" link below or use this web address to access the portal: <https://consolidatedclaims.my.site.com/ccginspector/&nbsp;>\n- All findings, pictures, and determinations should be submitted on the same day as the inspection. **Your deadline to submit is 24 hours from the scheduled appointment start time. Failure to do so may result in non-payment and could affect your rating.**\n- Your work order is not considered complete and payable until findings are submitted through the Android app or web portal and is approved by our Processing Department. Please make yourself available for follow-up calls if we have any questions regarding your findings.\n\n**Scheduling Requirements:**\n\n- These work orders most likely take place in a residential property, and therefore requires the ETA to be approved by the client.\n- When you are assigned this work order, please submit an ETA as soon as possible.\n- We will reach out to the client to confirm that they are able to be onsite during your proposed ETA. **The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.**\n- A project manager will message you via the Field Nation App when the ETA has been confirmed with the insured. If you go to the loss location before we confirm the appointment is set, you will not be afforded a trip fee in the event that the insured is not present when you arrive.\n- **You must update our project managers and dispatch coordinators regularly on work order progress, any service delays, or schedule conflicts. If you cannot make an appointment CALL OUR OFFICE IMMEDIATELY TO RESCHEDULE. Field Nation messages are not an accepted medium for rescheduling or canceling appointments!**\n- If you go to the property, but the client does not show for the appointment, call us immediately so we can follow up with the client and determine if they will be arriving soon. **If the client misses the appointment, you must take a clear photo of the house/property, showing the address so we can confirm you were there.**\n- StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the insured cannot make the appointment.\n- StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the scope of work cannot be completed for any reason\n- StrikeCheck will *not* provide a trip fee if you arrive at an appointment that has *not* been confirmed with the client and the project manager. **The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-14T08:00","end":"2026-09-14T10:00","latestStart":"2026-09-14T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":17},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 9/14/2026, 8:00:00 AM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-14T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-15T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-17T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"FN"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Busy"},{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"},{"start":"2026-09-04T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-05T13:30:00.000Z","summary":"DSS 9223 - Install (1) QNAP + UPS + Switch, Install (3) TP-Link Wireless Bridge, Install (3) 8 Port PoE Switch, Replace (15) Analog Cameras w/ (15) IP Cameras + Cable Runs - Lead Tech"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789407816752}
{"job":{"id":19948221,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"ASR tech","title":"Perform Maintenance on an Automated Package Locker System (MUST HAVE ALL REQUIRED TOOLS)","description":{"html":"<p><strong><em>**PLEASE&nbsp;<u>READ</u>&nbsp;THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER BEFORE ACCEPTING*</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>*PLEASE&nbsp;<u>READ&nbsp;</u>PROBLEM DESCRIPTION/SCOPE OF WORK BEFORE ACCEPTING*</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>*PLEASE&nbsp;<u>READ&nbsp;</u>TOOL REQUIREMENT BEFORE ACCEPTING**</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>**PROBLEM DESCRIPTION/SCOPE OF WORK**</u></strong></p><p><strong><em><u>&nbsp;The following has been reported:</u></em></strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Outdoor Zhilai - -</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">HIGH || Service Call - - Once onsite, Call Jon at 949-326-7349. If unavailable, call Field Service line 949-317-4169.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- No parts sent out</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- Requesting tech for Tuesday 9/15 after 11am, EDT</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- Need to:&nbsp;inspect cage 33, replace lock on door</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- General Maintenance (Open All Box, Package Maintenance, Disabled Doors, Test Camera, Barcode scanner)</span></p><p><strong><em>Ensure the system is fully functional. General Linux, electrical, and mechanical knowledge is required, but technical support will guide you through most of the process. Professionalism and attention to detail are required for this client.&nbsp;&nbsp;Please be mindful of how you are representing ASR and yourself.&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>**TOOL REQUIREMENT**ALL TOOLS LISTED ARE REQUIRED**</u></strong></p><p><strong>Government issued Identification</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Standard Technicians tool kit</strong></li><li><strong>Precision screwdriver set</strong></li><li><strong>Rubber Mallet</strong></li><li><strong>4' ladder</strong></li><li><strong>5\" round reusable hard surface sliders (or similar for floor protection)</strong></li><li><strong>Laptop w/ HyperTerminal or Putty, must be able to connect to CAT5 Cable and runs Windows XP or higher</strong></li><li><strong>Laptop must have Team Viewer</strong></li><li><strong>Drill/Driver</strong></li><li><strong>Laptop Charger</strong></li><li><strong>Wired USB Keyboard</strong></li><li><strong>6ft Crossover patch cable</strong></li><li><strong>6ft Standard patch cable</strong></li><li><strong>22-16 AWG&nbsp;wire splicing connectors</strong></li><li><strong>Silicone caulking (for end of self-tapping screws)</strong></li><li><strong>Crimper/Stripper tool</strong></li><li><strong>Punch Down tool (used to terminate keystone jacks)</strong></li><li><strong>Smart Phone with ability to access e-mail and open a mobile web page, Camera, Text</strong></li><li><strong>Smart Phone Charger</strong></li><li><strong>Digital Camera or the Smart Phone Camera (Must upload all photos of equipment worked on)</strong></li><li><strong>Dry Cloth/Towel and non-abrasive cleaner (wipe down lockers before leaving site)</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Download, print, review, and bring the attached PDFs to site:&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>ServiceCallChecklist rev1_1.pdf</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>SCOPE OF WORK MAY include open all box test, redelivering all packages, check for jammed/disabled doors, etc.</strong></p><p><strong>Some issues may take longer than expected.&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Potential issues can include any or all of the following:</p><ul><li>Jammed Door</li><li>Controller Unit Replacement</li><li>Sub Board Replacement</li><li>Solenoid Replacement</li><li>Clear Box/Redeliver Packages</li><li>If parts are to be returned, please use the prepaid return label provided</li><li>IMPORTANT:Please Take Photos of the equipment and parts before packing and returning</li></ul><p><strong><em><u>Professionalism, attention to detail, and customer care are required for this client, Customer Service skills are a must!&nbsp;Any discussion of prior work performed by anyone is not allowed. This may be reported back to Parcel and ASR. It may be interpreted as unprofessional behavior.</u></em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>ASR PROFESSIONALISM REQUIREMENTS</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Technician should NOT discuss any scheduling or payment issues with Parcel Pending support desk under any circumstances. Any scheduling or payment issues MUST be discussed with ASR.&nbsp;&nbsp;</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>If the customer reaches out directly to you, please refer them back to ASR.</u></strong></p><ul><li>Perform excellent customer service. Be friendly, communicate, and assure them they're in good hands.&nbsp;</li><li>Dress code is casual business attire with no logos.</li><li>Do not share any pricing information with client.&nbsp;</li><li>Do not leave personal business information or contact information with client.</li><li>Technician needs to ensure that each site is a DRUG-FREE WORKPLACE</li><li>The technician needs to ensure they do not smell or reek of odors or other substances.</li></ul><p><strong><u>ASR Services intends to help provide a safe and drug-free work environment for our clients.</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>The Company explicitly prohibits:</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>The use, possession, solicitation for, or sale of narcotics or other illegal drugs, alcohol, or prescription medication without a prescription on customer premises or while performing an assignment.</u></strong></p><p><strong><em><u>ASR Project Number: 887</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><u>STEP ONE:</u></strong></p><p><strong>CHECK-IN: With Parcel Pending, be mindful as you are in contact with the customer directly (your contact name and number is listed under the Problem Description)&nbsp;Ask if any Parts were shipped to site and who has the parts onsite. DO NOT PERFORM ANY WORK&nbsp;until you have contacted Parcel Pending.&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>Please contact our customer when you have arrived onsite.</strong></p><p><strong>***Always Leave a message if your contact does not answer and then call their Field Service line&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************</del></span>***</p><p><strong><u>STEP TWO:</u></strong></p><p><strong>CHECK-IN:On Field Nation - Please do not check in on&nbsp;Field Nation until you have checked in with Parcel Pending.&nbsp;​Your check-in/out times MUST match what Parcel Pending provides us.</strong></p><p><strong><u>STEP THREE:</u></strong></p><p><strong>LOCATE: Leasing/Rental Office, General Contractors Office, Concierge, Front Desk etc. Once in contact, ask for parts, if they were shipped.&nbsp;You would have this information from your contact in step one.</strong></p><p><strong><u>STEP FOUR:</u></strong></p><p><strong>FOLLOW: Direction from Parcel Pending.&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><u>STEP FIVE:</u></strong></p><p><strong>REPORT: PROBLEMS/ISSUES&nbsp;BEFORE LEAVING SITE and&nbsp;<u>CHECK-OUT.</u>&nbsp;&nbsp;Please do NOT check out on Field Nation until you have checked out with Parcel Pending.&nbsp;​(Number and tech support name will be under the Problem Description</strong>)&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Your check-in/out times MUST match what our customer provides us.</strong></p><p><strong><u>STEP SIX:</u></strong></p><p><strong>SUBMIT</strong>: W<strong>ork order for payment within 24 hours of scheduled date.&nbsp;</strong>Please provide&nbsp;<strong>detailed closing notes</strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>timeline&nbsp;</strong>when submitting this work order for payment.</p><p><strong><em>The name of the individual accepting this work must be the actual person who arrives on site and if we determine there was a substitution without prior notice, we will not pay for the work performed.&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Be sure to notify ASR by phone and message in work order prior to tech arriving onsite.&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong>ACCEPTING THIS WORK ORDER MEANS THAT YOU WILL HAVE ALL OF THE REQUIRED TOOLS.&nbsp;ALSO, HAVE READ AND UNDERSTAND THE SCOPE OF WORK.&nbsp;&nbsp;PLEASE UPDATE YOUR ETA AS SOON AS YOU ARE ASSIGNED. YOU WILL BE HELD RESPONSIBLE FOR ARRIVING ON THE SCHEDULED DATE AND TIME. ANY VIOLATIONS WILL BE ESCALATED TO FIELD NATION.&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><em>Parcel Pending and Site may provide a report card based on professionalism and understanding of work being done.&nbsp;</em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Tech should NOT discuss payment or scheduling discrepancies with Parcel Pending, Site Contact or anyone but ASR (NO exceptions)</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>***Please CALL Rodrigo R. 949-556-3604</strong>&nbsp;for any general questions/information.***</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>ONSITE DETAILS &amp; CONDUCT</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>If you are unable to make it to site, you must call/text Rodrigo </strong>(Phone number in Confidential Information)</li><li><strong>Work Order is subject to Penalty Fee at Buyers Discretion.&nbsp;</strong></li><li><strong>You will be representing ASR Services when communicating with the end user or Parcel Pending support.</strong></li><li><strong>All conversation on site should be kept to business related items and not personal matters.&nbsp;</strong></li><li><strong>Resolve the issues using the documentation provided with support from Technical Support.</strong></li><li><strong>Do not access the \"System Maintenance Screen\" unless instructed by Technical Support.</strong></li><li><strong><u>Upon completion of service:&nbsp;KEY NEEDS TO BE IN SECURE LOCATION</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>a: please return keys to MOD onsite. Will need first and last name of keyholder (this info is required for release from site and Work Order closure).</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>b: If no onsite personnel are onsite/available, ask Parcel Pending Support/ASR Support Team member with whom you are working for direction on where keys should be left.&nbsp;</u></strong></li><li><strong>If you are requested to do anything out side of the scope of work, including returning to site, or dealing with a DOA, you must call/text Rodrigo.&nbsp;</strong>(Phone number in Confidential Information)</li><li><strong>Tech must provide photos of any equipment that is worked on.</strong></li><li><strong>Tech must fill out the ServiceCallChecklist rev1_1.pdf COMPLETELY and have it signed by the property manager</strong></li><li><strong>Tech must note arrival and departure times on sign off sheet, document any site delays and requests that are made out of the scope of work in the closing notes.</strong></li><li><strong>During completion, tech must provide any photos, closing notes, open issues, service call checklist, sign off sheet, and name of person that released tech from site.</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>RETURNING EQUIPMENT</u></strong></p><p><strong>If any equipment needs to be returned to Parcel Pending after completion please take a photo of equipment or parts before leaving site (damaged or undamaged) to ensure responsibility.&nbsp;A return label will be in the shipping pouch behind the original shipping label.</strong></p><p><strong>If a return label was not provided, please contact Parcel Pending immediately to obtain BEFORE leaving site, they will email a return label to you.</strong></p><p><strong>***A release code will be provided to you once tracking shows that parts are on the way back to our customer***</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>PAYMENT</u></strong></p><p>2 hours on site will be paid at a fixed rate of $85 with a potential of up to 2 additional hours paid in 15 min intervals @ $40/hr.</p><p><strong>Some issues may take long.&nbsp;Any time on site, after 2 hours, will need to be approved by Parcel Pending.</strong></p><p><strong>Your check in/out times on this work order must match what our customer provides.</strong></p><p>Site abort where technician does not go to site, but within 24 hrs $30.00</p><p>Site abort with technician onsite – determined by time spent at site.</p><p>Cancellation with more than 24 hrs notice will be paid $0.</p>","markdown":"***\\*\\*PLEASE READ THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER BEFORE ACCEPTING\\****\n\n***\\*PLEASE READ PROBLEM DESCRIPTION/SCOPE OF WORK BEFORE ACCEPTING\\****\n\n***\\*PLEASE READ TOOL REQUIREMENT BEFORE ACCEPTING\\*\\****\n\n**\\*\\*PROBLEM DESCRIPTION/SCOPE OF WORK\\*\\***\n\n ***The following has been reported:***\n\nOutdoor Zhilai - -\n\nHIGH || Service Call - - Once onsite, Call Jon at 949-326-7349. If unavailable, call Field Service line 949-317-4169.\n\n\\- No parts sent out\n\n\\- Requesting tech for Tuesday 9/15 after 11am, EDT\n\n\\- Need to: inspect cage 33, replace lock on door\n\n\\- General Maintenance (Open All Box, Package Maintenance, Disabled Doors, Test Camera, Barcode scanner)\n\n***Ensure the system is fully functional. General Linux, electrical, and mechanical knowledge is required, but technical support will guide you through most of the process. Professionalism and attention to detail are required for this client. Please be mindful of how you are representing ASR and yourself.***\n\n**\\*\\*TOOL REQUIREMENT\\*\\*ALL TOOLS LISTED ARE REQUIRED\\*\\***\n\n**Government issued Identification**\n\n- **Standard Technicians tool kit**\n- **Precision screwdriver set**\n- **Rubber Mallet**\n- **4' ladder**\n- **5\" round reusable hard surface sliders (or similar for floor protection)**\n- **Laptop w/ HyperTerminal or Putty, must be able to connect to CAT5 Cable and runs Windows XP or higher**\n- **Laptop must have Team Viewer**\n- **Drill/Driver**\n- **Laptop Charger**\n- **Wired USB Keyboard**\n- **6ft Crossover patch cable**\n- **6ft Standard patch cable**\n- **22-16 AWG wire splicing connectors**\n- **Silicone caulking (for end of self-tapping screws)**\n- **Crimper/Stripper tool**\n- **Punch Down tool (used to terminate keystone jacks)**\n- **Smart Phone with ability to access e-mail and open a mobile web page, Camera, Text**\n- **Smart Phone Charger**\n- **Digital Camera or the Smart Phone Camera (Must upload all photos of equipment worked on)**\n- **Dry Cloth/Towel and non-abrasive cleaner (wipe down lockers before leaving site)**\n\n**Download, print, review, and bring the attached PDFs to site:**\n\n- ServiceCallChecklist rev1\\_1.pdf\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK MAY include open all box test, redelivering all packages, check for jammed/disabled doors, etc.**\n\n**Some issues may take longer than expected.**\n\nPotential issues can include any or all of the following:\n\n- Jammed Door\n- Controller Unit Replacement\n- Sub Board Replacement\n- Solenoid Replacement\n- Clear Box/Redeliver Packages\n- If parts are to be returned, please use the prepaid return label provided\n- IMPORTANT:Please Take Photos of the equipment and parts before packing and returning\n\n***Professionalism, attention to detail, and customer care are required for this client, Customer Service skills are a must! Any discussion of prior work performed by anyone is not allowed. This may be reported back to Parcel and ASR. It may be interpreted as unprofessional behavior.***\n\n**ASR PROFESSIONALISM REQUIREMENTS**\n\n**Technician should NOT discuss any scheduling or payment issues with Parcel Pending support desk under any circumstances. Any scheduling or payment issues MUST be discussed with ASR.**\n\n**If the customer reaches out directly to you, please refer them back to ASR.**\n\n- Perform excellent customer service. Be friendly, communicate, and assure them they're in good hands.\n- Dress code is casual business attire with no logos.\n- Do not share any pricing information with client.\n- Do not leave personal business information or contact information with client.\n- Technician needs to ensure that each site is a DRUG-FREE WORKPLACE\n- The technician needs to ensure they do not smell or reek of odors or other substances.\n\n**ASR Services intends to help provide a safe and drug-free work environment for our clients.**\n\n**The Company explicitly prohibits:**\n\n**The use, possession, solicitation for, or sale of narcotics or other illegal drugs, alcohol, or prescription medication without a prescription on customer premises or while performing an assignment.**\n\n***ASR Project Number: 887***\n\n**STEP ONE:**\n\n**CHECK-IN: With Parcel Pending, be mindful as you are in contact with the customer directly (your contact name and number is listed under the Problem Description) Ask if any Parts were shipped to site and who has the parts onsite. DO NOT PERFORM ANY WORK until you have contacted Parcel Pending.**\n\n**Please contact our customer when you have arrived onsite.**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*Always Leave a message if your contact does not answer and then call their Field Service line** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**STEP TWO:**\n\n**CHECK-IN:On Field Nation - Please do not check in on Field Nation until you have checked in with Parcel Pending. ​Your check-in/out times MUST match what Parcel Pending provides us.**\n\n**STEP THREE:**\n\n**LOCATE: Leasing/Rental Office, General Contractors Office, Concierge, Front Desk etc. Once in contact, ask for parts, if they were shipped. You would have this information from your contact in step one.**\n\n**STEP FOUR:**\n\n**FOLLOW: Direction from Parcel Pending.**\n\n**STEP FIVE:**\n\n**REPORT: PROBLEMS/ISSUES BEFORE LEAVING SITE and CHECK-OUT. Please do NOT check out on Field Nation until you have checked out with Parcel Pending. ​(Number and tech support name will be under the Problem Description**) **Your check-in/out times MUST match what our customer provides us.**\n\n**STEP SIX:**\n\n**SUBMIT**: W**ork order for payment within 24 hours of scheduled date.** Please provide **detailed closing notes** and **timeline** when submitting this work order for payment.\n\n***The name of the individual accepting this work must be the actual person who arrives on site and if we determine there was a substitution without prior notice, we will not pay for the work performed.***\n\n***Be sure to notify ASR by phone and message in work order prior to tech arriving onsite.***\n\n**ACCEPTING THIS WORK ORDER MEANS THAT YOU WILL HAVE ALL OF THE REQUIRED TOOLS. ALSO, HAVE READ AND UNDERSTAND THE SCOPE OF WORK. PLEASE UPDATE YOUR ETA AS SOON AS YOU ARE ASSIGNED. YOU WILL BE HELD RESPONSIBLE FOR ARRIVING ON THE SCHEDULED DATE AND TIME. ANY VIOLATIONS WILL BE ESCALATED TO FIELD NATION.**\n\n***Parcel Pending and Site may provide a report card based on professionalism and understanding of work being done.***\n\n**Tech should NOT discuss payment or scheduling discrepancies with Parcel Pending, Site Contact or anyone but ASR (NO exceptions)**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*Please CALL Rodrigo R. 949-556-3604** for any general questions/information.\\*\\*\\*\n\n**ONSITE DETAILS & CONDUCT**\n\n- **If you are unable to make it to site, you must call/text Rodrigo** (Phone number in Confidential Information)\n- **Work Order is subject to Penalty Fee at Buyers Discretion.**\n- **You will be representing ASR Services when communicating with the end user or Parcel Pending support.**\n- **All conversation on site should be kept to business related items and not personal matters.**\n- **Resolve the issues using the documentation provided with support from Technical Support.**\n- **Do not access the \"System Maintenance Screen\" unless instructed by Technical Support.**\n- **Upon completion of service: KEY NEEDS TO BE IN SECURE LOCATION**\n- **a: please return keys to MOD onsite. Will need first and last name of keyholder (this info is required for release from site and Work Order closure).**\n- **b: If no onsite personnel are onsite/available, ask Parcel Pending Support/ASR Support Team member with whom you are working for direction on where keys should be left.**\n- **If you are requested to do anything out side of the scope of work, including returning to site, or dealing with a DOA, you must call/text Rodrigo.** (Phone number in Confidential Information)\n- **Tech must provide photos of any equipment that is worked on.**\n- **Tech must fill out the ServiceCallChecklist rev1\\_1.pdf COMPLETELY and have it signed by the property manager**\n- **Tech must note arrival and departure times on sign off sheet, document any site delays and requests that are made out of the scope of work in the closing notes.**\n- **During completion, tech must provide any photos, closing notes, open issues, service call checklist, sign off sheet, and name of person that released tech from site.**\n\n**RETURNING EQUIPMENT**\n\n**If any equipment needs to be returned to Parcel Pending after completion please take a photo of equipment or parts before leaving site (damaged or undamaged) to ensure responsibility. A return label will be in the shipping pouch behind the original shipping label.**\n\n**If a return label was not provided, please contact Parcel Pending immediately to obtain BEFORE leaving site, they will email a return label to you.**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*A release code will be provided to you once tracking shows that parts are on the way back to our customer\\*\\*\\***\n\n**PAYMENT**\n\n2 hours on site will be paid at a fixed rate of $85 with a potential of up to 2 additional hours paid in 15 min intervals @ $40/hr.\n\n**Some issues may take long. Any time on site, after 2 hours, will need to be approved by Parcel Pending.**\n\n**Your check in/out times on this work order must match what our customer provides.**\n\nSite abort where technician does not go to site, but within 24 hrs $30.00\n\nSite abort with technician onsite – determined by time spent at site.\n\nCancellation with more than 24 hrs notice will be paid $0.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-15T11:00","end":"2026-09-15T13:00","latestStart":"2026-09-15T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":85,"max":125},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":85},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":40}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":18},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $125 is below minimum threshold $180"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-15T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-17T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"},{"start":"2026-09-04T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-05T13:30:00.000Z","summary":"DSS 9223 - Install (1) QNAP + UPS + Switch, Install (3) TP-Link Wireless Bridge, Inst