{"job":{"id":19949444,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Telcon Associates","title":"Tech to complete a comprehensive survey of existing services and equipment on site.","description":{"html":"<p>TTS_TR RPM Rigsbee Collection BNS 62916 MAH 63012</p><p>311 Rigsbee Ave, Durham NC 27701</p><p>POC: Manager (984) 271-7100</p><p>Hours: M,W, F 9-6 PM T &amp; Thurs 10-6 PM</p><p>Requestor: Brent Satterlee: 913-307-5945</p><p>SOW:&nbsp;</p><p>Tech to complete a comprehensive survey of existing services and equipment on site.</p><p>Tech to review spreadsheet and fill out as information is found onsite.</p><p>Tech to provide photo documentation of all equipment as requested in spread sheet.</p><p>Tech to gather any and all additional equipment/services that are found onsite that are not specified in the spread sheet for updating documents.</p><p>Tech to ensure that any lines or services that are not connected or not in use be called out on the spread sheet.</p><p>Tech to provide filled out spread sheet and photos to TTS Rep prior to leaving site.</p><p>Tech to review all photos and documentation with TTS Rep.</p>","markdown":"TTS\\_TR RPM Rigsbee Collection BNS 62916 MAH 63012\n\n311 Rigsbee Ave, Durham NC 27701\n\nPOC: Manager (984) 271-7100\n\nHours: M,W, F 9-6 PM T & Thurs 10-6 PM\n\nRequestor: Brent Satterlee: 913-307-5945\n\nSOW:\n\nTech to complete a comprehensive survey of existing services and equipment on site.\n\nTech to review spreadsheet and fill out as information is found onsite.\n\nTech to provide photo documentation of all equipment as requested in spread sheet.\n\nTech to gather any and all additional equipment/services that are found onsite that are not specified in the spread sheet for updating documents.\n\nTech to ensure that any lines or services that are not connected or not in use be called out on the spread sheet.\n\nTech to provide filled out spread sheet and photos to TTS Rep prior to leaving site.\n\nTech to review all photos and documentation with TTS Rep.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-17T10:00","end":"2026-09-17T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":70,"max":140},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":70,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":11},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $140 (countered: $140) is below minimum threshold $250"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-17T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"},{"start":"2026-09-04T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-05T13:30:00.000Z","summary":"DSS 9223 - Install (1) QNAP + UPS + Switch, Install (3) TP-Link Wireless Bridge, Install (3) 8 Port PoE Switch, Replace (15) Analog Cameras w/ (15) IP Cameras + Cable Runs - Lead Tech"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789408975541}
{"job":{"id":19949524,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Telco Holdings Inc","title":"Raleigh, NC - X ray sensor USB port broken - 9/21","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Provider, Please Read the following:</strong></p><p>By accepting this assignment, you confirm you have reviewed and understand all attached documentation, including floor plans and SOW documents.</p><p>Tobacco and vape use is prohibited onsite at all times, including inside, outside, and in personal vehicles while checked in or obtaining materials for this work order.</p><p>Technicians must maintain business-casual attire. No flip-flops, torn clothing, tank tops, shorts, hats, open/excessively revealing clothing, or athletic wear. Clean jeans and sneakers are acceptable.</p><p>The NTE listed on the work order is an estimated labor allowance only and does not guarantee payable hours.</p><p>Technician(s) requested to assist with an onsite dispatch. Technician must follow all steps below to ensure that work is completed:</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Service Address &amp; Details:</p><p>Service Ticket number: 632373 - Priority 2 - High Xray Sensors - X ray sensor USB port broken</p><p>Client Location Name: Guardian Dentistry Partners | Adams &amp; Cheek Dentistry</p><p>Client Location Address: 11001 Raven Ridge Rd Suite 101, Raleigh, NC&nbsp;27614</p><p>Number of Technicians: 1</p><p>Technician Type: Smart Hands</p><p>Technical Vetting Needed?: Able to run cable through a wall</p><p>****Technician MUST present as on-site for ThincForward Inc.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Access Hours:</p><p>Preferred Days/Times for On Site Dispatch: Monday 9/21 @ 1pm EST</p><p>NTE: 2 hours</p><p>****Business casual attire required – no flip flops, open toed shoes, or torn clothing.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Tools/Equipment Required:</p><p><br></p><p>***Bring a long USB 2.0 Extension cable</p><p><br></p><p>Laptop and Hot spot for internet access</p><p>Cable Tester and Toner</p><p>Screw drivers.</p><p>Spare Patch Cords (Length varies)</p><p>Spare Keystone Jacks for replacement of bad ones</p><p>Butt Set if troubleshooting Telecom Issues</p><p>Cable ties/cable management options for general cleanup where needed</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Local Site Contact Name and Number: <del>*** *** **** ********</del></p><p>Technical Support Contact (Off-Site):</p><p>ThincForward Helpdesk Support - 267-434-1600</p><p>*Please call and leave a message if there is no answer.&nbsp;If your call is not returned in 15 minutes, please call in again and if there is no answer, please call your Dispatcher/Work Order Manager for support.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Scope Of Work:</p><p>Technician(s) requested to assist with an onsite dispatch. Technician must follow all steps below to ensure that work is completed:</p><p>1) Upon arrival call your work order manager/dispatch contact to check in on site.</p><p>2) Once checked in please call the Technical Support Contact (ThincForward Helpdesk Support - 267-434-1600) to review SOW and then proceed to the front desk to check in with the site contact.</p><p>3) Introduce yourself to the site contact as onsite as ThincForward and briefly review the SOW you will be completing.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>4) Detailed Scope of Work: **Smart Hands technician needed on site to: **Tech must bring a long USB extension cable that can be run through a wall. Tech must confirm the current USB wall port doesn't work and if so, run the new cable through the wall to the computer to replace it. Call the IT Helpdesk for support.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>5) Take images of ALL completed work on site including cabling, jacks/faceplates, and replaced equipment in functional order.</p><p>6) *Old Equipment:*&nbsp;If you have replaced equipment on site, please follow the notes below regarding what to do with the old items.</p><p>Please dispose of the old equipment.</p><p>7) Once SOW is completed, Technician(s) must confirm all equipment on site is up and operational, and technician(s) must speak with technical support prior to leaving the site to ensure SOW is complete and to ensure there are no delays in payment.</p><p>8) Once the site and support have confirmed work is completed, technician(s) must check out with the work order manager/dispatch contact to sign out of the location.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Deliverables:</p><p>- Images of ALL completed work.</p><p>- Name of person worked with on site and in support.</p><p>- Confirmation that work area has been completely cleaned and is dust free.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>***DISCLAIMER - PLEASE READ***</strong></p><p><strong>*In order for the FN work order to be considered complete and approved for payment all assigned tasks must be executed. If tasks are not completed or information is missing, this may delay the approval process and payment for services rendered.&nbsp;*</strong></p><p><strong>﻿If you are early or late, you must notify your Work Order Manager.&nbsp;Please note that failure to adhere to the agreed hard start time in this ticket may affect payment.</strong></p><p><strong><em>&nbsp;</em></strong></p><ul><li><strong>Call</strong> Work Order Manager regarding your assigned Field Nation Work Order to check in</li><li><strong>Call</strong> Project Manager/Tech regarding Your FN Work Order to check in onsite and verify SOW</li><li><strong>After Work has been completed, ensure work area is cleaned up</strong></li><li><strong>Upload/take photo</strong> of Provide Images of all completed work</li><li><strong>Upload file</strong> of Complete Attached Tech Sign Off Sheet in full and collect onsite client signature</li><li><strong>Call</strong> Project Manager/Tech regarding Your FN Work Order to confirm all work is complete and check off site</li><li><strong>Call</strong> Work Order Manager regarding your assigned Field Nation Work Order to check off site</li></ul>","markdown":"**Provider, Please Read the following:**\n\nBy accepting this assignment, you confirm you have reviewed and understand all attached documentation, including floor plans and SOW documents.\n\nTobacco and vape use is prohibited onsite at all times, including inside, outside, and in personal vehicles while checked in or obtaining materials for this work order.\n\nTechnicians must maintain business-casual attire. No flip-flops, torn clothing, tank tops, shorts, hats, open/excessively revealing clothing, or athletic wear. Clean jeans and sneakers are acceptable.\n\nThe NTE listed on the work order is an estimated labor allowance only and does not guarantee payable hours.\n\nTechnician(s) requested to assist with an onsite dispatch. Technician must follow all steps below to ensure that work is completed:\n\nService Address & Details:\n\nService Ticket number: 632373 - Priority 2 - High Xray Sensors - X ray sensor USB port broken\n\nClient Location Name: Guardian Dentistry Partners | Adams & Cheek Dentistry\n\nClient Location Address: 11001 Raven Ridge Rd Suite 101, Raleigh, NC 27614\n\nNumber of Technicians: 1\n\nTechnician Type: Smart Hands\n\nTechnical Vetting Needed?: Able to run cable through a wall\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*Technician MUST present as on-site for ThincForward Inc.\n\nAccess Hours:\n\nPreferred Days/Times for On Site Dispatch: Monday 9/21 @ 1pm EST\n\nNTE: 2 hours\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*Business casual attire required – no flip flops, open toed shoes, or torn clothing.\n\nTools/Equipment Required:\n\n\\*\\*\\*Bring a long USB 2.0 Extension cable\n\nLaptop and Hot spot for internet access\n\nCable Tester and Toner\n\nScrew drivers.\n\nSpare Patch Cords (Length varies)\n\nSpare Keystone Jacks for replacement of bad ones\n\nButt Set if troubleshooting Telecom Issues\n\nCable ties/cable management options for general cleanup where needed\n\nLocal Site Contact Name and Number: \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nTechnical Support Contact (Off-Site):\n\nThincForward Helpdesk Support - 267-434-1600\n\n\\*Please call and leave a message if there is no answer. If your call is not returned in 15 minutes, please call in again and if there is no answer, please call your Dispatcher/Work Order Manager for support.\n\nScope Of Work:\n\nTechnician(s) requested to assist with an onsite dispatch. Technician must follow all steps below to ensure that work is completed:\n\n1\\) Upon arrival call your work order manager/dispatch contact to check in on site.\n\n2\\) Once checked in please call the Technical Support Contact (ThincForward Helpdesk Support - 267-434-1600) to review SOW and then proceed to the front desk to check in with the site contact.\n\n3\\) Introduce yourself to the site contact as onsite as ThincForward and briefly review the SOW you will be completing.\n\n4\\) Detailed Scope of Work: \\*\\*Smart Hands technician needed on site to: \\*\\*Tech must bring a long USB extension cable that can be run through a wall. Tech must confirm the current USB wall port doesn't work and if so, run the new cable through the wall to the computer to replace it. Call the IT Helpdesk for support.\n\n5\\) Take images of ALL completed work on site including cabling, jacks/faceplates, and replaced equipment in functional order.\n\n6\\) \\*Old Equipment:\\* If you have replaced equipment on site, please follow the notes below regarding what to do with the old items.\n\nPlease dispose of the old equipment.\n\n7\\) Once SOW is completed, Technician(s) must confirm all equipment on site is up and operational, and technician(s) must speak with technical support prior to leaving the site to ensure SOW is complete and to ensure there are no delays in payment.\n\n8\\) Once the site and support have confirmed work is completed, technician(s) must check out with the work order manager/dispatch contact to sign out of the location.\n\nDeliverables:\n\n\\- Images of ALL completed work.\n\n\\- Name of person worked with on site and in support.\n\n\\- Confirmation that work area has been completely cleaned and is dust free.\n\n**\\*\\*\\*DISCLAIMER - PLEASE READ\\*\\*\\***\n\n**\\*In order for the FN work order to be considered complete and approved for payment all assigned tasks must be executed. If tasks are not completed or information is missing, this may delay the approval process and payment for services rendered. \\***\n\n**﻿If you are early or late, you must notify your Work Order Manager. Please note that failure to adhere to the agreed hard start time in this ticket may affect payment.**\n\n- **Call** Work Order Manager regarding your assigned Field Nation Work Order to check in\n- **Call** Project Manager/Tech regarding Your FN Work Order to check in onsite and verify SOW\n- **After Work has been completed, ensure work area is cleaned up**\n- **Upload/take photo** of Provide Images of all completed work\n- **Upload file** of Complete Attached Tech Sign Off Sheet in full and collect onsite client signature\n- **Call** Project Manager/Tech regarding Your FN Work Order to confirm all work is complete and check off site\n- **Call** Work Order Manager regarding your assigned Field Nation Work Order to check off site","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-21T13:00","end":"2026-09-21T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":90,"max":180},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":90,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":8},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $180 (countered: $180) is below minimum threshold $250