{"job":{"id":19949318,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Global Net Commerce Inc GNCI","title":"Cellular Site Survey","description":{"html":"<p>Site survey to determine best cellular carrier.&nbsp;&nbsp;Test takes about about one hour to complete.</p><p><strong>***Survey kit will be shipped to FedEx***</strong></p><p><strong><u>Provider Must Bring The Following Required Equipment:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Smartphone</li><li>FWA02 Survey Kit (shipped to FedEx prior to survey date)</li><li>50’ Extension cord</li><li>6-Outlet Power Strip</li></ul><p><strong>Instructions:</strong></p><p>Upon arrival at location introduce yourself to site contact.&nbsp;Proceed to testing location and set up survey equipment per the attached <em>FWA02 Kit Guide</em>, then call GNCI (949-515-1960) to launch survey.&nbsp;After survey is complete, return survey kit in same box, in same condition as received, using provided FedEx return shipping label.</p><p><strong>Accepted Expenses:</strong></p><p>Parking fees and FedEx fees with a receipt of the total amount, unforeseen issues with the site contact or equipment resulting in extended time (each amount accepted will differ based on the situation), and extra tests that are added at the site ($50 added for extra tests).</p><p><strong>Unaccepted Expenses:</strong></p><p>Toll road expense, extended travel expense.</p><p><strong>Work order paid when return delivery is complete.</strong></p>","markdown":"Site survey to determine best cellular carrier. Test takes about about one hour to complete.\n\n**\\*\\*\\*Survey kit will be shipped to FedEx\\*\\*\\***\n\n**Provider Must Bring The Following Required Equipment:**\n\n- Smartphone\n- FWA02 Survey Kit (shipped to FedEx prior to survey date)\n- 50’ Extension cord\n- 6-Outlet Power Strip\n\n**Instructions:**\n\nUpon arrival at location introduce yourself to site contact. Proceed to testing location and set up survey equipment per the attached *FWA02 Kit Guide*, then call GNCI (949-515-1960) to launch survey. After survey is complete, return survey kit in same box, in same condition as received, using provided FedEx return shipping label.\n\n**Accepted Expenses:**\n\nParking fees and FedEx fees with a receipt of the total amount, unforeseen issues with the site contact or equipment resulting in extended time (each amount accepted will differ based on the situation), and extra tests that are added at the site ($50 added for extra tests).\n\n**Unaccepted Expenses:**\n\nToll road expense, extended travel expense.\n\n**Work order paid when return delivery is complete.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-21T11:00","end":"2026-09-21T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":61},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 is below minimum threshold $250"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"},{"start":"2026-09-04T13:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-05T13:30:00.000Z","summary":"DSS 9223 - Install (1) QNAP + UPS + Switch, Install (3) TP-Link Wireless Bridge, Install (3) 8 Port PoE Switch, Replace (15) Analog Cameras w/ (15) IP Cameras + Cable Runs - Lead Tech"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789409808825}
{"job":{"id":19321598,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Worldlink Integration Group","title":"DSS 9223 - Install (1) QNAP + UPS + Switch, Install (3) TP-Link Wireless Bridge, Install (3) 8 Port PoE Switch, Replace (15) Analog Cameras w/ (15) IP Cameras + Cable Runs - Lead Tech","description":{"html":"<p><strong>WE ARE WORKING TO IMPROVE THE APPROVAL PROCESS TO EXPEDITE PAYMENT.&nbsp;HERE IS WHAT IS NEEDED TO APPROVE THE WO:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>- All Deliverables provided and approved while onsite upon Check Out</strong></p>\n<p><strong>- Completed WO (Tasks, Closing Notes, Expenses submitted, Check In/Out, etc)</strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>IMPORTANT: ALL DELIVERABLES MUST BE UPLOADED TO FIELD NATION FROM SITE PRIOR TO CHECK OUT CALL/LEAVING SITE</u></strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Tech Skill Set:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Windows (must be able to assign laptop a Static IP address, and utilize tools like Angry IP Scanner)</li>\n<li>LV Cabling</li>\n<li>Networking</li>\n<li>CCTV / Surveillance</li>\n<li>Attention to Detail</li>\n<li>Communication</li>\n<li>Problem Solving</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Required Equipment:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Laptop with functioning ethernet port and Anydesk capability. Windows 10 or higher is recommended.</strong></li>\n<li>Laptop charger</li>\n<li>Wireless hotspot (needed in case of internet troubleshooting)</li>\n<li>Crimpers (IP and/or analog depending on the camera type(s))</li>\n<li>Network patch cables</li>\n<li>Smartphone + charger</li>\n<li>Cable testers</li>\n<li>Punch-down tool</li>\n<li>Ladder</li>\n<li>Basic Toolkit</li>\n<li>Allen wrenches (Metric and Standard)</li>\n<li>Assortment of Phillips and Flat Screwdrivers</li>\n<li>Core Drill (if there are any exterior cameras)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Required Materials</strong></p>\n<p><strong>**Material consumed will be reimbursed per the WO policies and procedures**</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Cat5e CMX Outdoor Direct Burial, Solid Copper, UTP<strong>(approx. ~200 - ~300ft per cable run)</strong></li>\n<li>NEMA 4/4X outdoor enclosure (14w x 14h x 6d) <strong>(QTY 3)</strong></li>\n<li>Parts for cabling (ex: RJ45 connectors, CAT5e cable, etc.)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Cable Run Requirements</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Cabling is not to be run on top of buildings, gutters, roofs, etc, without prior authorization from Worldlink. Cabling is only to be run horizontally along the roof line.</li>\n<li>All cabling terminating to a wall mounted device (switch, camera, wireless bridge) is to end with at least a 6 inch drip loop to prevent water damage.</li>\n<li>Cabling is to be&nbsp;bundled tightly together to ensure a consistent clean appearance.</li>\n<li><strong>If after confirming with Worldlink it is determined that running cable along the roof is required</strong>, all wireless must be installed on the roof itself with a vertical pole, and not wall mounted</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>** REVIEW THE SCOPE OF WORK AND ATTACHED SITE MAP IN ITS ENTIRETY BEFORE REQUESTING **</u></strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Remove 15 existing Analog cameras (14 are non-functional), run 15 new CAT5 cables to the existing camera locations</li>\n<li>Install 15 new IP cameras.</li>\n<li>No existing cameras will be integrated into Solink.</li>\n<li>Existing Equipment: DVR: Invid tech [PD2B-16NH: 16Ch + 8 Bonus IP Ch Universal Port Recorder] [Serial: E48855615]; Camera-Quantity - 15 Polestar - Camera Count: 1 [Analog] Crest - Camera Count: 11 [Analog] Pelco - Camera Count: 3 [Analog]</li>\n<li>Install wireless P2P x 3</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Refer</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Review the attached Site Map</strong></li>\n<li>Call the Worldlink Service Desk to check in: (210) 756-8651</li>\n<li>Meet with the manager on site and receive the equipment shipped to the site</li>\n<li>Inventory the equipment and ensure everything was received</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Solink QNAP</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">UPS</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">(1) x 16 Port PoE Switch</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">(3) x TP-Link EAP211/215 KIT</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">(3) x 8 Port PoE Switch</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">(15) x TURRET4W-2.8 (Illumivue Turret IP Camera) + junction box mount</li>\n<li>Install (3) NEMA enclosure &amp; (3) X 8-Port PoE Switch at the location marked Switch X</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Ensure there is power available for the switch. Location can be adjusted if necessary</li>\n<li>Install (3) TP-Link wireless bridge</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Refer to the site map for the location of each bridge</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-2\">The MAIN unit should be directly connected to a network source</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-2\">The CLIENT unit is the unit receiving the connection</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Ensure both units are connected to PoE power and have line of site</li>\n<li>Run (15) new CAT5e cables to Locations as shown in map</li>\n<li>Install (15) new IP cameras</li>\n<li>Install the Solink provided&nbsp;QNAP NAS, 1X 16-Port PoE switch, and UPS</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Install the provided hardware next to the existing NVR/DVR</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Check in using the Solink Install Tool:<del>********************************</del></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>Your Work Order ID is:</strong>DEP-56830</li>\n<li>Assist Solink in configuration/setup, and validate full functionality of the system</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">This includes integration of the remaining<strong>existing</strong> analog cameras into the Solink platform, as well as integration of the newly installed IP cameras</li>\n<li>Provide additional troubleshooting/\"smarthands\" assistance as needed</li>\n<li><strong>While the Solink agent is validating the install, Solink stickers included in QNAP box must be given to the store owner/manager.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Once the Solink Deployment Support Technician validates completion of installation, the technician is released.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Required Photos/Deliverables (must be uploaded and verified by Worldlink Coordinator prior to leaving site)</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>You will be asked to upload deliverables to the Solink Installation Tool. Please ensure you do so AND ALSO upload to FieldNation</strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">We understand this is a tedious process and are working to identify improvements</li>\n<li>DVR/NVR and network equipment&nbsp;<strong>(prior to install)</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Entire network cabinet / cage (prior to install)</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Newly installed/replaced cameras</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Cable test results for any new cable runs</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Newly installed QNAP</strong></li>\n<li><strong>DVR/NVR and network equipment (post install)</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Entire network cabinet / cage (post install)</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Monitor showing camera views</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Check In/Out &amp; Escalation Process:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Contact Worldlink Coordinator with the following information when arriving on site as well as prior to leaving (once all deliverables are uploaded)</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Site Name</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Technician Name</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Work Order #</li>\n<li>If any issues come up on site (missing equipment, access issues, site not ready, etc..). Please contact Worldlink Coordinator immediately</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Worldlink Contact:&nbsp;</strong>(210) 756-8651</p>\n<p><strong>﻿Help Desk Contact (if applicable):&nbsp;</strong></p>","markdown":"**WE ARE WORKING TO IMPROVE THE APPROVAL PROCESS TO EXPEDITE PAYMENT. HERE IS WHAT IS NEEDED TO APPROVE THE WO:**\n\n**- All Deliverables provided and approved while onsite upon Check Out**\n\n**- Completed WO (Tasks, Closing Notes, Expenses submitted, Check In/Out, etc)**\n\n**IMPORTANT: ALL DELIVERABLES MUST BE UPLOADED TO FIELD NATION FROM SITE PRIOR TO CHECK OUT CALL/LEAVING SITE**\n\n**Tech Skill Set:**\n\n- Windows (must be able to assign laptop a Static IP address, and utilize tools like Angry IP Scanner)\n- LV Cabling\n- Networking\n- CCTV / Surveillance\n- Attention to Detail\n- Communication\n- Problem Solving\n\n**Required Equipment:**\n\n- **Laptop with functioning ethernet port and Anydesk capability. Windows 10 or higher is recommended.**\n- Laptop charger\n- Wireless hotspot (needed in case of internet troubleshooting)\n- Crimpers (IP and/or analog depending on the camera type(s))\n- Network patch cables\n- Smartphone + charger\n- Cable testers\n- Punch-down tool\n- Ladder\n- Basic Toolkit\n- Allen wrenches (Metric and Standard)\n- Assortment of Phillips and Flat Screwdrivers\n- Core Drill (if there are any exterior cameras)\n\n**Required Materials**\n\n**\\*\\*Material consumed will be reimbursed per the WO policies and procedures\\*\\***\n\n- Cat5e CMX Outdoor Direct Burial, Solid Copper, UTP**(approx. ~200 - ~300ft per cable run)**\n- NEMA 4/4X outdoor enclosure (14w x 14h x 6d) **(QTY 3)**\n- Parts for cabling (ex: RJ45 connectors, CAT5e cable, etc.)\n\n**Cable Run Requirements**\n\n- Cabling is not to be run on top of buildings, gutters, roofs, etc, without prior authorization from Worldlink. Cabling is only to be run horizontally along the roof line.\n- All cabling terminating to a wall mounted device (switch, camera, wireless bridge) is to end with at least a 6 inch drip loop to prevent water damage.\n- Cabling is to be bundled tightly together to ensure a consistent clean appearance.\n- **If after confirming with Worldlink it is determined that running cable along the roof is required**, all wireless must be installed on the roof itself with a vertical pole, and not wall mounted\n\n**\\*\\* REVIEW THE SCOPE OF WORK AND ATTACHED SITE MAP IN ITS ENTIRETY BEFORE REQUESTING \\*\\***\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n- Remove 15 existing Analog cameras (14 are non-functional), run 15 new CAT5 cables to the existing camera locations\n- Install 15 new IP cameras.\n- No existing cameras will be integrated into Solink.\n- Existing Equipment: DVR: Invid tech \\[PD2B-16NH: 16Ch + 8 Bonus IP Ch Universal Port Recorder\\] \\[Serial: E48855615\\]; Camera-Quantity - 15 Polestar - Camera Count: 1 \\[Analog\\] Crest - Camera Count: 11 \\[Analog\\] Pelco - Camera Count: 3 \\[Analog\\]\n- Install wireless P2P x 3\n\nRefer\n\n- **Review the attached Site Map**\n- Call the Worldlink Service Desk to check in: (210) 756-8651\n- Meet with the manager on site and receive the equipment shipped to the site\n- Inventory the equipment and ensure everything was received\n- Solink QNAP\n- UPS\n- (1) x 16 Port PoE Switch\n- (3) x TP-Link EAP211/215 KIT\n- (3) x 8 Port PoE Switch\n- (15) x TURRET4W-2.8 (Illumivue Turret IP Camera) + junction box mount\n- Install (3) NEMA enclosure & (3) X 8-Port PoE Switch at the location marked Switch X\n- Ensure there is power available for the switch. Location can be adjusted if necessary\n- Install (3) TP-Link wireless bridge\n- Refer to the site map for the location of each bridge\n- The MAIN unit should be directly connected to a network source\n- The CLIENT unit is the unit receiving the connection\n- Ensure both units are connected to PoE power and have line of site\n- Run (15) new CAT5e cables to Locations as shown in map\n- Install (15) new IP cameras\n- Install the Solink provided QNAP NAS, 1X 16-Port PoE switch, and UPS\n- Install the provided hardware next to the existing NVR/DVR\n- Check in using the Solink Install Tool:\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- **Your Work Order ID is:**DEP-56830\n- Assist Solink in configuration/setup, and validate full functionality of the system\n- This includes integration of the remaining**existing** analog cameras into the Solink platform, as well as integration of the newly installed IP cameras\n- Provide additional troubleshooting/\"smarthands\" assistance as needed\n- **While the Solink agent is validating the install, Solink stickers included in QNAP box must be given to the store owner/manager.**\n- **Once the Solink Deployment Support Technician validates completion of installation, the technician is released.**\n\n**Required Photos/Deliverables (must be uploaded and verified by Worldlink Coordinator prior to leaving site)**\n\n- **You will be asked to upload deliverables to the Solink Installation Tool. Please ensure you do so AND ALSO upload to FieldNation**\n- We understand this is a tedious process and are working to identify improvements\n- DVR/NVR and network equipment **(prior to install)**\n- **Entire network cabinet / cage (prior to install)**\n- **Newly installed/replaced cameras**\n- **Cable test results for any new cable runs**\n- **Newly installed QNAP**\n- **DVR/NVR and network equipment (post install)**\n- **Entire network cabinet / cage (post install)**\n- **Monitor showing camera views**\n\n**Check In/Out & Escalation Process:**\n\n- Contact Worldlink Coordinator with the following information when arriving on site as well as prior to leaving (once all deliverables are uploaded)\n- Site Name\n- Technician Name\n- Work Order #\n- If any issues come up on site (missing equipment, access issues, site not ready, etc..). Please contact Worldlink Coordinator immediately\n\n**Worldlink Contact:** (210) 756-8651\n\n**﻿Help Desk Contact (if applicable):**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-04T09:30","end":"2026-09-04T33:30"},"payRange":{"min":1740,"max":1740},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":24,"distance":63},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 9/4/2026, 9:30:00 AM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-04T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-05T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-09T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-09T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-07T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-08T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Labor Day"},{"start":"2026-09-08T12:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-08T18:30:00.000Z","summary":"Epik"},{"start":"2026-09-08T18:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-09T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"Miniso day 1"},{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789410215562}
{"job":{"id":19949276,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Computech Technology Services","title":"Need A Technician Onsite to Move Data Cable from One Side of the Office to the Other w/Support - See Description","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Upon arrival and at departure, TECH MUST&nbsp;*<u>CALL <del>***** ********</del>* OR TEXT *<del>***** ********</del>*</u>&nbsp;TO CHECK IN AND OUT with Computech Technology Services dispatch. Check in/out is required for payment. Thank you.</strong></p><p>We need a technician to visit our clients site to move a data cable and jack over to the users desk from the opposite wall. Tech will need to supply a blank plate for the old junction box, and a mudring, jack and faceplate for the new location.</p><p><strong>LCON: <del>***** *****</del></strong></p><p><strong>Tech will work with the customers remote network admin <del>***** ******* ** ***** **************** ***** ********</del></strong></p><p>Materials used will be reimbursed at closing according to the pricing matrix below.</p><p><strong>Tech MUST have standard cabling tools:</strong></p><ul><li>Punch Tool</li><li>Cable Tester</li><li>Toner</li><li>Buttset</li><li>Push/Pull Rods</li><li>Fish Tape</li><li>Ladder(s)</li><li>Laptop (if configuration and/or testing needs to be performed)</li></ul><p><strong>Tech MUST be able to provide (and will be reimbursed for):</strong></p><ul><li>​Cat5e/Cat6 Cable</li><li>Cat5e/Cat6 Jacks</li><li>External Keystone Biscuits</li><li>Keystone Faceplates</li><li>Mudrings</li><li>Misc Patch Cable(s)</li></ul><p><strong>Deliverables:</strong></p><ul><li>Pictures of all equipment worked on, cable runs, etc as appropriate.</li><li>Print the FN work order, have it signed by onsite MOD and upload to work order.​ Digital signature using FN app is also acceptable.</li><li>Detailed description of what was done at the site including the final results.</li><li>ALL new cable runs must be tested and tech to provide proof of test results by either 1) A picture of the cable tester screen with positive result, or 2) Printable cert.</li></ul><p><strong>Material Compensation:</strong></p><p>PLEASE ITEMIZE ALL MATERIALS BASED ON LENGTH/QUANTITY FOR BILLING:</p><p>Item - Pre-Approved Pricing</p><p>Cat5e Riser - $0.18ft</p><p>Cat5e Plenum - $0.22ft</p><p>Cat6 Riser - $0.25ft</p><p>Cat6 Plenum - $0.28ft</p><p>RG59/RG6 - $0.12ft&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Siamese RG59 - $0.15ft</p><p>Cat5e Jack - $3.00ea</p><p>Cat6 Jack&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;- $3.75ea</p><p>Faceplate - $1.30ea</p><p>Surface Mount Box - $1.50ea</p><p>Patch Cable up to 10’ - $3.00ea</p><p>BNC Connectors - $3.00ea</p><p>Modular Plug - $0.55ea</p><p>Power Strip - $6.00ea</p><p>4’x4’ Plywood - $25.00ea</p><p>2'x2' Plywood - $16.00ea</p><p>Cable Tie Wraps - $0.10ea</p><p>Patch Panel - Negotiable/at cost</p><p>Telco 66block - Negotiable/at cost</p><p><br></p><p>Tech MUST be clean in appearance and professional at all times. Dress is business casual. Jeans, polo shirt are ok, but NO t-shirts, shorts, flip flops, etc.</p><p>At ALL times represent yourself as a technician with Computech Technology Services while onsite or in communication with the client site or their help desk. Thank you.</p>","markdown":"**Upon arrival and at departure, TECH MUST \\*CALL \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* OR TEXT \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* TO CHECK IN AND OUT with Computech Technology Services dispatch. Check in/out is required for payment. Thank you.**\n\nWe need a technician to visit our clients site to move a data cable and jack over to the users desk from the opposite wall. Tech will need to supply a blank plate for the old junction box, and a mudring, jack and faceplate for the new location.\n\n**LCON: \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**Tech will work with the customers remote network admin \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\nMaterials used will be reimbursed at closing according to the pricing matrix below.\n\n**Tech MUST have standard cabling tools:**\n\n- Punch Tool\n- Cable Tester\n- Toner\n- Buttset\n- Push/Pull Rods\n- Fish Tape\n- Ladder(s)\n- Laptop (if configuration and/or testing needs to be performed)\n\n**Tech MUST be able to provide (and will be reimbursed for):**\n\n- ​Cat5e/Cat6 Cable\n- Cat5e/Cat6 Jacks\n- External Keystone Biscuits\n- Keystone Faceplates\n- Mudrings\n- Misc Patch Cable(s)\n\n**Deliverables:**\n\n- Pictures of all equipment worked on, cable runs, etc as appropriate.\n- Print the FN work order, have it signed by onsite MOD and upload to work order.​ Digital signature using FN app is also acceptable.\n- Detailed description of what was done at the site including the final results.\n- ALL new cable runs must be tested and tech to provide proof of test results by either 1) A picture of the cable tester screen with positive result, or 2) Printable cert.\n\n**Material Compensation:**\n\nPLEASE ITEMIZE ALL MATERIALS BASED ON LENGTH/QUANTITY FOR BILLING:\n\nItem - Pre-Approved Pricing\n\nCat5e Riser - $0.18ft\n\nCat5e Plenum - $0.22ft\n\nCat6 Riser - $0.25ft\n\nCat6 Plenum - $0.28ft\n\nRG59/RG6 - $0.12ft\n\nSiamese RG59 - $0.15ft\n\nCat5e Jack - $3.00ea\n\nCat6 Jack - $3.75ea\n\nFaceplate - $1.30ea\n\nSurface Mount Box - $1.50ea\n\nPatch Cable up to 10’ - $3.00ea\n\nBNC Connectors - $3.00ea\n\nModular Plug - $0.55ea\n\nPower Strip - $6.00ea\n\n4’x4’ Plywood - $25.00ea\n\n2'x2' Plywood - $16.00ea\n\nCable Tie Wraps - $0.10ea\n\nPatch Panel - Negotiable/at cost\n\nTelco 66block - Negotiable/at cost\n\nTech MUST be clean in appearance and professional at all times. Dress is business casual. Jeans, polo shirt are ok, but NO t-shirts, shorts, flip flops, etc.\n\nAt ALL times represent yourself as a technician with Computech Technology Services while onsite or in communication with the client site or their help desk. Thank you.","actions":[]},