{"job":{"id":"3348981208","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"Move | Priority 2 | 09/15/2026 | Hard Start","description":"*** Non-standard tools requested:  Required Equipment:<br><br>Certified network cable tester and toner<br>Replacement Cat6 patch cables<br>(200ft) Cat6 cable and keystone jacks <br>Termination and punch-down tools<br>Labeling equipment<br>Appropriate ladder or access equipment ***<br><br>Service technician needed on site to move Cabling from current location Locate the camera on site that is not on. to new location See notes.<br><br>The technician should test with the following technical contacts: <br>• Testing contact #1: Robyn Fleming who can be reached via phone at (646) 513-2484 or email at robynfleming@veg.com.<br>• Testing contact #2: Diego Higuera who can be reached via phone at (646) 513-2484 or email at diegohiguera@veg.com.<br><br>Priority 1 – Cameras 1 and 17 Offline / Location and Cabling Investigation – VEG Cary<br><br>VEG Cary currently has two indoor Meraki MV12 cameras offline. Granite needs to dispatch a qualified technician to locate both cameras, identify their correct network connections, and restore service.<br><br>Site Information:<br><br>Site: VEG Cary Hospital<br>Address: 2030 Kildaire Farm Road, Cary, NC 27518<br>Affected Devices: Cameras 1 and 17<br>Camera Model: Meraki MV12<br>Impact: Loss of video coverage inside the hospital<br>Priority: P1 – Critical Service Impact<br><br>Known Camera Information:<br><br>Camera 1: Believed to be connected to Switch 1, Port 9 (SW01 P09). This connection must be verified.<br>Camera 17: Physical location and switch-port assignment are unknown. Camera 17 is an indoor Meraki MV12.<br><br>Required Scope of Work:<br><br>Contact the VEG Networking Team upon arrival and before making any changes.<br>Locate Camera 1 inside the hospital and verify whether it is connected to Switch 1, Port 9.<br>Locate Camera 17 by inspecting the indoor Meraki MV12 cameras throughout the hospital.<br>Do not assume that an unlabeled MV12 is Camera 17. Record the serial number, MAC address, physical location, and photographs of each possible camera and confirm its identity with the VEG Networking Team.<br>Begin cable tracing from each positively identified camera—not from an assumed switch port.<br>Tone each camera cable back to the patch panel and switch.<br>Document the correct patch-panel position and switch port for each camera.<br>Check the assigned switch ports for link status, PoE delivery, port errors, port security, and cable-test results.<br>Inspect and test the patch cables, patch-panel connections, keystones, terminations, camera-side connections, and complete cable runs.<br>Test all cable pairs using a certified network cable tester.<br>Replace defective patch cables and keystones and re-terminate connections as required.<br>If a camera cable cannot pass certification, repair or replace the complete Cat6 cable run.<br>Label each camera, cable, patch-panel position, and switch port.<br>Confirm stable PoE, network connectivity, recording, and live video for both cameras.<br>Provide cable-test results, photographs, materials used, updated port mapping, and detailed findings.<br>Contact the VEG Networking Team before leaving for final validation.<br><br>Important: Do not ask hospital employees to locate, reboot, disconnect, reconnect, trace, or otherwise handle the cameras or networking equipment. Hospital staff are actively caring for patients, and having untrained employees manipulate the equipment could cause additional disruptions or damage.<br><br>Do not close this ticket until Cameras 1 and 17 are positively identified, correctly mapped, online, stable, recording, and viewable by the VEG Networking Team.<br><br>Please provide the dispatch status, technician information, and ETA as soon as possible.","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-15T10:00","end":"2026-09-15T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":260},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":9.3},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":65,"baseAmount":260,"estHours":4,"travelExpense":0,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T18:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":60,"mode":"hours","reason":"arrival_window"}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-15T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-17T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1789410761047}
{"job":{"id":"6903766092","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey","description":"DESCRIPTION: \"Please check in and out with Property Manager<br>If the survey runs over 2 hours you need to get permission from the Property Manager to continue and please let them know about how much longer would be needed<br>Please survey for all fire alarms, burg alarms, elevators, pool phones(voice), fax<br>If there are different building on the property there are probably fire alarms in each one<br>Please work with Property Manager to make sure we get the correct information<br>If you have any issues please reach out to Hilal 9194246791 or 919-870-5080<br>Survey SOW: SOS must match dates and times that are in WorkMarket and MUST BE SIGNED BY THE CUSTOMER (LCON)<br>1. TECH MUST CALL LCON, 30 MINUTES BEFORE ARRIVAL.<br>2. Check in and out through Work Market. For any questions during the survey, please call the EPIK Technical Coordination (TC) Team at: 833-479-4768<br>3. Upon arrival, departure, and for questions about your scope of work or if you are unclear on instructions before starting the installation, check in with the EPIK Technical Coordination (TC) Team at 833-479-4768, otherwise Login to EPIK Wizard at https://wizard.epik.io to begin the Survey process. When you enter the Granite ticket number it will be recognized as a survey, and you will be taken to the Survey Wizard.  (Note: If you have completed a Wizard survey or install before, please be sure to refresh your browser window to ensure the current version is being used.)<br>4. Follow all instructions presented by the Survey Wizard.  If you run into any issues or have questions you may call the TC Team.  All sections of the survey are required and will require final sign off by Granite Technical Coordinator before you will be cleared to leave the site.  The Survey Wizard will guide you through this process.<br>5. Before departure call the EPIK Technical Coordination (TC) Team at 833-479- 4768 to review deliverables and receive approval on survey results.<br>6. Once your survey results have been approved by the TC Team, a TC Team representative will give you a checkout code to enter into WorkMarket which you will use to check out upon completion of the survey. Failure to checkout will result in delay or nonpayment for services. <br> <br>Materials/Tools Required: Laptop with ability to create hotspot, Smart Phone, Tone Generator and Wand, Punch Tool (66 &amp; 110) Electrician Scissors, Step Ladder, Flashlight and/or Headlamp, RJ11&amp;RJ45 Crimper, Ethernet Cable Tester, Masonry Bits, Impact Drill, Pencil and/or Marker, Level, Philips Driver Bits and Screwdriver Cordless Drill, Needle-Nose Pliers, Label-Maker, All-Purpose Screws (drywall, masonry, wood), Cable-Ties and Mountings, Cat3 or Better Cable (for analog devices), Cat6 Ethernet Cable (for data connections), CrossConnect Wire, Gel-Crimp Connecters, Label-Tape, RJ11 &amp; Cat6 Ethernet Keystone Jacks, RJ11 &amp; RJ45 Modular Plugs, Lineman’s Telephony Handset/Butt-Set, Infrared Temperature Gun\"","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-15T13:00","end":"2026-10-15T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":195},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":20.9},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":65,"baseAmount":195,"estHours":3,"travelExpense":40,"payStructure":null},"reason":"TRAVEL_REQUIRED","rejectDetails":"Travel required (20.9mi reported + 10mi padding = 30.9mi > 20mi)"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-15T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-16T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-16T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-19T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1789411282586}
{"job":{"id":19950222,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Loopdrive LLC","title":"Smart Home - Install & Pair Devices","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>FURNACE/HVAC Breakers MUST Be Turned Off When Removing/Wiring Thermostat</u>: </strong>Even though it's low voltage, replacing a thermostat without turning off the breaker can blow the fuse or transformer on the HVAC system. If this happens, the order will be closed without payment.&nbsp;ALWAYS TAKE PHOTOS OF ORIGINAL WIRING AND GO OFF THAT FOR NEW THERMOSTAT. WIRING MAY DIFFER FROM NEW WIRING DIAGRAM. CONTACT SITE MANAGER FOR ANY QUESTIONS.</p><p><br></p><p>------------------------------</p><p><strong><u>Summary:</u></strong><u>&nbsp;</u></p><p>Follow the instructions below to replace a smart home door lock &amp; thermostat, contact support line for pairing/configuration. Do not attempt pairing on your own. Plug in control hub near router and let boot while doing the install. Install The keypad, thermostat, and 3 sensors. Sensors are a door sensor, kitchen sink leak sensor, and water heater sensor. Sensors are installed with a couple of screws or double sided tape. Pull the plastic tab to activate battery and these are ready for pairing. This should only take 5-10 minutes for the sensors. DO NOT DISCUSS OR DEMAND PAY CHANGE WITH SUPPORT TEAM.</p><p>------------------------------</p><p><strong><u>Smart Home Job Requirements &amp; Guidelines</u></strong></p><p><strong>﻿</strong><em>By accepting this order, you agree to follow all outlined requirements and guidelines.&nbsp;</em><strong><em>Failure to comply may result in the order being closed without compensation.</em></strong></p><ul><li><strong>Help Line Availability</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">The Smart Home Help Line is available&nbsp;<strong>only between 9:00 AM and 5:00 PM EST</strong>.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If you arrive onsite too late for them to complete pairing on their end, the visit will need to be&nbsp;<strong>rescheduled—without additional compensation.</strong></li><li><strong>Professional Conduct</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Treat the Resident &amp; Smart Home Help Line staff with respect—they are a small team handling a high volume of repairs and are also our client.&nbsp;<strong>Disrespectful behavior may result in removal from the site without pay.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Orders are not considered complete until the Smart Home team has confirmed that all functional devices are properly paired and online.<strong>Completion Requirement</strong></li><li><strong>Help Line Availability</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If you can’t reach support right away, keep trying for at least 15 minutes. If there’s still no answer, contact the site manager for next steps.</li><li><strong>Scope Changes &amp; Compensation</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If the scope changes during the visit (e.g., another device is accidentally knocked offline),&nbsp;<strong>we may approve additional pay</strong>.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">To qualify, you must provide the following:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Photos of any&nbsp;<strong>additional devices</strong>&nbsp;serviced</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>Timestamped arrival and departure</strong>&nbsp;photos</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">A clear&nbsp;<strong>written closing statement</strong>&nbsp;detailing the added work</li><li><strong>Unable to Complete – Eligible Trip Fee Scenarios</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">You may request a&nbsp;<strong>$35 trip fee</strong>, but&nbsp;<strong>full payment will not be approved</strong>&nbsp;since the order was not completed.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>Resident no-show or refusal of access</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>Unrestrained dogs present</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>Inhospitable or unsafe environment</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>Power outage</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>Missing or incorrect parts</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Before leaving the site</strong>, you must:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>Call the site manager</strong>&nbsp;so we can attempt to resolve the issue.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Provide a&nbsp;<strong>timestamped photo of the front of the home</strong>, and if applicable, document the issue with additional photos or notes.</li><li><strong>Late Arrival Fee</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Arrival times are coordinated with the Smart Home team. If you arrive late, a&nbsp;<strong>$10 fee will be deducted</strong>&nbsp;from your pay. Please plan accordingly and arrive on time.</li><li><strong>Authorized Personnel</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Only the technician assigned to the work order is allowed on site. Do not bring children, friends, coworkers, employees, or assistants.</li></ul><p>------------------------------</p><p><strong><u>Instructions:</u></strong></p><ol><li>For this repair&nbsp;<strong>please identify yourself as a contractor working for Diamond Property Services,&nbsp;</strong>rather than Field Nation or your own company.</li><li><strong>Confirm Start Time in FN.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If you cannot keep your appointment, contact the site manager at 865-776-2593 immediately.</li><li><strong>Upon arrival</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Take a&nbsp;<strong>time-stamped</strong>&nbsp;<strong>photo</strong>&nbsp;of the home.&nbsp;<u>This is required to receive any additional allowances.</u></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Introduce yourself to the tenant and let them know you are there on behalf of&nbsp;<strong>Diamond Property Services</strong>&nbsp;to perform a smart home repair.</li><li><strong>Replace Device(s):</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>(1) Yale Pro 2 Smart Lock</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Likely removing this lock:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-3\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ciHoxeXDJjE</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Likely installing this lock:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-3\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e1Z0J-ZwmQc</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>EcoLink Thermostat</strong></li><li><strong>Prepare Doorlock for Pairing</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>If batteries are Horizontal (left to right), follow these steps:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Press and hold black button on back of unit</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">While holding the black button, press the gear button on the front (Gear &amp; 1 key should light up)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Release black button on back of unit.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Press these buttons: 1, gear, 1,8,6,5 (1865 is now the master code)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">The unit should light up and lock. The unit is now ready for pairing.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>If batteries are Vertical (up &amp; down)</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Press gear, 1, gear, 1,8,6,5</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">1865 is now the master code</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><u>If you cannot get the door lock into pairing mode, call the site manager before calling support.</u></li><li><strong>Do not attempt to pair these devices on your own.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Pairing must be done through the property manager's smart home app.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><u>Call the Support Hotline at&nbsp;</u><strong><u>330-970-2020</u></strong>. Identify yourself as calling on behalf of&nbsp;<strong>Diamond Property Services</strong>, and have the property address ready.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If the hotline is busy, keep trying for 10 minutes.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If you are unable to reach the Support Hotline, contact the site manager at 865-776-2593 and explain the issue.</li><li><strong>Once you're cleared by the support hotline</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Gather all required documentation listed below.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Upload everything to Field Nation to complete the work order.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>Required Deliverables:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Time stamped arrival</strong>&nbsp;<strong>photo</strong>&nbsp;of the front of residence showing the address.</li><li>Photos of all devices you installed/paired</li><li>Screenshot of your call log with support.</li><li>Photo of the tenants app showing the device(s) paired</li><li><strong>Time stamped departure</strong>&nbsp;<strong>photo</strong>&nbsp;of the front of residence showing the address.</li><li>A resolution statement:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Arrival time:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">What you did:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Who you speak with:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">What happened:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">What they said:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Departure time:</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Estimated Time:&nbsp;</strong>Less than 1 hour.</p>","markdown":"**FURNACE/HVAC Breakers MUST Be Turned Off When Removing/Wiring Thermostat:** Even though it's low voltage, replacing a thermostat without turning off the breaker can blow the fuse or transformer on the HVAC system. If this happens, the order will be closed without payment. ALWAYS TAKE PHOTOS OF ORIGINAL WIRING AND GO OFF THAT FOR NEW THERMOSTAT. WIRING MAY DIFFER FROM NEW WIRING DIAGRAM. CONTACT SITE MANAGER FOR ANY QUESTIONS.\n\n\\------------------------------\n\n**Summary:**\n\nFollow the instructions below to replace a smart home door lock & thermostat, contact support line for pairing/configuration. Do not attempt pairing on your own. Plug in control hub near router and let boot while doing the install. Install The keypad, thermostat, and 3 sensors. Sensors are a door sensor, kitchen sink leak sensor, and water heater sensor. Sensors are installed with a couple of screws or double sided tape. Pull the plastic tab to activate battery and these are ready for pairing. This should only take 5-10 minutes for the sensors. DO NOT DISCUSS OR DEMAND PAY CHANGE WITH SUPPORT TEAM.\n\n\\------------------------------\n\n**Smart Home Job Requirements & Guidelines**\n\n**﻿***By accepting this order, you agree to follow all outlined requirements and guidelines.* ***Failure to comply may result in the order being closed without compensation.***\n\n- **Help Line Availability**\n- The Smart Home Help Line is available **only between 9:00 AM and 5:00 PM EST**.\n- If you arrive onsite too late for them to complete pairing on their end, the visit will need to be **rescheduled—without additional compensation.**\n- **Professional Conduct**\n- Treat the Resident & Smart Home Help Line staff with respect—they are a small team handling a high volume of repairs and are also our client. **Disrespectful behavior may result in removal from the site without pay.**\n- Orders are not considered complete until the Smart Home team has confirmed that all functional devices are properly paired and online.**Completion Requirement**\n- **Help Line Availability**\n- If you can’t reach support right away, keep trying for at least 15 minutes. If there’s still no answer, contact the site manager for next steps.\n- **Scope Changes & Compensation**\n- If the scope changes during the visit (e.g., another device is accidentally knocked offline), **we may approve additional pay**.\n- To qualify, you must provide the following:\n- Photos of any **additional devices** serviced\n- **Timestamped arrival and departure** photos\n- A clear **written closing statement** detailing the added work\n- **Unable to Complete – Eligible Trip Fee Scenarios**\n- You may request a **$35 trip fee**, but **full payment will not be approved** since the order was not completed.\n- **Resident no-show or refusal of access**\n- **Unrestrained dogs present**\n- **Inhospitable or unsafe environment**\n- **Power outage**\n- **Missing or incorrect parts**\n- **Before leaving the site**, you must:\n- **Call the site manager** so we can attempt to resolve the issue.\n- Provide a **timestamped photo of the front of the home**, and if applicable, document the issue with additional photos or notes.\n- **Late Arrival Fee**\n- Arrival times are coordinated with the Smart Home team. If you arrive late, a **$10 fee will be deducted** from your pay. Please plan accordingly and arrive on time.\n- **Authorized Personnel**\n- Only the technician assigned to the work order is allowed on site. Do not bring children, friends, coworkers, employees, or assistants.\n\n\\------------------------------\n\n**Instructions:**\n\n1. For this repair **please identify yourself as a contractor working for Diamond Property Services,** rather than Field Nation or your own company.\n2. **Confirm Start Time in FN.**\n3. If you cannot keep your appointment, contact the site manager at 865-776-2593 immediately.\n4. **Upon arrival**\n5. Take a **time-stamped** **photo** of the home. This is required to receive any additional allowances.\n6. Introduce yourself to the tenant and let them know you are there on behalf of **Diamond Property Services** to perform a smart home repair.\n7. **Replace Device(s):**\n8. **(1) Yale Pro 2 Smart Lock**\n9. Likely removing this lock:\n10. <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ciHoxeXDJjE>\n11. Likely installing this lock:\n12. <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e1Z0J-ZwmQc>\n13. **EcoLink Thermostat**\n14. **Prepare Doorlock for Pairing**\n15. **If batteries are Horizontal (left to right), follow these steps:**\n16. Press and hold black button on back of unit\n17. While holding the black button, press the gear button on the front (Gear & 1 key should light up)\n18. Release black button on back of unit.\n19. Press these buttons: 1, gear, 1,8,6,5 (1865 is now the master code)\n20. The unit should light up and lock. The unit is now ready for pairing.\n21. **If batteries are Vertical (up & down)**\n22. Press gear, 1, gear, 1,8,6,5\n23. 1865 is now the master code\n24. If you cannot get the door lock into pairing mode, call the site manager before calling support.\n25. **Do not attempt to pair these devices on your own.**\n26. Pairing must be done through the property manager's smart home app.\n27. Call the Support Hotline at **330-970-2020**. Identify yourself as calling on behalf of **Diamond Property Services**, and have the property address ready.\n28. If the hotline is busy, keep trying for 10 minutes.\n29. If you are unable to reach the Support Hotline, contact the site manager at 865-776-2593 and explain the issue.\n30. **Once you're cleared by the support hotline**\n31. Gather all required documentation listed below.\n32. Upload everything to Field Nation to complete the work order.\n\n**Required Deliverables:**\n\n- **Time stamped arrival** **photo** of the front of residence showing the address.\n- Photos of all devices you installed/paired\n- Screenshot of your call log with support.\n- Photo of the tenants app showing the device(s) paired\n- **Time stamped departure** **photo** of the front of residence showing the address.\n- A resolution statement:\n- Arrival time:\n- What you did:\n- Who you speak with:\n- What happened:\n- What they said:\n- Departure time:\n\n**Estimated Time:** Less than 1 hour.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-24T15:00","end":"2026-09-24T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":60},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":34},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $60 is below minimum threshold $350"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-24T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789413301408}
{"job":{"id":19656003,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"ProAct Services","title":"Chipotle UPS installation","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Scope of Work</strong>: Replace existing UPS with a newer model. Install the new bracket and new UPS to the same wall where the old UPS was.</p><p>Tech must be onsite at 7 am. Install will take 2 hours or less to complete, including taking deliverables and testing. Install tech must be the same tech that requested the work order. He must be able to lift a 60lbs weight of UPS. <strong>Please review the attached install document and sample photos prior to accepting the work order.</strong></p><p>Tech should bring the following:</p><ul><li>stud finder for metal and wood</li><li>extension cord for large appliance - black or gray, 15 amp / 14 gauge (see attached sample photo)</li><li>4 pcs stainless steel FENDER washers size 1/4</li><li>4 pcs stainless steel FENDER washers size 3/8</li><li>6' ladder</li><li>toggle bolts that can hold 100 lbs unit (see attached sample photo)</li><li>packing tape (to seal the box for the old UPS)</li><li>power tester</li><li>measuring tape</li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li>Check in and out with ProAct PMO at 614-647-9944.</li><li>Confirm with ProAct coordinator once you have all 3 packages (2 boxes from NXT Power and 1 small box from Asset Enterprises).</li><li>Identify the location of the existing UPS in the back of house area or inside the manager's office. Evaluate the wall material to be sure it can hold the unit. The UPS weighs approximately 60 lbs. If the wall material is not sufficient then look above the ceiling tiles. Often there is wood you can attach to in the area above the ceiling tiles. <strong>MAKE SURE IT WILL BE INSTALLED SECURELY INTO THE WALL STUDS.</strong> Mark which part on the wall has studs.</li><li>Send photos to ProAct coordinator showing where the studs are, toggle bolts and extension cord still on the carton showing the label, existing UPS and bdp panel before you start. <strong>IMPORTANT NOTE: If you will find studs, use the lag bolts that came with the package. If no studs, use the approved toggle bolts and washers. Do not proceed without approval from ProAct</strong></li><li>Install the new bracket and new UPS to the same wall where the old UPS was. Follow the attached installation guide.</li><li>Tech will box up the old UPS and attach the customer provided shipping label. Leave the package to the manager and inform that it will be picked up by Fedex.</li><li>Submit all required photos. Do not leave until you receive a confirmation from ProAct coordinator.</li><li>Discard all trash generated during the installation and be sure work areas are clean.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>Deliverables/Required Photos:</strong></p><ul><li>Front and back of existing UPS</li><li>Broad view of the existing UPS</li><li>Ceiling/wall (thickness of the wall)</li><li>Stud finder on the wall showing where the studs are</li><li>Toggle bolts or extension cord still in carton showing the label</li><li>Bypass switch on bypass mode before removal of old UPS</li><li>Bracket installed</li><li>Photo of internal battery connected</li><li>Close up photos of each lag bolts front and side view</li><li>Broad view of the new UPS installed</li><li>Front and back of new UPS with web card installed</li><li>Serial Number of the new UPS</li><li>Close up photo of 8 small screws at the bottom of the UPS</li><li>Bypass switch on Normal Mode</li><li>Photos showing how you ran the network cable</li><li>Return Label&nbsp;</li><li>Boxed old UPS with shipping label attached</li><li>Sign off sheet/Checklist</li></ul>","markdown":"**Scope of Work**: Replace existing UPS with a newer model. Install the new bracket and new UPS to the same wall where the old UPS was.\n\nTech must be onsite at 7 am. Install will take 2 hours or less to complete, including taking deliverables and testing. Install tech must be the same tech that requested the work order. He must be able to lift a 60lbs weight of UPS. **Please review the attached install document and sample photos prior to accepting the work order.**\n\nTech should bring the following:\n\n- stud finder for metal and wood\n- extension cord for large appliance - black or gray, 15 amp / 14 gauge (see attached sample photo)\n- 4 pcs stainless steel FENDER washers size 1/4\n- 4 pcs stainless steel FENDER washers size 3/8\n- 6' ladder\n- toggle bolts that can hold 100 lbs unit (see attached sample photo)\n- packing tape (to seal the box for the old UPS)\n- power tester\n- measuring tape\n\n1. Check in and out with ProAct PMO at 614-647-9944.\n2. Confirm with ProAct coordinator once you have all 3 packages (2 boxes from NXT Power and 1 small box from Asset Enterprises).\n3. Identify the location of the existing UPS in the back of house area or inside the manager's office. Evaluate the wall material to be sure it can hold the unit. The UPS weighs approximately 60 lbs. If the wall material is not sufficient then look above the ceiling tiles. Often there is wood you can attach to in the area above the ceiling tiles. **MAKE SURE IT WILL BE INSTALLED SECURELY INTO THE WALL STUDS.** Mark which part on the wall has studs.\n4. Send photos to ProAct coordinator showing where the studs are, toggle bolts and extension cord still on the carton showing the label, existing UPS and bdp panel before you start. **IMPORTANT NOTE: If you will find studs, use the lag bolts that came with the package. If no studs, use the approved toggle bolts and washers. Do not proceed without approval from ProAct**\n5. Install the new bracket and new UPS to the same wall where the old UPS was. Follow the attached installation guide.\n6. Tech will box up the old UPS and attach the customer provided shipping label. Leave the package to the manager and inform that it will be picked up by Fedex.\n7. Submit all required photos. Do not leave until you receive a confirmation from ProAct coordinator.\n8. Discard all trash generated during the installation and be sure work areas are clean.\n\n**Deliverables/Required Photos:**\n\n- Front and back of existing UPS\n- Broad view of the existing UPS\n- Ceiling/wall (thickness of the wall)\n- Stud finder on the wall showing where the studs are\n- Toggle bolts or extension cord still in carton showing the label\n- Bypass switch on bypass mode before removal of old UPS\n- Bracket installed\n- Photo of internal battery connected\n- Close up photos of each lag bolts front and side view\n- Broad view of the new UPS installed\n- Front and back of new UPS with web card installed\n- Serial Number of the new UPS\n- Close up photo of 8 small screws at the bottom of the UPS\n- Bypass switch on Normal Mode\n- Photos showing how you ran the network cable\n- Return Label\n- Boxed old UPS with shipping label attached\n- Sign off sheet/Checklist","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-01T07:00","end":"2026-10-01T09:00"},"payRange":{"min":130,"max":130},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":20},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $130 is below minimum threshold $350"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789413654657}
{"job":{"id":"3496232042","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard","description":"\"Install antenna<br>pool phone 9192667763<br>if install goes over 3 hours need detailed notes of why it ran over<br>*****************************************************************************<br>Michelle Nolan<br>*****************************************************************************<br><br>SOW - EPIK Cutover &amp; Test<br>*************************************************************************************<br>Before Arrival<br>1.    Call the LCON 30 minutes before arrival.<br>2.    Review the EPIK install video if you are unfamiliar with EPIK:<br>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n7ZkeVrRRCo<br>3.    Arrive with all required tools and materials listed below.<br>On Arrival<br>1.    Check in on WorkMarket.<br>2.    Locate the customer contact and confirm the install location.<br>3.    Review the Special Instructions before starting work.<br>EPIK Install Requirements<br>1.    Mount the Epik device in the approve install location and EPIK 66 block or connect harmonica to RJ 21X on Epik.<br>2.    If EPIK device mounting location is not in a cool, clean, secure area reach out to Activation for an updated location. <br>3.    Power on the EPIK device before starting the Wizard.<br>Do not log into the Wizard until the device is powered on.<br>4.    If applicable connect the EPIK device to the customer network using the information provided in the Special Instructions.<br>5.    Log into the EPIK Install Wizard:<br>https://wizard.epik.io<br>6.    Follow the Wizard steps and complete the installation with the assigned Activations Representative. A member of the Activations team will reach out by text once assigned.<br>DO NOT CALL INTO THE QUEUE FOR WIZARD RELATED ISSUES<br>Checkout Requirement<br>1.    Confirm Activations has released you.<br>2.    Submit all WorkMarket deliverables.<br>3.    Enter the checkout code in WorkMarket.<br>4.    Check out on WorkMarket.<br> <br>The install is not considered valid unless the checkout code is entered in WorkMarket.<br> <br>Required Deliverables<br>Submit all required deliverables in WorkMarket before checkout:<br>1.    Photo of completed EPIK install.<br>2.    Photo of labeled 66 block / harmonica block.<br>3.    List of existing TNs and the new number that replaced each TN, if applicable.<br>4.    Customer signed sign-out sheet.<br>5.    Any additional deliverables listed in Special Instructions.<br> <br> <br>Required Tools<br>•    Laptop<br>•    Smartphone with hotspot<br>•    Tone generator and wand<br>•    66/110 punch tool<br>•    Butt set<br>       Infrared Temperature Gun <br>•    Electrician scissors<br>•    Step ladder<br>•    Flashlight/headlamp<br>•    RJ11/RJ45 crimper<br>•    Ethernet cable tester<br>•    Impact drill / cordless drill<br>•    Masonry bits<br>•    Screwdrivers / driver bits<br>•    Needle-nose pliers<br>•    Label maker and label tape<br>•    Cat3 or better cable<br>•    Cat6 Ethernet cable<br>•    Cross-connect wire<br>•    Gel-crimp connectors<br>•    Cable ties and mounting hardware<br>•    RJ11/RJ45 plugs and keystone jacks<br>•    Console cables: USB to DB9 PL2303 and USB to USB-mini<br>*************************************************************************************","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-21T10:00","end":"2026-09-21T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":195},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":10.5},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":65,"baseAmount":195,"estHours":3,"travelExpense":30,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T15:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":60,"mode":"hours","reason":"arrival_window"}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":