{"job":{"id":19950893,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"POSRG Remarketing Group","title":"Hard Drive Swap","description":{"html":"<p>**PLEASE NOT THIS IS A TIME SENSATIVE INSTALL SINCE IT IS HAPPENING BEFORE STORE OPENS. IF YOU SHOW UP LATE YOU WILL NOT BE ALLOWED TO START AND YOU WILL BE SENT HOME**</p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work</u></strong></p><p>Upon arrival, you will introduce self on behalf of&nbsp;<strong>POSRG</strong>.</p><p>**THE VERY FIRST THING YOU SHOULD DO BEFORE YOU CALL THE GENESCO HD TO CHECK IN IS READ THE ATTACHED INSTRUCTIONS**</p><p>The Genesco help desk will ask you if you have read through the instructions when you call to check in with them, TELL THEM THAT YOU HAVE!</p><p><br></p><p>TECH: Please check in with the Genesco POS Helpdesk at 615-649-0142 once onsite for further instructions. DO NOT START INSTALL WITHOUT READING THE ATTACHED INSTRUCTIONS DOCUMENT AND THEN SPEAKING WITH AN AGENT AFTER.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Basic Overview (Please see attached detailed instructions):</u></strong></p><p>Technician to Remove inoperable HDD from base unit.</p><p>Technician to install New HDD that has been shipped to site.</p><p>Technician will then use USB drive to test configuration script on terminal.</p><p>Technician will work with the help desk personnel to verify the connectivity and functionality of all the equipment after the SOW is complete.</p><p><strong><u>**There is sensitive data on the thumb drive that we will be using for this. The customer is asking us to take 2 pictures after the install. One picture of the thumb drive in the box with SSD that we will be sending back and one picture of the box sealed with return label on it. The site is going to ship everything back but they just want to make sure they have a record of the thumb drive in the box and then it sealed.**</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Parts Instructions</u></strong></p><p>Technician is required to have a <span style=\"color: black;\">Philips #0 (to remove engage one monitor) and Philips #00 (to remove M.2 screw).</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\">**THE #0 &amp; #00 NEED TO BE REGULAR SCREWDRIVERS. A BIT IN THE APEX OF A DRILL WILL BE TOO WIDE TO FIT INTO THE BRACKET TO REMOVE THE SCREWS</strong></p><p>PLEASE NOTE, THIS CUSTOMER DOES NOT ALLOW THE USE OF ZIP TIES FOR ANY REASON! PLEASE USE VELCO STRAPS IF NEEDED.</p><p>Technician will be compensated for all materials used on site.</p><p><strong><u>Required Deliverables to be Paid</u></strong></p><p>1.&nbsp;<strong><em>MUST</em></strong>&nbsp;check in &amp; out with the&nbsp;<strong>POSRG Work Order Manager</strong></p><p>2.&nbsp;<strong><em>MUST</em></strong>&nbsp;leave detailed closing notes explaining what was done on site and any problems you ran into while on site doing the SOW.</p><p>4. Take before &amp; after pictures to confirm work completion.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Work Order Acceptance</u></strong></p><p>Do&nbsp;<strong><em>NOT</em></strong>&nbsp;request the work order if you are&nbsp;<strong><em>NOT</em></strong>&nbsp;qualified to work on POS equipment, network equipment, or network cable runs.</p>","markdown":"\\*\\*PLEASE NOT THIS IS A TIME SENSATIVE INSTALL SINCE IT IS HAPPENING BEFORE STORE OPENS. IF YOU SHOW UP LATE YOU WILL NOT BE ALLOWED TO START AND YOU WILL BE SENT HOME\\*\\*\n\n**Scope of Work**\n\nUpon arrival, you will introduce self on behalf of **POSRG**.\n\n\\*\\*THE VERY FIRST THING YOU SHOULD DO BEFORE YOU CALL THE GENESCO HD TO CHECK IN IS READ THE ATTACHED INSTRUCTIONS\\*\\*\n\nThe Genesco help desk will ask you if you have read through the instructions when you call to check in with them, TELL THEM THAT YOU HAVE!\n\nTECH: Please check in with the Genesco POS Helpdesk at 615-649-0142 once onsite for further instructions. DO NOT START INSTALL WITHOUT READING THE ATTACHED INSTRUCTIONS DOCUMENT AND THEN SPEAKING WITH AN AGENT AFTER.\n\n**Basic Overview (Please see attached detailed instructions):**\n\nTechnician to Remove inoperable HDD from base unit.\n\nTechnician to install New HDD that has been shipped to site.\n\nTechnician will then use USB drive to test configuration script on terminal.\n\nTechnician will work with the help desk personnel to verify the connectivity and functionality of all the equipment after the SOW is complete.\n\n**\\*\\*There is sensitive data on the thumb drive that we will be using for this. The customer is asking us to take 2 pictures after the install. One picture of the thumb drive in the box with SSD that we will be sending back and one picture of the box sealed with return label on it. The site is going to ship everything back but they just want to make sure they have a record of the thumb drive in the box and then it sealed.\\*\\***\n\n**Parts Instructions**\n\nTechnician is required to have a Philips #0 (to remove engage one monitor) and Philips #00 (to remove M.2 screw).\n\n**\\*\\*THE #0 & #00 NEED TO BE REGULAR SCREWDRIVERS. A BIT IN THE APEX OF A DRILL WILL BE TOO WIDE TO FIT INTO THE BRACKET TO REMOVE THE SCREWS**\n\nPLEASE NOTE, THIS CUSTOMER DOES NOT ALLOW THE USE OF ZIP TIES FOR ANY REASON! PLEASE USE VELCO STRAPS IF NEEDED.\n\nTechnician will be compensated for all materials used on site.\n\n**Required Deliverables to be Paid**\n\n1\\. ***MUST*** check in & out with the **POSRG Work Order Manager**\n\n2\\. ***MUST*** leave detailed closing notes explaining what was done on site and any problems you ran into while on site doing the SOW.\n\n4\\. Take before & after pictures to confirm work completion.\n\n**Work Order Acceptance**\n\nDo ***NOT*** request the work order if you are ***NOT*** qualified to work on POS equipment, network equipment, or network cable runs.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-01T08:30","end":"2026-10-01T12:30"},"payRange":{"min":70,"max":280},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":70,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":62},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYME