{"job":{"id":19951816,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Vision Technologies","title":"Swap out router and MG cell back up SiteOne Landscape Supply / Branch 1126 / INC1026753 / SO0004888","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Technician must wear proper safety gear:</strong></p><ul><li>​<strong>High visibility shirt/vest</strong></li><li><strong>Safety boots(non-slip/cover ankle/resist penetration)</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>SCOPE OF WORK:</u></strong></p><p><strong>Must meet with MOD on arrival and if changing out any devices please call into help desk prior to the removal or installation of any device</strong></p><p><strong>Service Request - Remove and replace MX 95 &amp; MG 51. Replace patch cables as well.</strong></p><p><strong>Report to site and meet with manager, get the new devices and locate the network equipment, call into the help desk and work with their support to swap out the MX router and MG cell back, once swapped out verify everything comes back up on the network and is working properly</strong>. </p><p><strong>Call helpdesk (contact info under Confidential Information) prior to leaving site for work complete verification</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Please bring all material necessary to complete.</u></strong></p><p>Cell Phone</p><p>Laptop</p><p>6-8' Ladder</p><p>Network Testing and Installation Tools</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Please check-in and check-out with the Vision Technologies contact Gary Ledwell. If he does not answer, please leave VM or Text.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>You must be on time for the work order. If for some reason you are going to be late you must call the Vision representative&nbsp;&nbsp;an&nbsp;hour before the scheduled time.&nbsp;​</strong></p><p><strong><u>If you do not call within the hour time frame you will receive a pay deduction.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>***Safety Requirements***​</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>High Visibility Shirt\\Vest</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p>A high visibility safety vest or high visibility shirt must be worn at all times when working in areas where mobile equipment and/or vehicles are operated.&nbsp;This includes:</p><ul><li>All warehouses where forklift traffic is present; whether on or off of the forklift.&nbsp;This would include all areas in our drive-through branches</li><li>All nursery yards</li><li>All out door areas at non-nursery locations where equipment may operate and/or where there is traffic flow</li><li>All active worksites with vehicle traffic and/or mobile equipment in use</li><li>At all times when loading, unloading and taking deliveries, including when stopped roadside for DOT inspection, mechanical issues, and refueling</li></ul><p><strong><u>Footwear</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p>Acceptable:</p><ul><li>Be of substantial design and construction</li><li>Have soles that are strong and in good condition to prevent slipping on smooth, wet, or loose surfaces.&nbsp;Tread with random patterns perpendicular to the direction of travel are most slip-resistant​</li><li>Have soles that resist penetration by nails and debris</li><li>cover the ankle-providing additional ankle support and stability.&nbsp;Such footwear is intended to prevent and/or minimize the severity of ankle injuries</li><li>Steel toed shoes are recommended, but not mandatory unless required by government regulation</li></ul><p>Not Acceptable:</p><ul><li>Open toe shoes</li><li>Opened heeled shoes</li><li>Traditional cowboy boots (slick-sole, raised heel)</li><li>Tennis/running shoes</li><li>An footwear with tread that is worn smooth​</li></ul><p><strong>-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;Please check-in and check-out with the Vision Technologies contact. If they do not answer, please leave VM or Text.</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>Deliverables will include the work order form that is attached to this WO. The form must be signed by the tech and the office manager before leaving site.</strong></p><p><strong>Deliverables also include pictures of everything you worked on. The more pictures, the better.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>When returning deliverables please only post to Field Nation.</strong></p>","markdown":"**Technician must wear proper safety gear:**\n\n- ​**High visibility shirt/vest**\n- **Safety boots(non-slip/cover ankle/resist penetration)**\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK:**\n\n**Must meet with MOD on arrival and if changing out any devices please call into help desk prior to the removal or installation of any device**\n\n**Service Request - Remove and replace MX 95 & MG 51. Replace patch cables as well.**\n\n**Report to site and meet with manager, get the new devices and locate the network equipment, call into the help desk and work with their support to swap out the MX router and MG cell back, once swapped out verify everything comes back up on the network and is working properly**.\n\n**Call helpdesk (contact info under Confidential Information) prior to leaving site for work complete verification**\n\n**Please bring all material necessary to complete.**\n\nCell Phone\n\nLaptop\n\n6-8' Ladder\n\nNetwork Testing and Installation Tools\n\n**Please check-in and check-out with the Vision Technologies contact Gary Ledwell. If he does not answer, please leave VM or Text.**\n\n**You must be on time for the work order. If for some reason you are going to be late you must call the Vision representative an hour before the scheduled time. ​**\n\n**If you do not call within the hour time frame you will receive a pay deduction.**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*Safety Requirements\\*\\*\\*​**\n\n**High Visibility Shirt\\\\Vest**\n\nA high visibility safety vest or high visibility shirt must be worn at all times when working in areas where mobile equipment and/or vehicles are operated. This includes:\n\n- All warehouses where forklift traffic is present; whether on or off of the forklift. This would include all areas in our drive-through branches\n- All nursery yards\n- All out door areas at non-nursery locations where equipment may operate and/or where there is traffic flow\n- All active worksites with vehicle traffic and/or mobile equipment in use\n- At all times when loading, unloading and taking deliveries, including when stopped roadside for DOT inspection, mechanical issues, and refueling\n\n**Footwear**\n\nAcceptable:\n\n- Be of substantial design and construction\n- Have soles that are strong and in good condition to prevent slipping on smooth, wet, or loose surfaces. Tread with random patterns perpendicular to the direction of travel are most slip-resistant​\n- Have soles that resist penetration by nails and debris\n- cover the ankle-providing additional ankle support and stability. Such footwear is intended to prevent and/or minimize the severity of ankle injuries\n- Steel toed shoes are recommended, but not mandatory unless required by government regulation\n\nNot Acceptable:\n\n- Open toe shoes\n- Opened heeled shoes\n- Traditional cowboy boots (slick-sole, raised heel)\n- Tennis/running shoes\n- An footwear with tread that is worn smooth​\n\n**-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------**\n\n **Please check-in and check-out with the Vision Technologies contact. If they do not answer, please leave VM or Text.**\n\n**Deliverables will include the work order form that is attached to this WO. The form must be signed by the tech and the office manager before leaving site.**\n\n**Deliverables also include pictures of everything you worked on. The more pictures, the better.**\n\n**When returning deliverables please only post to Field Nation.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-15T12:00","end":"2026-09-15T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":200},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":100},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":8},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"blended","counterRate":60,"baseAmount":240,"estHours":2,"travelExpense":0,"payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":120},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":60}},"counterDate":{"start":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T18:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":60,"mode":"hours","reason":"arrival_window"}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-15T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-17T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-21T14:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T18:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974873-1820 at Centennial-EPIK Survey Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1789418335845}
{"job":{"id":19944994,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Zones LLC","title":"Nike - Request for SmartHands -   NikePOS registers refresh Tech 2","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>High Level Scope:</u></strong></p><p><strong>Please read the attachment install instructions prior to going onsite.</strong></p><p><strong>Upon arrival to site please check in on provided bridge number.</strong></p><p><strong>This is a high level overview</strong></p><p><strong><u>Network Preparation and Equipment:</u></strong></p><p>1. Each fixed POS station requires a total of 5 network ports, 4 broadcasted on VLAN 10 and&nbsp;one port Broadcasted on VLAN 15.</p><p>2. Network setups</p><p>3. NikePOS registers will be shipped to the site fully assembled and labelled for the correct&nbsp;station (register location).</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Installation:</u></strong></p><p>1. Unbox the Epson printer, Zebra hand scanner and NFC Reader and install it in location.</p><p>2. Unbox the first GAN unit (72445).</p><p>3. Unbox the AFD and install it into location</p><p>3. Unbox the second GAN unit (72445).</p><p>4. Unbox the CFD and install it into location.</p><p>5. The CFD should be securely fastened to the Cashwrap by using 4 screws&nbsp;</p><p>6. After the installation of the base plate, return the mount to the base plate and secure it&nbsp;by rotating the 2 grub screws clockwise</p><p>7. Turn on the AFD and CFD equipment and verify no visible issues are shown.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Device configuration:</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>Smoke Testing</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p>","markdown":"**High Level Scope:**\n\n**Please read the attachment install instructions prior to going onsite.**\n\n**Upon arrival to site please check in on provided bridge number.**\n\n**This is a high level overview**\n\n**Network Preparation and Equipment:**\n\n1\\. Each fixed POS station requires a total of 5 network ports, 4 broadcasted on VLAN 10 and one port Broadcasted on VLAN 15.\n\n2\\. Network setups\n\n3\\. NikePOS registers will be shipped to the site fully assembled and labelled for the correct station (register location).\n\n**Installation:**\n\n1\\. Unbox the Epson printer, Zebra hand scanner and NFC Reader and install it in location.\n\n2\\. Unbox the first GAN unit (72445).\n\n3\\. Unbox the AFD and install it into location\n\n3\\. Unbox the second GAN unit (72445).\n\n4\\. Unbox the CFD and install it into location.\n\n5\\. The CFD should be securely fastened to the Cashwrap by using 4 screws\n\n6\\. After the installation of the base plate, return the mount to the base plate and secure it by rotating the 2 grub screws clockwise\n\n7\\. Turn on the AFD and CFD equipment and verify no visible issues are shown.\n\n**Device configuration:**\n\n**Smoke Testing**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-21T15:00","end":"2026-10-21T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":130,"max":520},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":130},"additional":{"units":6,"amount":65}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":32},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"blended","counterRate":65,"baseAmount":520,"estHours":2,"travelExpense":55,"payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":130},"additional":{"units":6,"amount":65}}},"reason":"TRAVEL_REQUIRED","rejectDetails":"Travel required (32mi reported + 10mi padding = 42mi > 20mi)"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-21T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","su