{"job":{"id":19952163,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"National Video Monitoring Corp","title":"Troubleshoot Wireless Issue *24FT EXT LADDER REQ* ","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Specific SOW Below: Refer to Summary for additional Information</strong></p><p>Upon arrival technician will need to call-in to EyeQ for Check-in and out: 727-437-3586</p><p>Remote Support. 678-846-9271&nbsp;</p><p>Standard Requirements</p><p><br></p><p>Network tools</p><p>Laptop</p><p>Basic hand tools</p><p>Cable tester/toner if cabling needs to be validated</p><p>Issue to Address Onsite</p><p><br></p><p>Wireless connectivity appears to be impacting APs and Stations. Remote Support attempted remote recovery without success. Field technician needs to validate wireless device power, cabling, line of sight, alignment, link status, and connected downstream equipment.</p><p><br></p><p>Device Details</p><p><br></p><p>1. Building 306 Exterior (Parking) | Camera | univiewtec | IPV4E28X | IP: 172.17.221.61 | MAC: E4-F1-4C-4B-BC-CB | Status/Issue: DOWN</p><p><br></p><p>Remote Troubleshooting Already Attempted</p><p><br></p><p>Remote Support reviewed the issue and attempted remote recovery, but the affected device remained offline/unreachable.</p><p>Actions Required Onsite</p><p><br></p><p>Locate the affected wireless equipment onsite.</p><p>Validate power, cabling, PoE, link lights, and connected downstream equipment.</p><p>Check wireless alignment, line of sight, mounting stability, and physical condition.</p><p>Inspect for obstructions, damage, loose mounts, or cabling issues.</p><p>Work with Remote Support to confirm link quality and downstream device connectivity before leaving site.</p><p>Deliverables / What to Report Back</p><p><br></p><p>Photos of affected equipment.</p><p>Photos of cabling, terminations, switch ports, power supplies, and link lights.</p><p>Summary of troubleshooting performed onsite.</p><p>Root cause of the issue.</p><p>Final device status before leaving site.</p><p>Any remaining issues or required return visit details.</p><p>Required Remote Support Coordination</p><p><br></p><p>Technician must contact Field Coordination upon arrival before beginning work.</p><p>Technician must provide photos of the affected equipment, cabling, power, link lights, and surrounding area where applicable.</p><p>Technician must contact Remote Support before replacing, factory resetting, relocating, or removing any equipment unless specifically instructed in this SOW.</p><p>Technician must contact Remote Support before leaving site to confirm final device status and verify whether any additional action is required.</p><p>If the issue cannot be resolved onsite, technician must provide clear findings, suspected root cause, photos, and what is needed for a return visit.</p><p><strong>Time Management:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Approval:</strong> Call for additional time if the job exceeds 2 hours. Extra time without prior approval will not be compensated.</li><li><strong>Contact:</strong> Contact the Work Order Manager immediately if the onsite contact does not allow you to work.</li><li><strong>Work Hours:</strong> Complete the work during the specified timeframe and normal business hours unless otherwise stated.</li><li><strong>Completion:</strong> Do not leave without discussing unresolved issues with the Work Order Manager.</li></ul><p><strong>Required Equipment:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Ladders:</strong> 8/16' Little Giant Ladder or 8' A-frame and a 24' Extension Ladder.</li><li><strong>Cabling:</strong> Cat5 Cable (reimbursed at $0.18 per foot) and RJ-45 Cable Termination Ends.</li><li><strong>Tools:</strong> Network testing tools, toner, installation tools, voltmeter, smartphone with Field Nation app, laptop with RJ-45 and Wi-Fi, and a basic technician tool kit.</li><li><strong>Additional Instructions:</strong> Refer to the Standard Instructions section for standardized equipment reimbursement rates.</li></ul><p><strong>Important Policies:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Check-in/Out:</strong> Call 678-846-9271 before starting and after completing the work. Provide details if the Scope of Work cannot be completed.</li><li><strong>Technical Support:</strong> Available M-F, 9 AM-4:30 PM EST. Provide details on your work progress when contacting technical support.</li><li><strong>Equipment Return:</strong> Return unused equipment to EyeQ (NVMC) with original packaging. Contact the Work Order Manager for a return shipping label.</li><li><strong>Rescheduling Policy:</strong> If rescheduling is necessary due to EyeQ’s error (e.g., missing equipment), a $30 travel fee will be paid.</li><li><strong>Issue Diagnosis:</strong> For issues requiring a return trip, the ticket remains open with additional expenses. Misdiagnoses will not be compensated for a second trip.</li><li><strong>NTE (Not To Exceed) Hours:</strong> Additional time beyond the initial approved period requires prior approval from the Work Order Manager.</li></ul>","markdown":"**Specific SOW Below: Refer to Summary for additional Information**\n\nUpon arrival technician will need to call-in to EyeQ for Check-in and out: 727-437-3586\n\nRemote Support. 678-846-9271\n\nStandard Requirements\n\nNetwork tools\n\nLaptop\n\nBasic hand tools\n\nCable tester/toner if cabling needs to be validated\n\nIssue to Address Onsite\n\nWireless connectivity appears to be impacting APs and Stations. Remote Support attempted remote recovery without success. Field technician needs to validate wireless device power, cabling, line of sight, alignment, link status, and connected downstream equipment.\n\nDevice Details\n\n1\\. Building 306 Exterior (Parking) | Camera | univiewtec | IPV4E28X | IP: 172.17.221.61 | MAC: E4-F1-4C-4B-BC-CB | Status/Issue: DOWN\n\nRemote Troubleshooting Already Attempted\n\nRemote Support reviewed the issue and attempted remote recovery, but the affected device remained offline/unreachable.\n\nActions Required Onsite\n\nLocate the affected wireless equipment onsite.\n\nValidate power, cabling, PoE, link lights, and connected downstream equipment.\n\nCheck wireless alignment, line of sight, mounting stability, and physical condition.\n\nInspect for obstructions, damage, loose mounts, or cabling issues.\n\nWork with Remote Support to confirm link quality and downstream device connectivity before leaving site.\n\nDeliverables / What to Report Back\n\nPhotos of affected equipment.\n\nPhotos of cabling, terminations, switch ports, power supplies, and link lights.\n\nSummary of troubleshooting performed onsite.\n\nRoot cause of the issue.\n\nFinal device status before leaving site.\n\nAny remaining issues or required return visit details.\n\nRequired Remote Support Coordination\n\nTechnician must contact Field Coordination upon arrival before beginning work.\n\nTechnician must provide photos of the affected equipment, cabling, power, link lights, and surrounding area where applicable.\n\nTechnician must contact Remote Support before replacing, factory resetting, relocating, or removing any equipment unless specifically instructed in this SOW.\n\nTechnician must contact Remote Support before leaving site to confirm final device status and verify whether any additional action is required.\n\nIf the issue cannot be resolved onsite, technician must provide clear findings, suspected root cause, photos, and what is needed for a return visit.\n\n**Time Management:**\n\n- **Approval:** Call for additional time if the job exceeds 2 hours. Extra time without prior approval will not be compensated.\n- **Contact:** Contact the Work Order Manager immediately if the onsite contact does not allow you to work.\n- **Work Hours:** Complete the work during the specified timeframe and normal business hours unless otherwise stated.\n- **Completion:** Do not leave without discussing unresolved issues with the Work Order Manager.\n\n**Required Equipment:**\n\n- **Ladders:** 8/16' Little Giant Ladder or 8' A-frame and a 24' Extension Ladder.\n- **Cabling:** Cat5 Cable (reimbursed at $0.18 per foot) and RJ-45 Cable Termination Ends.\n- **Tools:** Network testing tools, toner, installation tools, voltmeter, smartphone with Field Nation app, laptop with RJ-45 and Wi-Fi, and a basic technician tool kit.\n- **Additional Instructions:** Refer to the Standard Instructions section for standardized equipment reimbursement rates.\n\n**Important Policies:**\n\n- **Check-in/Out:** Call 678-846-9271 before starting and after completing the work. Provide details if the Scope of Work cannot be completed.\n- **Technical Support:** Available M-F, 9 AM-4:30 PM EST. Provide details on your work progress when contacting technical support.\n- **Equipment Return:** Return unused equipment to EyeQ (NVMC) with original packaging. Contact the Work Order Manager for a return shipping label.\n- **Rescheduling Policy:** If rescheduling is necessary due to EyeQ’s error (e.g., missing equipment), a $30 travel fee will be paid.\n- **Issue Diagnosis:** For issues requiring a return trip, the ticket remains open with additional expenses. Misdiagnoses will not be compensated for a second trip.\n- **NTE (Not To Exceed) Hours:** Additional time beyond the initial approved period requires prior approval from the Work Order Manager.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-16T09:00","end":"2026-09-16T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":150},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":75,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":69},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $150 (countered: $150) is below minimum threshold $250"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789419504867}
