{"job":{"id":19954495,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"SISL Infotech (US) Inc","title":"DSS Support Required | Raleigh, NC","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Overview</u></strong>:-</p><p><strong>Total Number of Days Required -38 Days</strong></p><p><strong>Start Date – 21st September 2026</strong></p><p><strong>End Date – 13th November 2026</strong></p><p><strong>Address - 901 Main Campus Drive, Raleigh, NC - USA</strong></p><p><strong>Citizen – US citizen only</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><u>Roles &amp; Responsibilities</u> :-</p><ul><li>Install and configure desktops, laptops, mobile devices, peripherals, and related software.</li><li>Perform break–fix support, desk-side assistance, IMACD activities, data migration, device refreshes, and other technical tasks.</li><li>Execute onsite updates, configuration changes, and software installations.</li><li>Provide hands-on technical assistance and support to end users.</li><li>Identify potential issues that may affect end-user experience and take proactive measures to resolve or prevent them.</li><li>Manage assigned tickets and ensure timely resolution and closure within defined SLAs, providing regular updates to end users as required.</li><li>Coordinate with external vendors for hardware provisioning, warranty repairs, and replacements.</li><li>Support end-user activities related to security controls, compliance checks, access reviews, and facility inspections.</li><li>Collaborate with Level 3 support teams and project groups for service enhancements, maintenance activities, and upgrades.</li><li>Provide IT support for on-site and off-site events or meetings, including setup, coordination with venue IT/AV teams, and standby support.</li><li>Assist in disaster recovery activities and provide immediate response support during emergencies at local sites.</li><li>Participate in on-call support on a rotational basis, including outside normal business hours when required.</li><li>Provide hands-and-feet support for netwo