{"job":{"id":19954567,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"StrikeCheck","title":"Express Damage Assessment - StrikeCheck Appointment A-2714487","description":{"html":"<p>*Please make sure to read through all instructions to avoid a second visit to the property and/or non-payment*</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The following items need to be <strong><em>documented</em></strong>, <strong><em>inspected</em></strong>, <strong><em>tested</em></strong> and <strong><em>photographed, even if they are found to be non-damaged</em></strong>:</p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(32, 33, 36);\"><b><ul><li>Computer : Apple : 1</li><li>TV : Roku : 1</li><li>Keyboard : Nord : 1</li><li>Window Air Conditioner : Brand Unknown : 1</li></ul></b></span></p><p><br></p><p><strong>ATTENTION: Every technician must use the CCG IQ Inspection Wizard to submit their findings. We cannot complete our payment to you if the findings are submitted to the Field Nation platform or via email. All findings, including non-damaged items on your list, must be sent directly to StrikeCheck using our CCG IQ Inspection Wizard via our Android app or web portal. If any item cannot be documented you must include a statement in your notes explaining those circumstances.</strong></p><p><strong>If you are unsure of how to use our Android app or web portal, or are having issues while you are onsite, please call (888) 980-8544 and a live representative will talk you through the submission process. Android users will need to download the \"CCG IQ Inspection Wizard\" in the app store on your device. Our office hours are 8am-8pm EST Monday-Friday and 8am-5pm on Saturdays. If no one is available to take your call please leave a message and we will return your call ASAP!</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>Testing and Documentation Requirements:</strong></p><ol><li>Full testing and documentation procedures on a per-item type basis can be found under the “Resources” tab in our web app. Select “StrikeCheck” in the “Libraries” folder to review the requirements before every inspection to ensure all required data is being captured.</li><li>Basic continuity/ohm testing is required using a digital multimeter. Verify a functional power source or outlet with your meter and document those readings. If needed, reset any associated circuit breakers but do not otherwise alter the electrical panel.&nbsp;</li><li>Apply power and operationally test ALL FUNCTIONS of every item. Notate any connected items (speakers to receiver, cameras to DVR, etc.) and advise if further testing is necessary due to the failure of one of those components (\"Can't test speakers due to damaged receiver\").&nbsp;</li><li>Document and photograph all obtainable readings/testing. <strong>If the item is not damaged or has already been replaced with new equipment, we still need the same amount of evidence (photos and test results) to support your findings.</strong> If the item is not operating properly, determine the causation of damage.&nbsp;</li><li>In addition to photos of the loss location and your meter readings, we require that you provide a minimum of 3 pictures per item. These pictures should illustrate where/how the item is installed, the overall condition of the item, any visual damages, and <strong><em>most importantly, </em></strong>the data plate. Also photograph any associated components connected to the item you are inspecting. Additional photographs and documentation are always encouraged.</li></ol><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Inspection Requirements:</strong></p><ul><li>A smart phone with access to our Android app or web app portal for Apple iOS users is the preferred method to document and upload your findings in real time. Access the app or portal before the inspection begins and it will walk you through all steps required for each item you enter.</li><li>Use of a camera and our Technician Worksheets is an alternate option that will require a computer to access the web app portal in order to upload photos as well as transcribing your detailed technical documentation from the worksheets into our system.</li><li>Multimeter/VOM and a basic toolkit</li><li>Must be professionally dressed (wear a clean collared shirt and pants; No shorts, no t-shirts, no flip-flops, and no ripped jeans). Avoid wearing anything that will identify your personal employer/company name or contact info to prevent insureds from calling you directly after you complete your assignment. This is an independent inspection on behalf of StrikeCheck, an insurance consulting company. <strong>You</strong> <strong>must represent yourself as being with StrikeCheck</strong> <strong>when you arrive onsite</strong>.</li><li>Must be willing to display contractor photo identification (if issued) and must have appropriate background and skills to perform the listed work order requirements</li><li>Must have passed a background check and drug test.&nbsp;</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Submission Requirements:</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>iPhone/iPad users: Upload required information via our <strong>web portal</strong> the same day as the inspection using a secure password. Click the \"Login\" link below or use this web address to access the portal:&nbsp;https://consolidatedclaims.my.site.com/ccginspector/&nbsp;</li><li>All findings, pictures, and determinations should be submitted on the same day as the inspection. <strong>Your deadline to submit is 24 hours from the scheduled appointment start time. Failure to do so may result in non-payment and could affect your rating.</strong></li><li>Your work order is not considered complete and payable until findings are submitted through the Android app or web portal and is approved by our Processing Department. Please make yourself available for follow-up calls if we have any questions regarding your findings.</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">Scheduling Requirements:</strong></p><ul><li>These work orders most likely take place in a residential property, and therefore requires the ETA to be approved by the client.</li><li>When you are assigned this work order, please submit an ETA as soon as possible.</li><li>We will reach out to the client to confirm that they are able to be onsite during your proposed ETA. <strong><u>The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.</u></strong></li><li>A project manager will message you via the Field Nation App when the ETA has been confirmed with the insured. If you go to the loss location before we confirm the appointment is set, you will not be afforded a trip fee in the event that the insured is not present when you arrive.</li><li><strong>You must update our project managers and dispatch coordinators regularly on work order progress, any service delays, or schedule conflicts. If you cannot make an appointment CALL OUR OFFICE IMMEDIATELY TO RESCHEDULE. Field Nation messages are not an accepted medium for rescheduling or canceling appointments!</strong></li><li>If you go to the property, but the client does not show for the appointment, call us immediately so we can follow up with the client and determine if they will be arriving soon. <strong>If the client misses the appointment, you must take a clear photo of the house/property, showing the address so we can confirm you were there.</strong></li><li>StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the insured cannot make the appointment.&nbsp;</li><li>StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the scope of work cannot be completed for any reason</li><li>StrikeCheck will <em>not </em>provide a trip fee if you arrive at an appointment that has <em>not </em>been confirmed with the client and the project manager. <strong><u>The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.</u></strong></li></ul>","markdown":"\\*Please make sure to read through all instructions to avoid a second visit to the property and/or non-payment\\*\n\nThe following items need to be ***documented***, ***inspected***, ***tested*** and ***photographed, even if they are found to be non-damaged***:\n\n**- Computer : Apple : 1\n\\- TV : Roku : 1\n\\- Keyboard : Nord : 1\n\\- Window Air Conditioner : Brand Unknown : 1**\n\n**ATTENTION: Every technician must use the CCG IQ Inspection Wizard to submit their findings. We cannot complete our payment to you if the findings are submitted to the Field Nation platform or via email. All findings, including non-damaged items on your list, must be sent directly to StrikeCheck using our CCG IQ Inspection Wizard via our Android app or web portal. If any item cannot be documented you must include a statement in your notes explaining those circumstances.**\n\n**If you are unsure of how to use our Android app or web portal, or are having issues while you are onsite, please call (888) 980-8544 and a live representative will talk you through the submission process. Android users will need to download the \"CCG IQ Inspection Wizard\" in the app store on your device. Our office hours are 8am-8pm EST Monday-Friday and 8am-5pm on Saturdays. If no one is available to take your call please leave a message and we will return your call ASAP!**\n\n**Testing and Documentation Requirements:**\n\n1. Full testing and documentation procedures on a per-item type basis can be found under the “Resources” tab in our web app. Select “StrikeCheck” in the “Libraries” folder to review the requirements before every inspection to ensure all required data is being captured.\n2. Basic continuity/ohm testing is required using a digital multimeter. Verify a functional power source or outlet with your meter and document those readings. If needed, reset any associated circuit breakers but do not otherwise alter the electrical panel.\n3. Apply power and operationally test ALL FUNCTIONS of every item. Notate any connected items (speakers to receiver, cameras to DVR, etc.) and advise if further testing is necessary due to the failure of one of those components (\"Can't test speakers due to damaged receiver\").\n4. Document and photograph all obtainable readings/testing. **If the item is not damaged or has already been replaced with new equipment, we still need the same amount of evidence (photos and test results) to support your findings.** If the item is not operating properly, determine the causation of damage.\n5. In addition to photos of the loss location and your meter readings, we require that you provide a minimum of 3 pictures per item. These pictures should illustrate where/how the item is installed, the overall condition of the item, any visual damages, and ***most importantly,*** the data plate. Also photograph any associated components connected to the item you are inspecting. Additional photographs and documentation are always encouraged.\n\n**Inspection Requirements:**\n\n- A smart phone with access to our Android app or web app portal for Apple iOS users is the preferred method to document and upload your findings in real time. Access the app or portal before the inspection begins and it will walk you through all steps required for each item you enter.\n- Use of a camera and our Technician Worksheets is an alternate option that will require a computer to access the web app portal in order to upload photos as well as transcribing your detailed technical documentation from the worksheets into our system.\n- Multimeter/VOM and a basic toolkit\n- Must be professionally dressed (wear a clean collared shirt and pants; No shorts, no t-shirts, no flip-flops, and no ripped jeans). Avoid wearing anything that will identify your personal employer/company name or contact info to prevent insureds from calling you directly after you complete your assignment. This is an independent inspection on behalf of StrikeCheck, an insurance consulting company. **You** **must represent yourself as being with StrikeCheck** **when you arrive onsite**.\n- Must be willing to display contractor photo identification (if issued) and must have appropriate background and skills to perform the listed work order requirements\n- Must have passed a background check and drug test.\n\n**Submission Requirements:**\n\n- iPhone/iPad users: Upload required information via our **web portal** the same day as the inspection using a secure password. Click the \"Login\" link below or use this web address to access the portal: <https://consolidatedclaims.my.site.com/ccginspector/&nbsp;>\n- All findings, pictures, and determinations should be submitted on the same day as the inspection. **Your deadline to submit is 24 hours from the scheduled appointment start time. Failure to do so may result in non-payment and could affect your rating.**\n- Your work order is not considered complete and payable until findings are submitted through the Android app or web portal and is approved by our Processing Department. Please make yourself available for follow-up calls if we have any questions regarding your findings.\n\n**Scheduling Requirements:**\n\n- These work orders most likely take place in a residential property, and therefore requires the ETA to be approved by the client.\n- When you are assigned this work order, please submit an ETA as soon as possible.\n- We will reach out to the client to confirm that they are able to be onsite during your proposed ETA. **The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.**\n- A project manager will message you via the Field Nation App when the ETA has been confirmed with the insured. If you go to the loss location before we confirm the appointment is set, you will not be afforded a trip fee in the event that the insured is not present when you arrive.\n- **You must update our project managers and dispatch coordinators regularly on work order progress, any service delays, or schedule conflicts. If you cannot make an appointment CALL OUR OFFICE IMMEDIATELY TO RESCHEDULE. Field Nation messages are not an accepted medium for rescheduling or canceling appointments!**\n- If you go to the property, but the client does not show for the appointment, call us immediately so we can follow up with the client and determine if they will be arriving soon. **If the client misses the appointment, you must take a clear photo of the house/property, showing the address so we can confirm you were there.**\n- StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the insured cannot make the appointment.\n- StrikeCheck will provide a 50% trip fee to you up to $100 if the scope of work cannot be completed for any reason\n- StrikeCheck will *not* provide a trip fee if you arrive at an appointment that has *not* been confirmed with the client and the project manager. **The appointment is not considered scheduled until we follow up with you to confirm the proposed time works for all parties.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-15T15:00","end":"2026-09-15T17:00","latestStart":"2026-09-15T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":41},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-15T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-17T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T18:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-15T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"gap"},{"start":"2026-09-16T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2