{"job":{"id":19954790,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Tech Hub PS","title":"ARS Network Refresh – Network Equipment Installation (2 Technicians Required)","description":{"html":"<p><strong>&nbsp;Overview:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Seeking a technician with experience in Network Equipment Installation</li>\n<li>Must need to fill up the attached survey doc within 2 hours of the survey is completed.</li>\n<li>This will be the site survey, but after the site survey, we will also do an installation</li>\n<li>For Installation, we will need 2 techs after hours</li>\n<li><strong>Lead Tech Will Return the next morning for validation with the remote team</strong></li>\n<li>The estimated duration will be 4-6 Hours</li>\n<li><strong>Address yourself as a Technician from TechHub PS</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Dress Code:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Clean, professional work clothes - (Polo T-shirt, Jeans, Shoes)</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>1. Purpose</strong></p>\n<p>This Statement of Work (SOW) defines the scope of services for site survey, readiness validation, legacy equipment removal, installation of Cisco Meraki network equipment, cabling control, and activation verification for ARS Network Refresh locations.</p>\n<p>This SOW covers physical installation services only.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>2. Scope of Services</strong></p>\n<p>The service provider will perform the following tasks at each designated ARS site.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>3. Site Survey &amp; Pre-Installation Validation3.1 Pre-Arrival Requirements (Minimum 5 Business Days Prior)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>The following must be confirmed before scheduling installation:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Completed Site Readiness Checklist uploaded to portal</li>\n<li>Power availability verified (UPS/circuits confirmed)</li>\n<li>Rack space confirmed (RU availability documented)</li>\n<li>Patch panel capacity confirmed</li>\n<li>Cabling pathways clear</li>\n<li>HVAC operational</li>\n<li>Access credentials / escort / badges arranged</li>\n<li>Floor plans and device placement diagrams provided</li>\n<li>Rack elevation diagram received</li>\n<li>Port map diagram received (labeled connectivity)</li>\n<li>Firewall replacement plan received (if applicable)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>3.2 On-Site Hardware Verification (Day of Installation)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Upon arrival:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Check in with ARS onsite contact</li>\n<li>Verify all shipped hardware is onsite (Switches / APs / Firewalls)</li>\n<li>Verify patch cable kits (factory CAT6 28AWG or higher)</li>\n<li>Confirm Velcro / zip ties / cable covers available</li>\n<li>Verify shipment manifest vs received equipment</li>\n<li>Confirm all serial numbers match manifest</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>3.3 Mandatory Pre-Install Physical Survey (Photo Required)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Before beginning removal:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Take full rack front photo</li>\n<li>Take rack rear photo</li>\n<li>Take patch panel close-up photo</li>\n<li>Take existing switch connection photo</li>\n<li>Take firewall connection photo (if applicable)</li>\n<li>Document readiness gaps</li>\n<li>Log deviations</li>\n<li>Obtain ARS approval before proceeding if deviations exist</li>\n</ul>\n<p>No installation work shall begin without site survey documentation.</p>\n<p><strong>4. Critical Cable Label Control Procedure (Before Removal)</strong></p>\n<p>Before disconnecting any legacy equipment:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Verify every cable connected to existing switch is labeled</li>\n<li>If ANY cable is not labeled → STOP removal process</li>\n<li>Inform ARS and perform labeling before proceeding</li>\n</ul>\n<p>If labeling is required:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Label cables clearly</li>\n<li>Match labels to documented port map</li>\n<li>Clearly identify uplinks, trunk ports, firewall handoffs, AP ports</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Removal may not proceed without verified labeling.</p>\n<p><strong>5. Legacy Equipment Removal</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Unmount legacy switches</li>\n<li>Remove legacy patch cables (leave onsite for recycling)</li>\n<li>Remove legacy APs (reuse existing CAT6 cable)</li>\n<li>Leave removed hardware onsite for ARS recycling</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>6. Equipment Installation &amp; Cable Reinstallation</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Install new Cisco Meraki switches per rack elevation</li>\n<li>Install new Meraki APs using existing drops</li>\n<li>Install firewall(s) if applicable</li>\n<li>Use NEW factory-certified CAT6 28AWG (or higher) patch cables</li>\n<li>Reconnect cables using exact documented port mapping</li>\n<li>Follow previously created labels</li>\n<li>Ensure physical port numbers match logical port map</li>\n<li>Blue cables used for access ports</li>\n<li>Red cables used for uplink/trunk ports</li>\n<li>Apply clean cable bundling (Velcro preferred)</li>\n<li>Remove old cables</li>\n<li>Maintain rack cleanliness and airflow</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>7. Power-Up &amp; Dashboard Verification</strong></p>\n<p>After installation:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Confirm devices check in to Meraki dashboard</li>\n<li>Confirm serial numbers match expected inventory</li>\n<li>Confirm correct network claim</li>\n<li>Verify firmware version</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>8. Documentation &amp; Photo Requirements</strong></p>\n<p>The following must be uploaded to the project documentation portal:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Pre-install rack photos</li>\n<li>Post-install rack photos</li>\n<li>Cable management photos</li>\n<li>Label verification photos (if applicable)</li>\n<li>Hardware inventory confirmation</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>9. Check-Out &amp; Completion Requirements</strong></p>\n<p>Before leaving site:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Confirm no open physical installation issues remain</li>\n<li>Confirm all devices are online in dashboard</li>\n<li>Confirm cabling matches port map</li>\n<li>Obtain site contact acknowledgment of completed physical work</li>\n<li>Confirm removed equipment left onsite for recycling</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Work is considered complete when:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>All listed tasks are executed</li>\n<li>Devices are operational</li>\n<li>Documentation is uploaded</li>\n<li>Site acknowledgment is obtained</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>10. Exclusions</strong></p>\n<p>This SOW does not include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Logical network design</li>\n<li>Firewall rule creation</li>\n<li>Structured cabling installation</li>\n<li>Network redesign</li>\n<li>Ongoing managed services</li>\n<li>These remain the responsibility of ARS unless separately contracted.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Escalation Process:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>If clarification is needed on the work order, discuss it with<strong>&nbsp;Mathew Manik (858) 321 3947</strong></li>\n<li>Any issues or questions should be escalated to<strong>mbaroi@techhubps.com</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>&nbsp;All expenses must be discussed and pre-approved ahead of time</li>\n<li>Note - Any other tasks need approval by mail. Please take sign-off for the work order.</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**Overview:**\n\n- Seeking a technician with experience in Network Equipment Installation\n- Must need to fill up the attached survey doc within 2 hours of the survey is completed.\n- This will be the site survey, but after the site survey, we will also do an installation\n- For Installation, we will need 2 techs after hours\n- **Lead Tech Will Return the next morning for validation with the remote team**\n- The estimated duration will be 4-6 Hours\n- **Address yourself as a Technician from TechHub PS**\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n- **Clean, professional work clothes - (Polo T-shirt, Jeans, Shoes)**\n\n**1. Purpose**\n\nThis Statement of Work (SOW) defines the scope of services for site survey, readiness validation, legacy equipment removal, installation of Cisco Meraki network equipment, cabling control, and activation verification for ARS Network Refresh locations.\n\nThis SOW covers physical installation services only.\n\n**2. Scope of Services**\n\nThe service provider will perform the following tasks at each designated ARS site.\n\n**3. Site Survey & Pre-Installation Validation3.1 Pre-Arrival Requirements (Minimum 5 Business Days Prior)**\n\n**The following must be confirmed before scheduling installation:**\n\n- Completed Site Readiness Checklist uploaded to portal\n- Power availability verified (UPS/circuits confirmed)\n- Rack space confirmed (RU availability documented)\n- Patch panel capacity confirmed\n- Cabling pathways clear\n- HVAC operational\n- Access credentials / escort / badges arranged\n- Floor plans and device placement diagrams provided\n- Rack elevation diagram received\n- Port map diagram received (labeled connectivity)\n- Firewall replacement plan received (if applicable)\n\n**3.2 On-Site Hardware Verification (Day of Installation)**\n\n**Upon arrival:**\n\n- Check in with ARS onsite contact\n- Verify all shipped hardware is onsite (Switches / APs / Firewalls)\n- Verify patch cable kits (factory CAT6 28AWG or higher)\n- Confirm Velcro / zip ties / cable covers available\n- Verify shipment manifest vs received equipment\n- Confirm all serial numbers match manifest\n\n**3.3 Mandatory Pre-Install Physical Survey (Photo Required)**\n\n**Before beginning removal:**\n\n- Take full rack front photo\n- Take rack rear photo\n- Take patch panel close-up photo\n- Take existing switch connection photo\n- Take firewall connection photo (if applicable)\n- Document readiness gaps\n- Log deviations\n- Obtain ARS approval before proceeding if deviations exist\n\nNo installation work shall begin without site survey documentation.\n\n**4. Critical Cable Label Control Procedure (Before Removal)**\n\nBefore disconnecting any legacy equipment:\n\n- Verify every cable connected to existing switch is labeled\n- If ANY cable is not labeled → STOP removal process\n- Inform ARS and perform labeling before proceeding\n\nIf labeling is required:\n\n- Label cables clearly\n- Match labels to documented port map\n- Clearly identify uplinks, trunk ports, firewall handoffs, AP ports\n\nRemoval may not proceed without verified labeling.\n\n**5. Legacy Equipment Removal**\n\n- Unmount legacy switches\n- Remove legacy patch cables (leave onsite for recycling)\n- Remove legacy APs (reuse existing CAT6 cable)\n- Leave removed hardware onsite for ARS recycling\n\n**6. Equipment Installation & Cable Reinstallation**\n\n- Install new Cisco Meraki switches per rack elevation\n- Install new Meraki APs using existing drops\n- Install firewall(s) if applicable\n- Use NEW factory-certified CAT6 28AWG (or higher) patch cables\n- Reconnect cables using exact documented port mapping\n- Follow previously created labels\n- Ensure physical port numbers match logical port map\n- Blue cables used for access ports\n- Red cables used for uplink/trunk ports\n- Apply clean cable bundling (Velcro preferred)\n- Remove old cables\n- Maintain rack cleanliness and airflow\n\n**7. Power-Up & Dashboard Verification**\n\nAfter installation:\n\n- Confirm devices check in to Meraki dashboard\n- Confirm serial numbers match expected inventory\n- Confirm correct network claim\n- Verify firmware version\n\n**8. Documentation & Photo Requirements**\n\nThe following must be uploaded to the project documentation portal:\n\n- Pre-install rack photos\n- Post-install rack photos\n- Cable management photos\n- Label verification photos (if applicable)\n- Hardware inventory confirmation\n\n**9. Check-Out & Completion Requirements**\n\nBefore leaving site:\n\n- Confirm no open physical installation issues remain\n- Confirm all devices are online in dashboard\n- Confirm cabling matches port map\n- Obtain site contact acknowledgment of completed physical work\n- Confirm removed equipment left onsite for recycling\n\nWork is considered complete when:\n\n- All listed tasks are executed\n- Devices are operational\n- Documentation is uploaded\n- Site acknowledgment is obtained\n\n**10. Exclusions**\n\nThis SOW does not include:\n\n- Logical network design\n- Firewall rule creation\n- Structured cabling installation\n- Network redesign\n- Ongoing managed services\n- These remain the responsibility of ARS unless separately contracted.\n\n**Escalation Process:**\n\n- If clarification is needed on the work order, discuss it with **Mathew Manik (858) 321 3947**\n- Any issues or questions should be escalated to**mbaroi@techhubps.com**\n\n**Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy**\n\n- All expenses must be discussed and pre-approved ahead of time\n- Note - Any other tasks need approval by mail. Please take sign-off for the work order.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-24T17:00","end":"2026-09-24T27:00"},"payRange":{"min":110,"max":1100},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":110,"estLaborHours":10,"distance":59},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Thu, Sep 24, 5:00 PM\nChecked: Thu, Sep 24, Fri, Sep 25, Mon, Sep 28 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-24T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-21T14:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T18:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-