{"job":{"id":19955021,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"NETFOR","title":"U14 - Network Troubleshoot","description":{"html":"<p><strong>**<u>When arriving to site please contact you dispatch manager letting them know you have arrived. You will also need to check out with the dispatch manager when the site is completed or if technical support has released you for any reason.</u></strong></p><p><strong>**<u>Please review all documentation&nbsp;attached to the work order before arriving to site. There are multiple documents that will be helpful&nbsp;tools during the install. This will decrease&nbsp;the calls made technical support.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Scope of Work Guidelines:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Strict Adherence to Assigned Scope:</strong></li><li>Only perform tasks explicitly outlined in the assigned scope of work.</li><li>Any additional work requested on-site must receive prior approval from your Work Order Manager.</li><li><strong>***Any time beyond allotted amount of time must be approved by the Work Order Manager before proceeding.***</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Approval for Additional Work:</strong></p><ul><li>Unapproved work performed outside the defined scope <strong>will not</strong> be compensated.</li><li>Contact your Work Order Manager for authorization before proceeding with any unassigned tasks.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Tools &amp; Materials Not Covered in Scope:</strong></p><ul><li>Any required tools or materials not listed in the original scope must be pre-approved by your Work Order Manager.</li><li>Unapproved expenses will not be reimbursed.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Failure to comply may result in non-payment for unauthorized work or materials.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>SOW OF WORK</u></strong></p><ul><li>Network issues</li><li>Check cabling from the Fortinet back to all devices</li><li>Ensure they are connected correctly using the attached Fortinet guide</li><li>Repair/replace any cabling that may be damaged or defective</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Confirm&nbsp;<strong><u>ALL</u></strong>&nbsp;equipment is installed/troubleshot and operational with the site contact.&nbsp;</p><p>If this is not done and any equipment is not operational, tech will be required to return on a return visit under warranty.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>REQUIRED DELIVERABLES</u></strong></p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Work Order/checklist Signed by POC with Accurate date and Check In/Out times.</p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Pictures of work completed/troubleshot</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>CHECK IN/OUT PROCEDURES (DO NOT DEVIATE AWAY FROM THIS PROCEDURE)</u></strong></p><ol><li>Must arrive onsite at the scheduled time (call Netfor for any unforeseen issues)</li><li>Failure to call and notify Netfor could result in being blocked for future work. We take being notified very seriously so we have time to notify the client.</li><li>Check In via FN Portal</li><li>Check In with Netfor at 800-908-0226 opt 1. (Failure to check in could result in 25% withdrawn from payment)</li><li>Complete installation per SOW. Do not deviate away from the requested SOW unless you are authorized by or Netfor. If you are requested to complete additional work, inform Netfor immediately.&nbsp;&nbsp;<u>Document who approved the additional scope.</u>&nbsp;Without this we will not be able to pay and/or bill extra time.</li><li><strong>Check out Steps</strong></li></ol><p><strong><u>NOTE:&nbsp;</u></strong>Tech&nbsp;<strong><u>MUST</u></strong>&nbsp;upload pictures to platform before checking out with Netfor. Failure to upload documents and pictures within 24 hours could result in 25% withdrawn from payment. Tech will have approx. 2 days to close out ticket. Ticket MUST be closed out by Friday each week or it will be canceled.</p><ol><li>Have POC sign off on work order documenting check in and out times.</li><li>Check Out on Field Engineer (FN) Portal</li><li>Check out with Netfor at 800-908-0226 opt 1.</li></ol><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>TOOLS/MATERIALS</u></strong></p><p><strong>Prepare tool bag/box with the following:</strong></p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Tools Listed in the Job Description (Please read carefully)</p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Laptop</p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Basic PC Tools (Minimum 32 Gig Flashdrive)</p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Patch Cables</p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Digital Camera / Camera Phone with this ability to send pictures before leaving site</p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Copy of work order and job information</p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Any other tools/materials you may think you need to complete the job on the first visit.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Ensure a clean and wrinkle free uniform is ready:</strong></p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Long pants</p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Collared shirt</p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Netfor name badge</p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Close toe shoes</p><p>●&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Review SOW and inform Netfor of any question prior to arriving on site.</p>","markdown":"**\\*\\*When arriving to site please contact you dispatch manager letting them know you have arrived. You will also need to check out with the dispatch manager when the site is completed or if technical support has released you for any reason.**\n\n**\\*\\*Please review all documentation attached to the work order before arriving to site. There are multiple documents that will be helpful tools during the install. This will decrease the calls made technical support.**\n\n**Scope of Work Guidelines:**\n\n- **Strict Adherence to Assigned Scope:**\n- Only perform tasks explicitly outlined in the assigned scope of work.\n- Any additional work requested on-site must receive prior approval from your Work Order Manager.\n- **\\*\\*\\*Any time beyond allotted amount of time must be approved by the Work Order Manager before proceeding.\\*\\*\\***\n\n**Approval for Additional Work:**\n\n- Unapproved work performed outside the defined scope **will not** be compensated.\n- Contact your Work Order Manager for authorization before proceeding with any unassigned tasks.\n\n**Tools & Materials Not Covered in Scope:**\n\n- Any required tools or materials not listed in the original scope must be pre-approved by your Work Order Manager.\n- Unapproved expenses will not be reimbursed.\n\n**Failure to comply may result in non-payment for unauthorized work or materials.**\n\n**SOW OF WORK**\n\n- Network issues\n- Check cabling from the Fortinet back to all devices\n- Ensure they are connected correctly using the attached Fortinet guide\n- Repair/replace any cabling that may be damaged or defective\n\nConfirm **ALL** equipment is installed/troubleshot and operational with the site contact.\n\nIf this is not done and any equipment is not operational, tech will be required to return on a return visit under warranty.\n\n**REQUIRED DELIVERABLES**\n\n● Work Order/checklist Signed by POC with Accurate date and Check In/Out times.\n\n● Pictures of work completed/troubleshot\n\n**CHECK IN/OUT PROCEDURES (DO NOT DEVIATE AWAY FROM THIS PROCEDURE)**\n\n1. Must arrive onsite at the scheduled time (call Netfor for any unforeseen issues)\n2. Failure to call and notify Netfor could result in being blocked for future work. We take being notified very seriously so we have time to notify the client.\n3. Check In via FN Portal\n4. Check In with Netfor at 800-908-0226 opt 1. (Failure to check in could result in 25% withdrawn from payment)\n5. Complete installation per SOW. Do not deviate away from the requested SOW unless you are authorized by or Netfor. If you are requested to complete additional work, inform Netfor immediately. Document who approved the additional scope. Without this we will not be able to pay and/or bill extra time.\n6. **Check out Steps**\n\n**NOTE:** Tech **MUST** upload pictures to platform before checking out with Netfor. Failure to upload documents and pictures within 24 hours could result in 25% withdrawn from payment. Tech will have approx. 2 days to close out ticket. Ticket MUST be closed out by Friday each week or it will be canceled.\n\n1. Have POC sign off on work order documenting check in and out times.\n2. Check Out on Field Engineer (FN) Portal\n3. Check out with Netfor at 800-908-0226 opt 1.\n\n**TOOLS/MATERIALS**\n\n**Prepare tool bag/box with the following:**\n\n● Tools Listed in the Job Description (Please read carefully)\n\n● Laptop\n\n● Basic PC Tools (Minimum 32 Gig Flashdrive)\n\n● Patch Cables\n\n● Digital Camera / Camera Phone with this ability to send pictures before leaving site\n\n● Copy of work order and job information\n\n● Any other tools/materials you may think you need to complete the job on the first visit.\n\n**Ensure a clean and wrinkle free uniform is ready:**\n\n● Long pants\n\n● Collared shirt\n\n● Netfor name badge\n\n● Close toe shoes\n\n● Review SOW and inform Netfor of any question prior to arriving on site.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-16T11:00","end":"2026-09-16T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":50},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":13},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $50 (countered: $60) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789480009547}
