end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-21T14:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T18:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789482287406}
{"job":{"id":19955417,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Wachter - Nationwide Projects","title":"BDF Pinpad Refresh","description":{"html":"<p>WEAR ALL PPE</p><p>Check in with Grayson Hunter - 479-879-6017 or Phillip Harris 479-295-4151</p><p>Once onsite, the store manager will bring you:</p><p>-The new equipment for installation</p><p>-The shipping labels to return the old equipment</p><p>-A sign off form that we will need to fill out with asset tags and serial numbers.</p><p>SOW:</p><p>Main Scope is installing new chargers for their new handheld card readers, and updating and installing the new hand held card readers into these new chargers. Some devices will already be updated PLEASE CONFIRM SOFTWARE VERSION IS 1.129.</p><p>If the software version does not match, the devices will need to be updated. The PIN code to pull this update is \"2520\"</p><p>We can turn them all on at once and work through the update as needed.</p><p>NOTE - Once the new handhelds are being updated, the old handhelds will be taken offline and are no longer operational. This means that a store associate may have an old one on the floor when the cutover occurs and we will need to let them know it won't work.</p><p>CHARGING DOCKS - Charging docks are to be set up NEATLY and front facing. These charging docks need to be connected to an outlet or powerstrip OUTSIDE of the charging cart as those outlets are smart/managed outlets. If there are any issues with this, please reach out to us for next steps.</p><p>(2) of the new handheld devices will need to be installed at the counter on a mount that will ship with the devices. We will need to remove the old devices and mounts from the counter, they are on with adhesive and may require careful prying. These card readers will remain stationary at these counters. These handhelds are NOT SPECIFIC. So ANY of them may be used at the counter with no issues.</p><p>Check with the store manager to determine if there are any \"Bob's Squad Users\" where we may need to set up a handheld device. Not all stores will have this.</p><p>In addition to the card swipes, each store may have additional scope, please check with Grayson for confirmation. Those items are as follows:</p><p>Cradle Point Swap - The site may have a new cradle point and we can swap these 1 for 1.</p><p>SilverPeak - The SilverPeak router may be swapped at these stores. This involves installing the 1U SilverPeak near the top of the existing network rack. IT will have you move the WAN cable from the old device to the new device's Management Port so they can update it. Once updated, they will tell you which cables to cutover and in what order. This swap and update takes about 45 minutes give or take.</p><p>AP swap. Sites may require AP swaps. New AP's need to be configured by the Networking team prior to removing the old AP's. The new AP's have a larger range, so we will be replacing the existing AP's with a fewer count if applicable to your store. If the AP's are reachable from a ladder, and your store receives new AP's, we will swap them when IT tells us to. If a lift is required, let us know immediately and we will mark the site for revisit with a lift.</p><p>ALL old devices are to be carefully packed into the boxes the new equipment arrived in. The CC readers and AP's will go to separate locations, so there will be separate shipping labels.</p><p>Deliverables:</p><p>Pictures of all work completed including the counter mounted pin pads, the charging docks and pin pads installed on the charging cart, any additional devices that were installed.</p><p>A picture of the sign off sheet, filled out.</p><p>Lift Requirement Update so we know if a revisit is required.</p><p>Check out with Grayson.</p>","markdown":"WEAR ALL PPE\n\nCheck in with Grayson Hunter - 479-879-6017 or Phillip Harris 479-295-4151\n\nOnce onsite, the store manager will bring you:\n\n-The new equipment for installation\n\n-The shipping labels to return the old equipment\n\n-A sign off form that we will need to fill out with asset tags and serial numbers.\n\nSOW:\n\nMain Scope is installing new chargers for their new handheld card readers, and updating and installing the new hand held card readers into these new chargers. Some devices will already be updated PLEASE CONFIRM SOFTWARE VERSION IS 1.129.\n\nIf the software version does not match, the devices will need to be updated. The PIN code to pull this update is \"2520\"\n\nWe can turn them all on at once and work through the update as needed.\n\nNOTE - Once the new handhelds are being updated, the old handhelds will be taken offline and are no longer operational. This means that a store associate may have an old one on the floor when the cutover occurs and we will need to let them know it won't work.\n\nCHARGING DOCKS - Charging docks are to be set up NEATLY and front facing. These charging docks need to be connected to an outlet or powerstrip OUTSIDE of the charging cart as those outlets are smart/managed outlets. If there are any issues with this, please reach out to us for next steps.\n\n(2) of the new handheld devices will need to be installed at the counter on a mount that will ship with the devices. We will need to remove the old devices and mounts from the counter, they are on with adhesive and may require careful prying. These card readers will remain stationary at these counters. These handhelds are NOT SPECIFIC. So ANY of them may be used at the counter with no issues.\n\nCheck with the store manager to determine if there are any \"Bob's Squad Users\" where we may need to set up a handheld device. Not all stores will have this.\n\nIn addition to the card swipes, each store may have additional scope, please check with Grayson for confirmation. Those items are as follows:\n\nCradle Point Swap - The site may have a new cradle point and we can swap these 1 for 1.\n\nSilverPeak - The SilverPeak router may be swapped at these stores. This involves installing the 1U SilverPeak near the top of the existing network rack. IT will have you move the WAN cable from the old device to the new device's Management Port so they can update it. Once updated, they will tell you which cables to cutover and in what order. This swap and update takes about 45 minutes give or take.\n\nAP swap. Sites may require AP swaps. New AP's need to be configured by the Networking team prior to removing the old AP's. The new AP's have a larger range, so we will be replacing the existing AP's with a fewer count if applicable to your store. If the AP's are reachable from a ladder, and your store receives new AP's, we will swap them when IT tells us to. If a lift is required, let us know immediately and we will mark the site for revisit with a lift.\n\nALL old devices are to be carefully packed into the boxes the new equipment arrived in. The CC readers and AP's will go to separate locations, so there will be separate shipping labels.\n\nDeliverables:\n\nPictures of all work completed including the counter mounted pin pads, the charging docks and pin pads installed on the charging cart, any additional devices that were installed.\n\nA picture of the sign off sheet, filled out.\n\nLift Requirement Update so we know if a revisit is required.\n\nCheck out with Grayson.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-21T08:00","end":"2026-09-21T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":300},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":60,"estLaborHours":5,"distance":14},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $300 (countered: $300) is below minimum threshold $400"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:01:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-22T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-22T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-09-22T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-09-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-21T14:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T18:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789482416517}
{"job":{"id":19955475,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Essintial","title":"Assist Technician | Firm Start | Overnight Store Remodel - Network/Cabling/POS","description":{"html":"<p><strong>No unauthorized persons allowed on site. Any swaps or helpers must be approved by Essintial.</strong></p><p><br></p><p>SOW: Cash office, exterior camera, validation with management present</p><p>Processing / Exterior Scope</p><p>Install/validate .083 Compactor</p><p>Install/validate .086 Loading Dock</p><p>Install/validate .166 IP Speaker</p><p><br></p><p>Cash Office Verification</p><p>Verify Cash Office live-feed monitor</p><p><br></p><p>Final Closeout</p><p>Final CCTV validation with customer</p><p>Final cleanup</p><p>Customer signoff\"\"</p><p><br></p><p>Additional tool: Tech to bring mounting HW\"</p><p>Security Code: 862384</p><p>-----------------------------------------------------</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>REQUIRED SKILLS:&nbsp;</u></strong>Mid-Level Low Voltage Cabling, Mid-Level to Advanced Network Technician, Experience with Network &amp; Security/CCTV and Experience installing POS Equipment. Technician MUST be able to run cables neatly through various ceiling types, terminate cables with RJ45 plugs and or Keystone jacks.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work</u>:&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Seeking an Assist</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Technician to complete a Store Remodel at various Retailers. Technicians will be onsite working with LEAD TECHNICIAN to complete Low Voltage Cabling Runs, CCTV Installations (varies by site), POS De-Installations &amp; Re-Installations, TV Installations. (Every Remodel / STORE is slightly Different). Scope of work will take place&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Over Multiple</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">NIGHTs</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">. Each Night you will be scoped to complete specific items to stay on task to meet the store's cutover date. Technicians will be taking direction from Lead Technician and working with other assist technicians to complete the scope of work.</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>IMPORTANT CALL OUTS:</u></strong></p><ul><li>You&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;represent yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of <del>***</del></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Technicians&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">MUST</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;read the&nbsp;</span><u style=\"color: black;\">entire work order and all provided documentation</u><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">before</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;arriving on-site. All guides and plans&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">MUST</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;be printed and/or available on a laptop or tablet (not a phone) for review onsite.</span></li><li><strong><u>Important:</u></strong>&nbsp;<del>***</del> consists of multiple retailer companies/stores where we are supporting this scope of work, you could be scoped to complete work at a <del>** ***** ********** *********</del>, or other company within the <del>*** </del>umbrella!!!!! Your Workorder will call out what store you are scheduled to be at.</li><li><strong><u>Important:</u></strong>&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">Work TAKES place overnight – YOU WILL GET LOCKED IN ONCE MANAGER LEAVES FOR THE NIGHT!!!</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Techs&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;<u>ARRIVE ONTIME</u> - you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes before the store closes. You MUST arrive on time as you will NOT be able to gain access!!!! (<strong>PENALTIES APPLY</strong>)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>Techs MUST come prepared:</u></strong>&nbsp;bring all tools, food/drinks, medications, device chargers, etc. (anything you might need while working overnight!!!!!)</li><li><strong>Estimated Days to complete Work:&nbsp;</strong>Work is completed over multiple days, typically ranges between 3-5 days, maybe more. Work will most likely be scheduled in consecutive / back-to-back days but there could be gaps between.&nbsp;Every Site is different!!!!!!!</li><li><strong>Estimated Duration (Hours PER Day):</strong>&nbsp;expect 8-10+ Hours a night; there is a good chance you will be onsite past 7am / 8am most nights (some nights may end earlier while others may go longer. In most cases, techs MUST be out prior to store opening.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tech&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;report&nbsp;<strong>ANY/ALL DELAYS</strong>&nbsp;(whether you exceeded the Estimated Hours or not):&nbsp;You&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;report why and who/what caused the delay(s) and for how long.</li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(228, 5, 5);\"><em><u>Important: IF THIS IS YOUR FIRST TIME ASSIGNED TO COMPLETE THIS SCOPE OF WORK FOR <del>*** </del>REMODELS:</u></em></strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>Tech&nbsp;</u>MUS</strong>T&nbsp;<strong>complete</strong>&nbsp;<strong><del>*** ***</del> Frontline Installation Pre-Training Coursework via Moodle</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Training/Coursework takes ~45 Minutes</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Training Coursework&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;be completed at least&nbsp;<strong>2 Days PRIOR</strong>&nbsp;to your first night onsite</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>For Registration &amp; Login Information to complete the course</strong>,&nbsp;<strong>refer to this document&nbsp;</strong>-download to view full document:&nbsp;<strong><del>*** ****************** ********** ***********</del></strong><del>******</del><strong><del>****</del></strong><del>*******</del><del>*****************************************************************************************************************</del></li><li><strong>At the end of every night, your bags will be checked by security before leaving the building!!!!!!!</strong></li><li>This WO only covers ONE visit to site. If a customer requires a return visit, you MUST be assigned another WO by Essintial. Time logged for additional days onsite will be rejected for not following process.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Site Badging / Onsite Access Information:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Government Issued ID</li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">Special SECURITY Access Code&nbsp;</strong>-&nbsp;you will need to provide this upon your arrival to gain access to the store. If you were not provided one, please escalate to Essintial&nbsp;</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Required Tools / Material:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong><del>*** *******</del> - Tool &amp; Material List Document</strong>&nbsp;<strong>Link&nbsp;</strong>(download to view full document):&nbsp;https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdT/6tK9AbDXiMXWQ3ErLSVIvgM6TU7k.3gQB3jSDp6dXR8</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>SCHEDULE:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>Start Times:</strong>&nbsp;Varies, you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes or more prior to store closure.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Techs&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;<u>ARRIVE ONTIME&nbsp;</u>- you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes before the store closes. You MUST arrive on time as you will NOT be able to gain access!!!! (<strong>PENALTIES APPLY</strong>)</li><li><strong>Estimated Duration:&nbsp;Multiple Days&nbsp;</strong>estimated 8-10+ Hours a night - there is a good chance you will be onsite past 7am/8am most nights.</li><li>You will receive pre-calls 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will&nbsp;not&nbsp;be granted.</li><li>You will not be paid for work performed prior to your work order's scheduled start time. Please contact Essintial if the customer is asking you to deviate from this service date or time.</li><li>If you must remove yourself from this project, you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to be&nbsp;<strong>REMOVED&nbsp;</strong>and&nbsp;<strong><em>REMOVE YOURSELF&nbsp;</em></strong>from the work order.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>Important Site Information / Requirements:</em></strong></p><ul><li>You must represent yourself as an Essintial technician on behalf of NCR while on site.</li><li>These are live environments, and technician must act in a professional manner, taking care not to disrupt business.&nbsp;<strong>Be Respectful</strong>&nbsp;and limit any disruptions while on site.</li><li><strong><u>DRESS CODE:</u></strong>&nbsp;Professional appearance is mandatory. Business casual attire required: no T-Shirts, Jeans or holes - A plain collared or button-down shirts, slacks, and nice shoes. (No Jeans, T-Shirts/Hoodies and NO Graphics or HOLES in clothing)</li><li>You are required to be onsite no later than your scheduled time (penalties will be applied if you are late). Please escalate to Essintial Projects @ 855-612-2183</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;<strong><u>Pre-Site Requirements:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong><u>Download and then Print</u>&nbsp;all relevant attachments (guides, checklists, other important tech related documentation) in color to bring to the site.</strong>&nbsp;Please&nbsp;<strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">READ &amp; REVIEW</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;</span>all attachments prior to arriving onsite.&nbsp;<strong><em>Important Note:&nbsp;</em></strong>These Links will take you to / show you a&nbsp;<strong><u>PREVIEW</u></strong>&nbsp;of the document,&nbsp;<strong><em>IT IS VERY IMPORTANT</em></strong>&nbsp;that you&nbsp;<strong><em>DOWNLOAD</em></strong>&nbsp;the files from this view and then&nbsp;<strong>PRINT</strong>&nbsp;(<em>DO NOT PRINT FROM PREVIEW MODE</em>)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">General Project Specific &amp; STORE Specific Onsite Technician Documentation – via SharePoint Folder Link [VERY IMPORTANT]</strong><strong>:</strong>&nbsp;<del>***********************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************************</del></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><del>***</del>_Install Guides</strong>&nbsp;<strong>Link (DO NOT PRINT, JUST DOWNLOAD TO LAPTOP/TABLET as the guide is too large to print):&nbsp;</strong>https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdR/SsXKY4rG0i77fuyiNWtICR2utNJzPdwNCmrjgveVreQ</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><del>*** </del>Remodel - Tool &amp; Material List</strong>&nbsp;<strong>Link</strong>:&nbsp;https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdT/6tK9AbDXiMXWQ3ErLSVIvgM6TU7k.3gQB3jSDp6dXR8</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><del>*** ***</del>_Remodel_MOODLE Coursework Training Link</strong>:&nbsp;https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004hWdS/13XUqDuiwiOPWUoTws4Mopf0J7a9KOE09wftrGrGCM8</li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(234, 8, 8);\"><em><u>Important: IF THIS IS YOUR FIRST TIME ASSIGNED TO COMPLETE THIS SCOPE OF WORK FOR TJX REMODELS:</u></em></strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong><u>Tech&nbsp;</u>MUS</strong>T&nbsp;<strong>complete</strong>&nbsp;<strong><del>*** ***</del> Frontline Installation Pre-Training Coursework via Moodle</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Training/Coursework takes ~45 Minutes</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Training Coursework&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;be completed at least&nbsp;<strong>2 Days PRIOR</strong>&nbsp;to your first night onsite</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>For Registration &amp; Login Information to complete the course</strong>,&nbsp;<strong>refer to this document&nbsp;</strong>-download to view full document:&nbsp;<strong><del>*** ***</del>_Remodel_MOODLE Coursework Training.v1</strong>&nbsp;<strong>Link</strong>:&nbsp;<del>*****************************************************************************************************************</del></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Any Issues, Escalate to Essintial</strong></li><li>Confirm the start date and time. You will receive pre-calls at 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will not be granted.</li><li><strong>Bring the Required Tools &amp; Material with you to the site</strong></li><li><strong>Prior to going Onsite: OBTAIN/VERIFY you received the special SECURITY ACCESS CODE&nbsp;</strong>-&nbsp;you will need to provide this upon your arrival to gain access to the store. If you were not provided one, please escalate to Essintial</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>ARRIVAL:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>CHECK-IN TO YOUR WORK ORDER</strong>&nbsp;- if you are unable to do so then you<strong>&nbsp;MUST</strong>&nbsp;call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.</li><li><strong>CHECK-IN with the Manager On Duty -</strong>&nbsp;Introduce yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of NCR &amp; provide the&nbsp;<strong>SECURITY CODE to gain access</strong></li><li><strong>Check-<em>I</em>n with Essintial Lead Technician</strong></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\"><u>ONSITE:</u>&nbsp;Work with / take direction from the the Essintial LEAD TECHNICIAN while onsite &amp; refer to the Store Specific and General Project Level Technician Documentation to complete the scope of work.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>CLOSING OUT | COMPLETE BEFORE LEAVING SITE:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>Complete Nightly Completion Items</strong>&nbsp;- Refer to the Install Guide for nightly completion items. [I.E. nightly clean up / trash disposals, photos needing captured / provided to the bridge line, check-out requirements.</li><li><strong>Check-Out / Get Released from the site by the Essintial Lead Technician</strong></li><li><strong>Check-Out</strong>&nbsp;with Manager On Duty / Onsite POC</li><li><strong>Call&nbsp;</strong>- Essintial Project Team @&nbsp;855-612-2183&nbsp;opt 2 to perform your final check out</li><li><strong>Check-Out on your WO</strong>&nbsp;- if you are unable to do so then you&nbsp;<strong>MUST&nbsp;</strong>call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.&nbsp;<strong>NOTE</strong>: Your Check In and Check Out times must all match&nbsp;<em>(Work Order Platform and Final Check Out with Essintial)</em></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Closing / Completion Notes:</strong></p><ul><li>Detailed Description of the Work that took Place, including any issues.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>ESCALATION:</u>&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>Support Related / Issues Onsite related to the Scope of Work / Support should be escalated directly to the <del>*** </del>Remote RTC Team via the provided Bridge Line</li><li>All other issues should be escalated directly to the Essintial Project Team @&nbsp;855-612-2183&nbsp;opt 2&nbsp;</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS:</u></strong>&nbsp;Must be able to bend, kneel, stand and lift, carry 50lbs repeatedly for extended periods of time.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>DRESS CODE:&nbsp;</u></strong>Professional appearance is mandatory. Business casual attire required: no T-Shirts, Jeans or holes - A collared or button-down shirts (no t-shirts), slacks, and nice shoes.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:</u></strong></p><ul><li>All expenses such as tolls, parking, materials must be pre-approved and accompanied by a receipt. Reimbursements will not be increased to cover markups of any kind.</li><li>Technicians must contact Essintial for any deviations from the scheduled service date or time. No payment will be granted for work performed prior to the scheduled start time.</li></ul>","markdown":"**No unauthorized persons allowed on site. Any swaps or helpers must be approved by Essintial.**\n\nSOW: Cash office, exterior camera, validation with management present\n\nProcessing / Exterior Scope\n\nInstall/validate .083 Compactor\n\nInstall/validate .086 Loading Dock\n\nInstall/validate .166 IP Speaker\n\nCash Office Verification\n\nVerify Cash Office live-feed monitor\n\nFinal Closeout\n\nFinal CCTV validation with customer\n\nFinal cleanup\n\nCustomer signoff\"\"\n\nAdditional tool: Tech to bring mounting HW\"\n\nSecurity Code: 862384\n\n\\-----------------------------------------------------\n\n**REQUIRED SKILLS:** Mid-Level Low Voltage Cabling, Mid-Level to Advanced Network Technician, Experience with Network & Security/CCTV and Experience installing POS Equipment. Technician MUST be able to run cables neatly through various ceiling types, terminate cables with RJ45 plugs and or Keystone jacks.\n\n**Scope of Work:** Seeking an Assist Technician to complete a Store Remodel at various Retailers. Technicians will be onsite working with LEAD TECHNICIAN to complete Low Voltage Cabling Runs, CCTV Installations (varies by site), POS De-Installations & Re-Installations, TV Installations. (Every Remodel / STORE is slightly Different). Scope of work will take place **Over Multiple** **NIGHTs**. Each Night you will be scoped to complete specific items to stay on task to meet the store's cutover date. Technicians will be taking direction from Lead Technician and working with other assist technicians to complete the scope of work.\n\n**IMPORTANT CALL OUTS:**\n\n- You **MUST** represent yourself as an Essintial Technician on behalf of \\*\\*\\*\n- Technicians **MUST** read the entire work order and all provided documentation **before** arriving on-site. All guides and plans **MUST** be printed and/or available on a laptop or tablet (not a phone) for review onsite.\n- **Important:** \\*\\*\\* consists of multiple retailer companies/stores where we are supporting this scope of work, you could be scoped to complete work at a \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*, or other company within the \\*\\*\\* umbrella!!!!! Your Workorder will call out what store you are scheduled to be at.\n- **Important:** Work TAKES place overnight – YOU WILL GET LOCKED IN ONCE MANAGER LEAVES FOR THE NIGHT!!!\n- Techs **MUST** ARRIVE ONTIME - you will be scheduled to arrive 30 minutes before the store closes. You MUST arrive on time as you will NOT be able to gain access!!!! (**PENALTIES APPLY**)\n- **Techs MUST come prepared:** bring all tools, food/drinks, medications, device chargers, etc. (anything you might need while working overnight!!!!!)\n- **Estimated Days to complete Work:** Work is completed over multiple days, typically ranges between 3-5 days, maybe more. Work will most likely be scheduled in consecutive / back-to-back days but there could be gaps between. Every Site is different!!!!!!!\n- **Estimated Duration (Hours PER Day):** expect 8-10+ Hours a night; there is a good chance you will be onsite past 7am / 8am most nights (some nights may end earlier while others may go longer. In most cases, techs MUST be out prior to store opening.\n- Tech **MUST** report **ANY/ALL DELAYS** (whether you exceeded the Estimated Hours or not): You **MUST** report why and who/what caused the delay(s) and for how long.\n- ***Important: IF THIS IS YOUR FIRST TIME ASSIGNED TO COMPLETE THIS SCOPE OF WORK FOR \\*\\*\\* REMODELS:***\n- **Tech MUS**T **complete** **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* Frontline Installation Pre-Training Coursework via Moodle**\n- Training/Coursework takes ~45 Minutes\n- Training Coursework **MUST** be completed at least **2 Days PRIOR** to your first night onsite\n- **For Registration & Login Information to complete the course**, **refer to this document** -download to view full document: **\\*\\