{"job":{"id":19955708,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"All IT Supported","title":"Rack, TV, Conference Room Config/Setup (EXPERIENCED TECH NEEDED)","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Scope:</strong></p><ul><li>Tech to go onsite to help w/ the rack, TV, and conference room equipment setup/config.</li><li>Collaborate w/ Zazz support contact (check-in/out w/ them).</li><li>Bring a keyboard and mouse; patch cables are available in the IT room.</li><li>Unbox and set up the networking rack in the IT room, including mounting the firewall securely inside the rack.</li><li>Mount the network switch in the rack and uplink it to the firewall.</li><li>Mount/place the four Dell OptiPlex Micro 7020 computers in the rack. Serial numbers: 10W3994, 2XV3994, CBVN894, and D9VN894.</li><li>Connect each Dell computer to the network switch using Ethernet cables and confirm each device is online and receiving LAN connectivity.</li><li>Patch the HDMI balun kits from the four computers to their corresponding conference room TVs.</li><li>Ensure all HDMI baluns are properly powered, connected, and neatly secured, with cabling organized and tidy.</li><li>Confirm that the display output from each computer is successfully showing on its corresponding TV.</li><li>Configure the two ThinkSmart One Pro + IP Controller for Teams systems in the conference rooms.</li><li>Sign in to each Teams room device using the provided VAS-1 and VAS-2 accounts and verify the correct account is assigned to each room.</li><li>Test each conference room system for Teams video calls, including display, camera, microphone, speakers, and overall functionality.</li><li>Verify that all four Dell computers, network equipment, TVs, HDMI baluns, and conference room systems are fully operational.</li><li>Leave the IT room clean and organized, with the rack and cabling neatly arranged.</li><li>Before leaving the site, call (888) 959-0624 and press 1 so the support team can confirm that all relevant equipment is online.</li><li>Post closeout notes with check-in and check-out times on Field Nation after the job completion with the documented photos.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Conference Room Account &amp; Video Call Testing:</strong></p><ul><li>Sign in to the two ThinkSmart One Pro + IP Controller for Teams systems using the assigned accounts.</li><li><strong>Conference Room 1:</strong> VAS-1@vas-us.com</li><li><strong>Conference Room 2:</strong> VAS-2@vas-us.com</li><li>Retrieve the corresponding passwords from the provided OneTimeSecret links.</li><li>Test Teams video calling in each conference room.</li><li>Verify the camera, microphone, speakers, display, and Teams Controller are functioning properly.</li><li>Confirm each device is signed in with the correct account and ready for use.</li><li>Report any login, account, or video conferencing issues before leaving the site.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Tools Needed:</strong></p><ul><li>Laptop</li><li>Keyboard and mouse</li><li>Ethernet patch cables</li><li>Power drill</li><li>Screwdriver set</li><li>Cable tester</li><li>Cable ties/Velcro</li><li>Cable labels</li><li>Step ladder</li><li>HDMI/DisplayPort adapters</li><li>Basic hand tools</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>** REPRESENT ALL I.T. SUPPORTED ON BEHALF OF ZAZZ INC. **</strong></p>","markdown":"**Scope:**\n\n- Tech to go onsite to help w/ the rack, TV, and conference room equipment setup/config.\n- Collaborate w/ Zazz support contact (check-in/out w/ them).\n- Bring a keyboard and mouse; patch cables are available in the IT room.\n- Unbox and set up the networking rack in the IT room, including mounting the firewall securely inside the rack.\n- Mount the network switch in the rack and uplink it to the firewall.\n- Mount/place the four Dell OptiPlex Micro 7020 computers in the rack. Serial numbers: 10W3994, 2XV3994, CBVN894, and D9VN894.\n- Connect each Dell computer to the network switch using Ethernet cables and confirm each device is online and receiving LAN connectivity.\n- Patch the HDMI balun kits from the four computers to their corresponding conference room TVs.\n- Ensure all HDMI baluns are properly powered, connected, and neatly secured, with cabling organized and tidy.\n- Confirm that the display output from each computer is successfully showing on its corresponding TV.\n- Configure the two ThinkSmart One Pro + IP Controller for Teams systems in the conference rooms.\n- Sign in to each Teams room device using the provided VAS-1 and VAS-2 accounts and verify the correct account is assigned to each room.\n- Test each conference room system for Teams video calls, including display, camera, microphone, speakers, and overall functionality.\n- Verify that all four Dell computers, network equipment, TVs, HDMI baluns, and conference room systems are fully operational.\n- Leave the IT room clean and organized, with the rack and cabling neatly arranged.\n- Before leaving the site, call (888) 959-0624 and press 1 so the support team can confirm that all relevant equipment is online.\n- Post closeout notes with check-in and check-out times on Field Nation after the job completion with the documented photos.\n\n**Conference Room Account & Video Call Testing:**\n\n- Sign in to the two ThinkSmart One Pro + IP Controller for Teams systems using the assigned accounts.\n- **Conference Room 1:** VAS-1@vas-us.com\n- **Conference Room 2:** VAS-2@vas-us.com\n- Retrieve the corresponding passwords from the provided OneTimeSecret links.\n- Test Teams video calling in each conference room.\n- Verify the camera, microphone, speakers, display, and Teams Controller are functioning properly.\n- Confirm each device is signed in with the correct account and ready for use.\n- Report any login, account, or video conferencing issues before leaving the site.\n\n**Tools Needed:**\n\n- Laptop\n- Keyboard and mouse\n- Ethernet patch cables\n- Power drill\n- Screwdriver set\n- Cable tester\n- Cable ties/Velcro\n- Cable labels\n- Step ladder\n- HDMI/DisplayPort adapters\n- Basic hand tools\n\n**\\*\\* REPRESENT ALL I.T. SUPPORTED ON BEHALF OF ZAZZ INC. \\*\\***","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-17T10:00","end":"2026-09-17T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":360},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":60,"estLaborHours":6,"distance":70},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"TV\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-17T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T18:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:01:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-22T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-17T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"Danik Furniture"},{"start":"2026-09-21T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-21T14:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T18:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro 