{"job":{"id":"2833980468","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"JTI NETWORK LLC","title":"0015935 - SITE AUDITS - Need experienced FE, NEED CAMERA (SONY, CANNON, ETC.) Follow up support instructions, get all photos, fill up excel","description":"<p><strong>Good, clean and constant communication before the activity and while work on site is essential.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em><u>Note: Field Engineer needs to carry photo identity proof (Driving license or any govt affiliated photo ID).</u></em></strong></p><p>====================================================</p><p><br></p><p><strong>ONLY LEAVE THE SITE AFTER COMPLETING THE TASK.</strong></p><p><br></p><p>Site Audits</p><p><br></p><p>Scope of work:</p><p><br></p><p>Task needs to go smoothly, and the survey data correctly captured first time.</p><p><br></p><p>Need to:</p><p><br></p><p>Need whatsapp as well for communication</p><p>Identify customer rack</p><p>Check if all informations on excel sheet to see if it matches with onsite reality</p><p>Send many pictures with good quality resolution</p><p>Fill up Excel onsite real time with information on each tabs accordingly</p><p>Support needs to review and validate Excel, photos and info provided before you leave - Excel sheet is a must for ticket completion</p><p>Leave site after validation only</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Please can you provide resources for the following site audits:</p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Please find attached the runbook outlining the site audit requirements, along with the survey documents. - This will be attached on order</p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>It is critical that the assigned engineers strictly follow the additional processes and quality checks that have been put in place. We need to ensure all data is captured accurately and that every deliverable is completed 100% successfully before leaving site.</p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>We cannot afford any errors or missed information on these audits, as any slip-ups will greatly impact our future on this project.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Chapter 3.1 – Project Scope:</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Site Assessment (Site Survey)</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>The outputs of the site audit will include the following and be accompanied by site photographs:</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>§ Network Room Audit</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>- Rack Location Audit:</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>o Utilize provided excel template to confirm and update rack elevation of equipment in network equipment rooms (NER)</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>o Document equipment and power cords associated by outlet, PDU, or UPS receptacle.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>o Provide list of equipment, equipment names, and asset ID in spreadsheet.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>o Photograph rack front and rear</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>- Cable Audit:</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>o Document number of horizontal cables terminated at each patch panel</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>o Provide cable sheath identifiers and descriptions (category, shielded, color)</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>o Photograph horizontal cabling routing in equipment room</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>o Riser Backbone</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>o Create line drawing of riser backbone diagram</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>o Identify all riser backbone cabling routing between equipment rooms and to minimum point of entry (MPOE).</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>o Photograph terminations and labeling on each end of backbone cabling</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>o Service Provider Connection</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>o Document service provider connection location</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>o Identify the number of service providers present at MPOE</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>o Provide distance estimation from service provider MPOE and nearest NVIDIA equipment room</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>o Grounding</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>o Review grounding connections</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>o Verify all equipment and racks are connected to grounded</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>§ Power Audit</p><p><br></p><p>- NER Power Feed</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>o Document power receptacles in equipment rooms</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>o Identify PDU and UPS connections to power.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>o Document panels feeding equipment rooms including circuit identification</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>o Review available building power and determine if additional power can be added for network equipment rooms</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>- Power Distribution Units</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>o Document PDU inlet and outlet feeds</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>o Provide mean power draw on smart PDUs over 7 days</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>- UPS</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>o Document UPS inlet and outlet feeds</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>o Survey load balance</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>o Identify remaining capacity on each UPS</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>§ Cooling Audit</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>o NER Cooling</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>o Document cooling units for network equipment rooms.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>o Identify current and maximum cooling capacity for rooms.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>o Provide photo documentation of cooling units and leak/condensation drainage</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>§ Final Report for each site</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>- Format</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>o Naming convention for all files will be as follows: MMYYYY_NVIDIA-SITE NAME_FILE NAME-Vx</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>o MMYYYY is month in two numbers format followed by year</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>o SITE NAME is the name of the location of site</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>o FILE NAME is unique based on file</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>o Vx is the version</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>- Site Photos</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>o Photo of the room</p><p><br></p><p>o Top of the rack,</p><p><br></p><p>o Middle of the rack</p><p><br></p><p>o Bottom of the rack</p><p><br></p><p>o Front and Back of the rack</p><p><br></p><p>o PDU’s</p><p><br></p><p>o UPS’</p><p><br></p><p>o Cooling units and leak/condensation drainage</p><p><br></p><p>o Horizontal cabling routing in equipment room</p><p><br></p><p>o Terminations and labeling on each end of backbone cabling</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Engineer should have below tools:</strong></p><p>- Windows Laptop</p><p>- Working Console Cable and USB x Serial converter</p><p>- Working Ethernet / Rj45 port in Laptop</p><p>- Own internet - Putty / Team viewer / MS teams</p><p>- WhatsApp application</p><p>- Basic toolkit</p><p>- Own pendrive</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>=====================================================</p><p>&nbsp;<strong>This is all that you need to bring with you for the activity</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>1- Laptop;</p><p>1.0- Laptop with charger (should be fully charged);</p><p>1.1- Windows OS installed laptop ( No MacBook );</p><p>1.2- Some activities need to perform some tests on the equipment or link and it is necessary to turn off Anti-virus and Firewall from the laptop, make sure that your laptop can accomplish this. Note: Some company laptop does not allow it.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>2- Mobile phone;</p><p>2.1-&nbsp;Mobile phone with charger (should be fully charged) and take pictures with good resolution;</p><p>2.2-&nbsp;Mobile data connection (3G or 4G) on the mobile phone and share the connection to the laptop</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>3- Console Cable and USB x Serial converter;</p><p>- HDE USB to Serial Interface Cable with Serial to RJ45 Console Adapter Cable for Cisco Routers.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>4- Cables Straight RJ45 - CAT5</p><p>5- USB Pendrive (minimum 8GB);</p><p>6- Kit Screw Driver and Philips;</p><p>7- Labelling machine;</p><p>8- Headset.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>The technician needs to have WhatsApp application installed on his smartphone. If no, please install, we use this to facilitate the communication. - It's free to download&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.whatsapp.com/download/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://www.whatsapp.com/download/</a></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>PLEASE, DURING THE TASK KEEP YOUR CELL PHONE CLOSE TO YOU IN CASE WE NEED TO CALL OR TEXT YOU, TO KNOW ABOUT THE TASK STATUS.</p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-17T09:00","end":"2026-09-17T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":40,"max":160},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":40,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":12.4},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $160 (countered: $260) is below minimum threshold $400"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-17T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T18:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:01:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-22T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-17T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"Danik Furniture"},{"start":"2026-09-21T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-21T14:01:00.000