{"job":{"id":"3354542418","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"MG21 Gateway SIM Swap & Connection Verification","description":"Hilton SIM Swap SOW<br><br>Required Materials:<br>Laptop w/ Admin Rights and Ethernet Port<br>RJ45-RJ45 Ethernet Cable<br><br>Required Deliverables:<br>NEW SIM Number<br>MG21 with visible Purple status light<br>MG21 before and after pictures<br><br>SIM Card UPS Tracking: TBD<br><br>Please review the SIM Installation section of the attached PDF prior to dispatch.<br><br>Technician must be able to access and actively use Microsoft Teams, including Teams chat, for communication, coordination, and support during the installation<br>Upon arrival, the Granite Technician checks in with the Front Desk and asks for the Granite package containing the SIM card<br>For any access issues, please reach out to the Granite PM Jonathon at (401) 955-9477<br><br>When you have the SIM and locate the MG21, please call into the below bridge to work with Granite technical support:<br><br>Dial-In: +1 929-229-2436<br>Passcode: 355013377#<br><br>General Directions:<br>Validate the existing MG21 Gateway is fully operational with the local manager<br>Power down the existing MG21 Gateway<br>Record the serial number for Hilton Worldwide records<br>Disconnect the MG from power<br>Remove the existing SIM by unscrewing the back panel<br>Insert the new SIM and replace the back plate<br>Power on the unit and confirm a solid purple LED indicating proper configuration, active SIM, and cellular connectivity<br>If status light remains Amber (Orange): utilize laptop, console cable, and mobile phone for any required Hilton Worldwide APN configuration (see steps below)<br>Verify the MG21 router is online and all network services are operational<br>Before leaving site, confirm system functionality with the technical coordinator on the Teams meeting<br>Record the store manager’s name as confirmation of successful SIM migration<br><br>How to Manually Change APN<br><br>Step 1 — Physically Connect to the MG<br>Power on the Meraki MG.<br>Connect your laptop directly to the MG LAN port using an Ethernet cable.<br>Wait about 1–2 minutes for your computer to receive an IP address automatically via DHCP.<br><br>Step 2 — Open the Local Status Page (may need to use an incognito browser window)<br>Open a web browser and go to: mg.meraki.com  <br>If that does not work, try:<br>• setup.meraki.com<br>• my.meraki.com<br>If that still does not work, try:<br>Open the Command Prompt and perform an IPCONFIG<br>Get the Gateway IP<br>Copy or Type the Gateway IP in the Web Browser tab<br>Click Enter<br><br>Step 3 — Log Into the MG<br>For newer firmware:<br>Username: admin<br>Password:  (please include the dashes)<br>The serial number is located on the sticker on the bottom or back of the MG.<br><br>Step 4 — Navigate to the Configure Page<br>Select the Configure tab.<br>Locate the Bearer Settings or Cellular Configuration section.<br><br>Step 5 — Override the SIM APN Settings<br>Find the option labeled Cellular Override or Override SIM Settings.<br>Enable Override SIM Settings to manually configure the APN.<br>Step 6 — Enter the APN<br>In the APN field, enter: wbdata<br><br>Step 6: Leave Username and Password blank unless your carrier specifically requires them.<br>Example:<br>APN: wbdata<br>Username: blank<br>Password: blank<br> <br>Step 7 — Confirm/update the next fields<br>Cellular authorization:  None<br>Cellular IP type:  IPv4v6<br> <br>Step 8 — Save the Configuration<br>Scroll to the bottom of the page.<br>Click Save.<br>The MG may briefly reconnect to the cellular network while applying the new APN.<br><br>Step 9 — Verify Connectivity<br>Go to the Connection or Cellular Status page and verify:<br>Carrier is detected<br>APN shows wbdata<br>Signal strength is present<br>Internet connectivity is connected<br>Meraki cloud connectivity is connected<br><br>Troubleshooting<br>Cannot Reach mg.meraki.com:<br>Disconnect and reconnect Ethernet<br>Use another browser<br>Try incognito browser<br>Confirm Wi-Fi is off<br>Browse directly to the MG gateway IP<br>Try setup.meraki.com<br><br>APN Does Not Save:<br>Ensure you clicked Save<br>Reboot the MG<br>Recheck the APN spelling: wbdata<br><br>No Cellular Connectivity:<br>Verify SIM card is active<br>Verify SIM is fully inserted<br>Confirm carrier supports the device<br>Confirm APN is correct<br>Verify signal strength is adequate<br><br>Optional — Factory Reset<br>Press and hold the Reset button for at least 10 seconds.<br>Allow 5–10 minutes for reboot and reconfiguration.<br>Factory reset clears Local Status Page settings including APN configuration.<br><br>Document and provide any returned equipment to the hotel MOD","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-29T10:45","end":"2026-09-29T12:15"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":75},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":1.5,"distance":5.7},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $75 (countered: $98) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-21T14:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T18:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14: