hese Terms &amp; Conditions.</span></li></ul>","markdown":"**Scope of Work**We are seeking a reliable and professional technician to complete a retail display/fixture relocation (same store relocation) at a national retail location.\n\n**MUST SUBMIT DOCUMENTATION THAT INCLUDES PICTURES THROUGH FILLOUT PLATFORM (LINK BELOW) TO RECEIVE PAYMENT**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*LINK IS BELOW WITH PASSWORD SENT UPON ACCEPTANCE\\*\\*\\***\n\n<https://form.fillout.com/t/rFD1NDZJkSus>\n\n**Estimated Time on Site**Approximately **45–60 minutes**, depending on the store layout and display location.\n\nThe selected technician will be responsible for transporting the display from one location inside the store to another location (as deemed by store management) leaving the work areas clean and professional.\n\n- Check in with store management upon arrival.\n- Locate the display(s) needing to be relocated\n- Inspect the display for any visible damage.\n- Transport the display safely to the new approved sales floor location.\n- Position and level the display according to store management's direction.\n- Install any required display components or signage, if applicable.\n- Take required before-and-after photographs.\n- Complete the required digital completion report before leaving the site.\n\n**Professionalism & Appearance**- Maintain a clean, neat, and professional appearance.\n- Wear a plain collared shirt (no offensive language, graphics, or competitor branding), long pants or clean work shorts, and closed-toe shoes.\n- Follow all retailer policies and directions provided by store management.\n- Maintain a clean and organized work area throughout the installation and remove all installation debris before leaving.\n- Use professional language and conduct yourself in a professional manner\n\n**Technician Requirements**- Be professional and customer-focused.\n- Must be able to lift up to 50lbs and maneuver in tight spaces.\n- Be comfortable working inside retail environments during business hours.\n- Be able to safely move retail display fixtures using store-provided equipment when available.\n- Have a smartphone capable of submitting photos and electronic documentation.\n- Have basic hand tools, including a utility knife.\n\n**What You'll Need**- Smartphone with camera\n- Utility knife\n- Closed-toe shoes\n- Ability to safely operate a pallet jack\n\n**Completion Requirements**To receive payment, technicians must:\n\n- Complete all assigned work.\n- Submit all required photographs.\n- Complete the digital work order on platform \\*\\*Relocation reporting application will be sent upon acceptance\\*\\*\n\n**Important Information**- Work must be completed during the scheduled service window.\n- Displays must be relocated only in the location approved by store management.\n- The work area must be left clean and free of all installation materials.\n- Professional appearance and communication are expected at all times.\n\n**\\*\\*\\* Relocation Guide will be sent upon acceptance showing step-by-step instructions \\*\\*\\***\n\n**MUST SUBMIT DOCUMENTATION THAT INCLUDES PICTURES THROUGH FILLOUT PLATFORM (LINK BELOW) TO RECEIVE PAYMENT**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*LINK IS BELOW WITH PASSWORD SENT UPON ACCEPTANCE\\*\\*\\***\n\n<https://form.fillout.com/t/rFD1NDZJkSus>\n\n**\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_**\n\n  \n**POLICIES AND PROCEDURES****1. Work Order Terms & Conditions**By accepting and performing this work order, you (\"Producer\") acknowledge and agree to the following:\n\nProducer acknowledges they are an independent Producer and not an employee of Finish Line Services LLC. The Producer is solely responsible for all applicable taxes, insurance, licenses, permits, and legal obligations associated with their business.\n\n**2. Responsibility for Safe Work Practices**Producer agrees to perform all work in a safe and professional manner and in accordance with all applicable federal, state, local, retailer, and customer safety requirements. Producer shall immediately stop work if unsafe conditions exist and promptly notify Finish Line Services LLC.\n\n**3. Assumption of Risk**The producer voluntarily assumes all risks associated with performing the work described in this work order, including travel to and from the work location and any activities necessary to complete the assignment. By accepting this work order, Producer acknowledges that Finish Line Services LLC and its client shall not be liable for any injury, loss, damage, or claim arising from the performance of the work, except as required by applicable law.\n\n**4. Equipment**Producer is responsible for providing and maintaining all required tools, equipment, personal protective equipment (PPE), and transportation unless specifically stated otherwise within the work order.\n\n**5. Property Damage**The Producer is responsible for exercising reasonable care while performing services. Any accidental damage to customer property, merchandise, fixtures, equipment, or facilities falls under Producers \"Assumption Of Risk\" (3) and must be reported to Finish Line Services LLC.\n\n**6. Compliance with Customer Requirements**Producer agrees to comply with all customer site rules, store policies, check-in procedures, and instructions provided by authorized customer representatives.\n\n**7. Photographs & Documentation**Producer agrees to accurately complete all required documentation, photographs, signatures, and reporting before submitting this work order. Submission of false, incomplete, misleading, or altered information may result in non-payment and removal from future assignments.\n\n**8. Payment**Payment is contingent upon:\n\n- Successful completion of the assigned scope of work.\n- Submission of all required documentation.\n- Compliance with these Terms & Conditions.\n\n**9. Changes to Scope**Producer shall not perform additional work outside the authorized scope of work from posting without prior approval from Finish Line Services LLC.\n\n**10. Confidentiality**Producer agrees not to disclose customer information, pricing, internal procedures, photographs, or proprietary information obtained during the course of the assignment.\n\n**11. Insurance**Producer represents that they maintain any insurance required by applicable law or by their Producer agreement and accepts responsibility for losses arising from their own acts or omissions to the extent permitted by law.\n\n**12. No Employment Relationship**Acceptance of this work order does not create an employment relationship, partnership, joint venture, or agency relationship between Producer and Finish Line Services LLC.\n\n**13. Limitation of Liability**To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, Finish Line Services LLC shall not be liable for indirect, incidental, consequential, special, or punitive damages arising from or related to the performance of this work order. Nothing in these terms limits liability where such limitation is prohibited by law.\n\n**14. Indemnification**To the extent permitted by applicable law, Producer agrees to defend, indemnify, and hold harmless Finish Line Services LLC and its officers, employees, and clients from claims, damages, liabilities, costs, and expenses arising out of Producer's negligent acts, omissions, or breach of these Terms & Conditions.\n\n**15. Acknowledgement**By accepting this work order, completing this work order, and submitting the completion report, Producer certifies that:\n\n- They have personally completed the work described.\n- All information submitted is true and accurate.\n- All required photographs accurately depict the completed work.\n- They have read and agree to these Terms & Conditions.","actions":[]},