{"job":{"id":19957366,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"VEHTECH, INC","title":"TECH NEEDED TO REPAIR REFRIGERATOR ","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Need technician to repair&nbsp;a REFRIGERATOR.</u> </strong></p><ol><li><strong>SPECIFICS WILL BE IN THE PRODUCT DESCRIPTION. PLEASE INSTALL THE PARTS ON SITE DOCUMENT COMPLETED WORK WITH PICTURES AND NOTES FOR COMPLETE PAYMENT APPROVAL.</strong></li><li><strong>TECHNICIAN MUST INSTALL ALL PARTS ON SITE SHIPPED BY VENDOR.</strong></li><li><strong> <u>TAKE PICS OF SITE BEFORE AND AFTER WORK PERFORMED.</u>.</strong></li><li><strong> <u>MUST HAVE CUSTOMER SIGN OFF ON WORK ORDER SIGN OFF SHEET LOCATED IN DELIVERABLES. TAKE PICS OF UNIT BEFORE AND AFTER AND WORK SPACE. SIGN OFF SHEET MUST BE SIGNED AND COMPLETED BEFORE WORK ORDER IS APPROVED FOR PAYMENT.</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>PARTS ARE ONSITE AT CUSTOMERS HOME IN PACKAGE WITH CUSTOMERS INFORMATION INCLUDING THE PARTS LISTS.</u></strong></li><li><strong><em>MUST REPRESENT YOURSELF AS A VEHTECH, INC. TECHNICIAN. CALL AND INTRODUCE YOURSELF AS A VEHTECH TECHNICIAN CONFIRM THE APPOINTMENT TIME AND DATE. ESPECIALLY IF YOU HAVE REQUESTED TO COUNTER WITH A DIFFERENT DATE. THIS IS MANDATORY AS PART OF YOUR CHECK IN TASK.</em></strong></li><li><strong><em>Technicians please check in via ext 1005, with your check in time and check out time. If I am unavailable leave me a voicemail with your check in and check out time and any other pertinent information related to your work order. I will return your voicemail at my earliest convenience. If the work order is completed over the weekend you will be contacted on the next business day. </em></strong><em><u>Please be sure to take all parts with you the customer is not responsible for returning the parts it is part of your work order completion to receive payment approval NO EXCEPTIONS.</u></em></li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong><em>﻿</em></strong></p><p>B<strong>rand:WHIRLPOOL</strong></p><p><strong>Product:</strong>Refrigerator</p><p><strong>Model No.:</strong>WRX735SDH04</p><p><strong>PROBLEM DESCRIPTION:</strong>ICEMAKER NOT MAKING ICE </p><p><strong>PARTS SENT:</strong>Part Number: WPW10300024 Part Description: ICE MAKER ASSEMBLY Quantity: 1 If used during repair, requires return: No Tracking Number: 383473857859 Shipping Provider: FedEx 1 If used during repair, requires return:. Only replace parts needed for the repair. 2. Diagnose issue &amp; if parts sent don''t resolve the issue, please put the original parts back in the unit and back in original condition. 3. Take all parts sent to the customer with you upon leaving. Do not leave ANYTHING with the customer.</p><p><strong> <u>IF THE PARTS ARE NOT ON SITE PLEASE RUN THE CALL AS A TROUBLE SHOOTING AND DIAGNOSTICS. TAKE PICS OF THE MODEL AND SERIAL AND WRITE A SUMMARY OF THE PROBLEM DESCRIPTION AND THE POSSIBLE PARTS NEEDED TO REPAIR THE UNIT. </u></strong></p><p><strong>PICTURES</strong>: <strong>TAKE PICTURES OF THE HOUSE, AND THE UNIT IN THIS INSTANCE FOR VERIFICATION OF YOUR ARRIVAL AND DEPARTURE.</strong></p><p>Effective today July 20, 2021 new policy mandatory for all Vehtechnology technicians. Technicians must call the customer one hour before arriving on site, this is and has always been our policy. If you arrive at a customer's home and did not provide a courtesy call before arriving and the customer is not home you WILL NOT BE PAID FOR TRAVEL for this ticket. If you have an instance where you have contacted the customer and no response immediately contact myself or Vincent via text message or phone call, no exceptions.</p><p><br></p><ul><li><strong>TAKE PICTURES OF THE UNIT BEFORE THE REPAIRS AND AFTER TO COVER YOURSELF AND THE COMPANY FROM ANY LIABILITY!</strong></li><li><strong>PLEASE PRESENT YOURSELF AS A VEHTECH,INC REP. &amp; PLEASE PRESENT YOURSELF IN&nbsp;A PROFESSIONAL MANNER.</strong></li><li>&nbsp;<strong>CALL 770-788-2032 - UPON SITE Arrival for check in.</strong>&nbsp;IF unavailable leave check in time and check out time on voicemail.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>&nbsp;<strong>Failure to comply with these procedures will inhibit or void payment.</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>TAKE PARTS WITH YOU MUST BE RETURNED TO VEHTECH.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li><strong>&nbsp;cores/ parts must be returned to VEHTECH, INC before assignments are paid.</strong></li><li><strong>&nbsp;VEHTECH, INC. requires detailed work descriptions for the scope of work performed during repairs.</strong></li><li><strong>Please include the following : Before and After pictures of the unit showing findings as related to problem description.</strong></li><li><strong>Pictures of the Serial #, Model #, as well as any parts that need replacing include the part numbers as well. </strong></li><li><strong>Upload these findings at once after completing the assignment.</strong></li></ul><p><strong>REQUIRED TOOLS/ITEMS:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>TAKE PICTURES OF THE UNIT BEFORE THE REPAIRS AND AFTER TO COVER YOURSELF AND THE COMPANY FROM ANY LIABILITY!</strong></li><li><strong>PLEASE PRESENT YOURSELF AS A VEHTECH,INC REP. &amp; PLEASE PRESENT YOURSELF IN&nbsp;A PROFESSIONAL MANNER.</strong></li><li>&nbsp;<strong>CALL 770-788-2032 - UPON SITE Arrival for check in.</strong>&nbsp;IF unavailable leave check in time and check out time on voicemail.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>&nbsp;<strong>Failure to comply with these procedures will inhibit or void payment.</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>TAKE PARTS WITH YOU MUST BE RETURNED TO VEHTECH.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li><strong>&nbsp;cores/ parts must be returned to VEHTECH, INC before assignments are paid.</strong></li><li><strong>&nbsp;VEHTECH, INC. requires detailed work descriptions for the scope of work performed during repairs.</strong></li><li><strong>Please include the following : Before and After pictures of the unit showing findings as related to problem description.</strong></li><li><strong>Pictures of the Serial #, Model #, as well as any parts that need replacing include the part numbers as well. </strong></li><li><strong>Upload these findings at once after completing the assignment.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>REQUIRED TOOLS/ITEMS:</strong></li><li><strong>Multimeter </strong>($30–40): Use a multimeter to diagnose and troubleshoot an appliance’s electrical issues by measuring voltage, current, and resistance.</li><li><strong>Cordless electric drill</strong> ($20–80): Keep a portable drill to make disassembling and reassembling appliance parts easy.</li><li><strong>Rubber mallet </strong>($4–10): Unlike a hammer, a rubber mallet can deliver force without damaging surfaces—and that’s useful for adjusting or seating appliance components.</li><li><strong>Putty knife</strong> ($4–10): Use these knives to scrape residue, apply filler, or remove appliance components.</li><li><strong>Wire cutters</strong> ($20–50):<strong> </strong>When repairing or replacing electrical components, you’ll need to cut wires or small pins with a strong 