{"job":{"id":19957552,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Velocity Tech Solutions","title":"Remote Hands - Connect AT&T broadband circuit","description":{"html":"<p><strong><em><u>PLEASE NOTE THAT YOU ARE TO REPRESENT VTS AT ALL TIMES WHILE ONSITE.</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><u>Overview: </u></strong></p><p>Connect the newly installed AT&amp;T broad band circuit to the Fortinet firewall.&nbsp;The circuit will connect to port WAN2.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>1. Scope of Work</strong></p><p>The technician is responsible for performing onsite work as outlined below. All steps must be completed in the order listed unless otherwise directed by Support or the Work Order Manager.</p><p><strong>Task Sequence:</strong></p><ol><li>Confirm scheduled work 24 hours prior and again 1 hour prior to site arrival.</li><li>Upon arrival, call or text the Work Order Manager to check in.</li><li>Make contact with the Local Contact and confirm site access and work area.</li><li>Locate required parts and equipment as outlined in the work order.</li><li>Take BEFORE photos of all work areas and existing equipment.</li><li>Check in with IT Support prior to making any changes or beginning installation work.</li><li>Complete the work as specified in the work order or project documentation.</li><li>Take AFTER photos of completed work.</li><li>Test and verify functionality with IT Support (checkout process).</li><li>Clean up all work areas and ensure no debris or packaging remains.</li><li>Enter detailed closeout notes describing all work performed, issues encountered, and resolutions.</li><li>Upload and attach all required photo deliverables (BEFORE, AFTER, and any additional requested photos).</li><li>Checkout with Work Order Manager before leaving the site.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong>2. Tools and Equipment Required</strong></p><ul><li>Laptop</li><li>Console cables</li><li>Mobile hotspot or other internet connectivity</li><li>Basic networking tools (punchdown tool, crimper, etc.)</li><li>Basic hand tools (screwdrivers, pliers, etc.)</li><li>Ladder (as needed for access)</li><li>Cable tester</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>3. Deliverables Required</strong></p><ul><li>BEFORE photos of all work areas</li><li>AFTER photos of all completed work</li><li>Any additional photos specifically requested by the Work Order Manager, Client, or IT Support</li><li>Detailed closeout notes summarizing work performed, testing results, and any deviations</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>4. Acceptance Criteria</strong></p><ul><li>All steps in the Scope of Work have been completed.</li><li>IT Support confirms functionality and successful testing.</li><li>All required photo deliverables and closeout notes are submitted.</li><li>The Work Order Manager provides final checkout approval.</li></ul>","markdown":"***PLEASE NOTE THAT YOU ARE TO REPRESENT VTS AT ALL TIMES WHILE ONSITE.***\n\n**Overview:**\n\nConnect the newly installed AT&T broad band circuit to the Fortinet firewall. The circuit will connect to port WAN2.\n\n**1. Scope of Work**\n\nThe technician is responsible for performing onsite work as outlined below. All steps must be completed in the order listed unless otherwise directed by Support or the Work Order Manager.\n\n**Task Sequence:**\n\n1. Confirm scheduled work 24 hours prior and again 1 hour prior to site arrival.\n2. Upon arrival, call or text the Work Order Manager to check in.\n3. Make contact with the Local Contact and confirm site access and work area.\n4. Locate required parts and equipment as outlined in the work order.\n5. Take BEFORE photos of all work areas and existing equipment.\n6. Check in with IT Support prior to making any changes or beginning installation work.\n7. Complete the work as specified in the work order or project documentation.\n8. Take AFTER photos of completed work.\n9. Test and verify functionality with IT Support (checkout process).\n10. Clean up all work areas and ensure no debris or packaging remains.\n11. Enter detailed closeout notes describing all work performed, issues encountered, and resolutions.\n12. Upload and attach all required photo deliverables (BEFORE, AFTER, and any additional requested photos).\n13. Checkout with Work Order Manager before leaving the site.\n\n**2. Tools and Equipment Required**\n\n- Laptop\n- Console cables\n- Mobile hotspot or other internet connectivity\n- Basic networking tools (punchdown tool, crimper, etc.)\n- Basic hand tools (screwdrivers, pliers, etc.)\n- Ladder (as needed for access)\n- Cable tester\n\n**3. Deliverables Required**\n\n- BEFORE photos of all work areas\n- AFTER photos of all completed work\n- Any additional photos specifically requested by the Work Order Manager, Client, or IT Support\n- Detailed closeout notes summarizing work performed, testing results, and any deviations\n\n**4. Acceptance Criteria**\n\n- All steps in the Scope of Work have been completed.\n- IT Support confirms functionality and successful testing.\n- All required photo deliverables and closeout notes are submitted.\n- The Work Order Manager provides final checkout approval.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-18T09:00","end":"2026-09-18T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":90,"max":180},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":90},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":45}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":5},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $180 is below minimum threshold $400"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:01:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-22T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-22T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T00:0