ary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789492955176}
{"job":{"id":19949863,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"PurTeraIT","title":"Rally Bar Install ","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Scope Of Work:</u></strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>1. Verify the installation location, mounting position, wall condition, and availability of the required power,&nbsp;</p>\n<p>network, HDMI, and USB connections.</p>\n<p>2. Unbox and inspect the Poly Studio X52, Poly TC10, wall-mount kit, and associated customer provided&nbsp;</p>\n<p>components.</p>\n<p>3. Install the Poly Studio X52 wall-mount bracket at the customer-approved location.</p>\n<p>4. Mount and secure Poly Studio X52.</p>\n<p>5. Position and connect the Poly TC10 touch controller at the customer designated location.</p>\n<p>6. Connect Studio X52 and TC10 to the existing power, network, display, HDMI, USB, and other required&nbsp;</p>\n<p>connections.</p>\n<p>7. Dress and organize exposed cabling using the existing cable pathways and available cablemanagement provisions.</p>\n<p>8. Power on the equipment and verify normal device operation.</p>\n<p>9. Install applicable firmware updates.</p>\n<p>10. Configure and enroll the system as a Zoom Room using customer-provided licensing, credentials, and&nbsp;</p>\n<p>administrative access.</p>\n<p>11. Coordinate with the customer’s remote technical contact for validation and troubleshooting support.</p>\n<p>12. Test the camera, microphones, speakers, touch controller, content-sharing functionality, and display&nbsp;</p>\n<p>output.</p>\n<p>13. Complete a Zoom test call to validate audio and video functionality.</p>\n<p>14. Record installed equipment serial numbers and document any installation exceptions.</p>\n<p>15. Clean the immediate work area and place packaging materials in a designated onsite disposal location.</p>\n<p><br /></p>","markdown":"**Scope Of Work:**\n\n1\\. Verify the installation location, mounting position, wall condition, and availability of the required power,\n\nnetwork, HDMI, and USB connections.\n\n2\\. Unbox and inspect the Poly Studio X52, Poly TC10, wall-mount kit, and associated customer provided\n\ncomponents.\n\n3\\. Install the Poly Studio X52 wall-mount bracket at the customer-approved location.\n\n4\\. Mount and secure Poly Studio X52.\n\n5\\. Position and connect the Poly TC10 touch controller at the customer designated location.\n\n6\\. Connect Studio X52 and TC10 to the existing power, network, display, HDMI, USB, and other required\n\nconnections.\n\n7\\. Dress and organize exposed cabling using the existing cable pathways and available cablemanagement provisions.\n\n8\\. Power on the equipment and verify normal device operation.\n\n9\\. Install applicable firmware updates.\n\n10\\. Configure and enroll the system as a Zoom Room using customer-provided licensing, credentials, and\n\nadministrative access.\n\n11\\. Coordinate with the customer’s remote technical contact for validation and troubleshooting support.\n\n12\\. Test the camera, microphones, speakers, touch controller, content-sharing functionality, and display\n\noutput.\n\n13\\. Complete a Zoom test call to validate audio and video functionality.\n\n14\\. Record installed equipment serial numbers and document any installation exceptions.\n\n15\\. Clean the immediate work area and place packaging materials in a designated onsite disposal location.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-22T09:00","end":"2026-09-22T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":300,"max":300},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":6,"distance":13},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $300 is below minimum threshold $400"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789493729047}
