{"job":{"id":19958587,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Zayo Group","title":"Network Equipment and Cable Troubleshooting / Repair - Work with NOC","description":{"html":"<p><strong><em>NOTE: If travel/gas is required, it must be requested as a counter-offer BEFORE the ticket is assigned. Any requests made after ticket assignment may be denied.</em></strong></p><p><strong>DISPATCH OVERVIEW</strong></p><p>The objective of this dispatch is to perform onsite troubleshooting of the site’s WattBox, network equipment (CradlePoint and/or VeloCloud), and associated cabling. The technician is responsible for identifying and addressing the root cause of the issue in order to restore full network connectivity.</p><p>Please follow the troubleshooting steps outlined below in coordination with the NOC. The technician is expected to assist in diagnosing the issue and work with the NOC to confirm that connectivity has been successfully restored before leaving the site. Additional troubleshooting and/or repair steps may be requested by the NOC analyst during the dispatch, in addition to what is listed below.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>See \"Confidential Information\" section for device specific troubleshooting steps (if needed).</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Site Specific Information</strong></p><p>Ticket (INC) Reference Number (Number for tech to reference when calling into the NOC): INC1800465<br/><br/><br/>Equipment to Troubleshoot (make and model of equipment to ensure tech brings proper console cables if/when they are needed) and Port Assignments (if possible):<br/>Velocloud GE1<br/>Spectrum modem<br/><br/>ISP (Internet Service Provider) Name and Equipment (make/model):<br/>Spectrum modem located in the back room<br/>Modem MAC 3C2D9E97FE8C<br/><br/>Special Tools and/or Materials Required (other than what is listed in the tech minimum tool list - if not needed, leave blank):<br/>230ft cable<br/><br/>Tracking Number of Equipment Sent To Site (If not available or needed, leave blank):<br/><br/><br/>Special Tech Instructions (access requirements, etc. - if not needed, leave blank):<br/>Tech will do a cable run of 230ft between Spectrum modem to Velocloud.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Site Check-In and Initial Activities</strong></p><p><strong>-1-</strong> Upon arrival, call and check in with the NOC to review and confirm the scope of work to be performed before beginning any tasks.</p><p>--- NOC Phone Number: <del>**************</del></p><p><strong>-2-</strong> Check in with the site contact or manager (refer to the custom field “Site Contact Name &amp; Number” for contact information)</p><p><strong>-3-</strong> Capture all required before pictures as outlined in the photo documentation list below.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Cable Inspection, Testing, and Replacement</strong></p><p>The technician shall perform inspections and testing on any necessary patch cords (between networking equipment) and/or demarcation extensions. All findings, including any cable replacements, must be relayed to the assigned NOC analyst.</p><p><strong>-1-</strong> Visually inspect all cabling between the network equipment. Document any issues (damaged cable or MOD ends, broken clips, etc.)</p><p><strong>-2-</strong> Test any suspect cables and document the results</p><p><strong>-3-</strong> Replace any faulty cables that are identified and confirm functionality with the NOC analyst</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Network Equipment Power Inspection</strong></p><p>The technician shall perform an initial power inspection of all onsite network equipment, including but not limited to routers, switches, Cradlepoints, VeloCloud devices, and ISP-provided modems.</p><p><strong>-1-</strong> Inspect all power outlets / strips for signs of failure or loose power cords</p><p><strong>-2-</strong> Inspect any UPSs (uninterrupted power supplies or battery back-ups) for any signs of failure or loose power cords</p><p><strong>-3-</strong> Check for tripped circuit breakers - switch back on if they have been tripped</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Device Reboots and Link (Status) Light Verification on Network Equipment</strong></p><p>The technician shall perform a controlled reboot on all network equipment in coordination with the NOC analyst.</p><p><strong>-1-</strong> Reboot network devices one at a time to minimize disruption as directed by the NOC (Do NOT reboot any equipment without NOC approval first)</p><p><strong>-2-</strong> Document any observed changes in network behavior and/or status light indicators during and after each reboot</p><p><strong>-3-</strong> Collaborate with the NOC analyst to identify any ports that should display a green (active/good) status indicator but instead show red (fault/bad) or no status light at all</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Connectivity Testing</strong></p><p>The technician shall perform connectivity testing as directed by the NOC once all other steps have been completed and devices confirmed up.</p><p><strong>-1-</strong> Attempt to access an external website (such as google.com, yahoo.com, etc.) and document results</p><p><strong>-2-</strong> Perform a speed test (using google or speedtest.net) and document results</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Site Wrap-Up and Check-Out</strong></p><p><strong>-1-</strong> Confirm with the site manager or designated site contact that all systems are functioning properly on their end and that services have been fully restored. Document confirmation in your closing notes.</p><p><strong>-2-</strong> Clean up the work area to ensure it is left in a neat and orderly condition. Gather all tools, equipment, and materials brought onsite before departing.</p><p><strong>-3-</strong> Take all required after pictures (see pictures list below)</p><p><strong>-4-</strong> Upload all pictures to this work order and/or email to the NOC analyst as requested (NOC Email if/when needed: <del>**************</del>)</p><p><strong>-5-</strong> Please fill in the \"Reason For Outage\" custom field with a brief description, such as power outage, UPS failure, etc.</p><p><strong>-6-</strong> Check-out and get released from site by the NOC analyst</p><p>--- NOC Phone Number: <del>**************</del></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>****************************************************************************************************************************************</p><p><strong>Technician Minimum Required Tools/Materials</strong></p><p><strong>-1-</strong> Network cable tester/toner</p><p><strong>-2-</strong> Laptop w/charger and various console cables</p><p><strong>-3-</strong> Full charged cell phone w/camera and mobile hotspot</p><p><strong>-4-</strong> Various console cables</p><p><strong>-5-</strong> Various length of patch cables (or the ability to make while onsite)</p><p><strong>-6-</strong> Box of Cat5 or Cat6 cable with a minimum of 300' (foot)</p><p><strong>-7-</strong> Spare RJ-45 keystone jacks and mod ends</p><p><strong>-8-</strong> Basic hand tools (screwdrivers, star/hex head drivers, wrenches, pliers, etc.)</p><p><strong>-9-</strong> Minimum 6’ A-Frame ladder</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>****************************************************************************************************************************************</p><p><strong>Technician Required Photos (Additional may be requested/required by the NOC analyst)</strong></p><p><strong>-1-</strong> Existing equipment (close up) / equipment location (wide angle of network area/room) prior to starting work</p><p><strong>-2-</strong> Existing equipment (close up) / equipment location (wide angle of network area/room) after work is completed</p><p><strong>-3-</strong> Capture any additional photographs as requested by the NOC analyst during the course of the work</p><p><br></p><p>****************************************************************************************************************************************</p><p><strong>Equipment Shipment Instructions (If Needed)</strong></p><p>The removed equipment must be prepared for return. In most cases, this will require dropping it off at the nearest UPS Store. If the site manager prefers to handle the return, the technician must provide the old equipment securely boxed with the return label attached.</p><p><strong>-1-</strong> Return shipping label will be included inside the package containing the new equipment</p><p><strong>-2-</strong> The removed equipment shall be packaged using the original box and packing materials from the newly delivered device</p><p><strong>-3-</strong> Affix the return shipping label to the box, ensuring the original shipping label is fully covered or obscured (e.g., by placing the new label directly over it or blacking it out with a permanent marker)</p><p><strong>-4-</strong> Capture clear photographs of the packaged equipment with the return label securely attached</p><p><strong>-5-</strong> The packaged equipment may either be dropped off at the nearest UPS location or left with the designated site manager/contact for return</p><p><strong>-6-</strong> Capture a clear photograph of the drop off receipt from UPS (or other carrier) and upload to confirm date/time package dropped for shipping</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>****************************************************************************************************************************************</p><p><strong>Tech Requirements and Expectations</strong></p><p><strong>-1-</strong> Technicians are expected to adhere to a business casual dress code, which includes pants without holes and closed-toe shoes. Shorts, tank tops, and sleeveless shirts are not permitted</p><p><strong>-2-</strong> The technician must arrive onsite with the minimum required tools and materials as outlined in the Tool/Material List</p><p><strong>-3-</strong> Please note that only one site visit can be processed per work order. If a revisit is required, a new work order will be issued. Do not return to a site without explicit authorization and a new active work order</p>","markdown":"***NOTE: If travel/gas is required, it must be requested as a counter-offer BEFORE the ticket is assigned. Any requests made after ticket assignment may be denied.***\n\n**DISPATCH OVERVIEW**\n\nThe objective of this dispatch is to perform onsite troubleshooting of the site’s WattBox, network equipment (CradlePoint and/or VeloCloud), and associated cabling. The technician is responsible for identifying and addressing the root cause of the issue in order to restore full network connectivity.\n\nPlease follow the troubleshooting steps outlined below in coordination with the NOC. The technician is expected to assist in diagnosing the issue and work with the NOC to confirm that connectivity has been successfully restored before leaving the site. Additional troubleshooting and/or repair steps may be requested by the NOC analyst during the dispatch, in addition to what is listed below.\n\nSee \"Confidential Information\" section for device specific troubleshooting steps (if needed).\n\n**Site Specific Information**\n\nTicket (INC) Reference Number (Number for tech to reference when calling into the NOC): INC1800465  \n  \n  \nEquipment to Troubleshoot (make and model of equipment to ensure tech brings proper console cables if/when they are needed) and Port Assignments (if possible):  \nVelocloud GE1  \nSpectrum modem  \n  \nISP (Internet Service Provider) Name and Equipment (make/model):  \nSpectrum modem located in the back room  \nModem MAC 3C2D9E97FE8C  \n  \nSpecial Tools and/or Materials Required (other than what is listed in the tech minimum tool list - if not needed, leave blank):  \n230ft cable  \n  \nTracking Number of Equipment Sent To Site (If not available or needed, leave blank):  \n  \n  \nSpecial Tech Instructions (access requirements, etc. - if not needed, leave blank):  \nTech will do a cable run of 230ft between Spectrum modem to Velocloud.\n\n**Site Check-In and Initial Activities**\n\n**-1-** Upon arrival, call and check in with the NOC to review and confirm the scope of work to be performed before beginning any tasks.\n\n\\--- NOC Phone Number: \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**-2-** Check in with the site contact or manager (refer to the custom field “Site Contact Name & Number” for contact information)\n\n**-3-** Capture all required before pictures as outlined in the photo documentation list below.\n\n**Cable Inspection, Testing, and Replacement**\n\nThe technician shall perform inspections and testing on any necessary patch cords (between networking equipment) and/or demarcation extensions. All findings, including any cable replacements, must be relayed to the assigned NOC analyst.\n\n**-1-** Visually inspect all cabling between the network equipment. Document any issues (damaged cable or MOD ends, broken clips, etc.)\n\n**-2-** Test any suspect cables and document the results\n\n**-3-** Replace any faulty cables that are identified and confirm functionality with the NOC analyst\n\n**Network Equipment Power Inspection**\n\nThe technician shall perform an initial power inspection of all onsite network equipment, including but not limited to routers, switches, Cradlepoints, VeloCloud devices, and ISP-provided modems.\n\n**-1-** Inspect all power outlets / strips for signs of failure or loose power cords\n\n**-2-** Inspect any UPSs (uninterrupted power supplies or battery back-ups) for any signs of failure or loose power cords\n\n**-3-** Check for tripped circuit breakers - switch back on if they have been tripped\n\n**Device Reboots and Link (Status) Light Verification on Network Equipment**\n\nThe technician shall perform a controlled reboot on all network equipment in coordination with the NOC analyst.\n\n**-1-** Reboot network devices one at a time to minimize disruption as directed by the NOC (Do NOT reboot any equipment without NOC approval first)\n\n**-2-** Document any observed changes in network behavior and/or status light indicators during and after each reboot\n\n**-3-** Collaborate with the NOC analyst to identify any ports that should display a green (active/good) status indicator but instead show red (fault/bad) or no status light at all\n\n**Connectivity Testing**\n\nThe technician shall perform connectivity testing as directed by the NOC once all other steps have been completed and devices confirmed up.\n\n**-1-** Attempt to access an external website (such as google.com, yahoo.com, etc.) and document results\n\n**-2-** Perform a speed test (using google or speedtest.net) and document results\n\n**Site Wrap-Up and Check-Out**\n\n**-1-** Confirm with the site manager or designated site contact that all systems are functioning properly on their end and that services have been fully restored. Document confirmation in your closing notes.\n\n**-2-** Clean up the work area to ensure it is left in a neat and orderly condition. Gather all tools, equipment, and materials brought onsite before departing.\n\n**-3-** Take all required after pictures (see pictures list below)\n\n**-4-** Upload all pictures to this work order and/or email to the NOC analyst as requested (NOC Email if/when needed: \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*)\n\n**-5-** Please fill in the \"Reason For Outage\" custom field with a brief description, such as power outage, UPS failure, etc.\n\n**-6-** Check-out and get released from site by the NOC analyst\n\n\\--- NOC Phone Number: \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Technician Minimum Required Tools/Materials**\n\n**-1-** Network cable tester/toner\n\n**-2-** Laptop w/charger and various console cables\n\n**-3-** Full charged cell phone w/camera and mobile hotspot\n\n**-4-** Various console cables\n\n**-5-** Various length of patch cables (or the ability to make while onsite)\n\n**-6-** Box of Cat5 or Cat6 cable with a minimum of 300' (foot)\n\n**-7-** Spare RJ-45 keystone jacks and mod ends\n\n**-8-** Basic hand tools (screwdrivers, star/hex head drivers, wrenches, pliers, etc.)\n\n**-9-** Minimum 6’ A-Frame ladder\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Technician Required Photos (Additional may be requested/required by the NOC analyst)**\n\n**-1-** Existing equipment (close up) / equipment location (wide angle of network area/room) prior to starting work\n\n**-2-** Existing equipment (close up) / equipment location (wide angle of network area/room) after work is completed\n\n**-3-** Capture any additional photographs as requested by the NOC analyst during the course of the work\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Equipment Shipment Instructions (If Needed)**\n\nThe removed equipment must be prepared for return. In most cases, this will require dropping it off at the nearest UPS Store. If the site manager prefers to handle the return, the technician must provide the old equipment securely boxed with the return label attached.\n\n**-1-** Return shipping label will be included inside the package containing the new equipment\n\n**-2-** The removed equipment shall be packaged using the original box and packing materials from the newly delivered device\n\n**-3-** Affix the return shipping label to the box, ensuring the original shipping label is fully covered or obscured (e.g., by placing the new label directly over it or blacking it out with a permanent marker)\n\n**-4-** Capture clear photographs of the packaged equipment with the return label securely attached\n\n**-5-** The packaged equipment may either be dropped off at the nearest UPS location or left with the designated site manager/contact for return\n\n**-6-** Capture a clear photograph of the drop off receipt from UPS (or other carrier) and upload to confirm date/time package dropped for shipping\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Tech Requirements and Expectations**\n\n**-1-** Technicians are expected to adhere to a business casual dress code, which includes pants without holes and closed-toe shoes. Shorts, tank tops, and sleeveless shirts are not permitted\n\n**-2-** The technician must arrive onsite with the minimum required tools and materials as outlined in the Tool/Material List\n\n**-3-** Please note that only one site visit can be processed per work order. If a revisit is required, a new work order will be issued. Do not return to a site without explicit authorization and a new active work order","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-18T10:00","end":"2026-09-18T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":85,"max":145},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":1,"amount":85},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":60}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":8},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $145 is below minimum threshold $400"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:01:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-22T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-22T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-09-22T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-09-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-21T14:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T18:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974878-The Warehouse-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-21T