etro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789496869177}
{"job":{"id":19958732,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Envysion","title":"Resolve (#1) IP camera/s issues","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Overview:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Seeking a technician with experience in troubleshooting IP cameras.</li>\n<li>Tech is required to troubleshoot&nbsp;<strong>(</strong>Front door - Port 18<strong>)</strong>&nbsp;camera.</li>\n<li>Troubleshoot any offline camera equipment as needed.</li>\n<li>Clean any dirty cameras.</li>\n<li><strong><u>Tech needs to call to check in with the Envysion Helpdesk at (877) 258-9441&nbsp;Opt. 8</u></strong></li>\n<li><strong>HOW TO CLEAN CCTV CAMERA COVERS GUIDE ATTACHED</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Tools Required:&nbsp;</strong><em>must haves</em></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>8' - 15'</strong> Ladder: Tech will need to have both A frame and extension</li>\n<li>IP cable tester</li>\n<li>Toner</li>\n<li>Drill / screw driver with anything needed to troubleshoot the camera</li>\n<li>Crimping tool/ crimpers</li>\n<li>RJ45 connectors (Can be expenses if used)</li>\n<li>Spot monitor&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Recommending tech have PPE for dust and debris</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p>\n<p><strong><em>Pre-Site Requirements</em></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Please do not schedule your visit on weekends and during meal rushes. Envysion Support Center hours are 6:00 AM - 8:00 PM Mountain Time week days and 8am-4:30pm on weekends.&nbsp;</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If you go on the weekend without permission, you may have to return if the issue is not resolved, and you will not get a return bonus</li>\n<li>Call the site to introduce yourself and let them know you are on your way.&nbsp;</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Phone numbers are listed on Google Maps</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If there is an issue with the time window please let us know by messaging the work order manager or calling the support number for emergency. Envysion Support (877) 258-9441&nbsp;Opt. 8</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong><em>On-Site Tasks</em></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong><u>Tech needs to call to check in with the Envysion Helpdesk at (877) 258-9441&nbsp;#8</u></strong></li>\n<li>Introduce yourself to the manager on duty and explain you are with Envysion Support, here to work on the CCTV system</li>\n<li>The technician should be prepared to both troubleshoot and re-terminate RJ45, test the cable to the camera with a the cable tester, and test the video output by using a spot monitor or by switching to a known good port.</li>\n<li>Please take pictures of cable test and/or spot monitor image.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Before calling support please make sure you go through the PDF guides that are provided for troubleshooting our cameras.</li>\n<li>If you have been onsite for over an hour and a half, you need to reach out to the helpdesk and update them with the current progress.</li>\n<li>During some visits, rarely, it is possible that additional troubleshooting may be requested for CCTV cameras (This may include re-angling, removing obstructions, or resolving video quality issues) or network connections, please be prepared to encounter this if necessary.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If this is considered out of scope message work order manager for compensation.</li>\n<li>Check out with Envysion support. Envysion Support number (877) 258-9441 Option 8</li>\n<li>If a return visit is needed please do the return within 24 hours</li>\n<li>If checking out with support please be patient as sometimes there is a big volume of calls. Voicemail will not be considered as your check out</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong><em>Required On-Site Deliverables</em></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Upload any pictures that were taken as well upload any picture of expenses if needed.</li>\n<li>Check-out of work order via Field Nation and add any notes.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Dress code and behavior policy</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Remember to be respectful of site employees and Envysion support</strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Do not approach site employees if there is no need to, please reach out to the manager on duty only</strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>If there are any issues please find a manager or call Envysion support</strong></li>\n<li>Dress <strong>appropriately</strong> for work being done on site</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Escalation Process:</strong></p>\n<p>Contact Work Order Manager via direct message for non-work related issues such as: ETA adjustments, needing to do a return trip, questions regarding pay</p>\n<ul>\n<li>If immediate assistance is needed call the support line (877) 258-9441 Opt. 8</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Expenses</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Payment for additional expenses for equipment, such as Fuses, BNC connectors, RJ45 connectors, patch cables, and silicone caulk will be paid only if a receipt is submitted in the Field Nation App and approved by the Work Order Manager.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Additional hours</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">This is a fixed rate work order to complete the scope of work listed in the service description. There is no hourly rate if the tech goes past the times that we have estimated for completion. Any additional work completed or extenuating circumstances will be taken into consideration and adjustment may be made at the work order managers discretion. The only exception to this is if a counter offer was accepted by the work order manager prior to the the work order being assigned.</li>\n<li>Parking and toll road expenses will be paid only if a receipt is submitted in the Field Nation App and will then be approved by the Work Order Manager. Travel pay must be approved by the work order manager before the tech goes to the site.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>If you do not have the required tools you will be asked to go get that item. Please make sure you have all the required items.<strong><u>All bonuses will be forfeit if you do not bring the required equipment.</u></strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If unable to commit to a return visit with the requires tools you will be dismissed without pay</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Waiting on hold for more than 30 minutes</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Your patience is appreciated!</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">The phone could be busy but please call to check out. If you leave the site without a resolution and did not get released by support you will be asked to revisit the site without a bonus.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If on hold with Envysion support for greater than 30 minutes a $10 bonus will be added. To be approved, the phone number you call from will be checked in the Envysion phone system. Please reach out to the Work Order Manager.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">You can message the work order manager to see if they can check your work but not guarantee.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Please do not leave the site while on hold.</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**Overview:**\n\n- Seeking a technician with experience in troubleshooting IP cameras.\n- Tech is required to troubleshoot **(**Front door - Port 18**)** camera.\n- Troubleshoot any offline camera equipment as needed.\n- Clean any dirty cameras.\n- **Tech needs to call to check in with the Envysion Helpdesk at (877) 258-9441 Opt. 8**\n- **HOW TO CLEAN CCTV CAMERA COVERS GUIDE ATTACHED**\n\n**Tools Required:** *must haves*\n\n- **8' - 15'** Ladder: Tech will need to have both A frame and extension\n- IP cable tester\n- Toner\n- Drill / screw driver with anything needed to troubleshoot the camera\n- Crimping tool/ crimpers\n- RJ45 connectors (Can be expenses if used)\n- Spot monitor\n- Recommending tech have PPE for dust and debris\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n***Pre-Site Requirements***\n\n1. Please do not schedule your visit on weekends and during meal rushes. Envysion Support Center hours are 6:00 AM - 8:00 PM Mountain Time week days and 8am-4:30pm on weekends.\n2. If you go on the weekend without permission, you may have to return if the issue is not resolved, and you will not get a return bonus\n3. Call the site to introduce yourself and let them know you are on your way.\n4. Phone numbers are listed on Google Maps\n5. If there is an issue with the time window please let us know by messaging the work order manager or calling the support number for emergency. Envysion Support (877) 258-9441 Opt. 8\n\n***On-Site Tasks***\n\n1. **Tech needs to call to check in with the Envysion Helpdesk at (877) 258-9441 #8**\n2. Introduce yourself to the manager on duty and explain you are with Envysion Support, here to work on the CCTV system\n3. The technician should be prepared to both troubleshoot and re-terminate RJ45, test the cable to the camera with a the cable tester, and test the video output by using a spot monitor or by switching to a known good port.\n4. Please take pictures of cable test and/or spot monitor image.\n5. Before calling support please make sure you go through the PDF guides that are provided for troubleshooting our cameras.\n6. If you have been onsite for over an hour and a half, you need to reach out to the helpdesk and update them with the current progress.\n7. During some visits, rarely, it is possible that additional troubleshooting may be requested for CCTV cameras (This may include re-angling, removing obstructions, or resolving video quality issues) or network connections, please be prepared to encounter this if necessary.\n8. If this is considered out of scope message work order manager for compensation.\n9. Check out with Envysion support. Envysion Support number (877) 258-9441 Option 8\n10. If a return visit is needed please do the return within 24 hours\n11. If checking out with support please be patient as sometimes there is a big volume of calls. Voicemail will not be considered as your check out\n\n***Required On-Site Deliverables***\n\n1. Upload any pictures that were taken as well upload any picture of expenses if needed.\n2. Check-out of work order via Field Nation and add any notes.\n\n**Dress code and behavior policy**\n\n- **Remember to be respectful of site employees and Envysion support**\n- **Do not approach site employees if there is no need to, please reach out to the manager on duty only**\n- **If there are any issues please find a manager or call Envysion support**\n- Dress **appropriately** for work being done on site\n\n**Escalation Process:**\n\nContact Work Order Manager via direct message for non-work related issues such as: ETA adjustments, needing to do a return trip, questions regarding pay\n\n- If immediate assistance is needed call the support line (877) 258-9441 Opt. 8\n\n**Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy**\n\n- Expenses\n- Payment for additional expenses for equipment, such as Fuses, BNC connectors, RJ45 connectors, patch cables, and silicone caulk will be paid only if a receipt is submitted in the Field Nation App and approved by the Work Order Manager.\n- Additional hours\n- This is a fixed rate work order to complete the scope of work listed in the service description. There is no hourly rate if the tech goes past the times that we have estimated for completion. Any additional work completed or extenuating circumstances will be taken into consideration and adjustment may be made at the work order managers discretion. The only exception to this is if a counter offer was accepted by the work order manager prior to the the work order being assigned.\n- Parking and toll road expenses will be paid only if a receipt is submitted in the Field Nation App and will then be approved by the Work Order Manager. Travel pay must be approved by the work order manager before the tech goes to the site.\n- If you do not have the required tools you will be asked to go get that item. Please make sure you have all the required items.**All bonuses will be forfeit if you do not bring the required equipment.**\n- If unable to commit to a return visit with the requires tools you will be dismissed without pay\n\n**Waiting on hold for more than 30 minutes**\n\n- Your patience is appreciated!\n- The phone could be busy but please call to check out. If you leave the site without a resolution and did not get released by support you will be asked to revisit the site without a bonus.\n- If on hold with Envysion support for greater than 30 minutes a $10 bonus will be added. To be approved, the phone number you call from will be checked in the Envysion phone system. Please reach out to the Work Order Manager.\n- You can message the work order manager to see if they can check your work but not guarantee.\n- Please do not leave the site while on hold.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-16T07:00","end":"2026-09-16T09:00","latestStart":"2026-09-16T10:30"},"payRange":{"min":120,"max":120},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":16},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $120 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789497711882}
{"job":{"id":19951772,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"A+ Mobile","title":"Roxboro, NC -- Starlink Installation with Short Wall Mount","description":{"html":"<p><strong>PREFERRED EXPERIENCED STARLINK (or similar device mounting experience) FOR THE FOLLOWING:</strong></p><p><strong><u>ProSat Networks -- Work Order (WO)</u>:</strong></p><p><strong>You will be representing ProSat Networks</strong> (a sister company of <em>A+ Mobile Techs</em>) at all times during this WO (work order) and during all customer interactions.</p><p><strong><u>Customer</u>:<del> </del></strong><del>***** ************* ***** ********</del></p><p><strong><u>Onsite POC (point-of-contact)</u>:</strong> same as Customer</p><p><strong><u>ProSat Networks' WO Manager(s)</u>:&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>Prilla <del>*********** **** ************* *************************</del></strong></p><p>Haley&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>** ***** **** ************* *******************************</del></span></p><p><strong>*****************************************</strong></p><p><strong><u>SOW (scope of work):</u> see attached photo﻿</strong></p><p><strong>Estimated time to completion: &lt;3-4 hrs</strong></p><p><strong>Have STARLINK APP</strong> installed on your cell, <strong>OPEN and Test</strong> <strong>PRIOR</strong> to arriving onsite.</p><p>The goal is to install the customer's <strong>Starlink (installation) Kit</strong> resulting in a successful installation that matches or surpasses our customer's expectations.</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Installation Details</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Starlink Kit:&nbsp;TBD</strong></li><li><strong>Mount Type: Short wall mount</strong></li><li><strong>Mounting Surface: Fascia of the roof </strong></li><li><strong>Cable Route: Create a Wall Penetration </strong></li><li><strong>Router Location: office (2nd floor)</strong></li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Pre-Installation</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Verify all Starlink equipment and installation materials are onsite.</strong></li><li><strong>Take photos of the customer-supplied equipment.</strong></li><li><strong>Using the customer's Starlink App:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Do multiple <strong>OBSTRUCTIONS Tests to pinpoint</strong>: <strong style=\"color: rgb(111, 192, 64);\">GOOD experience</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Take Screen Shot showing the best Obstructions Test results found</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Save a screenshot of the final Obstruction Test.</strong></li><li><strong>Review and obtain customer approval for:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Mount location</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Outdoor-Indoor Cable Route</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Router location</strong></li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Installation</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Install the approved [Mount Type] securely.</strong></li><li><strong>Route the proprietary Starlink cable using the most direct and professional path.</strong></li><li><strong>Use an existing low-voltage pathway whenever available.</strong></li><li><strong>If no pathway exists, obtain customer approval before creating one (1) simple wall penetration.</strong></li><li><strong>Secure all exterior cabling using appropriate fasteners (e.g., cable tacks, clips, zip ties, or Velcro straps) to ensure a clean, secure, and professional installation.</strong></li><li><strong>Install a drip loop on exterior cable runs.</strong></li><li><strong>Seal all penetrations with weatherproof sealant.</strong></li><li><strong>Install the router in the customer's preferred location.</strong></li><li><strong>Clean up cables of router power supply professionally.</strong></li><li><strong>Connect and power on the Starlink system.</strong></li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 0, 0);\">Note: Initial Starlink activation may take up to 20 minutes.</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Configuration &amp; Testing</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Using the customer's Starlink App:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Configure the customer's Wi-Fi name (SSID) and password.</strong></li><li><strong>Verify the dish is Aligned. Take a screenshot.</strong></li><li><strong>Perform a Speed Test. Take a screenshot.&nbsp;(150 Mbps and up results only)</strong></li><li><strong>Confirm internet connectivity and ensure no errors on the Starlink app.</strong></li><li><strong>Assist the customer with connecting devices to the new Wi-Fi network.</strong></li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Customer Walkthrough</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Show the customer how to:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Access their SSID (wireless network name)</strong></li><li><strong>Input and Reset password</strong></li><li><strong>Run speed test</strong></li><li><strong>Remotely monitor and control</strong></li><li><strong>Reset/refresh Starlink network connection (handshake)</strong></li><li><strong>Adjust the Snow Melt feature</strong></li><li><strong>Answer customer questions that come up.</strong></li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Change of Scope</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> - </span><strong style=\"color: rgb(255, 0, 0);\">Stop &amp; Call WO Manager</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Do not proceed without approval if the job requires:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Attic cable routing.</strong></li><li><strong>Conduit installation.</strong></li><li><strong>Underground trenching.</strong></li><li><strong>Additional installation of any equipment.</strong></li><li><strong>Any work outside the approved Work Order.</strong></li></ul><p><strong>*Attention Installer: IF YOU ARE WORKING IN AN ATTIC</strong></p><p>It is imperative that you step only on the floor joists and NOT onto the attic insulation.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Report any site issues immediately to the WO manager if they may prevent a successful installation.</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">FINAL DELIVERABLES</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Upload:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>INVENTORY of supplied equipment and installation materials (laid out before installation)&nbsp;</strong></li><li><strong>BEFORE installation photos</strong></li><li><strong>AFTER installation photos</strong></li><li><strong>Starlink Installation Location</strong></li><li><strong>Outdoor Cable Entry</strong></li><li><strong>Indoor Cable Entry</strong></li><li><strong>Customer Starlink App screenshots:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Obstructions Test results</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Speed Test results</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Starlink Aligned results</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Closeout</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Review the completed installation with the customer.</strong></li><li><strong>Clean the work area. </strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">DO NOT LEAVE ANY TRASH BEHIND.</strong></li><li><strong>Upload all required photos and closeout notes before leaving the site.</strong></li></ul>","markdown":"**PREFERRED EXPERIENCED STARLINK (or similar device mounting experience) FOR THE FOLLOWING:**\n\n**ProSat Networks -- Work Order (WO):**\n\n**You will be representing ProSat Networks** (a sister company of *A+ Mobile Techs*) at all times during this WO (work order) and during all customer interactions.\n\n**Customer:** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Onsite POC (point-of-contact):** same as Customer\n\n**ProSat Networks' WO Manager(s):**\n\n**Prilla \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\nHaley \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**SOW (scope of work): see attached photo﻿**\n\n**Estimated time to completion: <3-4 hrs**\n\n**Have STARLINK APP** installed on your cell, **OPEN and Test** **PRIOR** to arriving onsite.\n\nThe goal is to install the customer's **Starlink (installation) Kit** resulting in a successful installation that matches or surpasses our customer's expectations.\n\n**Installation Details**\n\n- **Starlink Kit: TBD**\n- **Mount Type: Short wall mount**\n- **Mounting Surface: Fascia of the roof**\n- **Cable Route: Create a Wall Penetration**\n- **Router Location: office (2nd floor)**\n\n**Pre-Installation**\n\n- **Verify all Starlink equipment and installation materials are onsite.**\n- **Take photos of the customer-supplied equipment.**\n- **Using the customer's Starlink App:**\n- Do multiple **OBSTRUCTIONS Tests to pinpoint**: **GOOD experience**\n- Take Screen Shot showing the best Obstructions Test results found\n- **Save a screenshot of the final Obstruction Test.**\n- **Review and obtain customer approval for:**\n- **Mount location**\n- **Outdoor-Indoor Cable Route**\n- **Router location**\n\n**Installation**\n\n- **Install the approved \\[Mount Type\\] securely.**\n- **Route the proprietary Starlink cable using the most direct and professional path.**\n- **Use an existing low-voltage pathway whenever available.**\n- **If no pathway exists, obtain customer approval before creating one (1) simple wall penetration.**\n- **Secure all exterior cabling using appropriate fasteners (e.g., cable tacks, clips, zip ties, or Velcro straps) to ensure a clean, secure, and professional installation.**\n- **Install a drip loop on exterior cable runs.**\n- **Seal all penetrations with weatherproof sealant.**\n- **Install the router in the customer's preferred location.**\n- **Clean up cables of router power supply professionally.**\n- **Connect and power on the Starlink system.**\n\n**Note: Initial Starlink activation may take up to 20 minutes.**\n\n**Configuration & Testing**\n\n**Using the customer's Starlink App:**\n\n- **Configure the customer's Wi-Fi name (SSID) and password.**\n- **Verify the dish is Aligned. Take a screenshot.**\n- **Perform a Speed Test. Take a screenshot. (150 Mbps and up results only)**\n- **Confirm internet connectivity and ensure no errors on the Starlink app.**\n- **Assist the customer with connecting devices to the new Wi-Fi network.**\n\n**Customer Walkthrough**\n\n**Show the customer how to:**\n\n- **Access their SSID (wireless network name)**\n- **Input and Reset password**\n- **Run speed test**\n- **Remotely monitor and control**\n- **Reset/refresh Starlink network connection (handshake)**\n- **Adjust the Snow Melt feature**\n- **Answer customer questions that come up.**\n\n**Change of Scope** - **Stop & Call WO Manager**\n\n**Do not proceed without approval if the job requires:**\n\n- **Attic cable routing.**\n- **Conduit installation.**\n- **Underground trenching.**\n- **Additional installation of any equipment.**\n- **Any work outside the approved Work Order.**\n\n**\\*Attention Installer: IF YOU ARE WORKING IN AN ATTIC**\n\nIt is imperative that you step only on the floor joists and NOT onto the attic insulation.\n\n**Report any site issues immediately to the WO manager if they may prevent a successful installation.**\n\n**FINAL DELIVERABLES**\n\n**Upload:**\n\n- **INVENTORY of supplied equipment and installation materials (laid out before installation)**\n- **BEFORE installation photos**\n- **AFTER installation photos**\n- **Starlink Installation Location**\n- **Outdoor Cable Entry**\n- **Indoor Cable Entry**\n- **Customer Starlink App screenshots:**\n- Obstructions Test results\n- Speed Test results\n- Starlink Aligned results\n\n**Closeout**\n\n- **Review the completed installation with the customer.**\n- **Clean the work area.** **DO NOT LEAVE ANY TRASH BEHIND.**\n- **Upload all required photos and closeout notes before leaving the site.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-14T09:00","end":"2026-09-21T10:00"},"payRange":{"min":220,"max":220},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":45},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"starlink\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789497967974}
{"job":{"id":19959359,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Teceze","title":"Access Point (AP) Replacement & Installation","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><p>Technician is required to perform an Access Point (AP) technology refresh at the customer site. The work includes removal and replacement of existing APs, installation of new APs, cabling/patching, labeling, POST testing, documentation, and proper handling of replaced equipment.</p><p>Need to install 7 new Access Point (AP).</p><p><strong>Technician Responsibilities:</strong></p><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Site Check-In Check in with the designated site contact/SPOC upon arrival.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Follow all customer site access and safety requirements.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Confirm the assigned AP locations before starting work.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">AP Replacement &amp; Installation Identify existing APs scheduled for replacement.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Carefully remove existing APs.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Install and securely mount the new APs at the designated locations.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Ensure the AP is properly positioned and physically secured.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Cabling &amp; PatchingPatch/connect the new AP using the existing network cable where applicable.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Perform new cabling only where specifically required by the scope.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Verify that cable connections are secure and properly connected.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Labeling &amp; Tagging Label and tag all new/replaced APs strictly according to HCL standards.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Ensure labels are clearly visible and correctly placed.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">POST / Testing Perform POST (Power-On Self-Test) on each installed/replaced AP.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Verify AP power, connectivity, and basic network functionality.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Report any connectivity or hardware issues to the designated SPOC.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Documentation Update/confirm AP location information.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Provide AP mapping information for the applicable floor/area.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Capture required installation and labeling photos.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Document any issues, exceptions, or incomplete work.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Old Equipment Handling Carefully pack the removed/old APs.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Keep all removed equipment together and properly secured.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Hand over the old APs to the designated local SPOC.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Do not dispose of or remove customer equipment from the site unless specifically authorized.</li></ul><p>Required Closeout</p><p>Technician must provide:</p><ul><li>Before/after photos of AP installations</li><li>Photos showing AP labels/tags</li><li>Photos of cable connections where required</li><li>Confirmation that POST testing was completed</li><li>List of APs successfully replaced</li><li>Details of any AP/cabling/network issues</li><li>Confirmation that old APs were packed and handed over to the SPOC</li><li>Site SPOC confirmation/sign-off, if required</li></ul><p>Tools / Requirements</p><p>Technician should bring:</p><ul><li>Laptop</li><li>Basic hand tools / screwdriver kit</li><li>Console cable if required</li><li>Cable tester, if applicable</li><li>Phone/camera for documentation</li><li>Any additional tools required for AP mounting.</li></ul>","markdown":"**Scope of Work:**\n\nTechnician is required to perform an Access Point (AP) technology refresh at the customer site. The work includes removal and replacement of existing APs, installation of new APs, cabling/patching, labeling, POST testing, documentation, and proper handling of replaced equipment.\n\nNeed to install 7 new Access Point (AP).\n\n**Technician Responsibilities:**\n\n- Site Check-In Check in with the designated site contact/SPOC upon arrival.\n- Follow all customer site access and safety requirements.\n- Confirm the assigned AP locations before starting work.\n- AP Replacement & Installation Identify existing APs scheduled for replacement.\n- Carefully remove existing APs.\n- Install and securely mount the new APs at the designated locations.\n- Ensure the AP is properly positioned and physically secured.\n- Cabling & PatchingPatch/connect the new AP using the existing network cable where applicable.\n- Perform new cabling only where specifically required by the scope.\n- Verify that cable connections are secure and properly connected.\n- Labeling & Tagging Label and tag all new/replaced APs strictly according to HCL standards.\n- Ensure labels are clearly visible and correctly placed.\n- POST / Testing Perform POST (Power-On Self-Test) on each installed/replaced AP.\n- Verify AP power, connectivity, and basic network functionality.\n- Report any connectivity or hardware issues to the designated SPOC.\n- Documentation Update/confirm AP location information.\n- Provide AP mapping information for the applicable floor/area.\n- Capture required installation and labeling photos.\n- Document any issues, exceptions, or incomplete work.\n- Old Equipment Handling Carefully pack the removed/old APs.\n- Keep all removed equipment together and properly secured.\n- Hand over the old APs to the designated local SPOC.\n- Do not dispose of or remove customer equipment from the site unless specifically authorized.\n\nRequired Closeout\n\nTechnician must provide:\n\n- Before/after photos of AP installations\n- Photos showing AP labels/tags\n- Photos of cable connections where required\n- Confirmation that POST testing was completed\n- List of APs successfully replaced\n- Details of any AP/cabling/network issues\n- Confirmation that old APs were packed and handed over to the SPOC\n- Site SPOC confirmation/sign-off, if required\n\nTools / Requirements\n\nTechnician should bring:\n\n- Laptop\n- Basic hand tools / screwdriver kit\n- Console cable if required\n- Cable tester, if applicable\n- Phone/camera for documentation\n- Any additional tools required for AP mounting.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-21T08:00","end":"2026-09-21T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":200,"max":200},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":8,"distance":5},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $200 is below minimum threshold $400"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789498124002}
{"job":{"id":"5706417809","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Level 10","title":"Five Below | Install Router, AP(s), PC(s), and CP | LIFT REQ","description":"<p><br></p><p>Overview</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Level 10 tech will be onsite to perform an equipment upgrade to the router, access points, managers PC, register PCs, and Cradlepoint. Check the location profile of each workorder for the specific devices that will be replaced. Not all devices will be upgraded, it varies by site. Installation of devices MUST be completed in the specified order of this installation document.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p> </p><p>Installation Order:</p><p> </p><p><br></p><ol><li><br></li><li>Router</li><li><br></li><li>Access Point(s)</li><li>Managers PC</li><li><br></li><li>POS PC(s)</li><li><br></li><li>Cradlepoint</li><li><br></li></ol><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Work will start before store hours; it is imperative that at a minimum the router and specified access points have been installed and tested prior to store open to ensure the store network is up and ready for store opening and the lift has been removed from the store. Tech must call into Level 10 Support to test and validate all devices when requested during the installation process. All the old equipment removed will get boxed up and placed in the Level 10 box that was shipped to site. Affix the return label that was sent in the box over the existing label for equipment to get shipped back to Level 10. Contact UPS to schedule a pickup, note the confirmation in CompanyCam checklist. Complete the CompanyCam checklist and have it reviewed and approved by Level 10 Support prior to leaving stie.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p> </p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>COMPANY CAM USAGE:</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>1. Go to this URL:<a href=\"https://app.companycam.com/projects\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://app.companycam.com/projects</a></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p> </p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>2. Enter any of these Usernames:</p><p> </p><p><br></p><p> </p><p>CompanyCam@Level10.com</p><p> </p><p>CompanyCam2@Level10.com</p><p> </p><p>CompanyCam3@Level10.com</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p> </p><p>3. Enter this Password: Level10!L10</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p> </p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>4. Search for your Project by Site - Enter \"Customer and (site number)\"</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p> </p><p>5. Click on \"To Do's\"</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p> </p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>6. Click on \"Checklists\"</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p> </p><p>7. Select appropriate checklist.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p> </p><p>8. Upload all photos to the specified Checklist Only.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p> </p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Tools Required</p><p><br></p><ul><li><br></li><li>Power &amp; Impact Drill 18v min.</li><li><br></li><li>Assorted drill, masonry, and driver bits</li><li><br></li><li>Fully charged Labeler w/white backed labels and black font</li><li><br></li><li>Fully charged phone w/Digital Camera and w/CompanyCam app installed</li><li><br></li><li>Velcro for cable management above the ceiling</li><li><br></li><li>Tie Wraps for cable management above the ceiling</li><li><br></li><li>Razor Knife</li><li><br></li><li>Sharpie/Permanent Marker</li><li><br></li><li>Cable Push/Pull Rods, fiberglass Fish Sticks, Glow Rods</li><li><br></li><li>Punch Down Tool w/66 &amp; 110 blades</li><li><br></li><li>Modular RJ45 Crimper</li><li><br></li><li>Data Tester</li><li><br></li><li>Toner w/Probe</li><li><br></li><li>Ladder 8ft min. (a multi-position ladder is recommended)</li><li><br></li><li>Flashlight</li><li><br></li><li>Electrician Scissors</li><li><br></li><li>Screwdriver Flatblade, Assorted</li><li><br></li><li>Screwdriver Phillips, Assorted</li><li><br></li><li>Allen Wrench Set</li><li><br></li><li>Torx Set w/Security</li><li><br></li><li>Level</li><li><br></li><li>Tape Measure 35ft</li><li><br></li><li>Pliers, Long Nose</li><li><br></li><li>Pliers, Lineman</li></ul><p><strong>Support Contact</strong></p><ul><li>Tech will need to contact (800) 807-1733 to check in/out and to report any issues.</li></ul><p><strong>Documentation</strong></p><ul><li>Five Below Refresh Network and Equipment - Router, AP, PC, and CP</li><li>Companycam checklist</li></ul><p><strong>Special Requirements</strong></p><ul><li>Level 10 Technician will be required to work on a scissor lift in a new construction environment. Level 10 tech is responsible for providing all PPE as required by the General Contractor onsite.</li></ul><p>Deliverables</p><ul><li>Technician must have the CompanyCam app installed on their phone and have access to the site-specific CompanyCam project page. That page will contain a checklist that will need to be completed. This checklist will act as the required deliverables. Once the installation is complete, the checklist should have a green mark and a count (XX of XX) completed indicating that all deliverable items have been completed.</li></ul><p>€‚</p><p>€‚</p><p>€‹</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Expected Duration: 6.5 Hrs.</p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-02T08:00","end":"2026-10-02T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":0,"max":343.54095294},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":6.7},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $343.54095294 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-06T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14: