{"job":{"id":19959535,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"Allergy Partners-  Installs","description":{"html":"<p><br /></p>\n<p>:</p>\n<p>This install must follow the install guide please make sure you Print it out and have it on site with you,&nbsp; may include but not limited to:</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Mounting a back board - (can expense for sites that Need it,&nbsp; average is a 4x4&nbsp; 3/4 plywood,&nbsp; may need a way to Cut to modify it on site for space availability,&nbsp; &nbsp;Please look at the install guide, and Company cam prior to arriving on site&nbsp; ( should be mounted with Lag bolts and Toggles with washers)&nbsp; We need to make sure these are mounted solid.&nbsp; &nbsp;</p>\n<p>Make sure you have various installation materials screws, toggles, washers, lag bolts. various rack screws,&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Installing a new rack</p>\n<p>installing a new UPS&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Running multiple cables for aps&nbsp;</p>\n<p>swapping out existing old aps for new ones</p>\n<p>working with onsite contact for testing</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>working on a install bridge with client on with us (Please remember to use mute and be careful what you say) the client is listening&nbsp;</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>WWT has been contracted to assist in the deployment of new standardized network upgrade For Allergy Partners. The overall solution includes installing new Cat 6 cabling and installing new APs in the ceiling and installing new Network Switches in the rack.</p>\n<p>Must be able to follow heat map documents and mount APs in according area.</p>\n<p>Working with Support desk to test and troubleshooting to make sure all the new APS are online and operational before released from site.</p>\n<p>Will need the tools and equipment to test and do basic validation of new cable runs</p>\n<p><u>Will be Need to use Company Cam - There is a checklist that needs to be filled out as you do the installation collect appropriate pics and videos. Will set you up with access This is MUST for Competion!!</u></p>\n<p>Will Be Expected to clean up Cabling that is existing when you swing over to new switch gear.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>This IS a FLAT Rate JOB!! Will be on site for a possible 8 hrs.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Tech may be required to pick up materials at a local distribution center.</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Technicians will be selected with the following criteria:</strong></p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Demonstrated work experience in your FN work history (including cabling, termination, patch panel relocation)</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Field Nation score specifically timeliness, back-out ranking, and marketplace score</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Ability to work with other technicians.</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Distance from sites (no travel provided).</p>\n<p><strong>Technician Expectations:</strong></p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Attend required training.</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;On the bridge at all times.</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Have reliable transportation.</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Have the required tools identified in the Run-Book/Deployment Guide.</p>\n<p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Follow the directions from the bridge and</p>\n<p><strong>A fixed rate is a fixed rate, we do not accept counter offers, and we do not allow substitutions.</strong></p>","markdown":":\n\nThis install must follow the install guide please make sure you Print it out and have it on site with you, may include but not limited to:\n\nMounting a back board - (can expense for sites that Need it, average is a 4x4 3/4 plywood, may need a way to Cut to modify it on site for space availability, Please look at the install guide, and Company cam prior to arriving on site ( should be mounted with Lag bolts and Toggles with washers) We need to make sure these are mounted solid.\n\nMake sure you have various installation materials screws, toggles, washers, lag bolts. various rack screws,\n\nInstalling a new rack\n\ninstalling a new UPS\n\nRunning multiple cables for aps\n\nswapping out existing old aps for new ones\n\nworking with onsite contact for testing\n\nworking on a install bridge with client on with us (Please remember to use mute and be careful what you say) the client is listening\n\nWWT has been contracted to assist in the deployment of new standardized network upgrade For Allergy Partners. The overall solution includes installing new Cat 6 cabling and installing new APs in the ceiling and installing new Network Switches in the rack.\n\nMust be able to follow heat map documents and mount APs in according area.\n\nWorking with Support desk to test and troubleshooting to make sure all the new APS are online and operational before released from site.\n\nWill need the tools and equipment to test and do basic validation of new cable runs\n\nWill be Need to use Company Cam - There is a checklist that needs to be filled out as you do the installation collect appropriate pics and videos. Will set you up with access This is MUST for Competion!!\n\nWill Be Expected to clean up Cabling that is existing when you swing over to new switch gear.\n\n**This IS a FLAT Rate JOB!! Will be on site for a possible 8 hrs.**\n\n**Tech may be required to pick up materials at a local distribution center.**\n\n**Technicians will be selected with the following criteria:**\n\n· Demonstrated work experience in your FN work history (including cabling, termination, patch panel relocation)\n\n· Field Nation score specifically timeliness, back-out ranking, and marketplace score\n\n· Ability to work with other technicians.\n\n· Distance from sites (no travel provided).\n\n**Technician Expectations:**\n\n· Attend required training.\n\n· On 