{"job":{"id":19959892,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Sangoma US Inc","title":"02224483 - MSP Support Dispatch Request - Ruby Tuesday #5169","description":{"html":"<p><strong>***Special Instruction Notice***</strong></p>\n<p><strong>IF SITE REQUIRES A CABLE RUN. ALL EXPOSED CABLE FROM A CABLE RUN MUST BE HIDDEN IN CONDUIT OR CABLE MANAGEMENT SYSTEM. MUST ALSO TERMINATE TO AN RJ-45 BOX.&nbsp;FOR AP’s ON FALSE CEILINGS, ANY HOLES CREATED FOR CABLING MUST BE HIDDEN BY AP.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>BEFORE AND AFTER PICTURES REQUIRED TO BE UPLOADED TO WORK ORDER.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p>\n<p>Site address: 1800 E Franklin St, Chapel Hill, NC 27514, United States</p>\n<p>Company name: Bagel Brands / Einstein Bros. Bagels</p>\n<p>Customer's site hours: 6 AM - 2 PM</p>\n<p>Dispatch request date/time: 1 PM, Sept 16, Wednesday</p>\n<p>ONSITE CONTACT INFORMATION:</p>\n<p>Name: MOD</p>\n<p><del>***** ** ************</del></p>\n<p><del>****** ************************************** ********************</del></p>\n<p>Scope of work:</p>\n<p>Site is showing hard down. However, site has internet.</p>\n<p>Primary is up as per LEC. Both usable and GW are pinging.</p>\n<p>It appears that the site is running on primary. Secondary device appears to be offline.</p>\n<p>1. Check what device we have for the back up circuit.</p>\n<p>2. Do layer 1 on secondary modem then test it on laptop.</p>\n<p>3. Once secondary circuit is confirmed working, reconnect it to the Fortigate router.</p>\n<p>4. Sangoma NOC will log in to the router to check the router configuration to get the primary circuit up.</p>\n<p>***Tech needs to bring a laptop, console cable and a hotspot***</p>\n<p><strong>PLEASE READ THE CHECK IN PROCESS, TECHS MUST CALL OUR TEAM TO CHECK IN</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Laptop w/GigE port, console cable, hotspot, or the ability to tether a laptop to a mobile device (wireless connectivity), 350' Cat 6 Cable, Internal Wiring Tools. (Example: cable testers, crimper, etc.)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>*<em>Pre-Site Requirements</em></strong></p>\n<p>TECH CHECK-IN INSTRUCTIONS</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Call Sangoma Turn Up at <del>************ **** *</del></li>\n<li>If the call is transferred to voice mail, the tech MUST leave a message with their name and call back number.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Notice:</strong> In this section, Field Technicians can be defined as Sangoma employees or someone invited to complete work on behalf of Sangoma as a technician.</p>\n<p><strong><em>On-Site Tasks</em></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Check in with the front desk and identify themselves as a representative of Sangoma with the purpose of working on network equipment.</li>\n<li>Technicians will arrive on site and identify themselves to the CPM or MOD (construction project manager or manager on duty) as a technician from Sangoma here to perform an internet install.</li>\n<li>Your arrival will be communicated to the contact prior to the scheduled date. If the contact has any concerns with providing access, the technician should call <del>************ *** *</del>with the store number and the technician’s contact information.</li>\n<li>Someone will reach out to the store to confirm the appointment is legitimate.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong><em>Required On-Site Deliverables</em></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Pictures of the CPE/modem with DMARC information</li>\n<li>Pictures of all work done.</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**\\*\\*\\*Special Instruction Notice\\*\\*\\***\n\n**IF SITE REQUIRES A CABLE RUN. ALL EXPOSED CABLE FROM A CABLE RUN MUST BE HIDDEN IN CONDUIT OR CABLE MANAGEMENT SYSTEM. MUST ALSO TERMINATE TO AN RJ-45 BOX. FOR AP’s ON FALSE CEILINGS, ANY HOLES CREATED FOR CABLING MUST BE HIDDEN BY AP.**\n\n**BEFORE AND AFTER PICTURES REQUIRED TO BE UPLOADED TO WORK ORDER.**\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\nSite address: 1800 E Franklin St, Chapel Hill, NC 27514, United States\n\nCompany name: Bagel Brands / Einstein Bros. Bagels\n\nCustomer's site hours: 6 AM - 2 PM\n\nDispatch request date/time: 1 PM, Sept 16, Wednesday\n\nONSITE CONTACT INFORMATION:\n\nName: MOD\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nScope of work:\n\nSite is showing hard down. However, site has internet.\n\nPrimary is up as per LEC. Both usable and GW are pinging.\n\nIt appears that the site is running on primary. Secondary device appears to be offline.\n\n1\\. Check what device we have for the back up circuit.\n\n2\\. Do layer 1 on secondary modem then test it on laptop.\n\n3\\. Once secondary circuit is confirmed working, reconnect it to the Fortigate router.\n\n4\\. Sangoma NOC will log in to the router to check the router configuration to get the primary circuit up.\n\n\\*\\*\\*Tech needs to bring a laptop, console cable and a hotspot\\*\\*\\*\n\n**PLEASE READ THE CHECK IN PROCESS, TECHS MUST CALL OUR TEAM TO CHECK IN**\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Laptop w/GigE port, console cable, hotspot, or the ability to tether a laptop to a mobile device (wireless connectivity), 350' Cat 6 Cable, Internal Wiring Tools. (Example: cable testers, crimper, etc.)\n\n**\\**Pre-Site Requirements***\n\nTECH CHECK-IN INSTRUCTIONS\n\n1. Call Sangoma Turn Up at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\n2. If the call is transferred to voice mail, the tech MUST leave a message with their name and call back number.\n\n**Notice:** In this section, Field Technicians can be defined as Sangoma employees or someone invited to complete work on behalf of Sangoma as a technician.\n\n***On-Site Tasks***\n\n1. Check in with the front desk and identify themselves as a representative of Sangoma with the purpose of working on network equipment.\n2. Technicians will arrive on site and identify themselves to the CPM or MOD (construction project manager or manager on duty) as a technician from Sangoma here to perform an internet install.\n3. Your arrival will be communicated to the contact prior to the scheduled date. If the contact has any concerns with providing access, the technician should call \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*with the store number and the technician’s contact information.\n4. Someone will reach out to the store to confirm the appointment is legitimate.\n\n***Required On-Site Deliverables***\n\n- Pictures of the CPE/modem with DMARC information\n- Pictures of all work done.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-16T13:00","end":"2026-09-16T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":200,"max":480},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":200},"additional":{"units":4,"amount":70}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":16},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"blended","counterRate":100,"baseAmount":600,"estHours":2,"travelExpense":35,"payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":200},"additional":{"units":4,"amount":100}},"counterDate":{"start":"2026-09-16T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T19:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":60,"mode":"hours","reason":"arrival_window"}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-16T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-17T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-17T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T18:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-16T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"gap"},{"start":"2026-09-17T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"Possible cutover"},{"start":"2026-09-17T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"Danik Furni