{"job":{"id":19960105,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Thrive Networks","title":"NC Onsite Needed - Install two network lines","description":{"html":"<p>Install two network lines</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Scope of Work</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Make sure to include an accurate and detailed account of what was performed in your closing notes. Please do not just say \"completed\" or words to that effect. Need details to share with our client</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>When you arrive check in with POC and call and work with Thrive Remote Engineer</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Description of Work:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Install two network lines</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Expected Outcome:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>New office space will have two working network lines installed</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Procedural Steps to Complete Work:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Clinic has a new office space they need new lines installed. Space was used for storage originally. We need network ports installed on both walls in the room. Network rack is on the 2nd floor and room is on the first floor. Each run is going to be about 150-200 ft. Recommend bringing 400 ft of cabling. Ceilings are drop tiles and about 10-11 ft tall. Room is currently unused so you should be free to work on there without issue. Need line run from network rack to room. Ceilings are drop tiles. Port needs to got on each wall. Onsite contact, Jeff, can give you more details about the wall plate placement.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Please do not leave premises until Thrive Remote Engineer releases you</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Contacts</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><del>******** *** *********** ********************* ********</del></li>\n<li><del>****** ****** ******** * **** ****** ************ ***** ******** **** **** ***** *** ** **********</del></li>\n<li><del>****** ** * **** *****</del></li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Equipment Required</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Mobile phone</li>\n<li>Laptop</li>\n<li>Ladder to reach 10 ft ceiling</li>\n<li>Cable Testers and toners</li>\n<li>400 ft of cabling</li>\n<li>Qty (2) 7 ft patch cables for switch to patch panel</li>\n<li>rj 45 connectors</li>\n<li>punch down tool</li>\n<li>crimpers</li>\n<li>keystone jacks</li>\n<li>wall plates</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Dress code</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Your attire should be business professional</li>\n<li>Dress shoes, slacks, button-down shirt, polo shirt, or sweater</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Work Order Acceptance</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Check out with Thrive Support Contact before leaving</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"Install two network lines\n\n**Scope of Work**\n\n**Make sure to include an accurate and detailed account of what was performed in your closing notes. Please do not just say \"completed\" or words to that effect. Need details to share with our client**\n\n- When you arrive check in with POC and call and work with Thrive Remote Engineer\n\n**Description of Work:**\n\n- Install two network lines\n\n**Expected Outcome:**\n\n- New office space will have two working network lines installed\n\n**Procedural Steps to Complete Work:**\n\n- Clinic has a new office space they need new lines installed. Space was used for storage originally. We need network ports installed on both walls in the room. Network rack is on the 2nd floor and room is on the first floor. Each run is going to be about 150-200 ft. Recommend bringing 400 ft of cabling. Ceilings are drop tiles and about 10-11 ft tall. Room is currently unused so you should be free to work on there without issue. Need line run from network rack to room. Ceilings are drop tiles. Port needs to got on each wall. Onsite contact, Jeff, can give you more details about the wall plate placement.\n\n**Please do not leave premises until Thrive Remote Engineer releases you**\n\n**Contacts**\n\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* 