the customer to borrow equipment or any form of transportation. Remain Professional and Contact your project manager for assistance.</em></p><p>The preferred&nbsp;method of communication to the Project Manager is via Phone. If you can't reach the Project Manager via phone, send messages within the Field Nation work order.&nbsp;In cases where a problem needs to be escalated or contact cannot be established report this to&nbsp;mobile.pm@pro-vigil.com referencing the Field Nation work order number and TKT.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>If other issues arise and a simple and effective solution cannot be established contact your Project Manager as soon as the problem arises.</p><p><strong><em>If for any reason you are to leave the site call the Project Manager to ensure accountability and No delays on scheduled Project.</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>By No means will Technician leave the site without speaking to the Project Manager In Charge.&nbsp;</em></strong></p>","markdown":"**\\*\\*NEW \\*\\***\n\n**1. Must Take a picture of every solar unit installed (SG or SPS) which indicates that the solar panels are facing South. Failure to attach pictures will result in an incomplete job and can affect the payout. PV will request to go back on site and take pictures as mentioned above free of return charge before closing the WO. No Exceptions**\n\n**You can use the mobile app of AR Compass 3D & Timestamp Camera**\n\n**2. Please follow the step below to complete the install. Note the is MANDATORY for all the Technicians performing and Install starting 03/01/2024**\n\nWhen the installation is complete the technician must call (866) 413-9969\n\nTechnician must stay on site and provide information and documentation to the Field Tech Support Team to Completion. A technician can not leave site until they are released by the FTS team. *FTS SUPPORT LINE : 210-858-1108 - our agents can experience high call volumes at times, if you are having issues reaching FTS then please reach out to the PM team*\n\n**Subject: Mobile Install Support**\n\n**Zendesk Ticket Number: 1129103**\n\n**\\# of units to relocate: 1**\n\n**Unit numbers:** MDX2522 / SG1336\n\n**Was a forklift ordered? : Forklift scheduled**\n\n**Relocation details: Unit is currently located in the middle of the road and needed to be relocated on the same street. Please confirm placement with poc onsite**\n\n **Screenshot of the GPS location of the units install, mark also the direction that the cameras are pointing**\n\n**Clear pictures of the unit are required once install is completed (Unit numbers must be clear)**\n\n**Camera views must be approved by the site POC, if you are not able to reach the POC please reach out to the PM team**\n\nThis is mandatory, if pictures are not submitted, this may result in non-payment\n\n **\\*\\*\\* Travel needs to be approved prior to accepting the WO\\*\\*\\***\n\n**Provider Expectations**\n\n- Accepting this scope of work is an acknowledgment that failure to meet these requirements will result in a Non-Payment. Upon acceptance of work, Pro-Vigil will release payment.\n- All work performed must have a 30-day warranty on workmanship and the technician should be available within 48 hours of issues with the site.\n- Work that must be re-performed will be at no cost to Pro-Vigil and will result in non-payment or delayed payment.\n- *\\*\\* Equipment Rentals are the sole responsibility of Technician PV will not provide rentals upon request.*\n- We hold our employees and contractors to the highest standard\n- Pro-Vigil pays a Flat installation rate, Hourly charges and travel are not covered or considered for a change in payout.\n- Travel and delays are responsibilities of Technicians.\n- Technician Assumes all travel and time expenses necessary to complete this Project.\n- ***\\*\\*Ensure that all equipment is always accounted for.***\n\n**Overview:**\n\n1. Seeking technician with CCTV/LVC experience for installation of mobile security device.\n2. The start time mandatory and *you must show up on time.*\n3. Provider should expect to be onsite for up to 2 hours per unit.\n\n**Equipment Shipment Information**\n\n- Pro-Vigil ships all equipment to be installed to the service location.\n- Exception would be to local Fed Ex in some events. Must verify receipt of all equipment and pictures required.\n\n**Required Tools & Materials**\n\n*\\*\\*\\*\\*These Items are the* ***Minimum Required*** *Tools for Completion of Job. By no means will Technician show up to site without the following equipment. Items are the sole responsibility of technician.\\*\\*\\*\\*Do not contact the customer to borrow equipment or any form of transportation.*\n\n**Tools**\n\nWindows laptop\n\n25’ Cat6 ethernet patch cable\n\nImpact drill\n\nModular data cable crimper\n\nLittle Giant 22 ft A-Frame extension ladder\n\nHusky 5 Piece Torx Screwdriver Set\n\nImpact Nut Driving Set\n\n600V Auto Ranging Digital Multimeter\n\nTone & Probe PRO\n\nElectrical Wire Tracing Set (VDV500-820)\n\nScout Pro 3 Tester Kit\n\nScrewdriver Set 1/4\n\nKeystone & #2 Phillip Cushion Grip 2 pc\n\nStandard Long Nose\n\nSide Cutting Pliers\n\nLineman's Pliers with New England Nose\n\nHigh Leverage Diagonal Cutting Pliers\n\nSolid and Stranded Copper Wire Stripper and Cutter\n\n**Safety equipment**\n\nGeneral Purpose Full-Brim\n\nHard Hat\n\nSafety Boot, Steel Toe\n\nSafety Glasses\n\nU-Back Vests and D-Ring Slot for Fall Protection\n\nSafety Harness with 6 ft/Shock Absorbing Lanyard\n\n**Pre-Site Tasks**\n\n1. Set your ETA for the work order\n2. Verify you have received your TKT number and information from the PM\n\n**On-Site Tasks**\n\n*Contact the Project Manager with any issues.*\n\n1. Check-in\n2. Call tech support and refer to your TKT number, to check if they have access to the equipment *FTS SUPPORT LINE : 210-858-1108*\n3. Take a picture of Unit#\n4. Take pictures of solar panels connected to each mobile unit with compass confirmation that the panels are facing south\n5. Screenshot of the GPS location of the units install, mark also the direction that the cameras are pointing\n6. Tech Support will confirm camera views and updates SF and ZD ticket as confirmation that tech has checked in\n7. Once views are verified with site POC, upload a screenshot of the conversation\n8. Take a full picture of where the unit is sitting to verify the area is clean and up to quality standards\n\n*If for any reason you are to leave the site call the Project Manager to ensure accountability and No delays on the scheduled Project.*\n\n*By No means will the Technician leave the site without speaking to the FTS team.*\n\n**Post-Site Tasks, Deliverables Required For Approval and Payment**\n\n1. Pictures of MDX and SPS, MAC and Router IP\n2. Pictures of Air Card HEX, Static IP, Unit#\n3. Pictures of all units on site, along with solar panels connected to each mobile unit\n4. *If there are multiple units,* tech will provide a brief description of which unit is tied into. (I.E: MDX1234/SPS4567 add on camera 10.1.10.10)\n5. Run a speed test\n6. Pictures sent to mobile.pm@pro-vigil.com\n7. Install Pro-Vigil signs in the job site, make sure these are visible.\n8. Mark the work order as complete for payment\n\n**Required For Approval and Payment:**\n\n- Accepting this scope of work is an acknowledgment that failure to meet these requirements will result in a monetary penalty. Upon approval of work order, Pro-Vigil will release payment. All work performed must have a 30-day warranty on workmanship. Work that must be reperformed will be at no cost to Pro-Vigil and will result in non-payment or delayed payment.\n- Upon Pro-Vigil’s acceptance of work, payment will be made through Field Nation. Any amounts not outlined in this scope of work will not be paid. Any changes in the scope of work requiring monetary adjustments must be made in writing and approved by the assigned project manager.\n\n**Explanation of Pay**\n\n- Pro-Vigil will no longer accept counter offers or reimburse post-install\n- Accepting the WO is an agreement that Pro-Vigil will release payment upon completion of the scope of work\n- Any Extra Charges will need authorization before adding it as an extra expense otherwise it will be declined\n- Acceptance of the WO is also acceptance of the scope of work and Payout.\n- Work Order will only be approved once all the pictures will pass an approval process. Please provide enough pictures of the whole install or you will be asked to return on-site at your own expense. Failure to do so will result in Delay/No Payment,\n- A 10% - 20% penalty will be applied for delays caused by tech. A penalty will be applied, 10%-20%, if technician can't provide the required tools/software as listed in the Scope of Work.\n- Once Receipt of these documents has been fulfilled, Approval for payment will be authorized and approved on Field Nation. Failure to provide all of the deliverables will result in Delay/No Payment.\n\n**Escalation For Issues - *Who To Call When***\n\n*All communication will go thru from Technician to Project Manager and back. When complete the technician must call out Field Tech Support at FTS SUPPORT LINE : 210-858-1108 .When dealing with issues with layout and or site-specific problems the customer may be contacted. Do not contact the customer to borrow equipment or any form of transportation. Remain Professional and Contact your project manager for assistance.*\n\nThe preferred method of communication to the Project Manager is via Phone. If you can't reach the Project Manager via phone, send messages within the Field Nation work order. In cases where a problem needs to be escalated or contact cannot be established report this to mobile.pm@pro-vigil.com referencing the Field Nation work order number and TKT.\n\nIf other issues arise and a simple and effective solution cannot be established contact your Project Manager as soon as the problem arises.\n\n***If for any reason you are to leave the site call the Project Manager to ensure accountability and No delays on scheduled Project.***\n\n***By No means will Technician leave the site without speaking to the Project Manager In Charge.***","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-16T11:00","end":"2026-09-16T14:00","latestStart":"2026-09-16T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":450,"max":450},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":79},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"fixed","counterRate":150,"baseAmount":450,"estHours":3,"travelExpense":115,"payStructure":null},"reason":"TRAVEL_REQUIRED","rejectDetails":"Travel required (79mi reported + 10mi padding = 89mi > 20mi)"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-16T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-17T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-17T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T18:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-16T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"gap"},{"start":"2026-09-17T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"Possible cutover"},{"start":"2026-09-17T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"Danik Furniture"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-21T14:01:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T18:01:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 04546900 Preiss Co View at Legacy Oaks Cutover/Test Install Wizard (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 059