{"job":{"id":19960755,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Cloud5 Communications","title":"Tech Dispatch Request - Ticket 1551490","description":{"html":"<p>***Technician Check-In/Check-Out Requirements</p>\n<p>The assigned technician is required to perform both check-in and check-out procedures with onsite personnel and Cloud5 Remote Support throughout the service engagement.</p>\n<p>Check-In Procedure:</p>\n<p>Upon arrival, the technician must:</p>\n<p>Check in with the designated onsite contact.</p>\n<p>Immediately contact Cloud5 Remote Support to confirm arrival.</p>\n<p>Provide the full name of the onsite contact with whom they have checked in.</p>\n<p>Check-Out Procedure:</p>\n<p>Upon completion of all work, the technician must:</p>\n<p>Check out with the onsite contact.</p>\n<p>Contact Cloud5 Remote Support to confirm completion of work.</p>\n<p>Provide the full name of the onsite contact with whom they have checked out.</p>\n<p>Compliance Requirement:</p>\n<p>Adherence to these procedures is mandatory and failure to complete them may result in delays to payment processing and/or forfeiture of payment</p>\n<p>****Technicians may not enter any occupied guest room without an escort from site***</p>\n<p><strong>Issue: ****All 6th floor is experiencing the issue - HSIA</strong></p>\n<p>Room 614 TV is not working</p>\n<p>We need a tech dispatched to perform TROUBLESHOOTING OF MULTIPLE OFFLINE ACCESS POINTS, INCLUDING AP53119 IN ROOM 614, AND VERIFY PHYSICAL/CABLING CONNECTIVITY.</p>\n<p>Please make sure the tech has the following tools: A CABLE TESTER, TOOLS TO TROUBLESHOOT/REPAIR CAT5 CABLE, A LAPTOP, A CONSOLE CABLE.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>The dispatch should be scheduled for between 15th September 2026 and 18th September 2026.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Please make sure the tech has the following tools: A CABLE TESTER, TOOLS TO TROUBLESHOOT/REPAIR CAT5 CABLE, A LAPTOP, A CONSOLE CABLE.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>You must work with the NOC to resolve whatever issue the ticket/dispatch was requested for, and any other issue on site until resolution is confirmed by the NOC.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>We need a tech onsite to work with our NOC and investigate reported claims of issues with the wireless network at a site.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>The tech will need:</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>-Basic hand tools</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>-Butt Set</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>-Ladder</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>-Cat5/5e Cable</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>-Glow Rods</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>-Fish Tape</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>-Fully charged cell phone</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>-Charged Windows laptop with signal testing software and a functional ethernet port</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>-Serial cable</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>-Camera</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>-RJ45 crimp tool</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>-RJ45 CAT5e male and female ends</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>-Cable Qualifier/Certifier</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>-Toner</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Call our NOC upon arrival, 877.842.0107, and reference ticket 1551490. Work with our NOC to troubleshoot and restore service to access point down. You must work with the NOC to resolve whatever issue the ticket/dispatch was requested for, and any other issue on site until resolution is confirmed by the NOC.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>***Tech needs to check-in and work with remote support before beginning any work on site. Ensure the tech has the HSIA Onsite Tech phone number (877.842.0107) and understands he needs to check in as soon as he arrives onsite.***</p>","markdown":"\\*\\*\\*Technician Check-In/Check-Out Requirements\n\nThe assigned technician is required to perform both check-in and check-out procedures with onsite personnel and Cloud5 Remote Support throughout the service engagement.\n\nCheck-In Procedure:\n\nUpon arrival, the technician must:\n\nCheck in with the designated onsite contact.\n\nImmediately contact Cloud5 Remote Support to confirm arrival.\n\nProvide the full name of the onsite contact with whom they have checked in.\n\nCheck-Out Procedure:\n\nUpon completion of all work, the technician must:\n\nCheck out with the onsite contact.\n\nContact Cloud5 Remote Support to confirm completion of work.\n\nProvide the full name of the onsite contact with whom they have checked out.\n\nCompliance Requirement:\n\nAdherence to these procedures is mandatory and failure to complete them may result in delays to payment processing and/or forfeiture of payment\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*Technicians may not enter any occupied guest room without an escort from site\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Issue: \\*\\*\\*\\*All 6th floor is experiencing the issue - HSIA**\n\nRoom 614 TV is not working\n\nWe need a tech dispatched to perform TROUBLESHOOTING OF MULTIPLE OFFLINE ACCESS POINTS, INCLUDING AP53119 IN ROOM 614, AND VERIFY PHYSICAL/CABLING CONNECTIVITY.\n\nPlease make sure the tech has the following tools: A CABLE TESTER, TOOLS TO TROUBLESHOOT/REPAIR CAT5 CABLE, A LAPTOP, A CONSOLE CABLE.\n\nThe dispatch should be scheduled for between 15th September 2026 and 18th September 2026.\n\nPlease make sure the tech has the following tools: A CABLE TESTER, TOOLS TO TROUBLESHOOT/REPAIR CAT5 CABLE, A LAPTOP, A CONSOLE CABLE.\n\nYou must work with the NOC to resolve whatever issue the ticket/dispatch was requested for, and any other issue on site until resolution is confirmed by the NOC.\n\nWe need a tech onsite to work with our NOC and investigate reported claims of issues with the wireless network at a site.\n\nThe tech will need:\n\n-Basic hand tools\n\n-Butt Set\n\n-Ladder\n\n-Cat5/5e Cable\n\n-Glow Rods\n\n-Fish Tape\n\n-Fully charged cell phone\n\n-Charged Windows laptop with signal testing software and a functional ethernet port\n\n-Serial cable\n\n-Camera\n\n-RJ45 crimp tool\n\n-RJ45 CAT5e male and female ends\n\n-Cable Qualifier/Certifier\n\n-Toner\n\nCall our NOC upon arrival, 877.842.0107, and reference ticket 1551490. Work with our NOC to troubleshoot and restore service to access point down. You must work with the NOC to resolve whatever issue the ticket/dispatch was requested for, and any other issue on site until resolution is confirmed by the NOC.\n\n\\*\\*\\*Tech needs to check-in and work with remote support before beginning any work on site. Ensure the tech has the HSIA Onsite Tech phone number (877.842.0107) and understands he needs to check in as soon as he arrives onsite.\\*\\*\\*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-15T17:00","end":"2026-09-15T19:00","latestStart":"2026-09-15T23:00"},"payRange":{"min":85,"max":170},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":85,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":5},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $170 (countered: $170) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-15T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T16:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-15T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T16:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-17T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-17T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T18:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-15T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"gap"},{"start":"2026-09-15T