{"job":{"id":19960961,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Cloud Integrated Technologies","title":"Pole Mount installation","description":{"html":"<ul><li>This will be a pole-mount installation with a lift</li><li>Estimated duration will be 4 hours</li></ul><p><strong>Job Details:</strong></p><p>Go to Mygrant Glass - Knightdale to install and program the Starlink antenna. I've attached the Deployment Plan and the Starlink assembly instructions. This is how the installation must be completed.</p><p>Here's the picture they've provided.&nbsp;The Green X is where we proposed the wall penetration.</p><p>The red X and line show where they are asking us to mount a pole, do a wall penetration, and run the cable to the network room.</p><p>The service address is listed below as well. Also, bring a ladder in case it's needed.</p><p></p><p><strong>The address </strong></p><p><strong>Address: </strong>560 Hinton Oaks Blvd, Knightdale, NC 27545 US</p><p><strong>Facilities: TBC</strong></p><p><strong>﻿Site Contact #: TBC </strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">The technician will need to bring all of the equipment for wall penetration and cable run. (EMT and Junction Box for weather protection for the wall penetration) and the technician will also need to bring a 5 foot pole, with a diameter no larger than 2.3 inches.&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>IMPORTANT</u></strong>:</p><p>We have a change in process. Please do not touch any Starlink equipment in the box until you call into the installation conference bridge that will be provided. So, once on-site, please call into the conference bridge first before doing anything.</p><p>Once the cable is run from the Starlink antenna through the outer building shell to the designated data room, please attach the cable to the provided Starlink router and, with the help of the network engineer who is on the conference bridge, program the router to connect with the satellites.</p><p>Once testing and programming are complete, you are done.</p><p>Please leave the installation site clean.</p><p>Take installation through completion of project pictures, as these will be used as records for completion and to memorialize your work on that site on our website.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>This shouldn't take longer than 4 hours</strong></p><p><strong>The installer should bring a ladder (in case one is needed).</strong></p><p><strong>The installer must bring a laptop.&nbsp;</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Dress Code:</strong></p><ul><li>Business Casual.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Tools Required: Must-Haves</strong></p><ul><li>Laptop computer</li><li>Termination Tools.</li><li>Screws.</li><li>Hammer.</li><li><em>﻿Butt Set.</em></li><li><em>Cable Tester.</em></li><li><em>Fish tape.</em></li><li><em>Push/Pull Rods.</em></li><li><em>Tone Generator.</em></li><li><em>Crimper.</em></li><li><em>Screwdrivers.</em></li><li><em>Zip Ties.</em></li><li><em>Ladder.</em></li><li><em>Cordless Drill.</em></li><li><em>Cable Toners.</em></li><li><em>Structured Cabling</em></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><em>On-Site Tasks</em></strong></p><ol><li>Check in to the work order.</li><li>Call Juan at tel # 954-751-6202 to check in to work in order to discuss SOW.</li><li>Complete the work based on the job details above.</li><li>Upload photos of the completed work.</li><li>Call Juan to Check-out the work order and confirm that all work is completed.</li></ol><p><strong><em>Required On-Site Deliverables</em></strong></p><ol><li>&nbsp;Photos of both before and after</li><li>Photos of all work and tests</li><li>Collect a signature from on-site contact/manager</li><li>Check-out of work order</li></ol><p><strong>Escalation Process:</strong></p><p><strong>Contact WO Manager if the following are true:</strong></p><ul><li>If clarification is needed on the work order, discuss it with Juan</li><li>Any issues or questions should be escalated to Juan</li></ul><p><strong>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy</strong></p><ul><li>If the work projected goes past the number of hours allocated for the posted job, you must call the office at 954-751-6202 for approval of a requested extension of work.</li><li>If there are any additional material expenses, the materials must be preapproved. Please contact the office for preapproval and upload the receipt to Field Nation if the material is approved.</li><li>Any pay change request, or any additional expenses, must be preapproved.</li></ul>","markdown":"- This will be a pole-mount installation with a lift\n- Estimated duration will be 4 hours\n\n**Job Details:**\n\nGo to Mygrant Glass - Knightdale to install and program the Starlink antenna. I've attached the Deployment Plan and the Starlink assembly instructions. This is how the installation must be completed.\n\nHere's the picture they've provided. The Green X is where we proposed the wall penetration.\n\nThe red X and line show where they are asking us to mount a pole, do a wall penetration, and run the cable to the network room.\n\nThe service address is listed below as well. Also, bring a ladder in case it's needed.\n\n**The address**\n\n**Address:** 560 Hinton Oaks Blvd, Knightdale, NC 27545 US\n\n**Facilities: TBC**\n\n**﻿Site Contact #: TBC**\n\n**The technician will need to bring all of the equipment for wall penetration and cable run. (EMT and Junction Box for weather protection for the wall penetration) and the technician will also need to bring a 5 foot pole, with a diameter no larger than 2.3 inches.**\n\n**IMPORTANT**:\n\nWe have a change in process. Please do not touch any Starlink equipment in the box until you call into the installation conference bridge that will be provided. So, once on-site, please call into the conference bridge first before doing anything.\n\nOnce the cable is run from the Starlink antenna through the outer building shell to the designated data room, please attach the cable to the provided Starlink router and, with the help of the network engineer who is on the conference bridge, program the router to connect with the satellites.\n\nOnce testing and programming are complete, you are done.\n\nPlease leave the installation site clean.\n\nTake installation through completion of project pictures, as these will be used as records for completion and to memorialize your work on that site on our website.\n\n**This shouldn't take longer than 4 hours**\n\n**The installer should bring a ladder (in case one is needed).**\n\n**The installer must bring a laptop.**\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n- Business Casual.\n\n**Tools Required: Must-Haves**\n\n- Laptop computer\n- Termination Tools.\n- Screws.\n- Hammer.\n- *﻿Butt Set.*\n- *Cable Tester.*\n- *Fish tape.*\n- *Push/Pull Rods.*\n- *Tone Generator.*\n- *Crimper.*\n- *Screwdrivers.*\n- *Zip Ties.*\n- *Ladder.*\n- *Cordless Drill.*\n- *Cable Toners.*\n- *Structured Cabling*\n\n***On-Site Tasks***\n\n1. Check in to the work order.\n2. Call Juan at tel # 954-751-6202 to check in to work in order to discuss SOW.\n3. Complete the work based on the job details above.\n4. Upload photos of the completed work.\n5. Call Juan to Check-out the work order and confirm that all work is completed.\n\n***Required On-Site Deliverables***\n\n1. Photos of both before and after\n2. Photos of all work and tests\n3. Collect a signature from on-site contact/manager\n4. Check-out of work order\n\n**Escalation Process:**\n\n**Contact WO Manager if the following are true:**\n\n- If clarification is needed on the work order, discuss it with Juan\n- Any issues or questions should be escalated to Juan\n\n**Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy**\n\n- If the work projected goes past the number of hours allocated for the posted job, you must call the office at 954-751-6202 for approval of a requested extension of work.\n- If there are any additional material expenses, the materials must be preapproved. Please contact the office for preapproval and upload the receipt to Field Nation if the material is approved.\n- Any pay change request, or any additional expenses, must be preapproved.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-23T09:00","end":"2026-09-23T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":350,"max":350},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":13},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $350 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":