{"job":{"id":19955796,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Retail Imaging Management Group, Inc.","title":"Walmart  - Fuji 2x VNXT Kiosk Service Photo Center (Epson Flatbed Scanner Replacement) - 2 Hours Onsite","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>OVERVIEW:</u>&nbsp;</strong>Seeking a technician to perform service on a Walmart VNX-T Photo Kiosk Terminal located in the Photo Center. The service will include replacing the VNX-T Kiosk Flatbed Scanner and test functionality.</p><p><strong><u>SERVICE NOTES:</u></strong></p><p>VNXT-1.0<br /><br />MFGVNXT07472<br /><br />2X Epson Scanner replacement<br /><br />FIN: 281435<br /><br />FedEx Outbound #877171710524<br /><br />FedEx Return #877171733753<br /><br />FIN: 281408<br /><br />FedEx Outbound #877171643821<br /><br />FedEx Return #877171668696<br /></p><p><strong><u>PARTS CONFIRMATION:</u></strong></p><p>Parts Being Shipped See Shipment Field for Tracking.</p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\"><u>WALMART SCINTTILA IN-STORE APP ACCOUNT REQUIRED:</u></strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><em style=\"color: black;\">Walmart Scintilla In-Store Account Explanation Link:</em></p><p>https://training.rimg.net/shared/start/key:ZTLDNHRK</p><p><strong><u>LICENCES/CERTIFICATIONS/CHECKS REQUIRED:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Background Check with No Warrants</li><li>Walmart Scintilla In-Store App on Mobile Phone</li><li>Walmart Scintilla In-Store</li></ul><p><strong><u>TOOLS/SUPPLIES REQUIRED:</u></strong></p><ul><li>VNX-T Photo Kiosk Operations Manual (document attached to work order).</li><li>VNX-T Flatbed Scanner Replacement Guide (document attached to work order).</li><li>USB Keyboard and Mouse</li><li>Screwdriver Set (#1 and #2 Phillips)</li><li>Pliers</li><li>Basic Tool Kit</li><li>Parts (located at the store)</li><li>Fujifilm Technical Services ID Badge (or temporary badge from the customer service desk).</li></ul><p><strong><u>JOB SCOPE:</u></strong></p><p><em>Pre-Visit Tasks</em></p><ol><li>Within 24 hours of the visit contact the location to notify them of your ETA.</li><li>Confirm that all parts associated with the tracking number in the work order have been delivered&nbsp;<strong>before</strong>&nbsp;heading to the site.&nbsp;<strong>DO NOT GO ONSITE WITHOUT VERIFYING PARTS HAVE BEEN DELIVERED.</strong></li><li>Watch the training video links and review the attached support documents.</li></ol><p><em>Test Order Creation Instructions</em></p><p><del>*******************************************************</del></p><p><em>Parts Return Procedure: </em></p><p><del>***************************************************</del></p><p><em>Onsite Tasks</em></p><ol><li>When you arrive at the Walmart location, check in using the&nbsp;<strong>Walmart Scintilla&nbsp;In</strong>‑<strong>Store&nbsp;app</strong>. If you do not have a physical badge, go to the&nbsp;<strong>Customer Service desk</strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;notify them&nbsp;that you are a vendor&nbsp;representing&nbsp;<strong>Fujifilm Technical Services for the Photo Center</strong>. Inform them that you do not have a hard copy of your badge and need one printed. Show your Scintilla&nbsp;In‑Store&nbsp;ID badge in the app, and once issued, place the printed badge on the&nbsp;<strong>upper left side of your shirt</strong>.&nbsp;</li><li>Confirm the reported issue with the&nbsp;<strong>Manager on Duty (MOD)</strong>&nbsp;or the&nbsp;<strong>Photo Center operator</strong>.&nbsp;</li><li>If parts were shipped in advance,&nbsp;locate&nbsp;them and keep all the associated packaging, including the overpack box, as it may be used later to return parts after the service is complete.&nbsp;</li><li>Contact the&nbsp;<strong>support team at</strong>&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************</del></span>&nbsp;to confirm the troubleshooting steps needed to diagnose the issue.</li><li>After the service is complete, take a picture of the VNXT Kiosk in operation.&nbsp;<strong>Create an order</strong>&nbsp;and confirm with the Photo Center Operator that it transfers to the Landscape server.</li><li>Contact our&nbsp;<strong>support team at</strong>&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************</del></span>&nbsp;to remotely validate the VNXT kiosk is functional, confirm the deliverables and determine&nbsp;whether any parts must be&nbsp;<strong>returned, disposed of, or left on</strong>‑<strong>site</strong>&nbsp;if considered consumables.&nbsp;</li><li>All <strong>used and unused parts</strong> must be reviewed and confirmed by Support to determine return or disposal requirements. Use the Fuji Parts Return App link to review each part received and confirm their return disposition https://fujifilm-service.jotform.com/app/251316860580961?utm_source=share-qr&amp;utm_medium=website&amp;utm_campaign=portal-app&amp;utm_term=251316860580961. Take a screenshot of all the parts entered to confirm their disposition for return and upload as a deliverable for review.</li><li>If parts are approved for disposal, place them in the&nbsp;<strong>trash</strong>.&nbsp;</li><li>If parts&nbsp;are required to&nbsp;be returned, complete the&nbsp;<strong>Parts Return Form</strong>.&nbsp;</li><li>Pack return parts securely in the original or replacement packaging&nbsp;<strong>and the required overpack box</strong>.&nbsp;<strong>NOTE:&nbsp;</strong>All parts returned to Fujifilm must be shipped in an overpack box. Take a photo of the packaged parts before sealing the box, apply the&nbsp;<strong>FedEx return label</strong>, and clearly write the&nbsp;<strong>Astea Reference #</strong>&nbsp;next to the label.</li><li>If a FedEx return label is&nbsp;<strong>not used</strong>, it must be&nbsp;<strong>destroyed or taken with you</strong>&nbsp;for use on a future visit.&nbsp;</li><li><strong>Do not leave any return packages at the Walmart location</strong>. All returns must be dropped off at a&nbsp;<strong>FedEx pickup center</strong>, and a&nbsp;<strong>receipt must be&nbsp;retained</strong>&nbsp;to confirm transfer of possession.&nbsp;</li><li>Complete the work order, check out with the&nbsp;<strong>MOD</strong>, obtain their&nbsp;<strong>signature</strong>, and check out of the&nbsp;<strong>Walmart Scintilla&nbsp;In</strong>‑<strong>Store&nbsp;app</strong>&nbsp;before leaving the location.&nbsp;</li></ol><p><em>Post-Visit Tasks</em></p><ol><li>Take the return parts package to a local&nbsp;<strong>FedEx Pickup Center</strong>, have them scan the label and provide a received receipt. The received receipt must be uploaded to the Work Order for approval. This step is&nbsp;<strong>not compensated&nbsp;</strong>for in the hours worked as FedEx return packages can be dropped off at any Walgreens location and many other locations easily identified in a Google search.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong><u>DELIVERABLES REQUIRED:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Work Order Completed and Signed by Store Manager on Duty</li><li>Image of the VNXT Kiosk Before Service</li><li>Image of Any Parts Replaced</li><li>Image of the VNXT Kiosk After Service with the Software Running</li><li>Image of a Completed Order Receipt from the VNXT Kiosk</li><li>Image of the Parts Return Form Completed</li><li>Any part(s) being returned must be documented by taking a picture each of the&nbsp;<strong><em>part in the box packaged the same way the part was packaged when received to avoid damage</em></strong>,&nbsp;<strong><em>return form filled out</em></strong>,&nbsp;<strong><em>sealed packaging with return label attached</em></strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong><em>Astea # written on the outside of the box</em></strong>.</li><li>If parts are being returned, a picture of a received receipt showing the package was taken position by a FedEx pickup center.</li></ul><p><strong><u>CODE OF CONDUCT:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Review the following link as our expectations for onsite conduct while representing RIMG and their clients.</li></ul><p><em>RIMG Code of Conduct Policy</em></p><p>https://training.rimg.net/shared/start/key:ZTZDNHRK</p><p><strong><u>ESCALATION CONTACTS:</u></strong></p><ul><li>For technical support or clarification of the work order expectations call <del>***** ******** </del>and follow the menu prompts.</li></ul><p><strong><u>COMPENSATION:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Retail Imaging pays a Blended rate of $100.00 per service visit for two hours onsite, plus $50.00 per&nbsp;<u>pre-approved</u>&nbsp;additional hour worked onsite, and including all expenses. To approve the additional hour onsite you will need to call the escalation contact.</li><li><u>One hour</u>&nbsp;is approved onsite unless otherwise stated in a Work Order.&nbsp;The provider&nbsp;<u>must contact RIMG Support while onsite</u>&nbsp;to approve all additional hours if conditions require additional time to complete the assignment.</li><li>All requested compensation changes must use the<strong>&nbsp;Counteroffer</strong>&nbsp;function and must be submitted and approved&nbsp;<em><u>in advance</u></em><u>&nbsp;of the Work Order assignment</u>&nbsp;to be valid.&nbsp;A properly submitted and approved Counteroffer supersedes and replaces all previous compensation for that Work Order.</li><li>Any other Expenses must be&nbsp;<u>pre-approved</u>&nbsp;and shown in the Pay section of the Work Order before assignment. Expenses require submission of receipt(s) to be paid.</li><li>Failure to comply with this policy and/or failure to properly complete work as assigned, including completion of all tasks and deliverables, may result in non-payment of the Work Order, at Retail Imaging's sole discretion.</li></ul><p><strong><u>PENALTIES:</u></strong></p><p>Retail Imaging expects all Providers to meet or exceed the expectations outlined in each work order. If a Provider fails to do so, Retail Imaging reserves the right to apply penalties at its sole discretion. A minimum penalty of 25% of the total work order value may be applied for any of the following:</p><ul><li><strong>Incomplete or Poor-Quality Deliverables:</strong>&nbsp;Including but not limited to missing or low-quality photos, incomplete documentation, lack of detail on steps performed, or incorrect field entries.</li><li><strong>Arrival/Departure Issues:&nbsp;</strong>Including but not limited to arriving before parts are delivered, arriving outside the scheduled window (including next-day), or checking in/out from off-site.</li><li><strong>Lack of Preparation:</strong>&nbsp;Including but not limited to missing required tools, not reviewing attached documentation, or not watching required training video(s), etc.</li><li><strong>Part Return Violations:</strong>&nbsp;Including but not limited to bundling parts, missing overpack, failing to use original containers, missing or incorrect labels, missing documentation, or returning items that should not be returned.</li></ul><p><em>Penalties may be cumulative, up to 100% of the work order value. Retail Imaging’s decision to apply or waive a penalty does not set a precedent. We also reserve the right to pursue additional remedies in cases of misconduct.</em></p>","markdown":"**OVERVIEW:** Seeking a technician to perform service on a Walmart VNX-T Photo Kiosk Terminal located in the Photo Center. The service will include replacing the VNX-T Kiosk Flatbed Scanner and test functionality.\n\n**SERVICE NOTES:**\n\nVNXT-1.0  \n  \nMFGVNXT07472  \n  \n2X Epson Scanner replacement  \n  \nFIN: 281435  \n  \nFedEx Outbound #877171710524  \n  \nFedEx Return #877171733753  \n  \nFIN: 281408  \n  \nFedEx Outbound #877171643821  \n  \nFedEx Return #877171668696\n\n**PARTS CONFIRMATION:**\n\nParts Being Shipped See Shipment Field for Tracking.\n\n**WALMART SCINTTILA IN-STORE APP ACCOUNT REQUIRED:**\n\n*Walmart Scintilla In-Store Account Explanation Link:*\n\n<https://training.rimg.net/shared/start/key:ZTLDNHRK>\n\n**LICENCES/CERTIFICATIONS/CHECKS REQUIRED:**\n\n- Background Check with No Warrants\n- Walmart Scintilla In-Store App on Mobile Phone\n- Walmart Scintilla In-Store\n\n**TOOLS/SUPPLIES REQUIRED:**\n\n- VNX-T Photo Kiosk Operations Manual (document attached to work order).\n- VNX-T Flatbed Scanner Replacement Guide (document attached to work order).\n- USB Keyboard and Mouse\n- Screwdriver Set (#1 and #2 Phillips)\n- Pliers\n- Basic Tool Kit\n- Parts (located at the store)\n- Fujifilm Technical Services ID Badge (or temporary badge from the customer service desk).\n\n**JOB SCOPE:**\n\n*Pre-Visit Tasks*\n\n1. Within 24 hours of the visit contact the location to notify them of your ETA.\n2. Confirm that all parts associated with the tracking number in the work order have been delivered **before** heading to the site. **DO NOT GO ONSITE WITHOUT VERIFYING PARTS HAVE BEEN DELIVERED.**\n3. Watch the training video links and review the attached support documents.\n\n*Test Order Creation Instructions*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n*Parts Return Procedure:*\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n*Onsite Tasks*\n\n1. When you arrive at the Walmart location, check in using the **Walmart Scintilla In**‑**Store app**. If you do not have a physical badge, go to the **Customer Service desk** and notify them that you are a vendor representing **Fujifilm Technical Services for the Photo Center**. Inform them that you do not have a hard copy of your badge and need one printed. Show your Scintilla In‑Store ID badge in the app, and once issued, place the printed badge on the **upper left side of your shirt**.\n2. Confirm the reported issue with the **Manager on Duty (MOD)** or the **Photo Center operator**.\n3. If parts were shipped in advance, locate them and keep all the associated packaging, including the overpack box, as it may be used later to return parts after the service is complete.\n4. Contact the **support team at** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* to confirm the troubleshooting steps needed to diagnose the issue.\n5. After the service is complete, take a picture of the VNXT Kiosk in operation. **Create an order** and confirm with the Photo Center Operator that it transfers to the Landscape server.\n6. Contact our **support team at** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* to remotely validate the VNXT kiosk is functional, confirm the deliverables and determine whether any parts must be **returned, disposed of, or left on**‑**site** if considered consumables.\n7. All **used and unused parts** must be reviewed and confirmed by Support to determine return or disposal requirements. Use the Fuji Parts Return App link to review each part received and confirm their return disposition https://fujifilm-service.jotform.com/app/251316860580961?utm_source=share-qr&amp;utm_medium=website&amp;utm_campaign=portal-app&amp;utm_term=251316860580961. Take a screenshot of all the parts entered to confirm their disposition for return and upload as a deliverable for review.\n8. If parts are approved for disposal, place them in the **trash**.\n9. If parts are required to be returned, complete the **Parts Return Form**.\n10. Pack return parts securely in the original or replacement packaging **and the required overpack box**. **NOTE:** All parts returned to Fujifilm must be shipped in an overpack box. Take a photo of the packaged parts before sealing the box, apply the **FedEx return label**, and clearly write the **Astea Reference #** next to the label.\n11. If a FedEx return label is **not used**, it must be **destroyed or taken with you** for use on a future visit.\n12. **Do not leave any return packages at the Walmart location**. All returns must be dropped off at a **FedEx pickup center**, and a **receipt must be retained** to confirm transfer of possession.\n13. Complete the work order, check out with the **MOD**, obtain their **signature**, and check out of the **Walmart Scintilla In**‑**Store app** before leaving the location.\n\n*Post-Visit Tasks*\n\n1. Take the return parts package to a local **FedEx Pickup Center**, have them scan the label and provide a received receipt. The received receipt must be uploaded to the Work Order for approval. This step is **not compensated** for in the hours worked as FedEx return packages can be dropped off at any Walgreens location and many other locations easily identified in a Google search.\n\n**DELIVERABLES REQUIRED:**\n\n- Work Order Completed and Signed by Store Manager on Duty\n- Image of the VNXT Kiosk Before Service\n- Image of Any Parts Replaced\n- Image of the VNXT Kiosk After Service with the Software Running\n- Image of a Completed Order Receipt from the VNXT Kiosk\n- Image of the Parts Return Form Completed\n- Any part(s) being returned must be documented by taking a picture each of the ***part in the box packaged the same way the part was packaged when received to avoid damage***, ***return form filled out***, ***sealed packaging with return label attached*** and ***Astea # written on the outside of the box***.\n- If parts are being returned, a picture of a received receipt showing the package was taken position by a FedEx pickup center.\n\n**CODE OF CONDUCT:**\n\n- Review the following link as our expectations for onsite conduct while representing RIMG and their clients.\n\n*RIMG Code of Conduct Policy*\n\n<https://training.rimg.net/shared/start/key:ZTZDNHRK>\n\n**ESCALATION CONTACTS:**\n\n- For technical support or clarification of the work order expectations call \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* and follow the menu prompts.\n\n**COMPENSATION:**\n\n- Retail Imaging pays a Blended rate of $100.00 per service visit for two hours onsite, plus $50.00 per pre-approved additional hour worked onsite, and including all expenses. To approve the additional hour onsite you will need to call the escalation contact.\n- One hour is approved onsite unless otherwise stated in a Work Order. The provider must contact RIMG Support while onsite to approve all additional hours if conditions require additional time to complete the assignment.\n- All requested compensation changes must use the **Counteroffer** function and must be submitted and approved *in advance* of the Work Order assignment to be valid. A properly submitted and approved Counteroffer supersedes and replaces all previous compensation for that Work Order.\n- Any other Expenses must be pre-approved and shown in the Pay section of the Work Order before assignment. Expenses require submission of receipt(s) to be paid.\n- Failure to comply with this policy and/or failure to properly complete work as assigned, including completion of all tasks and deliverables, may result in non-payment of the Work Order, at Retail Imaging's sole discretion.\n\n**PENALTIES:**\n\nRetail Imaging expects all Providers to meet or exceed the expectations outlined in each work order. If a Provider fails to do so, Retail Imaging reserves the right to apply penalties at its sole discretion. A minimum penalty of 25% of the total work order value may be applied for any of the following:\n\n- **Incomplete or Poor-Quality Deliverables:** Including but not limited to missing or low-quality photos, incomplete documentation, lack of detail on steps performed, or incorrect field entries.\n- **Arrival/Departure Issues:** Including but not limited to arriving before parts are delivered, arriving outside the scheduled window (including next-day), or checking in/out from off-site.\n- **Lack of Preparation:** Including but not limited to missing required tools, not reviewing attached documentation, or not watching required training video(s), etc.\n- **Part Return Violations:** Including but not limited to bundling parts, missing overpack, failing to use original containers, missing or incorrect labels, missing documentation, or returning items that should not be returned.\n\n*Penalties may be cumulative, up to 100% of the work order value. Retail Imaging’s decision to apply or waive a penalty does not set a precedent. We also reserve the right to pursue additional remedies in cases of misconduct.*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-16T11:00","end":"2026-09-16T13:00","latestStart":"2026-09-16T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":150},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":100},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":88},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $150 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-16T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T16:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-17T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-17T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T18:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-16T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"gap"},{"start":"2026-09-17T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"Possible cutover"},{"start":"2026-09-17T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T00:30:00.000Z","summary":"Danik Furniture"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05980771-The Edition on Oberlin-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789508589448}
{"job":{"id":19966580,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Park Place Technologies","title":"Install Tech","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Scope</strong>: Installation of 6 devices</p><p><strong> 1</strong>: <span style=\"color: black;\">CX635adwe</span></p><p> <span style=\"color: black;\">75316250930MZ</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\">Old printer to be replaced:</strong></p><p> <span style=\"color: black;\">KM Bizhub C3351 - SN A92F011016911&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong>  2:</strong> <span style=\"color: black;\">MS632dwe</span></p><p> <span style=\"color: black;\">7566607070FH3</span></p><p> <strong style=\"color: black;\">Old printer to be replaced:</strong></p><p> <span style=\"color: black;\">KM Bizhub 4702P - SN 460092130VWPW&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong> 3</strong>: <span style=\"color: black;\">MS632dwe</span></p><p> <span style=\"color: black;\">7566615070WXV</span></p><p> <strong style=\"color: black;\">Old printer to be replaced:</strong></p><p> <span style=\"color: black;\">KM Bizhub C3351 - SN CNB9078914&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong> 4: </strong><span style=\"color: black;\">MX822adxe</span></p><p> <span style=\"color: black;\">7465422123461</span></p><p> <strong style=\"color: black;\">Old printer to be replaced:</strong></p><p> <span style=\"color: black;\">KM Bizhub 308e - SN AA6W017000192</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong> 5:</strong> <span style=\"color: black;\">CX963xse with Finisher PTU Fax card Badge Reader</span></p><p> <span style=\"color: black;\">460262540V89T</span></p><p> <strong style=\"color: black;\">Old printer to be replaced:</strong></p><p> <span style=\"color: black;\">KM Bizhub C308 - SN A7PY017016579&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\"> 6:</strong><span style=\"color: black;\"> CX963xse with Finisher PTU Fax card Badge Reader</span></p><p> <span style=\"color: black;\">460262940VWKN</span></p><p> <strong style=\"color: black;\">Old printer to be replaced:</strong></p><p> <span style=\"color: black;\">KM Bizhub C308 - SN A7PY017016579&nbsp;</span></p><p>  </p><p><br></p><p><strong>Quantity by Model(s):&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Note: If there are any items listed in the scope, terms of service, or deliverables section that you are uncertain of or you do not believe you were provided everything you need please email lexmarkprojects@parkplacetech.com and you will receive an immediate response, which will also be pasted into your ticket.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Overall Scope:</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Report any missing equipment to Park Place Technologies immediately so that we can work with our customer onsite to locate it while you are onsite. Failure to do so will result in return trip at your expense if equipment was onsite the whole time.&nbsp;</li><li>Must be able to safely lift up to 50 lbs on single person installs.</li><li>Technicians to check in/out based on workorder instructions that will be clearly defined, which may include, calling/emailing into Park Place Technologies, checking in/out on platform or calling a customer or Park Place Technologies bridge.&nbsp;</li><li>Print all documentation and take to site organized.&nbsp;</li><li>Technician to follow printed install instructions/checklists step by step.&nbsp;</li><li>If the work order requires installation of configuration files, firmware, or drivers, those files will be attached to the work order or a link to download them will be provided in the special instructions section. Technicians agree to take these files to site on 2 USB thumb-drives. (Primary &amp; Back-up).&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians should expect to provide brief training to customers on each newly installed device basic functions.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians may be required to un-box, re-box equipment onsite.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians are generally required to dispose of trash onsite and clean up the area, leaving no trash and debris.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians may be required to take and submit photos on some tickets for verification purposes.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians should have a basic toolset onsite which includes multi-head screwdrivers, plyers, bits, etc.&nbsp;</li><li>Technicians may be required to pass a brief test on the model being installed.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>Terms of Service:&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>By accepting this work order, technician agrees they will not solicit direct work from any Park Place Customers. This includes requesting our customer to share your information with Park Place Competitors that you do not already have a relationship with. Technicians shall abide by Field Nation Terms of Service and Community guidelines for all customer communication.&nbsp;</li><li>All requests for additional funds on ticket are to be made at the time of ticket request, unless otherwise agreed upon by Park Place in the scope of the ticket (Ex: reimbursement for supplies we request you bring or out of town travel costs). This means additional travel costs, bonus requests, expense reimbursements are visible up front to Park Place Technologies. Park Place does not agree to any additional costs paid for additional time onsite due to technicians' failure to read install documentation. Park Place recommends technicians immediately refer to the 1st steps in the install instructions on arrival to site to avoid delays onsite.</li><li>Additionally, at no time are technicians to share proprietary information with our customers, including rates, mode of assigning technicians, how and when paid or any other obviously proprietary information.&nbsp;</li><li>By accepting this work order you agree that you (the assigned technician) are doing the work on this ticket and no one is being sent in your place to perform the services. Failure to follow this term can result in non-payment of the ticket. All technicians approved by Park Place Technologies to do work must have their own profile with positive ratings and tech name and direct number listed and been vetted by Park Place Technologies as qualified to service our customers. Any deviance from this will result in removal from providing service for Park Place Technologies. Do not request this work order if you cannot abide by this term.&nbsp;</li><li>Dress is business causal - this means slacks or khakis, collared shirt, and shoes - no jeans, shorts, tennis shoes, t-shirts, 3rd party logos, ripped or dirty clothing, etc.</li><li>All Deliverable Instructions must be followed. Failure to comply will request in you returning within 24 hours to retrieve deliverables at your cost. Failure to return deliverables in 24 hours will result in Park Place Technologies hiring someone to retrieve them, and that amount deducted from your work order.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Time and Date: Time and date unless otherwise listed in the ticket is non-negotiable. Park Place Technologies understands there are at times extenuating circumstances that prevent on-time arrival. Notifying Park Place Technologies immediately in these circumstances by emailing lexmarkprojects@parkplacetech.com will ensure we are notified quickly.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li></ul>","markdown":"**Scope**: Installation of 6 devices\n\n **1**: CX635adwe\n\n 75316250930MZ\n\n**Old printer to be replaced:**\n\n KM Bizhub C3351 - SN A92F011016911\n\n **2:** MS632dwe\n\n 7566607070FH3\n\n **Old printer to be replaced:**\n\n KM Bizhub 4702P - SN 460092130VWPW\n\n **3**: MS632dwe\n\n 7566615070WXV\n\n **Old printer to be replaced:**\n\n KM Bizhub C3351 - SN CNB9078914\n\n **4:** MX822adxe\n\n 7465422123461\n\n **Old printer to be replaced:**\n\n KM Bizhub 308e - SN AA6W017000192\n\n **5:** CX963xse with Finisher PTU Fax card Badge Reader\n\n 460262540V89T\n\n **Old printer to be replaced:**\n\n KM Bizhub C308 - SN A7PY017016579\n\n **6:** CX963xse with Finisher PTU Fax card Badge Reader\n\n 460262940VWKN\n\n **Old printer to be replaced:**\n\n KM Bizhub C308 - SN A7PY017016579\n\n**Quantity by Model(s):**\n\nNote: If there are any items listed in the scope, 