{"job":{"id":19966341,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"SISL Infotech (US) Inc","title":"Scissors lift certified tech required || Greensboro, NC  27405 USA","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Overview</u></strong>:-</p><p>1 Engineer required for Cutover on 20th sep at 4:30 PM EST</p><p>1 Engineer required for Hypercare on 21 st sep 5:30 AM EST.</p><ul><li>Tech must have PPE kit , lanyard, harness, scissors lift operation certificate.</li><li>Onsite engineer to carry a flash drive with Cisco Code 17.15.5 code loaded on this, laptop, console cable, labeller.</li></ul><p><strong><u>Scope of Work</u></strong></p><p>1. Switch Activities</p><p>- Rack and stack the Cisco C9300/C9600 switches (Pre-configured) and remove/replace the legacy switches on site.</p><p>- Assist the remote team with configuration updates on the existing Cisco C9200 switches.</p><p>- Engineer will download required firmware in advance and copy it in a USB Pen Drive (Min. 8 or 16 GB) to the site.</p><p>- Label all new devices with hostnames per the agreed nomenclature.</p><p>- Swap all cables from old to new switches and label them per customer requirements (format: Switchname_Cable1, Cable2, etc.).</p><p>- Perform general cable management (dressing, routing, securing cables).</p><p>- Assist the remote team with execution of IQ/OQ testing.</p><p>- Take pre and post-work photographs of racks and switches, and complete switch details in customer rack template on site.</p><p>- Record make and model of all equipment mounted in the same rack in the customer provided template.</p><p>- Follow the customer agreed rollback plan in case the cutover cannot be completed successfully.</p><p>- Assist with providing console to the remote team to perform the post-cutover verification/Troubleshooting.</p><p>- Capture serial numbers of removed and installed switches for asset tracking.</p><p>- Follow customer instructions and handover the legacy devices to SPOC.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>2. Access Point Activities</p><p>- Replace existing Access Points with new models.</p><p>- Mount new APs at locations where cabling has already been laid out by customer team.</p><p>- Engineer will be provided with a floor map showing the new/existing AP locations.</p><p>- Label all APs per the agreed nomenclature.</p><p>- Confirm AP mounting height/weight and any special mounting hardware needed.</p><p>- Remote team will perform post-install verification that each AP is powered, joins the WLC, and is broadcasting as expected.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>3. Engineer Readiness</p><p>Our assigned technician will bring all necessary tools and equipment on site.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Screwdrivers, pliers, nippers, battery-powered screw gun, scissors, velcro strips,</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Label Printer with extra labels/cartage.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Flashlight</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Laptop with fully charged battery, and laptop charger</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Extension cord, if permitted on site</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Plug converter (C20 to NEMA 5-15/20R, or C13 to NEMA 5-15/20R) for connecting to rack power to charge laptop/Mobile phone, if permitted by the facility/customer</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Phone charger.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Phone camera for documenting completed work or issues.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Mobile hotspot for remote Teams/Webex sessions</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;USB flash drive (32 GB) preloaded with Cisco IOS code 17.15.5</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;USB-to-serial adapter for console access</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;USB A-to-B cable</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;USB A-to-mini-B cable</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;USB A-to-micro-B cable</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Appropriate clothing for a cold data center environment</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;5 new LAN patch cables, standard length 2 meters</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Ladder for Switch/Access Point installation activities within the office site.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Site-specific PPE (safety shoes, hi-vis vest, hard hat, etc.), if required beyond a standard office/data center environment.</p><p><strong><u>POST-SITE</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>REQUIRED DELIVERABLES</u></strong></p><ul><li>Completed excel data sheet.</li><li>Pictures of the IT equipment at site.</li></ul><p><strong><u>ESCALATIONS</u></strong></p><ul><li>All escalations to be directed to remote bridge line</li></ul><p><strong>Prerequisite:</strong></p><ul><li>All defined prerequisites items required for site access must be available and carried to customer site. In absence of any below listed item, access to site will not be granted and the work order will be cancelled simultaneously without further notice.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong><u>ADDITIONAL HOURS &amp; EXPENSES APPROVAL PAYMENT POLICY::</u></strong></p><ul><li>Unexpected expenses, such as parking fees, may be paid, ONLY if a receipt is submitted in the Field Nation App, and communicated to the Work Order Manager upon arrival to the work site.</li><li>Travel expenses such as mileage will not be paid when submitted upon completion of a work order. Any travel expenses must be included with a counteroffer to be eligible for consideration.</li><li>Additional hours will only be paid with prior approval from the Work Order Manager.</li></ul>","markdown":"**Overview**:-\n\n1 Engineer required for Cutover on 20th sep at 4:30 PM EST\n\n1 Engineer required for Hypercare on 21 st sep 5:30 AM EST.\n\n- Tech must have PPE kit , lanyard, harness, scissors lift operation certificate.\n- Onsite engineer to carry a flash drive with Cisco Code 17.15.5 code loaded on this, laptop, console cable, labeller.\n\n**Scope of Work**\n\n1\\. Switch Activities\n\n\\- Rack and stack the Cisco C9300/C9600 switches (Pre-configured) and remove/replace the legacy switches on site.\n\n\\- Assist the remote team with configuration updates on the existing Cisco C9200 switches.\n\n\\- Engineer will download required firmware in advance and copy it in a USB Pen Drive (Min. 8 or 16 GB) to the site.\n\n\\- Label all new devices with hostnames per the agreed nomenclature.\n\n\\- Swap all cables from old to new switches and label them per customer requirements (format: Switchname\\_Cable1, Cable2, etc.).\n\n\\- Perform general cable management (dressing, routing, securing cables).\n\n\\- Assist the remote team with execution of IQ/OQ testing.\n\n\\- Take pre and post-work photographs of racks and switches, and complete switch details in customer rack template on site.\n\n\\- Record make and model of all equipment mounted in the same rack in the customer provided template.\n\n\\- Follow the customer agreed rollback plan in case the cutover cannot be completed successfully.\n\n\\- Assist with providing console to the remote team to perform the post-cutover verification/Troubleshooting.\n\n\\- Capture serial numbers of removed and installed switches for asset tracking.\n\n\\- Follow customer instructions and handover the legacy devices to SPOC.\n\n2\\. Access Point Activities\n\n\\- Replace existing Access Points with new models.\n\n\\- Mount new APs at locations where cabling has already been laid out by customer team.\n\n\\- Engineer will be provided with a floor map showing the new/existing AP locations.\n\n\\- Label all APs per the agreed nomenclature.\n\n\\- Confirm AP mounting height/weight and any special mounting hardware needed.\n\n\\- Remote team will perform post-install verification that each AP is powered, joins the WLC, and is broadcasting as expected.\n\n3\\. Engineer Readiness\n\nOur assigned technician will bring all necessary tools and equipment on site.\n\n· Screwdrivers, pliers, nippers, battery-powered screw gun, scissors, velcro strips,\n\n· Label Printer with extra labels/cartage.\n\n· Flashlight\n\n· Laptop with fully charged battery, and laptop charger\n\n· Extension cord, if permitted on site\n\n· Plug converter (C20 to NEMA 5-15/20R, or C13 to NEMA 5-15/20R) for connecting to rack power to charge laptop/Mobile phone, if permitted by the facility/customer\n\n· Phone charger.\n\n· Phone camera for documenting completed work or issues.\n\n· Mobile hotspot for remote Teams/Webex sessions\n\n· USB flash drive (32 GB) preloaded with Cisco IOS code 17.15.5\n\n· USB-to-serial adapter for console access\n\n· USB A-to-B cable\n\n· USB A-to-mini-B cable\n\n· USB A-to-micro-B cable\n\n· Appropriate clothing for a cold data center environment\n\n· 5 new LAN patch cables, standard length 2 meters\n\n· Ladder for Switch/Access Point installation activities within the office site.\n\n· Site-specific PPE (safety shoes, hi-vis vest, hard hat, etc.), if required beyond a standard office/data center environment.\n\n**POST-SITE**\n\n**REQUIRED DELIVERABLES**\n\n- Completed excel data sheet.\n- Pictures of the IT equipment at site.\n\n**ESCALATIONS**\n\n- All escalations to be directed to remote bridge line\n\n**Prerequisite:**\n\n- All defined prerequisites items required for site access must be available and carried to customer site. In absence of any below listed item, access to site will not be granted and the work order will be cancelled simultaneously without further notice.\n\n**ADDITIONAL HOURS & EXPENSES APPROVAL PAYMENT POLICY::**\n\n- Unexpected expenses, such as parking fees, may be paid, ONLY if a receipt is submitted in the Field Nation App, and communicated to the Work Order Manager upon arrival to the work site.\n- Travel expenses such as mileage will not be paid when submitted upon completion of a work order. Any travel expenses must be included with a counteroffer to be eligible for consideration.\n- Additional hours will only be paid with prior approval from the Work Order Manager.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-20T16:30","end":"2026-09-20T24:30"},"payRange":{"min":35,"max":280},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":35,"estLaborHours":8,"distance":59},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":60,"baseAmount":480,"estHours":8,"travelExpense":90,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-09-24T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T13:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":0}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Miniso"},{"start":"2026-09-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-09-22T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.00