{"job":{"id":"8917272744","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Tech-Americas USA","title":"Incident #267027 - Equipment Board Installation&nbsp;/ ALARM - WAN - ANALOG SKILLS REQUIRED","description":"<p>Scope of Work: Replacing Customer Analog Lines</p><p>________________________________________</p><p>Pre-Application Requirements</p><p>Before submitting your application for any upcoming job:</p><p>•Verify your availability to avoid last-minute cancellations.</p><p>•Ensure smooth coordination by committing to the scheduled time.</p><p>•Analog skills are mandatory for this assignment.</p><p><br></p><p>Important:</p><p>•Technicians must not leave until providing pictures and the signed Work Order to Tech Americas.</p><p>•Hard start time and date.</p><p>•Date or time cannot be rescheduled by any means.</p><p>•Analog skills are a must.</p><p>________________________________________</p><p>PIAB Already Racked and Stacked</p><p>In many cases, the PIAB will already be installed on-site, making connection to the customer’s switch highly likely.</p><p>________________________________________</p><p>Check-In and Check-Out Requirements</p><p>•Check-In: Call 281-668-3211, option 3 upon arrival.</p><p>•Check-Out: Call 281-668-3211, option 3 immediately after completion.</p><p>•Failure to call for both check-in and check-out will result in payment deduction or no payment.</p><p>•If delayed in getting a response, email check-in/out details (site name, arrival/departure times, POC name) to support@tech-americas.com.</p><p>•Do not leave the site until all required photos and the signed Work Order are submitted to documents@tech-americas.com.</p><p>•Assigned date and time cannot be rescheduled.</p><p>________________________________________</p><p>Tech Americas Contacts:</p><p>Aida Flores: 210-830-7125, aflores@tech-americas.com&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Rafael Aparicio: (216) 998-4955, raparicio@tech-americas.com</p><p>Cesar Ayala: (409)340-0869,&nbsp;caayala@tech-americas.com&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Elias Garcia - (409) 340-0872, esgarcia@tech-americas.com</p><p>-----------</p><p>Cristo Guevara: (254) 308-6718, cguevara@tech-americas.com&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>________________________________________</p><p>Check-In / Check-Out Procedure</p><p>1. Check-In:</p><p>•Call Tech Americas upon arrival.</p><p>•Introduce yourself to the POC (name, company, purpose).</p><p>•Verify POC identity.</p><p>•If POC unavailable, call Tech Americas support immediately.</p><p>•Log arrival time.</p><p>2. Check-Out:</p><p>•Call Tech Americas immediately after job completion.</p><p>•Confirm site restored to original condition.</p><p>•Obtain POC signature on Work Order.</p><p>•Submit signed WO and required photos to documents@tech-americas.com within 24 hours.</p><p>•Do not leave until documentation is submitted.</p><p>________________________________________</p><p>***Future Visit – Scope of Work***</p><p><br></p><p>Technician must return to troubleshoot the LTE connectivity and complete the equipment installation.</p><p><br></p><p>Check in with Support and take pictures of the equipment.</p><p>Verify the lines and modem are not DSL or shared.</p><p>Test LTE signal and reposition the MIMO antenna to find the best signal.</p><p>Reboot equipment and swap SIM cards if directed by Support.</p><p>Perform signal and speed tests with Support.</p><p>If LTE remains unavailable, restore the lines to the original configuration.</p><p>Take final pictures and obtain the signed WO before leaving.</p><p>______________________________________________________________________________</p><p>Identification Requirements</p><p>Federal Sites: Must carry one of the following:</p><p>•State-Issued Enhanced Driver’s License or Enhanced Real ID</p><p>•U.S. Passport / Passport Card</p><p>•DHS Trusted Traveler Cards (Global Entry, NEXUS, SENTRI, FAST)</p><p>•DoD ID, Permanent Resident Card, Tribal Nation ID, HSPD-12 PIV Card, etc.</p><p>Non-Federal Sites: Standard driver’s license or state-issued ID (unless otherwise specified).</p><p>If ID is rejected: Contact Tech Americas support immediately.</p><p>________________________________________</p><p>Pre-Installation Tasks (On-Site)</p><p>1.Introduce yourself to the POC (name, company, purpose, estimated time).</p><p>2.Locate MTL equipment in telecom room.</p><p>3.Take before photos (equipment, telecom room, DMARC connections).</p><p>4.Verify LTE/Cell signal (-85 dBm minimum).</p><p>5.Verify existing lines using lineman’s handset and compare with inventory.</p><p>6.Check for permits if equipment/cable mounting is needed.</p><p>________________________________________</p><p>Installation Process</p><p>1.Mount MetTel Communications Board.</p><p>2.Mount MIMO Antenna.</p><p>3.Connect cables per installation guide.</p><p>4.Verify and test all lines.</p><p>5.Coordinate with MetTel Remote Support.</p><p>________________________________________</p><p>PIAB to Customer Switch Connection</p><p>•Connect if LTE signal is below -85 dBm or per instructions from Tech Americas/POC.</p><p>•Follow proper approval and documentation procedures.</p><p>•Take before and after photos of connections.</p><p>•Perform validation testing (dial tone, inbound/outbound calls, 933 address check).</p><p>________________________________________</p><p>Required Tools</p><p>•Laptop (serial/USB adapter, TeamViewer, 4G connection)</p><p>•Console cable, cable toner, punch-down tool, lineman’s handset</p><p>•Crimpers, multimeter, CAT5/6 cable, RJ jacks</p><p>•Power drill, power strip, ladder, splitters, modular plugs</p><p>________________________________________</p><p>Documentation Requirements</p><p>•Photos: Before and after (clear, labeled, JPEG).</p><p>•Line Verification Form: Submit as PDF.</p><p>•Signed Work Order: Submit as PDF.</p><p>•Submission Deadline: Must be submitted immediately after job completion, or within 24 hours at the latest. If not received within this timeframe, the job will be closed without payment. Please send to:</p><p>documents@tech-americas.com</p><p>•________________________________________</p><p>Contingency Plans</p><p>•POC Unavailable: Contact Tech Americas for backup contact.</p><p>•Equipment Failure: Report and await instructions.</p><p>•Poor Signal: Connect to customer switch or use approved antenna extension.</p><p>•Access Denial: Contact Tech Americas and site security.</p><p><br></p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-22T09:00","end":"2026-09-22T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":150},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":48.4},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $150 (countered: $195) is below minimum threshold $400"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-22T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-