xperienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-17T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Remote Hands - Connect AT&T broadband circuit"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789578820065}
{"job":{"id":19966151,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Paragon Development Systems, Inc","title":"Cabling Re-Route and Termination","description":{"html":"<p>Summary:</p><p>Technician previously had to circumnavigate the structured cabling from the patch panel rack to the switch rack. This visit is to pull the cable run through the proper pathway and complete the intended termination between the patch panel rack and switch rack. The estimated cable run is less than 50 feet. Technician is to supply the necessary materials to make the connection functional.</p><p><br></p><p>POC: MOD</p><p>Scope of Work:</p><ul><li>Dispatch a qualified data/low-voltage technician to properly route the structured cabling from the patch panel rack to the switch rack.</li><li>Pull the cable run through the proper pathway between the patch panel rack and switch rack.</li><li>The cable run is estimated to be less than 50 feet.</li><li>Properly terminate the cable at the patch panel and switch rack locations.</li><li>Technician to supply the necessary materials required to make the cable run functional.</li><li>Ensure the cable is properly secured and routed to prevent damage, strain, or interference with other equipment or cabling.</li><li>Label the cable at both termination points.</li><li>Test the completed cable run for continuity and proper wire map.</li><li>Verify the completed connection is functional.</li><li>Document the cable route, termination points, and testing results.</li></ul><p>Cisco Switch / Port Verification</p><ul><li>Locate and identify the Cisco 2960 switch serving the affected connection.</li><li>Register ports are assigned to Cisco Ports 11–26.</li><li>Computer ports are assigned to Cisco Ports 27–39.</li><li>Identify whether the new cable run is associated with a register or computer connection and verify the applicable Cisco switch port.</li><li>Trace the new data line from the patch panel to the Cisco 2960 switch.</li><li>Confirm the corresponding patch panel port and Cisco switch port.</li><li>Verify link/activity on the identified Cisco port.</li><li>Confirm the patch panel connection and patch cable are properly connected.</li><li>Document the exact Cisco switch port, patch panel port, and associated data jack.</li><li>Do not make Cisco switch configuration changes unless authorized by JCPenney IT.</li></ul><p>Testing &amp; Verification</p><ul><li>Test the Ethernet cable for continuity and proper wire map.</li><li>Test the data jack using a technician laptop, if applicable.</li><li>Verify DHCP/network connectivity, if available.</li><li>Verify the patch panel-to-switch connection.</li><li>Verify Cisco switch port link/activity.</li><li>Confirm the newly installed cable run is functional.</li><li>If the expected Cisco port is inactive, document the status and coordinate with JCPenney ITSD for further troubleshooting.</li><li>Determine whether any issue is related to the cable, termination, patch panel, switch port, or upstream network connection.</li><li>Coordinate with JCPenney ITSD as needed to verify network connectivity.</li></ul><p>IT Support</p><p>JCPenney ITSD: (800) 214-4822</p><ul><li>Technician should contact JCPenney ITSD as needed during troubleshooting and testing.</li><li>Provide ITSD with the identified Cisco switch port, patch panel information, data jack information, test results, and point of failure, if applicable.</li><li>Coordinate with JCPenney ITSD to verify network connectivity following completion of the cable installation.</li><li>Do not make Cisco switch configuration changes without IT authorization.</li></ul><p>Deliverables:</p><ul><li>Properly routed and terminated structured cable run between the patch panel rack and switch rack.</li><li>Technician-supplied materials required to make the connection functional.</li><li>Cable labeling at both termination points.</li><li>Exact Cisco switch port and patch panel port documented.</li><li>Continuity and wire-map test results.</li><li>Network connectivity/functionality verification.</li><li>Photos of the completed cable route, patch panel termination, and switch rack termination.</li><li>Documentation of any issues encountered and any additional work required.</li></ul><p>Technician Check-In/Check-Out and Assignment Requirements</p><ul><li>The assigned technician is required to use GPS-based check-in and check-out while onsite.</li><li>Check-in and check-out must be completed by the assigned technician only. Administrative staff, dispatchers, or any other individual may not check in or check out on behalf of the assigned technician.</li><li>Unauthorized or unapproved technicians will not be accepted or approved for the work.</li><li>If you are an organization or staffing provider, the technician must be preapproved prior to arriving onsite.</li><li>Substitutions are not permitted without prior approval.</li></ul><p>Scope of Work and Authorization Requirements</p><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Any changes, additions, or deviations from the approved Scope of Work must be approved in writing through this platform before the work is performed. The onsite POC is not authorized to approve scope changes, additional labor, materials, or costs unless they have been specifically designated as an authorized approver by the Work Order Manager. Work performed without prior written authorization may not be approved for payment.</li></ul><p><br></p>","markdown":"Summary:\n\nTechnician previously had to circumnavigate the structured cabling from the patch panel rack to the switch rack. This visit is to pull the cable run through the proper pathway and complete the intended termination between the patch panel rack and switch rack. The estimated cable run is less than 50 feet. Technician is to supply the necessary materials to make the connection functional.\n\nPOC: MOD\n\nScope of Work:\n\n- Dispatch a qualified data/low-voltage technician to properly route the structured cabling from the patch panel rack to the switch rack.\n- Pull the cable run through the proper pathway between the patch panel rack and switch rack.\n- The cable run is estimated to be less than 50 feet.\n- Properly terminate the cable at the patch panel and switch rack locations.\n- Technician to supply the necessary materials required to make the cable run functional.\n- Ensure the cable is properly secured and routed to prevent damage, strain, or interference with other equipment or cabling.\n- Label the cable at both termination points.\n- Test the completed cable run for continuity and proper wire map.\n- Verify the completed connection is functional.\n- Document the cable route, termination points, and testing results.\n\nCisco Switch / Port Verification\n\n- Locate and identify the Cisco 2960 switch serving the affected connection.\n- Register ports are assigned to Cisco Ports 11–26.\n- Computer ports are assigned to Cisco Ports 27–39.\n- Identify whether the new cable run is associated with a register or computer connection and verify the applicable Cisco switch port.\n- Trace the new data line from the patch panel to the Cisco 2960 switch.\n- Confirm the corresponding patch panel port and Cisco switch port.\n- Verify link/activity on the identified Cisco port.\n- Confirm the patch panel connection and patch cable are properly connected.\n- Document the exact Cisco switch port, patch panel port, and associated data jack.\n- Do not make Cisco switch configuration changes unless authorized by JCPenney IT.\n\nTesting & Verification\n\n- Test the Ethernet cable for continuity and proper wire map.\n- Test the data jack using a technician laptop, if applicable.\n- Verify DHCP/network connectivity, if available.\n- Verify the patch panel-to-switch connection.\n- Verify Cisco switch port link/activity.\n- Confirm the newly installed cable run is functional.\n- If the expected Cisco port is inactive, document the status and coordinate with JCPenney ITSD for further troubleshooting.\n- Determine whether any issue is related to the cable, termination, patch panel, switch port, or upstream network connection.\n- Coordinate with JCPenney ITSD as needed to verify network connectivity.\n\nIT Support\n\nJCPenney ITSD: (800) 214-4822\n\n- Technician should contact JCPenney ITSD as needed during troubleshooting and testing.\n- Provide ITSD with the identified Cisco switch port, patch panel information, data jack information, test results, and point of failure, if applicable.\n- Coordinate with JCPenney ITSD to verify network connectivity following completion of the cable installation.\n- Do not make Cisco switch configuration changes without IT authorization.\n\nDeliverables:\n\n- Properly routed and terminated structured cable run between the patch panel rack and switch rack.\n- Technician-supplied materials required to make the connection functional.\n- Cable labeling at both termination points.\n- Exact Cisco switch port and patch panel port documented.\n- Continuity and wire-map test results.\n- Network connectivity/functionality verification.\n- Photos of the completed cable route, patch panel termination, and switch rack termination.\n- Documentation of any issues encountered and any additional work required.\n\nTechnician Check-In/Check-Out and Assignment Requirements\n\n- The assigned technician is required to use GPS-based check-in and check-out while onsite.\n- Check-in and check-out must be completed by the assigned technician only. Administrative staff, dispatchers, or any other individual may not check in or check out on behalf of the assigned technician.\n- Unauthorized or unapproved technicians will not be accepted or approved for the work.\n- If you are an organization or staffing provider, the technician must be preapproved prior to arriving onsite.\n- Substitutions are not permitted without prior approval.\n\nScope of Work and Authorization Requirements\n\n- Any changes, additions, or deviations from the approved Scope of Work must be approved in writing through this platform before the work is performed. The onsite POC is not authorized to approve scope changes, additional labor, materials, or costs unless they have been specifically designated as an authorized approver by the Work Order Manager. Work performed without prior written authorization may not be approved for payment.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-18T11:00","end":"2026-09-18T15:00","latestStart":"2026-09-18T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":80,"max":320},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":80,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":57},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $320 (countered: $320) is below minimum threshold $400"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-21T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Miniso"},{"start":"2026-09-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-09-22T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-