{"job":{"id":"6673271244","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"Summary: INT13794989- T1080 - Raleigh Hwy 70– Voice Cable Check /Troubleshooting/ scissor lift","description":"<p><br></p><p>**Initial Description/Overview**</p><p><br></p><p>**Target / INT13794989**/ **Voice Cable Check / Troubleshooting / scissor lift**</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>**\\*\\*\\*TECH MUST PERFORM CABLE CHECK BEFORE TROUBLESHOOTING END DEVICE\\*\\*\\***</p><p><br></p><p>**\\\\\\*\\\\\\*\\\\\\*\\*\\*UPON ARRIVAL:\\*\\* TECH MUST CALL GRANITE **TARGET SUPPORT BRIDGE +1 929-229-2436,,6261761#**&nbsp;TO CHECK IN AND REVIEW SOW \\\\\\*\\\\\\*\\\\\\*&nbsp;**</p><p><br></p><p>* Proceed to the Guest Service Desk, provide Identification and ask for a Designated Leader</p><p>Scott Matschat</p><p>* </p><p>When meeting designated leader, provide the above incident number and reason for the service call, determine location of service call. Designated Store Lead will direct you to the package with replacement part that was delivered \\(see below for tracking details\\)&nbsp;</p><p>* If the store refuses the technician and work, the technician should ask the store leader/designated leader to call the CSC with the above incident number and service call number SR0080717</p><p><br></p><p>* **If Control Room Access is required, please reach out to CSC 612-304-4357 to obtain code – Tech Must read the attached Control Room Access and Regulations documents before requesting access.**</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>**ISSUE/SOW** **AudioCodes Gateway MP-124 \\(T1080VGW0001\\) offline\\) **perfor m an end to end cable check first before troubleshooting end device - \\(see attached Target Cable Check Doc\\) upload a picture of cable test – if phone is found to be daisy chained tech to move to dedicated cable \\(existing unused or new cable run\\) and port.&nbsp;Reac h out to your Granite Rep for new port assignment and further troubleshooting if needed, **Tech must call Granite rep before leaving site to run system cable check and final testing.&nbsp;DO NOT leave site without approval from your Granite Rep.**</p><p><br></p><p>GraniteNet technician tested the carrier network and found no issues. Line 718-434-6482 tested clean for both inbound and outbound calls at the demarcation point \\(Demarc\\). A test call to the line resulted in a busy signal.</p><p>Dispatch a technician to the store to inspect and troubleshoot the internal wiring between the Demarc and the Fire Alarm Panels. Check for wiring faults, line seizure issues, panel connectivity, or any equipment causing the line to remain busy</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>**Affected Device/Network Equipment:**</p><p>Equipment Type Voice Gateway</p><p>Manufacturer AudioCodes</p><p>Site Area: control room</p><p>Model: MP-124</p><p>Network Location: MDF</p><p>MAC: f00:90:8f:e2:a9:24</p><p>Hostname: : T1080VGW0001</p><p>SN 14854436</p><p>Switch: t1080swta0001</p><p>IP Address: n/a</p><p>**Replacement Device /Equipment Info/Tracking**</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>**@@ NOTE: Tech is responsible for returning any old or unused equipment.&nbsp;DO NOT leave onsite.&nbsp;&nbsp;Use provided return label and take it to a nearby UPS location to be returned.**</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>**Closeout Checklist:**</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Confirm ALL devices online with designated leader.</p><p>Call TARGET SUPPORT BRIDGE +1 929-229-2436,,6261761# to check out BEFORE leaving.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Provide before and after pictures of devices worked on</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Picture of SN#\\(s\\) one of existing/old and one of new/replaced equipment</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Pictures of certified cable tests</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Pictures of termination points</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Record first and last name of site contact and support contact you worked with</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;**If equipment was shipped,** Box up unused equipment \\(old or new\\) with return label provided and TECH is responsible for dropping off at a UPS location, a picture of the return label and the receipt from UPS at drop off is a required deliverable</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>**REQUIRED MATERIALS /TOOLS: Tech MUST have the following:**</p><p>Laptop with power supply</p><p>Cat5/Cat6 cable tester</p><p>Min 500ft CAT6 cable \\(White preferred\\)</p><p>CAT6 Jacks</p><p>CAT6 Patch cords various lengths</p><p>Basic hand tools</p><p>Pliers</p><p>Assorted screwdrivers</p><p>Precision screwdriver set</p><p>Drill</p><p>Velcro for cable management</p><p>Label maker \\(P touch or equivalent\\)</p><p>Patch cables</p><p>Cable tester Toner and Probe</p><p>Camera/Smart phone</p><p>8-10' Ladder&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>**REQUIRED DELIVERABLES/Closing Info:**</p><p>Failure to provide the following may result in delayed payment.</p><p>Before and after photos showing device\\(s\\) worked on</p><p>Capture Clear Pictures SN#'s of existing equipment and replacement equipment</p><p>Manage cables neatly and cleanup work area\\(s\\).</p><p>Confirm all devices are online and working properly before leaving site</p><p>Picture of the return label AND the receipt from UPS at drop off</p><p>Record name of site contact that has verified work completed at closing</p><p>SIGNED work order.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>**If Issue/SOW is unable to be resolved**, take necessary photos showing device\\(s\\), cable test results and any other problems preventing resolution, please describe findings and what was done on site.</p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-22T06:00","end":"2026-09-22T08:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":100},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":2