{"job":{"id":19964733,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"InnovateX IT Solutions LLC","title":"Site walk to verify access control installation info","description":{"html":"<p>Site contact: <del>**** *** ****** *** *******************************</del></p>\n<p><strong>1. SCOPE SUMMARY</strong></p>\n<p>This is a site walk only. The technician will assess and document existing conditions at the main entry doors so Innovatex can produce an accurate bill of materials, labor estimate, and installation plan for a single 8\" surface-mount intercom. No cabling, mounting, drilling, or device installation is to be performed on this visit.</p>\n<p>Known conditions going in:</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;One (1) 8\" surface intercom is planned at the main entry doors.</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The entry door has NO electrified locking hardware today. Existing hardware observed is a rim exit device (panic bar) and a surface-mounted door closer.</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Internet and power are located on the bottom floor. The cable path from that location up to the entry is the single largest unknown and is the priority of this visit.</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Because no electrified hardware exists, the technician must assess what it would take to add door release (electric strike, electric latch retraction, or equivalent) and any associated power supply, request-to-exit, and fire alarm tie-in.</p>\n<p><strong>2. TECHNICIAN RESPONSIBILITIES</strong></p>\n<p>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Call or text the site contact 30 minutes prior to arrival. Check in with Jose San Miguel on arrival.</p>\n<p>2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Check in to the work order at the start of the visit and check out at the end. Both are required.</p>\n<p>3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Walk the main entry and the bottom-floor network/power location with the site contact.</p>\n<p>4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Capture every data point in Section 3 below. Do not leave a field blank — write \"N/A\" or \"unknown, could not verify\" with a reason.</p>\n<p>5.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Measure the cable run from the bottom-floor network location to the proposed intercom position along the actual routed path. Report in feet.</p>\n<p>6.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Photograph all items listed in Section 6. Photos must be clear, well lit, and in focus.</p>\n<p>7.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Sketch or mark up a simple floor plan showing the entry, the proposed device location, the bottom-floor IDF, and the proposed cable route.</p>\n<p>8.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Identify anything that would block or delay installation — pathway obstructions, no PoE ports available, door/frame that cannot accept electrified hardware, landlord restrictions, permit or AHJ concerns.</p>\n<p>9.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Call the Innovatex PM before leaving site if any condition materially differs from this work order.</p>\n<p>10.&nbsp;Upload all photos, measurements, and notes to the work order before checking out.</p>\n<p><strong>3. DATA TO CAPTURE ON SITE</strong></p>\n<p>Record every item below. Do not leave one blank — enter \"N/A\" or \"unknown, could not verify\" with a reason.</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Intercom mounting location —</strong> Exact proposed location, mounting surface type (storefront mullion, masonry, drywall, metal panel), and available flat surface dimensions. Confirm an 8\" surface-mount unit physically fits without blocking hardware or glazing.</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Mounting height —</strong> Measured height to proposed center of device from finished floor. Flag any ADA reach-range concern.</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Cable run — length —</strong> Measured or paced cable distance from the bottom-floor IDF or network location to the intercom position. Report in feet, routed path, not straight line.</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Cable run — pathway —</strong> Available pathway: existing conduit, surface raceway, accessible ceiling, wall cavity, core drill required, exterior run. Note ceiling type and height, firewall penetrations, and any pathway that must be added.</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Network source —</strong>Bottom-floor IDF or closet location, rack or wall-mount, switch make and model, number of free ports, PoE availability and PoE budget headroom, and whether a new drop can be terminated there.</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Power source —</strong>Nearest available 120V receptacle to the IDF and to the door, circuit availability, and whether an electrician is required for any new power.</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Door hardware — existing —</strong> Confirm and photograph: rim exit device make and model, door closer make and model, door material and leaf count (single vs. pair), frame type, hinge side, swing direction, and existing strike or keeper.</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Door hardware — proposed —</strong> Assess feasibility of electrified hardware: electric strike vs. electric latch retraction exit device vs. mag lock. Note door prep required, frame depth, and whether the leaf or frame can accept a power transfer (EPT or door loop).</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Egress and code items —</strong> Existing request-to-exit provisions, fire alarm tie-in point, AHJ considerations, and whether the entry is a required means of egress.</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Existing systems —</strong> Any existing access control, camera, or intercom system on site — make, model, and whether the new intercom is expected to integrate.</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Site logistics —</strong>Parking, loading, badge or escort requirements, hours of access, ladder or lift needs, and any tenant or landlord restrictions.</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Cellular and connectivity —</strong> Carrier signal at the entry and in the IDF, for any hotspot or remote support needs.</p>\n<p><strong>4. REQUIRED SKILLS</strong></p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Low-voltage / structured cabling field experience.</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Working familiarity with access control and door hardware — electric strikes, electric latch retraction exit devices, power supplies, request-to-exit, door position switches.</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Ability to identify network switch models and assess PoE port availability.</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Comfortable producing clear written field notes and a legible pathway sketch.</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Professional, customer-facing presentation — this is a direct client interaction.</p>\n<p><strong>5. REQUIRED TOOLS</strong></p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;6 ft ladder (for ceiling and door-head inspection). Confirm with site contact prior to arrival if a taller ladder is needed.</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Standard PPE.</p>\n<p><strong>6. PHOTO REQUIREMENTS</strong></p>\n<p>Minimum photo set. Take more if anything is unclear.</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Wide shot of the main entry from outside and from inside.</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Proposed intercom mounting location, with a tape measure in frame showing available surface width and height.</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Close-up of the rim exit device, including any visible make/model markings.</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Close-up of the door closer and the door head.</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Door frame, hinge side, and strike/keeper.</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Full door leaf showing swing direction and whether it is a single or pair.</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Bottom-floor network location: rack/closet wide shot, switch front face showing ports, and available power receptacles.</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The full cable pathway — one photo at each turn, penetration, or obstruction.</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Ceiling type and height in the pathway area.</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Any existing surface raceway, conduit, or prior low-voltage work that could be reused.</p>\n<p><strong>7. DELIVERABLES</strong></p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Completed field notes covering every data point in Section 3.</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Full photo set per Section 6, uploaded to the work order.</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Measured cable run distance (routed path, in feet) from the bottom-floor network location to the proposed intercom position.</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Marked-up sketch or floor plan showing device location, IDF location, and proposed cable route.</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Written list of any obstructions, risks, or additional materials/trades required (electrician, locksmith, core drilling, permit).</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Technician recommendation on door release approach given the existing rim exit device.</p>\n<p><strong>8. ON-SITE REQUIREMENTS</strong></p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Arrive on time. The 10:00 AM window is a client commitment.</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Innovatex-branded or clean professional attire. No torn, stained, or logo-conflicting clothing.</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Check in and check out of the work order from the site.</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Site contact must be present for the walk. If the contact is unavailable on arrival, call the Innovatex PM before leaving.</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;This is an assessment visit only — no drilling, cutting, mounting, cabling, or hardware modification.</p>\n<p>•&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Leave the site exactly as found. Replace any ceiling tiles or raceway covers removed for inspection.</p>\n<p><strong>9. CRITICAL — FIELD POLICY</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Sign-off photos.</strong> All required photos must be uploaded before checkout. A work order closed without the complete photo set is subject to hold or non-payment.</p>\n<p><strong>Change approval.</strong> No work outside this scope is authorized. If the client requests additional work on site, the technician must stop and call the Innovatex PM for written approval before proceeding.</p>\n<p><strong>Scope creep protocol.</strong> Verbal direction from the client, landlord, or any third party does not change this work order. Only the Innovatex PM can modify scope.</p>\n<p><strong>Check-in / check-out accountability.</strong> Technician must check in on arrival and check out on departure from the site. Time not bracketed by a check-in and check-out is not billable.</p>\n<p><strong>No early departure.</strong> Technician may not leave the site until all deliverables in Section 7 are captured and the Innovatex PM has confirmed the visit is complete. If the walk finishes early, call the PM before departing.</p>\n<p><strong>Trash disposal.</strong> Remove all packaging, debris, and personal trash from the site. Nothing is to be left behind in client containers without permission.</p>\n<p><strong>Escalation.</strong> Any access issue, safety concern, or condition that blocks the walk: call the Innovatex PM immediately at 1-877-804-1004. Do not improvise.</p>","markdown":"Site contact: \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**1. SCOPE SUMMARY**\n\nThis is a site walk only. The technician will assess and document existing conditions at the main entry doors so Innovatex can produce an accurate bill of materials, labor estimate, and installation plan for a single 8\" surface-mount intercom. No cabling, mounting, drilling, or device installation is to be performed on this visit.\n\nKnown conditions going in:\n\n• One (1) 8\" surface intercom is planned at the main entry doors.\n\n• The entry door has NO electrified locking hardware today. Existing hardware observed is a rim exit device (panic bar) and a surface-mounted door closer.\n\n• Internet and power are located on the bottom floor. The cable path from that location up to the entry is the single largest unknown and is the priority of this visit.\n\n• Because no electrified hardware exists, the technician must assess what it would take to add door release (electric strike, electric latch retraction, or equivalent) and any associated power supply, request-to-exit, and fire alarm tie-in.\n\n**2. TECHNICIAN RESPONSIBILITIES**\n\n1\\. Call or text the site contact 30 minutes prior to arrival. Check in with Jose San Miguel on arrival.\n\n2\\. Check in to the work order at the start of the visit and check out at the end. Both are required.\n\n3\\. Walk the main entry and the bottom-floor network/power location with the site contact.\n\n4\\. Capture every data point in Section 3 below. Do not leave a field blank — write \"N/A\" or \"unknown, could not verify\" with a reason.\n\n5\\. Measure the cable run from the bottom-floor network location to the proposed intercom position along the actual routed path. Report in feet.\n\n6\\. Photograph all items listed in Section 6. Photos must be clear, well lit, and in focus.\n\n7\\. Sketch or mark up a simple floor plan showing the entry, the proposed device location, the bottom-floor IDF, and the proposed cable route.\n\n8\\. Identify anything that would block or delay installation — pathway obstructions, no PoE ports available, door/frame that cannot accept electrified hardware, landlord restrictions, permit or AHJ concerns.\n\n9\\. Call the Innovatex PM before leaving site if any condition materially differs from this work order.\n\n10\\. Upload all photos, measurements, and notes to the work order before checking out.\n\n**3. DATA TO CAPTURE ON SITE**\n\nRecord every item below. Do not leave one blank — enter \"N/A\" or \"unknown, could not verify\" with a reason.\n\n• **Intercom mounting location —** Exact proposed location, mounting surface type (storefront mullion, masonry, drywall, metal panel), and available flat surface dimensions. Confirm an 8\" surface-mount unit physically fits without blocking hardware or glazing.\n\n• **Mounting height —** Measured height to proposed center of device from finished floor. Flag any ADA reach-range concern.\n\n• **Cable run — length —** Measured or paced cable distance from the bottom-floor IDF or network location to the intercom position. Report in feet, routed path, not straight line.\n\n• **Cable run — pathway —** Available pathway: existing conduit, surface raceway, accessible ceiling, wall cavity, core drill required, exterior run. Note ceiling type and height, firewall penetrations, and any pathway that must be added.\n\n• **Network source —**Bottom-floor IDF or closet location, rack or wall-mount, switch make and model, number of free ports, PoE availability and PoE budget headroom, and whether a new drop can be terminated there.\n\n• **Power source —**Nearest available 120V receptacle to the IDF and to the door, circuit availability, and whether an electrician is required for any new power.\n\n• **Door hardware — existing —** Confirm and photograph: rim exit device make and model, door closer make and model, door material and leaf count (single vs. pair), frame type, hinge side, swing direction, and existing strike or keeper.\n\n• **Door hardware — proposed —** Assess feasibility of electrified hardware: electric strike vs. electric latch retraction exit device vs. mag lock. Note door prep required, frame depth, and whether the leaf or frame can accept a power transfer (EPT or door loop).\n\n• **Egress and code items —** Existing request-to-exit provisions, fire alarm tie-in point, AHJ considerations, and whether the entry is a required means of egress.\n\n• **Existing systems —** Any existing access control, camera, or intercom system on site — make, model, and whether the new intercom is expected to integrate.\n\n• **Site logistics —**Parking, loading, badge or escort requirements, hours of access, ladder or lift needs, and any tenant or landlord restrictions.\n\n• **Cellular and connectivity —** Carrier signal at the entry and in the IDF, for any hotspot or remote support needs.\n\n**4. REQUIRED SKILLS**\n\n• Low-voltage / structured cabling field experience.\n\n• Working familiarity with access control and door hardware — electric strikes, electric latch retraction exit devices, power supplies, request-to-exit, door position switches.\n\n• Ability to identify network switch models and assess PoE port availability.\n\n• Comfortable producing clear written field notes and a legible pathway sketch.\n\n• Professional, customer-facing presentation — this is a direct client interaction.\n\n**5. REQUIRED TOOLS**\n\n• 6 ft ladder (for ceiling and door-head inspection). Confirm with site contact prior to arrival if a taller ladder is needed.\n\n• Standard PPE.\n\n**6. PHOTO REQUIREMENTS**\n\nMinimum photo set. Take more if anything is unclear.\n\n• Wide shot of the main entry from outside and from inside.\n\n• Proposed intercom mounting location, with a tape measure in frame showing available surface width and height.\n\n• Close-up of the rim exit device, including any visible make/model markings.\n\n• Close-up of the door closer and the door head.\n\n• Door frame, hinge side, and strike/keeper.\n\n• Full door leaf showing swing direction and whether it is a single or pair.\n\n• Bottom-floor network location: rack/closet wide shot, switch front face showing ports, and available power receptacles.\n\n• The full cable pathway — one photo at each turn, penetration, or obstruction.\n\n• Ceiling type and height in the pathway area.\n\n• Any existing surface raceway, conduit, or prior low-voltage work that could be reused.\n\n**7. DELIVERABLES**\n\n• Completed field notes covering every data point in Section 3.\n\n• Full photo set per Section 6, uploaded to the work order.\n\n• Measured cable run distance (routed path, in feet) from the bottom-floor network location to the proposed intercom position.\n\n• Marked-up sketch or floor plan showing device location, IDF location, and proposed cable route.\n\n• Written list of any obstructions, risks, or additional materials/trades required (electrician, locksmith, core drilling, permit).\n\n• Technician recommendation on door release approach given the existing rim exit device.\n\n**8. ON-SITE REQUIREMENTS**\n\n• Arrive on time. The 10:00 AM window is a client commitment.\n\n• Innovatex-branded or clean professional attire. No torn, stained, or logo-conflicting clothing.\n\n• Check in and check out of the work order from the site.\n\n• Site contact must be present for the walk. If the contact is unavailable on arrival, call the Innovatex PM before leaving.\n\n• This is an assessment visit only — no drilling, cutting, mounting, cabling, or hardware modification.\n\n• Leave the site exactly as found. Replace any ceiling tiles or raceway covers removed for inspection.\n\n**9. CRITICAL — FIELD POLICY**\n\n**Sign-off photos.** All required photos must be uploaded before checkout. A work order closed without the complete photo set is subject to hold or non-payment.\n\n**Change approval.** No work outside this scope is authorized. If the client requests additional work on site, the technician must stop and call the Innovatex PM for written approval before proceeding.\n\n**Scope creep protocol.** Verbal direction from the client, landlord, or any third party does not change this work order. Only the Innovatex PM can modify scope.\n\n**Check-in / check-out accountability.** Technician must check in on arrival and check out on departure from the site. Time not bracketed by a check-in and check-out is not billable.\n\n**No early departure.** Technician may not leave the site until all deliverables in Section 7 are captured and the Innovatex PM has confirmed the visit is complete. If the walk finishes early, call the PM before departing.\n\n**Trash disposal.** Remove all packaging, debris, and personal trash from the site. Nothing is to be left behind in client containers without permission.\n\n**Escalation.** Any access issue, safety concern, or condition that blocks the walk: call the Innovatex PM immediately at 1-877-804-1004. Do not improvise.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-17T10:00","end":"2026-09-17T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":130},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":11},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $130 (countered: $130) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-17T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T17:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-17T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-21T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Miniso"},{"start":"2026-09-22T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-17T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Remote Hands - Connect AT&T broadband circuit"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789579030294}
{"job":{"id":19962304,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Emily Grene","title":"Serial comm to Waveshare Replacement","description":{"html":"<h2><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Required Procedures Upon Arrival and Before Departure from the Site</span></h2><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Upon arrival at the site, technicians must complete the following steps:</strong></p><h3><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">ServiceChannel Check-In</strong></h3><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Report to the store office and inform management that you are with&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Emily-Grene</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;and need to check in through&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">ServiceChannel</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;using the store phone.</span></p><h3><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">IVR Hotline Call</strong></h3><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Using the&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">store phone</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">, call the ServiceChannel IVR Hotline at&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">516-500-7776</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;to check in. Using the store phone ensures accurate location verification.</span></p><h3><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Check-Out Procedure</strong></h3><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Once all work has been completed, technicians must repeat the IVR call process using the&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">store phone</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;to check out before leaving the site.</span></p><h3><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">If IVR Cannot Be Completed</strong></h3><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">If you are unable to complete the IVR check-in or check-out for any reason, you&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">must obtain a store manager's signature before leaving the site</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">. The manager verification must include the date, arrival time, departure time, printed name, and signature.</span></p><h3><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">**IMPORTANT - PAYMENT REQUIREMENT**</strong></h3><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Completion of the ServiceChannel IVR check-in/check-out process, or obtaining a store manager's signed verification if IVR is unavailable, is&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">mandatory</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">. ServiceChannel requires this documentation to validate the service visit.</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Failure to complete one of these required verification methods may result in ServiceChannel denying payment for the work order. If Emily-Grene is unable to invoice or receive payment from ServiceChannel due to missing IVR documentation or manager verification, payment for the services performed may be withheld. Technicians are responsible for ensuring this requirement is completed before leaving the site.</strong></p><h2><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">ServiceChannel Information</span></h2><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">PIN:</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;5299239</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Note:</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;This phone number is used exclusively for checking into and out of the work order. For all technical support or troubleshooting needs, please contact the Emily-Grene Hotline at&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">(626) 314-5937</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">.</span></p><h3><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;</span>Overview</h3><p>The Tech is required to replace and secure connections for the new serial communication device related to the refrigeration monitoring system that has been shipped to the store.</p><p><strong>Estimated Duration:</strong> 30 minutes</p><h3>Dress Code</h3><ul><li>Collared shirt or polo</li><li>Black or khaki pants, no holes or tears</li><li>Clean, well-maintained clothing and good personal hygiene</li></ul><h3>Tools Required</h3><ul><li>Punch down tool (if necessary)</li><li>4-pair testers</li><li>Snips</li><li>Precision screwdrivers/flathead</li><li>Toner</li></ul><h3>Scope of Work</h3><h4>Pre-Site Requirements</h4><ul><li>Review the work order details prior to arrival.</li><li>Ensure you have all the required tools for the work order.</li></ul><h4>On-Site Tasks</h4><ol><li><strong>Check-in:</strong> Introduce yourself to a member of management, representing Emily Grene. Do not mention Field Nation while on-site.</li><li><strong>Inform Management:</strong> Communicate that you are there to replace the equipment for the connection to the refrigeration monitoring system. A Waveshare was sent onsite thru UPS. Should be located in the office.</li><li><strong>IMS Enclosure Key:</strong> Request the key to the IMS Enclosure from management. If unavailable, call <strong><em>(626) 314-5937.</em></strong></li><li><strong>Locate IMS Enclosure:</strong> The enclosure is black, located in the back room near the breaker panels, containing the serial communication device.</li><li><strong>Replace unit:</strong></li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Please take before and after photos of connections and new terminations. </strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Unplug the power cable from the serial communication device.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Remove all DB9 connections,</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Replace serial communications device with new wave share device.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Refer to the attached photos for guidance on the correct connections.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Comm1 of the serial comm will be going to RS-1 on the wave share, comm3 will be going to RS-3 so on and so forth.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Comm1 to RS-1 - B Negative - Black, white, orange stripe // A Positive - Clear, solid orange // Ground - Blues, browns, greens shield from cat6 (No shield from serial cable)</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Comm3 to RS-3 - B Negative - Black // A Positive - Red // Ground - Shield</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Rarely we will have a cable landed on comm2 and 4, please refer these connections just as comm3 is connected. The only unique connection will be comm1. </strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Power the wave share thru the blue USB, power cycle the PC \"Lenovo Think Edge\" for 2 mins. </strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Once powered back up both waveshape and PC give Tech Support a call at (626) 314-5937 to confirm visibility </strong></li></ul><ol><li><strong>Call for Support:</strong></li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Once the above steps are complete, call <strong><em>(626) 314-5937</em></strong> to speak with the help desk.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Follow the operator's instructions to verify the system and ensure the connection is established.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Confirm with the operator that the connection is successful before leaving the site, as payment will not be processed without confirmation.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Once confirmed take old serial comm to the nearest UPS, return label will be provided. If any additional chargers are needed, please provide receipt for reimbursement.</li></ul><h3>Escalation Process</h3><ul><li>If any clarification is needed, escalate to Emily Grene's support team at <strong><em>(626) 314-5937</em></strong></li><li><strong>Report any issues or questions to Emily Grene's support team.</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Disclaimer:</strong></p><p><strong>While the primary issue outlined in this work order is the main task to be completed, additional tasks may be identified or requested while you are on site. If time allows within the originally dispatched ticket, we may ask you to perform these tasks during the same visit. If more time is needed, we can dispatch a new ticket to cover the additional work while you remain on site.</strong></p><h3>Please note that the initial $100 flat rate includes the trip charge and covers the primary task. Any work performed beyond that will be compensated at a rate of $50 per hour.</h3><h3><br></h3>","markdown":"Required Procedures Upon Arrival and Before Departure from the Site\n-------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n**Upon arrival at the site, technicians must complete the following steps:**\n\n### **ServiceChannel Check-In**\n\nReport to the store office and inform management that you are with **Emily-Grene** and need to check in through **ServiceChannel** using the store phone.\n\n### **IVR Hotline Call**\n\nUsing the **store phone**, call the ServiceChannel IVR Hotline at **516-500-7776** to check in. Using the store phone ensures accurate location verification.\n\n### **Check-Out Procedure**\n\nOnce all work has been completed, technicians must repeat the IVR call process using the **store phone** to check out before leaving the site.\n\n### **If IVR Cannot Be Completed**\n\nIf you are unable to complete the IVR check-in or check-out for any reason, you **must obtain a store manager's signature before leaving the site**. The manager verification must include the date, arrival time, departure time, printed name, and signature.\n\n### **\\*\\*IMPORTANT - PAYMENT REQUIREMENT\\*\\***\n\nCompletion of the ServiceChannel IVR check-in/check-out process, or obtaining a store manager's signed verification if IVR is unavailable, is **mandatory**. ServiceChannel requires this documentation to validate the service visit.\n\n**Failure to complete one of these required verification methods may result in ServiceChannel denying payment for the work order. If Emily-Grene is unable to invoice or receive payment from ServiceChannel due to missing IVR documentation or manager verification, payment for the services performed may be withheld. Technicians are responsible for ensuring this requirement is completed before leaving the site.**\n\nServiceChannel Information\n--------------------------\n\n**PIN:** 5299239\n\n**Note:** This phone number is used exclusively for checking into and out of the work order. For all technical support or troubleshooting needs, please contact the Emily-Grene Hotline at **(626) 314-5937**.\n\n###  Overview\n\nThe Tech is required to replace and secure connections for the new serial communication device related to the refrigeration monitoring system that has been shipped to the store.\n\n**Estimated Duration:** 30 minutes\n\n### Dress Code\n\n- Collared shirt or polo\n- Black or khaki pants, no holes or tears\n- Clean, well-maintained clothing and good personal hygiene\n\n### Tools Required\n\n- Punch down tool (if necessary)\n- 4-pair testers\n- Snips\n- Precision screwdrivers/flathead\n- Toner\n\n### Scope of Work\n\n#### Pre-Site Requirements\n\n- Review the work order details prior to arrival.\n- Ensure you have all the required tools for the work order.\n\n#### On-Site Tasks\n\n1. **Check-in:** Introduce yourself to a member of management, representing Emily Grene. Do not mention Field Nation while on-site.\n2. **Inform Management:** Communicate that you are there to replace the equipment for the connection to the refrigeration monitoring system. A Waveshare was sent onsite thru UPS. Should be located in the office.\n3. **IMS Enclosure Key:** Request the key to the IMS Enclosure from management. If unavailable, call ***(626) 314-5937.***\n4. **Locate IMS Enclosure:** The enclosure is black, located in the back room near the breaker panels, containing the serial communication device.\n5. **Replace unit:**\n\n- **Please take before and after photos of connections and new terminations.**\n- **Unplug the power cable from the serial communication device.**\n- **Remove all DB9 connections,**\n- **Replace serial communications device with new wave share device.**\n- **Refer to the attached photos for guidance on the correct connections.**\n- **Comm1 of the serial comm will be going to RS-1 on the wave share, comm3 will be going to RS-3 so on and so forth.**\n- **Comm1 to RS-1 - B Negative - Black, white, orange stripe // A Positive - Clear, solid orange // Ground - Blues, browns, greens shield from cat6 (No shield from serial cable)**\n- **Comm3 to RS-3 - B Negative - Black // A Positive - Red // Ground - Shield**\n- **Rarely we will have a cable landed on comm2 and 4, please refer these connections just as comm3 is connected. The only unique connection will be comm1.**\n- **Power the wave share thru the blue USB, power cycle the PC \"Lenovo Think Edge\" for 2 mins.**\n- **Once powered back up both waveshape and PC give Tech Support a call at (626) 314-5937 to confirm visibility**\n\n1. **Call for Support:**\n\n- Once the above steps are complete, call ***(626) 314-5937*** to speak with the help desk.\n- Follow the operator's instructions to verify the system and ensure the connection is established.\n- Confirm with the operator that the connection is successful before leaving the site, as payment will not be processed without confirmation.\n- Once confirmed take old serial comm to the nearest UPS, return label will be provided. If any additional chargers are needed, please provide receipt for reimbursement.\n\n### Escalation Process\n\n- If any clarification is needed, escalate to Emily Grene's support team at ***(626) 314-5937***\n- **Report any issues or questions to Emily Grene's support team.**\n\n**Disclaimer:**\n\n**While the primary issue outlined in this work order is the main task to be completed, additional tasks may be identified or requested while you are on site. If time allows within the originally dispatched ticket, we may ask you to perform these tasks during the same visit. If more time is needed, we can dispatch a new ticket to cover the additional work while you remain on site.**\n\n### Please note that the initial $100 flat rate includes the trip charge and covers the primary task. Any work performed beyond that will be compensated at a rate of $50 per hour.\n\n###","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-18T15:00","end":"2026-09-18T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":45},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 is below minimum threshold $400"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-21T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Miniso"},{"start":"2026-09-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-09-22T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start"