{"job":{"id":"3475300687","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"DataMax Services, Inc","title":"​Concord Police Department - NC ( Phase 2 )","description":"<p>This work order is for the installation of hardware and the running of cable and wire for the Axon Interview Rooms project for policed departments.</p><p><br></p><p>The technician will work the Axon representative (TSM) on site to validate all installed devices and cable/wire runs. The TSM will be responsible for approving device placements, any hardware configuration or programming, and leading the tech through getting all cameras aimed and focused.</p><p><br></p><p>All required tools and materials are listed in the attached document \"Axon Interview Room Tools &amp; Materials Requirements.docx.\"</p><p><br></p><p>The document \"Axon Interview Room SOW.pdf\" document details the installation standard and procedure for all devices that can be included in an interview room installation.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>MATERIALS: </u>All consumable materials like 18 gauge wire, CAT6, jacks, low voltage rings, and general hardware are all included in the \"all in\" fixed price agreed upon with the technician unless a different pay structure is discussed and approved in advance.</strong></p><p><strong><u>&nbsp;</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>BUDGET &amp; SCOPE INCREASES:</u> Any out of scope or challenges on site that will require extra time and/or extra pay must be cleared with the Datamax PM while the work is in progress. Although the Axon TSM may acknowledge and approve extra work, the Datamax PM must clear it with the Axon PM to request a budget increase. If this info is not reported until later, the work may already have been invoiced. Please report all out of scope and time increases immediately. Your Datamax PM will also re-confirm any additions with you during your completion check out call.</strong></p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-21T08:00","end":"2026-09-21T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":0,"ma