{"job":{"id":19968634,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"POSRG Remarketing Group","title":"Hard Drive Swap","description":{"html":"<p>**PLEASE NOT THIS IS A TIME SENSATIVE INSTALL SINCE IT IS HAPPENING BEFORE STORE OPENS. IF YOU SHOW UP LATE YOU WILL NOT BE ALLOWED TO START AND YOU WILL BE SENT HOME**</p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work</u></strong></p><p>Upon arrival, you will introduce self on behalf of&nbsp;<strong>POSRG</strong>.</p><p>**THE VERY FIRST THING YOU SHOULD DO BEFORE YOU CALL THE GENESCO HD TO CHECK IN IS READ THE ATTACHED INSTRUCTIONS**</p><p>The Genesco help desk will ask you if you have read through the instructions when you call to check in with them, TELL THEM THAT YOU HAVE!</p><p><br></p><p>TECH: Please check in with the Genesco POS Helpdesk at 615-649-0142 once onsite for further instructions. DO NOT START INSTALL WITHOUT READING THE ATTACHED INSTRUCTIONS DOCUMENT AND THEN SPEAKING WITH AN AGENT AFTER.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Basic Overview (Please see attached detailed instructions):</u></strong></p><p>Technician to Remove inoperable HDD from base unit.</p><p>Technician to install New HDD that has been shipped to site.</p><p>Technician will then use USB drive to test configuration script on terminal.</p><p>Technician will work with the help desk personnel to verify the connectivity and functionality of all the equipment after the SOW is complete.</p><p><strong><u>**There is sensitive data on the thumb drive that we will be using for this. The customer is asking us to take 2 pictures after the install. One picture of the thumb drive in the box with SSD that we will be sending back and one picture of the box sealed with return label on it. The site is going to ship everything back but they just want to make sure they have a record of the thumb drive in the box and then it sealed.**</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Parts Instructions</u></strong></p><p>Technician is required to have a <span style=\"color: black;\">Philips #0 (to remove engage one monitor) and Philips #00 (to remove M.2 screw).</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\">**THE #0 &amp; #00 NEED TO BE REGULAR SCREWDRIVERS. A BIT IN THE APEX OF A DRILL WILL BE TOO WIDE TO FIT INTO THE BRACKET TO REMOVE THE SCREWS</strong></p><p>PLEASE NOTE, THIS CUSTOMER DOES NOT ALLOW THE USE OF ZIP TIES FOR ANY REASON! PLEASE USE VELCO STRAPS IF NEEDED.</p><p>Technician will be compensated for all materials used on site.</p><p><strong><u>Required Deliverables to be Paid</u></strong></p><p>1.&nbsp;<strong><em>MUST</em></strong>&nbsp;check in &amp; out with the&nbsp;<strong>POSRG Work Order Manager</strong></p><p>2.&nbsp;<strong><em>MUST</em></strong>&nbsp;leave detailed closing notes explaining what was done on site and any problems you ran into while on site doing the SOW.</p><p>4. Take before &amp; after pictures to confirm work completion.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Work Order Acceptance</u></strong></p><p>Do&nbsp;<strong><em>NOT</em></strong>&nbsp;request the work order if you are&nbsp;<strong><em>NOT</em></strong>&nbsp;qualified to work on POS equipment, network equipment, or network cable runs.</p>","markdown":"\\*\\*PLEASE NOT THIS IS A TIME SENSATIVE INSTALL SINCE IT IS HAPPENING BEFORE STORE OPENS. IF YOU SHOW UP LATE YOU WILL NOT BE ALLOWED TO START AND YOU WILL BE SENT HOME\\*\\*\n\n**Scope of Work**\n\nUpon arrival, you will introduce self on behalf of **POSRG**.\n\n\\*\\*THE VERY FIRST THING YOU SHOULD DO BEFORE YOU CALL THE GENESCO HD TO CHECK IN IS READ THE ATTACHED INSTRUCTIONS\\*\\*\n\nThe Genesco help desk will ask you if you have read through the instructions when you call to check in with them, TELL THEM THAT YOU HAVE!\n\nTECH: Please check in with the Genesco POS Helpdesk at 615-649-0142 once onsite for further instructions. DO NOT START INSTALL WITHOUT READING THE ATTACHED INSTRUCTIONS DOCUMENT AND THEN SPEAKING WITH AN AGENT AFTER.\n\n**Basic Overview (Please see attached detailed instructions):**\n\nTechnician to Remove inoperable HDD from base unit.\n\nTechnician to install New HDD that has been shipped to site.\n\nTechnician will then use USB drive to test configuration script on terminal.\n\nTechnician will work with the help desk personnel to verify the connectivity and functionality of all the equipment after the SOW is complete.\n\n**\\*\\*There is sensitive data on the thumb drive that we will be using for this. The customer is asking us to take 2 pictures after the install. One picture of the thumb drive in the box with SSD that we will be sending back and one picture of the box sealed with return label on it. The site is going to ship everything back but they just want to make sure they have a record of the thumb drive in the box and then it sealed.\\*\\***\n\n**Parts Instructions**\n\nTechnician is required to have a Philips #0 (to remove engage one monitor) and Philips #00 (to remove M.2 screw).\n\n**\\*\\*THE #0 & #00 NEED TO BE REGULAR SCREWDRIVERS. A BIT IN THE APEX OF A DRILL WILL BE TOO WIDE TO FIT INTO THE BRACKET TO REMOVE THE SCREWS**\n\nPLEASE NOTE, THIS CUSTOMER DOES NOT ALLOW THE USE OF ZIP TIES FOR ANY REASON! PLEASE USE VELCO STRAPS IF NEEDED.\n\nTechnician will be compensated for all materials used on site.\n\n**Required Deliverables to be Paid**\n\n1\\. ***MUST*** check in & out with the **POSRG Work Order Manager**\n\n2\\. ***MUST*** leave detailed closing notes explaining what was done on site and any problems you ran into while on site doing the SOW.\n\n4\\. Take before & after pictures to confirm work completion.\n\n**Work Order Acceptance**\n\nDo ***NOT*** request the work order if you are ***NOT*** qualified to work on POS equipment, network equipment, or network cable runs.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-14T07:30","end":"2026-10-14T11:30"},"payRange":{"min":70,"max":280},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":70,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":62},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $280 (countered: $280) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ​Concord Police Department - NC ( Phase 2 ) (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-17T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Remote Hands - Connect AT&T broadband circuit"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789585873793}
{"job":{"id":19968839,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Gigstreem","title":"Olde Raleigh -  Residential Service and troubleshooting AP  -#315185","description":{"html":"<p><strong>GiGstreem is a national Internet Service Provider delivering high-quality service to residential and commercial properties across the country.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Work Order Location:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Residential Property –</strong> Raleigh, 27612</p>\n<p><em>Refer to confidential notes for the exact address and customer contact information.</em></p>\n<p><em>CONFIRM YOU HAVE THE EXPERIENCE AND TOOLS REQUIRED BEFORE APPLYING FOR THIS WORK ORDER.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Scope of Work</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Dispatch an experienced network technician to perform advanced troubleshooting on apartment</strong> where the APs are intermittently going offline.</p>\n<p>A technician is needed to identify any underlying cabling or infrastructure issues causing the APs to lose connectivity.</p>\n<p><strong>Work Details</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Visit <strong>both affected units</strong> at the property.</li>\n<li>Thoroughly inspect and test the Ethernet cabling between each AP and the IDF.</li>\n<li>Verify cable integrity using a cable tester to check for opens, shorts, split pairs, excessive length, and intermittent faults.</li>\n<li>Inspect and re-terminate cable ends if necessary.</li>\n<li>Verify PoE delivery, switch port status, and AP uplink connectivity.</li>\n<li>Inspect patch panel connections and verify all terminations are secure.</li>\n<li>Identify any wiring, infrastructure, or environmental issues that may be causing the APs to go offline intermittently.</li>\n<li>Work directly with Gigstreem Engineering during troubleshooting.</li>\n<li>Do not leave the site until Engineering has reviewed the findings.</li>\n<li>Upload photos of the APs, IDF, cabling, and any repairs performed.</li>\n<li>Provide detailed notes, cable test results, and all findings upon completion.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Technician Expectations:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Confirm the appointment time</strong> with the customer before heading to the property.</li>\n<li><strong>Place a courtesy call at least 30 minutes prior to arrival</strong> to inform the customer of your estimated time of arrival (ETA).</li>\n<li>Upon arriving on site, all Field Nation technicians are required to <strong><u>check in at the leasing office or front desk before proceeding to any unit.</u></strong> Contractors must announce their arrival and present their Field Nation ID and credentials for verification. <strong><u>Entry into any resident’s unit is not permitted until this check‑in process is completed and approved by onsite staff.</u></strong></li>\n<li><strong>Represent the brand</strong> with professionalism. Appearance, communication, and the quality of your work must reflect high standards.</li>\n<li><strong>Do not overshare</strong> internal processes or technical details with the customer. Communication should be simple, courteous, and focused on resolving the issue.</li>\n<li>⚠️ <em>If the technician arrives unprepared, misinforms the customer, demonstrates poor presentation, or delivers substandard work, GiGstreem reserves the right to withhold payment for the work order.</em></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Required Experience:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Troubleshooting Ruckus Access Points (including reset, removal from wall mount, etc.)</li>\n<li>Networking/Telecommunications experience</li>\n<li>Experience with copper cabling: Cat5e/Cat6 testing, RJ45 termination</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Required Tools:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Laptop with Ethernet port or USB-to-Ethernet adapter</li>\n<li>Cable tester/certifier (capable of testing wiremap, opens, shorts, split pairs, cable length, and PoE)</li>\n<li>Tone generator and probe</li>\n<li>RJ45 crimping tool</li>\n<li>RJ45 connectors</li>\n<li>Punch-down tool</li>\n<li>Known-good Ethernet patch cables</li>\n<li>Basic hand tools</li>\n<li>Flashlight</li>\n<li>Smartphone for photos and documentation</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Coordination:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Troubleshoot in collaboration with GiGstreem’s Network Operations Team</li>\n<li>Refer to confidential notes for Network Operations and customer contact details.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>At Gigstreem, delivering reliable, high-performance internet service is our top priority. To maintain the integrity of our network and ensure consistent customer experiences, we follow strict guidelines regarding the equipment and solutions we support. This includes a clear stance on the use of Wi-Fi extenders.</p>\n<p><strong><u>Policy on Wi-Fi Extenders - Gigstreem Policy Reminder:</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>It is strictly against Gigstreem policy to utilize, install, or recommend Wi-Fi extenders as a solution for speed, coverage, or connectivity issues within a unit.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Why This Matters:</li>\n<li>Wi-Fi extenders are not part of our approved network architecture.</li>\n<li>They can introduce interference, degrade performance, and complicate troubleshooting.</li>\n<li>Recommending or installing extenders may lead to inconsistent service and customer dissatisfaction.</li>\n<li>Approved Resolution Methods:</li>\n<li>Thorough troubleshooting of the existing AP and network configuration</li>\n<li>Collaboration with engineering to assess AP configuration</li>\n<li>All technicians and support staff must adhere to this policy without exception. Any deviation should be escalated to management for review.</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**GiGstreem is a national Internet Service Provider delivering high-quality service to residential and commercial properties across the country.**\n\n**Work Order Location:**\n\n**Residential Property –** Raleigh, 27612\n\n*Refer to confidential notes for the exact address and customer contact information.*\n\n*CONFIRM YOU HAVE THE EXPERIENCE AND TOOLS REQUIRED BEFORE APPLYING FOR THIS WORK ORDER.*\n\n**Scope of Work**\n\n**Dispatch an experienced network technician to perform advanced troubleshooting on apartment** where the APs are intermittently going offline.\n\nA technician is needed to identify any underlying cabling or infrastructure issues causing the APs to lose connectivity.\n\n**Work Details**\n\n- Visit **both affected units** at the property.\n- Thoroughly inspect and test the Ethernet cabling between each AP and the IDF.\n- Verify cable integrity using a cable tester to check for opens, shorts, split pairs, excessive length, and intermittent faults.\n- Inspect and re-terminate cable ends if necessary.\n- Verify PoE delivery, switch port status, and AP uplink connectivity.\n- Inspect patch panel connections and verify all terminations are secure.\n- Identify any wiring, infrastructure, or environmental issues that may be causing the APs to go offline intermittently.\n- Work directly with Gigstreem Engineering during troubleshooting.\n- Do not leave the site until Engineering has reviewed the findings.\n- Upload photos of the APs, IDF, cabling, and any repairs performed.\n- Provide detailed notes, cable test results, and all findings upon completion.\n\n**Technician Expectations:**\n\n- **Confirm the appointment time** with the customer before heading to the property.\n- **Place a courtesy call at least 30 minutes prior to arrival** to inform the customer of your estimated time of arrival (ETA).\n- Upon arriving on site, all Field Nation technicians are required to **check in at the leasing office or front desk before proceeding to any unit.** Contractors must announce their arrival and present their Field Nation ID and credentials for verification. **Entry into any resident’s unit is not permitted until this check‑in process is completed and approved by onsite staff.**\n- **Represent the brand** with professionalism. Appearance, communication, and the quality of your work must reflect high standards.\n- **Do not overshare** internal processes or technical details with the customer. Communication should be simple, courteous, and focused on resolving the issue.\n- ⚠️ *If the technician arrives unprepared, misinforms the customer, demonstrates poor presentation, or delivers substandard work, GiGstreem reserves the right to withhold payment for the work order.*\n\n**Required Experience:**\n\n- Troubleshooting Ruckus Access Points (including reset, removal from wall mount, etc.)\n- Networking/Telecommunications experience\n- Experience with copper cabling: Cat5e/Cat6 testing, RJ45 termination\n\n**Required Tools:**\n\n- Laptop with Ethernet port or USB-to-Ethernet adapter\n- Cable tester/certifier (capable of testing wiremap, opens, shorts, split pairs, cable length, and PoE)\n- Tone generator and probe\n- RJ45 crimping tool\n- RJ45 connectors\n- Punch-down tool\n- Known-good Ethernet patch cables\n- Basic hand tools\n- Flashlight\n- Smartphone for photos and documentation\n\n**Coordination:**\n\n- Troubleshoot in collaboration with GiGstreem’s Network Operations Team\n- Refer to confidential notes for Network Operations and customer contact details.\n\nAt Gigstreem, delivering reliable, high-performance internet service is our top priority. To maintain the integrity of our network and ensure consistent customer experiences, we follow strict guidelines regarding the equipment and solutions we support. This includes a clear stance on the use of Wi-Fi extenders.\n\n**Policy on Wi-Fi Extenders - Gigstreem Policy Reminder:**\n\n**It is strictly against Gigstreem policy to utilize, install, or recommend Wi-Fi extenders as a solution for speed, coverage, or connectivity issues within a unit.**\n\n- Why This Matters:\n- Wi-Fi extenders are not part of our approved network architecture.\n- They can introduce interference, degrade performance, and complicate troubleshooting.\n- Recommending or installing extenders may lead to inconsistent service and customer dissatisfaction.\n- Approved Resolution Methods:\n- Thorough troubleshooting of the existing AP and network configuration\n- Collaboration with engineering to assess AP configuration\n- All technicians and support staff must adhere to this policy without exception. Any deviation should be escalated to management for review.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-18T10:00","end":"2026-09-18T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":200,"max":275},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":200},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":75}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":3},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $275 is below minimum threshold $400"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ​Concord Police Department - NC ( Phase 2 ) (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-17T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Remote Hands - Connect AT&T broadband circuit"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789586830584}
{"job":{"id":19937682,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"CIS","title":"Tractor Supply - Palo Alto Ion Replacement","description":{"html":"<p>The&nbsp;onsite&nbsp;Field&nbsp;Service&nbsp;Technician&nbsp;will&nbsp;work&nbsp;with&nbsp;a&nbsp;remote&nbsp;CIS&nbsp;support&nbsp;engineer&nbsp;to&nbsp;replace&nbsp;two&nbsp;existing&nbsp;Palo&nbsp;Alto&nbsp;Prisma&nbsp;SD-WAN&nbsp;ION&nbsp;2000&nbsp;appliances&nbsp;with&nbsp;new&nbsp;ION&nbsp;1200-S&nbsp;appliances&nbsp;at&nbsp;an&nbsp;active&nbsp;retail&nbsp;location.&nbsp;The&nbsp;technician&nbsp;will&nbsp;primarily&nbsp;perform&nbsp;physical&nbsp;installation,&nbsp;cabling,&nbsp;equipment&nbsp;identification,&nbsp;testing&nbsp;assistance,&nbsp;documentation,&nbsp;and&nbsp;removal/packaging&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;legacy&nbsp;equipment.&nbsp;All&nbsp;network&nbsp;configuration&nbsp;and&nbsp;backend&nbsp;changes&nbsp;will&nbsp;be&nbsp;performed&nbsp;remotely&nbsp;by&nbsp;CIS.</p>\n<p><strong>Field&nbsp;Technician&nbsp;Scope:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Check&nbsp;in&nbsp;with&nbsp;CIS's&nbsp;remote&nbsp;technical&nbsp;support&nbsp;and&nbsp;the&nbsp;onsite&nbsp;Manager&nbsp;on&nbsp;Duty&nbsp;(MOD)&nbsp;and&nbsp;confirm&nbsp;access&nbsp;to&nbsp;the&nbsp;network&nbsp;rack/cabinet.</li>\n<li>Locate&nbsp;and&nbsp;verify&nbsp;the&nbsp;replacement&nbsp;ION&nbsp;1200-S&nbsp;appliances,&nbsp;power&nbsp;supplies,&nbsp;mounting&nbsp;trays,&nbsp;cabling,&nbsp;and&nbsp;associated&nbsp;hardware.</li>\n<li>Identify&nbsp;the&nbsp;existing&nbsp;primary&nbsp;and&nbsp;backup&nbsp;ION&nbsp;2000&nbsp;appliances&nbsp;and&nbsp;associated&nbsp;WAN/LAN&nbsp;connections.</li>\n<li>Take&nbsp;clear&nbsp;before-work&nbsp;photographs&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;network&nbsp;rack,&nbsp;existing&nbsp;equipment,&nbsp;cabling,&nbsp;and&nbsp;port&nbsp;connections.</li>\n<li>Physically&nbsp;label&nbsp;the&nbsp;new&nbsp;primary&nbsp;and&nbsp;backup&nbsp;ION&nbsp;appliances&nbsp;as&nbsp;directed&nbsp;by&nbsp;the&nbsp;remote&nbsp;CIS&nbsp;engineer.</li>\n<li>Install&nbsp;and&nbsp;secure&nbsp;the&nbsp;supplied&nbsp;mounting&nbsp;trays&nbsp;and&nbsp;new&nbsp;ION&nbsp;1200-S&nbsp;appliances&nbsp;in&nbsp;the&nbsp;network&nbsp;rack/cabinet.</li>\n<li>Connect&nbsp;power&nbsp;and&nbsp;required&nbsp;inter-device&nbsp;cabling&nbsp;to&nbsp;the&nbsp;new&nbsp;appliances.</li>\n<li>Move&nbsp;existing&nbsp;cellular&nbsp;WAN,&nbsp;broadband&nbsp;WAN,&nbsp;and&nbsp;LAN/switch&nbsp;connections&nbsp;from&nbsp;the&nbsp;legacy&nbsp;appliances&nbsp;to&nbsp;the&nbsp;new&nbsp;appliances&nbsp;as&nbsp;directed&nbsp;by&nbsp;CIS.</li>\n<li>Manually&nbsp;reboot&nbsp;the&nbsp;onsite&nbsp;cellular&nbsp;gateway/Inseego&nbsp;device&nbsp;and&nbsp;broadband&nbsp;modem&nbsp;when&nbsp;instructed.</li>\n<li>Verify&nbsp;and/or&nbsp;reseat&nbsp;network&nbsp;cables&nbsp;when&nbsp;requested&nbsp;by&nbsp;the&nbsp;remote&nbsp;support&nbsp;team&nbsp;during&nbsp;testing.</li>\n<li>Remain&nbsp;onsite&nbsp;and&nbsp;available&nbsp;while&nbsp;CIS&nbsp;remotely&nbsp;validates&nbsp;appliance&nbsp;connectivity,&nbsp;VPN&nbsp;connectivity,&nbsp;HA&nbsp;operation,&nbsp;and&nbsp;store&nbsp;network&nbsp;connectivity.</li>\n<li>Coordinate&nbsp;with&nbsp;the&nbsp;MOD&nbsp;to&nbsp;validate&nbsp;critical&nbsp;store&nbsp;services,&nbsp;including&nbsp;POS/registers,&nbsp;workstation&nbsp;connectivity,&nbsp;Wi-Fi,&nbsp;phones,&nbsp;and&nbsp;printers.</li>\n<li>If&nbsp;required,&nbsp;assist&nbsp;with&nbsp;physical&nbsp;rollback&nbsp;by&nbsp;reconnecting&nbsp;the&nbsp;original&nbsp;equipment&nbsp;and&nbsp;cabling&nbsp;under&nbsp;CIS&nbsp;direction.</li>\n<li>Once&nbsp;final&nbsp;approval&nbsp;is&nbsp;received,&nbsp;remove&nbsp;the&nbsp;legacy&nbsp;ION&nbsp;2000&nbsp;appliances&nbsp;and&nbsp;associated&nbsp;mounting&nbsp;hardware.</li>\n<li>Package&nbsp;the&nbsp;legacy&nbsp;appliances,&nbsp;power&nbsp;supplies,&nbsp;and&nbsp;mounting&nbsp;hardware&nbsp;using&nbsp;the&nbsp;provided&nbsp;return&nbsp;materials&nbsp;and&nbsp;shipping&nbsp;labels.</li>\n<li>Perform&nbsp;final&nbsp;cable&nbsp;management&nbsp;and&nbsp;leave&nbsp;the&nbsp;network&nbsp;rack/cabinet&nbsp;clean&nbsp;and&nbsp;orderly.</li>\n<li>Provide&nbsp;required&nbsp;completion&nbsp;photographs,&nbsp;including&nbsp;final&nbsp;rack&nbsp;condition,&nbsp;appliance&nbsp;cabling/ports,&nbsp;and&nbsp;packaged&nbsp;return&nbsp;equipment.</li>\n<li>Provide&nbsp;legacy&nbsp;equipment&nbsp;serial&nbsp;numbers&nbsp;and&nbsp;any&nbsp;requested&nbsp;closeout&nbsp;information&nbsp;to&nbsp;the&nbsp;remote&nbsp;CIS&nbsp;support&nbsp;resource.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Technician&nbsp;Requirements:</strong></p>\n<p>Technician&nbsp;should&nbsp;have&nbsp;standard&nbsp;network&nbsp;field-service&nbsp;tools&nbsp;and&nbsp;be&nbsp;comfortable&nbsp;identifying,&nbsp;mounting,&nbsp;labeling,&nbsp;connecting,&nbsp;disconnecting,&nbsp;and&nbsp;documenting&nbsp;enterprise&nbsp;network&nbsp;equipment.&nbsp;The&nbsp;technician&nbsp;must&nbsp;follow&nbsp;remote&nbsp;CIS&nbsp;direction&nbsp;and&nbsp;should&nbsp;not&nbsp;move&nbsp;production&nbsp;network&nbsp;cabling&nbsp;or&nbsp;remove&nbsp;legacy&nbsp;equipment&nbsp;until&nbsp;specifically&nbsp;authorized.</p>\n<p><strong>Materials&nbsp;-&nbsp;**Please&nbsp;have&nbsp;extras&nbsp;of&nbsp;all&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;below:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Cat5e&nbsp;cable&nbsp;(at&nbsp;least&nbsp;200’)</li>\n<li>Single&nbsp;Port&nbsp;Surface&nbsp;Mount&nbsp;Boxes</li>\n<li>Cat5e&nbsp;Keystone&nbsp;Jacks</li>\n<li>Cat5e&nbsp;Patch&nbsp;Cables&nbsp;(Varying&nbsp;Lengths)</li>\n<li>Zip&nbsp;Ties</li>\n<li>Velcro&nbsp;Strips</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Required&nbsp;Tools:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Laptop&nbsp;w/Power&nbsp;supply</li>\n<li>Windows&nbsp;10&nbsp;(Caution:&nbsp;do&nbsp;not&nbsp;use&nbsp;a&nbsp;laptop&nbsp;with&nbsp;Windows&nbsp;7&nbsp;or&nbsp;earlier)</li>\n<li>With&nbsp;Ethernet&nbsp;port&nbsp;OR&nbsp;USB&nbsp;–&nbsp;Ethernet&nbsp;Adaptor</li>\n<li>Cable&nbsp;Tester</li>\n<li>Cable&nbsp;Toner</li>\n<li>Crimper</li>\n<li>Label&nbsp;Maker</li>\n<li>Cisco&nbsp;Console&nbsp;Cable</li>\n<li>General&nbsp;purpose&nbsp;tools&nbsp;for&nbsp;mounting&nbsp;equipment&nbsp;(e.g.,&nbsp;power&nbsp;drill,&nbsp;screwdriver&nbsp;etc.)</li>\n<li>Cell&nbsp;Phone&nbsp;w/full&nbsp;battery&nbsp;and&nbsp;Charger&nbsp;(camera&nbsp;required)</li>\n<li>Cellular&nbsp;Hotspot</li>\n<li>Standard&nbsp;Measuring&nbsp;tools</li>\n<li>Ladder/&nbsp;Folding&nbsp;Ladder&nbsp;of&nbsp;at&nbsp;least&nbsp;6’</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"The onsite Field Service Technician will work with a remote CIS support engineer to replace two existing Palo Alto Prisma SD-WAN ION 2000 appliances with new ION 1200-S appliances at an active retail location. The technician will primarily perform physical installation, cabling, equipment identification, testing assistance, documentation, and removal/packaging of the legacy equipment. All network configuration and backend changes will be performed remotely by CIS.\n\n**Field Technician Scope:**\n\n- Check in with CIS's remote technical support and the onsite Manager on Duty (MOD) and confirm access to the network rack/cabinet.\n- Locate and verify the replacement ION 1200-S appliances, power supplies, mounting trays, cabling, and associated hardware.\n- Identify the existing primary and backup ION 2000 appliances and associated WAN/LAN connections.\n- Take clear before-work photographs of the network rack, existing equipment, cabling, and port connections.\n- Physically label the new primary and backup ION appliances as directed by the remote CIS engineer.\n- Install and secure the supplied mounting trays and new ION 1200-S appliances in the network rack/cabinet.\n- Connect power and required inter-device cabling to the new appliances.\n- Move existing cellular WAN, broadband WAN, and LAN/switch connections from the legacy appliances to the new appliances as directed by CIS.\n- Manually reboot the onsite cellular gateway/Inseego device and broadband modem when instructed.\n- Verify and/or reseat network cables when requested by the remote support team during testing.\n- Remain onsite and available while CIS remotely validates appliance connectivity, VPN connectivity, HA operation, and store network connectivity.\n- Coordinate with the MOD to validate critical store services, including POS/registers, workstation connectivity, Wi-Fi, phones, and printers.\n- If required, assist with physical rollback by reconnecting the original equipment and cabling under CIS direction.\n- Once final approval is received, remove the legacy ION 2000 appliances and associated mounting hardware.\n- Package the legacy appliances, power supplies, and mounting hardware using the provided return materials and shipping labels.\n- Perform final cable management and leave the network rack/cabinet clean and orderly.\n- Provide required completion photographs, including final rack condition, appliance cabling/ports, and packaged return equipment.\n- Provide legacy equipment serial numbers and any requested closeout information to the remote CIS support resource.\n\n**Technician Requirements:**\n\nTechnician should have standard network field-service tools and be comfortable identifying, mounting, labeling, connecting, disconnecting, and documenting enterprise network equipment. The technician must follow remote CIS direction and should not move production network cabling or remove legacy equipment until specifically authorized.\n\n**Materials - \\*\\*Please have extras of all of the below:**\n\n- Cat5e cable (at least 200’)\n- Single Port Surface Mount Boxes\n- Cat5e Keystone Jacks\n- Cat5e Patch Cables (Varying Lengths)\n- Zip Ties\n- Velcro Strips\n\nRequired Tools:\n\n- Laptop w/Power supply\n- Windows 10 (Caution: do not use a laptop with Windows 7 or earlier)\n- With Ethernet port OR USB – Ethernet Adaptor\n- Cable Tester\n- Cable Toner\n- Crimper\n- Label Maker\n- Cisco Console Cable\n- General purpose tools for mounting equipment (e.g., power drill, screwdriver etc.)\n- Cell Phone w/full battery and Charger (camera required)\n- Cellular Hotspot\n- Standard Measuring tools\n- Ladder/ Folding Ladder of at least 6’","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-28T07:30","end":"2026-09-28T09:30"},"payRange":{"min":120,"max":120},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":44},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $120 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ​Concord Police Department - NC ( Phase 2 ) (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"star