{"job":{"id":19968630,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"PurTeraIT","title":"Fast Food Restaurant #766 — Refranchise Conversion — Greensboro, NC","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>OVERVIEW</u></strong></p><p>Provide onsite technical support at the assigned restaurant location. Work includes network cable moves, payment terminal reconfiguration, removal and packaging of legacy equipment, installation of a new manager workstation, testing, and completion documentation.</p><p><strong><u>IMPORTANT CUTOVER REQUIREMENT</u></strong></p><p>Do not begin network-related cable moves until the remote Installation Support Team confirms that the network migration is complete and the applicable firewalls and switches are online.</p><ul><li>Tech will be contacted by the support team a day or two in advance to review the documentation, tech will also be required to be on a pre call teams meeting 30 minutes prior to starting the conversion after arriving onsite. </li><li>Tech will be required to provide email address </li><li>Store specific documents will get added closer to install date, Examples have been added to review </li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Make sure that you follow the installation guide in order of the steps and do not skip ahead. If the steps are not done in order it will mess up the system and will cause things to not work and further troubleshooting will need to be done to get it back in sync. </u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>SCOPE OF WORK</u></strong></p><ol><li>Check in according to the work order instructions and contact the remote support team.</li><li>Review the site-specific installation guide and switch-port mapping before moving any cables.</li><li><strong>Reorganize network switch connections:</strong></li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Locate the applicable network switches.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Move existing Ethernet connections to the designated Meraki switch ports.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Add or remove Ethernet patch connections as directed.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Follow the documented sequence for all cable changes.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Notify remote support after completing the cable moves.</li></ul><ol><li><strong>Reconfigure applicable IP PIN pads, including kiosk payment terminals where present:</strong></li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Power-cycle the devices.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Access the required configuration workflow.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Enter the provided Merchant ID and Terminal ID information.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Complete the required reboot and configuration steps.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Perform or assist with a test transaction through the associated POS terminal.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Escalate configuration or transaction failures to remote support.</li></ul><ol><li><strong>Remove legacy equipment:</strong></li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Power down and disconnect the existing manager PC.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Disconnect power, network, video, keyboard, mouse, and peripheral connections.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Remove the identified legacy tablet and any applicable manager tablets.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Place all designated equipment in the provided return packaging.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Do not remove packaged equipment from the site.</li></ul><ol><li><strong>Install the new manager PC:</strong></li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Unbox and position the new workstation.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Connect the provided power, Ethernet, video, keyboard, mouse, and peripherals.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Install the provided HDMI adapter if required.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Connect the workstation to the designated switch port according to the site documentation.</li></ul><ol><li><strong>Test and close out:</strong></li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Work with remote support throughout the installation and cutover.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Troubleshoot physical connectivity issues directly related to the work performed.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Escalate application, payment-processing, configuration, or advanced network issues.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Complete a final walkthrough with available site personnel.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Document all unresolved issues and escalations.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Obtain authorization from remote support before leaving.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Check out through Field Nation and complete all required forms.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>REQUIRED TOOLS</u></strong></p><ul><li>Ethernet cable tester</li><li>Ethernet toner and probe</li><li>Basic technician hand-tool kit</li><li>Phillips and flathead screwdrivers</li><li>Flashlight</li><li>Smartphone capable of accessing project communications and taking clear photographs</li><li>Smartphone charger and portable power bank</li><li>Laptop with an Ethernet port or compatible Ethernet adapter</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>SITE-PROVIDED ITEMS</strong></p><p>The new workstation, required hardware, patch cables, labels, adapters, power and video cables, peripherals, return packaging, port maps, payment-terminal configuration information, and other installation materials are expected to be onsite. Report missing items immediately.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>REQUIRED DELIVERABLES</u></strong></p><ul><li>Check-in and check-out confirmation</li><li>Clear before-and-after installation photographs</li><li>Completed installation checklist or required online form</li><li>Confirmation of network cable moves</li><li>Confirmation of PIN pad configuration and transaction testing</li><li>Confirmation of manager PC replacement</li><li>Documentation of open issues and escalations</li><li>Final site completion status</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p>","markdown":"**OVERVIEW**\n\nProvide onsite technical support at the assigned restaurant location. Work includes network cable moves, payment terminal reconfiguration, removal and packaging of legacy equipment, installation of a new manager workstation, testing, and completion documentation.\n\n**IMPORTANT CUTOVER REQUIREMENT**\n\nDo not begin network-related cable moves until the remote Installation Support Team confirms that the network migration is complete and the applicable firewalls and switches are online.\n\n- Tech will be contacted by the support team a day or two in advance to review the documentation, tech will also be required to be on a pre call teams meeting 30 minutes prior to starting the conversion after arriving onsite.\n- Tech will be required to provide email address\n- Store specific documents will get added closer to install date, Examples have been added to review\n\n**Make sure that you follow the installation guide in order of the steps and do not skip ahead. If the steps are not done in order it will mess up the system and will cause things to not work and further troubleshooting will need to be done to get it back in sync.**\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK**\n\n1. Check in according to the work order instructions and contact the remote support team.\n2. Review the site-specific installation guide and switch-port mapping before moving any cables.\n3. **Reorganize network switch connections:**\n\n- Locate the applicable network switches.\n- Move existing Ethernet connections to the designated Meraki switch ports.\n- Add or remove Ethernet patch connections as directed.\n- Follow the documented sequence for all cable changes.\n- Notify remote support after completing the cable moves.\n\n1. **Reconfigure applicable IP PIN pads, including kiosk payment terminals where present:**\n\n- Power-cycle the devices.\n- Access the required configuration workflow.\n- Enter the provided Merchant ID and Terminal ID information.\n- Complete the required reboot and configuration steps.\n- Perform or assist with a test transaction through the associated POS terminal.\n- Escalate configuration or transaction failures to remote support.\n\n1. **Remove legacy equipment:**\n\n- Power down and disconnect the existing manager PC.\n- Disconnect power, network, video, keyboard, mouse, and peripheral connections.\n- Remove the identified legacy tablet and any applicable manager tablets.\n- Place all designated equipment in the provided return packaging.\n- Do not remove packaged equipment from the site.\n\n1. **Install the new manager PC:**\n\n- Unbox and position the new workstation.\n- Connect the provided power, Ethernet, video, keyboard, mouse, and peripherals.\n- Install the provided HDMI adapter if required.\n- Connect the workstation to the designated switch port according to the site documentation.\n\n1. **Test and close out:**\n\n- Work with remote support throughout the installation and cutover.\n- Troubleshoot physical connectivity issues directly related to the work performed.\n- Escalate application, payment-processing, configuration, or advanced network issues.\n- Complete a final walkthrough with available site personnel.\n- Document all unresolved issues and escalations.\n- Obtain authorization from remote support before leaving.\n- Check out through Field Nation and complete all required forms.\n\n**REQUIRED TOOLS**\n\n- Ethernet cable tester\n- Ethernet toner and probe\n- Basic technician hand-tool kit\n- Phillips and flathead screwdrivers\n- Flashlight\n- Smartphone capable of accessing project communications and taking clear photographs\n- Smartphone charger and portable power bank\n- Laptop with an Ethernet port or compatible Ethernet adapter\n\n**SITE-PROVIDED ITEMS**\n\nThe new workstation, required hardware, patch cables, labels, adapters, power and video cables, peripherals, return packaging, port maps, payment-terminal configuration information, and other installation materials are expected to be onsite. Report missing items immediately.\n\n**REQUIRED DELIVERABLES**\n\n- Check-in and check-out confirmation\n- Clear before-and-after installation photographs\n- Completed installation checklist or required online form\n- Confirmation of network cable moves\n- Confirmation of PIN pad configuration and transaction testing\n- Confirmation of manager PC replacement\n- Documentation of open issues and escalations\n- Final site completion status","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-22T16:00","end":"2026-09-22T20:00"},"payRange":{"min":300,"max":860},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":4,"amount":300},"additional":{"units":8,"amount":70}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":64},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"blended","counterRate":75,"baseAmount":900,"estHours":4,"travelExpense":95,"payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":4,"amount":300},"additional":{"units":8,"amount":75}},"counterDate":{"start":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T17:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":60,"mode":"hours","reason":"arrival_window"}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Miniso"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ​Concord Police Department - NC ( Phase 2 ) (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPM