uration, removal and packaging of legacy equipment, installation of a new manager workstation, testing, and completion documentation.\n\n**IMPORTANT CUTOVER REQUIREMENT**\n\nDo not begin network-related cable moves until the remote Installation Support Team confirms that the network migration is complete and the applicable firewalls and switches are online.\n\n- Tech will be contacted by the support team a day or two in advance to review the documentation, tech will also be required to be on a pre call teams meeting 30 minutes prior to starting the conversion after arriving onsite.\n- Tech will be required to provide email address\n- Store specific documents will get added closer to install date, Examples have been added to review\n\n**Make sure that you follow the installation guide in order of the steps and do not skip ahead. If the steps are not done in order it will mess up the system and will cause things to not work and further troubleshooting will need to be done to get it back in sync.**\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK**\n\n1. Check in according to the work order instructions and contact the remote support team.\n2. Review the site-specific installation guide and switch-port mapping before moving any cables.\n3. **Reorganize network switch connections:**\n\n- Locate the applicable network switches.\n- Move existing Ethernet connections to the designated Meraki switch ports.\n- Add or remove Ethernet patch connections as directed.\n- Follow the documented sequence for all cable changes.\n- Notify remote support after completing the cable moves.\n\n1. **Reconfigure applicable IP PIN pads, including kiosk payment terminals where present:**\n\n- Power-cycle the devices.\n- Access the required configuration workflow.\n- Enter the provided Merchant ID and Terminal ID information.\n- Complete the required reboot and configuration steps.\n- Perform or assist with a test transaction through the associated POS terminal.\n- Escalate configuration or transaction failures to remote support.\n\n1. **Remove legacy equipment:**\n\n- Power down and disconnect the existing manager PC.\n- Disconnect power, network, video, keyboard, mouse, and peripheral connections.\n- Remove the identified legacy tablet and any applicable manager tablets.\n- Place all designated equipment in the provided return packaging.\n- Do not remove packaged equipment from the site.\n\n1. **Install the new manager PC:**\n\n- Unbox and position the new workstation.\n- Connect the provided power, Ethernet, video, keyboard, mouse, and peripherals.\n- Install the provided HDMI adapter if required.\n- Connect the workstation to the designated switch port according to the site documentation.\n\n1. **Test and close out:**\n\n- Work with remote support throughout the installation and cutover.\n- Troubleshoot physical connectivity issues directly related to the work performed.\n- Escalate application, payment-processing, configuration, or advanced network issues.\n- Complete a final walkthrough with available site personnel.\n- Document all unresolved issues and escalations.\n- Obtain authorization from remote support before leaving.\n- Check out through Field Nation and complete all required forms.\n\n**REQUIRED TOOLS**\n\n- Ethernet cable tester\n- Ethernet toner and probe\n- Basic technician hand-tool kit\n- Phillips and flathead screwdrivers\n- Flashlight\n- Smartphone capable of accessing project communications and taking clear photographs\n- Smartphone charger and portable power bank\n- Laptop with an Ethernet port or compatible Ethernet adapter\n\n**SITE-PROVIDED ITEMS**\n\nThe new workstation, required hardware, patch cables, labels, adapters, power and video cables, peripherals, return packaging, port maps, payment-terminal configuration information, and other installation materials are expected to be onsite. Report missing items immediately.\n\n**REQUIRED DELIVERABLES**\n\n- Check-in and check-out confirmation\n- Clear before-and-after installation photographs\n- Completed installation checklist or required online form\n- Confirmation of network cable moves\n- Confirmation of PIN pad configuration and transaction testing\n- Confirmation of manager PC replacement\n- Documentation of open issues and escalations\n- Final site completion status","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-22T16:00","end":"2026-09-22T20:00"},"payRange":{"min":300,"max":860},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":4,"amount":300},"additional":{"units":8,"amount":70}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":37},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"blended","counterRate":75,"baseAmount":900,"estHours":4,"travelExpense":60,"payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":4,"amount":300},"additional":{"units":8,"amount":75}},"counterDate":{"start":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T17:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":60,"mode":"hours","reason":"arrival_window"}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Miniso"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ​Concord Police Department - NC ( Phase 2 ) (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-17T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Remote Hands - Connect AT&T broadband circuit"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1789589153567}
{"job":{"id":19969299,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"ASR tech","title":"Install (Outdoor) Automated Package Locker System (2 Techs Required) 2 DAYS REQUIRED 9/21 & 9/22","description":{"html":"<p><strong>INSTALLING AUTOMATED LOCKERS-High End Properties.</strong></p><p><strong><em><u>Full Work Description </u></em></strong>This work order is to install an automated lockers in a luxury apartment complex or other commercial property. Location may still be under construction so please be sure to have the required safety gear (Hard Hat, long pants, Safety Vest and Steel toed boots) as you may not be permitted onsite. <strong>To insure a successful install, entire work order MUST be read and understood. Technician is representing ASR and should be referred to as an ASR installer of Parcel Pending Lockers.&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><u>ASR PROFESSIONALISM REQUIREMENTS</u></strong></p><p><strong>SCHEDULING-FIRM START TIME: </strong>Work order may NOT be rescheduled. Accepting tech is required to be on site the date listed, no exceptions.</p><p><strong>Delays or issues arriving on time, CALL ASR SUPPORT TEAM: Contacts are listed under CONFIDENTIAL. IF YOU CALL ASR and do not leave a message it is not a phone call logged. </strong>Technician should only discuss scheduling or payment issues with ASR support desk, if the customer reaches out directly to you, please refer them back to ASR.</p><p><strong>TECHNICIAN ASSIGNED-</strong><u>The name of the individual accepting this work must be the actual person who arrives on site and if we determine there was a substitution without prior notice, we will not pay for the work performed.&nbsp;Be sure to notify ASR by phone and message in work order prior to scheduled start time and before techs arrival onsite. ASR SUPPPORT TEAM is listed under CONFIDENTIAL</u></p><p><strong>The accepting technician must meet ALL requirements below: </strong></p><p><strong>Technician must have working knowledge/experience with either mounting a flat screen and/or install and secure cabinet/fixtures to different types of walls (drywall w/ wood studs, drywall w/aluminum, plaster, Stucco, wood/aluminum siding, clay brick, cinder block or concrete. Tech must have a laptop with HyperTerminal or Putty to be able to SSH into Linux base device through Ethernet connection on laptop. </strong></p><p><strong>DRESS CODE-casual business attire with no logos.</strong></p><p><strong>CUSTOMER SERVICE- These sites are very particular of work performed onsite, technician must present professionalism at all times. </strong>Be friendly, communicate, and assure them they're in good hands.&nbsp;<strong>Please note: Parcel Pending will be sending a post install survey regarding the overall install and tech performance.&nbsp;Please be mindful of this. ALL Conversations must be professional at all times. It is extremely important to understand the scope of work and develop good communication with your ASR support member.</strong></p><p><strong>DRUG-FREE WORKPLACE- ASR</strong> Services intends to help provide a safe and drug-free work environment. The technician needs to ensure they do not smell or reek of odors or other substances. <strong>These sites are very particular of work performed onsite, technician must present professionalism at all times.</strong></p><p><strong>PAYMENT-</strong>Payment will be approved after the following:</p><ul><li>Completed BOL paperwork with tech and delivery team signatures e-mailed to parcelpendingsupport@asrepairtech.com and uploaded to work order as backup</li><li>Completed Install form is uploaded to work order and scanned/e-mailed to parcelpendingsupport@asrepairtech.com (and confirmed received)</li><li>Photos are uploaded to work order, reviewed by ASR Support Team and finished work is approved by ASR Support as completed.</li></ul><p><strong>Pay is a fixed rate for successful installed lockers approved by ASR support. Approvals are not verbal, approved installs are approved in writing by ASR support, pictures are reviewed and logged, any verbal approvals may not be considered. If you are asked to return to provide ANY missing pictures after you left site you must do so on your own time. It is extremely important to understand the scope of work and develop good communication with your ASR support member. Any work provided by technician must have a 30 day warranty.</strong></p><p><strong><u>Locker Installation pay for this work order is a FLAT RATE per tower and per canopy successfully installed. Work order will be discounted per locker/canopy that is not installed.&nbsp;</u>Any work provided by technician must have a 30 day warranty.</strong></p><p><strong>INSTALL ATTEMPT- Determined by time spent at site - IF for whatever reason you arrive onsite and the install does NOT happen as planned, pricing for the work order will be changed from the install pricing to the service call pricing which is $85 for the first 2 hours and $40 an hour every hour after that, GPS and Notes from ASR support will be reviewed and approved accordingly. A new ticket will be dispatched accordingly. You will be paid for your time onsite and a new ticket will be routed back to you.</strong></p><p><strong>NUMBER OF LOCKERS INSTALLED-If the original number of lockers to be installed change from original count the work order will be paid accordingly. Sometimes locker counts change as they may not be delivered at time of original delivery day; this is beyond everyone's control and try to minimize as much as possible. A new ticket will be dispatched accordingly. You will be paid for your time onsite and a new ticket will be routed back to you.</strong></p><p><strong>REIMBURSMENT- Items purchased will be reimbursed upon ASR support approval. RECIEPTS REQUIRED. Technicians pulling from own stock will be reasonably compensated at market value. </strong></p><p><strong>APPROVING WORK ORDERS-</strong>Tech must include arrival and departure times, <strong>GPS and Notes from ASR support will be reviewed and approved accordingly. </strong>Document any site delays and requests that are made out of the scope of work in the closing notes AGAIN <strong>It is extremely important to understand the scope of work and develop good communication with your ASR support member. Any work provided by technician must have a 30 day warranty.</strong>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>COMMUNICATING WITH ASR SUPPORT </u></strong></p><p>If ASR support cannot reach you and technician goes dark it may be considered that technician has abandoned site. AGAIN <strong>It is extremely important to understand the scope of work and develop good communication with your ASR support member.</strong></p><p>========================</p><p>Project Number: 887</p><p>========================</p><p><strong><u>DIRECTIONS</u></strong></p><p><strong>It is extremely important to understand the scope of work and develop good communication with your ASR support member.</strong></p><p>Prior to going on site, please review the documentation and ASR sign off form.</p><ol><li><strong>Upon accepting the work order, update the notes with e-mail address that you can access from your smartphone.</strong></li><li><strong>Install equipment/accessories will be in box that is located in Main tower (unit with display) in locker door below display.</strong></li><li><strong>Verify equipment/accessories box with checklist that is taped to lid of box.</strong></li><li><strong>You will receive an ASR work order with a link to the status update page that you will be required to update during the process.</strong></li><li><strong>Upon arrival, use the link provided in the e-mailed work order to check in.</strong></li><li><strong>Introduce yourself to the site contact as the&nbsp;ASR Technician&nbsp;there to install the locker.</strong></li><li><strong>You will be meeting the \"white glove\" service that will be placing the locker system within 5 feet from the final installation location.</strong></li><li><strong>Take and send photos of any damages and note on BOL before signing and releasing delivery team from site.</strong></li><li><strong>Follow the instructions that are attached to your work order.&nbsp;</strong></li><li><strong>Take the required photos outlined in the instructions (Parcel Pending Install Required Pictures v2)</strong></li><li><strong>Text/email pictures to ASR Support team at parcelpendingsupport@asrepairtech.com before leaving site. ASR Support must approve all pictures before tech can be released from site.</strong></li><li><strong>Have the manager sign off on the sign off sheet.</strong></li><li><strong>Get full name of site personnel that key is left with and text/email to ASR support Team member.&nbsp;</strong></li></ol><p><strong>Upon completion, use the link provided in the e-mailed work order check out. </strong></p><p><strong>TOOL REQUIREMENT: Additional Tools are required for Outdoor Lockers</strong></p><ul><li>Standard Technicians tool kit</li><li>Technician needs to bring a laptop, USB Keyboard and Mouse</li><li>Tape Measure</li><li>Socket/Ratchet set (7/16” socket, 6mm deep socket and 1/4'’ deep socket needed)</li><li>Vise grips/locking pliers</li><li>Stud Finder</li><li>Level (24” preferred)</li><li>Rubber Mallet</li><li>6 ft Ladder</li><li>Laptop w/HyperTerminal or Putty</li><li>Punchdown Tool for 110 block or Keystone Jack</li><li>6ft Crossover patch cable</li><li>6ft Standard patch cable</li><li>Hammer drill&nbsp;</li><li>Qty 2 - ½” masonry drill bit minimum 6” in length (concrete anchors)&nbsp;</li><li>Chalk line reel (marking floor for anchor drilling)&nbsp;</li><li>Chalk/pencil/marker (marking concrete for anchors)&nbsp;</li><li>&nbsp;Hammer (insert anchor into concrete)&nbsp;</li><li>7mm socket/open-end wrench or right angle Phillips screwdriver (Skirts – front and back)&nbsp;</li><li>2 - Adjustable wrenches minimum opening of 1” (adjust feet)&nbsp;</li><li>Vacuum (clean out holes drilled in floor)&nbsp;</li><li>3/4” deep socket or open-end wrench (tighten anchors to floor bracket)&nbsp;</li><li>T10 torx security bit (inside sensors and back panel of doors)&nbsp;</li><li>5.5mm socket/open-end wrench (Outside sensors – inside boxes outside wall)&nbsp;</li><li>5mm hex key (wire cover top of towers)&nbsp;</li><li>Standard flathead and Phillips screwdrivers (open I/O boards)&nbsp;</li><li>Precision flathead screwdriver (set dip switches on I/O boards)</li><li>#12 or #14 – 1 ½ “ min. length Wood, Metal and concrete screws (to secure “L” Brackets to wall</li><li>#10 or #12 – ¾ “ length self-tapping screws</li><li>Silicone caulking (for end of self tapping screws)</li><li>Smart Phone with ability to access e-mail and open a mobile web page (for checking in and out)</li><li>Digital Camera (Minimum 5 Megapixels)</li><li>Furniture sliders/gliders (minimum 8 discs)</li><li>Dry cloth/towel and non-abrasive cleaner</li></ul><p><strong>Please bring PPE (Personal Protective Equipment).&nbsp;Not all sites require PPE but you will need to have it just in case.</strong></p><p><strong>PPE is hardhat, safety vest, safety goggles, long pants and steel toe boots.</strong></p><p><strong><u>Attachments</u></strong></p><p><strong>0887-SYSTEMMAINTENANCEDOC-REV2-2.pdf</strong></p><p><strong>Parcel Pending Install Required Pictures v2.pdf</strong></p><p><strong><u>DAMAGE REPORTING- </u></strong></p><p><strong>﻿FLOORS, WALLS &amp; PROPERTY </strong>Please note that these properties may have extremely expensive flooring and custom wall finish.&nbsp;We need to ensure that YOU as a technician are extremely mindful of the care and protection of the flooring, walls and property itself.</p><p><strong>FAILURE TO NOTIFY ASR ANY PRE-EXISITING DAMAGE TO FLOOR, WALLS or PROPERTY ITSELF COULD/WILL RESULT IN TECHNICIAN BEING HELD LIABLE.</strong></p><p><strong>Installing technician is required to Inspect locker installation location.</strong></p><ul><li>Take photos of area where lockers are to be installed to document any pre-existing flaws/damages to floors, walls or property itself.&nbsp;Send to parcelpendingsupport@asrepairtech.com (this will release you of any liability)</li><li>If there is notable damage to install site&nbsp;NOTIFY ASR ASAP!!</li></ul><p><strong>IF we are not notified prior to install, tech WILL/COULD be held liable.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>***OUR CUSTOMER IS PROVIDING A WHITE GLOVE DELIVERY SERVICE***</u></strong></p><p><strong>Delivery is WHITE GLOVE SERVICE and delivery team is required to have the following: </strong></p><ul><li>2 man delivery team</li><li>Truck with liftgate</li><li>Pallet jack (manual or motorized)</li><li>800 lbs capacity appliance hand truck</li><li>Furniture dolly</li><li>Floor protective material (Must be masonite or similar) CARDBOARD is NOT acceptable floor protection.</li></ul><p><strong><u>TECH MUST PROVIDE THE FOLLOWING IF APPLICABLE:</u></strong></p><p>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If the exterior packaging is damage (dents, tears, rips and holes) – take at least two pictures before unwrapping</p><p>2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If there is damage to the tower (small or large) – take at least two pictures</p><p>3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Locate the bar coded serial number (some may not have one) – take at least two pictures</p><p>4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Notate on Bill of Lading&nbsp;</p><p>5.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Model Number (D13, D12, etc)</p><p>6.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Serial Number (if present)</p><p>7.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;After BOL is signed by technician and driver – take at least two pictures</p><p>8.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Email to Parcel Pending Support for review parcelpendingsupport@asrepairtech.com </p><p>9.&nbsp;&nbsp;We will review and notify if the tower can be installed</p><p><strong>In the event that the technician fails to complete the notification process, technician COULD/WILL be held liable for the damage.</strong></p><p><strong><u>PROPERTY</u></strong></p><p><strong>If the delivery company&nbsp;damages property, technician must complete the following guidelines.</strong></p><p>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If the property is damaged by the delivery company (dents, tears, rips and holes to floor and/or wall) – take at least two pictures send to your ASR support that you are working with phone, leave message, text etc. (a call without leaving a message does not count as a call)</p><p>2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Notate on Bill of Lading&nbsp;-Do not let drivers leave without notation on BOL and Sign and take pictures of BOL.</p><p>3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Type of damage</p><p>4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Location of damage</p><p>5.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;After BOL is signed by technician and driver – take at least two pictures Do not let drivers leave without pictures</p><p>6.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Email to Parcel Pending Logistics for review&nbsp;</p><p>7.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;We will review and notify the property of the damage</p><p><strong>In the event that the technician fails to complete the notification process, technician COULD/WILL be held liable for the damage.</strong></p><p>Once lockers are unpacked, take photos of any damages and escalate immediately to iTEK Services along with noting on Bill of Lading (BOL) and take photo of BOL.&nbsp;<strong>(The BOL is verification that both delivery team has delivered and the technician has received the lockers with either NO noted damage or damages are documented on BOL).&nbsp;</strong></p><p>After Installation of Lockers, please take photos of floors and walls to ensure tech left site the same way and no damages were made by tech.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><ol><li><strong><u>**Do not access the system maintenance screen unless instructed.**</u></strong></li></ol><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Please leave Locker key in Box 1.&nbsp;If Property Manager insists on Tech leaving key with them, Tech is instructed to call:</p><p><br></p><p>If no power onsite, please call ASR support for instructions.</p><p><br></p><p>=======================</p>","markdown":"**INSTALLING AUTOMATED LOCKERS-High End Properties.**\n\n***Full Work Description*** This work order is to install an automated lockers in a luxury apartment complex or other commercial property. Location may still be under construction so please be sure to have the required safety gear (Hard Hat, long pants, Safety Vest and Steel toed boots) as you may not be permitted onsite. **To insure a successful install, entire work order MUST be read and understood. Technician is representing ASR and should be referred to as an ASR installer of Parcel Pending Lockers.**\n\n**ASR PROFESSIONALISM REQUIREMENTS**\n\n**SCHEDULING-FIRM START TIME:** Work order may NOT be rescheduled. Accepting tech is required to be on site the date listed, no exceptions.\n\n**Delays or issues arriving on time, CALL ASR SUPPORT TEAM: Contacts are listed under CONFIDENTIAL. IF YOU CALL ASR and do not leave a message it is not a phone call logged.** Technician should only discuss scheduling or payment issues with ASR support desk, if the customer reaches out directly to you, please refer them back to ASR.\n\n**TECHNICIAN ASSIGNED-**The name of the individual accepting this work must be the actual person who arrives on site and if we determine there was a substitution without prior notice, we will not pay for the work performed. Be sure to notify ASR by phone and message in work order prior to scheduled start time and before techs arrival onsite. ASR SUPPPORT TEAM is listed under CONFIDENTIAL\n\n**The accepting technician must meet ALL requirements below:**\n\n**Technician must have working knowledge/experience with either mounting a flat screen and/or install and secure cabinet/fixtures to different types of walls (drywall w/ wood studs, drywall w/aluminum, plaster, Stucco, wood/aluminum siding, clay brick, cinder block or concrete. Tech must have a laptop with HyperTerminal or Putty to be able to SSH into Linux base device through Ethernet connection on laptop.**\n\n**DRESS CODE-casual business attire with no logos.**\n\n**CUSTOMER SERVICE- These sites are very particular of work performed onsite, technician must present professionalism at all times.** Be friendly, communicate, and assure them they're in good hands. **Please note: Parcel Pending will be sending a post install survey regarding the overall install and tech performance. Please be mindful of this. ALL Conversations must be professional at all times. It is extremely important to understand the scope of work and develop good communication with your ASR support member.**\n\n**DRUG-FREE WORKPLACE- ASR** Services intends to help provide a safe and drug-free work environment. The technician needs to ensure they do not smell or reek of odors or other substances. **These sites are very particular of work performed onsite, technician must present professionalism at all times.**\n\n**PAYMENT-**Payment will be approved after the following:\n\n- Completed BOL paperwork with tech and delivery team signatures e-mailed to parcelpendingsupport@asrepairtech.com and uploaded to work order as backup\n- Completed Install form is uploaded to work order and scanned/e-mailed to parcelpendingsupport@asrepairtech.com (and confirmed received)\n- Photos are uploaded to work order, reviewed by ASR Support Team and finished work is approved by ASR Support as completed.\n\n**Pay is a fixed rate for successful installed lockers approved by ASR support. Approvals are not verbal, approved installs are approved in writing by ASR support, pictures are reviewed and logged, any verbal approvals may not be considered. If you are asked to return to provide ANY missing pictures after you left site you must do so on your own time. It is extremely important to understand the scope of work and develop good communication with your ASR support member. Any work provided by technician must have a 30 day warranty.**\n\n**Locker Installation pay for this work order is a FLAT RATE per tower and per canopy successfully installed. Work order will be discounted per locker/canopy that is not installed. Any work provided by technician must have a 30 day warranty.**\n\n**INSTALL ATTEMPT- Determined by time spent at site - IF for whatever reason you arrive onsite and the install does NOT happen as planned, pricing for the work order will be changed from the install pricing to the service call pricing which is $85 for the first 2 hours and $40 an hour every hour after that, GPS and Notes from ASR support will be reviewed and approved accordingly. A new ticket will be dispatched accordingly. You will be paid for your time onsite and a new ticket will be routed back to you.**\n\n**NUMBER OF LOCKERS INSTALLED-If the original number of lockers to be installed change from original count the work order will be paid accordingly. Sometimes locker counts change as they may not be delivered at time of original delivery day; this is beyond everyone's control and try to minimize as much as possible. A new ticket will be dispatched accordingly. You will be paid for your time onsite and a new ticket will be routed back to you.**\n\n**REIMBURSMENT- Items purchased will be reimbursed upon ASR support approval. RECIEPTS REQUIRED. Technicians pulling from own stock will be reasonably compensated at market value.**\n\n**APPROVING WORK ORDERS-**Tech must include arrival and departure times, **GPS and Notes from ASR support will be reviewed and approved accordingly.** Document any site delays and requests that are made out of the scope of work in the closing notes AGAIN **It is extremely important to understand the scope of work and develop good communication with your ASR support member. Any work provided by technician must have a 30 day warranty.**\n\n**COMMUNICATING WITH ASR SUPPORT**\n\nIf ASR support cannot reach you and technician goes dark it may be considered that technician has abandoned site. AGAIN **It is extremely important to understand the scope of work and develop good communication with your ASR support member.**\n\n========================\n\nProject Number: 887\n\n========================\n\n**DIRECTIONS**\n\n**It is extremely important to understand the scope of work and develop good communication with your ASR support member.**\n\nPrior to going on site, please review the documentation and ASR sign off form.\n\n1. **Upon accepting the work order, update the notes with e-mail address that you can access from your smartphone.**\n2. **Install equipment/accessories will be in box that is located in Main tower (unit with display) in locker door below display.**\n3. **Verify equipment/accessories box with checklist that is taped to lid of box.**\n4. **You will receive an ASR work order with a link to the status update page that you will be required to update during the process.**\n5. **Upon arrival, use the link provided in the e-mailed work order to check in.**\n6. **Introduce yourself to the site contact as the ASR Technician there to install the locker.**\n7. **You will be meeting the \"white glove\" service that will be placing the locker system within 5 feet from the final installation location.**\n8. **Take and send photos of any damages and note on BOL before signing and releasing delivery team from site.**\n9. **Follow the instructions that are attached to your work order.**\n10. **Take the required photos outlined in the instructions (Parcel Pending Install Required Pictures v2)**\n11. **Text/email pictures to ASR Support team at parcelpendingsupport@asrepairtech.com before leaving site. ASR Support must approve all pictures before tech can be released from site.**\n12. **Have the manager sign off on the sign off sheet.**\n13. **Get full name of site personnel that key is left with and text/email to ASR support Team member.**\n\n**Upon completion, use the link provided in the e-mailed work order check out.**\n\n**TOOL REQUIREMENT: Additional Tools are required for Outdoor Lockers**\n\n- Standard Technicians tool kit\n- Technician needs to bring a laptop, USB Keyboard and Mouse\n- Tape Measure\n- Socket/Ratchet set (7/16” socket, 6mm deep socket and 1/4'’ deep socket needed)\n- Vise grips/locking pliers\n- Stud Finder\n- Level (24” preferred)\n- Rubber Mallet\n- 6 ft Ladder\n- Laptop w/HyperTerminal or Putty\n- Punchdown Tool for 110 block or Keystone Jack\n- 6ft Crossover patch cable\n- 6ft Standard patch cable\n- Hammer drill\n- Qty 2 - ½” masonry drill bit minimum 6” in length (concrete anchors)\n- Chalk line reel (marking floor for anchor drilling)\n- Chalk/pencil/marker (marking concrete for anchors)\n- Hammer (insert anchor into concrete)\n- 7mm socket/open-end wrench or right angle Phillips screwdriver (Skirts – front and back)\n- 2 - Adjustable wrenches minimum opening of 1” (adjust feet)\n- Vacuum (clean out holes drilled in floor)\n- 3/4” deep socket or open-end wrench (tighten anchors to floor bracket)\n- T10 torx security bit (inside sensors and back panel of doors)\n- 5.5mm socket/open-end wrench (Outside sensors – inside boxes outside wall)\n- 5mm hex key (wire cover top of towers)\n- Standard flathead and Phillips screwdrivers (open I/O boards)\n- Precision flathead screwdriver (set dip switches on I/O boards)\n- \\#12 or #14 – 1 ½ “ min. length Wood, Metal and concrete screws (to secure “L” Brackets to wall\n- \\#10 or #12 – ¾ “ length self-tapping screws\n- Silicone caulking (for end of self tapping screws)\n- Smart Phone with ability to access e-mail and open a mobile web page (for checking in and out)\n- Digital Camera (Minimum 5 Megapixels)\n- Furniture sliders/gliders (minimum 8 discs)\n- Dry cloth/towel and non-abrasive cleaner\n\n**Please bring PPE (Personal Protective Equipment). Not all sites require PPE but you will need to have it just in case.**\n\n**PPE is hardhat, safety vest, safety goggles, long pants and steel toe boots.**\n\n**Attachments**\n\n**0887-SYSTEMMAINTENANCEDOC-REV2-2.pdf**\n\n**Parcel Pending Install Required Pictures v2.pdf**\n\n**DAMAGE REPORTING-**\n\n**﻿FLOORS, WALLS & PROPERTY** Please note that these properties may have extremely expensive flooring and custom wall finish. We need to ensure that YOU as a technician are extremely mindful of the care and protection of the flooring, walls and property itself.\n\n**FAILURE TO NOTIFY ASR ANY PRE-EXISITING DAMAGE TO FLOOR, WALLS or PROPERTY ITSELF COULD/WILL RESULT IN TECHNICIAN BEING HELD LIABLE.**\n\n**Installing technician is required to Inspect locker installation location.**\n\n- Take photos of area where lockers are to be installed to document any pre-existing flaws/damages to floors, walls or property itself. Send to parcelpendingsupport@asrepairtech.com (this will release you of any liability)\n- If there is notable damage to install site NOTIFY ASR ASAP!!\n\n**IF we are not notified prior to install, tech WILL/COULD be held liable.**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*OUR CUSTOMER IS PROVIDING A WHITE GLOVE DELIVERY SERVICE\\*\\*\\***\n\n**Delivery is WHITE GLOVE SERVICE and delivery team is required to have the following:**\n\n- 2 man delivery team\n- Truck with liftgate\n- Pallet jack (manual or motorized)\n- 800 lbs capacity appliance hand truck\n- Furniture dolly\n- Floor protective material (Must be masonite or similar) CARDBOARD is NOT acceptable floor protection.\n\n**TECH MUST PROVIDE THE FOLLOWING IF APPLICABLE:**\n\n1\\. If the exterior packaging is damage (dents, tears, rips and holes) – take at least two pictures before unwrapping\n\n2\\. If there is damage to the tower (small or large) – take at least two pictures\n\n3\\. Locate the bar coded serial number (some may not have one) – take at least two pictures\n\n4\\. Notate on Bill of Lading\n\n5\\. Model Number (D13, D12, etc)\n\n6\\. Serial Number (if present)\n\n7\\. After BOL is signed by technician and driver – take at least two pictures\n\n8\\. Email to Parcel Pending Support for review parcelpendingsupport@asrepairtech.com\n\n9\\. We will review and notify if the tower can be installed\n\n**In the event that the technician fails to complete the notification process, technician COULD/WILL be held liable for the damage.**\n\n**PROPERTY**\n\n**If the delivery company damages property, technician must complete the following guidelines.**\n\n1\\. If the property is damaged by the delivery company (dents, tears, rips and holes to floor and/or wall) – take at least two pictures send to your ASR support that you are working with phone, leave message, text etc. (a call without leaving a message does not count as a call)\n\n2\\. Notate on Bill of Lading -Do not let drivers leave without notation on BOL and Sign and take pictures of BOL.\n\n3\\. Type of damage\n\n4\\. Location of damage\n\n5\\. After BOL is signed by technician and driver – take at least two pictures Do not let drivers leave without pictures\n\n6\\. Email to Parcel Pending Logistics for review\n\n7\\. We will review and notify the property of the damage\n\n**In the event that the technician fails to complete the notification process, technician COULD/WILL be held liable for the damage.**\n\nOnce lockers are unpacked, take photos of any damages and escalate immediately to iTEK Services along with noting on Bill of Lading (BOL) and take photo of BOL. **(The BOL is verification that both delivery team has delivered and the technician has received the lockers with either NO noted damage or damages are documented on BOL).**\n\nAfter Installation of Lockers, please take photos of floors and walls to ensure tech left site the same way and no damages were made by tech.\n\n1. **\\*\\*Do not access the system maintenance screen unless instructed.\\*\\***\n\nPlease leave Locker key in Box 1. If Property Manager insists on Tech leaving key with them, Tech is instructed to call:\n\nIf no power onsite, please call ASR support for instructions.\n\n=======================","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-21T09:30","end":"2026-09-21T15:30"},"payRange":{"min":660,"max":660},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours"