{"job":{"id":19935855,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"American Direct Logistics","title":"2 MAN (YOU MUST PROVIDE HELPER AND CARGO VAN, BOX TRUCK OR ENCLOSED TRAILER) OLD DISPLAY REMOVAL / DISPOSAL - CRATE DIMS:  130 LBS. 25.375”W X 77H” X 14.00”D","description":{"html":"<p>Maui Jim Display Disposal - Pick Up and Disposal Only</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>REQUIREMENTS FOR COMPLETING THIS DELIVERY:</p><p>1.\tCargo Van, Enclosed Trailer or Box Truck – no rented vehicles or other types of vehicles are allowed for this account</p><p>2.\tHelper – all deliveries require 2 People regardless of size or weight of product</p><p>4.\tDolly or Hand Truck to wheel unit into place on site</p><p>5.\tCompletion of Attached Policy Agreement – Complete and Submit to ADL Prior to Scheduling Appointment</p><p>6.\tCall ADL @ 800-988-3554 / 516-974-5094 to confirm receipt of agreement and to schedule appointment for delivery – you must speak to a representative in order to schedule the appointment.</p><p>8.\tCall the Location Contact on your work order when you are at least 30 minutes away from arriving to give ETA.&nbsp;Leave a message if no answer.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>**PLEASE LET ADL KNOW WHICH OF THE BELOW OPTIONS WORKS FOR YOU**</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>ASAP - PLEASE ADVISE WHICH DATE AND 2 HOUR WINDOW WORKS BEST FOR YOU - WE WILL THEN REACH OUT TO THE SITE REP TO SEE IF THE CAN ACCEPT OFFERED APPT&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Item: Maui Jim Old Spinner Display</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Box Dims / Weight: WEIGHT: 130 LBS. UNIT DIMENSIONS: 25.375”W X 77H” X 14.00”D</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>You need a helper.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Please pick up display, wheel out of store using dolly / helper and load into your vehicle.&nbsp;Please take photo of display that is being removed either outside or in vehicle, as proof of removal.&nbsp;Please haul away for disposal.&nbsp;Display cannot be sold, donated or reused by site.</p><p><br></p><p>1. YOU MUST HAUL AWAY THE OLD DISPLAY AND DISPOSE OF IT AT YOUR HOME OR THE LOCAL DUMP*</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>If you have any issues or the display is damaged, please call ADL Tech Support WHILE ON SITE:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Office: 800-988-3554 / 516-974-5094 (Cell after hours)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>MAKE SURE TO GET SITE SURVEY COMPLETION FORM SIGNED BY CUSTOMER ON SITE</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>PLEASE ALSO TAKE A PICTURE OF OLD DISPLAY THAT IS REMOVED FOR DISPOSAL</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>SEND ADL THE PHOTOS OF UNIT AND COMPLETION FORM FOR PAYMENT AFTER THE JOB IS COMPLETE.</p>","markdown":"Maui Jim Display Disposal - Pick Up and Disposal Only\n\nREQUIREMENTS FOR COMPLETING THIS DELIVERY:\n\n1\\. Cargo Van, Enclosed Trailer or Box Truck – no rented vehicles or other types of vehicles are allowed for this account\n\n2\\. Helper – all deliveries require 2 People regardless of size or weight of product\n\n4\\. Dolly or Hand Truck to wheel unit into place on site\n\n5\\. Completion of Attached Policy Agreement – Complete and Submit to ADL Prior to Scheduling Appointment\n\n6\\. Call ADL @ 800-988-3554 / 516-974-5094 to confirm receipt of agreement and to schedule appointment for delivery – you must speak to a representative in order to schedule the appointment.\n\n8\\. Call the Location Contact on your work order when you are at least 30 minutes away from arriving to give ETA. Leave a message if no answer.\n\n\\*\\*PLEASE LET ADL KNOW WHICH OF THE BELOW OPTIONS WORKS FOR YOU\\*\\*\n\nASAP - PLEASE ADVISE WHICH DATE AND 2 HOUR WINDOW WORKS BEST FOR YOU - WE WILL THEN REACH OUT TO THE SITE REP TO SEE IF THE CAN ACCEPT OFFERED APPT\n\nItem: Maui Jim Old Spinner Display\n\nBox Dims / Weight: WEIGHT: 130 LBS. UNIT DIMENSIONS: 25.375”W X 77H” X 14.00”D\n\nYou need a helper.\n\nPlease pick up display, wheel out of store using dolly / helper and load into your vehicle. Please take photo of display that is being removed either outside or in vehicle, as proof of removal. Please haul away for disposal. Display cannot be sold, donated or reused by site.\n\n1\\. YOU MUST HAUL AWAY THE OLD DISPLAY AND DISPOSE OF IT AT YOUR HOME OR THE LOCAL DUMP\\*\n\nIf you have any issues or the display is damaged, please call ADL Tech Support WHILE ON SITE:\n\nOffice: 800-988-3554 / 516-974-5094 (Cell after hours)\n\nMAKE SURE TO GET SITE SURVEY COMPLETION FORM SIGNED BY CUSTOMER ON SITE\n\nPLEASE ALSO TAKE A PICTURE OF OLD DISPLAY THAT IS REMOVED FOR DISPOSAL\n\nSEND ADL THE PHOTOS OF UNIT AND COMPLETION FORM FOR PAYMENT AFTER THE JOB IS COMPLETE.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-14T09:00","end":"2026-09-14T10:00","latestStart":"2026-09-14T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":162},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 9/14/2026, 9:00:00 AM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-14T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-15T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T16:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-15T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-16T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-16T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-17T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T17:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-17T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"FN"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Busy"},{"start":"2026-09-15T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T18:00:00.000Z","summary":"gap"},{"start":"2026-09-15T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-15T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Rest"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ​Concord Police Department - NC ( Phase 2 ) (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-17T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Remote Hands - Connect AT&T broadband circuit"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789594924186}
{"job":{"id":19970740,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Argus IT Services","title":"Smart H&F for Troubleshooting Network Devices - AP Down/300ft Cable Run","description":{"html":"<strong>HCL Onsite Network Support – Technician Field Guide</strong><strong>Purpose of Visit</strong><p>This ticket is to <strong>troubleshoot a network or store device</strong> on behalf of <strong>HCL</strong> in response to a reported <strong>Incident</strong>.</p><p><br></p><strong>Teams is required and must remain active for the full duration of the visit. If your time is different than what you were actively working with the NOC team on the bridge, your WO will be marked incomplete.</strong><br><strong><u>Travel expenses must be in your counter and accepted prior to you arriving at the store. Any travel tacked on afterwards, will be denied. All materials will be reimbursed on the WO.</u></strong><br><strong>1. Arrival &amp; Store Check-In</strong><ul><li>Present <strong>valid Photo ID</strong> (Driver’s License).</li><li>Identify yourself as an <strong>HCL Network Technician</strong>, dispatched <strong>on behalf of the NOC Team</strong> to troubleshoot a network device reported offline.</li><li>If denied access:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Notify the NOC team immediately on the bridge</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Contact the <strong>WO Manager</strong> for escalation</li></ul><strong>2. Onsite Procedures</strong><ul><li><strong>Join the Teams bridge</strong> using the link, ID, and passcode from the Confidential section</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>If it is saying the link doesn't exist/is valid, you need to uninstall/reinstall Teams. The link is valid and working.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Send an email to ADUSA_FSCC@hcltech.com with your Incident if you have issues with joining the bridge.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If that doesn't work, please try using browser and incognito mode and type in the meeting ID and password.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Stay connected for the entire visit</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Please tell them when you get there and when you leave, as well as what the next action is needed.</li><li>In the meeting chat, enter:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>INC#</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>Arrival time</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Departure time</strong></li><li><strong><u>Do not leave the site unless released by the NOC team</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>The NOC team on the bridge will you send you to a second bridge. If you have been on that second bridge for a while with no one from the NOC team joining, rejoin the primary bridge and let them know.</u></strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>They will create a secondary room for your specific ticket/issue. You will work with the team for your specific issue. Please join back the main bridge once you are finished to check out.</u></strong></p><p><strong>﻿</strong></p><strong>3. Post-Service Actions</strong><ul><li>Document all work performed in the <strong>FieldNation closing notes</strong></li><li>Notify <strong>Argus</strong> of the resolution prior to departure</li><li>Return any unused parts using the provided <strong>return label</strong> (if applicable)</li></ul><strong>4. Required Tools &amp; Equipment</strong><ul><li>Smartphone with hotspot</li><li>Laptop with admin access, Teams, Putty, and email</li><li>Console cables (USB to RJ45)</li><li>Cable Tester / Toner</li><li>Wi-Fi analyzer app</li><li>IT hardware repair kit</li><li>Patch cables, crimpers, cable testers</li><li>Spare RJ-45 connectors (<strong>MUST BE CAT6)</strong></li><li>Spare Ethernet cables (various lengths)</li><li>General hand tools and accessories</li></ul><p>\"Store manager Jeremy requested for visit on working hours, as soon as possible</p><p><br></p><p>Issue - AP01, AP03, AP05 down.</p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;What do they need from a field tech and any parts/tools that may be needed:</p><p><br></p><p>• console cable (proprietary, micro-B USB physical jack) which should be</p><p>compatible with ARUBA 535 Access Point.</p><p><br></p><p>The steps expected from the Technician to preform while onsite:</p><p><br></p><p>• Once Tech is onsite, he should connect with HCL wireless team through the</p><p>troubleshoot bridge.</p><p>• Need to provide console of AP, if required, to Wireless Team.</p><p>• Need to change the interface for AP if requested.</p><p>•Need to test the cable run for the AP.</p><p>• Need to check by connecting the AP with the short cable if needed.</p><p>• Need to factory reset the AP if requested.\"</p><p><strong><u>If you need a schedule change/want to request the work order - REQUEST A SCHEDULE CHANGE. We can troubleshoot as long as the store is open. Whatever time you get there, we will adjust on the WO so it doesn't impact your rating.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>The phone number on the Work Order is for on-site escalations and emergencies. Calling the number repeatedly everyday for future work consideration, will result in not using you as a technician for future engagements.</u></strong></p>","markdown":"**HCL Onsite Network Support – Technician Field Guide****Purpose of Visit**This ticket is to **troubleshoot a network or store device** on behalf of **HCL** in response to a reported **Incident**.\n\n**Teams is required and must remain active for the full duration of the visit. If your time is different than what you were actively working with the NOC team on the bridge, your WO will be marked incomplete.**  \n**Travel expenses must be in your counter and accepted prior to you arriving at the store. Any travel tacked on afterwards, will be denied. All materials will be reimbursed on the WO.**  \n**1. Arrival & Store Check-In**- Present **valid Photo ID** (Driver’s License).\n- Identify yourself as an **HCL Network Technician**, dispatched **on behalf of the NOC Team** to troubleshoot a network device reported offline.\n- If denied access:\n- **Notify the NOC team immediately on the bridge**\n- Contact the **WO Manager** for escalation\n\n**2. Onsite Procedures**- **Join the Teams bridge** using the link, ID, and passcode from the Confidential section\n- **If it is saying the link doesn't exist/is valid, you need to uninstall/reinstall Teams. The link is valid and working.**\n- **Send an email to ADUSA\\_FSCC@hcltech.com with your Incident if you have issues with joining the bridge.**\n- If that doesn't work, please try using browser and incognito mode and type in the meeting ID and password.\n- Stay connected for the entire visit\n- Please tell them when you get there and when you leave, as well as what the next action is needed.\n- In the meeting chat, enter:\n- **INC#**\n- **Arrival time**\n- **Departure time**\n- **Do not leave the site unless released by the NOC team**\n- **The NOC team on the bridge will you send you to a second bridge. If you have been on that second bridge for a while with no one from the NOC team joining, rejoin the primary bridge and let them know.**\n\n**They will create a secondary room for your specific ticket/issue. You will work with the team for your specific issue. Please join back the main bridge once you are finished to check out.**\n\n**﻿**\n\n**3. Post-Service Actions**- Document all work performed in the **FieldNation closing notes**\n- Notify **Argus** of the resolution prior to departure\n- Return any unused parts using the provided **return label** (if applicable)\n\n**4. Required Tools & Equipment**- Smartphone with hotspot\n- Laptop with admin access, Teams, Putty, and email\n- Console cables (USB to RJ45)\n- Cable Tester / Toner\n- Wi-Fi analyzer app\n- IT hardware repair kit\n- Patch cables, crimpers, cable testers\n- Spare RJ-45 connectors (**MUST BE CAT6)**\n- Spare Ethernet cables (various lengths)\n- General hand tools and accessories\n\n\"Store manager Jeremy requested for visit on working hours, as soon as possible\n\nIssue - AP01, AP03, AP05 down.\n\n What do they need from a field tech and any parts/tools that may be needed:\n\n• console cable (proprietary, micro-B USB physical jack) which should be\n\ncompatible with ARUBA 535 Access Point.\n\nThe steps expected from the Technician to preform while onsite:\n\n• Once Tech is onsite, he should connect with HCL wireless team through the\n\ntroubleshoot bridge.\n\n• Need to provide console of AP, if required, to Wireless Team.\n\n• Need to change the interface for AP if requested.\n\n•Need to test the cable run for the AP.\n\n• Need to check by connecting the AP with the short cable if needed.\n\n• Need to factory reset the AP if requested.\"\n\n**If you need a schedule change/want to request the work order - REQUEST A SCHEDULE CHANGE. We can troubleshoot as long as the store is open. Whatever time you get there, we will adjust on the WO so it doesn't impact your rating.**\n\n**The phone number on the Work Order is for on-site escalations and emergencies. Calling the number repeatedly everyday for future work consideration, will result in not using you as a technician for future engagements.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-18T07:00","end":"2026-09-18T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":220},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":16},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $220 (countered: $240) is below minimum threshold $400"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-21T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Busy"},{"start":"2026-09-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ​Concord Police Department - NC ( Phase 2 ) (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-17T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Remote Hands - Connect AT&T broadband circuit"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789596950620}
{"job":{"id":19970832,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"AVT Technology Solutions LLC","title":"No overhead music in frontline, Troubleshoot, call NTS once on site.","description":{"html":"<p>1. <strong>Scope of Work</strong> <strong>includes returning parts as detailed in the Part Module and in #2 Part Information below.</strong></p>\n<p><em>Scope of Work:</em></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><em>Skills Required:</em></p>\n<p><em>-You will need experience with 70v audio systems and analog telecom experience. Please do not accept this work order unless you have the needed experience and tools.</em></p>\n<p><em>Tools Required:</em></p>\n<p><em>-Make sure to have a wired set of headphones, a toner kit, a self-powered butt set with you. Check in with the manager using the code below.</em></p>\n<p><em>Scope of work: Speaker goes in and out (just the one speaker...on the Queue line)</em></p>\n<p><em>Ask for access to the rack and to the electrical room. Look for a 4x5 box with a label that says \"music\" on it. Make sure it has power, and there is a headphone cable plugged into the side of it. Trace that cable and see where it goes. Follow that connection all the way till you reach the Amp (normally Bose/TOA/Valcom) and get pictures of both the front and back. Speak with manager and get the location of any volume control switches located on the store floor. Once we have identified all volume control points, we need to adjust volume, so nothing is above 70%. Get photos of the plywood in the electrical room/rack room, and photos of the rack. If assistance is needed, once you have photos of everything, contact <del>*** ** ************ ****** ** ******** ** ************ ** *** ***** ***** *******</del></em></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><em>Site Security Code #<del>******</del></em></p>\n<p><em>Customer Incident#<del>**********</del></em></p>\n<p><em>Clients present issue: Speaker goes in and out (just the one speaker...on the queue line)</em></p>\n<p><em>Estimated time: 2-4 Hours</em></p>\n<p><em>Part shipped to the site?:(y/n)-No</em></p>\n<p><em>Please review the repair plans in the link below</em></p>\n<p><em>https://uploads.tdsynnex.com/f/0cc67a88e7289aa4</em></p>\n<p><em>Other Instructions:</em></p>\n<p><em><del>** ********** ** ******* ****** ***** ************ ****** * *</del></em></p>\n<p><em>Required Tool List:</em></p>\n<p><em>https://sigtech.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/i0000000JqJY/a/5A000000YQTH/9gnaImll4VecAy1sI2UPOKqG7leVPWHltq_ila4IVaA</em></p>\n<p><strong>Technician Support Process (Important)</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Before contacting Shyft/NTS Support, you MUST contact the</strong> <strong><del>*** **** **** ******</del></strong></p>\n<p><strong>If you encounter an issue while onsite:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Contact the <strong><del>*** **** ****</del></strong> and work through the issue with them.</li>\n<li>If the issue is resolved, continue and complete the work order.</li>\n<li>If the issue is <strong>not resolved after working with the</strong> <strong><del>*** **** **** ************ ****** * ****** * ****** *</del></strong>, then contact <strong>Shyft/NTS Support</strong> for further assistance.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Technicians who contact Shyft/NTS Support before working with the</strong> <strong><del>*** **** ****</del></strong><strong>will be instructed to contact the</strong> <strong><del>*** **** ****</del></strong><strong>first before additional support is provided.</strong></p>\n<p><strong><em>Completion Requirements:</em></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Closing Notes</strong> – <strong>Should entered prior to leaving the site and should pertain to the SOW of this workorder only.</strong> If working multiple tickets, please keep closing remarks specific to the scope of this workorder. This should be a detailed and concise statement about the work performed.<strong>Please do not include personal opinions, jargon, statements about pay or travel or any other feedback not directly related to the specifics of the repair; These other issues should be addressed directly with the Shyft Services Work Order Manager.&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p><em>2.</em> <strong>Part Information</strong>:&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Unused Parts</strong>: - Must be returned. - Use the return label included in the box.- Photos required: Serial Number + Asset Tag of installed and removed parts.</p>\n<p><strong>Used Parts</strong>: - If marked Returnable = Yes → Return required. - Photos required: Serial Number + Asset Tag of installed and removed parts.</p>\n<p><strong>Missing Return Label</strong>: - Email field_nation_parts@shyftservices.com. - Include Field Nation Work Order Number.&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>General Rules</strong>: - Return all returnable unused parts and all returnable used parts to FedEx with 24 hours of Check Out. - Parts belong to AVT/Shyft Services. - Do not leave parts onsite. Parts left onsite are subject to an Admin Process fee.</p>","markdown":"1\\. **Scope of Work** **includes returning parts as detailed in the Part Module and in #2 Part Information below.**\n\n*Scope of Work:*\n\n*Skills Required:*\n\n*-You will need experience with 70v audio systems and analog telecom experience. Please do not accept this work order unless you have the needed experience and tools.*\n\n*Tools Required:*\n\n*-Make sure to have a wired set of headphones, a toner kit, a self-powered butt set with you. Check in with the manager using the code below.*\n\n*Scope of work: Speaker goes in and out (just the one speaker...on the Queue line)*\n\n*Ask for access to the rack and to the electrical room. Look for a 4x5 box with a label that says \"music\" on it. Make sure it has power, and there is a headphone cable plugged into the side of it. Trace that cable and see where it goes. Follow that connection all the way till you reach the Amp (normally Bose/TOA/Valcom) and get pictures of both the front and back. Speak with manager and get the location of any volume control switches located on the store floor. Once we have identified all volume control points, we need to adjust volume, so nothing is above 70%. Get photos of the plywood in the electrical room/rack room, and photos of the rack. If assistance is needed, once you have photos of everything, contact \\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\**\n\n*Site Security Code #\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\**\n\n*Customer Incident#\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\**\n\n*Clients present issue: Speaker goes in and out (just the one speaker...on the queue line)*\n\n*Estimated time: 2-4 Hours*\n\n*Part shipped to the site?:(y/n)-No*\n\n*Please review the repair plans in the link below*\n\n*<https://uploads.tdsynnex.com/f/0cc67a88e7289aa4>*\n\n*Other Instructions:*\n\n*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\**\n\n*Required Tool List:*\n\n*https://sigtech.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/i0000000JqJY/a/5A000000YQTH/9gnaImll4VecAy1sI2UPOKqG7leVPWHltq_ila4IVaA*\n\n**Technician Support Process (Important)**\n\n**Before contacting Shyft/NTS Support, you MUST contact the** **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n\n**If you encounter an issue while onsite:**\n\n1. Contact the **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*** and work through the issue with them.\n2. If the issue is resolved, continue and complete the work order.\n3. If the issue is **not resolved after working with the** **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\***, then contact **Shyft/NTS Support** for further assistance.\n\n**Technicians who contact Shyft/NTS Support before working with the** **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*****will be instructed to contact the** **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*****first before additional support is provided.**\n\n***Completion Requirements:***\n\n**Closing Notes** – **Should entered prior to leaving the site and should pertain to the SOW of this workorder only.** If working multiple tickets, please keep closing remarks specific to the scope of this workorder. This should be a detailed and concise statement about the work performed.**Please do not include personal opinions, jargon, statements about pay or travel or any other feedback not directly related to the specifics of the repair; These other issues should be addressed directly with the Shyft Services Work Order Manager.**\n\n*2.* **Part Information**:\n\n**Unused Parts**: - Must be returned. - Use the return label included in the box.- Photos required: Serial Number + Asset Tag of installed and removed parts.\n\n**Used Parts**: - If marked Returnable = Yes → Return required. - Photos required: Serial Number + Asset Tag of installed and removed parts.\n\n**Missing Return Label**: - Email field\\_nation\\_parts@shyftservices.com. - Include Field Nation Work Order Number.\n\n**General Rules**: - Return all returnable unused parts and all returnable used parts to FedEx with 24 hours of Check Out. - Parts belong to AVT/Shyft Services. - Do not leave parts onsite. Parts left onsite are subject to an Admin Process fee.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-16T07:00","end":"2026-09-17T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":80,"max":80},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1.75,"distance":6},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 9/16/2026, 7:00:00 AM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-16T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-17T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-17T17:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-17T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBl