{"job":{"id":19971305,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Fayette Technologies LLC","title":"Cat5e Cable Installation - ASSIST TECH NEEDED","description":{"html":"<p><strong>WORK ORDER SCOPE &amp; TECHNICIAN REQUIREMENTS</strong></p>\n<p><strong>***PROVIDER MUST HAVE THE FOLLOWING QUALIFICATIONS***</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>\"Big-Box\" retail cabling and infrastructure experience</li>\n<li>Proper hand tools for pulling, securing and terminating low voltage cabling and potentially installing other items such as network racks, access points, etc.</li>\n<li>Professional dress (Khaki's or CLEAN jeans, collared shirt / polo, NO LOGOS, NO RIPPED OR TORN CLOTHING)</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong><u>Scope of Work</u></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>This project requires LABOR ONLY. All materials will be shipped to the site.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Pull and terminate approximately 26 Cat5e cables. All cables (or a vast majority of them) can be pulled simultaneously as they are all landing in the same general area.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>The majority of the pull is through open ceiling / trusses. A small portion will be pulled through a clean drop ceiling. Cabling must be neatly installed, not crossing or wrapping around conduit, water pipe, other cables, etc.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Please note that this is TEMPORARY cabling. It will be removed within 10 days.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Data closet terminations will be RJ45's.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Landing locations will be terminated on keystone jacks.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Work must be done between 9:00 PM and 5:00 AM. No exceptions.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>WE WILL HAVE A LEAD TECH ON SITE to assist. This project is expected to only require 1 night of work, but work can be extended to a 2nd night if needed.</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Technician is responsible for reviewing the complete scope of work before accepting the assignment and arriving prepared to complete all assigned tasks.</p>\n<p><strong><u>General Requirements</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Arrive on-site and be ready to work at the scheduled start time.</li>\n<li>Check in and check out according to the work order instructions.</li>\n<li>Maintain a professional appearance and conduct while on-site.</li>\n<li>Coordinate with the on-site contact and/or remote support personnel as required.</li>\n<li>Follow all site-specific safety, security, and access requirements.</li>\n<li>Maintain a clean and organized work area throughout the assignment.</li>\n<li>Do not perform work outside the authorized scope without approval.</li>\n<li>Immediately report any condition that may prevent or delay successful completion of the work.</li>\n<li>Clearly document any incomplete work, access issues, damaged equipment, site conditions, or other exceptions before leaving.</li>\n<li>Verify completed work and functionality whenever applicable before departure.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Technician Tools &amp; Equipment</u></strong></p>\n<p>Technicians are expected to arrive with the tools and equipment necessary to complete the assigned scope. Unless otherwise stated in the work order, technicians should have access to:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Standard hand tools</li>\n<li>Drill/impact driver and appropriate bits</li>\n<li>Screwdrivers and nut drivers</li>\n<li>Flashlight/work light</li>\n<li>Tape measure</li>\n<li>Label maker and labeling supplies</li>\n<li>Laptop with Ethernet connectivity and basic network troubleshooting capabilities</li>\n<li>Ethernet patch cables and appropriate adapters</li>\n<li>RJ45 crimping and termination tools</li>\n<li>Punch-down tool</li>\n<li>Cable stripping and cutting tools</li>\n<li>Network/cable tester</li>\n<li>Tone generator and probe</li>\n<li>Basic cable fishing and pulling tools</li>\n<li>Appropriate PPE, including safety glasses and work gloves</li>\n<li>Appropriate ladder when required by the scope</li>\n<li>Fiber tools required (depending on work order):</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Fiber optic VFL (minimum) and loss meter / tester</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Cleaver and other associated termination tools</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">ST, SC, LC terminations</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Additional specialized tools or equipment may be identified within the project-specific scope.</p>\n<p><strong><u>Cabling &amp; Installation Standards</u></strong></p>\n<p>When performing cabling or installation work:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>All work must be completed in a clean and professional manner.</li>\n<li>Cabling must be properly routed, dressed, and supported.</li>\n<li>Cables may not be laid across ceiling tiles or improperly supported by conduit, sprinkler piping, electrical systems, or other building infrastructure.</li>\n<li>Maintain appropriate separation from electrical wiring and other potential sources of interference.</li>\n<li>All cables and terminations must be clearly and consistently labeled.</li>\n<li>Copper cabling must be properly terminated and tested.</li>\n<li>Test results must be provided when requested.</li>\n<li>Penetrations, pathways, firestopping, and cable-support methods must comply with applicable site requirements and accepted installation practices.</li>\n<li>Existing cabling, equipment, or customer infrastructure must not be disconnected, relocated, or modified unless specifically authorized.</li>\n<li>Any damage or existing conditions discovered during the work must be documented and reported.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Scissor Lift / Aerial Lift Requirements</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Prior scissor lift operation experience is required when lift operation is included in the scope of work. Current scissor lift/aerial work platform certification is strongly preferred.</strong></p>\n<p>Technicians expected to operate a scissor lift or other aerial work platform must:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Have prior experience safely operating the applicable equipment.</li>\n<li>Be comfortable working at the heights required for the assignment.</li>\n<li>Follow all manufacturer and site-specific operating and safety requirements.</li>\n<li>Perform required pre-use inspections and immediately report unsafe equipment or conditions.</li>\n<li>Use required PPE and fall-protection equipment where applicable.</li>\n<li>Never operate equipment they are not qualified, experienced, or comfortable operating.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Site Cleanliness &amp; Cleanup</u></strong></p>\n<p>Technicians are responsible for maintaining a clean and professional work area throughout the assignment.</p>\n<p>Before leaving the site:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Remove all cable scraps, wire clippings, zip-tie ends, packaging, connectors, ceiling-tile debris, and other waste generated by the work.</li>\n<li>Remove tools, boxes, unused materials, and supplies from the work area unless specifically instructed otherwise.</li>\n<li>Return moved furniture, equipment, ceiling tiles, and other items to their proper locations.</li>\n<li>Sweep, vacuum, or otherwise clean the immediate work area when necessary.</li>\n<li>Do not leave debris above ceilings, in telecommunications rooms, data closets, equipment cabinets, or other work areas.</li>\n<li>Properly dispose of job-related waste in an approved location.</li>\n<li>Leave all work areas <strong>as clean as or cleaner than they were upon arrival</strong>.</li>\n<li>Provide photographs of the completed and cleaned work area when closeout photographs are required.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Cleanup is part of the scope of work. The assignment is not considered complete until all affected work areas have been cleaned and restored.</strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>Documentation &amp; Closeout</u></strong></p>\n<p>Before leaving the site, technicians must:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Confirm that the assigned scope has been completed.</li>\n<li>Verify operation and functionality of affected equipment when applicable.</li>\n<li>Provide clear photographs of completed work.</li>\n<li>Provide photographs of labels, terminations, equipment locations, cable pathways, racks/cabinets, and other requested items.</li>\n<li>Document any deviations from the original scope.</li>\n<li>Record applicable cable IDs, port numbers, serial numbers, equipment information, test results, or other requested information.</li>\n<li>Obtain required sign-off or completion acknowledgment when applicable.</li>\n<li>Ensure all required Field Nation deliverables, documentation, photographs, and closing notes have been submitted.</li>\n<li>Contact the designated project representative <strong>before leaving the site</strong> if any portion of the scope cannot be completed or if unresolved issues remain.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Important</u></strong></p>\n<p>Acceptance of this work order indicates that the technician has reviewed the scope and understands the requirements of the assignment.</p>\n<p>Technicians are expected to arrive with the appropriate experience, tools, equipment, and PPE necessary to perform the work unless an exception has been communicated and approved in advance.</p>\n<p><strong>Do not leave the site with incomplete work, unresolved issues, or outstanding questions without first contacting the designated project representative.</strong></p>","markdown":"**WORK ORDER SCOPE & TECHNICIAN REQUIREMENTS**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*PROVIDER MUST HAVE THE FOLLOWING QUALIFICATIONS\\*\\*\\***\n\n1. \"Big-Box\" retail cabling and infrastructure experience\n2. Proper hand tools for pulling, securing and terminating low voltage cabling and potentially installing other items such as network racks, access points, etc.\n3. Professional dress (Khaki's or CLEAN jeans, collared shirt / polo, NO LOGOS, NO RIPPED OR TORN CLOTHING)\n\n**Scope of Work**\n\n1. **This project requires LABOR ONLY. All materials will be shipped to the site.**\n2. **Pull and terminate approximately 26 Cat5e cables. All cables (or a vast majority of them) can be pulled simultaneously as they are all landing in the same general area.**\n3. **The majority of the pull is through open ceiling / trusses. A small portion will be pulled through a clean drop ceiling. Cabling must be neatly installed, not crossing or wrapping around conduit, water pipe, other cables, etc.**\n4. **Please note that this is TEMPORARY cabling. It will be removed within 10 days.**\n5. **Data closet terminations will be RJ45's.**\n6. **Landing locations will be terminated on keystone jacks.**\n7. **Work must be done between 9:00 PM and 5:00 AM. No exceptions.**\n8. **WE WILL HAVE A LEAD TECH ON SITE to assist. This project is expected to only require 1 night of work, but work can be extended to a 2nd night if needed.**\n\nTechnician is responsible for reviewing the complete scope of work before accepting the assignment and arriving prepared to complete all assigned tasks.\n\n**General Requirements**\n\n- Arrive on-site and be ready to work at the scheduled start time.\n- Check in and check out according to the work order instructions.\n- Maintain a professional appearance and conduct while on-site.\n- Coordinate with the on-site contact and/or remote support personnel as required.\n- Follow all site-specific safety, security, and access requirements.\n- Maintain a clean and organized work area throughout the assignment.\n- Do not perform work outside the authorized scope without approval.\n- Immediately report any condition that may prevent or delay successful completion of the work.\n- Clearly document any incomplete work, access issues, damaged equipment, site conditions, or other exceptions before leaving.\n- Verify completed work and functionality whenever applicable before departure.\n\n**Technician Tools & Equipment**\n\nTechnicians are expected to arrive with the tools and equipment necessary to complete the assigned scope. Unless otherwise stated in the work order, technicians should have access to:\n\n- Standard hand tools\n- Drill/impact driver and appropriate bits\n- Screwdrivers and nut drivers\n- Flashlight/work light\n- Tape measure\n- Label maker and labeling supplies\n- Laptop with Ethernet connectivity and basic network troubleshooting capabilities\n- Ethernet patch cables and appropriate adapters\n- RJ45 crimping and termination tools\n- Punch-down tool\n- Cable stripping and cutting tools\n- Network/cable tester\n- Tone generator and probe\n- Basic cable fishing and pulling tools\n- Appropriate PPE, including safety glasses and work gloves\n- Appropriate ladder when required by the scope\n- Fiber tools required (depending on work order):\n- Fiber optic VFL (minimum) and loss meter / tester\n- Cleaver and other associated termination tools\n- ST, SC, LC terminations\n\nAdditional specialized tools or equipment may be identified within the project-specific scope.\n\n**Cabling & Installation Standards**\n\nWhen performing cabling or installation work:\n\n- All work must be completed in a clean and professional manner.\n- Cabling must be properly routed, dressed, and supported.\n- Cables may not be laid across ceiling tiles or improperly supported by conduit, sprinkler piping, electrical systems, or other building infrastructure.\n- Maintain appropriate separation from electrical wiring and other potential sources of interference.\n- All cables and terminations must be clearly and consistently labeled.\n- Copper cabling must be properly terminated and tested.\n- Test results must be provided when requested.\n- Penetrations, pathways, firestopping, and cable-support methods must comply with applicable site requirements and accepted installation practices.\n- Existing cabling, equipment, or customer infrastructure must not be disconnected, relocated, or modified unless specifically authorized.\n- Any damage or existing conditions discovered during the work must be documented and reported.\n\n**Scissor Lift / Aerial Lift Requirements**\n\n**Prior scissor lift operation experience is required when lift operation is included in the scope of work. Current scissor lift/aerial work platform certification is strongly preferred.**\n\nTechnicians expected to operate a scissor lift or other aerial work platform must:\n\n- Have prior experience safely operating the applicable equipment.\n- Be comfortable working at the heights required for the assignment.\n- Follow all manufacturer and site-specific operating and safety requirements.\n- Perform required pre-use inspections and immediately report unsafe equipment or conditions.\n- Use required PPE and fall-protection equipment where applicable.\n- Never operate equipment they are not qualified, experienced, or comfortable operating.\n\n**Site Cleanliness & Cleanup**\n\nTechnicians are responsible for maintaining a clean and professional work area throughout the assignment.\n\nBefore leaving the site:\n\n- Remove all cable scraps, wire clippings, zip-tie ends, packaging, connectors, ceiling-tile debris, and other waste generated by the work.\n- Remove tools, boxes, unused materials, and supplies from the work area unless specifically instructed otherwise.\n- Return moved furniture, equipment, ceiling tiles, and other items to their proper locations.\n- Sweep, vacuum, or otherwise clean the immediate work area when necessary.\n- Do not leave debris above ceilings, in telecommunications rooms, data closets, equipment cabinets, or other work areas.\n- Properly dispose of job-related waste in an approved location.\n- Leave all work areas **as clean as or cleaner than they were upon arrival**.\n- Provide photographs of the completed and cleaned work area when closeout photographs are required.\n\n**Cleanup is part of the scope of work. The assignment is not considered complete until all affected work areas have been cleaned and restored.**\n\n**Documentation & Closeout**\n\nBefore leaving the site, technicians must:\n\n- Confirm that the assigned scope has been completed.\n- Verify operation and functionality of affected equipment when applicable.\n- Provide clear photographs of completed work.\n- Provide photographs of labels, terminations, equipment locations, cable pathways, racks/cabinets, and other requested items.\n- Document any deviations from the original scope.\n- Record applicable cable IDs, port numbers, serial numbers, equipment information, test results, or other requested information.\n- Obtain required sign-off or completion acknowledgment when applicable.\n- Ensure all required Field Nation deliverables, documentation, photographs, and closing notes have been submitted.\n- Contact the designated project representative **before leaving the site** if any portion of the scope cannot be completed or if unresolved issues remain.\n\n**Important**\n\nAcceptance of this work order indicates that the technician has reviewed the scope and understands the requirements of the assignment.\n\nTechnicians are expected to arrive with the appropriate experience, tools, equipment, and PPE necessary to perform the work unless an exception has been communicated and approved in advance.\n\n**Do not leave the site with incomplete work, unresolved issues, or outstanding questions without first contacting the designated project representative.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-23T20:30","end":"2026-09-23T26:30"},"payRange":{"min":550,"max":550},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":6,"distance":62},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No in-hours counter slot available\nRequested: Wed, Sep 23, 8:30 PM\nChecked: Wed, Sep 23, Thu, Sep 24, Fri, Sep 25 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Miniso"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19: