{"job":{"id":19985657,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Tsunami USA LLC","title":"Troubleshoot Pole Mounted Peplink Router in Durham, NC","description":{"html":"<p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Overview:</strong></p><ul><li>Communication with TSUNAMI Support will be necessary to complete tickets as well as pictures in many cases.</li><li>The technician will need to be able to climb a ladder with the necessary tools and equipment.</li><li>TSUNAMI Support will take care of all shipping costs associated with replacement parts, etc.</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Dress Code:</strong></p><ul><li>Professional Attire</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Tools Required:</strong><em style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;</em></p><ul><li>16-25’ Extension ladder</li><li>&nbsp;Laptop with Ethernet Port</li><li>&nbsp;Hotspot for Internet</li><li>Multimeter</li><li>Hand tools</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Scope of Work:</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">***(SEE TASKS section For Job Checklist)</strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><em>On-Site Tasks&nbsp;</em></strong></p><ul><li>Check-in to work order, contact TSUNAMI Support via phone, and introduce yourself to the onsite contact (when applicable). You represent TSUNAMI USA while onsite.</li><li>The TSUNAMI is a self-contained surveillance system that are typically installed 15 – 20 feet on a utility pole. Troubleshooting the Peplink will consist of climbing the ladder, opening the TSUNAMI box, checking the physical status of the Peplink, rebooting/unplugging if necessary, then confirming connectivity with Support</li><li>Tech is responsible for their own ladder.</li><li>TSUNAMI coordinates, badge, and nearest address will be located in the confidential section.</li><li>Service Technicians repair or replace modules, subassemblies and components of the TSUNAMI Surveillance System.</li><li>TSUNAMI Surveillance System in good operating condition as determined by the specifications.</li><li>TSUNAMI Support will provide all necessary parts needed for replacement.&nbsp;</li><li>Hardware to be maintained include but are not limited to IP cameras, routers, switches, hard drives, network video recorders, ptz cameras, LPR cameras, cables, and antennas.</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><em>Required On-Site Deliverables&nbsp;</em></strong></p><ul><li>Check-out of work order</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Communication Directory:&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>Tech must contact TSUNAMI Support for further instructions.</li><li>Support Line: <del>************</del></li><li>Support Hours:<del> *** * *** * ** * * ** ***</del></li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy</strong></p><ul><li>Any travel expenses must be applied as a counter-offer when requesting the work in order to get approved</li><li>Any additional hours must be requested and approved by WO Manager</li></ul>","markdown":"**Overview:**\n\n- Communication with TSUNAMI Support will be necessary to complete tickets as well as pictures in many cases.\n- The technician will need to be able to climb a ladder with the necessary tools and equipment.\n- TSUNAMI Support will take care of all shipping costs associated with replacement parts, etc.\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n- Professional Attire\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- 16-25’ Extension ladder\n- Laptop with Ethernet Port\n- Hotspot for Internet\n- Multimeter\n- Hand tools\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*(SEE TASKS section For Job Checklist)**\n\n***On-Site Tasks***\n\n- Check-in to work order, contact TSUNAMI Support via phone, and introduce yourself to the onsite contact (when applicable). You represent TSUNAMI USA while onsite.\n- The TSUNAMI is a self-contained surveillance system that are typically installed 15 – 20 feet on a utility pole. Troubleshooting the Peplink will consist of climbing the ladder, opening the TSUNAMI box, checking the physical status of the Peplink, rebooting/unplugging if necessary, then confirming connectivity with Support\n- Tech is responsible for their own ladder.\n- TSUNAMI coordinates, badge, and nearest address will be located in the confidential section.\n- Service Technicians repair or replace modules, subassemblies and components of the TSUNAMI Surveillance System.\n- TSUNAMI Surveillance System in good operating condition as determined by the specifications.\n- TSUNAMI Support will provide all necessary parts needed for replacement.\n- Hardware to be maintained include but are not limited to IP cameras, routers, switches, hard drives, network video recorders, ptz cameras, LPR cameras, cables, and antennas.\n\n***Required On-Site Deliverables***\n\n- Check-out of work order\n\n**Communication Directory:**\n\n- Tech must contact TSUNAMI Support for further instructions.\n- Support Line: \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- Support Hours: \\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\*\\* \\* \\*\\* \\* \\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\n\n**Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy**\n\n- Any travel expenses must be applied as a counter-offer when requesting the work in order to get approved\n- Any additional hours must be requested and approved by WO Manager","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-22T10:00","end":"2026-09-22T12:00","latestStart":"2026-09-22T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":95,"max":190},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":95,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":9},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $190 (countered: $190) is below minimum threshold $400"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"