{"job":{"id":19985874,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Trooh","title":"ST#567 University of Mount Olive - Campus Bookstore","description":{"html":"<p><span style=\"color: black;\">Hello! We need a technician to install parts needed on our</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;TV screen(s)</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;on site.</span></p><p><strong>**The technician should have experience working with TVs and external device controllers. They should be comfortable connecting media players, configuring settings, and troubleshooting communication between devices to ensure proper remote functionality.**</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Controller</strong>: minix- rs232</li><li><strong>Download WhatsApp</strong> and use this link to connect with IT Support - https://wa.me/19298379142</li><li><strong>MUST HAVE LAPTOP (with HDMI/Ethernet port), HDMI/ETHERNET CABLE, MOUSE/KEYBOARD &amp; ANY ADDITIONAL PARTS LISTED. </strong></li></ul><p>Some Important info to know to get the job done successfully</p><ul><li>Please call IT support when you arrive on site&nbsp;<strong>(929) 837-9142.</strong>&nbsp;They will be your point of contact throughout the duration of your visit and will release you when all work is completed.</li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Site Manager: Wesley Tilley </span>919-658-7763</li><li>Issue: Part Replacement</li><li>DIMS: 43\"</li><li>Quantity:1</li><li>Parts shipped:&nbsp;<strong>1X rs232, Serial adapter, universal remote</strong></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Parts required: USB mouse and keyboard, 8-10ft ladder, </span>Laptop with HDMI &amp; Ethernet ports/adapter, Universal remote for Samsung TV<span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">​</span></li><li>Special Instructions: <span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">provide hotspot connection (200 Megabytes per hr)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Special instructions: Contact SM upon arrival and retreive parts from SM.</span></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Before your leave</u></strong></p><p>Upload photos (Proof of Performance)</p><ul><li>Ensure Picture Area is Clean – No Clutter</li><li>Take wide angled photos showing the entire space</li><li>Take close up shots of the tower</li><li>Make Screen the Main Object of the Picture</li><li>5 Pictures Minimum</li><li>Ensure No Glare on Screens</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Skills Needed:</strong></p><ul><li>Knowledge of remote applications (TeamViewer or GoToAssist)</li><li>Connect to Network: Wireless, Wired or Router with SIM card</li><li>Basic windows knowledge &amp; computer troubleshooting skillset</li><li>Required to use Whatsapp and/or Google Meets</li><li>SIM card ejector (pin) needed</li></ul><p><br></p><p>Please contact us if you have any questions</p><p>Trooh Support - support@trooh.com</p>","markdown":"Hello! We need a technician to install parts needed on our **TV screen(s)** on site.\n\n**\\*\\*The technician should have experience working with TVs and external device controllers. They should be comfortable connecting media players, configuring settings, and troubleshooting communication between devices to ensure proper remote functionality.\\*\\***\n\n- **Controller**: minix- rs232\n- **Download WhatsApp** and use this link to connect with IT Support - <https://wa.me/19298379142>\n- **MUST HAVE LAPTOP (with HDMI/Ethernet port), HDMI/ETHERNET CABLE, MOUSE/KEYBOARD & ANY ADDITIONAL PARTS LISTED.**\n\nSome Important info to know to get the job done successfully\n\n- Please call IT support when you arrive on site **(929) 837-9142.** They will be your point of contact throughout the duration of your visit and will release you when all work is completed.\n- Site Manager: Wesley Tilley 919-658-7763\n- Issue: Part Replacement\n- DIMS: 43\"\n- Quantity:1\n- Parts shipped: **1X rs232, Serial adapter, universal remote**\n- Parts required: USB mouse and keyboard, 8-10ft ladder, Laptop with HDMI & Ethernet ports/adapter, Universal remote for Samsung TV​\n- Special Instructions: provide hotspot connection (200 Megabytes per hr)\n- Special instructions: Contact SM upon arrival and retreive parts from SM.\n\n**Before your leave**\n\nUpload photos (Proof of Performance)\n\n- Ensure Picture Area is Clean – No Clutter\n- Take wide angled photos showing the entire space\n- Take close up shots of the tower\n- Make Screen the Main Object of the Picture\n- 5 Pictures Minimum\n- Ensure No Glare on Screens\n\n**Skills Needed:**\n\n- Knowledge of remote applications (TeamViewer or GoToAssist)\n- Connect to Network: Wireless, Wired or Router with SIM card\n- Basic windows knowledge & computer troubleshooting skillset\n- Required to use Whatsapp and/or Google Meets\n- SIM card ejector (pin) needed\n\nPlease contact us if you have any questions\n\nTrooh Support - support@trooh.com","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-22T12:00","end":"2026-09-22T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":150,"max":200},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":150},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":59},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $200 is below minimum threshold $400"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-22T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"gap"},{"start":"2026-09-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Miniso"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ​Concord Police Department - NC ( Phase 2 ) (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #1523 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-22T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"Remote Hands - Connect AT&T broadband circuit"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789751633837}
{"job":{"id":19985349,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"ASR tech","title":"Site Survey for Automated Locker System","description":{"html":"<p><strong>PLEASE READ THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER BEFORE ACCEPTING. YOU WILL BE HELD RESPONSIBLE FOR ALL DELIVERABLES.</strong></p><p>Overview: This work order is to survey the location for a future install of an automated package holding locker in an apartment complex.</p><p>Background: Parcel Pending provides automated package(Fedex/UPS/USPS) holding lockers to apartment complexes. ASR is their onsite provider and installer.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>ASR PROFESSIONALISM REQUIREMENTS</u></strong></p><ul><li>Perform excellent customer service. Be friendly, communicate, and assure them they're in good hands.&nbsp;</li><li>Dress code is casual business attire with no logos.</li><li>Do not share any pricing information with client.&nbsp;</li><li>Do not leave personal business information or contact information with client.</li><li>Technician needs to ensure that each site is a DRUG-FREE WORKPLACE</li><li>The technician needs to ensure they do not smell or reek of odors or other substances.</li></ul><p>ASR Services intends to help provide a safe and drug-free work environment for our clients.</p><p>The Company explicitly prohibits:</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;The use, possession, solicitation for, or sale of narcotics or other illegal drugs, alcohol, or prescription medication without a prescription on customer premises or while performing an assignment.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Main Contacts</u></strong></p><p><strong>Mark or Rodrigo (Phone numbers in confidential information)</strong></p><p>Please call on arrival and before you leave site. Also, please contact us if you have any issues or questions.</p><ul><li><strong><u>We have a FIRM start time with this order, you may arrive up to 15 minutes earlier.</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>For any delays or issues arriving on time, CALL Mark or Rodrigo.</u></strong></li></ul><p>Tech must include arrival and departure times, document any site delays, and requests that are made out of the scope of work in the closing notes.</p><p>Indoor Zhilai -&nbsp;-</p><p>HIGH || Site Survey - Please request a tech for a site walk. POC: Ellie @ 980-800-7789 - 9/24 - 3 indoor locker || Locker Count: 3&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong>READ THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER</strong></p><p>========================</p><p>Project Number: 887</p><p>========================</p><p><strong>The accepting technician must meet ALL requirements below:</strong></p><p>Technician needs to know how to either mount a flat screen and/or install secure cabinet/fixtures to different types of walls(drywall w/ wood studs, drywall w/aluminum, plaster, Stucco, clay brick, cinder block or concrete.</p><p>Work order may NOT be rescheduled.&nbsp;Accepting tech is required to be on site the date listed, no exceptions.&nbsp;Tech is representing ASR and should refer to him/herself as an ASR technician when making contact with the MOD and calling into Parcel Pending. Tech should NOT discuss any scheduling or payment issues with the Parcel Pending support desk under any circumstances. Any scheduling or payment issues MUST be discussed with ASR. If technician runs into DOA equipment/out of box failures, tech MUST contact ASR. Prior to going on site, please review the documentation and ASR sign off form (will be in the box)</p><p><br></p><p><strong>TOOL REQUIREMENT:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Government issued Identification</strong></li><li><strong>Standard Technicians tool kit</strong></li><li><strong>Standard 25' retractable tape measure minimum</strong></li><li><strong>Laptop with ethernet port to test for live internet.</strong></li><li><strong>AC outlet tester to test if power outlet is live.</strong></li><li><strong>Stud Finder</strong></li><li><strong>Smart Phone with ability to access e-mail and open a mobile web page</strong>&nbsp;(for checking in and out)</li><li><strong>Digital Camera</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Please bring PPE (Personal Protective Equipment). Not all sites require PPE but you will need to have it just in case.</strong></p><p><strong>PPE is hardhat, safety vest, safety goggles, long pants and steel toe boots.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Attachment:</strong></p><p>0887-SITESURVEYDOC-REV3-0.pdf&nbsp;- Print and bring to site.</p><p>=======================</p><p>READ THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER</p><p>DIRECTIONS</p><ol><li>Introduce yourself to the site contact as the ASR Techinician there to survey the Parcel Pending locker location</li><li>Follow the instructions that will be e-mailed to you to perform the site survey. Minimum items required are:</li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Sketch of room where lockers will be located outling doorways, windows, obstructions, data and power locations, any other items relevent to the locker placement.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Measurements of room where locker will be installed.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Measurements of walls, doorways, hallways that locker may need to pass through.</li></ul><ol><li>Take the photos outline in the instructions.</li><li>Have the manager sign off on the sign off sheet.</li><li>Upon completion, use the link provided in the e-mailed work order check out</li><li><strong>Upload all photos and survey to this work order and email them to parcelpendingsupport@asrepairtech.com</strong></li><li><strong>Do not leave site until Mark, David, or Rodrigo have approved your work.</strong></li></ol><p>=======================</p><p>Site Aborts where technician does not go to site, but within 24 hrs $30.00</p><p>Site Abort with technician onsite – determined by time spent at site</p><p>Cancellation with more than 24 hrs notice will be paid $0.</p>","markdown":"**PLEASE READ THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER BEFORE ACCEPTING. YOU WILL BE HELD RESPONSIBLE FOR ALL DELIVERABLES.**\n\nOverview: This work order is to survey the location for a future install of an automated package holding locker in an apartment complex.\n\nBackground: Parcel Pending provides automated package(Fedex/UPS/USPS) holding lockers to apartment complexes. ASR is their onsite provider and installer.\n\n**ASR PROFESSIONALISM REQUIREMENTS**\n\n- Perform excellent customer service. Be friendly, communicate, and assure them they're in good hands.\n- Dress code is casual business attire with no logos.\n- Do not share any pricing information with client.\n- Do not leave personal business information or contact information with client.\n- Technician needs to ensure that each site is a DRUG-FREE WORKPLACE\n- The technician needs to ensure they do not smell or reek of odors or other substances.\n\nASR Services intends to help provide a safe and drug-free work environment for our clients.\n\nThe Company explicitly prohibits:\n\n· The use, possession, solicitation for, or sale of narcotics or other illegal drugs, alcohol, or prescription medication without a prescription on customer premises or while performing an assignment.\n\n**Main Contacts**\n\n**Mark or Rodrigo (Phone numbers in confidential information)**\n\nPlease call on arrival and before you leave site. Also, please contact us if you have any issues or questions.\n\n- **We have a FIRM start time with this order, you may arrive up to 15 minutes earlier.**\n- **For any delays or issues arriving on time, CALL Mark or Rodrigo.**\n\nTech must include arrival and departure times, document any site delays, and requests that are made out of the scope of work in the closing notes.\n\nIndoor Zhilai - -\n\nHIGH || Site Survey - Please request a tech for a site walk. POC: Ellie @ 980-800-7789 - 9/24 - 3 indoor locker || Locker Count: 3\n\n**READ THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER**\n\n========================\n\nProject Number: 887\n\n========================\n\n**The accepting technician must meet ALL requirements below:**\n\nTechnician needs to know how to either mount a flat screen and/or install secure cabinet/fixtures to different types of walls(drywall w/ wood studs, drywall w/aluminum, plaster, Stucco, clay brick, cinder block or concrete.\n\nWork order may NOT be rescheduled. Accepting tech is required to be on site the date listed, no exceptions. Tech is representing ASR and should refer to him/herself as an ASR technician when making contact with the MOD and calling into Parcel Pending. Tech should NOT discuss any scheduling or payment issues with the Parcel Pending support desk under any circumstances. Any scheduling or payment issues MUST be discussed with ASR. If technician runs into DOA equipment/out of box failures, tech MUST contact ASR. Prior to going on site, please review the documentation and ASR sign off form (will be in the box)\n\n**TOOL REQUIREMENT:**\n\n- **Government issued Identification**\n- **Standard Technicians tool kit**\n- **Standard 25' retractable tape measure minimum**\n- **Laptop with ethernet port to test for live internet.**\n- **AC outlet tester to test if power outlet is live.**\n- **Stud Finder**\n- **Smart Phone with ability to access e-mail and open a mobile web page** (for checking in and out)\n- **Digital Camera**\n\n**Please bring PPE (Personal Protective Equipment). Not all sites require PPE but you will need to have it just in case.**\n\n**PPE is hardhat, safety vest, safety goggles, long pants and steel toe boots.**\n\n**Attachment:**\n\n0887-SITESURVEYDOC-REV3-0.pdf - Print and bring to site.\n\n=======================\n\nREAD THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER\n\nDIRECTIONS\n\n1. Introduce yourself to the site contact as the ASR Techinician there to survey the Parcel Pending locker location\n2. Follow the instructions that will be e-mailed to you to perform the site survey. Minimum items required are:\n\n- Sketch of room where lockers will be located outling doorways, windows, obstructions, data and power locations, any other items relevent to the locker placement.\n- Measurements of room where locker will be installed.\n- Measurements of walls, doorways, hallways that locker may need to pass through.\n\n1. Take the photos outline in the instructions.\n2. Have the manager sign off on the sign off sheet.\n3. Upon completion, use the link provided in the e-mailed work order check out\n4. **Upload all photos and survey to this work order and email them to parcelpendingsupport@asrepairtech.com**\n5. **Do not leave site until Mark, David, or Rodrigo have approved your work.**\n\n=======================\n\nSite Aborts where technician does not go to site, but within 24 hrs $30.00\n\nSite Abort with technician onsite – determined by time spent at site\n\nCancellation with more than 24 hrs notice will be paid $0.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-24T10:00","end":"2026-09-24T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":65},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":11},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $65 is below minimum threshold $400"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Miniso"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ​Concord Police Department - NC ( Phase 2 ) (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"