{"job":{"id":19985234,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"PIVITAL","title":"Site Activation/Turn -UP/ Test MB2794705","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Connect the circuit to PODS equipment such as the <strong>Meraki MX68 or Meraki MX68W</strong></li><li>Determine best location for installation of the Meraki MX68</li><li>Installation of the Meraki MX68</li><li>Patching of circuit into the Meraki MX68</li><li>Completion of the activation of the circuit</li><li>Testing to confirm circuit is active</li><li>If client can provide identifying details to allow Pivital to determine the correct device, then the following can be completed:</li><li>Disconnect the existing provider’s circuit</li><li>Remove the legacy SD Wan device</li><li>Place SD Wan device on client provided pallet or package SD wan device and attach client provided shipping label</li><li>Ship device to client provided address </li></ul><p><strong>***There is no bridge call, Support Number in the confidential section***</strong></p><p><br></p><p><em>Review the “Confidential Section” listed at the bottom of the work order for specific detailed information regarding this dispatch including bridge line details, lcon info, and equipment information</em></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">Please bring a </span><span style=\"color: rgb(244, 5, 5);\">NEWER working Windows laptop (Win10 or higher) with a 1gb Ethernet port (or 1gb Ethernet dongle), a hotspot and team viewer already installed with the ability to log into a network device using a Console connection AND Ethernet connection. </span><span style=\"color: rgb(31, 31, 31);\">This is required for all techs at the minimum. Preferably have ALL of the tools listed below in the Tool Requirements</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Tool Requirements:</u></strong></p><ul><li>WIN10 or higher Laptop (No Mac laptops) – with1gb Ethernet connection, charger &amp; TeamViewer Installed</li><li>Hot Spot or Internet Dongle</li><li>Standard Tool Kit</li><li>Cell Phone - with Charger</li><li>Console Cable</li><li>Spare Patch Cables &amp; Cabling Equipment (Rj45, Biscuits, Etc..)</li></ul><p><strong><u>Site Security Requirements:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Photo ID required</li><li>Names of all technicians going to the site must be provided in advance</li><li>Check-in with site contacts representing <span style=\"background-color: rgb(22, 39, 65); color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>******* ******** ****** ************** *******</del></span></li><li>Workers to be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment</li><li>Professional environment expecting professional conduct and clean business casual attire</li><li>If PPE required: professional environment expecting professional conduct, clean work attire with appropriate PPE</li></ul>","markdown":"**Scope of Work:**\n\n- Connect the circuit to PODS equipment such as the **Meraki MX68 or Meraki MX68W**\n- Determine best location for installation of the Meraki MX68\n- Installation of the Meraki MX68\n- Patching of circuit into the Meraki MX68\n- Completion of the activation of the circuit\n- Testing to confirm circuit is active\n- If client can provide identifying details to allow Pivital to determine the correct device, then the following can be completed:\n- Disconnect the existing provider’s circuit\n- Remove the legacy SD Wan device\n- Place SD Wan device on client provided pallet or package SD wan device and attach client provided shipping label\n- Ship device to client provided address\n\n**\\*\\*\\*There is no bridge call, Support Number in the confidential section\\*\\*\\***\n\n*Review the “Confidential Section” listed at the bottom of the work order for specific detailed information regarding this dispatch including bridge line details, lcon info, and equipment information*\n\nPlease bring a NEWER working Windows laptop (Win10 or higher) with a 1gb Ethernet port (or 1gb Ethernet dongle), a hotspot and team viewer already installed with the ability to log into a network device using a Console connection AND Ethernet connection. This is required for all techs at the minimum. Preferably have ALL of the tools listed below in the Tool Requirements\n\n**Tool Requirements:**\n\n- WIN10 or higher Laptop (No Mac laptops) – with1gb Ethernet connection, charger & TeamViewer Installed\n- Hot Spot or Internet Dongle\n- Standard Tool Kit\n- Cell Phone - with Charger\n- Console Cable\n- Spare Patch Cables & Cabling Equipment (Rj45, Biscuits, Etc..)\n\n**Site Security Requirements:**\n\n- Photo ID required\n- Names of all technicians going to the site must be provided in advance\n- Check-in with site contacts representing \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- Workers to be fully equipped to complete all work without the need for any customer tools or equipment\n- Professional environment expecting professional conduct and clean business casual attire\n- If PPE required: professional environment expecting professional conduct, clean work attire with appropriate PPE","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-25T10:00","end":"2026-09-25T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":35,"max":105},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":35,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":15},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $105 (countered: $180) is below minimum threshold $400"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Miniso Durham"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ​Concord Police Department - NC ( Phase 2 ) (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #1523 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-22T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"Remote Hands - Connect AT&T broadband circuit"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789751652178}
{"job":{"id":19985021,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Loopdrive LLC","title":"Smart Home - Diagnostic & Pairing","description":{"html":"<p><strong>YOU REPRESENT DIAMOND PROPERTY SERVICES ON THIS JOB. Identify yourself to the resident and Smart Home Support as a contractor working for Diamond Property Services—not Field Nation or your own company.</strong></p>Smart Home - Diagnostic &amp; Pairing<p><strong>Reported problem:</strong> Please assess existing non-powered video doorbell. Once power issue is resolved, please pair the video doorbell and help resident set up and connect and access the VD in app and see live feed. Reset internally, if needed</p><p>Troubleshoot the existing smart-home system and resolve the reported device issues where possible. Work may include checking power, batteries and connections; correcting loose connections; and performing device resets. Call Smart Home Support for pairing and configuration.</p><p>Test each serviced device with the resident—not just its online status. For video doorbells, verify live video and doorbell/chime operation; for locks, verify locking/unlocking and resident codes; for thermostats, verify operation. If an issue cannot be resolved, contact the Site Manager before leaving and document the cause, work performed, and what is needed to finish.</p><p><strong>Additional devices: If other devices need service outside this scope, photograph and detail each item worked on in your closeout. You may request $10 per additional item in your final bill. Sensor pairing is included and does not qualify for the additional $10 allowance. Do not discuss billing with Smart Home Support.</strong></p>1. CALL THE SITE MANAGER WHEN THERE IS A PROBLEM<p><strong>For calls and texts, contact the site manager at (901) 675-6129.</strong></p><p>Call immediately if:</p><ul><li>You will be late, need to cancel, or cannot attend.</li><li>The resident does not answer, refuses access, or the site is not ready.</li><li>Parts are missing/incorrect or you cannot complete the work.</li><li>You encounter wiring questions, equipment damage, or another problem preventing completion.</li></ul><p><strong>If your call is unanswered, text the same number immediately. Include the property address, problem, and your ETA if running late.</strong></p><p>For access or site-readiness problems, call and, if unanswered, text while still at the property, before leaving, so we can try to reach the resident.</p><p>An FN message or call to Smart Home Support does not replace contacting the Site Manager. Schedule changes require Site Manager approval.</p>2. DEVICE REQUIREMENTS<p><strong>THERMOSTAT POWER MUST BE OFF — applies if thermostat wiring is required; pairing alone does not authorize a thermostat replacement.</strong></p><p>Before disconnecting or connecting thermostat wires:</p><ul><li>Identify and shut off the furnace/air-handler and any other power source supplying the thermostat.</li><li>Verify power is absent at the thermostat wiring using an appropriate meter. Thermostat OFF mode, a blank screen, or an assumed breaker label is not proof.</li><li>Photograph the shutoff used and original wiring. Record how you verified power was off.</li><li>If you cannot identify or verify the correct shutoff, stop and contact the Site Manager.</li></ul><p><strong>If you fail to shut off power to the air handler and blow a fuse during thermostat work, you must replace the fuse with the correct type and rating and restore operation at your own expense. If you do not correct the issue, the work order will be closed without payment to cover the cost of dispatching an emergency repair technician.</strong></p><p>Photograph completed thermostat wiring before attaching the display. Restore power and verify heating/cooling operation as appropriate for the equipment and conditions. Report any failed or unperformed test.</p><p>Install and service devices according to the equipment manufacturer’s requirements. Photograph original connections before changing them and completed work afterward. Follow Smart Home Support instructions for resets and pairing preparation; do not independently pair devices.</p>3. PAIRING AND CHECKOUT<p><strong>Smart Home Support: 330-970-2020 | Hours: 9 AM–5 PM Eastern</strong></p><p>Call with the property address for pairing and checkout. If you do not reach support immediately, call the Site Manager immediately; if that call is unanswered, text the Site Manager immediately. Support must confirm pairing and online status. Report any unresolved issue before leaving. If your late arrival prevents pairing before support closes, you may be required to return during support's normal hours to complete pairing.</p>4. REQUIRED PHOTOS AND DEVICE REPORT<p>Upload:</p><ul><li>Timestamped arrival and departure photos showing the property/address.</li><li>For thermostat wiring work: power-shutoff, original wiring, completed wiring, and installed-device photos.</li><li>Before/after photos of every device serviced, including original/completed connections where applicable.</li><li>Support call-log screenshot and available app evidence of paired devices.</li></ul><p><strong>Report every scoped device and every additional device worked on, one line per device:</strong></p><p><strong>Device/location | Work performed | Final result</strong></p><p>Example: Hall thermostat | Replaced and paired | Operation tested; online. Kitchen leak sensor | Paired existing sensor only | Online.</p><p>Distinguish replacement, new installation, pairing only, diagnosis, and battery replacement. List incomplete or unperformed work and the reason. Include arrival/departure times, support representative, and Site Manager instructions received.</p><p><strong>“Completed” or “all devices paired” alone is not an acceptable report.</strong></p>5. SERVICE AND PAYMENT TERMS<p>Only the assigned technician may attend. Treat the resident and support staff professionally.</p><p>Completion requires the listed work, operational verification, support checkout, and required documentation. Correct incomplete or inaccurate documentation before requesting approval.</p><p>For resident no-access, site not ready, power outage, or missing/incorrect parts preventing completion, you may request the $35 trip fee with documented contact attempts and site evidence; full completion pay does not apply. A $10 late-arrival deduction applies when you arrive after the agreed appointment time.</p>","markdown":"**YOU REPRESENT DIAMOND PROPERTY SERVICES ON THIS JOB. Identify yourself to the resident and Smart Home Support as a contractor working for Diamond Property Services—not Field Nation or your own company.**\n\nSmart Home - Diagnostic & Pairing**Reported problem:** Please assess existing non-powered video doorbell. Once power issue is resolved, please pair the video doorbell and help resident set up and connect and access the VD in app and see live feed. Reset internally, if needed\n\nTroubleshoot the existing smart-home system and resolve the reported device issues where possible. Work may include checking power, batteries and connections; correcting loose connections; and performing device resets. Call Smart Home Support for pairing and configuration.\n\nTest each serviced device with the resident—not just its online status. For video doorbells, verify live video and doorbell/chime operation; for locks, verify locking/unlocking and resident codes; for thermostats, verify operation. If an issue cannot be resolved, contact the Site Manager before leaving and document the cause, work performed, and what is needed to finish.\n\n**Additional devices: If other devices need service outside this scope, photograph and detail each item worked on in your closeout. You may request $10 per additional item in your final bill. Sensor pairing is included and does not qualify for the additional $10 allowance. Do not discuss billing with Smart Home Support.**\n\n1. CALL THE SITE MANAGER WHEN THERE IS A PROBLEM**For calls and texts, contact the site manager at (901) 675-6129.**\n\nCall immediately if:\n\n- You will be late, need to cancel, or cannot attend.\n- The resident does not answer, refuses access, or the site is not ready.\n- Parts are missing/incorrect or you cannot complete the work.\n- You encounter wiring questions, equipment damage, or another problem preventing completion.\n\n**If your call is unanswered, text the same number immediately. Include the property address, problem, and your ETA if running late.**\n\nFor access or site-readiness problems, call and, if unanswered, text while still at the property, before leaving, so we can try to reach the resident.\n\nAn FN message or call to Smart Home Support does not replace contacting the Site Manager. Schedule changes require Site Manager approval.\n\n2. DEVICE REQUIREMENTS**THERMOSTAT POWER MUST BE OFF — applies if thermostat wiring is required; pairing alone does not authorize a thermostat replacement.**\n\nBefore disconnecting or connecting thermostat wires:\n\n- Identify and shut off the furnace/air-handler and any other power source supplying the thermostat.\n- Verify power is absent at the thermostat wiring using an appropriate meter. Thermostat OFF mode, a blank screen, or an assumed breaker label is not proof.\n- Photograph the shutoff used and original wiring. Record how you verified power was off.\n- If you cannot identify or verify the correct shutoff, stop and contact the Site Manager.\n\n**If you fail to shut off power to the air handler and blow a fuse during thermostat work, you must replace the fuse with the correct type and rating and restore operation at your own expense. If you do not correct the issue, the work order will be closed without payment to cover the cost of dispatching an emergency repair technician.**\n\nPhotograph completed thermostat wiring before attaching the display. Restore power and verify heating/cooling operation as appropriate for the equipment and conditions. Report any failed or unperformed test.\n\nInstall and service devices according to the equipment manufacturer’s requirements. Photograph original connections before changing them and completed work afterward. Follow Smart Home Support instructions for resets and pairing preparation; do not independently pair devices.\n\n3. PAIRING AND CHECKOUT**Smart Home Support: 330-970-2020 | Hours: 9 AM–5 PM Eastern**\n\nCall with the property address for pairing and checkout. If you do not reach support immediately, call the Site Manager immediately; if that call is unanswered, text the Site Manager immediately. Support must confirm pairing and online status. Report any unresolved issue before leaving. If your late arrival prevents pairing before support closes, you may be required to return during support's normal hours to complete pairing.\n\n4. REQUIRED PHOTOS AND DEVICE REPORTUpload:\n\n- Timestamped arrival and departure photos showing the property/address.\n- For thermostat wiring work: power-shutoff, original wiring, completed wiring, and installed-device photos.\n- Before/after photos of every device serviced, including original/completed connections where applicable.\n- Support call-log screenshot and available app evidence of paired devices.\n\n**Report every scoped device and every additional device worked on, one line per device:**\n\n**Device/location | Work performed | Final result**\n\nExample: Hall thermostat | Replaced and paired | Operation tested; online. Kitchen leak sensor | Paired existing sensor only | Online.\n\nDistinguish replacement, new installation, pairing only, diagnosis, and battery replacement. List incomplete or unperformed work and the reason. Include arrival/departure times, support representative, and Site Manager instructions received.\n\n**“Completed” or “all devices paired” alone is not an acceptable report.**\n\n5. SERVICE AND PAYMENT TERMSOnly the assigned technician may attend. Treat the resident and support staff professionally.\n\nCompletion requires the listed work, operational verification, support checkout, and required documentation. Correct incomplete or inaccurate documentation before requesting approval.\n\nFor resident no-access, site not ready, power outage, or missing/incorrect parts preventing completion, you may request the $35 trip fee with documented contact attempts and site evidence; full completion pay does not apply. A $10 late-arrival deduction applies when you arrive after the agreed appointment time.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-28T12:00","end":"2026-09-28T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":60},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":28},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $60 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Miniso Durham"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ​Concord Police Department - NC ( Phase 2 ) (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"}