{"job":{"id":19985103,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Wachter - Nationwide Projects","title":"DSG 1361 - Store Closure - Register","description":{"html":"<p>Wear ALL appropriate PPE</p><p>Check in with Wachter PM Lauren Whitmore at <del>************</del></p><p><strong>Text Eric at DSG <del>************</del> with Name, Store #, Closing Store - UPON ARRIVING ONSITE</strong></p><p><br></p><p>GENERAL CLOSING SCOPE</p><p><br></p><p>- OUT OF SCOPE Items:&nbsp;tech is NOT responsible for de-installing these items</p><p>o TV’s, LP equipment, Audio Equipment, Security Cameras, Actual Network Racks, Patch Panels, CAT6 Cabling&nbsp;</p><p>- SHIPPING SUPPLIES:&nbsp;DSG supplies the boxes and packing supplies&nbsp;</p><p>o On a rare occasion, technician (vendor) could be requested to purchase supplies and will be re-imbursed.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>o Supplies ordered for each closure</p><p><br></p><p>QTY Product Intended Use</p><p>1 1’2” Bubble Roll, 24” x 250’&nbsp;&nbsp;- 2 rolls Packing heavier equipment&nbsp;</p><p>2-3 rolls 3/16” 24”W x 175’ General packing</p><p>2-3 18” x 300’ Paper rolls&nbsp;&nbsp;(size of roll could vary upon availability General packing&nbsp;</p><p>1 or 2 packs of 15 boxes 20”x20”x12” Shipping Box&nbsp;(exact size and qty could differ upon availability General Packing&nbsp;</p><p>1x10 24\"x24\"x20\" Double Wall Boxes&nbsp;(exact size and qty could differ upon availability Pack Registers&nbsp;</p><p>1 Extra Wide Packing Tape w/ 2 rolls ( 2.8”x 54.6 yds) General Packing</p><p>5 36\"x 24\"x 24\" Double Wall Boxes (exact size and qty could differ upon availability Packing Servers/Network</p><p><br></p><p>- DSG (Store) to supply pallets and Shrink wrap&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>*NOTE* If this is a day 1 Decom ONLY, disregard day 2 scope. A list of decom equipment will be provided for everything that we need.</p><p><br></p><p>REGISTER &amp; SURFTHING DE-INSTALLATION PROCESS:&nbsp;1 Day&nbsp;</p><p>- Tech arrives at the store at 8:00 AM&nbsp;</p><p>o Front doors should be open (not automatic)&nbsp;</p><p>o Buzzer inside first set of doors will alert store tech is there</p><p>o Call or Text DSG to let them know you are in the store</p><p>- Tech locates shipping supplies&nbsp;</p><p>o Inform DSG on anything missing</p><p>o NOTE: tech can use any available boxes and supplies that are available</p><p><br></p><p>REGISTER PACKING</p><p>- Tech will pack up the ENTIRE register solution (Register + peripherals) except for the security pads (Grey Pad that de-magnetizes security devices on products)&nbsp;</p><p>o Tech to get with the closing manager on where to place all of these security pads/devices.&nbsp;DSG’s LP team will arrange for shipping/pickup&nbsp;</p><p>- Pack up registers as securely as possible to ensure they are not damaged in transit (as much as you can)&nbsp;</p><p>- After boxing up all the registers, tech will need to palletize the boxes of registers&nbsp;</p><p>o Use good judgement when building/stacking pallets&nbsp;</p><p>- Shrink Wrap the pallets&nbsp;</p><p>- Place the BOL on each pallet and secure the BOL inside one level of shrink wrap</p><p>o If shrink wrap is colored – place the BOL on the outside of the shrink wrap and place tape over the entire BOL to make sure it stays in tact and legible for our DEPOT warehouse upon arrival</p><p><br></p><p>SURFTHING:</p><p>- Locate the equipment (usually a PC with Keyboard + Mouse) and a Golf Swing analyzer (floor device to measure golf swing)</p><p>- Pack this in a regular box – write “SURFTHING” on the box and give it to the closing manager&nbsp;</p><p>o He/She will use the provided FedEx Label to send it back to Surfthing.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>- The Surfthing equipment DOES NOT go on the pallet with the registers</p><p><br></p><p>DELIVERABLES:</p><p>- Pictures of the Pallets shrink wrapped with BOL attached&nbsp;</p><p>- Picture of the Surfthing Box completed&nbsp;</p>","markdown":"Wear ALL appropriate PPE\n\nCheck in with Wachter PM Lauren Whitmore at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Text Eric at DSG \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* with Name, Store #, Closing Store - UPON ARRIVING ONSITE**\n\nGENERAL CLOSING SCOPE\n\n  \n\\\n\n\\- OUT OF SCOPE Items: tech is NOT responsible for de-installing these items\n\no TV’s, LP equipment, Audio Equipment, Security Cameras, Actual Network Racks, Patch Panels, CAT6 Cabling\n\n\\- SHIPPING SUPPLIES: DSG supplies the boxes and packing supplies\n\no On a rare occasion, technician (vendor) could be requested to purchase supplies and will be re-imbursed.\n\no Supplies ordered for each closure\n\nQTY Product Intended Use\n\n1 1’2” Bubble Roll, 24” x 250’ - 2 rolls Packing heavier equipment\n\n2-3 rolls 3/16” 24”W x 175’ General packing\n\n2-3 18” x 300’ Paper rolls (size of roll could vary upon availability General packing\n\n1 or 2 packs of 15 boxes 20”x20”x12” Shipping Box (exact size and qty could differ upon availability General Packing\n\n1x10 24\"x24\"x20\" Double Wall Boxes (exact size and qty could differ upon availability Pack Registers\n\n1 Extra Wide Packing Tape w/ 2 rolls ( 2.8”x 54.6 yds) General Packing\n\n5 36\"x 24\"x 24\" Double Wall Boxes (exact size and qty could differ upon availability Packing Servers/Network\n\n  \n\\\n\n\\- DSG (Store) to supply pallets and Shrink wrap\n\n\\*NOTE\\* If this is a day 1 Decom ONLY, disregard day 2 scope. A list of decom equipment will be provided for everything that we need.\n\nREGISTER & SURFTHING DE-INSTALLATION PROCESS: 1 Day\n\n\\- Tech arrives at the store at 8:00 AM\n\no Front doors should be open (not automatic)\n\no Buzzer inside first set of doors will alert store tech is there\n\no Call or Text DSG to let them know you are in the store\n\n\\- Tech locates shipping supplies\n\no Inform DSG on anything missing\n\no NOTE: tech can use any available boxes and supplies that are available\n\nREGISTER PACKING\n\n\\- Tech will pack up the ENTIRE register solution (Register + peripherals) except for the security pads (Grey Pad that de-magnetizes security devices on products)\n\no Tech to get with the closing manager on where to place all of these security pads/devices. DSG’s LP team will arrange for shipping/pickup\n\n\\- Pack up registers as securely as possible to ensure they are not damaged in transit (as much as you can)\n\n\\- After boxing up all the registers, tech will need to palletize the boxes of registers\n\no Use good judgement when building/stacking pallets\n\n\\- Shrink Wrap the pallets\n\n\\- Place the BOL on each pallet and secure the BOL inside one level of shrink wrap\n\no If shrink wrap is colored – place the BOL on the outside of the shrink wrap and place tape over the entire BOL to make sure it stays in tact and legible for our DEPOT warehouse upon arrival\n\nSURFTHING:\n\n\\- Locate the equipment (usually a PC with Keyboard + Mouse) and a Golf Swing analyzer (floor device to measure golf swing)\n\n\\- Pack this in a regular box – write “SURFTHING” on the box and give it to the closing manager\n\no He/She will use the provided FedEx Label to send it back to Surfthing.\n\n\\- The Surfthing equipment DOES NOT go on the pallet with the registers\n\nDELIVERABLES:\n\n\\- Pictures of the Pallets shrink wrapped with BOL attached\n\n\\- Picture of the Surfthing Box completed","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-02T08:00","end":"2026-10-02T20:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":660},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":12,"distance":2},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No in-hours counter slot available\nRequested: Fri, Oct 2, 8:00 AM\nChecked: Fri, Oct 2, Mon, Oct 5, Tue, Oct 6 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-06T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ​Concord Police Department - NC ( Phase 2 ) (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #1523 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-22T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"Remote Hands - Connect AT&T broadband circuit"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":17897516