{"job":{"id":19985128,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Integris","title":"#11412660 | Raleigh - Internet Issue | Artisent Floors","description":{"html":"<p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Overview:</strong></p><ul><li>Seeking a technician with experience in __<strong>Networking</strong>___.</li><li>Tech is required to __<strong>Assist in getting ISP back online</strong>___.</li><li>Estimated duration will be__<strong>3 hours</strong>__</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Scope of Work:</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><em>On-Site Tasks</em></strong></p><ol><li>Check-in to work order</li><li>What needs to be done?</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">connect new circuit to the firewall and configure the firewall with the Circuit information.</li><li>Why does this need to be done on site?</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">cannot be done remotely. </li><li>Onsite point of contact:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Jaimie Walker - (770) 409-8228</li><li>Is the client requesting a specific time/date?</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Install will be done on September 8th so we probably need to be out on 9th. </li><li>Will this require more than one technician? (heavy equipment, etc.)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">no</li><li>Is downtime required, if so, downtime explanation?</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">No</li><li>What tools will we need to complete the task?</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Laptop</li><li>Who should the onsite tech reach out to if they need higher level/remote help?</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Jose Quijano</li><li>Check-out of work order</li></ol><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Escalation Process:</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Contact WO Engineer - </span><strong>Jose Quijano</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> at </span><strong>(404) 551-5492</strong> <span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">if the following are true:</span></p><ol><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If clarification is needed on work order, discuss with _<strong>Jose Quijano</strong>__</li></ol><ul><li>Any issues or questions should be escalated to __<strong>Jose Quijano</strong>__</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy</strong></p><ul><li>Parking &amp; travel expenses will NOT be paid.</li></ul>","markdown":"**Overview:**\n\n- Seeking a technician with experience in \\_\\_**Networking**\\_\\_\\_.\n- Tech is required to \\_\\_**Assist in getting ISP back online**\\_\\_\\_.\n- Estimated duration will be\\_\\_**3 hours**\\_\\_\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n***On-Site Tasks***\n\n1. Check-in to work order\n2. What needs to be done?\n3. connect new circuit to the firewall and configure the firewall with the Circuit information.\n4. Why does this need to be done on site?\n5. cannot be done remotely.\n6. Onsite point of contact:\n7. Jaimie Walker - (770) 409-8228\n8. Is the client requesting a specific time/date?\n9. Install will be done on September 8th so we probably need to be out on 9th.\n10. Will this require more than one technician? (heavy equipment, etc.)\n11. no\n12. Is downtime required, if so, downtime explanation?\n13. No\n14. What tools will we need to complete the task?\n15. Laptop\n16. Who should the onsite tech reach out to if they need higher level/remote help?\n17. Jose Quijano\n18. Check-out of work order\n\n**Escalation Process:**\n\nContact WO Engineer - **Jose Quijano** at **(404) 551-5492** if the following are true:\n\n1. If clarification is needed on work order, discuss with \\_**Jose Quijano**\\_\\_\n\n- Any issues or questions should be escalated to \\_\\_**Jose Quijano**\\_\\_\n\n**Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy**\n\n- Parking & travel expenses will NOT be paid.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-23T10:00","end":"2026-09-23T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":85,"max":340},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":85,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":5},"result":