{"job":{"id":19984946,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Pursuant Health","title":"Diagnose, Report, and Repair Cause(s) of Inaccurate Blood Pressure Results, Diagnose, Report, and Repair Cause(s) of Inaccurate BMI / Weight Results and PM Kiosk","description":{"html":"<ul><li>A Release Code must be obtained upon completion of the work order, prior to leaving the site. <strong>Failure to obtain Release Code</strong> will result in deduction and/or cancellation of the work order.</li><li>CAUTION: Do not plug any power tools or cleaning devices into the kiosk’s internal power strips. Doing so may result in blown fuses and system failure. Use only approved connections as directed.</li><li>CONNECT to WIFI - Poor connection may result in difficulties accessing work instructions and contacting support. If you are having connectivity issues please connect to the site&#39;s WIFI connection.</li><li>REMOVE MIRROR BOX (FM kiosks only) - Is a mirror box currently installed in kiosk? If so, remove and set aside for disposal. Instructions: https://bit.ly/KioskMirrorBox</li><li><strong><em><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Before Replacing Parts:</span> </em>Diagnose, Report, and Repair Cause(s) of Inaccurate Blood Pressure Results</strong><br /><ul><li><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Prior to replacing any parts</span>, test functionality and accuracy of the Blood Pressure System, and report your findings to Technical Support at https://bit.ly/m/Pursuant<ul><li>Begin an assessment in the kiosk software.</li><li>Record your results.</li></ul></li><li>After reporting findings, continue with part replacement. Please refer to the step-by-step guides in the links below:<ul><li>Cuff / Hose: https://bit.ly/MAVBPCuff</li><li>Stop Button / Wiring Harness: https://bit.ly/MAVBP</li><li>Pump: https://bit.ly/MAVBP-Pump</li><li>Pump Decal: https://bit.ly/MAVBP-Pump-Decal</li></ul></li><li>After installing all parts, take a photo of the Calibration Decal and upload to your Work Order.</li><li>Return <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">all</span> replaced parts to Pursuant Health after completion of work.</li></ul></li><li><strong><em><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Before Replacing Parts:</span> </em>Diagnose, Report, and Repair Cause(s) of Inaccurate BMI / Weight Results</strong><br /><ul><li><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">Prior to replacing any parts</span>, test functionality and accuracy of the BMI / Weight System, and report your findings to Technical Support at https://bit.ly/m/Pursuant<ul><li>Begin an assessment in the kiosk software.</li><li>Record your results.</li></ul></li><li>After reporting findings, continue with part replacement. Please refer to the step-by-step guides in the link below, selecting the following guides:<ul><li>https://bit.ly/MAVWeight &gt; &#34;How-To: Replace the Load Cell&#34;</li><li>https://bit.ly/MAVWeight &gt; &#34;How-To: Replace the Mantracourt&#34;</li><li>https://bit.ly/MAVWeight &gt; &#34;How-To: Replace the Load Cell Extension Cable&#34;</li></ul></li><li>After installing all supplied BMI components, calibrate the BMI / Weight system.</li><li>Return <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">all</span> replaced parts to Pursuant Health after completion of work.</li></ul></li><li><span>STOP BUTTON PHOTO (FM and PH kiosks only) - Verify the stop button is wired and secured correctly, then take a clear photo showing the wiring/mounting hardware. This photo will be needed during the checkout process to obtain your release code.</span></li></ul>","markdown":"- A Release Code must be obtained upon completion of the work order, prior to leaving the site. **Failure to obtain Release Code** will result in deduction and/or cancellation of the work order.\n- CAUTION: Do not plug any power tools or cleaning devices into the kiosk’s internal power strips. Doing so may result in blown fuses and system failure. Use only approved connections as directed.\n- CONNECT to WIFI - Poor connection may result in difficulties accessing work instructions and contacting support. If you are having connectivity issues please connect to the site's WIFI connection.\n- REMOVE MIRROR BOX (FM kiosks only) - Is a mirror box currently installed in kiosk? If so, remove and set aside for disposal. Instructions: <https://bit.ly/KioskMirrorBox>\n- ***Before Replacing Parts:* Diagnose, Report, and Repair Cause(s) of Inaccurate Blood Pressure Results**  \n  \n  - Prior to replacing any parts, test functionality and accuracy of the Blood Pressure System, and report your findings to Technical Support at <https://bit.ly/m/Pursuant>\n      - Begin an assessment in the kiosk software.\n      - Record your results.\n  - After reporting findings, continue with part replacement. Please refer to the step-by-step guides in the links below:\n      - Cuff / Hose: <https://bit.ly/MAVBPCuff>\n      - Stop Button / Wiring Harness: <https://bit.ly/MAVBP>\n      - Pump: <https://bit.ly/MAVBP-Pump>\n      - Pump Decal: <https://bit.ly/MAVBP-Pump-Decal>\n  - After installing all parts, take a photo of the Calibration Decal and upload to your Work Order.\n  - Return all replaced parts to Pursuant Health after completion of work.\n- ***Before Replacing Parts:* Diagnose, Report, and Repair Cause(s) of Inaccurate BMI / Weight Results**  \n  \n  - Prior to replacing any parts, test functionality and accuracy of the BMI / Weight System, and report your findings to Technical Support at <https://bit.ly/m/Pursuant>\n      - Begin an assessment in the kiosk software.\n      - Record your results.\n  - After reporting findings, continue with part replacement. Please refer to the step-by-step guides in the link below, selecting the following guides:\n      - <https://bit.ly/MAVWeight> > \"How-To: Replace the Load Cell\"\n      - <https://bit.ly/MAVWeight> > \"How-To: Replace the Mantracourt\"\n      - <https://bit.ly/MAVWeight> > \"How-To: Replace the Load Cell Extension Cable\"\n  - After installing all supplied BMI components, calibrate the BMI / Weight system.\n  - Return all replaced parts to Pursuant Health after completion of work.\n- STOP BUTTON PHOTO (FM and PH kiosks only) - Verify the stop button is wired and secured correctly, then take a clear photo showing the wiring/mounting hardware. This photo will be needed during the checkout process to obtain your release code.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-24T11:00","end":"2026-09-24T14:30","latestStart":"2026-09-24T11:45"},"payRange":{"min":190,"max":190},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3.5,"distance":49},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $190 is below minimum threshold $400"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Miniso"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ​Concord Police Department - NC ( Phase 2 ) (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossi