{"job":{"id":19984620,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"OHO Connect","title":"Experienced Telecom / VoIP Technician Requested","description":{"html":"<p>Need tech onsite to troubleshoot remote access and guest room phone.</p><p><strong>Do NOT take FN work order to site, use attached PDF work order. Assigned tech should be the tech onsite unless you have prior approval; substituting a tech may result in $0 paid.</strong></p><p>Requesting technician experienced with Telecom and Voice/Data Cabling troubleshooting to go onsite and determine cause of customer complaint. Diagnose and repair to restore service on same trip, if possible. If parts are required, work with tech support to complete the order.&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Required Tools/Materials:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Bulk CAT5 cable on hand in case a cable run is required (reimbursed per-ft.)</li><li>Laptop with working serial Com port (can be USB to serial)</li><li>WINDOWS Laptop must have serial emulation program either Putty, HyperTerminal, similar</li><li>RS232 DB25&nbsp;serial Loop back tester</li><li>RS232 DB25 and DB8 Null Modem adapters</li><li>Straight thru RS232 DB25 and DB9&nbsp;serial cables</li><li>RS232 gender changers, Null modem adapters,&nbsp;serial adapters, and any miscellaneous connectors/terminations</li><li>Telephone tools required to repair and troubleshoot dial tone or cable pair issues</li><li>Electronic Multi-Meter</li><li>Butt Set</li><li>Basic Telephony Tools</li><li>Basic Hand Tools</li><li>Fox &amp; Hound (Toner and Wand)</li><li>Punch Down Tools (66 &amp; 110 block sets)</li><li>Misc. Telecom Terminators &amp; Cable</li><li>Ladder 6-8ft.</li><li>Digital Camera</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>** Please review \"Important Instructions\" section prior to going onsite **</strong></p><p><strong> **IMPORTANT INSTRUCTIONS**</strong></p><ul><li>At <u>NO</u>&nbsp;time are you to mention Field Nation or present any Field Nation documents to the client</li><li>You are to represent yourself as \"A Technician for Cloud 5\" while onsite</li><li>There should be no discussion of rates with the client; direct all payment questions to One Hour Onsite or service@ohoconnect.com</li><li>Signed work order with a release code is a required deliverable</li><li>Site Survey Form is a required deliverable (if attached)</li><li>If parts are required or you are unable to repair the unit on this visit, Service must be notified at the above contact numbers&nbsp;<u>BEFORE YOU LEAVE SITE</u>.&nbsp;</li><li>Work order close-out notes, part numbers for any parts required, and all deliverables are&nbsp;<strong>due within 24 hours</strong>&nbsp;of service visit</li><li>If out of scope work is encountered, Service must be notified immediately - No spend limit increases will be approved without prior consent.</li><li>If a quote for additional work is requested by the client you are to notify One Hour Onsite immediately to follow-up. <strong>Onsite Technicians will not provide quotations</strong> to the client under any circumstances.</li><li>By accepting a work order to perform a survey or prepare a quote you are agreeing to return and complete the work at the cost proposed. Quotes alone will not be accepted and the work order will be cancelled.</li><li>If the client attempts to schedule a return visit with you directly you are to notify One Hour Onsite immediately to follow-up. <strong>Onsite Technicians will not schedule service visits</strong> with the client under any circumstances.</li><li>Trip Charges, Tolls, Parking fees, etc. must be approved&nbsp;<u>prior</u>&nbsp;to work order acceptance. Spend Limit Increases for unapproved fees will be denied and $0 paid</li><li>If you fail to follow these instructions, your work order may be cancelled and $0 paid</li><li>If you arrive onsite unprepared for the scope of work either without the required experience/skill set or the required tools, your work order may be cancelled and $0 paid</li><li>•If any person other than the assigned technician goes onsite, your work order may be cancelled and $0 paid. We are NOT required to accept a technician swap. If a swap is not accepted, the assigned tech MUST be onsite.</li><li>By accepting this work order you are agreeing to a 30 day workmanship guarantee for any services performed</li></ul>","markdown":"Need tech onsite to troubleshoot remote access and guest room phone.\n\n**Do NOT take FN work order to site, use attached PDF work order. Assigned tech should be the tech onsite unless you have prior approval; substituting a tech may result in $0 paid.**\n\nRequesting technician experienced with Telecom and Voice/Data Cabling troubleshooting to go onsite and determine cause of customer complaint. Diagnose and repair to restore service on same trip, if possible. If parts are required, work with tech support to complete the order.\n\n**Required Tools/Materials:**\n\n- Bulk CAT5 cable on hand in case a cable run is required (reimbursed per-ft.)\n- Laptop with working serial Com port (can be USB to serial)\n- WINDOWS Laptop must have serial emulation program either Putty, HyperTerminal, similar\n- RS232 DB25 serial Loop back tester\n- RS232 DB25 and DB8 Null Modem adapters\n- Straight thru RS232 DB25 and DB9 serial cables\n- RS232 gender changers, Null modem adapters, serial adapters, and any miscellaneous connectors/terminations\n- Telephone tools required to repair and troubleshoot dial tone or cable pair issues\n- Electronic Multi-Meter\n- Butt Set\n- Basic Telephony Tools\n- Basic Hand Tools\n- Fox & Hound (Toner and Wand)\n- Punch Down Tools (66 & 110 block sets)\n- Misc. Telecom Terminators & Cable\n- Ladder 6-8ft.\n- Digital Camera\n\n**\\*\\* Please review \"Important Instructions\" section prior to going onsite \\*\\***\n\n **\\*\\*IMPORTANT INSTRUCTIONS\\*\\***\n\n- At NO time are you to mention Field Nation or present any Field Nation documents to the client\n- You are to represent yourself as \"A Technician for Cloud 5\" while onsite\n- There should be no discussion of rates with the client; direct all payment questions to One Hour Onsite or service@ohoconnect.com\n- Signed work order with a release code is a required deliverable\n- Site Survey Form is a required deliverable (if attached)\n- If parts are required or you are unable to repair the unit on this visit, Service must be notified at the above contact numbers BEFORE YOU LEAVE SITE.\n- Work order close-out notes, part numbers for any parts required, and all deliverables are **due within 24 hours** of service visit\n- If out of scope work is encountered, Service must be notified immediately - No spend limit increases will be approved without prior consent.\n- If a quote for additional work is requested by the client you are to notify One Hour Onsite immediately to follow-up. **Onsite Technicians will not provide quotations** to the client under any circumstances.\n- By accepting a work order to perform a survey or prepare a quote you are agreeing to return and complete the work at the cost proposed. Quotes alone will not be accepted and the work order will be cancelled.\n- If the client attempts to schedule a return visit with you directly you are to notify One Hour Onsite immediately to follow-up. **Onsite Technicians will not schedule service visits** with the client under any circumstances.\n- Trip Charges, Tolls, Parking fees, etc. must be approved prior to work order acceptance. Spend Limit Increases for unapproved fees will be denied and $0 paid\n- If you fail to follow these instructions, your work order may be cancelled and $0 paid\n- If you arrive onsite unprepared for the scope of work either without the required experience/skill set or the required tools, your work order may be cancelled and $0 paid\n- •If any person other than the assigned technician goes onsite, your work order may be cancelled and $0 paid. We are NOT required to accept a technician swap. If a swap is not accepted, the assigned tech MUST be onsite.\n- By accepting this work order you are agreeing to a 30 day workmanship guarantee for any services performed","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-21T09:00","end":"2026-09-21T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":83},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":1.5,"distance":58},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $83 (countered: $90) is below minimum threshold $400"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Busy"},{"start":"2026-09-22T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"gap"},{"start":"2026-09-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Miniso"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ​Concord Police Department - NC ( Phase 2 ) (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00: