{"job":{"id":19979009,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"VEHTECH, INC","title":"WASHER REPAIR","description":{"html":"<ol>\n<li>TECHNICIAN NEEDED TO REPAIR WASHER <strong>{PARTS ONSITE WITH CUSTOMER. NOTE: TECHNICIAN MUST INSTALL ALL PARTS ON SITE SHIPPED BY VENDOR.}</strong></li>\n<li><strong>&nbsp;<u>TECH MUST CHECK IN ARRIVAL NO CHECK IN NO PAY 7707882032. TAKE PICTURES OF THE UNIT BEFORE AND AFTER THE REPAIRS AND THE WORK SPACE THESE PICTURES ARE MANDATORY. THE SIGN OFF SHEET MUST BE SIGNED AND UPLOADED TO MARK WORK ORDER COMPLETE FOR PAYMENT TO BE APPROVED.</u></strong></li>\n<li><strong><em>MUST REPRESENT YOURSELF AS A VEHTECH, INC. TECHNICIAN. CALL AND INTRODUCE YOURSELF AS A VEHTECH TECHNICIAN CONFIRM THE APPOINTMENT TIME AND DATE. ESPECIALLY IF YOU HAVE REQUESTED TO COUNTER WITH A DIFFERENT DATE. THIS IS MANDATORY AS PART OF YOUR CHECK IN TASK.</em></strong></li>\n<li><strong>Effective today July 20, 2021 new policy mandatory for all Vehtechnology technicians. Technicians must call the customer one hour before arriving on site, this is and has always been our policy. If you arrive at a customer's home and did not provide a courtesy call before arriving and the customer is not home you WILL NOT BE PAID FOR TRAVEL for this ticket. If you have an instance where you have contacted the customer and no response immediately contact myself or Vincent via text message or phone call, no exceptions.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>﻿<em>Technicians please check in via ext 1005, with your check in time and check out time. If I am unavailable leave me a voicemail with your check in and check out time and any other pertinent information related to your work order. I will return your voicemail at my earliest convenience. If the work order is completed over the weekend you will be contacted on the next business day.</em></strong> <em><u>Please be sure to take all parts with you the customer is not responsible for returning the parts it is part of your work order completion to receive payment approval NO EXCEPTIONS.</u></em></li>\n<li><u>﻿</u><strong>No technician will be permitted to work while under the influence of any legal or illegal substance (i.e. marijuana, alcohol, stimulants or narcotic substances) see additional information below:</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Prohibited Conduct</strong></p>\n<p>Technicians or subcontractors may not:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Report to assignments/ work or remain on duty while impaired by alcohol or drugs</li>\n<li>Possess, use, sell, or distribute illegal drugs on Company property or while conducting Vehtechnology business.</li>\n<li>Misuse legally prescribed or over-the-counter medication in a way that impairs job performance or safety.</li>\n<li>Consume alcohol during work hours.</li>\n<li>This policy applies to all employees, contractors, temporary workers, and interns, while on working on Vehtechnology Assignments or contracted work through Field Nation any premises, conducting Vehtechnology business residential or commercial sites.</li>\n<li>Technicians taking medication that may impair job performance, alertness, or coordination should inform work order Manager to determine if you are permitted to proceed with work order.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Testing</p>\n<p>The Company may conduct drug and/or alcohol testing under the following circumstances, in accordance with applicable state law:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Reasonable suspicion:</strong> When a Customer or Vendor reports or documents specific, objective signs of impairment. If you a customer believes that you are under the influence of drugs or alcohol you will be asked to leave the site and you will not be paid for this assignment. Field Nation will be notified and an investigation immediately will determine if you will be compensated for travel or work.</li>\n<li><strong>Post-accident:</strong> Following a workplace accident meeting the threshold defined by the Company (e.g., resulting in injury requiring medical treatment or significant property damage)</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li><br /></li>\n<li><br /></li>\n</ol>\n<p><br /></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>WASHER REPAIR</strong></li>\n<li><strong>MAKE:</strong> Maytag</li>\n<li><strong>MODEL:</strong>MVW4505MW</li>\n<li><strong>PROBLEM DESCRIPTION:</strong>CX STATED THAT SHE START A CYCLE THEN NOW SHE IS UNABLE TO OPEN THE WASHER DOOR AND ALL THE LIGHTS ARE BLINKING.</li>\n<li><strong>PARTS SENT:</strong>Part Number: W11626074 Part Description: CNTRL-ELEC Quantity: 1 If used during repair, requires return: Yes Part Number: W11399437 Part Description: WASHER DRAIN PUMP Quantity: 1 If used during repair, requires return: DURING REPAIR: 1. Only replace parts needed for the repair. 2. Diagnose issue &amp; if parts sent don''t resolve the issue, please put the original parts back in the unit and back in original condition. 3. Take all parts sent to the customer with you upon leaving. Do not leave ANYTHING with the customer.</li>\n<li><strong>﻿<u>IF THE PARTS ARE NOT ON SITE PLEASE RUN THE CALL AS A TROUBLE SHOOTING AND DIAGNOSTICS. TAKE PICS OF THE MODEL AND SERIAL AND WRITE A SUMMARY OF THE PROBLEM DESCRIPTION AND THE POSSIBLE PARTS NEEDED TO REPAIR THE UNIT.</u></strong></li>\n<li><strong>PICTURES</strong>: <strong>TAKE PICTURES OF THE HOUSE, AND THE UNIT IN THIS INSTANCE FOR VERIFICATION OF YOUR ARRIVAL AND DEPARTURE.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>TAKE PICTURES OF THE UNIT BEFORE THE REPAIRS AND AFTER TO COVER YOURSELF AND THE COMPANY FROM ANY LIABILITY!</strong></li>\n<li><strong>PARTS&nbsp;WILL BE&nbsp;ONSITE FOR REPAIRS AND INSTALLATIONS.&nbsp;</strong></li>\n<li><strong>PLEASE PRESENT YOURSELF AS A VEHTECH,INC REP. &amp; PLEASE PRESENT YOURSELF IN&nbsp;A PROFESSIONAL MANNER.</strong></li>\n<li>&nbsp;<strong>CALL 770-788-2032 - UPON SITE Arrival for check in.</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;IF NO ANSWER LEAVE VOICEMAIL WITH CHECK IN TIME AND CHECK OUT.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<ul>\n<li>&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>TAKE PARTS WITH YOU. MUST BE RETURNED TO VEHTECH!!!!&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\n<li><strong>&nbsp;cores/ parts must be returned to VEHTECH, INC before assignments are paid.</strong></li>\n<li><strong><u>Please request a return label from the office at 770/788/2032.</u></strong></li>\n<li><strong>&nbsp;Vehtech, INC. requires detailed work descriptions for the scope of work performed during repairs.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Please include the following : Before and After pictures of the unit showing findings as related to problem description.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Pictures of the Serial #, Model #, as well as any parts that need replacing include the part numbers as well.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Upload these findings at once after completing the assignment.</strong></li>\n</ul>","markdown":"1. TECHNICIAN NEEDED TO REPAIR WASHER **{PARTS ONSITE WITH CUSTOMER. NOTE: TECHNICIAN MUST INSTALL ALL PARTS ON SITE SHIPPED BY VENDOR.}**\n2. **TECH MUST CHECK IN ARRIVAL NO CHECK IN NO PAY 7707882032. TAKE PICTURES OF THE UNIT BEFORE AND AFTER THE REPAIRS AND THE WORK SPACE THESE PICTURES ARE MANDATORY. THE SIGN OFF SHEET MUST BE SIGNED AND UPLOADED TO MARK WORK ORDER COMPLETE FOR PAYMENT TO BE APPROVED.**\n3. ***MUST REPRESENT YOURSELF AS A VEHTECH, INC. TECHNICIAN. CALL AND INTRODUCE YOURSELF AS A VEHTECH TECHNICIAN CONFIRM THE APPOINTMENT TIME AND DATE. ESPECIALLY IF YOU HAVE REQUESTED TO COUNTER WITH A DIFFERENT DATE. THIS IS MANDATORY AS PART OF YOUR CHECK IN TASK.***\n4. **Effective today July 20, 2021 new policy mandatory for all Vehtechnology technicians. Technicians must call the customer one hour before arriving on site, this is and has always been our policy. If you arrive at a customer's home and did not provide a courtesy call before arriving and the customer is not home you WILL NOT BE PAID FOR TRAVEL for this ticket. If you have an instance where you have contacted the customer and no response immediately contact myself or Vincent via text message or phone call, no exceptions.**\n5. **﻿*Technicians please check in via ext 1005, with your check in time and check out time. If I am unavailable leave me a voicemail with your check in and check out time and any other pertinent information related to your work order. I will return your voicemail at my earliest convenience. If the work order is completed over the weekend you will be contacted on the next business day.*** *Please be sure to take all parts with you the customer is not responsible for returning the parts it is part of your work order completion to receive payment approval NO EXCEPTIONS.*\n6. ﻿**No technician will be permitted to work while under the influence of any legal or illegal substance (i.e. marijuana, alcohol, stimulants or narcotic substances) see additional information below:**\n\n**Prohibited Conduct**\n\nTechnicians or subcontractors may not:\n\n- Report to assignments/ work or remain on duty while impaired by alcohol or drugs\n- Possess, use, sell, or distribute illegal drugs on Company property or while conducting Vehtechnology business.\n- Misuse legally prescribed or over-the-counter medication in a way that impairs job performance or safety.\n- Consume alcohol during work hours.\n- This policy applies to all employees, contractors, temporary workers, and interns, while on working on Vehtechnology Assignments or contracted work through Field Nation any premises, conducting Vehtechnology business residential or commercial sites.\n- Technicians taking medication that may impair job performance, alertness, or coordination should inform work order Manager to determine if you are permitted to proceed with work order.\n\nTesting\n\nThe Company may conduct drug and/or alcohol testing under the following circumstances, in accordance with applicable state law:\n\n- **Reasonable suspicion:** When a Customer or Vendor reports or documents specific, objective signs of impairment. If you a customer believes that you are under the influence of drugs or alcohol you will be asked to leave the site and you will not be paid for this assignment. Field Nation will be notified and an investigation immediately will determine if you will be compensated for travel or work.\n- **Post-accident:** Following a workplace accident meeting the threshold defined by the Company (e.g., resulting in injury requiring medical treatment or significant property damage)\n\n1. \n2. \n\n- **WASHER REPAIR**\n- **MAKE:** Maytag\n- **MODEL:**MVW4505MW\n- **PROBLEM DESCRIPTION:**CX STATED THAT SHE START A CYCLE THEN NOW SHE IS UNABLE TO OPEN THE WASHER DOOR AND ALL THE LIGHTS ARE BLINKING.\n- **PARTS SENT:**Part Number: W11626074 Part Description: CNTRL-ELEC Quantity: 1 If used during repair, requires return: Yes Part Number: W11399437 Part Description: WASHER DRAIN PUMP Quantity: 1 If used during repair, requires return: DURING REPAIR: 1. Only replace parts needed for the repair. 2. Diagnose issue & if parts sent don''t resolve the issue, please put the original parts back in the unit and back in original condition. 3. Take all parts sent to the customer with you upon leaving. Do not leave ANYTHING with the customer.\n- **﻿IF THE PARTS ARE NOT ON SITE PLEASE RUN THE CALL AS A TROUBLE SHOOTING AND DIAGNOSTICS. TAKE PICS OF THE MODEL AND SERIAL AND WRITE A SUMMARY OF THE PROBLEM DESCRIPTION AND THE POSSIBLE PARTS NEEDED TO REPAIR THE UNIT.**\n- **PICTURES**: **TAKE PICTURES OF THE HOUSE, AND THE UNIT IN THIS INSTANCE FOR VERIFICATION OF YOUR ARRIVAL AND DEPARTURE.**\n- **TAKE PICTURES OF THE UNIT BEFORE THE REPAIRS AND AFTER TO COVER YOURSELF AND THE COMPANY FROM ANY LIABILITY!**\n- **PARTS WILL BE ONSITE FOR REPAIRS AND INSTALLATIONS.**\n- **PLEASE PRESENT YOURSELF AS A VEHTECH,INC REP. & PLEASE PRESENT YOURSELF IN A PROFESSIONAL MANNER.**\n- **CALL 770-788-2032 - UPON SITE Arrival for check in.** IF NO ANSWER LEAVE VOICEMAIL WITH CHECK IN TIME AND CHECK OUT.\n\n- **TAKE PARTS WITH YOU. MUST BE RETURNED TO VEHTECH!!!!**\n- **cores/ parts must be returned to VEHTECH, INC before assignments are paid.**\n- **Please request a return label from the office at 770/788/2032.**\n- **Vehtech, INC. requires detailed work descriptions for the scope of work performed during repairs.**\n- **Please include the following : Before and After pictures of the unit showing findings as related to problem description.**\n- **Pictures of the Serial #, Model #, as well as any parts that need replacing include the part numbers as well.**\n- **Upload these findings at once after completing the assignment.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-21T08:00","end":"2026-09-21T10:00","latestStart":"2026-09-21T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":58},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 is below minimum threshold $400"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Busy"},{"start":"2026-09-22T18:00:00.000Z