{"job":{"id":19978640,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"CommandLink","title":"Connect Broadband Circuit to Router","description":{"html":"<p><strong style=\"color: red;\">PLEASE BE EARLY OR ON TIME&nbsp;</strong><strong>(no more than 15 minutes ahead of start time)</strong></p><p><strong>Please bring assorted patch cables up to and including 30 ft in length - preferably CAT6 but at least CAT5</strong></p><p><strong>Connect Broadband Circuit to Cradlepoint</strong></p><p>Service</p><p>Bandwidth|Link 500M/20M Broadband Internet (Spectrum)</p><p>Circuit ID</p><p>8349120112627053</p><p>Access Provider Circuit ID</p><p><br></p><p>Carrier Modem Make/Model/Mac Address</p><p>Wireless MAC: 0833edd9f9c3</p><p>Wireless Make: Askey</p><p>Wireless Model: sax1v1k</p><p>| Data Mac: 94f7be4474c0</p><p>Data Make: Sercomm</p><p>Data Model: ES2251</p><p>DeMarc Location</p><p><br></p><p>Hand Off Type</p><p>Copper/Electrical/RJ45</p><p>Network Information <strong style=\"color: white;\">Public</strong></p><p>IP Address Block: 96.10.213.40/29</p><p>Gateway: 96.10.213.41</p><p>Usable IP Range: 96.10.213.42 - 96.10.213.46</p><p>Subnet Mask: 255.255.255.248</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">Document existing/legacy modem and take pictures.&nbsp;Trace the Cradlepoint WAN port and determine what's providing internet today.&nbsp;Take a picture of both the device and the MAC address sticker and upload them to FN platform.&nbsp;(OR NOTE NO LEGACY CKT)</strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>Field Tech Instructions/Required Deliverables to be paid:</strong></p><p><strong>You have a hard start at 8 am local. If you need to arrive early to park, find the restaurant, ETC please do.</strong></p><p><strong>Perform the scope of work below exactly as it is written. The purpose of the scope of work is to connect the newly installed circuit listed above to the customer’s cradlepoint router. Do not interact with any other devices on site.</strong></p><p><strong>You must bring the following items to qualify for this work order:</strong></p><p><strong>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Toner and wand</strong></p><p><strong>2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Laptop with Ethernet port</strong></p><p><strong>3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Ladder</strong></p><p><strong>SCOPE OF WORK</strong></p><ol><li>Enable GPS when en route to site for ETA.</li><li>Upon arrival, check in with Dispatch via phone at 385-533-9167 &amp; obtain Check In Code</li><li>Touch base with the onsite contact - <strong>&lt;</strong>Wendy White 469-663-4979<strong>&gt;</strong></li><li>Take “before” pictures of the network cabinet in the manager’s office.</li><li>Locate the circuit listed above. Connect your laptop and confirm you can browse the internet from the circuit.</li><li>Perform a speed test and screenshot the result.</li><li>Test the IP’s and screenshot the result.</li><li>Locate the cradlepoint above the doorway in the manager’s office. Tone out to find the cable going from the WAN port on the cradlepoint to the IT cabinet above the manager’s desk (across the room). Find the other end of the cable</li><li>If the other end of the cable is plugged into anything, <strong>stop</strong> and call dispatch coordinator at 385-533-9167 and <strong>await further instructions</strong></li><li>If the other end of the cable is <strong>not</strong> plugged into anything, plug it into the broadband modem in the manager’s office that you tested. Use the MAC ID listed at the top of this work order to confirm you are plugging into the correct device. Call dispatch coordinator at 385-533-9167 and notify.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If there is no cable plugged into the WAN port of the cradlepoint, check above the dropped ceiling tile to see if there is a cable coiled above the ceiling. Plug 1 end into the WAN port of the cradlepoint and safely route the other end over the ceiling and behind the IT cabinet above the manager’s desk. P the other end into the broadband modem in the manager’s office that you tested. Call dispatch coordinator at 385-533-9167 and notify.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If there is no cable plugged into the WAN port of the cradlepoint and no cable coiled above the dropped ceiling tile that you can find, run a new cable safely above the dropped ceiling and behind the IT cabinet above the manager’s desk. Plug it into the new modem and call dispatch coordinator at 385-533-9167 to notify.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If you cannot find a way to safely run a new cable, complete a site survey for the labor and materials to return and safely run the new cable.</li><li>Check if WIFI light is lit on the broadband modem and let dispatch coordinator know at 385-533-9167 if so.</li><li>Complete cable management.</li><li>Take “after” pictures of the IT cabinet in the manager’s office.</li><li>Check out with dispatch coordinator at 385-533-9167 and get checkout code.</li></ol>","markdown":"**PLEASE BE EARLY OR ON TIME** **(no more than 15 minutes ahead of start time)**\n\n**Please bring assorted patch cables up to and including 30 ft in length - preferably CAT6 but at least CAT5**\n\n**Connect Broadband Circuit to Cradlepoint**\n\nService\n\nBandwidth|Link 500M/20M Broadband Internet (Spectrum)\n\nCircuit ID\n\n8349120112627053\n\nAccess Provider Circuit ID\n\nCarrier Modem Make/Model/Mac Address\n\nWireless MAC: 0833edd9f9c3\n\nWireless Make: Askey\n\nWireless Model: sax1v1k\n\n| Data Mac: 94f7be4474c0\n\nData Make: Sercomm\n\nData Model: ES2251\n\nDeMarc Location\n\nHand Off Type\n\nCopper/Electrical/RJ45\n\nNetwork Information **Public**\n\nIP Address Block: 96.10.213.40/29\n\nGateway: 96.10.213.41\n\nUsable IP Range: 96.10.213.42 - 96.10.213.46\n\nSubnet Mask: 255.255.255.248\n\n**Document existing/legacy modem and take pictures. Trace the Cradlepoint WAN port and determine what's providing internet today. Take a picture of both the device and the MAC address sticker and upload them to FN platform. (OR NOTE NO LEGACY CKT)**\n\n**Field Tech Instructions/Required Deliverables to be paid:**\n\n**You have a hard start at 8 am local. If you need to arrive early to park, find the restaurant, ETC please do.**\n\n**Perform the scope of work below exactly as it is written. The purpose of the scope of work is to connect the newly installed circuit listed above to the customer’s cradlepoint router. Do not interact with any other devices on site.**\n\n**You must bring the following items to qualify for this work order:**\n\n**1. Toner and wand**\n\n**2. Laptop with Ethernet port**\n\n**3. Ladder**\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK**\n\n1. Enable GPS when en route to site for ETA.\n2. Upon arrival, check in with Dispatch via phone at 385-533-9167 & obtain Check In Code\n3. Touch base with the onsite contact - **<**Wendy White 469-663-4979**>**\n4. Take “before” pictures of the network cabinet in the manager’s office.\n5. Locate the circuit listed above. Connect your laptop and confirm you can browse the internet from the circuit.\n6. Perform a speed test and screenshot the result.\n7. Test the IP’s and screenshot the result.\n8. Locate the cradlepoint above the doorway in the manager’s office. Tone out to find the cable going from the WAN port on the cradlepoint to the IT cabinet above the manager’s desk (across the room). Find the other end of the cable\n9. If the other end of the cable is plugged into anything, **stop** and call dispatch coordinator at 385-533-9167 and **await further instructions**\n10. If the other end of the cable is **not** plugged into anything, plug it into the broadband modem in the manager’s office that you tested. Use the MAC ID listed at the top of this work order to confirm you are plugging into the correct device. Call dispatch coordinator at 385-533-9167 and notify.\n11. If there is no cable plugged into the WAN port of the cradlepoint, check above the dropped ceiling tile to see if there is a cable coiled above the ceiling. Plug 1 end into the WAN port of the cradlepoint and safely route the other end over the ceiling and behind the IT cabinet above the manager’s desk. P the other end into the broadband modem in the manager’s office that you tested. Call dispatch coordinator at 385-533-9167 and notify.\n12. If there is no cable plugged into the WAN port of the cradlepoint and no cable coiled above the dropped ceiling tile that you can find, run a new cable safely above the dropped ceiling and behind the IT cabinet above the manager’s desk. Plug it into the new modem and call dispatch coordinator at 385-533-9167 to notify.\n13. If you cannot find a way to safely run a new cable, complete a site survey for the labor and materials to return and safely run the new cable.\n14. Check if WIFI light is lit on the broadband modem and let dispatch coordinator know at 385-533-9167 if so.\n15. Complete cable management.\n16. Take “after” pictures of the IT cabinet in the manager’s office.\n17. Check out with dispatch coordinator at 385-533-9167 and get checkout code.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-21T08:00","end":"2026-09-21T10:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":150},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":75,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":57},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $150 (countered: $150) is below minimum threshold $400"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Busy"},{"start":"2026-09-22T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"gap"},{"start":"2026-09-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T03:00:00.000Z"