{"job":{"id":19978421,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Essintial","title":"FIRM START | QSIC Pendant Speaker Installation [Tech 1 / Lead Tech]","description":{"html":"<p><b>No unauthorized persons allowed on site. Any swaps or helpers must be approved by Essintial.</b></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\"><u>IMPORTANT:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong><u>You MUST represent yourself as a QSIC Technician</u></strong></li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">Important</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">: Technicians&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">MUST</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;read the&nbsp;</span><u style=\"color: black;\">entire work order and all provided documentation</u><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">before</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;arriving on-site. All guides and plans&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">MUST</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;be printed and/or available on a laptop or tablet (not a phone) for review onsite</span></li><li><strong style=\"color: black;\">Dress Code: Professional work dress code</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;is mandatory: Technicians should present a clean, professional appearance. A plain polo / collared / or button-down shirt, slacks / durable work pants (no shorts), and nice shoes / steel- or composite-toe slip-resistant shoes or boots.&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">Not allowed</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">: T‑shirts, hoodies, graphics, holes, or stained clothing.</span></li><li>These are live environments, technicians must act in a professional manner, taking care not to disrupt business.</li><li><strong>Penalties Apply IF you do not</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">PRINT and Take with you to the site the LOA-Letter of Authorization!!!!!</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Do Not Call&nbsp;<strong>Essintial Project Technical Support @&nbsp;717-610-3070</strong>&nbsp;if you are exceeding&nbsp;<strong>4 Hours Onsite</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Submit the Essintial Online Deliverable and Check-Out / Gain Approval Deliverable Approval from Essintial Project Technical Support Team BEFORE leaving the site</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Techs&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;Check-Out and Place your WORK ORDER in a WORKDONE STATUS BEFORE leaving the site</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><u>Required Skills:</u></strong>&nbsp;Technicians should have experience in installing and mounting speakers as well as running, terminating, and testing cables. Technicians also need to have Audio Visual skills as well</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work Overview:</u></strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>&nbsp;<strong><u>Scope of Work:</u></strong>&nbsp;Technician needed onsite to install QTY of 8 <span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">“Pendant Speakers” by mounting to the ceiling.</span> <span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Technician will install, configure, and test/validate the QSIC audio system within Dollar General locations. Techs will be responsible for speaker placement, AVA installation and back of house equipment setup. Technicians must verify all materials, install speakers per floor plans set to 70V–15W and complete all cabling in a clean and professional manner. Proper routing, labeling and concealed runs are to be preformed while ensuring all equipment is securely wall-mounted and networked using designated ports. The system must be fully tested confirming audio playback across all speakers, proper AVA functionality and the AVA microphone installed above the checkout area. Final completion requires submission of all required photos, validation through HQ Admin and live volume adjustment with store personnel are required for final sign off approval.</span></li><li><strong><u>Technicians MUST refer to and follow instructions called out in the Onsite Installation Guide –</u></strong>&nbsp;any questions or issues need to be escalated to the&nbsp;<strong style=\"color: black;\">Essintial Project Technical Support @&nbsp;717-610-3070</strong></li><li>Techs <strong>MUST</strong> PRINT and Take with you to the site the LOA-Letter of Authorization!!!!! Penalties could apply!</li><li><strong><u>Techs&nbsp;</u>MUST</strong>&nbsp;stay out of unauthorized areas and note that every location is monitored. Please dress and act accordingly.</li><li>Technicians (Tech 1/Lead &amp; Assist)&nbsp;<strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;complete the Essintial Online Deliverable – Please Note the Tech 1 / Lead Tech will be responsible for capturing/submitting onsite deliverable photos/forms.</li><li><strong>Please Note there will be Multiple Technicians Onsite to complete the scope of work&nbsp;</strong>-<strong>One tech will be designated as a Lead Tech</strong>&nbsp;and the other technician will be designated as an&nbsp;<strong>Assist Tech, your WORK ORDER TITLE WILL CALL OUT IF YOU ARE LEAD or ASSIST</strong>.&nbsp;</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Communication Requirements</u></strong></p><ul><li>ALL installation questions must go to&nbsp;<strong style=\"color: black;\">Essintial Project Technical Support @&nbsp;717-610-3070</strong></li><li><strong><u>Tech&nbsp;</u>MUST</strong>&nbsp;call&nbsp;<strong style=\"color: black;\">Essintial Project Technical Support @&nbsp;717-610-3070 if you will be exceeding 4 Hours Onsite – You MUST obtain approval!!!</strong></li><li>Technicians <strong>MUST</strong> Check-In and Check-Out with the <strong style=\"color: black;\">Essintial Project Technical Support @ 717-610-3070</strong></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Required Tools / Material:</u></strong></p><ul><li>6.5\" Hole Saw (shipped to site)</li><li>Cell Phone or other device that has a phone, camera, and internet ability (for online deliverable)</li><li>Laptop / tablet / phone with Wi-Fi</li><li>Standard Hand Tools</li><li>10Ft-12Ft Ladder</li><li>Drill with at least two batteries (both impact and non)</li><li>Long fiberglass push rods</li><li>wire strippers</li><li>Electrical Dykes</li><li>Utility Knife</li><li>Cat6 tester, crimping tools and connectors</li><li>Multi-meter&nbsp;- Capable of reading Ohms</li><li>Small Alan wrench – for pendant lock</li><li>Small Phillips and flat head screw driver</li><li>Micro flathead screwdriver</li><li>Laser Distance Measure &amp; Tape Measure</li><li>Velcro</li><li>Label maker</li><li>Government Issued ID</li><li>LOA – Letter of Authorization</li></ul><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Bill of Material:</u></strong>&nbsp;Refer to Onsite Installation Guide; any questions escalate to&nbsp;<strong style=\"color: black;\">Essintial Project Technical Support @&nbsp;717-610-3070</strong></p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;<strong><u>SCHEDULE:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>Start Times:</strong>&nbsp;FIRM START TIME!!!! YOU MUST ARRIVE AT ONTIME BASED ON THE START TIME SET BY ESSINTIAL. You are required to be onsite no later than your scheduled time (penalties will be applied if you are late). Please escalate to Essintial Projects @ 855-612-2183</li><li><strong>Estimated Duration:&nbsp;</strong>4 Hours, If you are approaching that time, you must contact&nbsp;<strong>Essintial Technical Support&nbsp;</strong>to gain approval. If you cannot start work immediately, please reach out to Essintial and gain guidance.</li><li>You will receive pre-calls 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will&nbsp;not&nbsp;be granted.</li><li>You will not be paid for work performed prior to your work order’s scheduled start time. Please contact Essintial if the customer is asking you to deviate from this service date or time.</li><li>If you must remove yourself from this project, you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to be&nbsp;<strong>REMOVED&nbsp;</strong>and&nbsp;<strong><em>REMOVE YOURSELF&nbsp;</em></strong>from the work order.</li><li>&nbsp;This WO only covers ONE visit to site. If a customer requires a return visit, you MUST be assigned another WO by Essintial. Time logged for additional days onsite will be rejected for not following process.&nbsp;</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Pre-Site Requirements:</strong></p><ul><li><strong><u>Download and then Print</u>&nbsp;all relevant attachments (guides and checklists) in color to bring to the site.</strong>&nbsp;Please review all attachments prior to arriving onsite.&nbsp;<strong style=\"color: rgb(247, 10, 10);\"><em><u>Important Note:&nbsp;</u></em></strong>These Links will take you to / show you a&nbsp;<strong><u>PREVIEW</u></strong>&nbsp;of the document,&nbsp;<strong><em>IT IS VERY IMPORTANT</em></strong>&nbsp;that you&nbsp;<strong><em>DOWNLOAD</em></strong>&nbsp;the files from this view and then&nbsp;<strong>PRINT</strong>&nbsp;(<em>DO NOT PRINT FROM PREVIEW MODE</em>)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>LOA – Letter of Authorization -&nbsp;DG Media Network Audio System Installation</strong>&nbsp;<strong>Link [</strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">MUST BE PRINTED</strong><strong>]</strong>:&nbsp;https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004rk42/DWfTfK4eWhH6.idtwsbiv2oPzIZBbP.VLjiAt6hIisI</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Dollar General Installation Guide – 2026</strong>&nbsp;<strong>Link</strong>:&nbsp;https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004rk41/ED1SkYNAzCnYrokC3tVlbVa4ZHs4Qr_TyUc80z_oDYE</li><li>Confirm the start date and time. You will receive pre-calls at 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will not be granted.</li><li>Bring the Required Tools &amp; Material with you to the site</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>ARRIVAL:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>CHECK IN TO YOUR WORK ORDER</strong>–if you are unable to do so then you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.</li><li><strong>CHECK IN with Onsite POC / Manager: Introduce yourself as the QSIC Technician onsite for the Speaker Install Project, present the LOA and Verify Store Number</strong></li><li><strong>Call &amp; Check-In with</strong> the <strong style=\"color: black;\">Essintial Project Technical Support @ 717-610-3070</strong></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>ONSITE:</u></strong></p><ul><li>REFER TO and FOLLOW Instructions called out in the Onsite Installation Guide - Any questions escalate to&nbsp;<strong style=\"color: black;\">Essintial Project Technical Support @&nbsp;717-610-3070</strong></li><li><strong>Ensure you clean up after yourself and dispose of any trash</strong></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>CLOSING OUT | COMPLETE BEFORE LEAVING SITE:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Confirm device operation with Onsite POC</li><li><strong>Complete and Submit Online Deliverable</strong>&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">(Due back to Essintial PRIOR TO LEAVING SITE):</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tech will be asked to confirm site/location details</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tech will be asked to upload requested photos (Tech 1 / Lead Tech)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">You will be asked to enter closing/completion notes</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">You will be asked to obtain Manager/POC Signature</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tech will be asked to provide the confirmation code received upon completion of your online deliverables.</li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(29, 28, 29);\">Call &amp; Check-Out</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(29, 28, 29);\">&nbsp;with the&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">Essintial Project Technical Support @ 717-610-3070&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(29, 28, 29);\">to review/gain deliverable approval and perform your final check out</span></li><li><strong>Check-Out on your WO</strong>&nbsp;- if you are unable to do so then you&nbsp;<strong>MUST&nbsp;</strong>call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.&nbsp;<strong>NOTE</strong>: Your Check In and Check Out times must all match&nbsp;<em>(Work Order Platform and Final Check Out with Essintial)</em></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Closing / Completion Notes:</strong></p><ul><li>Did you complete the online deliverable? If so, please provide confirmation code</li><li>Provide DETAILED notes of the work that took place including any problems and resolutions steps taken</li><li>Provide DETAILED notes of any problems onsite that would have caused a delay over 4 hours<span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>ESCALATION:</u>&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>Support Related Questions and Any Issues onsite / Related to the scope of work should be escalated directly to the&nbsp;<strong style=\"color: black;\">Essintial Project Technical Support @&nbsp;717-610-3070</strong></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;<strong><u>Out of Scope Information</u>:</strong></p><ul><li>If you are asked to do anything onsite that is outside of the work scope on this work order or attached documents, please report to Essintial immediately for approval of additional/different scope.</li><li>If the instruction you are receiving onsite deviates from what is listed on your work order or attached documents, please report to Essintial immediately for approval of additional/different scope.</li><li>If the work onsite is about to go over the scoped/estimated time onsite, you MUST call Essintial immediately to provide the reason for going over that timeframe. You will also be required to provide this reason upon close out on your Online Deliverable.</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS:</u></strong>&nbsp;Must be able to bend, kneel, stand and lift, carry 50lbs repeatedly for extended periods of time.</p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\"><u>DRESS CODE:</u></strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">Professional work dress code</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;is mandatory: Technicians should present a clean, professional appearance. A plain polo / collared / or button-down shirt, slacks / durable work pants (no shorts), and nice shoes / steel- or composite-toe slip-resistant shoes or boots.&nbsp;</span><strong style=\"color: black;\">Not allowed</strong><span style=\"color: black;\">: T‑shirts, hoodies, graphics, holes, or stained clothing.</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:</strong></p><ul><li>All expenses such as tolls, parking, materials must be pre-approved and accompanied by a receipt. Reimbursements will not be increased to cover markups of any kind.</li><li>Technicians must contact Essintial for any deviations from the scheduled service date or time. No payment will be granted for work performed prior to the scheduled start time.</li></ul>","markdown":"**No unauthorized persons allowed on site. Any swaps or helpers must be approved by Essintial.**\n\n**IMPORTANT:**\n\n- **You MUST represent yourself as a QSIC Technician**\n- **Important**: Technicians **MUST** read the entire work order and all provided documentation **before** arriving on-site. All guides and plans **MUST** be printed and/or available on a laptop or tablet (not a phone) for review onsite\n- **Dress Code: Professional work dress code** is mandatory: Technicians should present a clean, professional appearance. A plain polo / collared / or button-down shirt, slacks / durable work pants (no shorts), and nice shoes / steel- or composite-toe slip-resistant shoes or boots. **Not allowed**: T‑shirts, hoodies, graphics, holes, or stained clothing.\n- These are live environments, technicians must act in a professional manner, taking care not to disrupt business.\n- **Penalties Apply IF you do not**\n- PRINT and Take with you to the site the LOA-Letter of Authorization!!!!!\n- Do Not Call **Essintial Project Technical Support @ 717-610-3070** if you are exceeding **4 Hours Onsite**\n- Submit the Essintial Online Deliverable and Check-Out / Gain Approval Deliverable Approval from Essintial Project Technical Support Team BEFORE leaving the site\n- Techs **MUST** Check-Out and Place your WORK ORDER in a WORKDONE STATUS BEFORE leaving the site\n\n**Required Skills:** Technicians should have experience in installing and mounting speakers as well as running, terminating, and testing cables. Technicians also need to have Audio Visual skills as well\n\n**Scope of Work Overview:**\n\n- **Scope of Work:** Technician needed onsite to install QTY of 8 “Pendant Speakers” by mounting to the ceiling. Technician will install, configure, and test/validate the QSIC audio system within Dollar General locations. Techs will be responsible for speaker placement, AVA installation and back of house equipment setup. Technicians must verify all materials, install speakers per floor plans set to 70V–15W and complete all cabling in a clean and professional manner. Proper routing, labeling and concealed runs are to be preformed while ensuring all equipment is securely wall-mounted and networked using designated ports. The system must be fully tested confirming audio playback across all speakers, proper AVA functionality and the AVA microphone installed above the checkout area. Final completion requires submission of all required photos, validation through HQ Admin and live volume adjustment with store personnel are required for final sign off approval.\n- **Technicians MUST refer to and follow instructions called out in the Onsite Installation Guide –** any questions or issues need to be escalated to the **Essintial Project Technical Support @ 717-610-3070**\n- Techs **MUST** PRINT and Take with you to the site the LOA-Letter of Authorization!!!!! Penalties could apply!\n- **Techs MUST** stay out of unauthorized areas and note that every location is monitored. Please dress and act accordingly.\n- Technicians (Tech 1/Lead & Assist) **MUST** complete the Essintial Online Deliverable – Please Note the Tech 1 / Lead Tech will be responsible for capturing/submitting onsite deliverable photos/forms.\n- **Please Note there will be Multiple Technicians Onsite to complete the scope of work** -**One tech will be designated as a Lead Tech** and the other technician will be designated as an **Assist Tech, your WORK ORDER TITLE WILL CALL OUT IF YOU ARE LEAD or ASSIST**.\n\n**Communication Requirements**\n\n- ALL installation questions must go to **Essintial Project Technical Support @ 717-610-3070**\n- **Tech MUST** call **Essintial Project Technical Support @ 717-610-3070 if you will be exceeding 4 Hours Onsite – You MUST obtain approval!!!**\n- Technicians **MUST** Check-In and Check-Out with the **Essintial Project Technical Support @ 717-610-3070**\n\n**Required Tools / Material:**\n\n- 6.5\" Hole Saw (shipped to site)\n- Cell Phone or other device that has a phone, camera, and internet ability (for online deliverable)\n- Laptop / tablet / phone with Wi-Fi\n- Standard Hand Tools\n- 10Ft-12Ft Ladder\n- Drill with at least two batteries (both impact and non)\n- Long fiberglass push rods\n- wire strippers\n- Electrical Dykes\n- Utility Knife\n- Cat6 tester, crimping tools and connectors\n- Multi-meter - Capable of reading Ohms\n- Small Alan wrench – for pendant lock\n- Small Phillips and flat head screw driver\n- Micro flathead screwdriver\n- Laser Distance Measure & Tape Measure\n- Velcro\n- Label maker\n- Government Issued ID\n- LOA – Letter of Authorization\n\n**Bill of Material:** Refer to Onsite Installation Guide; any questions escalate to **Essintial Project Technical Support @ 717-610-3070**\n\n **SCHEDULE:**\n\n- **Start Times:** FIRM START TIME!!!! YOU MUST ARRIVE AT ONTIME BASED ON THE START TIME SET BY ESSINTIAL. You are required to be onsite no later than your scheduled time (penalties will be applied if you are late). Please escalate to Essintial Projects @ 855-612-2183\n- **Estimated Duration:** 4 Hours, If you are approaching that time, you must contact **Essintial Technical Support** to gain approval. If you cannot start work immediately, please reach out to Essintial and gain guidance.\n- You will receive pre-calls 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will not be granted.\n- You will not be paid for work performed prior to your work order’s scheduled start time. Please contact Essintial if the customer is asking you to deviate from this service date or time.\n- If you must remove yourself from this project, you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to be **REMOVED** and ***REMOVE YOURSELF*** from the work order.\n- This WO only covers ONE visit to site. If a customer requires a return visit, you MUST be assigned another WO by Essintial. Time logged for additional days onsite will be rejected for not following process.\n\n**Pre-Site Requirements:**\n\n- **Download and then Print all relevant attachments (guides and checklists) in color to bring to the site.** Please review all attachments prior to arriving onsite. ***Important Note:*** These Links will take you to / show you a **PREVIEW** of the document, ***IT IS VERY IMPORTANT*** that you ***DOWNLOAD*** the files from this view and then **PRINT** (*DO NOT PRINT FROM PREVIEW MODE*)\n- **LOA – Letter of Authorization - DG Media Network Audio System Installation** **Link \\[****MUST BE PRINTED****\\]**: <https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004rk42/DWfTfK4eWhH6.idtwsbiv2oPzIZBbP.VLjiAt6hIisI>\n- **Dollar General Installation Guide – 2026** **Link**: https://essintial.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/300000000D47/a/Ua000004rk41/ED1SkYNAzCnYrokC3tVlbVa4ZHs4Qr_TyUc80z_oDYE\n- Confirm the start date and time. You will receive pre-calls at 24 hours and 2 hours prior to your ETA. If you do not answer or reply, you may lose the work as confirmation is a contractual obligation, and a cancellation fee will not be granted.\n- Bring the Required Tools & Material with you to the site\n\n**ARRIVAL:**\n\n- **CHECK IN TO YOUR WORK ORDER**–if you are unable to do so then you MUST call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in.\n- **CHECK IN with Onsite POC / Manager: Introduce yourself as the QSIC Technician onsite for the Speaker Install Project, present the LOA and Verify Store Number**\n- **Call & Check-In with** the **Essintial Project Technical Support @ 717-610-3070**\n\n**ONSITE:**\n\n- REFER TO and FOLLOW Instructions called out in the Onsite Installation Guide - Any questions escalate to **Essintial Project Technical Support @ 717-610-3070**\n- **Ensure you clean up after yourself and dispose of any trash**\n\n**CLOSING OUT | COMPLETE BEFORE LEAVING SITE:**\n\n- Confirm device operation with Onsite POC\n- **Complete and Submit Online Deliverable** (Due back to Essintial PRIOR TO LEAVING SITE):\n- Tech will be asked to confirm site/location details\n- Tech will be asked to upload requested photos (Tech 1 / Lead Tech)\n- You will be asked to enter closing/completion notes\n- You will be asked to obtain Manager/POC Signature\n- Tech will be asked to provide the confirmation code received upon completion of your online deliverables.\n- **Call & Check-Out** with the **Essintial Project Technical Support @ 717-610-3070** to review/gain deliverable approval and perform your final check out\n- **Check-Out on your WO** - if you are unable to do so then you **MUST** call Essintial @ 855-612-2183 to check in. **NOTE**: Your Check In and Check Out times must all match *(Work Order Platform and Final Check Out with Essintial)*\n\n**Closing / Completion Notes:**\n\n- Did you complete the online deliverable? If so, please provide confirmation code\n- Provide DETAILED notes of the work that took place including any problems and resolutions steps taken\n- Provide DETAILED notes of any problems onsite that would have caused a delay over 4 hours\n\n**ESCALATION:**\n\n- Support Related Questions and Any Issues onsite / Related to the scope of work should be escalated directly to the **Essintial Project Technical Support @ 717-610-3070**\n\n **Out of Scope Information:**\n\n- If you are asked to do anything onsite that is outside of the work scope on this work order or attached documents, please report to Essintial immediately for approval of additional/different scope.\n- If the instruction you are receiving onsite deviates from what is listed on your work order or attached documents, please report to Essintial immediately for approval of additional/different scope.\n- If the work onsite is about to go over the scoped/estimated time onsite, you MUST call Essintial immediately to provide the reason for going over that timeframe. You will also be required to provide this reason upon close out on your Online Deliverable.\n\n**PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS:** Must be able to bend, kneel, stand and lift, carry 50lbs repeatedly for extended periods of time.\n\n**DRESS CODE:** **Professional work dress code** is mandatory: Technicians should present a clean, professional appearance. A plain polo / collared / or button-down shirt, slacks / durable work pants (no shorts), and nice shoes / steel- or composite-toe slip-resistant shoes or boots. **Not allowed**: T‑shirts, hoodies, graphics, holes, or stained clothing.\n\n**Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy:**\n\n- All expenses such as tolls, parking, materials must be pre-approved and accompanied by a receipt. Reimbursements will not be increased to cover markups of any kind.\n- Technicians must contact Essintial for any deviations from the scheduled service date or time. No payment will be granted for work performed prior to the scheduled start time.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-15T08:00","end":"2026-10-15T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":160,"max":240},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":4,"amount":160},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":40}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":43},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $240 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-19T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-20T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ​Concord Police Department - NC ( Phase 2 ) (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #1523 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-22T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"Remote Hands - Connect AT&T broadband circuit"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789752167962}
{"job":{"id":19985973,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"NewBold Technologies","title":"Switch Refresh Installation (RETAIL STORE) - Lead Installer","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Switch refresh</strong></p><p><strong>Tech will be working with a Lead tech. Expectation is each tech is responsible for 6 switches each. Lead controls the work flow.</strong></p><p><strong>The purpose of this work order is to complete the replacement of switches within the site. A full runbook for the site will be provided in the documents section. Please review all information 1 week prior to site visit.</strong></p><p><strong>Please do not schedule another job for the morning after this work order. Any hours over estimate will be paid at an hourly rate.</strong></p><p><strong><u>REVIEW INSTALL GUIDE BEFORE ACCEPTING WO</u></strong></p><p><strong>&nbsp;A.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Read this guide in its entirety- Verify with Field PM</strong></p><p><strong>B.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Download MS Teams ( used for project bridge)</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>REQUIRED TOOLS:</u></strong></p><p><strong>A. Drill/Impact/Screwdrivers</strong></p><p><strong>B. Basic termination tools ( in case an AP comes up at less than gig)</strong></p><p><strong>C. Velcro/ Scissors</strong></p><p><strong>D. Label maker/ extra tape/ markers/Sharpies</strong></p><p><strong>E. MISC standard technician tool kit</strong></p><p><strong>F. Zip Ties</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>DAY OF:</u></strong></p><p><strong>A. You must arrive a Minimum of 30 minutes before close. Validate/check in with Field PM . This time is not flexible and you must be on site by the agreed upon time.</strong> <strong><u>FOR SWITCH SITES YOU MUST CALL IN TO TEAMS BEFORE POWERING ON EITHER STACK AFTER SWAP. THIS IS CRITICAL.</u></strong></p><p><strong>B. When you enter- you must have everything with you and enter once, you can not leave the building until everything is completed. So no breaks outside the building.</strong></p><p><strong>C. You must enter through the rear of the building at loading dock. There will be a keypad (referenced as HIRSCH keypad from hereout), Enter Hirsch code and enter the building</strong></p><p><strong>D. Enter Hirsch code and enter the building</strong></p><p><strong>E. After bringing in all of your items&nbsp;*ALL items* Locate the Lead Tech.&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>F. Verify with the MIC that end-of-day store activities are completed- ( This is usually 45-1hour after close)&nbsp;* can do BOH areas with permission from MIC</strong></p><p><strong>G. Determine the front of the store for installation purposes and verify inventory on site.</strong></p><p><strong>H. Please update PM that all inventory is on site and accounted for.</strong></p><p><strong>I. Contact Field PM to let them know Switches been replaced. Please let them know when finished so they can start health checks. This is key to begin health checks and directly affects how quickly your site is signed off and marked completed&nbsp;</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>COMPLETION CHECKLIST:</u></strong></p><p><strong>A. Ensure all areas are cleaned up</strong></p><p><strong>B. Ensure all switches are left stacked with SN facing out.</strong></p><p><strong>C. Ensure all Photos for switches for sites with replacements are uploaded</strong></p><p><strong>D. We need to verify the phones are back online. Procced to a phone- look at display- call your cell phone etc to verify online- (Take photo of phone with display visible). Must call from one in back area and one on sales floor.</strong></p><p><strong>E. Dispose of all trash properly. Tiles that were removed during install should be removed and leaned or stacked near garbage.</strong></p>","markdown":"**Switch refresh**\n\n**Tech will be working with a Lead tech. Expectation is each tech is responsible for 6 switches each. Lead controls the work flow.**\n\n**The purpose of this work order is to complete the replacement of switches within the site. A full runbook for the site will be provided in the documents section. Please review all information 1 week prior to site visit.**\n\n**Please do not schedule another job for the morning after this work order. Any hours over estimate will be paid at an hourly rate.**\n\n**REVIEW INSTALL GUIDE BEFORE ACCEPTING WO**\n\n **A. Read this guide in its entirety- Verify with Field PM**\n\n**B. Download MS Teams ( used for project bridge)**\n\n**REQUIRED TOOLS:**\n\n**A. Drill/Impact/Screwdrivers**\n\n**B. Basic termination tools ( in case an AP comes up at less than gig)**\n\n**C. Velcro/ Scissors**\n\n**D. Label maker/ extra tape/ markers/Sharpies**\n\n**E. MISC standard technician tool kit**\n\n**F. Zip Ties**\n\n**DAY OF:**\n\n**A. You must arrive a Minimum of 30 minutes before close. Validate/check in with Field PM . This time is not flexible and you must be on site by the agreed upon time.** **FOR SWITCH SITES YOU MUST CALL IN TO TEAMS BEFORE POWERING ON EITHER STACK AFTER SWAP. THIS IS CRITICAL.**\n\n**B. When you enter- you must have everything with you and enter once, you can not leave the building until everything is completed. So no breaks outside the building.**\n\n**C. You must enter through the rear of the building at loading dock. There will be a keypad (referenced as HIRSCH keypad from hereout), Enter Hirsch code and enter the building**\n\n**D. Enter Hirsch code and enter the building**\n\n**E. After bringing in all of your items \\*ALL items\\* Locate the Lead Tech.**\n\n**F. Verify with the MIC that end-of-day store activities are completed- ( This is usually 45-1hour after close) \\* can do BOH areas with permission from MIC**\n\n**G. Determine the front of the store for installation purposes and verify inventory on site.**\n\n**H. Please update PM that all inventory is on site and accounted for.**\n\n**I. Contact Field PM to let them know Switches been replaced. Please let them know when finished so they can start health checks. This is key to begin health checks and directly affects how quickly your site is signed off and marked completed**\n\n**COMPLETION CHECKLIST:**\n\n**A. Ensure all areas are cleaned up**\n\n**B. Ensure all switches are left stacked with SN facing out.**\n\n**C. Ensure all Photos for switches for sites with replacements are uploaded**\n\n**D. We need to verify the phones are back online. Procced to a phone- look at display- call your cell phone etc to verify online- (Take photo of phone with display visible). Must call from one in back area and one on sales floor.**\n\n**E. Dispose of all trash properly. Tiles that were removed during install should be removed and leaned or stacked near garbage.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-29T19:30","end":"2026-09-29T27:30"},"payRange":{"min":650,"max":650},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":8,"distance":11},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"fixed","counterRate":81,"baseAmount":650,"estHours":8,"travelExpense":30,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":0}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Miniso Durham"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ​Concord Police Department - NC ( Phase 2 ) (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #1523 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-22T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"Remote Hands - Connect AT&T broadband circuit"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1789752244382}
{"job":{"id":19968568,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"PurTeraIT","title":"Fast Food Restaurant #777 — Refranchise Conversion — Greensboro, NC","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u><br /></u></strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>OVERVIEW</u></strong></p>\n<p>Provide onsite technical support at the assigned restaurant location. Work includes network cable moves, payment terminal reconfiguration, removal and packaging of legacy equipment, installation of a new manager workstation, testing, and completion documentation.</p>\n<p><strong><u>IMPORTANT CUTOVER REQUIREMENT</u></strong></p>\n<p>Do not begin network-related cable moves until the remote Installation Support Team confirms that the network migration is complete and the applicable firewalls and switches are online.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Tech will be contacted by the support team a day or two in advance to review the documentation, tech will also be required to be on a pre call teams meeting 30 minutes prior to starting the conversion after arriving onsite.</li>\n<li>Tech will be required to provide email address</li>\n<li>Store specific documents will get added closer to install date, Examples have been added to review</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br />\n<br />\n<strong><u>Technicians must bring thin painter’s tape for labeling cables and print all required documentation before arriving onsite. If you cannot print prior to getting onsite you can print it off once you get onsite.</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong><u><br /></u></strong></p>\n<p><u><br />\n<br />\n<strong>Before moving any cables, label each cable with the switch name/number and port number it is connected to upon arrival. Use thin painter’s tape for all labels. Once every cable has been clearly labeled, begin moving the cables to the correct ports according to the provided documentation.</strong></u><br />\n<br />\n<br />\n<br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Make sure that you follow the installation guide in order of the steps and do not skip ahead. If the steps are not done in order it will mess up the system and will cause things to not work and further troubleshooting will need to be done to get it back in sync.</u></strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>SCOPE OF WORK</u></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>check in by calling the check in line 863-888-0112</strong></li>\n<li>Review the site-specific installation guide and switch-port mapping before moving any cables.</li>\n<li><strong>Reorganize network switch connections:</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Locate the applicable network switches.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Move existing Ethernet connections to the designated Meraki switch ports.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Add or remove Ethernet patch connections as directed.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Follow the documented sequence for all cable changes.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Notify remote support after completing the cable moves.</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Reconfigure applicable IP PIN pads, including kiosk payment terminals where present:</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Power-cycle the devices.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Access the required configuration workflow.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Enter the provided Merchant ID and Terminal ID information.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Complete the required reboot and configuration steps.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Perform or assist with a test transaction through the associated POS terminal.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Escalate configuration or transaction failures to remote support.</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Remove legacy equipment:</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Power down and disconnect the existing manager PC.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Disconnect power, network, video, keyboard, mouse, and peripheral connections.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Remove the identified legacy tablet and any applicable manager tablets.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Place all designated equipment in the provided return packaging.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Do not remove packaged equipment from the site.</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Install the new manager PC:</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Unbox and position the new workstation.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Connect the provided power, Ethernet, video, keyboard, mouse, and peripherals.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Install the provided HDMI adapter if required.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Connect the workstation to the designated switch port according to the site documentation.</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Test and close out:</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Work with remote support throughout the installation and cutover.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Troubleshoot physical connectivity issues directly related to the work performed.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Escalate application, payment-processing, configuration, or advanced network issues.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Complete a final walkthrough with available site personnel.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Document all unresolved issues and escalations.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Obtain authorization from remote support before leaving.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Check out through Field Nation and complete all required forms.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>REQUIRED TOOLS</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Ethernet cable tester</li>\n<li>Ethernet toner and probe</li>\n<li>Basic technician hand-tool kit</li>\n<li>Phillips and flathead screwdrivers</li>\n<li>Flashlight</li>\n<li>Smartphone capable of accessing project communications and taking clear photographs</li>\n<li>Smartphone charger and portable power bank</li>\n<li>Laptop with an Ethernet port or compatible Ethernet adapter</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>SITE-PROVIDED ITEMS</strong></p>\n<p>The new workstation, required hardware, patch cables, labels, adapters, power and video cables, peripherals, return packaging, port maps, payment-terminal configuration information, and other installation materials are expected to be onsite. Report missing items immediately.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>REQUIRED DELIVERABLES</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Check-in and check-out confirmation</li>\n<li>Clear before-and-after installation photographs</li>\n<li>Completed installation checklist or required online form</li>\n<li>Confirmation of network cable moves</li>\n<li>Confirmation of PIN pad configuration and transaction testing</li>\n<li>Confirmation of manager PC replacement</li>\n<li>Documentation of open issues and escalations</li>\n<li>Final site completion status</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>","markdown":"**OVERVIEW**\n\nProvide onsite technical support at the assigned restaurant location. Work includes network cable moves, payment terminal reconfiguration, removal and packaging of legacy equipment, installation of a new manager workstation, testing, and completion documentation.\n\n**IMPORTANT CUTOVER REQUIREMENT**\n\nDo not begin network-related cable moves until the remote Installation Support Team confirms that the network migration is complete and the applicable firewalls and switches are online.\n\n- Tech will be contacted by the support team a day or two in advance to review the documentation, tech will also be required to be on a pre call teams meeting 30 minutes prior to starting the conversion after arriving onsite.\n- Tech will be required to provide email address\n- Store specific documents will get added closer to install date, Examples have been added to review\n\n  \n  \n**Technicians must bring thin painter’s tape for labeling cables and print all required documentation before arriving onsite. If you cannot print prior to getting onsite you can print it off once you get onsite.**\n\n  \n  \n**Before moving any cables, label each cable with the switch name/number and port number it is connected to upon arrival. Use thin painter’s tape for all labels. Once every cable has been clearly labeled, begin moving the cables to the correct ports according to the provided documentation.**\n\n**Make sure that you follow the installation guide in order of the steps and do not skip ahead. If the steps are not done in order it will mess up the system and will cause things to not work and further troubleshooting will need to be done to get it back in sync.**\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK**\n\n1. **check in by calling the check in line 863-888-0112**\n2. Review the site-specific installation guide and switch-port mapping before moving any cables.\n3. **Reorganize network switch connections:**\n\n- Locate the applicable network switches.\n- Move existing Ethernet connections to the designated Meraki switch ports.\n- Add or remove Ethernet patch connections as directed.\n- Follow the documented sequence for all cable changes.\n- Notify remote support after completing the cable moves.\n\n1. **Reconfigure applicable IP PIN pads, including kiosk payment terminals where present:**\n\n- Power-cycle the devices.\n- Access the required configuration workflow.\n- Enter the provided Merchant ID and Terminal ID information.\n- Complete the required reboot and configuration steps.\n- Perform or assist with a test transaction through the associated POS terminal.\n- Escalate configuration or transaction failures to remote support.\n\n1. **Remove legacy equipment:**\n\n- Power down and disconnect the existing manager PC.\n- Disconnect power, network, video, keyboard, mouse, and peripheral connections.\n- Remove the identified legacy tablet and any applicable manager tablets.\n- Place all designated equipment in the provided return packaging.\n- Do not remove packaged equipment from the site.\n\n1. **Install the new manager PC:**\n\n- Unbox and position the new workstation.\n- Connect the provided power, Ethernet, video, keyboard, mouse, and peripherals.\n- Install the provided HDMI adapter if required.\n- Connect the workstation to the designated switch port according to the site documentation.\n\n1. **Test and close out:**\n\n- Work with remote support throughout the installation and cutover.\n- Troubleshoot physical connectivity issues directly related to the work performed.\n- Escalate application, payment-processing, configuration, or advanced network issues.\n- Complete a final walkthrough with available site personnel.\n- Document all unresolved issues and escalations.\n- Obtain authorization from remote support before leaving.\n- Check out through Field Nation and complete all required forms.\n\n**REQUIRED TOOLS**\n\n- Ethernet cable tester\n- Ethernet toner and probe\n- Basic technician hand-tool kit\n- Phillips and flathead screwdrivers\n- Flashlight\n- Smartphone capable of accessing project communications and taking clear photographs\n- Smartphone charger and portable power bank\n- Laptop with an Ethernet port or compatible Ethernet adapter\n\n**SITE-PROVIDED ITEMS**\n\nThe new workstation, required hardware, patch cables, labels, adapters, power and video cables, peripherals, return packaging, port maps, payment-terminal configuration information, and other installation materials are expected to be onsite. Report missing items immediately.\n\n**REQUIRED DELIVERABLES**\n\n- Check-in and check-out confirmation\n- Clear before-and-after installation photographs\n- Completed installation checklist or required online form\n- Confirmation of network cable moves\n- Confirmation of PIN pad configuration and transaction testing\n- Confirmation of manager PC replacement\n- Documentation of open issues and escalations\n- Final site completion status","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-22T22:00","end":"2026-09-22T26:00"},"payRange":{"min":300,"max":860},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":4,"amount":300},"additional":{"units":8,"amount":70}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":58},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"blended","counterRate":75,"baseAmount":900,"estHours":4,"travelExpense":85,"payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":4,"amount":300},"additional":{"units":8,"amount":75}},"counterDate":{"start":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T17:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":60,"mode":"hours","reason":"arrival_window"}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-22T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"gap"},{"start":"2026-09-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-09-23T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Miniso"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ​Concord Police Department - NC ( Phase 2 ) (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #1523 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-22T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"Remote Hands - Connect AT&T broadband circuit"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1789752244464}
{"job":{"id":19976286,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Netview Inc.","title":"Site Survey","description":{"html":"<p><strong><em>NOTE: YOU WILL BE ASKED BY THE BRIDGE TO UPLOAD SOME PICTURES IN THE CHAT WHILE ONSITE. YOU STILL NEED TO UPLOAD ALL DELIVERABLES TO THIS WORK ORDER BEFORE WE CAN CLOSE THE WORK ORDER. EVEN IF YOU UPLOADED THEM ON THE BRIDGE. WE ARE NOT ON THE BRIDGE SO WE DO NOT SEE WHAT YOU UPLOADED AND WE MUST HAVE ALL THOSE DELIVERABLES WHICH INCLUDE (COMPLETED USER ACCEPTANCE TESTING (3 pages completed), MOP (with serial #'s &amp; locations added), ALL PICTURES LISTED BELOW, FLOORPLAN (marking where AP's and MDF/IDF's are located). THIS IS NOT OPTIONAL!!!</em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>Once the survey is completed, the technician must validate the survey with the Project Coordinator and Jason before leaving the site. The technician can only be released once approval is received from the CompuCom team, after which the survey can be marked as successfully completed.</u></strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>SOW:</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>LOCATING: 1 Firewall(s) &amp; 0 AP(s)</u></strong></p>\n<p>Vendor field services will perform the following tasks during site survey:</p>\n<p>• Objectives include validating site readiness, confirming equipment quantities, reducing failed installation visits, ensuring E911 compliance readiness, and producing standardized documentation for deployment planning.</p>\n<p>• Vendor shall perform on-site discovery and assessment activities and provide standardized documentation and readiness classifications.</p>\n<p>• Vendor shall coordinate site access through Customer team, validate MDF/IDF access, confirm physical security, and identify access constraints.</p>\n<p>• Assess MDF/IDF conditions including rack type, RU availability, power, airflow, and cabling condition. Cable cleanup shall be assessed and documented only.</p>\n<p>• Document existing mounting, power, WAN handoffs, demarc location, and cellular failover presence.</p>\n<p>• Perform per-AP discovery documenting model, mounting, orientation, cable condition, and room location.</p>\n<p>• Collect address validation and AP location data required to support E911 compliance readiness. No live E911 configuration changes or service provide updates are included. Identify the closest room number or distinguishing location details per AP location</p>\n<p>• Provide photos of MDF/IDF, firewall, switches, APs and AP location, cellular devices, and rack condition. Photos must be clear and properly labeled.</p>\n<p>• Deliverables include a site discovery report, photo package, site readiness classification, blocking issues log, and program summary if requested by Customer</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>DOCUMENT ATTACHED WITH DETAILED INFORMATION on SCOPE OF WORK REQUIREMENTS</u></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>When arriving onsite tech MUST check in with Netview (contacts in Confidential Info section)</li>\n<li>After checking in with Netview tech MUST call into the bridge to notify them you are onsite (bridge info is in the confidential information)</li>\n<li><strong>After checking in Document and take pictures of all devices in the MDF/IDF(s), pictures of the location of all AP's onsite and review with support engineer.</strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>NOTE: The support engineer will ask you to send him all pictures....YOU MUST STILL UPLOAD ALL PICTURES IN THIS WORK ORDER IN ORDER TO BE PAID.</strong></li>\n<li>Techs are REQUIRED to attend a Technical Review call prior to day of site visit. Invites for technical review will be sent to your email noted on your FN profile. Please watch email for invite.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>REQUIRED DELIVERABLES: (must be uploaded to this work order and/or emailed to wmdispatch@teamnetview.com in order to be paid)</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Pictures of all items and devices surveyed</li>\n<li><em>Floorplan - We must have a \"map\" of the site showing the location of the MDF/IDF(s) and all AP's - You can take a picture of the sites Emergency Evacuation map then write in the location of the MDF or IDF and all AP's.</em></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Documents Required:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><u>Once the survey is completed, the technician must validate the survey with the Project Coordinator and Jason before leaving the site. The technician can only be released once approval is received from the CompuCom team, after which the survey can be marked as successfully completed.</u></strong></li>\n<li><em>You MUST fill in the serial number of each device on the survey form AND a brief location of that device.</em></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><em>Example: Firewall will be in the MDF or IDF, you can write MDF as the location</em></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><em>Example: AP's will be in different areas of the building. Note the general area such as AP2 in Conference Room or AP2 outside Managers Office, AP3 in Souteast corner of Warehouse, etc</em></li>\n<li>ALL PICTURES MUST BE NAMED INDICATING THE DEVICE WE ARE LOOKING AT IN THE PICTURES</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><em>Picture Naming Examples: MDF Full Room, MDF Close Up, AP1 Full Room, AP1 Close Up, Cable Test AP1 Run, Cable Test Firewall, etc)</em></li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Required Tools:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Standard Hand Tools (Screwdrivers, Drill, etc.)</li>\n<li>Velcro for cable management</li>\n<li>Laptop:&nbsp;With a functioning LAN port and Teams installed.</li>\n<li>Console Cable</li>\n<li>Mobile Hotspot</li>\n<li>Cable Tester</li>\n<li>Ladder&nbsp;(8'-10')</li>\n<li>Lift will be ordered if necessary</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong><u>You are done with the physical survey portion of the assignment when the bridge releases you. You are not done with the full assignment until Netview has all deliverables and SOMEONE AT NETVIEW RELEASES YOU! You are to stay onsite until Netview confirms we have everything we need. Then you can have the site contact sign off on your User Acceptance Testing document.</u></strong></p>","markdown":"***NOTE: YOU WILL BE ASKED BY THE BRIDGE TO UPLOAD SOME PICTURES IN THE CHAT WHILE ONSITE. YOU STILL NEED TO UPLOAD ALL DELIVERABLES TO THIS WORK ORDER BEFORE WE CAN CLOSE THE WORK ORDER. EVEN IF YOU UPLOADED THEM ON THE BRIDGE. WE ARE NOT ON THE BRIDGE SO WE DO NOT SEE WHAT YOU UPLOADED AND WE MUST HAVE ALL THOSE DELIVERABLES WHICH INCLUDE (COMPLETED USER ACCEPTANCE TESTING (3 pages completed), MOP (with serial #'s & locations added), ALL PICTURES LISTED BELOW, FLOORPLAN (marking where AP's and MDF/IDF's are located). THIS IS NOT OPTIONAL!!!***\n\n**Once the survey is completed, the technician must validate the survey with the Project Coordinator and Jason before leaving the site. The technician can only be released once approval is received from the CompuCom team, after which the survey can be marked as successfully completed.**\n\n**SOW:**\n\n**LOCATING: 1 Firewall(s) & 0 AP(s)**\n\nVendor field services will perform the following tasks during site survey:\n\n• Objectives include validating site readiness, confirming equipment quantities, reducing failed installation visits, ensuring E911 compliance readiness, and producing standardized documentation for deployment planning.\n\n• Vendor shall perform on-site discovery and assessment activities and provide standardized documentation and readiness classifications.\n\n• Vendor shall coordinate site access through Customer team, validate MDF/IDF access, confirm physical security, and identify access constraints.\n\n• Assess MDF/IDF conditions including rack type, RU availability, power, airflow, and cabling condition. Cable cleanup shall be assessed and documented only.\n\n• Document existing mounting, power, WAN handoffs, demarc location, and cellular failover presence.\n\n• Perform per-AP discovery documenting model, mounting, orientation, cable condition, and room location.\n\n• Collect address validation and AP location data required to support E911 compliance readiness. No live E911 configuration changes or service provide updates are included. Identify the closest room number or distinguishing location details per AP location\n\n• Provide photos of MDF/IDF, firewall, switches, APs and AP location, cellular devices, and rack condition. Photos must be clear and properly labeled.\n\n• Deliverables include a site discovery report, photo package, site readiness classification, blocking issues log, and program summary if requested by Customer\n\n**DOCUMENT ATTACHED WITH DETAILED INFORMATION on SCOPE OF WORK REQUIREMENTS**\n\n1. When arriving onsite tech MUST check in with Netview (contacts in Confidential Info section)\n2. After checking in with Netview tech MUST call into the bridge to notify them you are onsite (bridge info is in the confidential information)\n3. **After checking in Document and take pictures of all devices in the MDF/IDF(s), pictures of the location of all AP's onsite and review with support engineer.**\n4. **NOTE: The support engineer will ask you to send him all pictures....YOU MUST STILL UPLOAD ALL PICTURES IN THIS WORK ORDER IN ORDER TO BE PAID.**\n5. Techs are REQUIRED to attend a Technical Review call prior to day of site visit. Invites for technical review will be sent to your email noted on your FN profile. Please watch email for invite.\n\n**REQUIRED DELIVERABLES: (must be uploaded to this work order and/or emailed to wmdispatch@teamnetview.com in order to be paid)**\n\n- Pictures of all items and devices surveyed\n- *Floorplan - We must have a \"map\" of the site showing the location of the MDF/IDF(s) and all AP's - You can take a picture of the sites Emergency Evacuation map then write in the location of the MDF or IDF and all AP's.*\n\n**Documents Required:**\n\n- **Once the survey is completed, the technician must validate the survey with the Project Coordinator and Jason before leaving the site. The technician can only be released once approval is received from the CompuCom team, after which the survey can be marked as successfully completed.**\n- *You MUST fill in the serial number of each device on the survey form AND a brief location of that device.*\n- *Example: Firewall will be in the MDF or IDF, you can write MDF as the location*\n- *Example: AP's will be in different areas of the building. Note the general area such as AP2 in Conference Room or AP2 outside Managers Office, AP3 in Souteast corner of Warehouse, etc*\n- ALL PICTURES MUST BE NAMED INDICATING THE DEVICE WE ARE LOOKING AT IN THE PICTURES\n- *Picture Naming Examples: MDF Full Room, MDF Close Up, AP1 Full Room, AP1 Close Up, Cable Test AP1 Run, Cable Test Firewall, etc)*\n\n**Required Tools:**\n\n- Standard Hand Tools (Screwdrivers, Drill, etc.)\n- Velcro for cable management\n- Laptop: With a functioning LAN port and Teams installed.\n- Console Cable\n- Mobile Hotspot\n- Cable Tester\n- Ladder (8'-10')\n- Lift will be ordered if necessary\n\n**You are done with the physical survey portion of the assignment when the bridge releases you. You are not done with the full assignment until Netview has all deliverables and SOMEONE AT NETVIEW RELEASES YOU! You are to stay onsite until Netview confirms we have everything we need. Then you can have the site contact sign off on your User Acceptance Testing document.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-23T09:00","end":"2026-10-23T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":36},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00