u can have the site contact sign off on your User Acceptance Testing document.</u></strong></p>","markdown":"***NOTE: YOU WILL BE ASKED BY THE BRIDGE TO UPLOAD SOME PICTURES IN THE CHAT WHILE ONSITE. YOU STILL NEED TO UPLOAD ALL DELIVERABLES TO THIS WORK ORDER BEFORE WE CAN CLOSE THE WORK ORDER. EVEN IF YOU UPLOADED THEM ON THE BRIDGE. WE ARE NOT ON THE BRIDGE SO WE DO NOT SEE WHAT YOU UPLOADED AND WE MUST HAVE ALL THOSE DELIVERABLES WHICH INCLUDE (COMPLETED USER ACCEPTANCE TESTING (3 pages completed), MOP (with serial #'s & locations added), ALL PICTURES LISTED BELOW, FLOORPLAN (marking where AP's and MDF/IDF's are located). THIS IS NOT OPTIONAL!!!***\n\n**Once the survey is completed, the technician must validate the survey with the Project Coordinator and Jason before leaving the site. The technician can only be released once approval is received from the CompuCom team, after which the survey can be marked as successfully completed.**\n\n**SOW:**\n\n**LOCATING: 1 Firewall(s) & 1 AP(s)**\n\nVendor field services will perform the following tasks during site survey:\n\n• Objectives include validating site readiness, confirming equipment quantities, reducing failed installation visits, ensuring E911 compliance readiness, and producing standardized documentation for deployment planning.\n\n• Vendor shall perform on-site discovery and assessment activities and provide standardized documentation and readiness classifications.\n\n• Vendor shall coordinate site access through Customer team, validate MDF/IDF access, confirm physical security, and identify access constraints.\n\n• Assess MDF/IDF conditions including rack type, RU availability, power, airflow, and cabling condition. Cable cleanup shall be assessed and documented only.\n\n• Document existing mounting, power, WAN handoffs, demarc location, and cellular failover presence.\n\n• Perform per-AP discovery documenting model, mounting, orientation, cable condition, and room location.\n\n• Collect address validation and AP location data required to support E911 compliance readiness. No live E911 configuration changes or service provide updates are included. Identify the closest room number or distinguishing location details per AP location\n\n• Provide photos of MDF/IDF, firewall, switches, APs and AP location, cellular devices, and rack condition. Photos must be clear and properly labeled.\n\n• Deliverables include a site discovery report, photo package, site readiness classification, blocking issues log, and program summary if requested by Customer\n\n**DOCUMENT ATTACHED WITH DETAILED INFORMATION on SCOPE OF WORK REQUIREMENTS**\n\n1. When arriving onsite tech MUST check in with Netview (contacts in Confidential Info section)\n2. After checking in with Netview tech MUST call into the bridge to notify them you are onsite (bridge info is in the confidential information)\n3. **After checking in Document and take pictures of all devices in the MDF/IDF(s), pictures of the location of all AP's onsite and review with support engineer.**\n4. **NOTE: The support engineer will ask you to send him all pictures....YOU MUST STILL UPLOAD ALL PICTURES IN THIS WORK ORDER IN ORDER TO BE PAID.**\n5. Techs are REQUIRED to attend a Technical Review call prior to day of site visit. Invites for technical review will be sent to your email noted on your FN profile. Please watch email for invite.\n\n**REQUIRED DELIVERABLES: (must be uploaded to this work order and/or emailed to wmdispatch@teamnetview.com in order to be paid)**\n\n- Pictures of all items and devices surveyed\n- *Floorplan - We must have a \"map\" of the site showing the location of the MDF/IDF(s) and all AP's - You can take a picture of the sites Emergency Evacuation map then write in the location of the MDF or IDF and all AP's.*\n\n**Documents Required:**\n\n- **Once the survey is completed, the technician must validate the survey with the Project Coordinator and Jason before leaving the site. The technician can only be released once approval is received from the CompuCom team, after which the survey can be marked as successfully completed.**\n- *You MUST fill in the serial number of each device on the survey form AND a brief location of that device.*\n- *Example: Firewall will be in the MDF or IDF, you can write MDF as the location*\n- *Example: AP's will be in different areas of the building. Note the general area such as AP2 in Conference Room or AP2 outside Managers Office, AP3 in Souteast corner of Warehouse, etc*\n- ALL PICTURES MUST BE NAMED INDICATING THE DEVICE WE ARE LOOKING AT IN THE PICTURES\n- *Picture Naming Examples: MDF Full Room, MDF Close Up, AP1 Full Room, AP1 Close Up, Cable Test AP1 Run, Cable Test Firewall, etc)*\n\n**Required Tools:**\n\n- Standard Hand Tools (Screwdrivers, Drill, etc.)\n- Velcro for cable management\n- Laptop: With a functioning LAN port and Teams installed.\n- Console Cable\n- Mobile Hotspot\n- Cable Tester\n- Ladder (8'-10')\n- Lift will be ordered if necessary\n\n**You are done with the physical survey portion of the assignment when the bridge releases you. You are not done with the full assignment until Netview has all deliverables and SOMEONE AT NETVIEW RELEASES YOU! You are to stay onsite until Netview confirms we have everything we need. Then you can have the site contact sign off on your User Acceptance Testing document.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-23T11:00","end":"2026-10-23T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":56},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-26T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-27T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00