{"job":{"id":19986013,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"NewBold Technologies","title":" AP Refresh Installation (RETAIL STORE) - Lead Installer","description":{"html":"<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<strong>AP Refresh Only</strong>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Each job is planned around installing 15 APs within 8-hours. We have had much success with this timeline so this pace should be very achievable.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Pay is for UP TO 8 hours onsite.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>If the job runs longer than 8 hours due to circumstances out of your control, you will need to document these events, and the amount of time you were delayed, &nbsp;and provide proof of sign off from the Lead onsite. There will be no exceptions. &nbsp;</strong></li>\n<li><strong>If you finish ahead of the 8 hours, you're free to head out. Once you check out with the lead on site</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<strong><br />\nA Lift and Ladders will be provided. Tech must be lift certified to drive the lift.</strong><br />\nThe purpose of this work order is to complete the replacement of AP's within the site. A full Asbuilt Map will be provided in the documents section, please print this. Please review all information prior to site visit. Please do not schedule another job for the morning after this work order. Any hours over estimated will be paid at an hourly rate.<br />\nDownload MS Teams (used for project bridge) Download MIST AI App, by Juniper Networks. This will be used to upload photos of the AP's.<br />\n<u>REQUIRED TOOLS:</u>A. Drill/Impact/Screwdrivers B. Basic termination tools ( in case an AP comes up at less than gig) C. Velcro/ Scissors D. Label maker/ extra tape/ markers/Sharpies E. MISC standard technician tool kit F. Zip Ties<br />\n<u>DAY OF:</u>A. You must arrive a Minimum of 30 minutes before close. Validate/check in with Field PM. This time is not flexible, and you must be on site by the agreed upon time. B. When you enter- you must have everything with you and enter once, you cannot leave the building until everything is completed. So, there are no breaks outside the building. C. You must enter through the rear of the building at loading the dock. There will be a keypad (referenced as HIRSCH keypad from hereout), Enter Hirsch code and enter the building D. Enter Hirsch code and enter the building E. After bringing in all of your items&nbsp;*ALL items* Locate the Lead Tech.&nbsp; F. Verify with the MIC that end-of-day store activities are completed- ( This is usually 45-1hour after close)&nbsp;* can do BOH areas with permission from MIC G. Determine the front of the store for installation purposes and verify inventory on site. H. Please update PM that all inventory is on site and accounted for. I. Contact Field PM to let them know AP's been replaced. The lead will control this. Please let them know when finished so they can start health checks. This is key to begin health checks and directly affects how quickly your site is signed off and marked completed&nbsp; &nbsp;<u>COMPLETION CHECKLIST:</u>A. Ensure all areas are cleaned up B. Ensure all old AP's are left in boxes that new came in, Do not box these back up into little boxes just toss into the large boxes loose. C. Ensure all Photos for AP's are loaded into MIST app. D. We need to verify that the phones are back online. Procced to a phone- look at display- call your cell phone etc to verify online- (Take photo of phone with display visible). Must call from one in the back area and one on the sales floor. E. Dispose of all trash properly. Tiles that were removed during install should be removed and leaned or stacked near garbage.\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>","markdown":"**AP Refresh Only**- **Each job is planned around installing 15 APs within 8-hours. We have had much success with this timeline so this pace should be very achievable.**\n- **Pay is for UP TO 8 hours onsite.**\n- **If the job runs longer than 8 hours due to circumstances out of your control, you will need to document these events, and the amount of time you were delayed, and provide proof of sign off from the Lead onsite. There will be no exceptions.**\n- **If you finish ahead of the 8 hours, you're free to head out. Once you check out with the lead on site**.\n\n **A Lift and Ladders will be provided. Tech must be lift certified to drive the lift.**  \nThe purpose of this work order is to complete the replacement of AP's within the site. A full Asbuilt Map will be provided in the documents section, please print this. Please review all information prior to site visit. Please do not schedule another job for the morning after this work order. Any hours over estimated will be paid at an hourly rate.  \nDownload MS Teams (used for project bridge) Download MIST AI App, by Juniper Networks. This will be used to upload photos of the AP's.  \nREQUIRED TOOLS:A. Drill/Impact/Screwdrivers B. Basic termination tools ( in case an AP comes up at less than gig) C. Velcro/ Scissors D. Label maker/ extra tape/ markers/Sharpies E. MISC standard technician tool kit F. Zip Ties  \nDAY OF:A. You must arrive a Minimum of 30 minutes before close. Validate/check in with Field PM. This time is not flexible, and you must be on site by the agreed upon time. B. When you enter- you must have everything with you and enter once, you cannot leave the building until everything is completed. So, there are no breaks outside the building. C. You must enter through the rear of the building at loading the dock. There will be a keypad (referenced as HIRSCH keypad from hereout), Enter Hirsch code and enter the building D. Enter Hirsch code and enter the building E. After bringing in all of your items \\*ALL items\\* Locate the Lead Tech. F. Verify with the MIC that end-of-day store activities are completed- ( This is usually 45-1hour after close) \\* can do BOH areas with permission from MIC G. Determine the front of the store for installation purposes and verify inventory on site. H. Please update PM that all inventory is on site and accounted for. I. Contact Field PM to let them know AP's been replaced. The lead will control this. Please let them know when finished so they can start health checks. This is key to begin health checks and directly affects how quickly your site is signed off and marked completed COMPLETION CHECKLIST:A. Ensure all areas are cleaned up B. Ensure all old AP's are left in boxes that new came in, Do not box these back up into little boxes just toss into the large boxes loose. C. Ensure all Photos for AP's are loaded into MIST app. D. We need to verify that the phones are back online. Procced to a phone- look at display- call your cell phone etc to verify online- (Take photo of phone with display visible). Must call from one in the back area and one on the sales floor. E. Dispose of all trash properly. Tiles that were removed during install should be removed and leaned or stacked near garbage.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-30T19:30","end":"2026-09-30T27:30"},"payRange":{"min":650,"max":650},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":8,"distance":11},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"fixed","counterRate":81,"baseAmount":650,"estHours":8,"travelExpense":30,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":0}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ​Concord Police Department - NC ( Phase 2 ) (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","en