{"job":{"id":19957552,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Velocity Tech Solutions","title":"Remote Hands - Connect AT&T broadband circuit","description":{"html":"<p><strong><em><u>PLEASE NOTE THAT YOU ARE TO REPRESENT VTS AT ALL TIMES WHILE ONSITE.</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>Overview:</u></strong></p>\n<p>Connect the newly installed AT&amp;T broad band circuit to the Fortinet firewall.&nbsp;The circuit will connect to port WAN2.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>In addition, if there is time, rack and connect the Arctic Wolf appliance we brought over from the old office.</p>\n<p>IT Support: Andy Andreatta 904-574-7545</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>1. Scope of Work</strong></p>\n<p>The technician is responsible for performing onsite work as outlined below. All steps must be completed in the order listed unless otherwise directed by Support or the Work Order Manager.</p>\n<p><strong>Task Sequence:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Confirm scheduled work 24 hours prior and again 1 hour prior to site arrival.</li>\n<li>Upon arrival, call or text the Work Order Manager to check in.</li>\n<li>Make contact with the Local Contact and confirm site access and work area.</li>\n<li>Locate required parts and equipment as outlined in the work order.</li>\n<li>Take BEFORE photos of all work areas and existing equipment.</li>\n<li>Check in with IT Support prior to making any changes or beginning installation work.</li>\n<li>Complete the work as specified in the work order or project documentation.</li>\n<li>Take AFTER photos of completed work.</li>\n<li>Test and verify functionality with IT Support (checkout process).</li>\n<li>Clean up all work areas and ensure no debris or packaging remains.</li>\n<li>Enter detailed closeout notes describing all work performed, issues encountered, and resolutions.</li>\n<li>Upload and attach all required photo deliverables (BEFORE, AFTER, and any additional requested photos).</li>\n<li>Checkout with Work Order Manager before leaving the site.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>2. Tools and Equipment Required</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Laptop</li>\n<li>Console cables</li>\n<li>Mobile hotspot or other internet connectivity</li>\n<li>Basic networking tools (punchdown tool, crimper, etc.)</li>\n<li>Basic hand tools (screwdrivers, pliers, etc.)</li>\n<li>Ladder (as needed for access)</li>\n<li>Cable tester</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>3. Deliverables Required</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>BEFORE photos of all work areas</li>\n<li>AFTER photos of all completed work</li>\n<li>Any additional photos specifically requested by the Work Order Manager, Client, or IT Support</li>\n<li>Detailed closeout notes summarizing work performed, testing results, and any deviations</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>4. Acceptance Criteria</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>All steps in the Scope of Work have been completed.</li>\n<li>IT Support confirms functionality and successful testing.</li>\n<li>All required photo deliverables and closeout notes are submitted.</li>\n<li>The Work Order Manager provides final checkout approval.</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"***PLEASE NOTE THAT YOU ARE TO REPRESENT VTS AT ALL TIMES WHILE ONSITE.***\n\n**Overview:**\n\nConnect the newly installed AT&T broad band circuit to the Fortinet firewall. The circuit will connect to port WAN2.\n\nIn addition, if there is time, rack and connect the Arctic Wolf appliance we brought over from the old office.\n\nIT Support: Andy Andreatta 904-574-7545\n\n**1. Scope of Work**\n\nThe technician is responsible for performing onsite work as outlined below. All steps must be completed in the order listed unless otherwise directed by Support or the Work Order Manager.\n\n**Task Sequence:**\n\n1. Confirm scheduled work 24 hours prior and again 1 hour prior to site arrival.\n2. Upon arrival, call or text the Work Order Manager to check in.\n3. Make contact with the Local Contact and confirm site access and work area.\n4. Locate required parts and equipment as outlined in the work order.\n5. Take BEFORE photos of all work areas and existing equipment.\n6. Check in with IT Support prior to making any changes or beginning installation work.\n7. Complete the work as specified in the work order or project documentation.\n8. Take AFTER photos of completed work.\n9. Test and verify functionality with IT Support (checkout process).\n10. Clean up all work areas and ensure no debris or packaging remains.\n11. Enter detailed closeout notes describing all work performed, issues encountered, and resolutions.\n12. Upload and attach all required photo deliverables (BEFORE, AFTER, and any additional requested photos).\n13. Checkout with Work Order Manager before leaving the site.\n\n**2. Tools and Equipment Required**\n\n- Laptop\n- Console cables\n- Mobile hotspot or other internet connectivity\n- Basic networking tools (punchdown tool, crimper, etc.)\n- Basic hand tools (screwdrivers, pliers, etc.)\n- Ladder (as needed for access)\n- Cable tester\n\n**3. Deliverables Required**\n\n- BEFORE photos of all work areas\n- AFTER photos of all completed work\n- Any additional photos specifically requested by the Work Order Manager, Client, or IT Support\n- Detailed closeout notes summarizing work performed, testing results, and any deviations\n\n**4. Acceptance Criteria**\n\n- All steps in the Scope of Work have been completed.\n- IT Support confirms functionality and successful testing.\n- All required photo deliverables and closeout notes are submitted.\n- The Work Order Manager provides final checkout approval.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-22T10:00","end":"2026-09-22T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":130,"max":260},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":130},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":65}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":5},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $260 is below minimum threshold $400"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-22T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"gap"},{"start":"2026-09-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-09-23T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Miniso"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ​Concord Police Department - NC ( Phase 2 ) (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #1523 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-22T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"Remote Hands - Connect AT&T broadband circuit"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789752373995}
{"job":{"id":19975331,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Gigstreem","title":"Olde Raleigh -  Residential Service and troubleshooting AP  -#315185","description":{"html":"<p>Here’s a cleaned-up SOW in the same format, focused specifically on the resident’s Wi-Fi coverage complaint and onsite testing.</p><p><strong>GiGstreem is a national Internet Service Provider delivering high-quality service to residential and commercial properties across the country.</strong></p><p><strong>Work Order Location:</strong></p><p><strong>Residential Property –</strong> <em>Refer to confidential notes for property location.</em></p><p><em>Refer to confidential notes for the exact address, unit number, resident contact information, and property management contact.</em></p><p><em>CONFIRM YOU HAVE THE EXPERIENCE AND TOOLS REQUIRED BEFORE APPLYING FOR THIS WORK ORDER.</em></p><strong>Scope of Work</strong><p><strong>Dispatch an experienced network technician to perform onsite Wi-Fi signal, connectivity, and performance testing within the resident’s apartment.</strong></p><p><strong>The resident is reporting poor or no usable Wi-Fi signal in the bedroom located furthest from the Access Point (AP).</strong></p><p><strong>Remote monitoring currently indicates that the network equipment and AP are online and operating normally</strong>. This dispatch is intended to perform <strong>onsite location-based testing</strong> throughout the unit to verify actual Wi-Fi coverage and performance from the resident’s perspective.</p><p>The technician must document the results and work directly with GiGstreem Support/Network Operations to confirm that the network and AP are functioning properly.</p><strong>Work Details</strong><ul><li>Check in with the leasing office/property staff before entering the resident’s unit.</li><li>Contact <strong>GiGstreem Support/Network Operations</strong> upon arrival and coordinate testing.</li><li>Verify that the installed AP is online and operating normally.</li><li>Visually inspect the AP and surrounding area for any obvious physical or environmental issues.</li><li>Using the <strong>provider/technician laptop</strong>, connect to the GiGstreem Wi-Fi network and perform onsite testing.</li><li>Perform Wi-Fi <strong>signal, connectivity, and speed testing throughout the apartment</strong>.</li><li>Test directly near the AP to establish a baseline.</li><li>Test from the living room and other primary areas of the unit.</li><li><strong>Test from the furthest bedroom where the resident is reporting poor or no signal.</strong></li><li><strong>Record Wi-Fi signal strength/RSSI, connection quality, download speed, upload speed, and latency where available.</strong></li><li><strong>Verify whether the provider laptop maintains a stable Wi-Fi connection in the affected bedroom.</strong></li><li><strong>Compare testing from the provider laptop with the resident’s device when possible to determine whether there is a significant difference between devices.</strong></li><li><strong>If the resident's device experiences an issue that cannot be duplicated using the provider laptop, clearly document this in the work order.</strong></li><li><strong>Verify the resident is connecting to the correct GiGstreem Wi-Fi network/SSID.</strong></li><li><strong>Test multiple locations within the affected bedroom when necessary to determine the extent of the coverage issue.</strong></li><li><strong>Contact GiGstreem Support/Network Operations</strong> and review all test results before completing the visit.</li><li>Follow any additional troubleshooting instructions provided by Support/Engineering.</li><li>Take photos of the AP location and any relevant equipment or conditions.</li><li>Upload detailed documentation showing <strong>where each test was performed and the results of each test</strong>.</li><li><strong>Before leaving the property, contact the manager listed in the confidential notes and provide the onsite testing results and findings.</strong></li><li><strong>Do not leave the site until GiGstreem Support/Network Operations has reviewed the findings and the manager listed in the confidential notes has been contacted.</strong></li></ul><strong>Required Testing Documentation</strong><p>Technician must provide clear testing results for each major location within the unit, especially:</p><p><strong>1. Near the Access Point</strong></p><ul><li>Signal/RSSI</li><li>Download speed</li><li>Upload speed</li><li>Latency/ping</li><li>Connection stability</li></ul><p><strong>2. Living Room / Main Area</strong></p><ul><li>Signal/RSSI</li><li>Download speed</li><li>Upload speed</li><li>Latency/ping</li><li>Connection stability</li></ul><p><strong>3. Furthest Bedroom / Reported Problem Area</strong></p><ul><li>Signal/RSSI</li><li>Download speed</li><li>Upload speed</li><li>Latency/ping</li><li>Connection stability</li></ul><p>Clearly identify whether the issue was <strong>duplicated using the provider laptop</strong>.</p><strong>Technician Expectations</strong><ul><li><strong>Confirm the appointment time</strong> with the customer before heading to the property.</li><li><strong>Place a courtesy call at least 30 minutes prior to arrival</strong> to inform the customer of your estimated time of arrival (ETA).</li><li>Upon arriving on site, all Field Nation technicians are required to <strong>check in at the leasing office or front desk before proceeding to the unit.</strong> Contractors must announce their arrival and present their Field Nation ID and credentials for verification. <strong>Entry into any resident’s unit is not permitted until this check-in process is completed and approved by onsite staff.</strong></li><li><strong>Represent the brand</strong> with professionalism. Appearance, communication, and the quality of work must reflect high standards.</li><li><strong>Do not overshare</strong> internal processes or technical details with the customer. Communication should be simple, courteous, and focused on testing and resolving the reported issue.</li><li>Do not promise equipment changes, AP relocation, additional APs, credits, or other solutions unless specifically authorized by GiGstreem.</li><li>⚠️ <em>If the technician arrives unprepared, misinforms the customer, demonstrates poor presentation, or delivers substandard work, GiGstreem reserves the right to withhold payment for the work order.</em></li></ul><strong>Required Experience</strong><ul><li>Wi-Fi signal and performance troubleshooting</li><li>Troubleshooting Ruckus Access Points</li><li>Networking/Telecommunications experience</li><li>Understanding of Wi-Fi RSSI/signal strength, interference, latency, throughput, and coverage</li><li>Ability to perform and document location-based Wi-Fi testing</li><li>Experience working with remote Network Operations/Engineering teams</li></ul><strong>Required Tools</strong><ul><li><strong>Laptop with Wi-Fi and Ethernet capability</strong></li><li><strong>USB-to-Ethernet adapter if laptop does not have an Ethernet port</strong></li><li><strong>Wi-Fi signal/RSSI testing capability</strong></li><li><strong>Speed test capability</strong></li><li><strong>Cable tester</strong></li><li><strong>Known-good Ethernet patch cables</strong></li><li><strong>Basic hand tools</strong></li><li><strong>Flashlight</strong></li><li><strong>Smartphone for photos and documentation</strong></li><li><strong>Mobile hotspot for communication with Support if needed</strong></li></ul><strong>Coordination</strong><ul><li>Troubleshoot in collaboration with <strong>GiGstreem Support/Network Operations</strong>.</li><li>Remote monitoring currently indicates the network and AP are online; therefore, <strong>onsite location testing and documentation are critical for this dispatch.</strong></li><li><strong>Refer to confidential notes for Network Operations, resident, and property management contact details.</strong></li><li><strong>Contact the manager listed in the confidential notes before leaving the property to provide the final testing results.</strong></li></ul><strong>Policy on Wi-Fi Extenders – GiGstreem Policy Reminder</strong><p>At GiGstreem, delivering reliable, high-performance internet service is our top priority. To maintain the integrity of our network and ensure consistent customer experiences, we follow strict guidelines regarding the equipment and solutions we support.</p><p><strong>It is strictly against GiGstreem policy to utilize, install, or recommend Wi-Fi extenders as a solution for speed, coverage, or connectivity issues within a unit.</strong></p><p><strong>Why This Matters:</strong></p><ul><li>Wi-Fi extenders are not part of our approved network architecture.</li><li>They can introduce interference, degrade performance, and complicate troubleshooting.</li><li>Recommending or installing extenders may lead to inconsistent service and customer dissatisfaction.</li></ul><p><strong>Approved Resolution Methods:</strong></p><ul><li>Thorough onsite testing of the existing AP and network configuration.</li><li>Wi-Fi signal and performance testing from multiple locations within the unit.</li><li>Comparison testing using a GiGstreem/provider laptop versus the resident’s device.</li><li>Collaboration with Support/Engineering to assess AP performance and configuration.</li><li>Documentation and escalation of confirmed coverage issues for management/Engineering review.</li></ul><p><strong>Technicians must not relocate an AP, install additional equipment, or recommend Wi-Fi extenders without authorization from GiGstreem Support/Engineering or management.</strong></p><p><strong>All technicians and support staff must adhere to this policy without exception. Any deviation or recommended network modification must be escalated to GiGstreem management for review.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>I specifically made the furthest bedroom test the priority</strong>, while also requiring a baseline near the AP and comparison with the provider laptop. That should give you solid evidence to determine whether this is an actual coverage issue, a resident-device issue, or something Engineering needs to address.</li></ul>","markdown":"Here’s a cleaned-up SOW in the same format, focused specifically on the resident’s Wi-Fi coverage complaint and onsite testing.\n\n**GiGstreem is a national Internet Service Provider delivering high-quality service to residential and commercial properties across the country.**\n\n**Work Order Location:**\n\n**Residential Property –** *Refer to confidential notes for property location.*\n\n*Refer to confidential notes for the exact address, unit number, resident contact information, and property management contact.*\n\n*CONFIRM YOU HAVE THE EXPERIENCE AND TOOLS REQUIRED BEFORE APPLYING FOR THIS WORK ORDER.*\n\n**Scope of Work****Dispatch an experienced network technician to perform onsite Wi-Fi signal, connectivity, and performance testing within the resident’s apartment.**\n\n**The resident is reporting poor or no usable Wi-Fi signal in the bedroom located furthest from the Access Point (AP).**\n\n**Remote monitoring currently indicates that the network equipment and AP are online and operating normally**. This dispatch is intended to perform **onsite location-based testing** throughout the unit to verify actual Wi-Fi coverage and performance from the resident’s perspective.\n\nThe technician must document the results and work directly with GiGstreem Support/Network Operations to confirm that the network and AP are functioning properly.\n\n**Work Details**- Check in with the leasing office/property staff before entering the resident’s unit.\n- Contact **GiGstreem Support/Network Operations** upon arrival and coordinate testing.\n- Verify that the installed AP is online and operating normally.\n- Visually inspect the AP and surrounding area for any obvious physical or environmental issues.\n- Using the **provider/technician laptop**, connect to the GiGstreem Wi-Fi network and perform onsite testing.\n- Perform Wi-Fi **signal, connectivity, and speed testing throughout the apartment**.\n- Test directly near the AP to establish a baseline.\n- Test from the living room and other primary areas of the unit.\n- **Test from the furthest bedroom where the resident is reporting poor or no signal.**\n- **Record Wi-Fi signal strength/RSSI, connection quality, download speed, upload speed, and latency where available.**\n- **Verify whether the provider laptop maintains a stable Wi-Fi connection in the affected bedroom.**\n- **Compare testing from the provider laptop with the resident’s device when possible to determine whether there is a significant difference between devices.**\n- **If the resident's device experiences an issue that cannot be duplicated using the provider laptop, clearly document this in the work order.**\n- **Verify the resident is connecting to the correct GiGstreem Wi-Fi network/SSID.**\n- **Test multiple locations within the affected bedroom when necessary to determine the extent of the coverage issue.**\n- **Contact GiGstreem Support/Network Operations** and review all test results before completing the visit.\n- Follow any additional troubleshooting instructions provided by Support/Engineering.\n- Take photos of the AP location and any relevant equipment or conditions.\n- Upload detailed documentation showing **where each test was performed and the results of each test**.\n- **Before leaving the property, contact the manager listed in the confidential notes and provide the onsite testing results and findings.**\n- **Do not leave the site until GiGstreem Support/Network Operations has reviewed the findings and the manager listed in the confidential notes has been contacted.**\n\n**Required Testing Documentation**Technician must provide clear testing results for each major location within the unit, especially:\n\n**1. Near the Access Point**\n\n- Signal/RSSI\n- Download speed\n- Upload speed\n- Latency/ping\n- Connection stability\n\n**2. Living Room / Main Area**\n\n- Signal/RSSI\n- Download speed\n- Upload speed\n- Latency/ping\n- Connection stability\n\n**3. Furthest Bedroom / Reported Problem Area**\n\n- Signal/RSSI\n- Download speed\n- Upload speed\n- Latency/ping\n- Connection stability\n\nClearly identify whether the issue was **duplicated using the provider laptop**.\n\n**Technician Expectations**- **Confirm the appointment time** with the customer before heading to the property.\n- **Place a courtesy call at least 30 minutes prior to arrival** to inform the customer of your estimated time of arrival (ETA).\n- Upon arriving on site, all Field Nation technicians are required to **check in at the leasing office or front desk before proceeding to the unit.** Contractors must announce their arrival and present their Field Nation ID and credentials for verification. **Entry into any resident’s unit is not permitted until this check-in process is completed and approved by onsite staff.**\n- **Represent the brand** with professionalism. Appearance, communication, and the quality of work must reflect high standards.\n- **Do not overshare** internal processes or technical details with the customer. Communication should be simple, courteous, and focused on testing and resolving the reported issue.\n- Do not promise equipment changes, AP relocation, additional APs, credits, or other solutions unless specifically authorized by GiGstreem.\n- ⚠️ *If the technician arrives unprepared, misinforms the customer, demonstrates poor presentation, or delivers substandard work, GiGstreem reserves the right to withhold payment for the work order.*\n\n**Required Experience**- Wi-Fi signal and performance troubleshooting\n- Troubleshooting Ruckus Access Points\n- Networking/Telecommunications experience\n- Understanding of Wi-Fi RSSI/signal strength, interference, latency, throughput, and coverage\n- Ability to perform and document location-based Wi-Fi testing\n- Experience working with remote Network Operations/Engineering teams\n\n**Required Tools**- **Laptop with Wi-Fi and Ethernet capability**\n- **USB-to-Ethernet adapter if laptop does not have an Ethernet port**\n- **Wi-Fi signal/RSSI testing capability**\n- **Speed test capability**\n- **Cable tester**\n- **Known-good Ethernet patch cables**\n- **Basic hand tools**\n- **Flashlight**\n- **Smartphone for photos and documentation**\n- **Mobile hotspot for communication with Support if needed**\n\n**Coordination**- Troubleshoot in collaboration with **GiGstreem Support/Network Operations**.\n- Remote monitoring currently indicates the network and AP are online; therefore, **onsite location testing and documentation are critical for this dispatch.**\n- **Refer to confidential notes for Network Operations, resident, and property management contact details.**\n- **Contact the manager listed in the confidential notes before leaving the property to provide the final testing results.**\n\n**Policy on Wi-Fi Extenders – GiGstreem Policy Reminder**At GiGstreem, delivering reliable, high-performance internet service is our top priority. To maintain the integrity of our network and ensure consistent customer experiences, we follow strict guidelines regarding the equipment and solutions we support.\n\n**It is strictly against GiGstreem policy to utilize, install, or recommend Wi-Fi extenders as a solution for speed, coverage, or connectivity issues within a unit.**\n\n**Why This Matters:**\n\n- Wi-Fi extenders are not part of our approved network architecture.\n- They can introduce interference, degrade performance, and complicate troubleshooting.\n- Recommending or installing extenders may lead to inconsistent service and customer dissatisfaction.\n\n**Approved Resolution Methods:**\n\n- Thorough onsite testing of the existing AP and network configuration.\n- Wi-Fi signal and performance testing from multiple locations within the unit.\n- Comparison testing using a GiGstreem/provider laptop versus the resident’s device.\n- Collaboration with Support/Engineering to assess AP performance and configuration.\n- Documentation and escalation of confirmed coverage issues for management/Engineering review.\n\n**Technicians must not relocate an AP, install additional equipment, or recommend Wi-Fi extenders without authorization from GiGstreem Support/Engineering or management.**\n\n**All technicians and support staff must adhere to this policy without exception. Any deviation or recommended network modification must be escalated to GiGstreem management for review.**\n\n- **I specifically made the furthest bedroom test the priority**, while also requiring a baseline near the AP and comparison with the provider laptop. That should give you solid evidence to determine whether this is an actual coverage issue, a resident-device issue, or something Engineering needs to address.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-21T10:00","end":"2026-09-21T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":200,"max":275},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":200},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":75}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":3},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $275 is below minimum threshold $400"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Busy"},{"start":"2026-09-22T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"gap"},{"start":"2026-09-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-09-23T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"sta