{"job":{"id":19972550,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Brandpoint Services","title":"Troubleshoot & Possibly Rerun Cat6 Drop at Costco","description":{"html":"<p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Ref:MSG1737232_0jRFXbZblJPjNYZIkryR</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Service request: First Available ETA at 4:30 AM</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Warehouse #: 1587 (Raleigh, NC)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Number of technicians required: (1)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Time allocated for SOW: 5.5 hours (Contact PRN support for additional time if required)</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Description: The warehouse would like a technician to Repair/Replace (2) Cat6 drops, Restore media player connectivity, Connect parts &amp; Restore all TVs with Costco feed, Perform Cable cleanup/management, Verify PRN system wiring, Check HDMI cables from Amp to TVs, Configure TVs to HOME mode, Re-label all cables</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Confirm media player connectivity</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Point of Contact: Jordan</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">PRN Doc110uments (Download or view directly from the link)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">• </span>https://bit.ly/CostcoTVNetwork</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Tools:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">A Cable Label maker is required, and clear scotch tape</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">White Cat cable required (300'-400' white CAT6 cable)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">The technician must bring white CAT6 cable, tester/toner, and labels to label cables. cable management supplies</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Check-in: (Before starting any work in the warehouse)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">1. Contact Brandpoint tier 1: 856-382-2645 TEXT ONLY or email </span>checkoutteam@brandpointservices.com<span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\"> and copy costcosupport@stratacache to check-in</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">2. PRN/Stratacache tier 1: call support 888-776-5589 (on overnights and weekends also email </span>costcosupport@stratacache.com<span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">) -- if no answer: BKUP line 415-617-9752</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">3. Upon arrival in TV department, locate the site contact listed below</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">4. Check in with the point of contact below, review the SOW</span></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Initial Checks before starting work: (Costco feed is Blue/white or yellow/white concierge logo, top right corner of the TVs)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Enter the building through the back door</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Speak with the point of contact listed above for the TV department</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">1. Review the scope of work with the POC</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">2. Request the TV remotes' location or the box of remotes to turn on all the TVs</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">3. With the TVs turned ON, perform a count of what's playing Costco feed out of the total number of TVs in the department (x out of y)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">4. Take before pictures and email them to the service vendor list above</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">4a. Capture pictures of any broken TVs and inform the managers before starting any work</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">5. Confirm with the service vendor that the BrightSign player is online</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">5a. Proceed to perform the SOW below</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">SOW:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Locate the Super Plate (BrightSign 4K player)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Start from the Super Plate (4K Player and a batch of Cat6 cables coming down)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Costco content is the blue/white concierge logo in the top right corner of the TV</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Verify with the vendor that the media player is online</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">First priority - Repair/Replace Cat6 drops and connect parts &amp; restore the Costco feed on all TVs</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Second priority - Restore media player connectivity, Verify the PRN system is wired correctly</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Third priority - Survey the TV department if additional parts are requested, Perform cable clean up &amp; management (zip tie HDMI &amp; Cat6 cables)</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Turn ON all TVs</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Upon arrival, perform a count of the TVs playing Costco content and the total number of TVs in the department</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Costco feed is Blue/white or yellow/white concierge logo top right corner of the TVs</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Restore media player connectivity (the PRN Homerun)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Troubleshoot the Homerun media player (verify it is fully seated and Cat6 cable is labeled PRN-HR that is connected)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">-- If the Cat6 cable has a link light, contact PRN support 888-776-5589 to verify connectivity</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Troubleshoot the Homerun Cat6 cable</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Repair the homerun Cat6 cable if damaged</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">-- If the Homerun is damaged near the TV department install an RJ45 biscuit/surface jack in rafters (label jack as PRN HR)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">-- Run a patch cable from the biscuit/surface jack to the media player - label the patch cable \"PRN HR\"</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Label the Homerun as \"PRN Homerun\" in three places on the Cat6 cable</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Restore Costco content playback on TVs</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Repair/Replace (2) Cat6 drops - Manager to identify</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">-- For each location verify/take picture of playing Costco feed</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">-- Label each drop on both ends (take picture of the label)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Connect parts &amp; restore Costco feed on all TVs (except waterfalls and endcaps) - yellow/white concierge logo top right corner of the TVs</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Verify the PRN system is wired correctly</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Connect HDMI cables from the Amp to TVs for Costco content playback</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Locate all Distribution Amps and confirm there is a 4K TV connected to OUTPUT 1 port</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Each Amp should have a TV connected to an OUTPUT 1 port</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Verify all Amp dip switches are set correctly</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Check cables (damaged HDMI &amp; Cat6 drop), repair any damaged Cat6 drop and replace HDMI cables</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Cable management and clean up</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Perform cable clean-up (remove old unused Cat6 drops)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Perform cable management of Cat6 and HDMI cables (secure HDMI and Cat6 cables with zip ties)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Re-label all Cat6 drops</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Configure all TVs to HOME mode</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Label each Cat6 per instructions in the label guide doc</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Verify Media player connectivity with support</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Take lots of before and after pictures of all aisles and PODs playing Costco content</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Locate all Distribution Amps and confirm there is a 4K TV connected to the HDMI OUTPUT 1 port</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Each Amp should have a TV connected to an OUTPUT 1 port</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Re-label all Cat6 cables being used to pass the Costco signal</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- All labels should be legible and clear to read on both ends</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Label the CAT6 cable the same on both ends (6\" from the connector with a Sharpie and 12\" out with a label maker, wrap with clear scotch tape)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- CAT6 cable naming scheme: (G1 being gondola/pod)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Cat6 Cable drop labeling scheme: G1-4K, G2-4K, G3-4K, and ON</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Cat6 DON'Ts</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- DO NOT USE jumpers on Cat6 cable runs that are passing Costco feed HDMI video signal</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Verify the Extender has a solid BLUE LED = Good operation</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Blue/Green flashing = bad CAT6 or HDMI cable (cannot communicate with transmitter correctly)</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Startech/GEFEN extenders are POE, only the Sender/Transmitter requires power</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Check-out process:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">1. Verify the media player is still ONLINE after the work with the service vendor</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">2. Take lots of after pictures of all aisles and PODs playing Costco feed</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">3. Pictures of Cat6 drops ran their labels on both ends</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">4. TV playing Costco feed playback</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">5. Clean up and conduct a walk-through with the manager, making sure they are pleased with the work</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">6. If parts are required and management does not have inventory, create a parts list and provide the details during checkout to the service vendor</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">7. Complete the latest manager &amp; technician checklist &amp; upload it to the portal, and email it to PRN support</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- A checklist is required for every visit (even if the work is not completed)</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">On completion of work, to receive the release code:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- M-F: Contact Brandpoint | on Weekends: contact PRN/Stratacache</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Contact Brandpoint at 856-382-2645 TEXT ONLY to ensure the media player is/are online and that no further troubleshooting is needed.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Check out with the manager on duty, perform a walkthrough of the TV department, and confirm that they are happy with the work</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">- Send photos of the concepts that were serviced, showing the system powered on with a valid Costco feed and manager's sign-off checklist</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Email: </span>checkoutteam@brandpointservices.com<span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\"> and/or </span>costcosupport@stratacache.com</p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">If needed, contact PRN/Stratacache Support #: 888-776-5589 for support</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">The above check-in and check-out deliverables are required and must be received for the checkout code</span></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Required equipment:&nbsp;</p><p>WHITE cat6 (500'+ preferable), crimp tool, RJ45 male connectors, cat6 tester/toner, labeling and wire management supplies.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Required Skills:</p><p>Cat6, HDMI, HDMI-Cat-6 Converters, Video Wall Setup. Scissor Lift.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>AN ACTUAL LEGACY DISPATCH WILL BE SENT <u>BY EMAIL</u> WITH ALL THE PROPER JOB ATTACHMENTS YOU WILL NEED TO ACCURATELY COMPLETE THE JOB AND GET PAID.&nbsp;WORK MARKET WILL JUST BE OUR PLATFORM FOR PAYMENT</p><p><br></p>","markdown":"Ref:MSG1737232\\_0jRFXbZblJPjNYZIkryR\n\nService request: First Available ETA at 4:30 AM\n\nWarehouse #: 1587 (Raleigh, NC)\n\nNumber of technicians required: (1)\n\nTime allocated for SOW: 5.5 hours (Contact PRN support for additional time if required)\n\nDescription: The warehouse would like a technician to Repair/Replace (2) Cat6 drops, Restore media player connectivity, Connect parts & Restore all TVs with Costco feed, Perform Cable cleanup/management, Verify PRN system wiring, Check HDMI cables from Amp to TVs, Configure TVs to HOME mode, Re-label all cables\n\nConfirm media player connectivity\n\nPoint of Contact: Jordan\n\nPRN Doc110uments (Download or view directly from the link)\n\n• <https://bit.ly/CostcoTVNetwork>\n\nTools:\n\nA Cable Label maker is required, and clear scotch tape\n\nWhite Cat cable required (300'-400' white CAT6 cable)\n\nThe technician must bring white CAT6 cable, tester/toner, and labels to label cables. cable management supplies\n\nCheck-in: (Before starting any work in the warehouse)\n\n1\\. Contact Brandpoint tier 1: 856-382-2645 TEXT ONLY or email checkoutteam@brandpointservices.com and copy costcosupport@stratacache to check-in\n\n2\\. PRN/Stratacache tier 1: call support 888-776-5589 (on overnights and weekends also email costcosupport@stratacache.com) -- if no answer: BKUP line 415-617-9752\n\n3\\. Upon arrival in TV department, locate the site contact listed below\n\n4\\. Check in with the point of contact below, review the SOW\n\nInitial Checks before starting work: (Costco feed is Blue/white or yellow/white concierge logo, top right corner of the TVs)\n\nEnter the building through the back door\n\nSpeak with the point of contact listed above for the TV department\n\n1\\. Review the scope of work with the POC\n\n2\\. Request the TV remotes' location or the box of remotes to turn on all the TVs\n\n3\\. With the TVs turned ON, perform a count of what's playing Costco feed out of the total number of TVs in the department (x out of y)\n\n4\\. Take before pictures and email them to the service vendor list above\n\n4a. Capture pictures of any broken TVs and inform the managers before starting any work\n\n5\\. Confirm with the service vendor that the BrightSign player is online\n\n5a. Proceed to perform the SOW below\n\nSOW:\n\nLocate the Super Plate (BrightSign 4K player)\n\nStart from the Super Plate (4K Player and a batch of Cat6 cables coming down)\n\nCostco content is the blue/white concierge logo in the top right corner of the TV\n\nVerify with the vendor that the media player is online\n\nFirst priority - Repair/Replace Cat6 drops and connect parts & restore the Costco feed on all TVs\n\nSecond priority - Restore media player connectivity, Verify the PRN system is wired correctly\n\nThird priority - Survey the TV department if additional parts are requested, Perform cable clean up & management (zip tie HDMI & Cat6 cables)\n\n  \n\\\n\n\\- Turn ON all TVs\n\n\\- Upon arrival, perform a count of the TVs playing Costco content and the total number of TVs in the department\n\nCostco feed is Blue/white or yellow/white concierge logo top right corner of the TVs\n\nRestore media player connectivity (the PRN Homerun)\n\n\\- Troubleshoot the Homerun media player (verify it is fully seated and Cat6 cable is labeled PRN-HR that is connected)\n\n\\-- If the Cat6 cable has a link light, contact PRN support 888-776-5589 to verify connectivity\n\n\\- Troubleshoot the Homerun Cat6 cable\n\n\\- Repair the homerun Cat6 cable if damaged\n\n\\-- If the Homerun is damaged near the TV department install an RJ45 biscuit/surface jack in rafters (label jack as PRN HR)\n\n\\-- Run a patch cable from the biscuit/surface jack to the media player - label the patch cable \"PRN HR\"\n\n\\- Label the Homerun as \"PRN Homerun\" in three places on the Cat6 cable\n\nRestore Costco content playback on TVs\n\n\\- Repair/Replace (2) Cat6 drops - Manager to identify\n\n\\-- For each location verify/take picture of playing Costco feed\n\n\\-- Label each drop on both ends (take picture of the label)\n\n\\- Connect parts & restore Costco feed on all TVs (except waterfalls and endcaps) - yellow/white concierge logo top right corner of the TVs\n\n\\- Verify the PRN system is wired correctly\n\n\\- Connect HDMI cables from the Amp to TVs for Costco content playback\n\n\\- Locate all Distribution Amps and confirm there is a 4K TV connected to OUTPUT 1 port\n\n\\- Each Amp should have a TV connected to an OUTPUT 1 port\n\n  \n\\\n\n\\- Verify all Amp dip switches are set correctly\n\n\\- Check cables (damaged HDMI & Cat6 drop), repair any damaged Cat6 drop and replace HDMI cables\n\nCable management and clean up\n\n\\- Perform cable clean-up (remove old unused Cat6 drops)\n\n\\- Perform cable management of Cat6 and HDMI cables (secure HDMI and Cat6 cables with zip ties)\n\n\\- Re-label all Cat6 drops\n\n  \n\\\n\n\\- Configure all TVs to HOME mode\n\n\\- Label each Cat6 per instructions in the label guide doc\n\n\\- Verify Media player connectivity with support\n\n  \n\\\n\n\\- Take lots of before and after pictures of all aisles and PODs playing Costco content\n\nLocate all Distribution Amps and confirm there is a 4K TV connected to the HDMI OUTPUT 1 port\n\n\\- Each Amp should have a TV connected to an OUTPUT 1 port\n\nRe-label all Cat6 cables being used to pass the Costco signal\n\n\\- All labels should be legible and clear to read on both ends\n\n\\- Label the CAT6 cable the same on both ends (6\" from the connector with a Sharpie and 12\" out with a label maker, wrap with clear scotch tape)\n\n\\- CAT6 cable naming scheme: (G1 being gondola/pod)\n\n\\- Cat6 Cable drop labeling scheme: G1-4K, G2-4K, G3-4K, and ON\n\nCat6 DON'Ts\n\n\\- DO NOT USE jumpers on Cat6 cable runs that are passing Costco feed HDMI video signal\n\nVerify the Extender has a solid BLUE LED = Good operation\n\nBlue/Green flashing = bad CAT6 or HDMI cable (cannot communicate with transmitter correctly)\n\nStartech/GEFEN extenders are POE, only the Sender/Transmitter requires power\n\nCheck-out process:\n\n1\\. Verify the media player is still ONLINE after the work with the service vendor\n\n2\\. Take lots of after pictures of all aisles and PODs playing Costco feed\n\n3\\. Pictures of Cat6 drops ran their labels on both ends\n\n4\\. TV playing Costco feed playback\n\n5\\. Clean up and conduct a walk-through with the manager, making sure they are pleased with the work\n\n6\\. If parts are required and management does not have inventory, create a parts list and provide the details during checkout to the service vendor\n\n7\\. Complete the latest manager & technician checklist & upload it to the portal, and email it to PRN support\n\n\\- A checklist is required for every visit (even if the work is not completed)\n\nOn completion of work, to receive the release code:\n\n\\- M-F: Contact Brandpoint | on Weekends: contact PRN/Stratacache\n\n\\- Contact Brandpoint at 856-382-2645 TEXT ONLY to ensure the media player is/are online and that no further troubleshooting is needed.\n\n\\- Check out with the manager on duty, perform a walkthrough of the TV department, and confirm that they are happy with the work\n\n\\- Send photos of the concepts that were serviced, showing the system powered on with a valid Costco feed and manager's sign-off checklist\n\nEmail: checkoutteam@brandpointservices.com and/or costcosupport@stratacache.com\n\nIf needed, contact PRN/Stratacache Support #: 888-776-5589 for support\n\nThe above check-in and check-out deliverables are required and must be received for the checkout code\n\nRequired equipment:\n\nWHITE cat6 (500'+ preferable), crimp tool, RJ45 male connectors, cat6 tester/toner, labeling and wire management supplies.\n\nRequired Skills:\n\nCat6, HDMI, HDMI-Cat-6 Converters, Video Wall Setup. Scissor Lift.\n\nAN ACTUAL LEGACY DISPATCH WILL BE SENT BY EMAIL WITH ALL THE PROPER JOB ATTACHMENTS YOU WILL NEED TO ACCURATELY COMPLETE THE JOB AND GET PAID. WORK MARKET WILL JUST BE OUR PLATFORM FOR PAYMENT","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-18T04:30","end":"2026-09-25T04:30"},"payRange":{"min":130,"max":350},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":130},"additional":{"units":4,"amount":55}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":14},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 9/18/2026, 4:30:00 AM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-18T21:00:0