{"job":{"id":"7936423906","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"LEGACY Retail Services","title":"Troubleshoot A/V System and Possible Rerun WHITE Cat 6 w/ Device Install at Retail Store","description":"<p>On arrival you must check in with your brandpoint support rep at 856-382-2645 via text. This number will not receive phone calls.</p><p><br></p><p>Ref:MSG1737232_0jRFXbZblJPjNYZIkryR</p><p><br></p><p>Service request: First Available ETA at 4:30 AM</p><p>Warehouse #: 1587 (Raleigh, NC)</p><p>Number of technicians required: (1)</p><p>Time allocated for SOW: 5.5 hours (Contact PRN support for additional time if required)</p><p><br></p><p>Description: The warehouse would like a technician to Repair/Replace (2) Cat6 drops, Restore media player connectivity, Connect parts &amp; Restore all TVs with Costco feed, Perform Cable cleanup/management, Verify PRN system wiring, Check HDMI cables from Amp to TVs, Configure TVs to HOME mode, Re-label all cables</p><p>Confirm media player connectivity</p><p><br></p><p>Point of Contact: Jordan</p><p><br></p><p>PRN Doc110uments (Download or view directly from the link)</p><p>• <a href=\"https://bit.ly/CostcoTVNetwork\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bit.ly/CostcoTVNetwork</a></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Tools:</p><p>A Cable Label maker is required, and clear scotch tape</p><p>White Cat cable required (300'-400' white CAT6 cable)</p><p>The technician must bring white CAT6 cable, tester/toner, and labels to label cables. cable management supplies</p><p><br></p><p>Check-in: (Before starting any work in the warehouse)</p><p>1. Contact Brandpoint tier 1: 856-382-2645 TEXT ONLY or email <a href=\"mailto:checkoutteam@brandpointservices.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">checkoutteam@brandpointservices.com</a> and copy costcosupport@stratacache to check-in</p><p>2. PRN/Stratacache tier 1: call support 888-776-5589 (on overnights and weekends also email <a href=\"mailto:costcosupport@stratacache.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">costcosupport@stratacache.com</a>) -- if no answer: BKUP line 415-617-9752</p><p>3. Upon arrival in TV department, locate the site contact listed below</p><p>4. Check in with the point of contact below, review the SOW</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Initial Checks before starting work: (Costco feed is Blue/white or yellow/white concierge logo, top right corner of the TVs)</p><p>Enter the building through the back door</p><p>Speak with the point of contact listed above for the TV department</p><p>1. Review the scope of work with the POC</p><p>2. Request the TV remotes' location or the box of remotes to turn on all the TVs</p><p>3. With the TVs turned ON, perform a count of what's playing Costco feed out of the total number of TVs in the department (x out of y)</p><p>4. Take before pictures and email them to the service vendor list above</p><p>4a. Capture pictures of any broken TVs and inform the managers before starting any work</p><p>5. Confirm with the service vendor that the BrightSign player is online</p><p>5a. Proceed to perform the SOW below</p><p><br></p><p>SOW:</p><p>Locate the Super Plate (BrightSign 4K player)</p><p>Start from the Super Plate (4K Player and a batch of Cat6 cables coming down)</p><p>Costco content is the blue/white concierge logo in the top right corner of the TV</p><p>Verify with the vendor that the media player is online</p><p><br></p><p>First priority - Repair/Replace Cat6 drops and connect parts &amp; restore the Costco feed on all TVs</p><p>Second priority - Restore media player connectivity, Verify the PRN system is wired correctly</p><p>Third priority - Survey the TV department if additional parts are requested, Perform cable clean up &amp; management (zip tie HDMI &amp; Cat6 cables)</p><p><br></p><p>- Turn ON all TVs</p><p>- Upon arrival, perform a count of the TVs playing Costco content and the total number of TVs in the department</p><p><br></p><p>Costco feed is Blue/white or yellow/white concierge logo top right corner of the TVs</p><p><br></p><p>Restore media player connectivity (the PRN Homerun)</p><p>- Troubleshoot the Homerun media player (verify it is fully seated and Cat6 cable is labeled PRN-HR that is connected)</p><p>-- If the Cat6 cable has a link light, contact PRN support 888-776-5589 to verify connectivity</p><p>- Troubleshoot the Homerun Cat6 cable</p><p>- Repair the homerun Cat6 cable if damaged</p><p>-- If the Homerun is damaged near the TV department install an RJ45 biscuit/surface jack in rafters (label jack as PRN HR)</p><p>-- Run a patch cable from the biscuit/surface jack to the media player - label the patch cable \"PRN HR\"</p><p>- Label the Homerun as \"PRN Homerun\" in three places on the Cat6 cable</p><p><br></p><p>Restore Costco content playback on TVs</p><p>- Repair/Replace (2) Cat6 drops - Manager to identify</p><p>-- For each location verify/take picture of playing Costco feed</p><p>-- Label each drop on both ends (take picture of the label)</p><p>- Connect parts &amp; restore Costco feed on all TVs (except waterfalls and endcaps) - yellow/white concierge logo top right corner of the TVs</p><p>- Verify the PRN system is wired correctly</p><p>- Connect HDMI cables from the Amp to TVs for Costco content playback</p><p>- Locate all Distribution Amps and confirm there is a 4K TV connected to OUTPUT 1 port</p><p>- Each Amp should have a TV connected to an OUTPUT 1 port</p><p><br></p><p>- Verify all Amp dip switches are set correctly</p><p>- Check cables (damaged HDMI &amp; Cat6 drop), repair any damaged Cat6 drop and replace HDMI cables</p><p><br></p><p>Cable management and clean up</p><p>- Perform cable clean-up (remove old unused Cat6 drops)</p><p>- Perform cable management of Cat6 and HDMI cables (secure HDMI and Cat6 cables with zip ties)</p><p>- Re-label all Cat6 drops</p><p><br></p><p>- Configure all TVs to HOME mode</p><p>- Label each Cat6 per instructions in the label guide doc</p><p>- Verify Media player connectivity with support</p><p><br></p><p>- Take lots of before and after pictures of all aisles and PODs playing Costco content</p><p><br></p><p>Locate all Distribution Amps and confirm there is a 4K TV connected to the HDMI OUTPUT 1 port</p><p>- Each Amp should have a TV connected to an OUTPUT 1 port</p><p><br></p><p>Re-label all Cat6 cables being used to pass the Costco signal</p><p>- All labels should be legible and clear to read on both ends</p><p>- Label the CAT6 cable the same on both ends (6\" from the connector with a Sharpie and 12\" out with a label maker, wrap with clear scotch tape)</p><p>- CAT6 cable naming scheme: (G1 being gondola/pod)</p><p>- Cat6 Cable drop labeling scheme: G1-4K, G2-4K, G3-4K, and ON</p><p><br></p><p>Cat6 DON'Ts</p><p>- DO NOT USE jumpers on Cat6 cable runs that are passing Costco feed HDMI video signal</p><p><br></p><p>Verify the Extender has a solid BLUE LED = Good operation</p><p>Blue/Green flashing = bad CAT6 or HDMI cable (cannot communicate with transmitter correctly)</p><p>Startech/GEFEN extenders are POE, only the Sender/Transmitter requires power</p><p><br></p><p>Check-out process:</p><p>1. Verify the media player is still ONLINE after the work with the service vendor</p><p>2. Take lots of after pictures of all aisles and PODs playing Costco feed</p><p>3. Pictures of Cat6 drops ran their labels on both ends</p><p>4. TV playing Costco feed playback</p><p><br></p><p>5. Clean up and conduct a walk-through with the manager, making sure they are pleased with the work</p><p>6. If parts are required and management does not have inventory, create a parts list and provide the details during checkout to the service vendor</p><p>7. Complete the latest manager &amp; technician checklist &amp; upload it to the portal, and email it to PRN support</p><p>- A checklist is required for every visit (even if the work is not completed)</p><p><br></p><p>On completion of work, to receive the release code:</p><p>- M-F: Contact Brandpoint | on Weekends: contact PRN/Stratacache</p><p>- Contact Brandpoint at 856-382-2645 TEXT ONLY to ensure the media player is/are online and that no further troubleshooting is needed.</p><p>- Check out with the manager on duty, perform a walkthrough of the TV department, and confirm that they are happy with the work</p><p>- Send photos of the concepts that were serviced, showing the system powered on with a valid Costco feed and manager's sign-off checklist</p><p>Email: <a href=\"mailto:checkoutteam@brandpointservices.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">checkoutteam@brandpointservices.com</a> and/or <a href=\"mailto:costcosupport@stratacache.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">costcosupport@stratacache.com</a></p><p>If needed, contact PRN/Stratacache Support #: 888-776-5589 for support</p><p><br></p><p>The above check-in and check-out deliverables are required and must be received for the checkout code</p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-18T04:30","end":"2026-09-18T06:30"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":350},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":12.7},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"TV\" in description"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-21T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Busy"},{"start":"2026-09-22T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"gap"},{"start":"2026-09-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ​Concord Police Department - NC ( Phase 2 ) (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-2