{"job":{"id":19985940,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TruMed Systems","title":"Vaccine Management Machine - Near excursion alert - 50102","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Scope of Work OVERVIEW</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">Reported Issues: Tech is to clean the air filters on the unit with a T2 and after PM post assessment determine if a TXV is needed.. Tracking: No Parts Required</span></p><p><strong>Video Tutorials Below</strong></p><p><strong><u>**If there is no tracking, there is no package**</u></strong></p><p><del>************ *********** ********** </del><del>****************************</del></p><p><del>*** ** **** *** **** ** *** **** </del><del>****************************</del></p><p><del>*** ** ****** *** </del><del>****************************</del></p><p><del>*** ** ******* ***** ***** ******** </del><del>****************************</del></p><p><del>*** ** ******* ******** **** *************</del><del>*******************************************</del></p><p><strong>TRUMED TRAINING REQUIRED TO BE ELIGIBLE FOR THIS WO</strong>. The training is paid and available to any interested technician. Email Darrell.Hulse@trumedsystems.com to have the training assigned to you.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>You MUST have the tools listed in the file: TOOLS REQUIRED TO GET PAID.</strong></p><p><strong>Scope Specific Tools</strong></p><ul><li>PPE</li><li>T20 Torx Driver</li><li>T10 Torx Driver</li><li>T10 Allen key</li><li>4 mm Allen key or Flat Head Screwdriver</li><li>Magnetizer </li><li>Magnetic screw dish</li></ul><p>DO NOT USE POWER TOOLS </p><p>&nbsp;<strong>Essential Hardware</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Torx tools</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>T20 Torx Dri</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">T10 Torx Driver</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">T5 Torx Driver</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">1.3 mm driver&nbsp;</li><li>Sharpie</li><li>6mm, 5mm, 4mm, 3mm, 2.5mm, 2mm Allen wrench set</li><li>T20, T10, T8 Driver or T-Tool</li><li>Torx key set (T20, T15, T10, T8, T5)</li><li>Mini ratchet with T30, T20, T15, T10, T8, T5 bits</li><li>Standard 4&ndash;6\" Phillips screwdriver</li><li>Large flathead screwdriver or pry tool</li><li>Wire cutters</li><li>Wire stripping tool</li><li>Wire crimping tool</li><li>Wire butt connectors</li><li>13mm crescent wrench</li><li>Socket set with ratchet including:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">6mm</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">6.5mm</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">7mm</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">8mm</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">10mm</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">11mm</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">12mm</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">13mm</li><li>Digital multimeter / voltmeter</li><li>Handheld vacuum</li><li>Needle-nose pliers</li><li>Standard pliers</li><li>Channel-lock pliers</li><li>Extendable magnetic pickup tool for dropped screws</li><li>Tool magnetizer for retaining screws on driver heads</li><li>Utility knife</li><li>X-Acto knife</li><li>4\" (small) zip ties</li><li>Electrical tape</li><li>Suction cup (90 lb. rating)</li><li>Standard sheet of paper (used as a feeler gauge to check for seal gaps)</li></ul><p><strong>Cleaning &amp; Advanced Repair</strong></p><ul><li>Double-sided foam tape (3M or equivalent)</li><li>Heat gun (required only for L-bracket repair jobs)</li><li>Square-edge X-Acto blade (required only for L-bracket repair jobs)</li><li>Alcohol wipes</li><li>Window cleaner</li><li>Paper towels</li><li>Nitrile gloves</li><li>Cup, container, or plastic case for storing screws</li><li>10-amp automotive fuse</li><li>15-amp automotive fuse</li></ul><p><strong>Convenience &amp; Specialty Tools</strong></p><ul><li>Sharpie or permanent marker</li><li>EZ-Out stripped bolt extractor</li><li>Step stool (minimum 12\" height; required for external battery units)</li><li>Tool bag or hard case carrier</li><li>Magnetized tray or magnetic parts bin for screw storage (recommended)</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Professional Conduct Requirements</strong></p><ul><li>Arrive fit for duty</li><li>No drug or alcohol impairment while performing work</li><li>No odor of marijuana, alcohol, or other substances while onsite</li><li>Unauthorized technician substitutions are prohibited</li><li>Only the technician approved and assigned through the Field Nation work order may perform the work unless prior written approval is obtained</li><li>Comply with all customer site policies, security requirements, and safety procedures</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Physical Requirements</strong></p><ul><li>Ability to safely lift up to 30 lbs. overhead</li><li>Ability to safely lift up to 60 lbs. at ground level</li><li>Ability to kneel, crouch, bend, and work at floor level for extended periods</li><li>Ability to work in pharmacies, clinics, healthcare facilities, offices, equipment rooms, and commercial environments</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>DRESS CODE:&nbsp;</strong>Professional and clean attire. No hats or baseball caps; only collared shirts without business logos are allowed.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>***YOU MUST FOLLOW THE WORK INSTRUCTIONS TO BE SUCCESSFUL.***</strong></p><ul><li>Confirm you have the required tools. (Torx tools are a MUST)</li><li>Covid safe PPE and work behavior expected onsite at all times</li><li>Ensure timely arrival on-site</li><li>Locate AccuVax kiosk and confirm serial number</li></ul><p>Call TruMed Support and review the Scope of Work, if you are having issues reaching a Tech call Darrell (858)240-5229 or Thomas Goins (844)878-6331x763 right away to help expedite help.</p><ul><li>DO NOT remove the interior panel unless directed by TruMed Support</li><li>DO NOT move the robot by hand unless directed</li><li><strong>ALWAYS </strong>fully assemble the unit after you are done</li><li>Most repairs take 2-3 hours. If you have time constraints state them up front.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(182, 66, 76);\"><span class=\"ql-cursor\">﻿</span>Travel &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(182, 66, 76);\"> Travel expense under 60 miles round trip, or over .70 / mile, will not be approved. All requests must be pre-approved via counteroffer.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Payments are processed within a reasonable timeframe following completion of services.</strong></p>","markdown":"**Scope of Work OVERVIEW**\n\nReported Issues: Tech is to clean the air filters on the unit with a T2 and after PM post assessment determine if a TXV is needed.. Tracking: No Parts Required\n\n**Video Tutorials Below**\n\n**\\*\\*If there is no tracking, there is no package\\*\\***\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**TRUMED TRAINING REQUIRED TO BE ELIGIBLE FOR THIS WO**. The training is paid and available to any interested technician. Email Darrell.Hulse@trumedsystems.com to have the training assigned to you.\n\n**You MUST have the tools listed in the file: TOOLS REQUIRED TO GET PAID.**\n\n**Scope Specific Tools**\n\n- PPE\n- T20 Torx Driver\n- T10 Torx Driver\n- T10 Allen key\n- 4 mm Allen key or Flat Head Screwdriver\n- Magnetizer\n- Magnetic screw dish\n\nDO NOT USE POWER TOOLS\n\n **Essential Hardware**\n\n- **Torx tools**\n- **T20 Torx Dri**\n- T10 Torx Driver\n- T5 Torx Driver\n- 1.3 mm driver\n- Sharpie\n- 6mm, 5mm, 4mm, 3mm, 2.5mm, 2mm Allen wrench set\n- T20, T10, T8 Driver or T-Tool\n- Torx key set (T20, T15, T10, T8, T5)\n- Mini ratchet with T30, T20, T15, T10, T8, T5 bits\n- Standard 4–6\" Phillips screwdriver\n- Large flathead screwdriver or pry tool\n- Wire cutters\n- Wire stripping tool\n- Wire crimping tool\n- Wire butt connectors\n- 13mm crescent wrench\n- Socket set with ratchet including:\n- 6mm\n- 6.5mm\n- 7mm\n- 8mm\n- 10mm\n- 11mm\n- 12mm\n- 13mm\n- Digital multimeter / voltmeter\n- Handheld vacuum\n- Needle-nose pliers\n- Standard pliers\n- Channel-lock pliers\n- Extendable magnetic pickup tool for dropped screws\n- Tool magnetizer for retaining screws on driver heads\n- Utility knife\n- X-Acto knife\n- 4\" (small) zip ties\n- Electrical tape\n- Suction cup (90 lb. rating)\n- Standard sheet of paper (used as a feeler gauge to check for seal gaps)\n\n**Cleaning & Advanced Repair**\n\n- Double-sided foam tape (3M or equivalent)\n- Heat gun (required only for L-bracket repair jobs)\n- Square-edge X-Acto blade (required only for L-bracket repair jobs)\n- Alcohol wipes\n- Window cleaner\n- Paper towels\n- Nitrile gloves\n- Cup, container, or plastic case for storing screws\n- 10-amp automotive fuse\n- 15-amp automotive fuse\n\n**Convenience & Specialty Tools**\n\n- Sharpie or permanent marker\n- EZ-Out stripped bolt extractor\n- Step stool (minimum 12\" height; required for external battery units)\n- Tool bag or hard case carrier\n- Magnetized tray or magnetic parts bin for screw storage (recommended)\n\n**Professional Conduct Requirements**\n\n- Arrive fit for duty\n- No drug or alcohol impairment while performing work\n- No odor of marijuana, alcohol, or other substances while onsite\n- Unauthorized technician substitutions are prohibited\n- Only the technician approved and assigned through the Field Nation work order may perform the work unless prior written approval is obtained\n- Comply with all customer site policies, security requirements, and safety procedures\n\n**Physical Requirements**\n\n- Ability to safely lift up to 30 lbs. overhead\n- Ability to safely lift up to 60 lbs. at ground level\n- Ability to kneel, crouch, bend, and work at floor level for extended periods\n- Ability to work in pharmacies, clinics, healthcare facilities, offices, equipment rooms, and commercial environments\n\n**DRESS CODE:** Professional and clean attire. No hats or baseball caps; only collared shirts without business logos are allowed.\n\n**\\*\\*\\*YOU MUST FOLLOW THE WORK INSTRUCTIONS TO BE SUCCESSFUL.\\*\\*\\***\n\n- Confirm you have the required tools. (Torx tools are a MUST)\n- Covid safe PPE and work behavior expected onsite at all times\n- Ensure timely arrival on-site\n- Locate AccuVax kiosk and confirm serial number\n\nCall TruMed Support and review the Scope of Work, if you are having issues reaching a Tech call Darrell (858)240-5229 or Thomas Goins (844)878-6331x763 right away to help expedite help.\n\n- DO NOT remove the interior panel unless directed by TruMed Support\n- DO NOT move the robot by hand unless directed\n- **ALWAYS** fully assemble the unit after you are done\n- Most repairs take 2-3 hours. If you have time constraints state them up front.\n\n**﻿Travel & Expenses Approval Payment Policy:** Travel expense under 60 miles round trip, or over .70 / mile, will not be approved. All requests must be pre-approved via counteroffer.\n\n**Payments are processed within a reasonable timeframe following completion of services.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-21T10:00","end":"2026-09-21T14:00","latestStart":"2026-09-21T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":260},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":4},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":