{"job":{"id":19986473,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Ovation Workplace Services","title":"Need Logistic Support technician ","description":{"html":"<p><strong><em><u>Job Role – Tech Logistics Support Technician Logistics-experience required 1-3 years</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em><u>Job Summary</u></em></strong>:</p><p>The Tech Logistics Support Technician will provide daily <strong><u>logistical support-on site,</u></strong> for the Tech Logistics North America Hub located in North Carolina.&nbsp;The role requires the applicant to master the daily logistics tasks which make up the logistics role. The logistics tech role interacts and supports all other roles in the TechHub. Daily tasks may include and are not limited to:</p><p>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><u>Bundle assets and consumables</u></strong> for shipment to end users for requests.</p><p>2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong><u>Processing/Shipping Hardware Reclaims</u></strong> to US and Canada for requests.</p><ol><li><strong><u>Use UPS WorldShip Application </u></strong>to ship assets, return cartons, and send ERLs (electronic return labels) to users outside of the normal Service Now ticketing system.</li><li><strong><u>Trac</u></strong>k shipments for user inquiries and provide information to resolve delayed and lost shipments, by contacting UPS and creating incidents. &nbsp;</li><li><strong><u>Work in ServiceNow </u></strong>to create requests, document updates, complete tasks, monitor requests for user updates and respond with required information in a timely efficient manner. </li><li><strong><u>Assist in the Preparation of obsolete equipment for disposa</u></strong>l and coordination of salvage shipments (ITAD) when required. </li><li><strong><u>Maintain Inventory of supplies</u></strong> to ensure proper stock of boxes and packing materials associated with shipping/receiving. </li><li><strong><u>Verify and update </u></strong>receiving spreadsheets for shipments of new PCs and consumables when required.</li><li><strong><u>Check logistics equipment</u></strong> for proper operation to ensure safety, escalate concerns for repair or replacement to TechHub team lead.</li><li><strong><u>Assisting/Cross training in other areas as needed to ensure positive user experiences within SLA.</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>Strong communication skills both verbal and written to support clients and team members to ensure a positive environment.</u></strong></li></ol><p>The ideal candidate should have 1-3 years’ relevant experience in one or more of the following areas: Logistics <strong><u>(Shipping /Receiving), Inventory Control</u></strong>, <strong><u>ITAD,</u></strong> <strong><u>fulfilling hardware requests</u></strong> through a ticketing program (ServiceNow, Remedy, etc.), and excellent written and oral communication skills. Willing to train the right person with a team-oriented attitude.&nbsp;</p><p>Other qualities and duties:</p><p>a) Knowledge of domestic (US) and/or international shipping procedures and applications such as UPS Worldship, FEDEX, DHL, etc., </p><p>b) Post ticket updates for <strong><u>all </u></strong>individual work completed.</p><p>&nbsp;c) Have a working knowledge of Microsoft Office 365 Office Suite -Outlook, Excel, and Word.</p><p>d) This position requires standing, bending and lifting packages up to 50lbs. without assistance. </p><p>&nbsp;e) The ability to work in a fast-paced environment requiring flexibility and <strong><u>teamwork.</u></strong> </p><p>i.) Perform other duties as assigned to help team succeed and meet goals. </p><p>&nbsp;</p>","markdown":"***Job Role – Tech Logistics Support Technician Logistics-experience required 1-3 years***\n\n***Job Summary***:\n\nThe Tech Logistics Support Technician will provide daily **logistical support-on site,** for the Tech Logistics North America Hub located in North Carolina. The role requires the applicant to master the daily logistics tasks which make up the logistics role. The logistics tech role interacts and supports all other roles in the TechHub. Daily tasks may include and are not limited to:\n\n1\\. **Bundle assets and consumables** for shipment to end users for requests.\n\n2\\. **Processing/Shipping Hardware Reclaims** to US and Canada for requests.\n\n1. **Use UPS WorldShip Application** to ship assets, return cartons, and send ERLs (electronic return labels) to users outside of the normal Service Now ticketing system.\n2. **Trac**k shipments for user inquiries and provide information to resolve delayed and lost shipments, by contacting UPS and creating incidents.\n3. **Work in ServiceNow** to create requests, document updates, complete tasks, monitor requests for user updates and respond with required information in a timely efficient manner.\n4. **Assist in the Preparation of obsolete equipment for disposa**l and coordination of salvage shipments (ITAD) when required.\n5. **Maintain Inventory of supplies** to ensure proper stock of boxes and packing materials associated with shipping/receiving.\n6. **Verify and update** receiving spreadsheets for shipments of new PCs and consumables when required.\n7. **Check logistics equipment** for proper operation to ensure safety, escalate concerns for repair or replacement to TechHub team lead.\n8. **Assisting/Cross training in other areas as needed to ensure positive user experiences within SLA.**\n9. **Strong communication skills both verbal and written to support clients and team members to ensure a positive environment.**\n\nThe ideal candidate should have 1-3 years’ relevant experience in one or more of the following areas: Logistics **(Shipping /Receiving), Inventory Control**, **ITAD,** **fulfilling hardware requests** through a ticketing program (ServiceNow, Remedy, etc.), and excellent written and oral communication skills. Willing to train the right person with a team-oriented attitude.\n\nOther qualities and duties:\n\na) Knowledge of domestic (US) and/or international shipping procedures and applications such as UPS Worldship, FEDEX, DHL, etc.,\n\nb) Post ticket updates for **all** individual work completed.\n\n c) Have a working knowledge of Microsoft Office 365 Office Suite -Outlook, Excel, and Word.\n\nd) This position requires standing, bending and lifting packages up to 50lbs. without assistance.\n\n e) The ability to work in a fast-paced environment requiring flexibility and **teamwork.**\n\ni.) Perform other duties as assigned to help team succeed and meet goals.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-21T08:00","end":"2026-09-21T40:00"},"payRange":{"min":40,"max":1280},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":40,"estLaborHours":32,"distance":7},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No in-hours counter slot available\nRequested: Mon, Sep 21, 8:00 AM\nChecked: Mon, Sep 21, Tue, Sep 22, Wed, Sep 23, Thu, Sep 24, Fri, Sep 25 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Busy"},{"start":"2026-09-22T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"gap"},{"start":"2026-09-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-09-23T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Miniso"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ​Concord Police Department - NC ( Phase 2 ) (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-22T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"Remote Hands - Connect AT&T broadband circuit"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789753842379}
{"job":{"id":19984860,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Insight Enterprises Inc.","title":"Insight | Hilton | New Hardware Placement | Service Tech | Schedule date/time is FIRM","description":{"html":"<p>Insight has been engaged by Hilton Hotels to perform New Hardware Placements at their locations nation wide. The qualified resource will have the skill set and ability to perform the work, follow instructions and report to Insight. Hilton is expecting we are onsite until the job is complete</p><p>We are seeking a senior service technician/Network Smart Hands level tech. There is no network configuration but you must rack and stack devices. The expected duration is 4-8 hours depending on the device count.</p><p><strong><u>Scope (see also attached document as applicable):</u></strong></p><p>- Rack and Stack (connect cables and power) configured network devices:&nbsp;Server, Switch and UPS</p><p>- Unbox new workstations and accessories</p><p>- IF cable has been run to front desk and offices set up each computer in the required desk/office location.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;- Proper cable management for a neat look at all stations</p><p>- IF cable has not been run then connect all think clients directly to the switch in the network room</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;- Hotel manager will move computers to required location at a later date</p><p>- Run Systems check on each computer to verify no DOA</p><p>- Verify Remote Technical support can connect to each thin client</p><p>- Once onsite contact Technical Support to get instructions and direction.&nbsp;There are no field instructions at this time, direction and instruction comes from technical support.</p><p><strong><u>Dress:</u></strong>&nbsp;Business Casual. No sneakers, jeans, t-shirts, etc.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Penalties/Deductions</strong>:</p><p>10% Deduction for 15 minutes or more late.</p><p>10% Deduction for being unprepared.</p><p>Tech swaps MUST be approved in advance. Failure to do so will result in no pay of WO.</p><p>Unauthorized assistants are prohibited from all Insight work. Those assistants will be asked to leave and wait offsite for you to complete the job.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Terms for Travel:</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Payment amount listed on this WO is an all-in rate</p><p>If provider is seeking additional compensation for travel time due to distance from work order, this must be requested as a counter-offer PRIOR to assignment</p><p>If submitted post-assignment, pay increase requests for travel time will not be approved</p><p>Tolls or Parking fees will only be eligible for reimbursement if receipt is attached to the work order when closed out</p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Terms for Additional Time Required Onsite</strong>:</p><p>Technician must call buyer contact listed in WO immediately upon realizing additional time over max hours in WO will be required</p><p>If additional time required is due to factors agreed to by buyer as outside of tech control; technician may submit request for pay increase for time onsite over max in WO&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;IMPORTANT: Pay increase for additional time must be requested and Approved by buyer while tech is onsite; additional time logged by tech on WO or pay increase requests will only be paid if tech obtained pre-approval from buyer POC while onsite</p><p>Tech must enter name of buyer contact who approved increase to ensure any approval questions are directed accordingly</p><p><br></p><p><em>The job is considered incomplete if you leave site before sending any required deliverables and calling Insight Command Center to check out, which will cause a delay in pay or no compensation.&nbsp;</em></p>","markdown":"Insight has been engaged by Hilton Hotels to perform New Hardware Placements at their locations nation wide. The qualified resource will have the skill set and ability to perform the work, follow instructions and report to Insight. Hilton is expecting we are onsite until the job is complete\n\nWe are seeking a senior service technician/Network Smart Hands level tech. There is no network configuration but you must rack and stack devices. The expected duration is 4-8 hours depending on the device count.\n\n**Scope (see also attached document as applicable):**\n\n\\- Rack and Stack (connect cables and power) configured network devices: Server, Switch and UPS\n\n\\- Unbox new workstations and accessories\n\n\\- IF cable has been run to front desk and offices set up each computer in the required desk/office location.\n\n\\- Proper cable management for a neat look at all stations\n\n\\- IF cable has not been run then connect all think clients directly to the switch in the network room\n\n\\- Hotel manager will move computers to required location at a later date\n\n\\- Run Systems check on each computer to verify no DOA\n\n\\- Verify Remote Technical support can connect to each thin client\n\n\\- Once onsite contact Technical Support to get instructions and direction. There are no field instructions at this time, direction and instruction comes from technical support.\n\n**Dress:** Business Casual. No sneakers, jeans, t-shirts, etc.\n\n**Penalties/Deductions**:\n\n10% Deduction for 15 minutes or more late.\n\n10% Deduction for being unprepared.\n\nTech swaps MUST be approved in advance. Failure to do so will result in no pay of WO.\n\nUnauthorized assistants are prohibited from all Insight work. Those assistants will be asked to leave and wait offsite for you to complete the job.\n\n**Terms for Travel:**\n\nPayment amount listed on this WO is an all-in rate\n\nIf provider is seeking additional compensation for travel time due to distance from work order, this must be requested as a counter-offer PRIOR to assignment\n\nIf submitted post-assignment, pay increase requests for travel time will not be approved\n\nTolls or Parking fees will only be eligible for reimbursement if receipt is attached to the work order when closed out\n\n**Terms for Additional Time Required Onsite**:\n\nTechnician must call buyer contact listed in WO immediately upon realizing additional time over max hours in WO will be required\n\nIf additional time required is due to factors agreed to by buyer as outside of tech control; technician may submit request for pay increase for time onsite over max in WO\n\n IMPORTANT: Pay increase for additional time must be requested and Approved by buyer while tech is onsite; additional time logged by tech on WO or pay increase requests will only be paid if tech obtained pre-approval from buyer POC while onsite\n\nTech must enter name of buyer contact who approved increase to ensure any approval questions are directed accordingly\n\n*The job is considered incomplete if you leave site before sending any required deliverables and calling Insight Command Center to check out, which will cause a delay in pay or no compensation.*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-23T09:00","end":"2026-09-23T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":180,"max":450},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":4,"amount":180},"additional":{"units":6,"amount":45}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":7},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"blended","counterRate":60,"baseAmount":600,"estHours":4,"travelExpense":0,"payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":4,"amount":240},"additional":{"units":6,"amount":60}},"counterDate":{"start":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T17:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":60,"mode":"hours","reason":"arrival_window"}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"}],"bu