:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1789754302949}
{"job":{"id":19986384,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Argus IT Services","title":"Smart H&F for Troubleshooting Network Devices - APs Down/300ft Cable Run","description":{"html":"<strong>HCL Onsite Network Support – Technician Field Guide</strong><strong>Purpose of Visit</strong><p>This ticket is to <strong>troubleshoot a network or store device</strong> on behalf of <strong>HCL</strong> in response to a reported <strong>Incident</strong>.</p><p><br></p><strong>Teams is required and must remain active for the full duration of the visit. If your time is different than what you were actively working with the NOC team on the bridge, your WO will be marked incomplete.</strong><br><strong><u>Travel expenses must be in your counter and accepted prior to you arriving at the store. Any travel tacked on afterwards, will be denied. All materials will be reimbursed on the WO.</u></strong><br><strong>1. Arrival &amp; Store Check-In</strong><ul><li>Present <strong>valid Photo ID</strong> (Driver’s License).</li><li>Identify yourself as an <strong>HCL Network Technician</strong>, dispatched <strong>on behalf of the NOC Team</strong> to troubleshoot a network device reported offline.</li><li>If denied access:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Notify the NOC team immediately on the bridge</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Contact the <strong>WO Manager</strong> for escalation</li></ul><strong>2. Onsite Procedures</strong><ul><li><strong>Join the Teams bridge</strong> using the link, ID, and passcode from the Confidential section</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>If it is saying the link doesn't exist/is valid, you need to uninstall/reinstall Teams. The link is valid and working.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Send an email to ADUSA_FSCC@hcltech.com with your Incident if you have issues with joining the bridge.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If that doesn't work, please try using browser and incognito mode and type in the meeting ID and password.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Stay connected for the entire visit</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Please tell them when you get there and when you leave, as well as what the next action is needed.</li><li>In the meeting chat, enter:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>INC#</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>Arrival time</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Departure time</strong></li><li><strong><u>Do not leave the site unless released by the NOC team</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>The NOC team on the bridge will you send you to a second bridge. If you have been on that second bridge for a while with no one from the NOC team joining, rejoin the primary bridge and let them know.</u></strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>They will create a secondary room for your specific ticket/issue. You will work with the team for your specific issue. Please join back the main bridge once you are finished to check out.</u></strong></p><p><strong>﻿</strong></p><strong>3. Post-Service Actions</strong><ul><li>Document all work performed in the <strong>FieldNation closing notes</strong></li><li>Notify <strong>Argus</strong> of the resolution prior to departure</li><li>Return any unused parts using the provided <strong>return label</strong> (if applicable)</li></ul><strong>4. Required Tools &amp; Equipment</strong><ul><li>Smartphone with hotspot</li><li>Laptop with admin access, Teams, Putty, and email</li><li>Console cables (USB to RJ45)</li><li>Cable Tester / Toner</li><li>Wi-Fi analyzer app</li><li>IT hardware repair kit</li><li>Patch cables, crimpers, cable testers</li><li>Spare RJ-45 connectors (<strong>MUST BE CAT6)</strong></li><li>Spare Ethernet cables (various lengths)</li><li>General hand tools and accessories</li></ul><p><strong>5. Ticket notes from client:</strong></p><p>\"Required 19ft. lift and std1586ap90 has issue with cabling</p><p>Need to align the tech any day, 7 AM - 10 PM EST.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Requirement Details:</p><p><br></p><p>1. Impacted Device: Aruba AP-635, Aruba AP-677 (std1586ap06, std1586ap90)</p><p>2. Location: Food Lion - 1586 Carthage</p><p>3. Problem Statement: std1586ap06, std1586ap90 has issue with cabling</p><p>4. What troubleshooting has been completed:</p><p>Noticed that one of the pairs of the cable run is open for AP06.</p><p>sw1586a#show cable-diagnostics tdr interface gigabitEthernet 2/0/24</p><p>TDR test last run on: September 07 04:37:29</p><p>Interface Speed Local pair Pair length Remote pair Pair status</p><p>--------- ----- ---------- ------------------ ----------- --------------------</p><p>Gi2/0/24 auto Pair A 0 +/- 10 meters N/A Open</p><p>Pair B 1 +/- 10 meters N/A Open</p><p>Pair C 0 +/- 10 meters N/A Open</p><p>Pair D 1 +/- 10 meters N/A Open</p><p>sw1586a#show cable-diagnostics tdr interface gigabitEthernet 2/0/35</p><p>TDR test last run on: September 07 04:37:34</p><p>Interface Speed Local pair Pair length Remote pair Pair status</p><p>--------- ----- ---------- ------------------ ----------- --------------------</p><p>Gi2/0/35 1000M Pair A 72 +/- 10 meters Pair B Normal</p><p>Pair B 72 +/- 10 meters Pair A Normal</p><p>Pair C 72 +/- 10 meters Pair D Normal</p><p>Pair D 72 +/- 10 meters Pair C Normal</p><p>5. What do they need from a field tech and any parts/tools that may be needed:</p><p>• Laptop with internet connection and teams installed. Before visiting the location, please make sure that the laptop should be able to take console.</p><p>• Compatible console cable (AP-CBL-SERU) for Aruba AP635, Short cable, Cable tester, patch cables are required.</p><p>Lift required : May or may not be required</p><p>6.The steps expected from the Technician to preform while onsite:</p><p>• Once Tech is onsite, he should connect with the HCL wireless team through the troubleshoot bridge.</p><p>• Need to run the cable test.</p><p>• Need to provide console of AP, if required, to Wireless Team.</p><p>• Need to change the interface for AP if requested.</p><p>• Need to check by connecting the AP with the short cable if needed.</p><p>• Need to re-terminate the ends of the cable, if requested.</p><p>• Need to run the new cable from the AP to the switch, if required\"</p><p><strong><u>If you need a schedule change/want to request the work order - REQUEST A SCHEDULE CHANGE. We can troubleshoot as long as the store is open. Whatever time you get there, we will adjust on the WO so it doesn't impact your rating.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>The phone number on the Work Order is for on-site escalations and emergencies. Calling the number repeatedly everyday for future work consideration, will result in not using you as a technician for future engagements.</u></strong></p>","markdown":"**HCL Onsite Network Support – Technician Field Guide****Purpose of Visit**This ticket is to **troubleshoot a network or store device** on behalf of **HCL** in response to a reported **Incident**.\n\n**Teams is required and must remain active for the full duration of the visit. If your time is different than what you were actively working with the NOC team on the bridge, your WO will be marked incomplete.**  \n**Travel expenses must be in your counter and accepted prior to you arriving at the store. Any travel tacked on afterwards, will be denied. All materials will be reimbursed on the WO.**  \n**1. Arrival & Store Check-In**- Present **valid Photo ID** (Driver’s License).\n- Identify yourself as an **HCL Network Technician**, dispatched **on behalf of the NOC Team** to troubleshoot a network device reported offline.\n- If denied access:\n- **Notify the NOC team immediately on the bridge**\n- Contact the **WO Manager** for escalation\n\n**2. Onsite Procedures**- **Join the Teams bridge** using the link, ID, and passcode from the Confidential section\n- **If it is saying the link doesn't exist/is valid, you need to uninstall/reinstall Teams. The link is valid and working.**\n- **Send an email to ADUSA\\_FSCC@hcltech.com with your Incident if you have issues with joining the bridge.**\n- If that doesn't work, please try using browser and incognito mode and type in the meeting ID and password.\n- Stay connected for the entire visit\n- Please tell them when you get there and when you leave, as well as what the next action is needed.\n- In the meeting chat, enter:\n- **INC#**\n- **Arrival time**\n- **Departure time**\n- **Do not leave the site unless released by the NOC team**\n- **The NOC team on the bridge will you send you to a second bridge. If you have been on that second bridge for a while with no one from the NOC team joining, rejoin the primary bridge and let them know.**\n\n**They will create a secondary room for your specific ticket/issue. You will work with the team for your specific issue. Please join back the main bridge once you are finished to check out.**\n\n**﻿**\n\n**3. Post-Service Actions**- Document all work performed in the **FieldNation closing notes**\n- Notify **Argus** of the resolution prior to departure\n- Return any unused parts using the provided **return label** (if applicable)\n\n**4. Required Tools & Equipment**- Smartphone with hotspot\n- Laptop with admin access, Teams, Putty, and email\n- Console cables (USB to RJ45)\n- Cable Tester / Toner\n- Wi-Fi analyzer app\n- IT hardware repair kit\n- Patch cables, crimpers, cable testers\n- Spare RJ-45 connectors (**MUST BE CAT6)**\n- Spare Ethernet cables (various lengths)\n- General hand tools and accessories\n\n**5. Ticket notes from client:**\n\n\"Required 19ft. lift and std1586ap90 has issue with cabling\n\nNeed to align the tech any day, 7 AM - 10 PM EST.\n\nRequirement Details:\n\n1\\. Impacted Device: Aruba AP-635, Aruba AP-677 (std1586ap06, std1586ap90)\n\n2\\. Location: Food Lion - 1586 Carthage\n\n3\\. Problem Statement: std1586ap06, std1586ap90 has issue with cabling\n\n4\\. What troubleshooting has been completed:\n\nNoticed that one of the pairs of the cable run is open for AP06.\n\nsw1586a#show cable-diagnostics tdr interface gigabitEthernet 2/0/24\n\nTDR test last run on: September 07 04:37:29\n\nInterface Speed Local pair Pair length Remote pair Pair status\n\n\\--------- ----- ---------- ------------------ ----------- --------------------\n\nGi2/0/24 auto Pair A 0 +/- 10 meters N/A Open\n\nPair B 1 +/- 10 meters N/A Open\n\nPair C 0 +/- 10 meters N/A Open\n\nPair D 1 +/- 10 meters N/A Open\n\nsw1586a#show cable-diagnostics tdr interface gigabitEthernet 2/0/35\n\nTDR test last run on: September 07 04:37:34\n\nInterface Speed Local pair Pair length Remote pair Pair status\n\n\\--------- ----- ---------- ------------------ ----------- --------------------\n\nGi2/0/35 1000M Pair A 72 +/- 10 meters Pair B Normal\n\nPair B 72 +/- 10 meters Pair A Normal\n\nPair C 72 +/- 10 meters Pair D Normal\n\nPair D 72 +/- 10 meters Pair C Normal\n\n5\\. What do they need from a field tech and any parts/tools that may be needed:\n\n• Laptop with internet connection and teams installed. Before visiting the location, please make sure that the laptop should be able to take console.\n\n• Compatible console cable (AP-CBL-SERU) for Aruba AP635, Short cable, Cable tester, patch cables are required.\n\nLift required : May or may not be required\n\n6.The steps expected from the Technician to preform while onsite:\n\n• Once Tech is onsite, he should connect with the HCL wireless team through the troubleshoot bridge.\n\n• Need to run the cable test.\n\n• Need to provide console of AP, if required, to Wireless Team.\n\n• Need to change the interface for AP if requested.\n\n• Need to check by connecting the AP with the short cable if needed.\n\n• Need to re-terminate the ends of the cable, if requested.\n\n• Need to run the new cable from the AP to the switch, if required\"\n\n**If you need a schedule change/want to request the work order - REQUEST A SCHEDULE CHANGE. We can troubleshoot as long as the store is open. Whatever time you get there, we will adjust on the WO so it doesn't impact your rating.**\n\n**The phone number on the Work Order is for on-site escalations and emergencies. Calling the number repeatedly everyday for future work consideration, will result in not using you as a technician for future engagements.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-22T07:00","end":"2026-09-22T19:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":220},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":52},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $220 (countered: $240) is below minimum threshold $400"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-22T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"gap"},{"start":"2026-09-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-09-23T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Miniso"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ​Concord Police Department - NC ( Phase 2 ) (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 059749