{"job":{"id":19978229,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Randstad Technologies","title":"Nike Circuit Activation","description":{"html":"<p><u>Expected time onsite 1 - 4 hours</u></p><p><strong>Technician MUST arrive onsite with enough time to set up and connect to the bridge call at the time indicated on the bridge invitation.</strong></p><p><strong>Technician MUST arrive with laptop, printed run book and have the Zoom app installed. </strong></p><p><strong>***Please note that the bridge call will include 4 - 7 participants and you may be asked to activate your camera with focus on the room &amp; equipment</strong></p><p><strong>Must be able to terminate and test Cat5E/6 cables while on site.</strong></p><p><strong>A working laptop w 100 Mbps full duplex testing to connect to client network is absolutely required to complete this order- a spare is recommended.</strong></p><p>Runbook will be provided prior to arrival onsite with specific tasks for site visit.</p><p>Have a hard copy of provided run book and CSO with you on site.</p><p><strong>Tools required:</strong></p><ul><li>Laptop (to run speed tests), spare recommended</li><li>Zoom pre-installed on laptop or mobile device</li><li>Cable Crimper and Tester</li><li>min 20ft CAT6 Plenum cable or two 10' CAT6 patch cables (reimbursed if used)</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work</u></strong></p><p><u>Site visit to include:</u></p><ul><li>Contact the Work Order Manager then join the customer ZOOM bridge upon arriving onsite</li><li>Locate new circuit on site by Circuit ID provided</li><li>Conduct speed tests- SPEEDTEST.GOOGLEFIBER.NET need photos of three(3) screen captures of completed speed tests on laptop.</li><li>Determine length of patch cable needed to connect new circuit to laptop first then dress in rack once testing complete</li><li>Complete cable run as directed by customer w IP and Port info from your printed run book sheet</li><li>Follow all client PM/Eng verbal directions given on the bridge</li><li>Test and Turn Up New Circuit</li><li>Circuit test prior to activation, do not disconnect old circuit or connect new circuit until directed by client’s tech.</li><li><strong>Photos Needed:</strong> Please make sure to upload the requested photos to the work order, and email those photos to the customer (their email is in the text/runbook).</li><li>Work with customer to test circuit and network connectivity throughout retail store</li><li>Clean up – perform cable management</li><li>No equipment is to be removed from site.</li></ul><p><strong>Cable Run may be required (tech will be made aware before time and go over the plan with the tech)</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Deliverables (Due within 24 hours of site completion):</u></strong></p><ul><li>Before and after photos of equipment</li><li>3 Speedtest Screen Captures</li><li>Signed Customer Sign Off Form</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Status as Independent Contractor</strong></p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;In the performance of the Services, the Provider shall act solely as an independent contractor, and nothing herein contained or implied will at any time be construed so as to create the relationship of employer and employee, partnership, principal and agent, or joint venture as between Company and the Provider or Company’s end client and Provider. Provider shall have no authority to bind the Company or Company’s end client in any way or make any representations or warranties on behalf of the Company and shall not represent to any person or entity that Provider has such authority.&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Acceptance of the Work Order by Provider shall be construed as Provider’s acknowledgment and acceptance of this Section and Provider’s willingness to indemnify Company and Company’s end client in the event of a breach of this Section.</strong></p><p><strong>PER THE PROVIDER POLICY - UNAUTHORIZED SUBSTITUTION OF THE ASSIGNED PROVIDER IS NOT ALLOWED.</strong></p><p><em><u>**UNDER NO CIRCUMSTANCE IS AN ASSIGNED PROVIDER ALLOWED TO SUBSTITUTE A TECHNICIAN WITHOUT PRIOR APPROVAL FROM THE DESIGNATED RANDSTAD CONTACT LISTED. FAILURE TO FOLLOW THIS REQUIREMENT MAY RESULT IN REMOVAL FROM THE PROJECT WITHOUT PAY AND BLOCKED FROM ANY FUTURE WORK WITH RANDSTAD.**</u></em></p><ul><li>Along with platform check-in/out, please call the Support Contact listed in the work order when you arrive onsite and before you leave site for the day.</li><li><em>Unless otherwise agreed upon PRIOR to work order acceptance, Randstad WILL NOT be responsible for or raise spend limits for Provider fees, Workers Compensation fees, gas, mileage, drive time or any other fees incurred by Provider after acceptance of the work order.</em></li><li><em>If you accept the work order, you are accepting and agreeing to the rates shown.</em></li><li><em>This does not apply to additional time onsite due to no fault of Provider.&nbsp;<u>ANY/ALL</u>&nbsp;additional time onsite, special tools not called out in the work order or Out of Scope work&nbsp;<u>MUST</u>&nbsp;be approved by the designated Randstad contact PRIOR to being performed or purchased. Any tools, materials, additional time onsite or out of scope work performed without prior approval by the Randstad contact will be done at the&nbsp;<u>Provider's expense</u>&nbsp;and compensation for such will be at the discretion of Randstad.</em></li><li><em>Under no circumstances should work order details such as re-scheduling, compensation, out of scope work, etc., be discussed with the Customer/End User. All communications of this type should be addressed with the designated Randstad contact only.</em></li></ul><p><em>If you cannot abide by the agreed upon terms, then please do not apply to the work order. If you wish to discuss compensation for these fees, then kindly follow protocol and submit a conditional offer or clarification question prior to assignment of the work order.&nbsp;</em></p><p><u>ONCE THE WORK ORDER IS ACCEPTED, THE RATE IS SET AS STATED.</u></p>","markdown":"Expected time onsite 1 - 4 hours\n\n**Technician MUST arrive onsite with enough time to set up and connect to the bridge call at the time indicated on the bridge invitation.**\n\n**Technician MUST arrive with laptop, printed run book and have the Zoom app installed.**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*Please note that the bridge call will include 4 - 7 participants and you may be asked to activate your camera with focus on the room & equipment**\n\n**Must be able to terminate and test Cat5E/6 cables while on site.**\n\n**A working laptop w 100 Mbps full duplex testing to connect to client network is absolutely required to complete this order- a spare is recommended.**\n\nRunbook will be provided prior to arrival onsite with specific tasks for site visit.\n\nHave a hard copy of provided run book and CSO with you on site.\n\n**Tools required:**\n\n- Laptop (to run speed tests), spare recommended\n- Zoom pre-installed on laptop or mobile device\n- Cable Crimper and Tester\n- min 20ft CAT6 Plenum cable or two 10' CAT6 patch cables (reimbursed if used)\n\n**Scope of Work**\n\nSite visit to include:\n\n- Contact the Work Order Manager then join the customer ZOOM bridge upon arriving onsite\n- Locate new circuit on site by Circuit ID provided\n- Conduct speed tests- SPEEDTEST.GOOGLEFIBER.NET need photos of three(3) screen captures of completed speed tests on laptop.\n- Determine length of patch cable needed to connect new circuit to laptop first then dress in rack once testing complete\n- Complete cable run as directed by customer w IP and Port info from your printed run book sheet\n- Follow all client PM/Eng verbal directions given on the bridge\n- Test and Turn Up New Circuit\n- Circuit test prior to activation, do not disconnect old circuit or connect new circuit until directed by client’s tech.\n- **Photos Needed:** Please make sure to upload the requested photos to the work order, and email those photos to the customer (their email is in the text/runbook).\n- Work with customer to test circuit and network connectivity throughout retail store\n- Clean up – perform cable management\n- No equipment is to be removed from site.\n\n**Cable Run may be required (tech will be made aware before time and go over the plan with the tech)**\n\n**Deliverables (Due within 24 hours of site completion):**\n\n- Before and after photos of equipment\n- 3 Speedtest Screen Captures\n- Signed Customer Sign Off Form\n\n**Status as Independent Contractor**\n\n**· In the performance of the Services, the Provider shall act solely as an independent contractor, and nothing herein contained or implied will at any time be construed so as to create the relationship of employer and employee, partnership, principal and agent, or joint venture as between Company and the Provider or Company’s end client and Provider. Provider shall have no authority to bind the Company or Company’s end client in any way or make any representations or warranties on behalf of the Company and shall not represent to any person or entity that Provider has such authority.**\n\n**· Acceptance of the Work Order by Provider shall be construed as Provider’s acknowledgment and acceptance of this Section and Provider’s willingness to indemnify Company and Company’s end client in the event of a breach of this Section.**\n\n**PER THE PROVIDER POLICY - UNAUTHORIZED SUBSTITUTION OF THE ASSIGNED PROVIDER IS NOT ALLOWED.**\n\n*\\*\\*UNDER NO CIRCUMSTANCE IS AN ASSIGNED PROVIDER ALLOWED TO SUBSTITUTE A TECHNICIAN WITHOUT PRIOR APPROVAL FROM THE DESIGNATED RANDSTAD CONTACT LISTED. FAILURE TO FOLLOW THIS REQUIREMENT MAY RESULT IN REMOVAL FROM THE PROJECT WITHOUT PAY AND BLOCKED FROM ANY FUTURE WORK WITH RANDSTAD.\\*\\**\n\n- Along with platform check-in/out, please call the Support Contact listed in the work order when you arrive onsite and before you leave site for the day.\n- *Unless otherwise agreed upon PRIOR to work order acceptance, Randstad WILL NOT be responsible for or raise spend limits for Provider fees, Workers Compensation fees, gas, mileage, drive time or any other fees incurred by Provider after acceptance of the work order.*\n- *If you accept the work order, you are accepting and agreeing to the rates shown.*\n- *This does not apply to additional time onsite due to no fault of Provider. ANY/ALL additional time onsite, special tools not called out in the work order or Out of Scope work MUST be approved by the designated Randstad contact PRIOR to being performed or purchased. Any tools, materials, additional time onsite or out of scope work performed without prior approval by the Randstad contact will be done at the Provider's expense and compensation for such will be at the discretion of Randstad.*\n- *Under no circumstances should work order details such as re-scheduling, compensation, out of scope work, etc., be discussed with the Customer/End User. All communications of this type should be addressed with the designated Randstad contact only.*\n\n*If you cannot abide by the agreed upon terms, then please do not apply to the work order. If you wish to discuss compensation for these fees, then kindly follow protocol and submit a conditional offer or clarification question prior to assignment of the work order.*\n\nONCE THE WORK ORDER IS ACCEPTED, THE RATE IS SET AS STATED.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-13T07:45","end":"2026-10-13T10:45"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":150},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":32},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $150 (countered: $180) is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-12T04:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-18T04:00:00.000Z","summary":"Durham RTP"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"