g distance calls unless the client provides toll free number. We will not reimburse you for long distance calls. Please insist on Microsoft Teams meeting instead (if they don't provide it, contact Telesol).</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope of work</u></strong></p><p>Dispatch description:</p><p>Troubleshoot current NID and if necessary install replacement NID </p><p>Work Type: <span style=\"color: rgb(24, 24, 24);\">Repair</span></p><p><strong>﻿</strong>Additional task details provided in&nbsp;<em>Confidential Information</em>&nbsp;section below.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Special access requirements (if any):</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Special tools (if any):</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Required Tool List</strong></p><ul><li>Screwdriver and Rack Screws for racking/mounting equipment</li><li>Label Maker</li><li>Mobile Internet access with charger (hot spot)</li><li>Mobile phone with charger</li><li>Mask &amp; gloves available (PPE as needed) if customer requires</li><li>Windows based laptop with charger (no Chromebook, mac, or tablets)</li><li>Laptop with ethernet connection (via built‑in port or USB‑to‑Ethernet adapter) must support speeds up to <strong>1000 Mbps (1G)</strong>, Teamveiwer software installed</li><li>Ability to change/assign static IP on Laptop (Admin Access)</li><li>Screen sharing software (AnyDesk):</li><li>Hyper-Terminal/Putty or other console emulator software:</li><li>1G USB-Ethernet Adapter with correct drivers and ready to use</li><li>Cisco DB9 to Serial USB Adapter</li><li>Cisco RJ-45 to Serial USB Adapter</li><li>Standard DB9 to Serial USB Adapter</li><li>Cisco micro-USB to Serial USB Adapter</li><li>Spare cables to be left at the site as needed:</li><li>(4-6) Ethernet cables</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><em>Preferred but not required</em></strong></p><ul><li>SC-LC and LC-LC Single Mode Fiber and Multi-Mode Fiber Patch Cables</li><li>Standard Telecom tool set (snips, punch down, crimpers, cable toner/probe, wire strippers, etc.) For Legacy Products DSL, Voice etc.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Escalation Process:</strong></p><ul><li><strong><em>Any issues or questions should be escalated to <u><del> ********************</del></u></em></strong></li><li><strong><em>Contact</em></strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\"><em> number - ​USA Toll-free:&nbsp;</em></strong><strong><em><u><del>** ***** ********</del></u></em></strong></li></ul>","markdown":"- **All travel and/or other additional costs must be preapproved by Telesol. Please report all additional expenses in a counteroffer, otherwise they will not be approved when processing the payment, thank you.**\n- **You are required to provide your email address so that we can provide you with the link to our reporting platform (TTR).** **Engineer must complete the online Telesol Ticket Report (TTR) and the WO in Field Nation before leaving site. TTR is in online form and there is no need to print it.**\n- **Engineer needs to update us on ticket progress at least once every hour. If the job is taking longer than two hours, it should be reported to us immediately.**\n- **The bridge will open at the top of the hour! In the 30 minutes, you should check in with LCON, get access, check the equipment and join the call at the top of the hour.**\n- **Please do not remove or take any equipment from the site unless it’s specified in the WO or instructed to by a remote support agent. Any questions or concerns from the customer about onsite equipment should be directed back to noc@telesolgroup.com.**\n- **The Provider cannot leave the site before being released by the customer or Telesol!**\n- **You are to represent yourself as working on behalf of Telesol Group for** **\\*\\*\\*****. The equipment being installed is for** **\\*\\*\\*****.**\n- **Never use long distance calls unless the client provides toll free number. We will not reimburse you for long distance calls. Please insist on Microsoft Teams meeting instead 