{"job":{"id":19867087,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Direct Source","title":"Register Refresh & Server Replacement","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>Scope of Services:</u></strong> This is a complex project with detailed tasks to be performed by DSI, Technician and the End Customer, as documented in the Technical Guide or in a signed Change Authorization.</p><p>An overview of the services to be performed by the Technician include, but are not limited to:</p><ul><li>Check in with Direct Source Support Desk upon arrival at each site to check in.</li><li>If the Manager is not on-site at time of arrival, obtain a photo of the front of the store and escalate to the DSI Support Desk.</li></ul><p><strong><u>Pre-Installation Quality Check</u></strong>:</p><ol><li>Verify items such as register count, location of switch, and any existing hardware included in scope before starting.</li><li>Check Terminal numbers on bottom left corner of each register screen &ndash;&nbsp;<em>The Register (Terminal) # does not always match the Fixture Lane #.</em></li><li>Check with MOD for pre-existing issues and report to DSI Support Desk.</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Inventory</u></strong>: Complete a full inventory of new equipment received &ndash; Escalate to the DSI Support Desk if any damages or missing equipment are found.</p><ul><li><strong><u>Contact Direct Source Support Desk after inventory is complete to have all registers removed from the domain.</u></strong></li><li>Power down all legacy registers.</li></ul><p><strong><u>POS Server Installation</u></strong>:&nbsp;</p><ul><li><strong>The new POS Server MUST be installed first!&nbsp;It is critical that upon completing inventory, tech contact DSI Support Desk to remove all old registers from the domain and then power down the old registers</strong>.</li><li>Proceed with installing the new POS server - You will need to locate the existing network switch to assess the best location to mount the new server.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">All legacy registers must be unplugged PRIOR to making the new server connections.</li></ul><p><strong>-Tech must change network connections at the switch before beginning.</strong>.</p><p>-Must&nbsp;<strong>come prepared with wood screws 1\", drywall anchors AND concrete screws</strong>&nbsp;since the server could be mounted on varying materials throughout the different stores.</p><p><strong>-Once the server is mounted &amp; online, you MUST contact the DSI Support Desk to ping the server to confirm functionality.</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;This is critical as none of the new registers will be able to download successfully if there are any issues with the server connection.</p><p>-Proceed with replacing the registers and their required peripherals following the instructions in the Installation Guide &ndash;</p><p>-You must start with register 2 first and work your way down the lanes.</p><ol><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Register 2 must be installed in its entirety, tested, and fully functional to hand over to the manager to open on time.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Note</strong>: The final register at the store will be installed at Lane 1, as there is no actual \"Register 1\" at the store anymore.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Must notify DSI Support of Register 2 handover &amp; store open time</strong>, or escalate if any assistance is needed troubleshooting POS issues.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Install remaining registers 3-5 as applicable. Follow same steps as for Reg 2.</li></ol><p>Remaining hardware installation may include a variety of the following, as identified in the site-specific scope.</p><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Installation of new Monitor.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Installation of new scanners (Wired, wireless, or flatbed)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Installation of new receipt printers.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Installation of new cash drawers and keyboards.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Installation of new surge protector at each lane.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">You must use the supplied velcro for the hub shroud to attach to the bottom of the new surge protector and to the bottom of the register to secure the surge protector in place.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Possible installation of the new Thin Client PC</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">If required per site specific scope, this must be installed in the office. If currently at a kiosk, the fixture will need to be demo'd and the patch cable connection adjusted at the switch.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Possible installation of new laser printer</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Installation of new HIP Printer and PDT.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Installed in the office, per installation guide.</li></ul><p>-Complete cable clean-up and cable management as needed;</p><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">This includes routing cables for the register and associated peripherals through the monitor stands and cabinets, using Velcro as needed.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Customer Requirements</u></strong><u>:</u></p><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">ONLY&nbsp;<strong>black</strong>&nbsp;Velcro may be used.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Inside the cash wrap fixture, cable management must be completed on each cable individually. Cables should not all be velcro'd together as one giant bundle.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">A photo of cable management for each lane will be a required deliverable.</li></ul><p>-Complete testing as per the installation guide and verify with the store manager that all equipment is working properly.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Return Shipments:</u></strong></p><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">&nbsp;Deinstall and consolidate old hardware for return.&nbsp;Place return label on the outside of the box for carrier pickup</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">DSI will provide FedEx return labels with new hardware shipments to facilitate old equipment returns to Green Tech Assets.&nbsp;<strong>These labels will need to be attached to the sealed box(es) prior to leaving site.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">HIP Printers and power adapters</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">PDT, cradle and power supplied</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Epson V6 receipt printers</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">All other equipment will be returned to Greentech. DSI will provide FedEx return labels with new hardware shipments to facilitate old equipment returns to Green Tech Assets. <strong>These labels will need to be attached to the sealed box(es) prior to leaving site.</strong> \t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If there are any overages, DOA (Dead on Arrival) equipment, or newly issued items that should not be returned to Greentech, DSI will provide a Direct Source Inc. return label. You will be responsible for returning this hardware by dropping it off at a nearby FedEx location and providing a FedEx drop-off receipt.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Clean up and dispose of all trash.</li></ul><p><strong><u>Service Completion:</u></strong>&nbsp;Technician&nbsp;will call the Direct Source Support Desk prior to leaving each site to complete a check out procedure and to record unique DSI checkout code on the SAF&nbsp;(voice mail is not an acceptable check out and could result in the technician returning to the site at the technicians own expense).</p><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Technician to provide and validate return shipment tracking numbers and any other checkout information.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Technician will provide quality check on all completed work to ensure that all work has been completed and is free from any defects.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Submittal of pictures and paperwork (\"Deliverables\") due within&nbsp;<strong>24 hours</strong>&nbsp;of site completion to the Direct Source Portal (for installations on multiple dates &ndash; submit daily deliverables).</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(28, 116, 167);\"><u>OBF/DOA Equipment</u></strong><strong>:</strong></p><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>If the site requires a revisit to install replacement hardware due to an OBF or DOA device</strong>, the technician must notify the Direct Source Support Desk for troubleshooting and coordination.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Technician must box the OBF hardware in its original packaging, mark the outside of the box as \"OBF\" AND \"DSI Return\", secure package closed and give to the manager</strong>. Explain that a return label will be emailed to them to print off and attach to the box and they will need to give this to FedEx next time they come to the store.&nbsp;</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>This box will be returned back to the Direct Source Warehouse, so do NOT use a provided GreenTech Return Label.﻿</strong></li></ul><p><strong><u>Technician Required Equipment, Tools, &amp; Hardware:</u></strong>&nbsp;Technician is required to have the following list of equipment and materials that will be used throughout the Technician's agreed upon assignment to this project.</p><ul><li>Standard Tool Kit (Multi-size screw drivers, hammer, etc)</li><li>Basic tech tools including a cell phone with fully charged battery, charger, and ongoing active account with your carrier.</li><li>Printed copy of the SAF Installation Checklist, the Technical Installation Guide and any other required project paperwork</li><li>Corded or cordless drill with fully charged battery, back up battery and drill bits (Various sizes)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Must have Drill Bits for Metal, Wood, and Concrete (1/8\")</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>1\" Wood Screws, drywall anchors AND Concrete Screws-Tapcon</strong>&nbsp;(These are used for mounting the Edge Server)</li><li>Torpedo level</li><li>Portable vacuum</li><li><strong>Black Velcro</strong>&nbsp;to secure cables as needed (Note: Zip ties or Velcro of any color but black, is NOT acceptable).</li><li>Hex Key Set (Must include a 3/16\" and a 5/32\" key)</li><li><strong>Bolts, washers, and nuts</strong>&nbsp;(This is for mounting new POS hub shrouds)</li><li>Spare&nbsp;<strong>M4 X 0.7 10mm Pan Head or Flat Head Screws &ndash; QTY 4 per register&nbsp;</strong>( New HP monitors require longer screws to attach to the existing pole mounts)</li><li>Security Bits</li><li>Flexible Bit Extender</li><li>Right Angle Drill Adapter</li><li>Flashlight</li><li>Packing Tape (as back up if not available at store)</li><li>Sharpies/Markers</li><li>Cable Tester/Toner</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>For Scopes that require a new Thin Client Cable Run:&nbsp;</u></strong></p><ul><li>10-12' Ladder</li><li>Spare patch cables (3' preferred)</li><li>Cable Materials (Cat5e or Cat6 plenum cable, RJ45 jacks, biscuit or surface mount boxes and cable support materials &ndash; J-Hooks, Beam Clamps, Arlington Straps, etc)</li><li>Cable pulling tools (Fish Stick or Tape, Crimper, etc)</li><li>Label Maker with Spare Labels</li><li>Wire Snips</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Project Summary:</u></strong> The Technician shall provide services to DSI and their client, End Customer, for the purpose of the installation of registers and new POS servers and new registers nationwide. Select stores may also receive a new Thin Client PC and/or Laser Printer. As a whole Direct Source is providing hardware integration and installation services. All Services provided by the technician herein are subject to the terms set forth in this Agreement.</p><p><strong><u>Project Schedule:</u></strong> Direct Source's project duration is April 2026 to January 2027. The Technician is to refer to the specific schedule provided on the Direct Source Portal for specific site start/end dates. Because the project includes specific coordination of labor resources and specific hardware arrival requirements, Direct Source or the End Customer are the only parties authorized to change the assigned Technician's schedule. Schedules CANNOT be changed or adjusted by the Technician. Direct Source shall not be responsible for any costs or expenses incurred by the Technician as a result of the change in schedule.</p><p>All installation work completed by the Technician shall be Monday through Fridays between store hours or two hours prior to the store opening. Technician may not work outside of these dates and times without permission from DSI Project Management and is expected to stay on site until work is complete or the Technician has been released by the DSI Support Desk or DSI Project Manager.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Direct Source Obligations:</u></strong> Direct Source will provide all Technicians with their pre-confirmed schedules, including device counts per site. All project related documents will be made available on the Direct Source Portal for download. Technician is expected to log on and print out the documents from the DSI Portal prior to the start of their assignment.</p><p>Direct Source Project Related Documents includes:</p><ul><li>DSI Technical Guide</li><li>Direct Source Contact information, Support Desk numbers and escalation plan</li><li>Service Acceptance Form(s) (SAF)</li><li>Letter of Authorization (LOA)</li></ul><p><strong><u>Project Preparation / Orientation:</u> The Technician who will be onsite </strong>must complete a mandatory technician orientation conference call session prior to the start of their first installation unless other arrangements are mutually agreed upon. During that session, the Technician will learn Direct Source's and End Customer's expectations, processes, deliverable requirements, project scope as well as lessons learned from previous installations.<strong> Direct Source will provide a detailed Technical Guide (Technician Installation Guide) on the Direct Source Portal, which must be reviewed prior to project orientation, and must be brought to each installation.</strong></p><p><strong><u>NEW DSI Technician Requirements Only:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Successful completion of a criminal background/credit check will be required for any new technician to Direct Source Inc.</li><li>Failure to successfully pass a criminal background/credit check will result in the disqualification of the Technician to participate in any End Customer or other DSI projects.&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong><u>Deliverables &amp; Reporting:</u> </strong>Deliverables are defined as any documentation and/or digital photos required per the Technical Guide. All Deliverables must be uploaded via the Direct Source Mobile App (preferred) or via the Direct Source portal.</p><p>Required deliverables are the following:</p><ul><li>Completed Service Acceptance Form (SAF)</li><li>&nbsp;Digital Pictures with proper naming conventions as outlined in the Installation Guide.&nbsp;</li><li><strong>Submit all photos to DSI for approval prior to leaving the store.</strong></li></ul><p><strong><u>Payment Information:</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>Payment Amounts:</u></strong> Payment amount is inclusive of labor, any applicable sales or use taxes, and expenses including but not limited to hotel, meals, and local travel. No other expenses will be reimbursed in excess of the payment amounts listed, unless agreed upon in writing. For purposes of this Work Order \"Payment Information\", the term \"Completed Site\" shall mean each site where: (i) Technician has completed the work in accordance with the specifications set forth herein; (ii) all required documentation related to the site has been submitted to DSI within the time frames set forth below.</p><p><strong><u>Time &amp; Material Rate:</u> $60 </strong>per hour for work that exceeds the total of 5 hours of onsite time, due to no fault of the Technician, will be paid at the hourly T&amp;M rate in 15-minute increments. T&amp;M will ONLY be paid when the issue was reported immediately, the DSI Support Desk or DSI Project Manager has documented the issue and an incident ticket number has been assigned.</p><p>In the event additional resources are required due to reasons outside the Technician's control, the Technician will notify the DSI Project Manager of the situation via electronic communication, propose a solution and obtain pre-approval for any additional costs for materials, labor or expenses. Verbal agreements with anyone other than the Project Manager will be considered invalid.</p><p><strong><u>Store Revisits</u></strong><u>:</u> Store revisits will be paid at $60 per hour with a 2-hour minimum if the revisit cause is due to no fault of the Technician.</p><p><strong><u>Same Day Cancellation (SDC) or Same Day Reschedule (SDR):</u> </strong></p><p>Any Site that is Cancelled or Rescheduled on the planned installation date due to conditions outside of the Technician's control (Examples include, inventory shortages, customer site readiness or customer late or no arrival). The on-site issue must be escalated immediately to the DSI Support Desk. <strong>The Technician may not leave the End Customer's site without the Direct Source escalation &amp; authorization in order to qualify for payment.</strong></p><p>Any site that is rescheduled due to conditions under the Technician's control; no payment is owed to the Technician. (Examples include, but are not limited to:&nbsp;Technician late arrival, missed pre-site informational meeting/ 'tech orientation' or lack of required tools or materials as specified within this Statement of Work or the Technical Guide).</p><p><strong><u>Service Acceptance:</u></strong> All service tasks must be completed, in order, as specified in the Technical Guide unless otherwise expressly approved by the DSI Project Manager in writing. Local End Customer DOES NOT have the authorization to change service tasks. If the End Customer is asking for you to do any out of scope work, call the DSI Support Desk immediately.</p><p>Failure to fully and accurately complete or deliver on time, all required deliverables, or failure to deliver Services would result in the Service Order being deemed incomplete. Direct Source agrees to notify the Technician within 5 days of the site's completion, the specific nature of any such failure to conform to the contracted service and afford the Technician the opportunity to remedy such failure in a mutually agreeable and timely fashion.</p><p><strong><u>Service Level Agreements:</u></strong> <em>All days below are from the day of installation .</em></p><p><strong>Deliverables:</strong></p><p><strong><u>1 Business Day</u>: All required deliverables are due to the Direct Source Portal: No Fee Incurred</strong></p><p><strong><u>2 Business Days:</u> (Late penalties 30% per affected site. Payment for that site(s) may be withheld):</strong> If DSI has not received or has rejected the required deliverables due to failure to meet requirements, DSI will notify the Technician via the Late Deliverable email, indicating what is still outstanding.</p><p>The Technician will have up to the 5th business day to:</p><p><strong>a)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong>submit the outstanding item(s) OR</p><p><strong>b)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong>return to the site at the Technician's expense to remedy the outstanding items</p><p><strong><u>5 Business Days: </u>(Late penalties, The cost of dispatching a technician to obtain the required deliverables): </strong>In the absence of the Technician remedying the outstanding deliverable item(s), penalties equal to the cost of dispatching a technician to obtain the required deliverables, will be applied to the outstanding invoice amount for the affected site(s).</p><p>Late deliverables are defined as any documentation and/or digital photos required per the Technical Guide and that is not received by the end of the next business day after the scheduled installation date. This also includes deliverables that are incomplete, inaccurate, or illegible.</p><p>Late fee penalties will not be waived unless the Technician received written notice from the Direct Source Project Manager for each occurrence.</p><p><strong><u>Same Day Reschedule/Cancellation</u></strong></p><ul><li>Site was rescheduled or cancelled after technician arrived at site, but no work was completed due to no fault of technician: $30 reschedule fee + Contracted Trip Charge</li><li>Site was rescheduled or cancelled in less than 24 hours: $30 reschedule fee</li><li>Technician arrived onsite and was able to complete some work, (example: inventory) but due to no fault of technician, site was rescheduled or cancelled: Minimum of 2 hours of T&amp;M + Contracted Trip Charge</li></ul><p><strong><u>Reschedule/Cancellation</u></strong></p><ul><li>Site was rescheduled or cancelled with more than 24-hour notice: Nothing is owed</li></ul>","markdown":"**Scope of Services:** This is a complex project with detailed tasks to be performed by DSI, Technician and the End Customer, as documented in the Technical Guide or in a signed Change Authorization.\n\nAn overview of the services to be performed by the Technician include, but are not limited to:\n\n- Check in with Direct Source Support Desk upon arrival at each site to check in.\n- If the Manager is not on-site at time of arrival, obtain a photo of the front of the store and escalate to the DSI Support Desk.\n\n**Pre-Installation Quality Check**:\n\n1. Verify items such as register count, location of switch, and any existing hardware included in scope before starting.\n2. Check Terminal numbers on bottom left corner of each register screen – *The Register (Terminal) # does not always match the Fixture Lane #.*\n3. Check with MOD for pre-existing issues and report to DSI Support Desk.\n\n**Inventory**: Complete a full inventory of new equipment received – Escalate to the DSI Support Desk if any damages or missing equipment are found.\n\n- **Contact Direct Source Support Desk after inventory is complete to have all registers removed from the domain.**\n- Power down all legacy registers.\n\n**POS Server Installation**:\n\n- **The new POS Server MUST be installed first! It is critical that upon completing inventory, tech contact DSI Support Desk to remove all old registers from the domain and then power down the old registers**.\n- Proceed with installing the new POS server - You will need to locate the existing network switch to assess the best location to mount the new server.\n- All legacy registers must be unplugged PRIOR to making the new server connections.\n\n**-Tech must change network connections at the switch before beginning.**.\n\n-Must **come prepared with wood screws 1\", drywall anchors AND concrete screws** since the server could be mounted on varying materials throughout the different stores.\n\n**-Once the server is mounted & online, you MUST contact the DSI Support Desk to ping the server to confirm functionality.** This is critical as none of the new registers will be able to download successfully if there are any issues with the server connection.\n\n-Proceed with replacing the registers and their required peripherals following the instructions in the Installation Guide –\n\n-You must start with register 2 first and work your way down the lanes.\n\n1. **Register 2 must be installed in its entirety, tested, and fully functional to hand over to the manager to open on time.**\n2. **Note**: The final register at the store will be installed at Lane 1, as there is no actual \"Register 1\" at the store anymore.\n3. **Must notify DSI Support of Register 2 handover & store open time**, or escalate if any assistance is needed troubleshooting POS issues.\n4. Install remaining registers 3-5 as applicable. Follow same steps as for Reg 2.\n\nRemaining hardware installation may include a variety of the following, as identified in the site-specific scope.\n\n- Installation of new Monitor.\n- Installation of new scanners (Wired, wireless, or flatbed)\n- Installation of new receipt printers.\n- Installation of new cash drawers and keyboards.\n- Installation of new surge protector at each lane.\n- You must use the supplied velcro for the hub shroud to attach to the bottom of the new surge protector and to the bottom of the register to secure the surge protector in place.\n- Possible installation of the new Thin Client PC\n- If required per site specific scope, this must be installed in the office. If currently at a kiosk, the fixture will need to be demo'd and the patch cable connection adjusted at the switch.\n- Possible installation of new laser printer\n- Installation of new HIP Printer and PDT.\n- Installed in the office, per installation guide.\n\n-Complete cable clean-up and cable management as needed;\n\n- This includes routing cables for the register and associated peripherals through the monitor stands and cabinets, using Velcro as needed.\n\n**Customer Requirements**:\n\n- ONLY **black** Velcro may be used.\n- Inside the cash wrap fixture, cable management must be completed on each cable individually. Cables should not all be velcro'd together as one giant bundle.\n- A photo of cable management for each lane will be a required deliverable.\n\n-Complete testing as per the installation guide and verify with the store manager that all equipment is working properly.\n\n**Return Shipments:**\n\n- Deinstall and consolidate old hardware for return. Place return label on the outside of the box for carrier pickup\n- DSI will provide FedEx return labels with new hardware shipments to facilitate old equipment returns to Green Tech Assets. **These labels will need to be attached to the sealed box(es) prior to leaving site.**\n- HIP Printers and power adapters\n- PDT, cradle and power supplied\n- Epson V6 receipt printers\n- All other equipment will be returned to Greentech. DSI will provide FedEx return labels with new hardware shipments to facilitate old equipment returns to Green Tech Assets. **These labels will need to be attached to the sealed box(es) prior to leaving site.**\n- If there are any overages, DOA (Dead on Arrival) equipment, or newly issued items that should not be returned to Greentech, DSI will provide a Direct Source Inc. return label. You will be responsible for returning this hardware by dropping it off at a nearby FedEx location and providing a FedEx drop-off receipt.\n- Clean up and dispose of all trash.\n\n**Service Completion:** Technician will call the Direct Source Support Desk prior to leaving each site to complete a check out procedure and to record unique DSI checkout code on the SAF (voice mail is not an acceptable check out and could result in the technician returning to the site at the technicians own expense).\n\n- Technician to provide and validate return shipment tracking numbers and any other checkout information.\n- Technician will provide quality check on all completed work to ensure that all work has been completed and is free from any defects.\n- Submittal of pictures and paperwork (\"Deliverables\") due within **24 hours** of site completion to the Direct Source Portal (for installations on multiple dates – submit daily deliverables).\n\n**OBF/DOA Equipment****:**\n\n- **If the site requires a revisit to install replacement hardware due to an OBF or DOA device**, the technician must notify the Direct Source Support Desk for troubleshooting and coordination.\n- **Technician must box the OBF hardware in its original packaging, mark the outside of the box as \"OBF\" AND \"DSI Return\", secure package closed and give to the manager**. Explain that a return label will be emailed to them to print off and attach to the box and they will need to give this to FedEx next time they come to the store.\n- **This box will be returned back to the Direct Source Warehouse, so do NOT use a provided GreenTech Return Label.﻿**\n\n**Technician Required Equipment, Tools, & Hardware:** Technician is required to have the following list of equipment and materials that will be used throughout the Technician's agreed upon assignment to this project.\n\n- Standard Tool Kit (Multi-size screw drivers, hammer, etc)\n- Basic tech tools including a cell phone with fully charged battery, charger, and ongoing active account with your carrier.\n- Printed copy of the SAF Installation Checklist, the Technical Installation Guide and any other required project paperwork\n- Corded or cordless drill with fully charged battery, back up battery and drill bits (Various sizes)\n- Must have Drill Bits for Metal, Wood, and Concrete (1/8\")\n- **1\" Wood Screws, drywall anchors AND Concrete Screws-Tapcon** (These are used for mounting the Edge Server)\n- Torpedo level\n- Portable vacuum\n- **Black Velcro** to secure cables as needed (Note: Zip ties or Velcro of any color but black, is NOT acceptable).\n- Hex Key Set (Must include a 3/16\" and a 5/32\" key)\n- **Bolts, washers, and nuts** (This is for mounting new POS hub shrouds)\n- Spare **M4 X 0.7 10mm Pan Head or Flat Head Screws – QTY 4 per register** ( New HP monitors require longer screws to attach to the existing pole mounts)\n- Security Bits\n- Flexible Bit Extender\n- Right Angle Drill Adapter\n- Flashlight\n- Packing Tape (as back up if not available at store)\n- Sharpies/Markers\n- Cable Tester/Toner\n\n**For Scopes that require a new Thin Client Cable Run:**\n\n- 10-12' Ladder\n- Spare patch cables (3' preferred)\n- Cable Materials (Cat5e or Cat6 plenum cable, RJ45 jacks, biscuit or surface mount boxes and cable support materials – J-Hooks, Beam Clamps, Arlington Straps, etc)\n- Cable pulling tools (Fish Stick or Tape, Crimper, etc)\n- Label Maker with Spare Labels\n- Wire Snips\n\n**Project Summary:** The Technician shall provide services to DSI and their client, End Customer, for the purpose of the installation of registers and new POS servers and new registers nationwide. Select stores may also receive a new Thin Client PC and/or Laser Printer. As a whole Direct Source is providing hardware integration and installation services. All Services provided by the technician herein are subject to the terms set forth in this Agreement.\n\n**Project Schedule:** Direct Source's project duration is April 2026 to January 2027. The Technician is to refer to the specific schedule provided on the Direct Source Portal for specific site start/end dates. Because the project includes specific coordination of labor resources and specific hardware arrival requirements, Direct Source or the End Customer are the only parties authorized to change the assigned Technician's schedule. Schedules CANNOT be changed or adjusted by the Technician. Direct Source shall not be responsible for any costs or expenses incurred by the Technician as a result of the change in schedule.\n\nAll installation work completed by the Technician shall be Monday through Fridays between store hours or two hours prior to the store opening. Technician may not work outside of these dates and times without permission from DSI Project Management and is expected to stay on site until work is complete or the Technician has been released by the DSI Support Desk or DSI Project Manager.\n\n**Direct Source Obligations:** Direct Source will provide all Technicians with their pre-confirmed schedules, including device counts per site. All project related documents will be made available on the Direct Source Portal for download. Technician is expected to log on and print out the documents from the DSI Portal prior to the start of their assignment.\n\nDirect Source Project Related Documents includes:\n\n- DSI Technical Guide\n- Direct Source Contact information, Support Desk numbers and escalation plan\n- Service Acceptance Form(s) (SAF)\n- Letter of Authorization (LOA)\n\n**Project Preparation / Orientation: The Technician who will be onsite** must complete a mandatory technician orientation conference call session prior to the start of their first installation unless other arrangements are mutually agreed upon. During that session, the Technician will learn Direct Source's and End Customer's expectations, processes, deliverable requirements, project scope as well as lessons learned from previous installations. **Direct Source will provide a detailed Technical Guide (Technician Installation Guide) on the Direct Source Portal, which must be reviewed prior to project orientation, and must be brought to each installation.**\n\n**NEW DSI Technician Requirements Only:**\n\n- Successful completion of a criminal background/credit check will be required for any new technician to Direct Source Inc.\n- Failure to successfully pass a criminal background/credit check will result in the disqualification of the Technician to participate in any End Customer or other DSI projects.\n\n**Deliverables & Reporting:** Deliverables are defined as any documentation and/or digital photos required per the Technical Guide. All Deliverables must be uploaded via the Direct Source Mobile App (preferred) or via the Direct Source portal.\n\nRequired deliverables are the following:\n\n- Completed Service Acceptance Form (SAF)\n- Digital Pictures with proper naming conventions as outlined in the Installation Guide.\n- **Submit all photos to DSI for approval prior to leaving the store.**\n\n**Payment Information:**\n\n**Payment Amounts:** Payment amount is inclusive of labor, any applicable sales or use taxes, and expenses including but not limited to hotel, meals, and local travel. No other expenses will be reimbursed in excess of the payment amounts listed, unless agreed upon in writing. For purposes of this Work Order \"Payment Information\", the term \"Completed Site\" shall mean each site where: (i) Technician has completed the work in accordance with the specifications set forth herein; (ii) all required documentation related to the site has been submitted to DSI within the time frames set forth below.\n\n**Time & Material Rate: $60** per hour for work that exceeds the total of 5 hours of onsite time, due to no fault of the Technician, will be paid at the hourly T&M rate in 15-minute increments. T&M will ONLY be paid when the issue was reported immediately, the DSI Support Desk or DSI Project Manager has documented the issue and an incident ticket number has been assigned.\n\nIn the event additional resources are required due to reasons outside the Technician's control, the Technician will notify the DSI Project Manager of the situation via electronic communication, propose a solution and obtain pre-approval for any additional costs for materials, labor or expenses. Verbal agreements with anyone other than the Project Manager will be considered invalid.\n\n**Store Revisits**: Store revisits will be paid at $60 per hour with a 2-hour minimum if the revisit cause is due to no fault of the Technician.\n\n**Same Day Cancellation (SDC) or Same Day Reschedule (SDR):**\n\nAny Site that is Cancelled or Rescheduled on the planned installation date due to conditions outside of the Technician's control (Examples include, inventory shortages, customer site readiness or customer late or no arrival). The on-site issue must be escalated immediately to the DSI Support Desk. **The Technician may not leave the End Customer's site without the Direct Source escalation & authorization in order to qualify for payment.**\n\nAny site that is rescheduled due to conditions under the Technician's control; no payment is owed to the Technician. (Examples include, but are not limited to: Technician late arrival, missed pre-site informational meeting/ 'tech orientation' or lack of required tools or materials as specified within this Statement of Work or the Technical Guide).\n\n**Service Acceptance:** All service tasks must be completed, in order, as specified in the Technical Guide unless otherwise expressly approved by the DSI Project Manager in writing. Local End Customer DOES NOT have the authorization to change service tasks. If the End Customer is asking for you to do any out of scope work, call the DSI Support Desk immediately.\n\nFailure to fully and accurately complete or deliver on time, all required deliverables, or failure to deliver Services would result in the Service Order being deemed incomplete. Direct Source agrees to notify the Technician within 5 days of the site's completion, the specific nature of any such failure to conform to the contracted service and afford the Technician the opportunity to remedy such failure in a mutually agreeable and timely fashion.\n\n**Service Level Agreements:** *All days below are from the day of installation .*\n\n**Deliverables:**\n\n**1 Business Day: All required deliverables are due to the Direct Source Portal: No Fee Incurred**\n\n**2 Business Days: (Late penalties 30% per affected site. Payment for that site(s) may be withheld):** If DSI has not received or has rejected the required deliverables due to failure to meet requirements, DSI will notify the Technician via the Late Deliverable email, indicating what is still outstanding.\n\nThe Technician will have up to the 5th business day to:\n\n**a)** submit the outstanding item(s) OR\n\n**b)** return to the site at the Technician's expense to remedy the outstanding items\n\n**5 Business Days: (Late penalties, The cost of dispatching a technician to obtain the required deliverables):** In the absence of the Technician remedying the outstanding deliverable item(s), penalties equal to the cost of dispatching a technician to obtain the required deliverables, will be applied to the outstanding invoice amount for the affected site(s).\n\nLate deliverables are defined as any documentation and/or digital photos required per the Technical Guide and that is not received by the end of the next business day after the scheduled installation date. This also includes deliverables that are incomplete, inaccurate, or illegible.\n\nLate fee penalties will not be waived unless the Technician received written notice from the Direct Source Project Manager for each occurrence.\n\n**Same Day Reschedule/Cancellation**\n\n- Site was rescheduled or cancelled after technician arrived at site, but no work was completed due to no fault of technician: $30 reschedule fee + Contracted Trip Charge\n- Site was rescheduled or cancelled in less than 24 hours: $30 reschedule fee\n- Technician arrived onsite and was able to complete some work, (example: inventory) but due to no fault of technician, site was rescheduled or cancelled: Minimum of 2 hours of T&M + Contracted Trip Charge\n\n**Reschedule/Cancellation**\n\n- Site was rescheduled or cancelled with more than 24-hour notice: Nothing is owed","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-06T06:00","end":"2026-10-06T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":300,"max":300},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":5,"distance":71},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $300 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-06T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ​Concord Police Department - NC ( Phase 2 ) (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-22T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"Remote Hands - Connect AT&T broadband circuit"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789755041121}
{"job":{"id":19986725,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"NCR Atleos","title":"British Telecom - Onsite Rack & Stack | Estimated 8 hours onsite | Cisco experience preferred","description":{"html":"<p><strong>IMPORTANT GENERAL RULES:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>EVERY TRAVEL EXPENSE NEEDS TO BE PRE-COMMUNICATED AND APPROVED BY THE NCR PROJECT MANAGER, ALL AFTERWARDS ADDED TRAVEL EXPENSES WILL NOT BE APPROVED.</strong></li><li><strong>Incomplete WOs (no Provider fault - store&nbsp;turnaways, site not ready, etc.). Technician MUST contact WO manager to advise of the situation and reason the WO cannot be completed, as well as adding a comment in the closeout notes;&nbsp;</strong>must be checked-in on time per the&nbsp;<strong>original&nbsp;</strong>time log.</li><li>o <strong>If work is aborted within 1 hour of arrival</strong>:</li><li>§ <em>Hourly Rate</em>&nbsp;- lf Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed, pay will be limited to $50 or 1 hour at the agreed-upon rate, whichever is greater, plus pre-approved travel expenses.</li><li>§ <em>Fixed Rate</em>&nbsp;- If Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed, pay will be limited to 1 hour at an hourly conversion rate of the fixed rate amount at assignment divided by max hours at assignment, plus pre-approved travel expenses.</li><li>o <strong>If work is aborted between 1 and 2 hours of arrival</strong>:</li><li>o <em>Hourly Rate</em>&nbsp;- lf Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed, payment will be limited to 2 hours at hourly rate at time of assignment, plus pre-approved travel expenses.</li><li>o <em>Fixed Rate</em>&nbsp;-&nbsp;&nbsp;lf Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed, payment will be limited to 2 hours at an hourly conversion rate of the fixed rate amount at assignment divided by max hours at assignment, plus pre-approved travel expenses.</li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li><strong><u>SCOPE OVERVIEW</u></strong></li></ul><p><s