 any restriction&nbsp;</li></ul><p>Estimated 8 hours onsite time</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>REQUIREMENTS</u></strong></p><p><u>Dress Code</u></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">Casual Business:&nbsp;Button up, golf shirt, polo shirt, or blouse.&nbsp;Work pants, khakis, or clean jeans.&nbsp;Close toed shoes or boots</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">Not Allowed – hats, T-shirts, tank tops, muscle shirts, sweatshirts, shorts, sweatpants, sandals, flip-flops, athletic shoes, crocs, or open toed shoes</span></li></ul><p><u>Equipment</u></p><ul><li>Laptop + Charger</li><li>Cisco Console cable</li><li>USB drive</li><li>Mobile Hotspot</li><li>Networking Tool kit</li><li>Microsoft Teams</li><li>WEBEX</li><li>Terminal Emulation software (ex Putty)</li><li>Newest updated drivers</li><li>Label Maker</li></ul><p><u>Expectations</u></p><ul><li>Timely Arrival</li><li>Read scope and escalation path carefully.</li><li>Any out-of-scope work requires work order manager approval.</li></ul><p><u>Onsite:</u></p><ul><li>Meet the POC and be guided to work area. The POC will also provide the parts used in the installation.</li><li>Take a picture of the rack before installation begins.</li><li>Unbox the components to be installed and take inventory.</li><li>Take a photograph of the serial number of each device to be installed.</li><li><strong style=\"color: red;\">GOVERNMENT ISSUED PHOTO IDENTIFICATION ( ID ) IS A MUST !</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Below is the pre – requisites for the activity.</p><p>Carry console cable (with converter could be require) to provide the console of the devices.</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Ensure your access to internet (Carry Dongle with good speed and Data).</p><p>·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Ensure “Webex &amp; Teams Application” installed in your laptop so that your screen can be shared, and control can be requested (Please note in web based we will not be able to take your laptop control or access you need to install the Webex &amp; Teams Application).&nbsp;</p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work</u></strong>:</p><p>(a)&nbsp;&nbsp;Provide Console access of Cisco FWs to BT Remote Engineer.</p><p>(b)&nbsp;&nbsp;Provide any other onsite support as requested by BT remote engineer.</p><p>(f)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;FE should have:</p><ul><li>Working Laptop with MS Teams/ Cisco Webex and Internet access</li><li>Backup/ spare Console Cable for firewall</li><li>Should carry PEN/USB/FLASH drive during support.</li><li>Should have working 4G/Internet connection.</li><li>Must have <strong>WinSCP and Notepad ++ install on FE’s laptop</strong> for Open Gear set up at site. à <strong>MANDATORY</strong></li><li>Laptop admin access to share the screen and control access to BT TM via teams’ application.</li><li>There should be No language Barrier, should understand English.</li><li>Should have more than 1 Console cable (Putty/ Tera-Term/ Secure CRT)</li><li>FE needs to have laptop without any restriction&nbsp;</li></ul><p>Estimated 8 hours onsite time\t</p><p><br></p><ul><li>Fill out the Device Information custom field section below.</li><li>Take a picture of installed component in rack.</li><li>Break down and dispose of all packaging waste.</li><li>Ensure you are released from site by bridge line representative.</li></ul><p><strong><u>DELIVERABLES REQUIRED</u></strong></p><ul><li>Picture of rack before work begins.</li><li>Picture of each installed component's serial number</li><li>Each serial number entered into a custom field.</li><li>Picture of rack after installation is complete.</li></ul><p><strong><u>ESCALATIONS</u></strong></p><ul><li>Level 1 Escalation -Installation Coordinator: <del>** ******* **** *</del><del>**************************** *** *** *** ****</del><del> </del>Any onsite escalation ( Example: late arrival, site contact not onsite, team bridge check in problems, etc)</li><li>Level 2 Escalation -Project Manager: <strong><del>*** ****** ****** ** * </del></strong><span style=\"color: rgb(27, 30, 31);\"><del>**************</del>&nbsp;&nbsp;</span> - in case Level 1 not responding -30 min</li></ul>","markdown":"**IMPORTANT GENERAL RULES:**\n\n- **EVERY TRAVEL EXPENSE NEEDS TO BE PRE-COMMUNICATED AND APPROVED BY THE NCR PROJECT MANAGER, ALL AFTERWARDS ADDED TRAVEL EXPENSES WILL NOT BE APPROVED.**\n- **Incomplete WOs (no Provider fault - store turnaways, site not ready, etc.). Technician MUST contact WO manager to advise of the situation and reason the WO cannot be completed, as well as adding a comment in the closeout notes;** must be checked-in on time per the **original** time log.\n- o **If work is aborted within 1 hour of arrival**:\n- § *Hourly Rate* - lf Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed, pay will be limited to $50 or 1 hour at the agreed-upon rate, whichever is greater, plus pre-approved travel expenses.\n- § *Fixed Rate* - If Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed, pay will be limited to 1 hour at an hourly conversion rate of the fixed rate amount at assignment divided by max hours at assignment, plus pre-approved travel expenses.\n- o **If work is aborted between 1 and 2 hours of arrival**:\n- o *Hourly Rate* - lf Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed, payment will be limited to 2 hours at hourly rate at time of assignment, plus pre-approved travel expenses.\n- o *Fixed Rate* - lf Provider was on time and prepared to complete the SOW as agreed, payment will be limited to 2 hours at an hourly conversion rate of the fixed rate amount at assignment divided by max hours at assignment, plus pre-approved travel expenses.\n\n- **SCOPE OVERVIEW**\n\n**﻿PLEASE NOTE BECAUSE OF DATA PRIVACY WE SHARED THE NEARBY ADDRESS OF THE LOCATION IN THE WO, ONCE THE WO IS ACCEPTED THE FULL ACTUAL ADDRESS, END CUSTOMER NAME AND LOCAL CONTACT WILL BE ADDED IN THE WO.**\n\n**THE SCOPE AND REQUIREMENTS ARE LISTED , THIS WILL NOT CHANGE WITH THE ASSIGNMENT.**\n\n- **GOVERNMENT ISSUED PHOTO IDENTIFICATION ( ID ) IS MANDATORY TO HAVE ONSITE!**\n\nBelow is the pre – requisites for the activity.\n\nCarry console cable (with converter could be require) to provide the console of the devices.\n\n· Ensure your access to internet (Carry Dongle with good speed and Data).\n\n· Ensure “Webex & Teams Application” installed in your laptop so that your screen can be shared, and control can be requested (Please note in web based we will not be able to take your laptop control or access you need to install the Webex & Teams Application).\n\n**Scope of Work**:\n\n(a) Provide Console access of Cisco FWs to BT Remote Engineer.\n\n(b) Provide any other onsite support as requested by BT remote engineer.\n\n(f) FE should have:\n\n- Working Laptop with MS Teams/ Cisco Webex and Internet access\n- Backup/ spare Console Cable for firewall\n- Should carry PEN/USB/FLASH drive during support.\n- Should have working 4G/Internet connection.\n- Must have **WinSCP and Notepad ++ install on FE’s laptop** for Open Gear set up at site. à **MANDATORY**\n- Laptop admin access to share the screen and control access to BT TM via teams’ application.\n- There should be No language Barrier, should understand English.\n- Should have more than 1 Console cable (Putty/ Tera-Term/ Secure CRT)\n- FE needs to have laptop without any restriction\n\nEstimated 8 hours onsite time\n\n**REQUIREMENTS**\n\nDress Code\n\n- Casual Business: Button up, golf shirt, polo shirt, or blouse. Work pants, khakis, or clean jeans. Close toed shoes or boots\n- Not Allowed – hats, T-shirts, tank tops, muscle shirts, sweatshirts, shorts, sweatpants, sandals, flip-flops, athletic shoes, crocs, or open toed shoes\n\nEquipment\n\n- Laptop + Charger\n- Cisco Console cable\n- USB drive\n- Mobile Hotspot\n- Networking Tool kit\n- Microsoft Teams\n- WEBEX\n- Terminal Emulation software (ex Putty)\n- Newest updated drivers\n- Label Maker\n\nExpectations\n\n- Timely Arrival\n- Read scope and escalation path carefully.\n- Any out-of-scope work requires work order manager approval.\n\nOnsite:\n\n- Meet the POC and be guided to work area. The POC will also provide the parts used in the installation.\n- Take a picture of the rack before installation begins.\n- Unbox the components to be installed and take inventory.\n- Take a photograph of the serial number of each device to be installed.\n- **GOVERNMENT ISSUED PHOTO IDENTIFICATION ( ID ) IS A MUST !**\n\nBelow is the pre – requisites for the activity.\n\nCarry console cable (with converter could be require) to provide the console of the devices.\n\n· Ensure your access to internet (Carry Dongle with good speed and Data).\n\n· Ensure “Webex & Teams Application” installed in your laptop so that your screen can be shared, and control can be requested (Please note in web based we will not be able to take your laptop control or access you need to install the Webex & Teams Application).\n\n**Scope of Work**:\n\n(a) Provide Console access of Cisco FWs to BT Remote Engineer.\n\n(b) Provide any other onsite support as requested by BT remote engineer.\n\n(f) FE should have:\n\n- Working Laptop with MS Teams/ Cisco Webex and Internet access\n- Backup/ spare Console Cable for firewall\n- Should carry PEN/USB/FLASH drive during support.\n- Should have working 4G/Internet connection.\n- Must have **WinSCP and Notepad ++ install on FE’s laptop** for Open Gear set up at site. à **MANDATORY**\n- Laptop admin access to share the screen and control access to BT TM via teams’ application.\n- There should be No language Barrier, should understand English.\n- Should have more than 1 Console cable (Putty/ Tera-Term/ Secure CRT)\n- FE needs to have laptop without any restriction\n\nEstimated 8 hours onsite time\n\n- Fill out the Device Information custom field section below.\n- Take a picture of installed component in rack.\n- Break down and dispose of all packaging waste.\n- Ensure you are released from site by bridge line representative.\n\n**DELIVERABLES REQUIRED**\n\n- Picture of rack before work begins.\n- Picture of each installed component's serial number\n- Each serial number entered into a custom field.\n- Picture of rack after installation is complete.\n\n**ESCALATIONS**\n\n- Level 1 Escalation -Installation Coordinator: \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* Any onsite escalation ( Example: late arrival, site contact not onsite, team bridge check in problems, etc)\n- Level 2 Escalation -Project Manager: **\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*  - in case Level 1 not responding -30 min","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-29T08:45","end":"2026-09-29T16:45"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":440},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":8,"distance":61},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":60,"baseAmount":480,"estHours":8,"travelExpense":90,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":0}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Miniso Durham"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ​Concord Police Department - NC ( Phase 2 ) (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12: