{"job":{"id":19987379,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Gigstreem","title":"Olde Raleigh -  Residential Service and troubleshooting AP  -#315185","description":{"html":"<p><strong>GiGstreem is a national Internet Service Provider delivering high-quality service to residential and commercial properties across the country.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Work Order Location:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Residential Property –</strong> Raleigh, 27612</p>\n<p><em>Refer to confidential notes for the exact address and customer contact information.</em></p>\n<p><em>CONFIRM YOU HAVE THE EXPERIENCE AND TOOLS REQUIRED BEFORE APPLYING FOR THIS WORK ORDER.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Scope of Work</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Dispatch an experienced network technician to perform advanced troubleshooting on apartment</strong> where the APs are intermittently going offline.</p>\n<p>A technician is needed to identify any underlying cabling or infrastructure issues causing the APs to lose connectivity.</p>\n<p><strong>Work Details</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Visit <strong>both affected units</strong> at the property.</li>\n<li>Thoroughly inspect and test the Ethernet cabling between each AP and the IDF.</li>\n<li>Verify cable integrity using a cable tester to check for opens, shorts, split pairs, excessive length, and intermittent faults.</li>\n<li>Inspect and re-terminate cable ends if necessary.</li>\n<li>Verify PoE delivery, switch port status, and AP uplink connectivity.</li>\n<li>Inspect patch panel connections and verify all terminations are secure.</li>\n<li>Identify any wiring, infrastructure, or environmental issues that may be causing the APs to go offline intermittently.</li>\n<li>Work directly with Gigstreem Engineering during troubleshooting.</li>\n<li>Do not leave the site until Engineering has reviewed the findings.</li>\n<li>Upload photos of the APs, IDF, cabling, and any repairs performed.</li>\n<li>Provide detailed notes, cable test results, and all findings upon completion.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Technician Expectations:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Confirm the appointment time</strong> with the customer before heading to the property.</li>\n<li><strong>Place a courtesy call at least 30 minutes prior to arrival</strong> to inform the customer of your estimated time of arrival (ETA).</li>\n<li>Upon arriving on site, all Field Nation technicians are required to <strong><u>check in at the leasing office or front desk before proceeding to any unit.</u></strong> Contractors must announce their arrival and present their Field Nation ID and credentials for verification. <strong><u>Entry into any resident’s unit is not permitted until this check‑in process is completed and approved by onsite staff.</u></strong></li>\n<li><strong>Represent the brand</strong> with professionalism. Appearance, communication, and the quality of your work must reflect high standards.</li>\n<li><strong>Do not overshare</strong> internal processes or technical details with the customer. Communication should be simple, courteous, and focused on resolving the issue.</li>\n<li>⚠️ <em>If the technician arrives unprepared, misinforms the customer, demonstrates poor presentation, or delivers substandard work, GiGstreem reserves the right to withhold payment for the work order.</em></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Required Experience:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Troubleshooting Ruckus Access Points (including reset, removal from wall mount, etc.)</li>\n<li>Networking/Telecommunications experience</li>\n<li>Experience with copper cabling: Cat5e/Cat6 testing, RJ45 termination</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Required Tools:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Laptop with Ethernet port or USB-to-Ethernet adapter</li>\n<li>Cable tester/certifier (capable of testing wiremap, opens, shorts, split pairs, cable length, and PoE)</li>\n<li>Tone generator and probe</li>\n<li>RJ45 crimping tool</li>\n<li>RJ45 connectors</li>\n<li>Punch-down tool</li>\n<li>Known-good Ethernet patch cables</li>\n<li>Basic hand tools</li>\n<li>Flashlight</li>\n<li>Smartphone for photos and documentation</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Coordination:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Troubleshoot in collaboration with GiGstreem’s Network Operations Team</li>\n<li>Refer to confidential notes for Network Operations and customer contact details.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>At Gigstreem, delivering reliable, high-performance internet service is our top priority. To maintain the integrity of our network and ensure consistent customer experiences, we follow strict guidelines regarding the equipment and solutions we support. This includes a clear stance on the use of Wi-Fi extenders.</p>\n<p><strong><u>Policy on Wi-Fi Extenders - Gigstreem Policy Reminder:</u></strong></p>\n<p><strong>It is strictly against Gigstreem policy to utilize, install, or recommend Wi-Fi extenders as a solution for speed, coverage, or connectivity issues within a unit.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Why This Matters:</li>\n<li>Wi-Fi extenders are not part of our approved network architecture.</li>\n<li>They can introduce interference, degrade performance, and complicate troubleshooting.</li>\n<li>Recommending or installing extenders may lead to inconsistent service and customer dissatisfaction.</li>\n<li>Approved Resolution Methods:</li>\n<li>Thorough troubleshooting of the existing AP and network configuration</li>\n<li>Collaboration with engineering to assess AP configuration</li>\n<li>All technicians and support staff must adhere to this policy without exception. Any deviation should be escalated to management for review.</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**GiGstreem is a national Internet Service Provider delivering high-quality service to residential and commercial properties across the country.**\n\n**Work Order Location:**\n\n**Residential Property –** Raleigh, 27612\n\n*Refer to confidential notes for the exact address and customer contact information.*\n\n*CONFIRM YOU HAVE THE EXPERIENCE AND TOOLS REQUIRED BEFORE APPLYING FOR THIS WORK ORDER.*\n\n**Scope of Work**\n\n**Dispatch an experienced network technician to perform advanced troubleshooting on apartment** where the APs are intermittently going offline.\n\nA technician is needed to identify any underlying cabling or infrastructure issues causing the APs to lose connectivity.\n\n**Work Details**\n\n- Visit **both affected units** at the property.\n- Thoroughly inspect and test the Ethernet cabling between each AP and the IDF.\n- Verify cable integrity using a cable tester to check for opens, shorts, split pairs, excessive length, and intermittent faults.\n- Inspect and re-terminate cable ends if necessary.\n- Verify PoE delivery, switch port status, and AP uplink connectivity.\n- Inspect patch panel connections and verify all terminations are secure.\n- Identify any wiring, infrastructure, or environmental issues that may be causing the APs to go offline intermittently.\n- Work directly with Gigstreem Engineering during troubleshooting.\n- Do not leave the site until Engineering has reviewed the findings.\n- Upload photos of the APs, IDF, cabling, and any repairs performed.\n- Provide detailed notes, cable test results, and all findings upon completion.\n\n**Technician Expectations:**\n\n- **Confirm the appointment time** with the customer before heading to the property.\n- **Place a courtesy call at least 30 minutes prior to arrival** to inform the customer of your estimated time of arrival (ETA).\n- Upon arriving on site, all Field Nation technicians are required to **check in at the leasing office or front desk before proceeding to any unit.** Contractors must announce their arrival and present their Field Nation ID and credentials for verification. **Entry into any resident’s unit is not permitted until this check‑in process is completed and approved by onsite staff.**\n- **Represent the brand** with professionalism. Appearance, communication, and the quality of your work must reflect high standards.\n- **Do not overshare** internal processes or technical details with the customer. Communication should be simple, courteous, and focused on resolving the issue.\n- ⚠️ *If the technician arrives unprepared, misinforms the customer, demonstrates poor presentation, or delivers substandard work, GiGstreem reserves the right to withhold payment for the work order.*\n\n**Required Experience:**\n\n- Troubleshooting Ruckus Access Points (including reset, removal from wall mount, etc.)\n- Networking/Telecommunications experience\n- Experience with copper cabling: Cat5e/Cat6 testing, RJ45 termination\n\n**Required Tools:**\n\n- Laptop with Ethernet port or USB-to-Ethernet adapter\n- Cable tester/certifier (capable of testing wiremap, opens, shorts, split pairs, cable length, and PoE)\n- Tone generator and probe\n- RJ45 crimping tool\n- RJ45 connectors\n- Punch-down tool\n- Known-good Ethernet patch cables\n- Basic hand tools\n- Flashlight\n- Smartphone for photos and documentation\n\n**Coordination:**\n\n- Troubleshoot in collaboration with GiGstreem’s Network Operations Team\n- Refer to confidential notes for Network Operations and customer contact details.\n\nAt Gigstreem, delivering reliable, high-performance internet service is our top priority. To maintain the integrity of our network and ensure consistent customer experiences, we follow strict guidelines regarding the equipment and solutions we support. This includes a clear stance on the use of Wi-Fi extenders.\n\n**Policy on Wi-Fi Extenders - Gigstreem Policy Reminder:**\n\n**It is strictly against Gigstreem policy to utilize, install, or recommend Wi-Fi extenders as a solution for speed, coverage, or connectivity issues within a unit.**\n\n- Why This Matters:\n- Wi-Fi extenders are not part of our approved network architecture.\n- They can introduce interference, degrade performance, and complicate troubleshooting.\n- Recommending or installing extenders may lead to inconsistent service and customer dissatisfaction.\n- Approved Resolution Methods:\n- Thorough troubleshooting of the existing AP and network configuration\n- Collaboration with engineering to assess AP configuration\n- All technicians and support staff must adhere to this policy without exception. Any deviation should be escalated to management for review.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-21T10:00","end":"2026-09-21T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":200,"max":275},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":200},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":75}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":3},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $275 is below minimum threshold $400"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Busy"},{"start":"2026-09-22T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"gap"},{"start":"2026-09-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-09-23T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Miniso"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ​Concord Police Department - NC ( Phase 2 ) (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-22T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"Remote Hands - Connect AT&T broadband circuit"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"},{"start":"2026-09-14T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789758721781}
{"job":{"id":19987331,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Gigstreem","title":"Cortland Brier Creek - Starlink Patch, TTU & Power Provisioning - #320968","description":{"html":"Read the work order carefully and confirm you have all the tools before requesting this work.<br>Scope of Work<p>Dispatch a qualified network technician to <strong>Cortland Brier Creek</strong> to work directly with the assigned Gigstreem Engineer for the <strong>temporary Starlink circuit patch-in, turn-up (TTU), and power provisioning validation</strong>.</p><p>The assigned Engineer will work remotely with the Field Technician throughout the process.</p>1. Pre-Work Verification<ul><li>Check in with property management and obtain access to the designated network equipment location.</li><li>Contact the assigned GigStreem Engineer before beginning any work.</li><li>Locate the Starlink handoff and applicable patch-in materials.</li><li>Locate and identify the Edge-Router.</li><li>Verify the correct circuit and designated Edge-Router port with Engineering before making any connection.</li><li>Visually inspect the existing equipment and report any unexpected conditions before proceeding.</li></ul>2. Temporary Starlink Circuit Patch-In<p>Working directly with Engineering:</p><ul><li>Identify the temporary Starlink circuit handoff.</li><li>Verify the required patching with Engineering.</li><li>Patch the circuit into the Edge-Router port designated by Engineering:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Primary → SFP+1</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Redundant → SFP+2</strong></li><li>Confirm with Engineering whether Starlink is being used as the primary or redundant connection <strong>before patching</strong>.</li><li>Do not disconnect or modify an existing production circuit unless explicitly instructed by Engineering.</li><li>Verify physical link status after completing the patch.</li><li>Assist Engineering with local or console access to the MikroTik Edge-Router if required.</li><li>Work with Engineering through the <strong>turn-up (TTU)</strong> and connectivity validation.</li><li>Perform any connectivity or speed testing requested by Engineering.</li><li>Report any handoff, cabling, SFP, interface, or connectivity issue immediately.</li></ul>3. UPS / EBM / PDU Visual Inspection<p>Working with Engineering and using the approved rack elevation/design diagram:</p><ul><li>Verify the LCP/MDF is built according to the approved rack elevation.</li><li>Verify the UPS battery is properly connected behind the front faceplate.</li><li>Verify the EBM umbilical and data cords are properly connected.</li><li>Verify the UPS is connected to <strong>Gateway eth7</strong>.</li><li>Report any loose, missing, damaged, or incorrectly connected components.</li></ul>4. Power Connection &amp; Label Verification<p>Verify that power supplies are labeled at both ends and connected according to the approved design.</p><p><strong>Edge Router</strong></p><ul><li>PS-A → Verify designated PDU connection.</li><li>PS-B → Verify designated UPS-critical connection.</li></ul><p><strong>Gateway</strong></p><ul><li>PS-A → Verify designated PDU connection.</li><li>PS-B → Verify designated UPS-critical connection.</li></ul><p><strong>MDF Aggregation Switch</strong></p><ul><li>PS-A → Verify designated PDU connection.</li><li>PS-B → Verify designated UPS-critical connection.</li></ul><p><strong>Provider Equipment</strong></p><ul><li>Verify PS-A and PS-B labeling at both ends.</li><li>Verify the power connections match the designated PDU/UPS-noncritical configuration shown in the design.</li></ul><p>Do not move or change any power connection unless specifically authorized by Engineering.</p>5. UPS Failover Testing<p>After the visual inspection is complete and Engineering authorizes testing:</p><ul><li>Coordinate with Engineering before removing commercial power.</li><li>Pull commercial power <strong>only when specifically directed by Engineering</strong>.</li><li>Verify the UPS successfully takes over and carries the connected load.</li><li>Confirm no breakers trip during the transfer.</li><li>Monitor the equipment for unexpected shutdowns or abnormal behavior.</li><li>Immediately notify Engineering if the UPS fails to carry the load, a breaker trips, or any equipment unexpectedly loses power.</li></ul>6. PDU / Power Supply Validation<p>The assigned Engineer will remotely access the UPS/PDU and perform controlled power-supply testing.</p><ul><li>Engineering will turn off <strong>one power supply at a time</strong> based on the existing labeling.</li><li>Technician will physically verify that the expected device/power supply is affected.</li><li>Confirm the correct power supply was turned off.</li><li>Engineering will restore the power supply before proceeding to the next device.</li><li>Repeat for each power supply requested by Engineering.</li><li>Report any mismatch between the PDU outlet/label and the actual equipment affected.</li></ul>7. Final Verification &amp; Documentation<p>Before leaving the property:</p><ul><li>Confirm with Engineering that the temporary Starlink circuit is online and the TTU is complete.</li><li>Confirm all required power provisioning/failover tests are complete.</li><li>Verify all tested power supplies have been restored to their normal operational state.</li><li>Verify all applicable network equipment remains powered and operational.</li><li>Provide clear photos of:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Starlink circuit handoff.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Final Edge-Router patch-in.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">LCP/MDF equipment.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">UPS, EBM, and PDU.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Relevant power connections and labels.</li><li>Document any circuit, cabling, labeling, power, or equipment issues.</li><li>Obtain Engineering confirmation that all work is complete before leaving the site.</li></ul>Tools Required<p>Technician must arrive with:</p><ul><li><strong>Windows laptop with Winbox and PuTTY installed and operational.</strong></li><li>Laptop charger.</li><li>Standard RJ45 Ethernet cable / known-good Cat6 patch cable.</li><li><strong>RJ45-to-USB console cable for the MikroTik console port.</strong></li><li>RJ45-to-DB9 cable and DB9-to-USB adapter, if applicable.</li><li>USB-to-Ethernet adapter if the laptop does not have an Ethernet port.</li><li>Basic network/hand-tool kit.</li><li>Ethernet cable tester.</li><li>Phone/camera for documentation and communication with Engineering.</li><li>Flashlight/headlamp.</li><li>Appropriate PPE required by the property.</li></ul>Technician Experience Required<p>Technician should have experience with:</p><ul><li>Circuit patch-in and turn-up (TTU).</li><li>MikroTik routers and Winbox.</li><li>Console access using PuTTY.</li><li>Ethernet and SFP/SFP+ interfaces.</li><li>Carrier/ISP handoffs and temporary WAN connections.</li><li>LCP/MDF network environments.</li><li>UPS/PDU systems and A/B redundant power.</li><li>Controlled power/failover testing.</li><li>Working directly with remote Network Engineering during circuit activation and testing.</li></ul>","markdown":"Read the work order carefully and confirm you have all the tools before requesting this work.  \nScope of Work\n\nDispatch a qualified network technician to **Cortland Brier Creek** to work directly with the assigned Gigstreem Engineer for the **temporary Starlink circuit patch-in, turn-up (TTU), and power provisioning validation**.\n\nThe assigned Engineer will work remotely with the Field Technician throughout the process.\n\n1. Pre-Work Verification- Check in with property management and obtain access to the designated network equipment location.\n- Contact the assigned GigStreem Engineer before beginning any work.\n- Locate the Starlink handoff and applicable patch-in materials.\n- Locate and identify the Edge-Router.\n- Verify the correct circuit and designated Edge-Router port with Engineering before making any connection.\n- Visually inspect the existing equipment and report any unexpected conditions before proceeding.\n\n2. Temporary Starlink Circuit Patch-InWorking directly with Engineering:\n\n- Identify the temporary Starlink circuit handoff.\n- Verify the required patching with Engineering.\n- Patch the circuit into the Edge-Router port designated by Engineering:\n- **Primary → SFP+1**\n- **Redundant → SFP+2**\n- Confirm with Engineering whether Starlink is being used as the primary or redundant connection **before patching**.\n- Do not disconnect or modify an existing production circuit unless explicitly instructed by Engineering.\n- Verify physical link status after completing the patch.\n- Assist Engineering with local or console access to the MikroTik Edge-Router if required.\n- Work with Engineering through the **turn-up (TTU)** and connectivity validation.\n- Perform any connectivity or speed testing requested by Engineering.\n- Report any handoff, cabling, SFP, interface, or connectivity issue immediately.\n\n3. UPS / EBM / PDU Visual InspectionWorking with Engineering and using the approved rack elevation/design diagram:\n\n- Verify the LCP/MDF is built according to the approved rack elevation.\n- Verify the UPS battery is properly connected behind the front faceplate.\n- Verify the EBM umbilical and data cords are properly connected.\n- Verify the UPS is connected to **Gateway eth7**.\n- Report any loose, missing, damaged, or incorrectly connected components.\n\n4. Power Connection & Label VerificationVerify that power supplies are labeled at both ends and connected according to the approved design.\n\n**Edge Router**\n\n- PS-A → Verify designated PDU connection.\n- PS-B → Verify designated UPS-critical connection.\n\n**Gateway**\n\n- PS-A → Verify designated PDU connection.\n- PS-B → Verify designated UPS-critical connection.\n\n**MDF Aggregation Switch**\n\n- PS-A → Verify designated PDU connection.\n- PS-B → Verify designated UPS-critical connection.\n\n**Provider Equipment**\n\n- Verify PS-A and PS-B labeling at both ends.\n- Verify the power connections match the designated PDU/UPS-noncritical configuration shown in the design.\n\nDo not move or change any power connection unless specifically authorized by Engineering.\n\n5. UPS Failover TestingAfter the visual inspection is complete and Engineering authorizes testing:\n\n- Coordinate with Engineering before removing commercial power.\n- Pull commercial power **only when specifically directed by Engineering**.\n- Verify the UPS successfully takes over and carries the connected load.\n- Confirm no breakers trip during the transfer.\n- Monitor the equipment for unexpected shutdowns or abnormal behavior.\n- Immediately notify Engineering if the UPS fails to carry the load, a breaker trips, or any equipment unexpectedly loses power.\n\n6. PDU / Power Supply ValidationThe assigned Engineer will remotely access the UPS/PDU and perform controlled power-supply testing.\n\n- Engineering will turn off **one power supply at a time** based on the existing labeling.\n- Technician will physically verify that the expected device/power supply is affected.\n- Confirm the correct power supply was turned off.\n- Engineering will restore the power supply before proceeding to the next device.\n- Repeat for each power supply requested by Engineering.\n- Report any mismatch between the PDU outlet/label and the actual equipment affected.\n\n7. Final Verification & DocumentationBefore leaving the property:\n\n- Confirm with Engineering that the temporary Starlink circuit is online and the TTU is complete.\n- Confirm all required power provisioning/failover tests are complete.\n- Verify all tested power supplies have been restored to their normal operational state.\n- Verify all applicable network equipment remains powered and operational.\n- Provide clear photos of:\n- Starlink circuit handoff.\n- Final Edge-Router patch-in.\n- LCP/MDF equipment.\n- UPS, EBM, and PDU.\n- Relevant power connections and labels.\n- Document any circuit, cabling, labeling, power, or equipment issues.\n- Obtain Engineering confirmation that all work is complete before leaving the site.\n\nTools RequiredTechnician must arrive with:\n\n- **Windows laptop with Winbox and PuTTY installed and operational.**\n- Laptop charger.\n- Standard RJ45 Ethernet cable / known-good Cat6 patch cable.\n- **RJ45-to-USB console cable for the MikroTik console port.**\n- RJ45-to-DB9 cable and DB9-to-USB adapter, if applicable.\n- USB-to-Ethernet adapter if the laptop does not have an Ethernet port.\n- Basic network/hand-tool kit.\n- Ethernet cable tester.\n- Phone/camera for documentation and communication with Engineering.\n- Flashlight/headlamp.\n- Appropriate PPE required by the property.\n\nTechnician Experience RequiredTechnician should have experience with:\n\n- Circuit patch-in and turn-up (TTU).\n- MikroTik routers and Winbox.\n- Console access using PuTTY.\n- Ethernet and SFP/SFP+ interfaces.\n- Carrier/ISP handoffs and temporary WAN connections.\n- LCP/MDF network environments.\n- UPS/PDU systems and A/B redundant power.\n- Controlled power/failover testing.\n- Working directly with remote Network Engineering during circuit activation and testing.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-22T10:00","end":"2026-09-22T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":200,"max":350},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":200},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":75}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":2},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"starlink\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-22T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"gap"},{"start":"2026-09-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-09-23T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Miniso"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ​Concord Police Department - NC ( Phase 2 ) (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-22T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"Remote Hands - Connect AT&T broadband circuit"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14