{"job":{"id":19986864,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"buyer name hidden","title":"T: T20260918.0326 - Roxboro, North Carolina - Ubiquiti U6 Pro WAP Offline Troubleshooting, Cable/PoE Testing, & Replacement (8 ft to 10 ft Ladder required)","description":{"html":"<strong><u>It is preferred that the technician performing the on-site service is the same individual who was initially assigned to the job.</u></strong><br><strong>MANDATORY: DO NOT ENTER THE SITE WITHOUT SPEAKING WITH THE DQ SUPPORT. Be prepared to show ID as requested</strong><p><br></p><strong>Scope of work:</strong><br><strong>1. Arrival, Check-In &amp; Etiquette</strong><ul><li>Arrive onsite at <strong>10:00 AM EST on Monday, September 21, 2026</strong>.</li><li>Check in with the site contact <del>*</del><strong><del>******* *****</del></strong><del> ** *************</del> and introduce yourself as representing <strong><del>******* *****</del></strong><del>*</del></li><li><strong>CRITICAL INSTRUCTION:</strong> Do <strong>NOT</strong> ask the local client contact to answer any technical questions regarding the network or work order.</li><li>Call the <strong><del>** ****</del> POC (<del>******* ********* ** *************</del></strong><del> </del>upon arrival to log start time.</li></ul><strong>2. Physical &amp; Line Inspection (U6 Pro WAP)</strong><ul><li>Locate the offline <strong>Ubiquiti U6 Pro WAP</strong> (<del>**** *****************</del>) on the ceiling using an A-Frame ladder.</li><li>Unmount the WAP and check for physical power/LED status.</li><li>Use a cable tester to perform tone/wiremap testing on the drop cable and patch panel/switch port. Verify proper 802.3at PoE power delivery from the switch port.</li></ul><strong>3. Hardware Swap &amp; Network Commissioning</strong><ul><li>If the line is healthy but the WAP is unrecoverable, work directly with<del> ** ****** ******</del>t to swap or adopt the replacement WAP unit.</li><li>Re-mount the access point securely to the ceiling tile/grid and verify solid PoE connection and link lights.</li></ul><strong>4. Validation &amp; Checkout</strong><ul><li>Work with <del>******* ********* </del>to confirm the WAP is online, broadcasting SSIDs, and adopting cleanly into the network controller.</li><li>Clean up the work area, upload photo deliverables, and call <del>** *******</del> for final check-out.</li></ul><strong>Deliverables: Photos to Upload</strong><p>Before checking out, upload the following clear photos:</p><ul><li><strong>WAP MAC / Serial Tag:</strong> Close-up photo showing the MAC address label (60:22:32:a7:8b:29) on the back of the Ubiquiti U6 Pro unit.</li><li><strong>Cable Tester PASS / Line Test:</strong> Photo showing cable tester results verifying continuity and PoE power delivery on the drop.</li><li><strong>Mounted WAP Active LED:</strong> Photo showing the access point securely re-mounted to the ceiling with its blue/white status LED powered on.</li><li><strong>Switch Port Status:</strong> Photo of the network switch port showing active PoE and link LEDs for the WAP line.</li></ul><p><br></p><ul><li>Complete all tasks listed in the WO.</li><li>Represent the CLIENT professionally and keep the site clean. Dress code: Professional attire.</li><li>Work closely with our remote support.</li></ul><p><br></p><strong>Date of Visit: 10:00 AM EST on Monday, September 21, 2026</strong>.<p><br></p><strong>Required Tools:</strong><strong>Testing &amp; Access</strong><ul><li><strong>A-Frame Ladder (8 ft to 10 ft)</strong> <em>(Required to access ceiling-mounted WAP)</em></li><li>Laptop with Native Ethernet Port (NIC) &amp; Console Cable</li><li>Mobile Hotspot</li><li>Network Cable Tester &amp; Tone/Probe Kit</li></ul><strong>Consumables &amp; Hand Tools</strong><ul><li>Cat6 RJ45 Patch Cables &amp; RJ45 Crimper / Connectors</li><li>Basic Hand Tools (screwdrivers, wire snips)</li><li>Smartphone for communication and Field Nation photo deliverables</li></ul><p><br></p><strong>1. Pre-Site Preparation</strong><ul><li><strong>Review:</strong>&nbsp;Study the WO and all attachments.</li><li><strong>Inventory:</strong>&nbsp;Verify all shipped equipment and ensure you have all necessary tools/parts.</li><li><strong>Support:</strong>&nbsp;Contact Support Tech with any pre-trip questions.</li></ul><strong>2. On-Site Procedures</strong><ul><li><strong>Check-In:</strong>&nbsp;Log into the WO, call&nbsp;<strong>Support Tech (470-470-7757)</strong>, and introduce yourself to the On-site Contact/Manager.</li><li><strong>Execution:</strong>&nbsp;Complete work, record the Manager on Duty’s name, and keep the work area clean.</li><li><strong>Professionalism:</strong>&nbsp;Do&nbsp;<strong>not</strong>&nbsp;discuss Field Nation with the client; Support Tech handles all reporting.</li></ul><strong>3. Required Deliverables</strong><ul><li><strong>Documentation:</strong>&nbsp;Detailed work notes and the Manager on Duty’s name.</li><li><strong>Photos:</strong>&nbsp;Clear Before/During/After photos of the work.</li><li><strong>Hardware:</strong>&nbsp;Serial and Model numbers (as applicable).</li><li><strong>Completion:</strong>&nbsp;Confirm full functionality with remote support before check-out.</li></ul><strong>4. Check-Out &amp; Submission</strong><ul><li><strong>Final Call:</strong>&nbsp;Contact&nbsp;<strong>Support Tech (470-470-7757)</strong>&nbsp;before leaving to review deliverables and obtain release code.</li><li><strong>Deadline:</strong>&nbsp;Upload all deliverables and submit the WO within&nbsp;<strong>24 hours</strong>.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>⚠️Payment &amp; Expense Policy</strong></p><p><strong>1. Flat Rate &amp; Travel Agreement</strong></p><p>This is a <strong>fixed-budget assignment</strong>. By accepting this Work Order without a prior counteroffer, the Service Provider agrees the listed rate is <strong>all-inclusive</strong> of labor, tools, and travel.</p><ul><li><strong>Trip Charges:</strong> No \"Trip Charges,\" \"Fuel Surcharges,\" or \"Travel Fees\" will be approved if added after the work is completed.</li><li><strong>Prior Approval:</strong> Any travel adjustments must have been submitted via counteroffer and approved by the Project/WO Manager <strong>prior to assignment</strong>.</li></ul><p><strong>2. Onsite Hours &amp; Completion</strong></p><p>All onsite hours will be compensated provided they are reasonable and the scope is fully completed.</p><ul><li><strong>Documentation:</strong> You must document any onsite delays or issues in the work order notes, clearly stating the reason for the delay.</li></ul><p><strong>3. Unauthorized Expenses</strong></p><p>Any expenses added to the final invoice that were not pre-authorized in writing via the platform's messaging system will be <strong>automatically rejected</strong>.</p><p><br></p><strong>⚠️ Compliance Alert</strong><p>Reductions in pay or penalties may apply for:</p><ul><li>Leaving site without posting deliverables or obtaining a release code.</li><li>Failing to submit the WO within the 24-hour window.</li></ul>","markdown":"**It is preferred that the technician performing the on-site service is the same individual who was initially assigned to the job.**  \n**MANDATORY: DO NOT ENTER THE SITE WITHOUT SPEAKING WITH THE DQ SUPPORT. Be prepared to show ID as requested****Scope of work:**  \n**1. Arrival, Check-In & Etiquette**- Arrive onsite at **10:00 AM EST on Monday, September 21, 2026**.\n- Check in with the site contact \\***\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*** \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* and introduce yourself as representing **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\\*\n- **CRITICAL INSTRUCTION:** Do **NOT** ask the local client contact to answer any technical questions regarding the network or work order.\n- Call the **\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\* POC (\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*** upon arrival to log start time.\n\n**2. Physical & Line Inspection (U6 Pro WAP)**- Locate the offline **Ubiquiti U6 Pro WAP** (\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*) on the ceiling using an A-Frame ladder.\n- Unmount the WAP and check for physical power/LED status.\n- Use a cable tester to perform tone/wiremap testing on the drop cable and patch panel/switch port. Verify proper 802.3at PoE power delivery from the switch port.\n\n**3. Hardware Swap & Network Commissioning**- If the line is healthy but the WAP is unrecoverable, work directly with \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*t to swap or adopt the replacement WAP unit.\n- Re-mount the access point securely to the ceiling tile/grid and verify solid PoE connection and link lights.\n\n**4. Validation & Checkout**- Work with \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* to confirm the WAP is online, broadcasting SSIDs, and adopting cleanly into the network controller.\n- Clean up the work area, upload photo deliverables, and call \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* for final check-out.\n\n**Deliverables: Photos to Upload**Before checking out, upload the following clear photos:\n\n- **WAP MAC / Serial Tag:** Close-up photo showing the MAC address label (60:22:32:a7:8b:29) on the back of the Ubiquiti U6 Pro unit.\n- **Cable Tester PASS / Line Test:** Photo showing cable tester results verifying continuity and PoE power delivery on the drop.\n- **Mounted WAP Active LED:** Photo showing the access point securely re-mounted to the ceiling with its blue/white status LED powered on.\n- **Switch Port Status:** Photo of the network switch port showing active PoE and link LEDs for the WAP line.\n\n- Complete all tasks listed in the WO.\n- Represent the CLIENT professionally and keep the site clean. Dress code: Professional attire.\n- Work closely with our remote support.\n\n**Date of Visit: 10:00 AM EST on Monday, September 21, 2026**.**Required Tools:****Testing & Access**- **A-Frame Ladder (8 ft to 10 ft)** *(Required to access ceiling-mounted WAP)*\n- Laptop with Native Ethernet Port (NIC) & Console Cable\n- Mobile Hotspot\n- Network Cable Tester & Tone/Probe Kit\n\n**Consumables & Hand Tools**- Cat6 RJ45 Patch Cables & RJ45 Crimper / Connectors\n- Basic Hand Tools (screwdrivers, wire snips)\n- Smartphone for communication and Field Nation photo deliverables\n\n**1. Pre-Site Preparation**- **Review:** Study the WO and all attachments.\n- **Inventory:** Verify all shipped equipment and ensure you have all necessary tools/parts.\n- **Support:** Contact Support Tech with any pre-trip questions.\n\n**2. On-Site Procedures**- **Check-In:** Log into the WO, call **Support Tech (470-470-7757)**, and introduce yourself to the On-site Contact/Manager.\n- **Execution:** Complete work, record the Manager on Duty’s name, and keep the work area clean.\n- **Professionalism:** Do **not** discuss Field Nation with the client; Support Tech handles all reporting.\n\n**3. Required Deliverables**- **Documentation:** Detailed work notes and the Manager on Duty’s name.\n- **Photos:** Clear Before/During/After photos of the work.\n- **Hardware:** Serial and Model numbers (as applicable).\n- **Completion:** Confirm full functionality with remote support before check-out.\n\n**4. Check-Out & Submission**- **Final Call:** Contact **Support Tech (470-470-7757)** before leaving to review deliverables and obtain release code.\n- **Deadline:** Upload all deliverables and submit the WO within **24 hours**.\n\n**⚠️Payment & Expense Policy**\n\n**1. Flat Rate & Travel Agreement**\n\nThis is a **fixed-budget assignment**. By accepting this Work Order without a prior counteroffer, the Service Provider agrees the listed rate is **all-inclusive** of labor, tools, and travel.\n\n- **Trip Charges:** No \"Trip Charges,\" \"Fuel Surcharges,\" or \"Travel Fees\" will be approved if added after the work is completed.\n- **Prior Approval:** Any travel adjustments must have been submitted via counteroffer and approved by the Project/WO Manager **prior to assignment**.\n\n**2. Onsite Hours & Completion**\n\nAll onsite hours will be compensated provided they are reasonable and the scope is fully completed.\n\n- **Documentation:** You must document any onsite delays or issues in the work order notes, clearly stating the reason for the delay.\n\n**3. Unauthorized Expenses**\n\nAny expenses added to the final invoice that were not pre-authorized in writing via the platform's messaging system will be **automatically rejected**.\n\n**⚠️ Compliance Alert**Reductions in pay or penalties may apply for:\n\n- Leaving site without posting deliverables or obtaining a release code.\n- Failing to submit the WO within the 24-hour window.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-21T10:00","end":"2026-09-21T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":100},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":50,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":33},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 (countered: $120) is below minimum threshold $400"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Busy"},{"start":"2026-09-22T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"gap"},{"start":"2026-09-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-09-23T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Miniso"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-2