{"job":{"id":19918269,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Cipe Solutions","title":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | 3rd Party AMP | Amplifier & Speaker Upgrade","description":{"html":"<p><strong>PLEASE READ THE FOLLOWING CAREFULLY. FAILURE TO COMPLY MAY RESULT IN WITHHELD PAYMENTS</strong></p><p>Call or chat <strong>Activations</strong> for check in as well as more detailed instruction.</p><ul><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">(888)747-9530, Ext. 888</strong></li><li><strong>techonsite.chat</strong></li></ul><br><p><strong>TICKET SUMMARY:</strong> JBL CSA140Z AMPLIFIER, CSR-V VOLUME CONTROL &amp; THREE (3) SPEAKER REPLACEMENTS, 70V CIRCUIT AUDIT &amp; RACK OPTIMIZATION</p><p><br></p><strong>I. PROJECT SUMMARY</strong><p>A technician with commercial audio experience is required on-site to install a new <strong>JBL CSA140Z-U-US Amplifier</strong>, mount a <strong>CSR-V Volume Control</strong> wall plate, replace <strong>three (3) old/failing 70V speakers</strong> with new replacement units, perform a mandatory 70V speaker circuit audit, and execute a full cable management overhaul of the IT/audio rack.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>KEY EXECUTION MANDATES:</strong></p><p><br></p><ul><li><strong>VOLUME CONTROL CABLING:</strong> Pull a new Cat6 home run from the wall volume control location to the audio rack, terminating both ends to the T568B standard.</li><li><strong>SPEAKER REPLACEMENT &amp; CIRCUIT AUDIT:</strong> Unmount the three (3) defective speakers and install the three (3) new replacement units. Test all speaker line impedance ($\\Omega$) with a multimeter and physically inspect/set every speaker transformer tap (both new and remaining existing units) to ensure total load does not exceed the amplifier's 40W per channel rating before applying power.</li><li><strong>DEFECTIVE ASSET DISPOSAL:</strong> Upon successful installation and testing, box up all legacy hardware (old amplifier, old volume control, and the three replaced speakers), mark the package clearly as <strong>\"DEFECTIVE - FOR SITE DISPOSAL,\"</strong> and stage it in a designated out-of-the-way area on-site. Do not remove hardware from the property.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>DUAL SIGN-OFF MANDATE:</strong> The technician must obtain explicit operational and audio testing confirmation from remote <strong>Activations</strong> and the on-site <strong>Manager on Duty (MOD)</strong> prior to departing the facility.</p><p><br></p><strong>II. REQUIRED TOOLS &amp; SUPPLIES</strong><ul><li><strong>LAPTOP WITH PHYSICAL ETHERNET PORT &amp; MOBILE HOTSPOT!</strong> (<strong>Absolute Mandatory Requirement</strong> for audio interface checks, DSP/amplifier configuration, and local network verification)</li><li><strong>6–8ft Ladder &amp; Pull Rods / Fish Tape</strong> (For pulling the new Cat6 volume control line and accessing ceiling/wall speakers)</li><li><strong>Volt Meter / Multimeter &amp; Audio Cable Tester / Toner</strong> (<strong>Mandatory</strong> for speaker line impedance $\\Omega$, ground fault testing, and Cat6 continuity)</li><li><strong>Cat5e/6 &amp; 16/2 or 18/2 Speaker Wire Supplies:</strong> RJ45 connectors, keystone jacks, wire nuts/B-connectors, modular crimpers, wire strippers, and snips</li><li><strong>General Tool Kit w/ Power Drill, Bits, &amp; Mounting Hardware</strong> (Including drywall anchors, wall screws, and rack hardware)</li><li><strong>Cable Management Supplies:</strong> High-quality <strong>Velcro ties</strong> (preferred) or zip ties, <strong>Label Maker</strong>, and packaging tape</li><li><strong>Mobile Smart-Phone</strong> (Required for live on-site check-in/check-out tracking via browser chat)</li></ul><p><br></p><strong>III. ON-SITE EXECUTION STEPS</strong><strong>PHASE 1: ARRIVAL &amp; STRATEGIC ALIGNMENT</strong><ol><li><strong>MANDATORY CHECK-IN:</strong> Visit <strong>CIPE.CHAT</strong> in your mobile device's browser with your Name and Service Ticket #. If you receive no response, contact Dispatch at <strong>(888) 747-9530, Ext. 888</strong>.</li><li><strong>MOD CONTACT:</strong> Meet with the Manager on Duty (MOD). Have them walk you to the main audio/network rack, the volume control wall location, and the three (3) failing speaker locations. Collect the newly shipped hardware boxes.</li><li><strong>SUPPORT ENGAGEMENT:</strong> Call <strong>Activations at (888) 747-9530, Ext. 411</strong>. Review the SOW, speaker replacement plan, and tap configuration with remote support before disconnecting active equipment.</li></ol><p><br></p><strong>PHASE 2: CABLE PULL, SPEAKER REPLACEMENTS &amp; MANDATORY CIRCUIT AUDIT</strong><ol><li><strong>CAT6 HOME RUN:</strong> Pull a new Cat6 home run from the volume control wall location back to the audio rack. Terminate both ends to the <strong>T568B Standard</strong> and verify continuity with your cable tester.</li><li><strong>SPEAKER DECOMMISSIONING &amp; REPLACEMENT:</strong></li></ol><ul><li>Power off the existing amplifier.</li><li>Unmount the three (3) old/failing speakers from their ceiling/wall positions.</li><li>Mount the three (3) new replacement speakers securely using appropriate brackets and mounting hardware.</li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><strong>SPEAKER WIRE RESISTANCE TESTING:</strong> Use your <strong>multimeter</strong> to measure and log resistance ($\\Omega$) across all speaker runs. Check for short circuits, open loops, or shorts to ground.</li><li><strong>TAP SETTING VERIFICATION:</strong> Access every 70V speaker in the facility (including the 3 newly installed units) using your ladder. Verify that physical transformer tap settings are set correctly for a 70V system and that total combined wattage load <strong>does not exceed the JBL CSA140Z amplifier's 40W per channel rating</strong>.</li><li><strong>SUPPORT HOLD:</strong> Submit wire test readings and total calculated tap wattage to Activations (Ext. 411). <strong>DO NOT</strong> power on the new JBL amplifier until Support validates these readings.</li></ol><p><br></p><strong>PHASE 3: HARDWARE INSTALLATION &amp; RACK OVERHAUL</strong><ol><li><strong>HARDWARE MOUNTING:</strong> Remove the old amplifier. Rack-mount the new JBL CSA140Z amplifier in the rack frame and mount the CSR-V volume control on the wall.</li><li><strong>RACK CABLE MANAGEMENT:</strong> Organize, bundle, and route all existing and new cables within the network/audio rack using <strong>Velcro ties</strong>. Dress cables cleanly along the side of the rack rails.</li><li><strong>LABELING:</strong> Print labels using your label maker. Label the new Cat6 <strong>\"Volume Control\"</strong> and label each speaker pair (e.g., \"Zone 1 - Main Floor\") at the amplifier terminal block.</li></ol><p><br></p><strong>PHASE 4: SYSTEM TESTING &amp; DUAL VERIFICATION</strong><ol><li><strong>POWER RESTORATION:</strong> Turn on the JBL CSA140Z amplifier under Support direction.</li><li><strong>AUDIO AUDIT:</strong> Play music through the system. Walk all zones with the MOD and Support to confirm clear audio playback across all speakers (paying specific attention to the 3 new units) and verify responsive CSR-V volume control functionality.</li></ol><p><br></p><strong>PHASE 5: SITE DISPOSAL &amp; CLEANUP</strong><ol><li><strong>STAGING FOR DISPOSAL:</strong> Box up the old amplifier, legacy volume control, and the three (3) decommissioned speakers. Mark the package clearly as <strong>\"DEFECTIVE - FOR SITE DISPOSAL\"</strong> and stage it in the store's designated IT storage area. <strong>Do not remove hardware from the property.</strong></li><li><strong>CLEANUP:</strong> Gather up all wire snippets, insulation scraps, drywall dust, packaging waste, and debris. Ensure the server room, volume control wall, and speaker replacement areas are left spotless.</li></ol><p><br></p><strong>IV. REQUIRED PHOTO DELIVERABLES (TO BE ATTACHED TO TICKET)</strong><ul><li>[ ] <strong>New Amp &amp; Managed Rack:</strong> Clear wide-angle photo showing neat cabling, labeling, and the new JBL amplifier powered on (<strong>Full view, cabinet door OPEN</strong>).</li><li>[ ] <strong>New CSR-V Installed:</strong> Photo of the new CSR-V volume control cleanly mounted on the wall.</li><li>[ ] <strong>Three (3) New Speakers Installed:</strong> Photos showing each of the 3 new replacement speakers cleanly mounted in their ceiling/wall positions.</li><li>[ ] <strong>Multimeter Readings:</strong> Photo displaying multimeter resistance/impedance ($\\Omega$) measurements taken on the speaker lines.</li><li>[ ] <strong>T568B Termination Close-up:</strong> Close-up photo showing B-Standard pinout terminations on the new Cat6 line.</li><li>[ ] <strong>Staged Defective Hardware:</strong> Photo showing the old amplifier, old volume control, and 3 legacy speakers boxed and staged in the designated site disposal area.</li><li>[ ] <strong>Immaculate Workspace:</strong> Photo proving the server room floor, volume control area, and speaker locations are swept clean.</li></ul><p><br></p><strong>V. FINAL SIGN-OFF &amp; TICKET CLOSEOUT</strong><ol><li><strong>DUAL CONFIRMATION MANDATE:</strong></li></ol><ul><li><strong>Activations:</strong> Confirm verbal sign-off from remote support (Ext. 411) that audio telemetry, line impedance, tap settings, and volume control performance are 100% operational.</li><li><strong>MOD Acceptance:</strong> Walk the store with the manager to demonstrate clear audio playback across all zones (including the 3 new speakers), confirm volume control operation, and obtain operational sign-off.</li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><strong>SIGN-OFF:</strong> Secure the MOD's signature on your physical or digital work order layout confirming completed installation, audio testing, and site cleanliness.</li><li><strong>MANDATORY CHECK-OUT:</strong> Visit <strong>CIPE.CHAT</strong> in your mobile browser to execute your final check-out tracking loop with Support (or call Dispatch at <strong>(888) 747-9530, Ext. 888</strong> if no response).</li><li><strong>TICKET LOGS:</strong> Update ticket notes detailing multimeter readings ($\\Omega$), tap settings verified across all speakers, and hardware installation parameters before closing the work order.</li></ol><p>____________________________</p><p><strong><u>TERMS AND CONDITIONS</u></strong></p><ul><li>Cipe Activations team is empowered to Verbally approve labor overages</li><li><strong>Smoking and vaping are strictly Prohibited on premises!!</strong></li><li>All technicians must wear full-length pants as part of the dress code; shorts are strictly prohibited. Technicians are required to wear closed-toe shoes at all times. Slip-on or open-toe footwear is strictly prohibited.</li><li>Technicians are required to remove any debris, boxes or trash from work area prior to leaving.</li></ul><p><strong>Cancellation Fee:</strong> A flat <strong>$100 cancellation fee</strong> will apply in lieu of all hourly, fixed, or blended rates when scheduled work cannot be performed (and tech has already checked in) due to missing hardware, site refusal/turn-away, or the work being completed before technician arrival (provided the technician arrives within 15 minutes of the scheduled time).</p><ul><li>If the technician is unprepared for the agreed scope of work, lacks required equipment, or arrives more than 15 minutes late(for hard start), and the work cannot be completed due to these circumstances, both the <strong>$100 cancellation fee and all agreed service rates are waived</strong>.</li></ul><p><em>In order for work order to be considered complete and tech to receive prompt payment, all work order tasks must be completed and tech must be released by CIPE Support.</em></p>","markdown":"**PLEASE READ THE FOLLOWING CAREFULLY. FAILURE TO COMPLY MAY RESULT IN WITHHELD PAYMENTS**\n\nCall or chat **Activations** for check in as well as more detailed instruction.\n\n- **(888)747-9530, Ext. 888**\n- **techonsite.chat**\n\n  \n**TICKET SUMMARY:** JBL CSA140Z AMPLIFIER, CSR-V VOLUME CONTROL & THREE (3) SPEAKER REPLACEMENTS, 70V CIRCUIT AUDIT & RACK OPTIMIZATION\n\n**I. PROJECT SUMMARY**A technician with commercial audio experience is required on-site to install a new **JBL CSA140Z-U-US Amplifier**, mount a **CSR-V Volume Control** wall plate, replace **three (3) old/failing 70V speakers** with new replacement units, perform a mandatory 70V speaker circuit audit, and execute a full cable management overhaul of the IT/audio rack.\n\n**KEY EXECUTION MANDATES:**\n\n- **VOLUME CONTROL CABLING:** Pull a new Cat6 home run from the wall volume control location to the audio rack, terminating both ends to the T568B standard.\n- **SPEAKER REPLACEMENT & CIRCUIT AUDIT:** Unmount the three (3) defective speakers and install the three (3) new replacement units. Test all speaker line impedance ($\\\\Omega$) with a multimeter and physically inspect/set every speaker transformer tap (both new and remaining existing units) to ensure total load does not exceed the amplifier's 40W per channel rating before applying power.\n- **DEFECTIVE ASSET DISPOSAL:** Upon successful installation and testing, box up all legacy hardware (old amplifier, old volume control, and the three replaced speakers), mark the package clearly as **\"DEFECTIVE - FOR SITE DISPOSAL,\"** and stage it in a designated out-of-the-way area on-site. Do not remove hardware from the property.\n\n**DUAL SIGN-OFF MANDATE:** The technician must obtain explicit operational and audio testing confirmation from remote **Activations** and the on-site **Manager on Duty (MOD)** prior to departing the facility.\n\n**II. REQUIRED TOOLS & SUPPLIES**- **LAPTOP WITH PHYSICAL ETHERNET PORT & MOBILE HOTSPOT!** (**Absolute Mandatory Requirement** for audio interface checks, DSP/amplifier configuration, and local network verification)\n- **6–8ft Ladder & Pull Rods / Fish Tape** (For pulling the new Cat6 volume control line and accessing ceiling/wall speakers)\n- **Volt Meter / Multimeter & Audio Cable Tester / Toner** (**Mandatory** for speaker line impedance $\\\\Omega$, ground fault testing, and Cat6 continuity)\n- **Cat5e/6 & 16/2 or 18/2 Speaker Wire Supplies:** RJ45 connectors, keystone jacks, wire nuts/B-connectors, modular crimpers, wire strippers, and snips\n- **General Tool Kit w/ Power Drill, Bits, & Mounting Hardware** (Including drywall anchors, wall screws, and rack hardware)\n- **Cable Management Supplies:** High-quality **Velcro ties** (preferred) or zip ties, **Label Maker**, and packaging tape\n- **Mobile Smart-Phone** (Required for live on-site check-in/check-out tracking via browser chat)\n\n**III. ON-SITE EXECUTION STEPS****PHASE 1: ARRIVAL & STRATEGIC ALIGNMENT**1. **MANDATORY CHECK-IN:** Visit **CIPE.CHAT** in your mobile device's browser with your Name and Service Ticket #. If you receive no response, contact Dispatch at **(888) 747-9530, Ext. 888**.\n2. **MOD CONTACT:** Meet with the Manager on Duty (MOD). Have them walk you to the main audio/network rack, the volume control wall location, and the three (3) failing speaker locations. Collect the newly shipped hardware boxes.\n3. **SUPPORT ENGAGEMENT:** Call **Activations at (888) 747-9530, Ext. 411**. Review the SOW, speaker replacement plan, and tap configuration with remote support before disconnecting active equipment.\n\n**PHASE 2: CABLE PULL, SPEAKER REPLACEMENTS & MANDATORY CIRCUIT AUDIT**1. **CAT6 HOME RUN:** Pull a new Cat6 home run from the volume control wall location back to the audio rack. Terminate both ends to the **T568B Standard** and verify continuity with your cable tester.\n2. **SPEAKER DECOMMISSIONING & REPLACEMENT:**\n\n- Power off the existing amplifier.\n- Unmount the three (3) old/failing speakers from their ceiling/wall positions.\n- Mount the three (3) new replacement speakers securely using appropriate brackets and mounting hardware.\n\n1. **SPEAKER WIRE RESISTANCE TESTING:** Use your **multimeter** to measure and log resistance ($\\\\Omega$) across all speaker runs. Check for short circuits, open loops, or shorts to ground.\n2. **TAP SETTING VERIFICATION:** Access every 70V speaker in the facility (including the 3 newly installed units) using your ladder. Verify that physical transformer tap settings are set correctly for a 70V system and that total combined wattage load **does not exceed the JBL CSA140Z amplifier's 40W per channel rating**.\n3. **SUPPORT HOLD:** Submit wire test readings and total calculated tap wattage to Activations (Ext. 411). **DO NOT** power on the new JBL amplifier until Support validates these readings.\n\n**PHASE 3: HARDWARE INSTALLATION & RACK OVERHAUL**1. **HARDWARE MOUNTING:** Remove the old amplifier. Rack-mount the new JBL CSA140Z amplifier in the rack frame and mount the CSR-V volume control on the wall.\n2. **RACK CABLE MANAGEMENT:** Organize, bundle, and route all existing and new cables within the network/audio rack using **Velcro ties**. Dress cables cleanly along the side of the rack rails.\n3. **LABELING:** Print labels using your label maker. Label the new Cat6 **\"Volume Control\"** and label each speaker pair (e.g., \"Zone 1 - Main Floor\") at the amplifier terminal block.\n\n**PHASE 4: SYSTEM TESTING & DUAL VERIFICATION**1. **POWER RESTORATION:** Turn on the JBL CSA140Z amplifier under Support direction.\n2. **AUDIO AUDIT:** Play music through the system. Walk all zones with the MOD and Support to confirm clear audio playback across all speakers (paying specific attention to the 3 new units) and verify responsive CSR-V volume control functionality.\n\n**PHASE 5: SITE DISPOSAL & CLEANUP**1. **STAGING FOR DISPOSAL:** Box up the old amplifier, legacy volume control, and the three (3) decommissioned speakers. Mark the package clearly as **\"DEFECTIVE - FOR SITE DISPOSAL\"** and stage it in the store's designated IT storage area. **Do not remove hardware from the property.**\n2. **CLEANUP:** Gather up all wire snippets, insulation scraps, drywall dust, packaging waste, and debris. Ensure the server room, volume control wall, and speaker replacement areas are left spotless.\n\n**IV. REQUIRED PHOTO DELIVERABLES (TO BE ATTACHED TO TICKET)**- \\[ \\] **New Amp & Managed Rack:** Clear wide-angle photo showing neat cabling, labeling, and the new JBL amplifier powered on (**Full view, cabinet door OPEN**).\n- \\[ \\] **New CSR-V Installed:** Photo of the new CSR-V volume control cleanly mounted on the wall.\n- \\[ \\] **Three (3) New Speakers Installed:** Photos showing each of the 3 new replacement speakers cleanly mounted in their ceiling/wall positions.\n- \\[ \\] **Multimeter Readings:** Photo displaying multimeter resistance/impedance ($\\\\Omega$) measurements taken on the speaker lines.\n- \\[ \\] **T568B Termination Close-up:** Close-up photo showing B-Standard pinout terminations on the new Cat6 line.\n- \\[ \\] **Staged Defective Hardware:** Photo showing the old amplifier, old volume control, and 3 legacy speakers boxed and staged in the designated site disposal area.\n- \\[ \\] **Immaculate Workspace:** Photo proving the server room floor, volume control area, and speaker locations are swept clean.\n\n**V. FINAL SIGN-OFF & TICKET CLOSEOUT**1. **DUAL CONFIRMATION MANDATE:**\n\n- **Activations:** Confirm verbal sign-off from remote support (Ext. 411) that audio telemetry, line impedance, tap settings, and volume control performance are 100% operational.\n- **MOD Acceptance:** Walk the store with the manager to demonstrate clear audio playback across all zones (including the 3 new speakers), confirm volume control operation, and obtain operational sign-off.\n\n1. **SIGN-OFF:** Secure the MOD's signature on your physical or digital work order layout confirming completed installation, audio testing, and site cleanliness.\n2. **MANDATORY CHECK-OUT:** Visit **CIPE.CHAT** in your mobile browser to execute your final check-out tracking loop with Support (or call Dispatch at **(888) 747-9530, Ext. 888** if no response).\n3. **TICKET LOGS:** Update ticket notes detailing multimeter readings ($\\\\Omega$), tap settings verified across all speakers, and hardware installation parameters before closing the work order.\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\n**TERMS AND CONDITIONS**\n\n- Cipe Activations team is empowered to Verbally approve labor overages\n- **Smoking and vaping are strictly Prohibited on premises!!**\n- All technicians must wear full-length pants as part of the dress code; shorts are strictly prohibited. Technicians are required to wear closed-toe shoes at all times. Slip-on or open-toe footwear is strictly prohibited.\n- Technicians are required to remove any debris, boxes or trash from work area prior to leaving.\n\n**Cancellation Fee:** A flat **$100 cancellation fee** will apply in lieu of all hourly, fixed, or blended rates when scheduled work cannot be performed (and tech has already checked in) due to missing hardware, site refusal/turn-away, or the work being completed before technician arrival (provided the technician arrives within 15 minutes of the scheduled time).\n\n- If the technician is unprepared for the agreed scope of work, lacks required equipment, or arrives more than 15 minutes late(for hard start), and the work cannot be completed due to these circumstances, both the **$100 cancellation fee and all agreed service rates are waived**.\n\n*In order for work order to be considered complete and tech to receive prompt payment, all work order tasks must be completed and tech must be released by CIPE Support.*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-14T09:00","end":"2026-09-14T11:00","latestStart":"2026-09-14T10:00"},"payRange":{"min":525,"max":525},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":150},"additional":{"units":5,"amount":75}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":14},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 9/14/2026, 9:00:00 AM is in the past"},"availableBloc