{"job":{"id":19975636,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Direct Source","title":"Pin Pad Installation","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Call the End Client Command Center along with the Direct Source Support Desk prior to leaving each site to complete a check out procedure and to record unique DSI checkout code </strong>(voice mail is not an acceptable check out and could result in the Tech nician returning to the site at the Technician's own expense).</p><p><strong>Submittal of pictures and paperwork (\"Deliverables\") due to End Client by emailing the End Client Command Center team BEFORE checking out with them.</strong></p><p><strong>Submittal of pictures and paperwork (\"Deliverables\") due to DSI by uploading to the DSI Mobile App BEFORE leaving site</strong> (or within 24 hours of site completion if there are issues uploading from site).</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Services</u></strong>: This is a complex project with detailed tasks to be performed by DSI, Technician and the End Customer, as documented in the Technical Guide or in a signed Change Authorization.</p><p>An overview of the services to be performed by the Technician include, but are not limited to:</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Check In using the DSI Mobile App or contact the Direct Source Support Desk upon arrival at each site.</strong></p><p>Check in with MOD and confirm hardware and work location. May need to show a form of ID along with your Customer Letter of Authorization form.</p><p>Check in with the End Client Command Center by calling into their Support Bridge.</p><p><strong><u>Required Deliverables</u>: </strong>Obtain <strong>\"BEFORE\"</strong> <strong>images of all Registers or Cash Wrap areas PRIOR to starting</strong> <strong>any work.</strong></p><p>Upload photos as necessary deliverables via the DSI Mobile App.</p><p>Email all required photos to the End Client Command Center throughout the installation.</p><p><strong>Pre-Installation inventory</strong> of new hardware at the store location.</p><ul><li><strong><u>Required Deliverables</u>: Take a required deliverable photo of the packing slip.</strong></li><li>Record inventory counts or any issues on the End Client Command Center Check In / Out Form.</li></ul><p>Inspect existing devices for condition and power status. Document any device(s) not working properly and have MOD signoff on the End Client Check In / Out Form.</p><p>Begin installing the new Verifone m450s, cables, and adapter plates &ndash; Can work on only TWO LANES at a time to begin with.</p><ul><li>You will stage each new pin pad by disconnecting the old pin pad cable, install the new pin pad cable and connect to the register. .</li><li><strong>Security Screws</strong>: Each M450 has a security screw in a brown piece of paper in the box. This must be installed to secure the plastic cover over the pin pad connection.</li><li><strong>P-Clips</strong>: Each pin pad cable <strong>must be routed down and behind each pin pad</strong> and secured with the supplied P-Clip.</li><li><strong>Verify Mounting Bracket orientation</strong>: When passing the pin pad cable through the top mounting bracket, make sure it is facing the right way to flip down and onto the pin pad.</li><li><strong>Notify the End Client Support Team upon completion of each register </strong>&ndash; Ross will perform the required software updates and then the MOD can test each lane.</li></ul><p>Proceed with replacing the remaining Pin Pads and update the End Client Command Center after each new device is booted up so they can complete the updates.</p><ul><li>Do not power down a register as that may cause delays.</li></ul><p>Neatly manage the new pin pad cable in the same manner the original cable was found. Use Velcro to secure it.</p><p>MOD to validate pin pads are functional.</p><ul><li>The MOD can test each lane once End Client verifies updates are done. They do not need to wait until the end of the install.</li></ul><p><strong>Hardware Return</strong>: Package old hardware and cables in the new hardware boxes and ready for return shipment. Leave with MOD when done.</p><ul><li><strong>Ensure the correct return labels are placed on each box</strong>.</li><li>Place the <strong>old cables &amp; anti-skimmer plates</strong> inside the smaller box &ndash; RETURN TO UNPLUGGED C/O \"Burg Electronic Recovery\" for Disposal.</li><li>Place the <strong>old MX915 pin pads</strong> inside the master pack box using bubble wrap &ndash; RETURN to LEVEL10 (End Client's Depot Stock) for break/fix.</li></ul><p>Clean up all work areas and throw away extra boxes and packing materials in designated location.</p><p>Complete the Check In / Out form and obtain MOD signature.</p><p>Sign off on the MOD Validation Form and obtain MOD signature.</p><p>The technician will provide End Client project team pictures via email distribution of installed pin pads to validate correct installation/placement before checkout.</p><ul><li><strong><u>Required Deliverables</u>: </strong>Obtain <strong>\"AFTER\"</strong> <strong>images of all Registers (one photo per lane) and the hardware return with tracking numbers clearly visible. </strong></li><li>Email all final deliverables including the 2 checklists / sign off forms to the End Client Command Center.</li></ul><p>Check out with the End Client Command Center Support Team.</p><p><strong>Check out with Direct Source/End Customer Support Desk prior to leaving each site to complete a check out procedure</strong> (voice mail is not an acceptable checkout and could result in the Technician returning to the site at the Technician's own expense).</p><p>Technician will provide quality checks on all completed work to ensure that all work has been completed and is free from any defects.</p><p>Submittal of pictures and paperwork (\"Deliverables\") due while onsite or else within 24 hours of site completion to the Direct Source Portal (for installations on multiple dates &ndash; submit daily deliverables).</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Technician Required Equipment, Tools &amp; Hardware:</u></strong></p><p>Standard&nbsp;Technician Tool kit (multi-size screwdrivers, cordless drill &amp; various bits, hammer, etc.)</p><p>Cell phone with fully charged battery, charger, and ongoing active account with your carrier</p><p><strong>Phone charger required</strong> -&nbsp;will need to be on the phone majority of the install with ROSS Support</p><p>Printed copy of the End Client Check In and Out Form [Installation Checklist] and the Technical Installation Guide &ndash;&nbsp;<strong>Included in Shipment</strong>.</p><p># 1&nbsp;Philips screwdriver</p><p># 2 Philips screwdriver</p><p>T8 Torx Bit &ndash; Screwdriver or Allen Key type</p><p>Step drill bit (Unibit) - to enlarge the mounting hole or make hole in counter, if required</p><p>Packing tape</p><p>Velcro (for cable management)</p><p>Electrical tape</p><p>Headlamp or small portable light (suggested) - the store lights dim after closing, so extra light should be helpful</p><p>Ear buds or headset (suggested) - can be hands-free when working and still talk to the End Client Command Center as needed</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Project Preparation/ Orientation:</u></strong></p><p><strong>The Technician who will be onsite</strong>, must complete a mandatory conference call orientation session prior to the start of their assigned installation(s) unless other arrangements are mutually agreed upon. During that session, the Technician will learn Direct Source's and End Customer's expectations, processes, deliverable requirements, project scope as well as lessons learned from previous installations. <strong>Direct Source will provide a detailed Installation Service Guide (Technical Guide) on the Direct Source Portal, which must be reviewed prior to project orientation, and must be brought with to each installation.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Deliverables &amp; Reporting</u></strong>: Deliverables are defined as any documentation and/or digital photos required per the Technical Guide. All Deliverables must be uploaded to the Direct Source Portal or via the DSI Mobile App (preferred).</p><p><strong>Deliverables must be EMAILED TO End Client BEFORE CHECKOUT and then uploaded to DSI via Mobile App or Web Portal BEFORE leaving site for the project team to review the next morning. </strong>If there are any issues doing so, photos must be uploaded no later than 24 hours after site completion.<strong> </strong></p><ul><li>Digital photos are outlined in the current version of the installation guide. ALL photos are required by the Customer.</li><li>Photos need to include a note card or piece of paper that includes the Technician's last name, store # and date. [EX: J. Doe,&nbsp;#4321 06/03/2026]</li><li>Required deliverables include the following:</li></ul><p>- Completed End Client Check In / Out Form [Installation Checklist] with MOD signature</p><p>- Digital Pictures with proper naming conventions as outlined in the Technical Installation Guide</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Direct Source Obligations:&nbsp;</u></strong></p><p>Direct Source will provide all Technicians with their pre-confirmed schedules. All project related documents will be made available on the Direct Source Portal for download.&nbsp;<strong><u>Technician is expected to log on and print out the documents prior to the start of their assignment.</u></strong></p><p><strong>Direct Source Project Related Documents includes:&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>DSI Technical Guide/Project Overview Manual</li><li>Direct Source Contact information, Support Desk numbers and escalation plan</li><li>Ross Installation Manual</li><li>End Client Check In/Out Form</li><li>Itemized Hardware/Material List [Site Packing Slip &ndash; located on the outside of the box in a sealed window]</li><li>End Client Letter of Authorization</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Payment Information:</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>Payment Amounts:</u> </strong> $260.00 per successfully Completed Site. Payment amount is inclusive of labor, any applicable sales or use taxes, and expenses (except flight costs) including but not limited to hotel, meals, and local travel. No other expenses will be reimbursed in excess of the payment amounts listed, unless agreed upon in writing. For purposes of this Work Order, the term \"Completed Site\" shall mean each site where: (i) Technician has completed the Work in accordance with the specifications set forth herein; (ii) all required documentation related to the site has been submitted to DSI within the time frames set forth below.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Time &amp; Material Rate:</u></strong> $65.00 per hour for work that exceeds the total scheduled onsite time, due to no fault of the Technician, will be paid at the hourly T&amp;M rate in 15-minute increments. <strong>T&amp;M will ONLY be paid when the issue was reported immediately and the DSI Support Desk or DSI Project Manager has documented the issue, and an incident number or ticket number has been assigned.</strong></p><p>In the event additional resources are required due to reasons outside the Technician's control, the Technician will notify the DSI Project Manager of the situation in writing, propose a solution and obtain <u>pre-approval</u> for any additional costs for materials, labor or expenses. Verbal agreements with anyone other than the Project Manager will be considered invalid.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Store Revisits:</u></strong> Store revisits will be paid at $65.00 per hour with a 2-hour minimum, if the revisit cause is due to no fault of the Technician.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Same Day Cancellation (SDC) or Same Day Reschedule (SDR):</u></strong></p><p>Any Site that is Cancelled or Rescheduled on the planned installation date due to conditions outside of the Technician's control (Examples include, inventory shortages, customer site readiness or customer late or no arrival). The on-site issue must be escalated immediately to the DSI Support Desk. <strong>The Technician may not leave the End Customer's site without the Direct Source escalation &amp; authorization in order to qualify for payment.</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Any site that is rescheduled due to conditions under the Technician's control; no payment is owed to the Technician. (Examples include, but are not limited to: Technician late arrival, missed pre-site informational meeting/ 'tech orientation' or lack of required tools or materials as specified within this Work Order or the Technical Guide).</p><p><strong><u>Cancellation and Reschedule Fees​:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Any site that is SAME DAY RESCHEDULE; Site was rescheduled after Technician arrived to site but no work was completed due to no fault of Technician - $30 reschedule fee + Contracted Trip Charge</li><li>Any site that is SAME DAY RESCHEDULE; Site was rescheduled in less than 24 hours but prior to Technician arrival - $30 reschedule fee</li><li>Any site that is SAME DAY RESCHEDULE; Technician arrived onsite and was able to complete some work, (example: inventory) but due to no fault of Technician, site was rescheduled - Minimum of 2 hours T&amp;M + Contracted Trip Charge</li><li>Any site that is RESCHEDULE; Site was rescheduled with more than 24 hour notice - Nothing is owed</li><li>Any site that is SAME DAY CANCELLATION; Site that was canceled with less than a 24 hour notice but prior to Technician arrival - $30 cancellation fee</li><li>Any site that is SAME DAY CANCELLATION; Site was cancelled when Technician arrived onsite - $30 cancellation fee + Contracted Trip Charge</li><li>Any site that is CANCELLED; Site that was canceled with at least 24 hour notice - Nothing is owe</li></ul><p><strong><u>SERVICE LEVEL AGREEMENTS:</u></strong><em>&nbsp;All below dates are from the day of the installation date.</em></p><ul><li>1 Business Day: All required deliverables are due to Direct Source Portal - No fee incurred​</li><li>2 Business Days (Late penalties apply at this time): If DSI has not received or has rejected the required deliverables due to failure to meet requirements, DSI will notify the Technician via the Late Deliverable email, indicating what is still outstanding.</li><li>The Technician will have up to the 5th business day to:</li><li>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;- submit the outstanding item(s) or,</li><li>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;- return to the site at the Technician's expense to remedy the outstanding items</li><li><strong>The late penalty will apply at this time - NO EXCEPTIONS unless otherwise stated by the Project Team.</strong> 3<strong>0% per affected site. Invoice Payment for that site(s) may be withheld.</strong></li><li>5 Business Days: In the absence of the Technician remedying the outstanding deliverable item(s), penalties equal to the cost of dispatching a technician to obtain the required deliverables will be applied to the outstanding invoice amount for the effected site(s). - The cost of dispatching a technician to obtain the required deliverables.</li></ul><p>- Late deliverables are defined as any documentation and/or digital photos required per the Installation Guide, and that is not received by the end of the next business day after the scheduled installation date. This also includes deliverables that are incomplete, inaccurate or illegible.</p><p>- Late fee penalties will not be waived unless Technician received written notice from Direct Source Project Manager for each occurrence.</p><p>- DSI reserves the right to re-assign previously awarded sites to another Technician due to the awarded Technician's failure to meet due dates, complete work according to DSI and the End Customer's standards and specifications, or put the site in an \"at-risk\" state without a mutually agreeable corrective action plan. DSI shall have no additional liability to the Technician other than for work completed and accepted.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Expectations &amp; Requirements:</u></strong></p><p>Direct Source and End Customer have a specific Code of Conduct that must be adhered to at all times. Code of Conduct and other requirements are as follows:</p><p><strong><u>Dress Code:</u></strong></p><p><strong>Allowed: </strong> Comfortable clothing such as khakis, jeans, polos, plain T-shirts or collared shirts</p><p><strong>Not Allowed:</strong> Clothing that's ripped, dirty, has holes, or may be considered offensive; shorts, sandals, T-shirts with sayings on them (small clothing manufacturer logos are acceptable).</p><p><strong><u>Presentation:</u></strong></p><p>Technicians are expected to present themselves in a professional fashion. If Direct Source receives reports or feels there is a need for concern over a Technician's behavior that could jeopardize our relationship with the End Customer or create a safety concern, Direct Source reserves the right to cancel Technician from the project. Specific examples include, but are not limited to: damage or loss to equipment or property, theft of equipment or property, suspected use of alcohol or drugs, smelling of alcohol or drugs, theft, offensive language or gestures, or other inappropriate behavior.</p><p><strong><u>Travel Arrangements:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Technician is expected to make and pay for their own travel arrangements such as car rental and hotel.&nbsp;</li><li>Technician MUST be able to rent a car, if required, or have a RELIABLE transportation.</li><li>Technician is responsible for determining their own travel path between sites.</li><li>Technician MUST have a usable major credit card for use throughout this project.</li></ul><p><strong><u>Deductions:</u></strong></p><p>Direct Source will deduct the current retail value of equipment or property that is not returned (for any reason, including without limitation, as a result of theft) when requested by Direct Source or is damaged. Direct Source may also deduct the value of damage caused during the install or thereafter by the Technician and its contractors. If value of any unreturned or damaged equipment or property exceeds the payment amount due under this Agreement, Direct Source will invoice the Technician for the difference, and Technician shall pay such invoiced amount within 15 days of receipt of such notice.</p>","markdown":"**Call the End Client Command Center along with the Direct Source Support Desk prior to leaving each site to complete a check out procedure and to record unique DSI checkout code** (voice mail is not an acceptable check out and could result in the Tech nician returning to the site at the Technician's own expense).\n\n**Submittal of pictures and paperwork (\"Deliverables\") due to End Client by emailing the End Client Command Center team BEFORE checking out with them.**\n\n**Submittal of pictures and paperwork (\"Deliverables\") due to DSI by uploading to the DSI Mobile App BEFORE leaving site** (or within 24 hours of site completion if there are issues uploading from site).\n\n**Scope of Services**: This is a complex project with detailed tasks to be performed by DSI, Technician and the End Customer, as documented in the Technical Guide or in a signed Change Authorization.\n\nAn overview of the services to be performed by the Technician include, but are not limited to:\n\n**Check In using the DSI Mobile App or contact the Direct Source Support Desk upon arrival at each site.**\n\nCheck in with MOD and confirm hardware and work location. May need to show a form of ID along with your Customer Letter of Authorization form.\n\nCheck in with the End Client Command Center by calling into their Support Bridge.\n\n**Required Deliverables:** Obtain **\"BEFORE\"** **images of all Registers or Cash Wrap areas PRIOR to starting** **any work.**\n\nUpload photos as necessary deliverables via the DSI Mobile App.\n\nEmail all required photos to the End Client Command Center throughout the installation.\n\n**Pre-Installation inventory** of new hardware at the store location.\n\n- **Required Deliverables: Take a required deliverable photo of the packing slip.**\n- Record inventory counts or any issues on the End Client Command Center Check In / Out Form.\n\nInspect existing devices for condition and power status. Document any device(s) not working properly and have MOD signoff on the End Client Check In / Out Form.\n\nBegin installing the new Verifone m450s, cables, and adapter plates – Can work on only TWO LANES at a time to begin with.\n\n- You will stage each new pin pad by disconnecting the old pin pad cable, install the new pin pad cable and connect to the register. .\n- **Security Screws**: Each M450 has a security screw in a brown piece of paper in the box. This must be installed to secure the plastic cover over the pin pad connection.\n- **P-Clips**: Each pin pad cable **must be routed down and behind each pin pad** and secured with the supplied P-Clip.\n- **Verify Mounting Bracket orientation**: When passing the pin pad cable through the top mounting bracket, make sure it is facing the right way to flip down and onto the pin pad.\n- **Notify the End Client Support Team upon completion of each register** – Ross will perform the required software updates and then the MOD can test each lane.\n\nProceed with replacing the remaining Pin Pads and update the End Client Command Center after each new device is booted up so they can complete the updates.\n\n- Do not power down a register as that may cause delays.\n\nNeatly manage the new pin pad cable in the same manner the original cable was found. Use Velcro to secure it.\n\nMOD to validate pin pads are functional.\n\n- The MOD can test each lane once End Client verifies updates are done. They do not need to wait until the end of the install.\n\n**Hardware Return**: Package old hardware and cables in the new hardware boxes and ready for return shipment. Leave with MOD when done.\n\n- **Ensure the correct return labels are placed on each box**.\n- Place the **old cables & anti-skimmer plates** inside the smaller box – RETURN TO UNPLUGGED C/O \"Burg Electronic Recovery\" for Disposal.\n- Place the **old MX915 pin pads** inside the master pack box using bubble wrap – RETURN to LEVEL10 (End Client's Depot Stock) for break/fix.\n\nClean up all work areas and throw away extra boxes and packing materials in designated location.\n\nComplete the Check In / Out form and obtain MOD signature.\n\nSign off on the MOD Validation Form and obtain MOD signature.\n\nThe technician will provide End Client project team pictures via email distribution of installed pin pads to validate correct installation/placement before checkout.\n\n- **Required Deliverables:** Obtain **\"AFTER\"** **images of all Registers (one photo per lane) and the hardware return with tracking numbers clearly visible.**\n- Email all final deliverables including the 2 checklists / sign off forms to the End Client Command Center.\n\nCheck out with the End Client Command Center Support Team.\n\n**Check out with Direct Source/End Customer Support Desk prior to leaving each site to complete a check out procedure** (voice mail is not an acceptable checkout and could result in the Technician returning to the site at the Technician's own expense).\n\nTechnician will provide quality checks on all completed work to ensure that all work has been completed and is free from any defects.\n\nSubmittal of pictures and paperwork (\"Deliverables\") due while onsite or else within 24 hours of site completion to the Direct Source Portal (for installations on multiple dates – submit daily deliverables).\n\n**Technician Required Equipment, Tools & Hardware:**\n\nStandard Technician Tool kit (multi-size screwdrivers, cordless drill & various bits, hammer, etc.)\n\nCell phone with fully charged battery, charger, and ongoing active account with your carrier\n\n**Phone charger required** - will need to be on the phone majority of the install with ROSS Support\n\nPrinted copy of the End Client Check In and Out Form \\[Installation Checklist\\] and the Technical Installation Guide – **Included in Shipment**.\n\n\\# 1 Philips screwdriver\n\n\\# 2 Philips screwdriver\n\nT8 Torx Bit – Screwdriver or Allen Key type\n\nStep drill bit (Unibit) - to enlarge the mounting hole or make hole in counter, if required\n\nPacking tape\n\nVelcro (for cable management)\n\nElectrical tape\n\nHeadlamp or small portable light (suggested) - the store lights dim after closing, so extra light should be helpful\n\nEar buds or headset (suggested) - can be hands-free when working and still talk to the End Client Command Center as needed\n\n**Project Preparation/ Orientation:**\n\n**The Technician who will be onsite**, must complete a mandatory conference call orientation session prior to the start of their assigned installation(s) unless other arrangements are mutually agreed upon. During that session, the Technician will learn Direct Source's and End Customer's expectations, processes, deliverable requirements, project scope as well as lessons learned from previous installations. **Direct Source will provide a detailed Installation Service Guide (Technical Guide) on the Direct Source Portal, which must be reviewed prior to project orientation, and must be brought with to each installation.**\n\n**Deliverables & Reporting**: Deliverables are defined as any documentation and/or digital photos required per the Technical Guide. All Deliverables must be uploaded to the Direct Source Portal or via the DSI Mobile App (preferred).\n\n**Deliverables must be EMAILED TO End Client BEFORE CHECKOUT and then uploaded to DSI via Mobile App or Web Portal BEFORE leaving site for the project team to review the next morning.** If there are any issues doing so, photos must be uploaded no later than 24 hours after site completion.\n\n- Digital photos are outlined in the current version of the installation guide. ALL photos are required by the Customer.\n- Photos need to include a note card or piece of paper that includes the Technician's last name, store # and date. \\[EX: J. Doe, #4321 06/03/2026\\]\n- Required deliverables include the following:\n\n\\- Completed End Client Check In / Out Form \\[Installation Checklist\\] with MOD signature\n\n\\- Digital Pictures with proper naming conventions as outlined in the Technical Installation Guide\n\n**Direct Source Obligations:**\n\nDirect Source will provide all Technicians with their pre-confirmed schedules. All project related documents will be made available on the Direct Source Portal for download. **Technician is expected to log on and print out the documents prior to the start of their assignment.**\n\n**Direct Source Project Related Documents includes:**\n\n- DSI Technical Guide/Project Overview Manual\n- Direct Source Contact information, Support Desk numbers and escalation plan\n- Ross Installation Manual\n- End Client Check In/Out Form\n- Itemized Hardware/Material List \\[Site Packing Slip – located on the outside of the box in a sealed window\\]\n- End Client Letter of Authorization\n\n**Payment Information:**\n\n**Payment Amounts:**  $260.00 per successfully Completed Site. Payment amount is inclusive of labor, any applicable sales or use taxes, and expenses (except flight costs) including but not limited to hotel, meals, and local travel. No other expenses will be reimbursed in excess of the payment amounts listed, unless agreed upon in writing. For purposes of this Work Order, the term \"Completed Site\" shall mean each site where: (i) Technician has completed the Work in accordance with the specifications set forth herein; (ii) all required documentation related to the site has been submitted to DSI within the time frames set forth below.\n\n**Time & Material Rate:** $65.00 per hour for work that exceeds the total scheduled onsite time, due to no fault of the Technician, will be paid at the hourly T&M rate in 15-minute increments. **T&M will ONLY be paid when the issue was reported immediately and the DSI Support Desk or DSI Project Manager has documented the issue, and an incident number or ticket number has been assigned.**\n\nIn the event additional resources are required due to reasons outside the Technician's control, the Technician will notify the DSI Project Manager of the situation in writing, propose a solution and obtain pre-approval for any additional costs for materials, labor or expenses. Verbal agreements with anyone other than the Project Manager will be considered invalid.\n\n**Store Revisits:** Store revisits will be paid at $65.00 per hour with a 2-hour minimum, if the revisit cause is due to no fault of the Technician.\n\n**Same Day Cancellation (SDC) or Same Day Reschedule (SDR):**\n\nAny Site that is Cancelled or Rescheduled on the planned installation date due to conditions outside of the Technician's control (Examples include, inventory shortages, customer site readiness or customer late or no arrival). The on-site issue must be escalated immediately to the DSI Support Desk. **The Technician may not leave the End Customer's site without the Direct Source escalation & authorization in order to qualify for payment.**\n\nAny site that is rescheduled due to conditions under the Technician's control; no payment is owed to the Technician. (Examples include, but are not limited to: Technician late arrival, missed pre-site informational meeting/ 'tech orientation' or lack of required tools or materials as specified within this Work Order or the Technical Guide).\n\n**Cancellation and Reschedule Fees​:**\n\n- Any site that is SAME DAY RESCHEDULE; Site was rescheduled after Technician arrived to site but no work was completed due to no fault of Technician - $30 reschedule fee + Contracted Trip Charge\n- Any site that is SAME DAY RESCHEDULE; Site was rescheduled in less than 24 hours but prior to Technician arrival - $30 reschedule fee\n- Any site that is SAME DAY RESCHEDULE; Technician arrived onsite and was able to complete some work, (example: inventory) but due to no fault of Technician, site was rescheduled - Minimum of 2 hours T&M + Contracted Trip Charge\n- Any site that is RESCHEDULE; Site was rescheduled with more than 24 hour notice - Nothing is owed\n- Any site that is SAME DAY CANCELLATION; Site that was canceled with less than a 24 hour notice but prior to Technician arrival - $30 cancellation fee\n- Any site that is SAME DAY CANCELLATION; Site was cancelled when Technician arrived onsite - $30 cancellation fee + Contracted Trip Charge\n- Any site that is CANCELLED; Site that was canceled with at least 24 hour notice - Nothing is owe\n\n**SERVICE LEVEL AGREEMENTS:** *All below dates are from the day of the installation date.*\n\n- 1 Business Day: All required deliverables are due to Direct Source Portal - No fee incurred​\n- 2 Business Days (Late penalties apply at this time): If DSI has not received or has rejected the required deliverables due to failure to meet requirements, DSI will notify the Technician via the Late Deliverable email, indicating what is still outstanding.\n- The Technician will have up to the 5th business day to:\n- - submit the outstanding item(s) or,\n- - return to the site at the Technician's expense to remedy the outstanding items\n- **The late penalty will apply at this time - NO EXCEPTIONS unless otherwise stated by the Project Team.** 3**0% per affected site. Invoice Payment for that site(s) may be withheld.**\n- 5 Business Days: In the absence of the Technician remedying the outstanding deliverable item(s), penalties equal to the cost of dispatching a technician to obtain the required deliverables will be applied to the outstanding invoice amount for the effected site(s). - The cost of dispatching a technician to obtain the required deliverables.\n\n\\- Late deliverables are defined as any documentation and/or digital photos required per the Installation Guide, and that is not received by the end of the next business day after the scheduled installation date. This also includes deliverables that are incomplete, inaccurate or illegible.\n\n\\- Late fee penalties will not be waived unless Technician received written notice from Direct Source Project Manager for each occurrence.\n\n\\- DSI reserves the right to re-assign previously awarded sites to another Technician due to the awarded Technician's failure to meet due dates, complete work according to DSI and the End Customer's standards and specifications, or put the site in an \"at-risk\" state without a mutually agreeable corrective action plan. DSI shall have no additional liability to the Technician other than for work completed and accepted.\n\n**Expectations & Requirements:**\n\nDirect Source and End Customer have a specific Code of Conduct that must be adhered to at all times. Code of Conduct and other requirements are as follows:\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n**Allowed:**  Comfortable clothing such as khakis, jeans, polos, plain T-shirts or collared shirts\n\n**Not Allowed:** Clothing that's ripped, dirty, has holes, or may be considered offensive; shorts, sandals, T-shirts with sayings on them (small clothing manufacturer logos are acceptable).\n\n**Presentation:**\n\nTechnicians are expected to present themselves in a professional fashion. If Direct Source receives reports or feels there is a need for concern over a Technician's behavior that could jeopardize our relationship with the End Customer or create a safety concern, Direct Source reserves the right to cancel Technician from the project. Specific examples include, but are not limited to: damage or loss to equipment or property, theft of equipment or property, suspected use of alcohol or drugs, smelling of alcohol or drugs, theft, offensive language or gestures, or other inappropriate behavior.\n\n**Travel Arrangements:**\n\n- Technician is expected to make and pay for their own travel arrangements such as car rental and hotel.\n- Technician MUST be able to rent a car, if required, or have a RELIABLE transportation.\n- Technician is responsible for determining their own travel path between sites.\n- Technician MUST have a usable major credit card for use throughout this project.\n\n**Deductions:**\n\nDirect Source will deduct the current retail value of equipment or property that is not returned (for any reason, including without limitation, as a result of theft) when requested by Direct Source or is damaged. Direct Source may also deduct the value of damage caused during the install or thereafter by the Technician and its contractors. If value of any unreturned or damaged equipment or property exceeds the payment amount due under this Agreement, Direct Source will invoice the Technician for the difference, and Technician shall pay such invoiced amount within 15 days of receipt of such notice.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-06T21:45","end":"2026-10-06T25:45"},"payRange":{"min":260,"max":260},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":15},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $260 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-06T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ​Concord Police Department - NC ( Phase 2 ) (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-22T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"Remote Hands - Connect AT&T broadband circuit"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789765889409}
{"job":{"id":19975654,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Direct Source","title":"Pin Pad Installation","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Call the End Client Command Center along with the Direct Source Support Desk prior to leaving each site to complete a check out procedure and to record unique DSI checkout code </strong>(voice mail is not an acceptable check out and could result in the Tech nician returning to the site at the Technician's own expense).</p><p><strong>Submittal of pictures and paperwork (\"Deliverables\") due to End Client by emailing the End Client Command Center team BEFORE checking out with them.</strong></p><p><strong>Submittal of pictures and paperwork (\"Deliverables\") due to DSI by uploading to the DSI Mobile App BEFORE leaving site</strong> (or within 24 hours of site completion if there are issues uploading from site).</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Services</u></strong>: This is a complex project with detailed tasks to be performed by DSI, Technician and the End Customer, as documented in the Technical Guide or in a signed Change Authorization.</p><p>An overview of the services to be performed by the Technician include, but are not limited to:</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Check In using the DSI Mobile App or contact the Direct Source Support Desk upon arrival at each site.</strong></p><p>Check in with MOD and confirm hardware and work location. May need to show a form of ID along with your Customer Letter of Authorization form.</p><p>Check in with the End Client Command Center by calling into their Support Bridge.</p><p><strong><u>Required Deliverables</u>: </strong>Obtain <strong>\"BEFORE\"</strong> <strong>images of all Registers or Cash Wrap areas PRIOR to starting</strong> <strong>any work.</strong></p><p>Upload photos as necessary deliverables via the DSI Mobile App.</p><p>Email all required photos to the End Client Command Center throughout the installation.</p><p><strong>Pre-Installation inventory</strong> of new hardware at the store location.</p><ul><li><strong><u>Required Deliverables</u>: Take a required deliverable photo of the packing slip.</strong></li><li>Record inventory counts or any issues on the End Client Command Center Check In / Out Form.</li></ul><p>Inspect existing devices for condition and power status. Document any device(s) not working properly and have MOD signoff on the End Client Check In / Out Form.</p><p>Begin installing the new Verifone m450s, cables, and adapter plates &ndash; Can work on only TWO LANES at a time to begin with.</p><ul><li>You will stage each new pin pad by disconnecting the old pin pad cable, install the new pin pad cable and connect to the register. .</li><li><strong>Security Screws</strong>: Each M450 has a security screw in a brown piece of paper in the box. This must be installed to secure the plastic cover over the pin pad connection.</li><li><strong>P-Clips</strong>: Each pin pad cable <strong>must be routed down and behind each pin pad</strong> and secured with the supplied P-Clip.</li><li><strong>Verify Mounting Bracket orientation</strong>: When passing the pin pad cable through the top mounting bracket, make sure it is facing the right way to flip down and onto the pin pad.</li><li><strong>Notify the End Client Support Team upon completion of each register </strong>&ndash; Ross will perform the required software updates and then the MOD can test each lane.</li></ul><p>Proceed with replacing the remaining Pin Pads and update the End Client Command Center after each new device is booted up so they can complete the updates.</p><ul><li>Do not power down a register as that may cause delays.</li></ul><p>Neatly manage the new pin pad cable in the same manner the original cable was found. Use Velcro to secure it.</p><p>MOD to validate pin pads are functional.</p><ul><li>The MOD can test each lane once End Client verifies updates are done. They do not need to wait until the end of the install.</li></ul><p><strong>Hardware Return</strong>: Package old hardware and cables in the new hardware boxes and ready for return shipment. Leave with MOD when done.</p><ul><li><strong>Ensure the correct return labels are placed on each box</strong>.</li><li>Place the <strong>old cables &amp; anti-skimmer plates</strong> inside the smaller box &ndash; RETURN TO UNPLUGGED C/O \"Burg Electronic Recovery\" for Disposal.</li><li>Place the <strong>old MX915 pin pads</strong> inside the master pack box using bubble wrap &ndash; RETURN to LEVEL10 (End Client's Depot Stock) for break/fix.</li></ul><p>Clean up all work areas and throw away extra boxes and packing materials in designated location.</p><p>Complete the Check In / Out form and obtain MOD signature.</p><p>Sign off on the MOD Validation Form and obtain MOD signature.</p><p>The technician will provide End Client project team pictures via email distribution of installed pin pads to validate correct installation/placement before checkout.</p><ul><li><strong><u>Required Deliverables</u>: </strong>Obtain <strong>\"AFTER\"</strong> <strong>images of all Registers (one photo per lane) and the hardware return with tracking numbers clearly visible. </strong></li><li>Email all final deliverables including the 2 checklists / sign off forms to the End Client Command Center.</li></ul><p>Check out with the End Client Command Center Support Team.</p><p><strong>Check out with Direct Source/End Customer Support Desk prior to leaving each site to complete a check out procedure</strong> (voice mail is not an acceptable checkout and could result in the Technician returning to the site at the Technician's own expense).</p><p>Technician will provide quality checks on all completed work to ensure that all work has been completed and is free from any defects.</p><p>Submittal of pictures and paperwork (\"Deliverables\") due while onsite or else within 24 hours of site completion to the Direct Source Portal (for installations on multiple dates &ndash; submit daily deliverables).</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Technician Required Equipment, Tools &amp; Hardware:</u></strong></p><p>Standard&nbsp;Technician Tool kit (multi-size screwdrivers, cordless drill &amp; various bits, hammer, etc.)</p><p>Cell phone with fully charged battery, charger, and ongoing active account with your carrier</p><p><strong>Phone charger required</strong> -&nbsp;will need to be on the phone majority of the install with ROSS Support</p><p>Printed copy of the End Client Check In and Out Form [Installation Checklist] and the Technical Installation Guide &ndash;&nbsp;<strong>Included in Shipment</strong>.</p><p># 1&nbsp;Philips screwdriver</p><p># 2 Philips screwdriver</p><p>T8 Torx Bit &ndash; Screwdriver or Allen Key type</p><p>Step drill bit (Unibit) - to enlarge the mounting hole or make hole in counter, if required</p><p>Packing tape</p><p>Velcro (for cable management)</p><p>Electrical tape</p><p>Headlamp or small portable light (suggested) - the store lights dim after closing, so extra light should be helpful</p><p>Ear buds or headset (suggested) - can be hands-free when working and still talk to the End Client Command Center as needed</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Project Preparation/ Orientation:</u></strong></p><p><strong>The Technician who will be onsite</strong>, must complete a mandatory conference call orientation session prior to the start of their assigned installation(s) unless other arrangements are mutually agreed upon. During that session, the Technician will learn Direct Source's and End Customer's expectations, processes, deliverable requirements, project scope as well as lessons learned from previous installations. <strong>Direct Source will provide a detailed Installation Service Guide (Technical Guide) on the Direct Source Portal, which must be reviewed prior to project orientation, and must be brought with to each installation.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Deliverables &amp; Reporting</u></strong>: Deliverables are defined as any documentation and/or digital photos required per the Technical Guide. All Deliverables must be uploaded to the Direct Source Portal or via the DSI Mobile App (preferred).</p><p><strong>Deliverables must be EMAILED TO End Client BEFORE CHECKOUT and then uploaded to DSI via Mobile App or Web Portal BEFORE leaving site for the project team to review the next morning. </strong>If there are any issues doing so, photos must be uploaded no later than 24 hours after site completion.<strong> </strong></p><ul><li>Digital photos are outlined in the current version of the installation guide. ALL photos are required by the Customer.</li><li>Photos need to include a note card or piece of paper that includes the Technician's last name, store # and date. [EX: J. Doe,&nbsp;#4321 06/03/2026]</li><li>Required deliverables include the following:</li></ul><p>- Completed End Client Check In / Out Form [Installation Checklist] with MOD signature</p><p>- Digital Pictures with proper naming conventions as outlined in the Technical Installation Guide</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Direct Source Obligations:&nbsp;</u></strong></p><p>Direct Source will provide all Technicians with their pre-confirmed schedules. All project related documents will be made available on the Direct Source Portal for download.&nbsp;<strong><u>Technician is expected to log on and print out the documents prior to the start of their assignment.</u></strong></p><p><strong>Direct Source Project Related Documents includes:&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>DSI Technical Guide/Project Overview Manual</li><li>Direct Source Contact information, Support Desk numbers and escalation plan</li><li>Ross Installation Manual</li><li>End Client Check In/Out Form</li><li>Itemized Hardware/Material List [Site Packing Slip &ndash; located on the outside of the box in a sealed window]</li><li>End Client Letter of Authorization</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Payment Information:</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>Payment Amounts:</u> </strong> $260.00 per successfully Completed Site. Payment amount is inclusive of labor, any applicable sales or use taxes, and expenses (except flight costs) including but not limited to hotel, meals, and local travel. No other expenses will be reimbursed in excess of the payment amounts listed, unless agreed upon in writing. For purposes of this Work Order, the term \"Completed Site\" shall mean each site where: (i) Technician has completed the Work in accordance with the specifications set forth herein; (ii) all required documentation related to the site has been submitted to DSI within the time frames set forth below.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Time &amp; Material Rate:</u></strong> $65.00 per hour for work that exceeds the total scheduled onsite time, due to no fault of the Technician, will be paid at the hourly T&amp;M rate in 15-minute increments. <strong>T&amp;M will ONLY be paid when the issue was reported immediately and the DSI Support Desk or DSI Project Manager has documented the issue, and an incident number or ticket number has been assigned.</strong></p><p>In the event additional resources are required due to reasons outside the Technician's control, the Technician will notify the DSI Project Manager of the situation in writing, propose a solution and obtain <u>pre-approval</u> for any additional costs for materials, labor or expenses. Verbal agreements with anyone other than the Project Manager will be considered invalid.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Store Revisits:</u></strong> Store revisits will be paid at $65.00 per hour with a 2-hour minimum, if the revisit cause is due to no fault of the Technician.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Same Day Cancellation (SDC) or Same Day Reschedule (SDR):</u></strong></p><p>Any Site that is Cancelled or Rescheduled on the planned installation date due to conditions outside of the Technician's control (Examples include, inventory shortages, customer site readiness or customer late or no arrival). The on-site issue must be escalated immediately to the DSI Support Desk. <strong>The Technician may not leave the End Customer's site without the Direct Source escalation &amp; authorization in order to qualify for payment.</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>Any site that is rescheduled due to conditions under the Technician's control; no payment is owed to the Technician. (Examples include, but are not limited to: Technician late arrival, missed pre-site informational meeting/ 'tech orientation' or lack of required tools or materials as specified within this Work Order or the Technical Guide).</p><p><strong><u>Cancellation and Reschedule Fees​:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Any site that is SAME DAY RESCHEDULE; Site was rescheduled after Technician arrived to site but no work was completed due to no fault of Technician - $30 reschedule fee + Contracted Trip Charge</li><li>Any site that is SAME DAY RESCHEDULE; Site was rescheduled in less than 24 hours but prior to Technician arrival - $30 reschedule fee</li><li>Any site that is SAME DAY RESCHEDULE; Technician arrived onsite and was able to complete some work, (example: inventory) but due to no fault of Technician, site was rescheduled - Minimum of 2 hours T&amp;M + Contracted Trip Charge</li><li>Any site that is RESCHEDULE; Site was rescheduled with more than 24 hour notice - Nothing is owed</li><li>Any site that is SAME DAY CANCELLATION; Site that was canceled with less than a 24 hour notice but prior to Technician arrival - $30 cancellation fee</li><li>Any site that is SAME DAY CANCELLATION; Site was cancelled when Technician arrived onsite - $30 cancellation fee + Contracted Trip Charge</li><li>Any site that is CANCELLED; Site that was canceled with at least 24 hour notice - Nothing is owe</li></ul><p><strong><u>SERVICE LEVEL AGREEMENTS:</u></strong><em>&nbsp;All below dates are from the day of the installation date.</em></p><ul><li>1 Business Day: All required deliverables are due to Direct Source Portal - No fee incurred​</li><li>2 Business Days (Late penalties apply at this time): If DSI has not received or has rejected the required deliverables due to failure to meet requirements, DSI will notify the Technician via the Late Deliverable email, indicating what is still outstanding.</li><li>The Technician will have up to the 5th business day to:</li><li>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;- submit the outstanding item(s) or,</li><li>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;- return to the site at the Technician's expense to remedy the outstanding items</li><li><strong>The late penalty will apply at this time - NO EXCEPTIONS unless otherwise stated by the Project Team.</strong> 3<strong>0% per affected site. Invoice Payment for that site(s) may be withheld.</strong></li><li>5 Business Days: In the absence of the Technician remedying the outstanding deliverable item(s), penalties equal to the cost of dispatching a technician to obtain the required deliverables will be applied to the outstanding invoice amount for the effected site(s). - The cost of dispatching a technician to obtain the required deliverables.</li></ul><p>- Late deliverables are defined as any documentation and/or digital photos required per the Installation Guide, and that is not received by the end of the next business day after the scheduled installation date. This also includes deliverables that are incomplete, inaccurate or illegible.</p><p>- Late fee penalties will not be waived unless Technician received written notice from Direct Source Project Manager for each occurrence.</p><p>- DSI reserves the right to re-assign previously awarded sites to another Technician due to the awarded Technician's failure to meet due dates, complete work according to DSI and the End Customer's standards and specifications, or put the site in an \"at-risk\" state without a mutually agreeable corrective action plan. DSI shall have no additional liability to the Technician other than for work completed and accepted.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Expectations &amp; Requirements:</u></strong></p><p>Direct Source and End Customer have a specific Code of Conduct that must be adhered to at all times. Code of Conduct and other requirements are as follows:</p><p><strong><u>Dress Code:</u></strong></p><p><strong>Allowed: </strong> Comfortable clothing such as khakis, jeans, polos, plain T-shirts or collared shirts</p><p><strong>Not Allowed:</strong> Clothing that's ripped, dirty, has holes, or may be considered offensive; shorts, sandals, T-shirts with sayings on them (small clothing manufacturer logos are acceptable).</p><p><strong><u>Presentation:</u></strong></p><p>Technicians are expected to present themselves in a professional fashion. If Direct Source receives reports or feels there is a need for concern over a Technician's behavior that could jeopardize our relationship with the End Customer or create a safety concern, Direct Source reserves the right to cancel Technician from the project. Specific examples include, but are not limited to: damage or loss to equipment or property, theft of equipment or property, suspected use of alcohol or drugs, smelling of alcohol or drugs, theft, offensive language or gestures, or other inappropriate behavior.</p><p><strong><u>Travel Arrangements:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Technician is expected to make and pay for their own travel arrangements such as car rental and hotel.&nbsp;</li><li>Technician MUST be able to rent a car, if required, or have a RELIABLE transportation.</li><li>Technician is responsible for determining their own travel path between sites.</li><li>Technician MUST have a usable major credit card for use throughout this project.</li></ul><p><strong><u>Deductions:</u></strong></p><p>Direct Source will deduct the current retail value of equipment or property that is not returned (for any reason, including without limitation, as a result of theft) when requested by Direct Source or is damaged. Direct Source may also deduct the value of damage caused during the install or thereafter by the Technician and its contractors. If value of any unreturned or damaged equipment or property exceeds the payment amount due under this Agreement, Direct Source will invoice the Technician for the difference, and Technician shall pay such invoiced amount within 15 days of receipt of such notice.</p>","markdown":"**Call the End Client Command Center along with the Direct Source Support Desk prior to leaving each site to complete a check out procedure and to record unique DSI checkout code** (voice mail is not an acceptable check out and could result in the Tech nician returning to the site at the Technician's own expense).\n\n**Submittal of pictures and paperwork (\"Deliverables\") due to End Client by emailing the End Client Command Center team BEFORE checking out with them.**\n\n**Submittal of pictures and paperwork (\"Deliverables\") due to DSI by uploading to the DSI Mobile App BEFORE leaving site** (or within 24 hours of site completion if there are issues uploading from site).\n\n**Scope of Services**: This is a complex project with detailed tasks to be performed by DSI, Technician and the End Customer, as documented in the Technical Guide or in a signed Change Authorization.\n\nAn overview of the services to be performed by the Technician include, but are not limited to:\n\n**Check In using the DSI Mobile App or contact the Direct Source Support Desk upon arrival at each site.**\n\nCheck in with MOD and confirm hardware and work location. May need to show a form of ID along with your Customer Letter of Authorization form.\n\nCheck in with the End Client Command Center by calling into their Support Bridge.\n\n**Required Deliverables:** Obtain **\"BEFORE\"** **images of all Registers or Cash Wrap areas PRIOR to starting** **any work.**\n\nUpload photos as necessary deliverables via the DSI Mobile App.\n\nEmail all required photos to the End Client Command Center throughout the installation.\n\n**Pre-Installation inventory** of new hardware at the store location.\n\n- **Required Deliverables: Take a required deliverable photo of the packing slip.**\n- Record inventory counts or any issues on the End Client Command Center Check In / Out Form.\n\nInspect existing devices for condition and power status. Document any device(s) not working properly and have MOD signoff on the End Client Check In / Out Form.\n\nBegin installing the new Verifone m450s, cables, and adapter plates – Can work on only TWO LANES at a time to begin with.\n\n- You will stage each new pin pad by disconnecting the old pin pad cable, install the new pin pad cable and connect to the register. .\n- **Security Screws**: Each M450 has a security screw in a brown piece of paper in the box. This must be installed to secure the plastic cover over the pin pad connection.\n- **P-Clips**: Each pin pad cable **must be routed down and behind each pin pad** and secured with the supplied P-Clip.\n- **Verify Mounting Bracket orientation**: When passing the pin pad cable through the top mounting bracket, make sure it is facing the right way to flip down and onto the pin pad.\n- **Notify the End Client Support Team upon completion of each register** – Ross will perform the required software updates and then the MOD can test each lane.\n\nProceed with replacing the remaining Pin Pads and update the End Client Command Center after each new device is booted up so they can complete the updates.\n\n- Do not power down a register as that may cause delays.\n\nNeatly manage the new pin pad cable in the same manner the original cable was found. Use Velcro to secure it.\n\nMOD to validate pin pads are functional.\n\n- The MOD can test each lane once End Client verifies updates are done. They do not need to wait until the end of the install.\n\n**Hardware Return**: Package old hardware and cables in the new hardware boxes and ready for return shipment. Leave with MOD when done.\n\n- **Ensure the correct return labels are placed on each box**.\n- Place the **old cables & anti-skimmer plates** inside the smaller box – RETURN TO UNPLUGGED C/O \"Burg Electronic Recovery\" for Disposal.\n- Place the **old MX915 pin pads** inside the master pack box using bubble wrap – RETURN to LEVEL10 (End Client's Depot Stock) for break/fix.\n\nClean up all work areas and throw away extra boxes and packing materials in designated location.\n\nComplete the Check In / Out form and obtain MOD signature.\n\nSign off on the MOD Validation Form and obtain MOD signature.\n\nThe technician will provide End Client project team pictures via email distribution of installed pin pads to validate correct installation/placement before checkout.\n\n- **Required Deliverables:** Obtain **\"AFTER\"** **images of all Registers (one photo per lane) and the hardware return with tracking numbers clearly visible.**\n- Email all final deliverables including the 2 checklists / sign off forms to the End Client Command Center.\n\nCheck out with the End Client Command Center Support Team.\n\n**Check out with Direct Source/End Customer Support Desk prior to leaving each site to complete a check out procedure** (voice mail is not an acceptable checkout and could result in the Technician returning to the site at the Technician's own expense).\n\nTechnician will provide quality checks on all completed work to ensure that all work has been completed and is free from any defects.\n\nSubmittal of pictures and paperwork (\"Deliverables\") due while onsite or else within 24 hours of site completion to the Direct Source Portal (for installations on multiple dates – submit daily deliverables).\n\n**Technician Required Equipment, Tools & Hardware:**\n\nStandard Technician Tool kit (multi-size screwdrivers, cordless drill & various bits, hammer, etc.)\n\nCell phone with fully charged battery, charger, and ongoing active account with your carrier\n\n**Phone charger required** - will need to be on the phone majority of the install with ROSS Support\n\nPrinted copy of the End Client Check In and Out Form \\[Installation Checklist\\] and the Technical Installation Guide – **Included in Shipment**.\n\n\\# 1 Philips screwdriver\n\n\\# 2 Philips screwdriver\n\nT8 Torx Bit – Screwdriver or Allen Key type\n\nStep drill bit (Unibit) - to enlarge the mounting hole or make hole in counter, if required\n\nPacking tape\n\nVelcro (for cable management)\n\nElectrical tape\n\nHeadlamp or small portable light (suggested) - the store lights dim after closing, so extra light should be helpful\n\nEar buds or headset (suggested) - can be hands-free when working and still talk to the End Client Command Center as needed\n\n**Project Preparation/ Orientation:**\n\n**The Technician who will be onsite**, must complete a mandatory conference call orientation session prior to the start of their assigned installation(s) unless other arrangements are mutually agreed upon. During that session, the Technician will learn Direct Source's and End Customer's expectations, processes, deliverable requirements, project scope as well as lessons learned from previous installations. **Direct Source will provide a detailed Installation Service Guide (Technical Guide) on the Direct Source Portal, which must be reviewed prior to project orientation, and must be brought with to each installation.**\n\n**Deliverables & Reporting**: Deliverables are defined as any documentation and/or digital photos required per the Technical Guide. All Deliverables must be uploaded to the Direct Source Portal or via the DSI Mobile App (preferred).\n\n**Deliverables must be EMAILED TO End Client BEFORE CHECKOUT and then uploaded to DSI via Mobile App or Web Portal BEFORE leaving site for the project team to review the next morning.** If there are any issues doing so, photos must be uploaded no later than 24 hours after site completion.\n\n- Digital photos are outlined in the current version of the installation guide. ALL photos are required by the Customer.\n- Photos need to include a note card or piece of paper that includes the Technician's last name, store # and date. \\[EX: J. Doe, #4321 06/03/2026\\]\n- Required deliverables include the following:\n\n\\- Completed End Client Check In / Out Form \\[Installation Checklist\\] with MOD signature\n\n\\- Digital Pictures with proper naming conventions as outlined in the Technical Installation Guide\n\n**Direct Source Obligations:**\n\nDirect Source will provide all Technicians with their pre-confirmed schedules. All project related documents will be made available on the Direct Source Portal for download. **Technician is expected to log on and print out the documents prior to the start of their assignment.**\n\n**Direct Source Project Related Documents includes:**\n\n- DSI Technical Guide/Project Overview Manual\n- Direct Source Contact information, Support Desk numbers and escalation plan\n- Ross Installation Manual\n- End Client Check In/Out Form\n- Itemized Hardware/Material List \\[Site Packing Slip – located on the outside of the box in a sealed window\\]\n- End Client Letter of Authorization\n\n**Payment Information:**\n\n**Payment Amounts:**  $260.00 per successfully Completed Site. Payment amount is inclusive of labor, any applicable sales or use taxes, and expenses (except flight costs) including but not limited to hotel, meals, and local travel. No other expenses will be reimbursed in excess of the payment amounts listed, unless agreed upon in writing. For purposes of this Work Order, the term \"Completed Site\" shall mean each site where: (i) Technician has completed the Work in accordance with the specifications set forth herein; (ii) all required documentation related to the site has been submitted to DSI within the time frames set forth below.\n\n**Time & Material Rate:** $65.00 per hour for work that exceeds the total scheduled onsite time, due to no fault of the Technician, will be paid at the hourly T&M rate in 15-minute increments. **T&M will ONLY be paid when the issue was reported immediately and the DSI Support Desk or DSI Project Manager has documented the issue, and an incident number or ticket number has been assigned.**\n\nIn the event additional resources are required due to reasons outside the Technician's control, the Technician will notify the DSI Project Manager of the situation in writing, propose a solution and obtain pre-approval for any additional costs for materials, labor or expenses. Verbal agreements with anyone other than the Project Manager will be considered invalid.\n\n**Store Revisits:** Store revisits will be paid at $65.00 per hour with a 2-hour minimum, if the revisit cause is due to no fault of the Technician.\n\n**Same Day Cancellation (SDC) or Same Day Reschedule (SDR):**\n\nAny Site that is Cancelled or Rescheduled on the planned installation date due to conditions outside of the Technician's control (Examples include, inventory shortages, customer site readiness or customer late or no arrival). The on-site issue must be escalated immediately to the DSI Support Desk. **The Technician may not leave the End Customer's site without the Direct Source escalation & authorization in order to qualify for payment.**\n\nAny site that is rescheduled due to conditions under the Technician's control; no payment is owed to the Technician. (Examples include, but are not limited to: Technician late arrival, missed pre-site informational meeting/ 'tech orientation' or lack of required tools or materials as specified within this Work Order or the Technical Guide).\n\n**Cancellation and Reschedule Fees​:**\n\n- Any site that is SAME DAY RESCHEDULE; Site was rescheduled after Technician arrived to site but no work was completed due to no fault of Technician - $30 reschedule fee + Contracted Trip Charge\n- Any site that is SAME DAY RESCHEDULE; Site was rescheduled in less than 24 hours but prior to Technician arrival - $30 reschedule fee\n- Any site that is SAME DAY RESCHEDULE; Technician arrived onsite and was able to complete some work, (example: inventory) but due to no fault of Technician, site was rescheduled - Minimum of 2 hours T&M + Contracted Trip Charge\n- Any site that is RESCHEDULE; Site was rescheduled with more than 24 hour notice - Nothing is owed\n- Any site that is SAME DAY CANCELLATION; Site that was canceled with less than a 24 hour notice but prior to Technician arrival - $30 cancellation fee\n- Any site that is SAME DAY CANCELLATION; Site was cancelled when Technician arrived onsite - $30 cancellation fee + Contracted Trip Charge\n- Any site that is CANCELLED; Site that was canceled with at least 24 hour notice - Nothing is owe\n\n**SERVICE LEVEL AGREEMENTS:** *All below dates are from the day of the installation date.*\n\n- 1 Business Day: All required deliverables are due to Direct Source Portal - No fee incurred​\n- 2 Business Days (Late penalties apply at this time): If DSI has not received or has rejected the required deliverables due to failure to meet requirements, DSI will notify the Technician via the Late Deliverable email, indicating what is still outstanding.\n- The Technician will have up to the 5th business day to:\n- - submit the outstanding item(s) or,\n- - return to the site at the Technician's expense to remedy the outstanding items\n- **The late penalty will apply at this time - NO EXCEPTIONS unless otherwise stated by the Project Team.** 3**0% per affected site. Invoice Payment for that site(s) may be withheld.**\n- 5 Business Days: In the absence of the Technician remedying the outstanding deliverable item(s), penalties equal to the cost of dispatching a technician to obtain the required deliverables will be applied to the outstanding invoice amount for the effected site(s). - The cost of dispatching a technician to obtain the required deliverables.\n\n\\- Late deliverables are defined as any documentation and/or digital photos required per the Installation Guide, and that is not received by the end of the next business day after the scheduled installation date. This also includes deliverables that are incomplete, inaccurate or illegible.\n\n\\- Late fee penalties will not be waived unless Technician received written notice from Direct Source Project Manager for each occurrence.\n\n\\- DSI reserves the right to re-assign previously awarded sites to another Technician due to the awarded Technician's failure to meet due dates, complete work according to DSI and the End Customer's standards and specifications, or put the site in an \"at-risk\" state without a mutually agreeable corrective action plan. DSI shall have no additional liability to the Technician other than for work completed and accepted.\n\n**Expectations & Requirements:**\n\nDirect Source and End Customer have a specific Code of Conduct that must be adhered to at all times. Code of Conduct and other requirements are as follows:\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n**Allowed:**  Comfortable clothing such as khakis, jeans, polos, plain T-shirts or collared shirts\n\n**Not Allowed:** Clothing that's ripped, dirty, has holes, or may be considered offensive; shorts, sandals, T-shirts with sayings on them (small clothing manufacturer logos are acceptable).\n\n**Presentation:**\n\nTechnicians are expected to present themselves in a professional fashion. If Direct Source receives reports or feels there is a need for concern over a Technician's behavior that could jeopardize our relationship with the End Customer or create a safety concern, Direct Source reserves the right to cancel Technician from the project. Specific examples include, but are not limited to: damage or loss to equipment or property, theft of equipment or property, suspected use of alcohol or drugs, smelling of alcohol or drugs, theft, offensive language or gestures, or other inappropriate behavior.\n\n**Travel Arrangements:**\n\n- Technician is expected to make and pay for their own travel arrangements such as car rental and hotel.\n- Technician MUST be able to rent a car, if required, or have a RELIABLE transportation.\n- Technician is responsible for determining their own travel path between sites.\n- Technician MUST have a usable major credit card for use throughout this project.\n\n**Deductions:**\n\nDirect Source will deduct the current retail value of equipment or property that is not returned (for any reason, including without limitation, as a result of theft) when requested by Direct Source or is damaged. Direct Source may also deduct the value of damage caused during the install or thereafter by the Technician and its contractors. If value of any unreturned or damaged equipment or property exceeds the payment amount due under this Agreement, Direct Source will invoice the Technician for the difference, and Technician shall pay such invoiced amount within 15 days of receipt of such notice.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-07T20:45","end":"2026-10-07T24:45"},"payRange":{"min":260,"max":260},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":52},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $260 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-07T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ​Concord Police Department - NC ( Phase 2 ) (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-22T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"Remote Hands - Connect AT&T broadband circuit"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789766273159}
{"job":{"id":19989047,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Argus IT Services","title":"Smart H&F for Troubleshooting Network Devices - Wifi Slow","description":{"html":"<strong>HCL Onsite Network Support – Technician Field Guide</strong><strong>Purpose of Visit</strong><p>This ticket is to <strong>troubleshoot a network or store device</strong> on behalf of <strong>HCL</strong> in response to a reported <strong>Incident</strong>.</p><p><br></p><strong>Teams is required and must remain active for the full duration of the visit. If your time is different than what you were actively working with the NOC team on the bridge, your WO will be marked incomplete.</strong><br><strong><u>Travel expenses must be in your counter and accepted prior to you arriving at the store. Any travel tacked on afterwards, will be denied. All materials will be reimbursed on the WO.</u></strong><br><strong>1. Arrival &amp; Store Check-In</strong><ul><li>Present <strong>valid Photo ID</strong> (Driver’s License).</li><li>Identify yourself as an <strong>HCL Network Technician</strong>, dispatched <strong>on behalf of the NOC Team</strong> to troubleshoot a network device reported offline.</li><li>If denied access:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Notify the NOC team immediately on the bridge</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Contact the <strong>WO Manager</strong> for escalation</li></ul><strong>2. Onsite Procedures</strong><ul><li><strong>Join the Teams bridge</strong> using the link, ID, and passcode from the Confidential section</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>If it is saying the link doesn't exist/is valid, you need to uninstall/reinstall Teams. The link is valid and working.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Send an email to ADUSA_FSCC@hcltech.com with your Incident if you have issues with joining the bridge.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If that doesn't work, please try using browser and incognito mode and type in the meeting ID and password.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Stay connected for the entire visit</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Please tell them when you get there and when you leave, as well as what the next action is needed.</li><li>In the meeting chat, enter:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>INC#</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>Arrival time</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Departure time</strong></li><li><strong><u>Do not leave the site unless released by the NOC team</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>The NOC team on the bridge will you send you to a second bridge. If you have been on that second bridge for a while with no one from the NOC team joining, rejoin the primary bridge and let them know.</u></strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>They will create a secondary room for your specific ticket/issue. You will work with the team for your specific issue. Please join back the main bridge once you are finished to check out.</u></strong></p><p><strong>﻿</strong></p><strong>3. Post-Service Actions</strong><ul><li>Document all work performed in the <strong>FieldNation closing notes</strong></li><li>Notify <strong>Argus</strong> of the resolution prior to departure</li><li>Return any unused parts using the provided <strong>return label</strong> (if applicable)</li></ul><strong>4. Required Tools &amp; Equipment</strong><ul><li>Smartphone with hotspot</li><li>Laptop with admin access, Teams, Putty, and email</li><li>Console cables (USB to RJ45)</li><li>Cable Tester / Toner</li><li>Wi-Fi analyzer app</li><li>IT hardware repair kit</li><li>Patch cables, crimpers, cable testers</li><li>Spare RJ-45 connectors (<strong>MUST BE CAT6)</strong></li><li>Spare Ethernet cables (various lengths)</li><li>General hand tools and accessories</li></ul><p><strong>5. Ticket notes from client:</strong></p><p>\"Required 19ft. lift</p><p>Need to align tech Mon-Fri, after 8 PM EST.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Dispatch Notes:</p><p><br></p><p>1. Which piece of equipment it is: Wireless devices.</p><p><br></p><p>2. Where it is: Food Lion - 1573 Raleigh</p><p><br></p><p>3. What its DNS is: N/A</p><p><br></p><p>4. What the problem is: Handheld devices experience connectivity issues near the back of Aisle 6 and the back-middle area of the store.</p><p><br></p><p>5. What troubleshooting has been completed: Verified the network configuration on the wireless controller. All the APs are up and working. Wireless users are seen connecting without any issue. Handheld devices experience connectivity issues near the back of Aisle 6 and the back-middle area of the store</p><p><br></p><p>6. What do they need from a field tech and any parts/tools that may be needed: Need to check the wireless connectivity, as the devices are affected in the store. Assist in bringing them up on the wireless network and test the issue.</p><p><br></p><p>7. The steps expected for the technician to perform while onsite: Initiate a call with Wireless team, assist in checking the wireless connectivity of the affected devices in the store. Need to assist in checking the signal strength in the area where the customers are facing issue.\"</p><p><strong><u>If you need a schedule change/want to request the work order - REQUEST A SCHEDULE CHANGE. We can troubleshoot as long as the store is open. Whatever time you get there, we will adjust on the WO so it doesn't impact your rating.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>The phone number on the Work Order is for on-site escalations and emergencies. Calling the number repeatedly everyday for future work consideration, will result in not using you as a technician for future engagements.</u></strong></p>","markdown":"**HCL Onsite Network Support – Technician Field Guide****Purpose of Visit**This ticket is to **troubleshoot a network or store device** on behalf of **HCL** in response to a reported **Incident**.\n\n**Teams is required and must remain active for the full duration of the visit. If your time is different than what you were actively working with the NOC team on the bridge, your WO will be marked incomplete.**  \n**Travel expenses must be in your counter and accepted prior to you arriving at the store. Any travel tacked on afterwards, will be denied. All materials will be reimbursed on the WO.**  \n**1. Arrival & Store Check-In**- Present **valid Photo ID** (Driver’s License).\n- Identify yourself as an **HCL Network Technician**, dispatched **on behalf of the NOC Team** to troubleshoot a network device reported offline.\n- If denied access:\n- **Notify the NOC team immediately on the bridge**\n- Contact the **WO Manager** for escalation\n\n**2. Onsite Procedures**- **Join the Teams bridge** using the link, ID, and passcode from the Confidential section\n- **If it is saying the link doesn't exist/is valid, you need to uninstall/reinstall Teams. The link is valid and working.**\n- **Send an email to ADUSA\\_FSCC@hcltech.com with your Incident if you have issues with joining the bridge.**\n- If that doesn't work, please try using browser and incognito mode and type in the meeting ID and password.\n- Stay connected for the entire visit\n- Please tell them when you get there and when you leave, as well as what the next action is needed.\n- In the meeting chat, enter:\n- **INC#**\n- **Arrival time**\n- **Departure time**\n- **Do not leave the site unless released by the NOC team**\n- **The NOC team on the bridge will you send you to a second bridge. If you have been on that second bridge for a while with no one from the NOC team joining, rejoin the primary bridge and let them know.**\n\n**They will create a secondary room for your specific ticket/issue. You will work with the team for your specific issue. Please join back the main bridge once you are finished to check out.**\n\n**﻿**\n\n**3. Post-Service Actions**- Document all work performed in the **FieldNation closing notes**\n- Notify **Argus** of the resolution prior to departure\n- Return any unused parts using the provided **return label** (if applicable)\n\n**4. Required Tools & Equipment**- Smartphone with hotspot\n- Laptop with admin access, Teams, Putty, and email\n- Console cables (USB to RJ45)\n- Cable Tester / Toner\n- Wi-Fi analyzer app\n- IT hardware repair kit\n- Patch cables, crimpers, cable testers\n- Spare RJ-45 connectors (**MUST BE CAT6)**\n- Spare Ethernet cables (various lengths)\n- General hand tools and accessories\n\n**5. Ticket notes from client:**\n\n\"Required 19ft. lift\n\nNeed to align tech Mon-Fri, after 8 PM EST.\n\nDispatch Notes:\n\n1\\. Which piece of equipment it is: Wireless devices.\n\n2\\. Where it is: Food Lion - 1573 Raleigh\n\n3\\. What its DNS is: N/A\n\n4\\. What the problem is: Handheld devices experience connectivity issues near the back of Aisle 6 and the back-middle area of the store.\n\n5\\. What troubleshooting has been completed: Verified the network configuration on the wireless controller. All the APs are up and working. Wireless users are seen connecting without any issue. Handheld devices experience connectivity issues near the back of Aisle 6 and the back-middle area of the store\n\n6\\. What do they need from a field tech and any parts/tools that may be needed: Need to check the wireless connectivity, as the devices are affected in the store. Assist in bringing them up on the wireless network and test the issue.\n\n7\\. The steps expected for the technician to perform while onsite: Initiate a call with Wireless team, assist in checking the wireless connectivity of the affected devices in the store. Need to assist in checking the signal strength in the area where the customers are facing issue.\"\n\n**If you need a schedule change/want to request the work order - REQUEST A SCHEDULE CHANGE. We can troubleshoot as long as the store is open. Whatever time you get there, we will adjust on the WO so it doesn't impact your rating.**\n\n**The phone number on the Work Order is for on-site escalations and emergencies. Calling the number repeatedly everyday for future work consideration, will result in not using you as a technician for future engagements.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-22T20:00","end":"2026-09-22T24:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":220},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":7},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $220 (countered: $240) is below minimum threshold $400"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789766833792}
{"job":{"id":19968120,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Envysion","title":"Replace and Seal (1) IP camera","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Overview:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Seeking a technician with experience in replacing IP cameras.</li>\n<li>Tech is required to replace&nbsp;<strong>(</strong>Front door - Port 18<strong>)</strong>&nbsp;camera.</li>\n<li>Troubleshoot any offline camera equipment.</li>\n<li>Clean any dirty cameras.</li>\n<li><strong><u>Tech needs to call to check in with the Envysion Helpdesk at (877) 258-9441&nbsp;Opt. 8</u></strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Tools Required:&nbsp;</strong><em>must haves</em></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>8' - 15'</strong> Ladder: Tech will need to have both A frame and extension</li>\n<li>IP cable tester</li>\n<li>Toner</li>\n<li>Drill / screw driver with anything needed to troubleshoot the camera</li>\n<li>Crimping tool/ crimpers</li>\n<li>RJ45 connectors (Can be expenses if used)</li>\n<li>Spot monitor</li>\n<li>Recommending tech have PPE for dust and debris.&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p>\n<p><strong><em>Pre-Site Requirements</em></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Please do not schedule your visit on weekends and during meal rushes. Envysion Support Center hours are 6:00 AM - 8:00 PM Mountain Time week days and 8am-4:30pm on weekends.&nbsp;</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If you go on the weekend without permission, you may have to return if the issue is not resolved, and you will not get a return bonus</li>\n<li>Call the site to introduce yourself and let them know you are on your way.&nbsp;</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Phone numbers are listed on Google Maps</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If there is an issue with the time window please let us know by messaging the work order manager or calling the support number for emergency. Envysion Support (877) 258-9441 Option 8</li>\n<li>Check tracking if provided. If not then the replacement is on site already. If you go to the site and don't check the tracking then you will not receive the return bonus.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong><em>On-Site Tasks</em></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong><u>Tech needs to call to check in with the Envysion Helpdesk at (877) 258-9441&nbsp;&nbsp;Option 8</u></strong></li>\n<li>Introduce yourself to the manager on duty and explain you are with Envysion Support, here to work on the CCTV system</li>\n<li>Replace the camera(s). <strong>Equipment must be replaced even if the current equipment is working.</strong></li>\n<li>The technician should be prepared to both troubleshoot and re-terminate RJ45, test the cable to the camera with a the cable tester, and test the video output by using a spot monitor or by switching to a known good port.</li>\n<li>Please take pictures of cable test and/or spot monitor image if the camera is not working&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Before calling support please make sure you go through the PDF guides that are provided for troubleshooting our cameras if the camera is not working.</li>\n<li>If you have been onsite for over an hour and a half, you need to reach out to the helpdesk and update them with the current progress.</li>\n<li>During some visits, rarely, it is possible that additional troubleshooting may be requested for CCTV cameras (This may include re-angling, removing obstructions, or resolving video quality issues) or network connections, please be prepared to encounter this if necessary.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If this is considered out of scope message work order manager for compensation.</li>\n<li>Check out with Envysion support. Envysion Support number (877) 258-9441 #8</li>\n<li><strong>Leave any old equipment with the site.</strong></li>\n<li>If a return visit is needed please do the return within 24 hours</li>\n<li>If checking out with support please be patient as sometimes there is a big volume of calls. Voicemail will not be considered as your check out</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong><em>Required On-Site Deliverables</em></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Upload any pictures that were taken as well upload any picture of expenses if needed.</li>\n<li>Check-out of work order via Field Nation and add any notes.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Dress code and behavior policy</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Remember to be respectful of site employees and Envysion support</strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Do not approach site employees if there is no need to, please reach out to the manager on duty only</strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>If there are any issues please find a manager or call Envysion support</strong></li>\n<li>Dress <strong>appropriately</strong> for work being done on site</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Escalation Process:</strong></p>\n<p>Contact Work Order Manager via direct message for non-work related issues such as: ETA adjustments, needing to do a return trip, questions regarding pay</p>\n<ul>\n<li>If immediate assistance is needed call the support line (877) 258-9441&nbsp;Opt. 8</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Expenses</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Payment for additional expenses for equipment, such as Fuses, BNC connectors, RJ45 connectors, patch cables, and silicone caulk will be paid only if a receipt is submitted in the Field Nation App and approved by the Work Order Manager.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Additional hours</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">This is a fixed rate work order to complete the scope of work listed in the service description. There is no hourly rate if the tech goes past the times that we have estimated for completion. Any additional work completed or extenuating circumstances will be taken into consideration and adjustment may be made at the work order managers discretion. The only exception to this is if a counter offer was accepted by the work order manager prior to the the work order being assigned.</li>\n<li>Parking and toll road expenses will be paid only if a receipt is submitted in the Field Nation App and will then be approved by the Work Order Manager. Travel pay must be approved by the work order manager before the tech goes to the site.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>If you do not have the required tools you will be asked to go get that item. Please make sure you have all the required items.<strong><u>All bonuses will be forfeit if you do not bring the required equipment.</u></strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If unable to commit to a return visit with the requires tools you will be dismissed without pay</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Waiting on hold for more than 30 minutes</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Your patience is appreciated!</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">The phone could be busy but please call to check out. If you leave the site without a resolution and did not get released by support you will be asked to revisit the site without a bonus.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If on hold with Envysion support for greater than 30 minutes a $10 bonus will be added. To be approved, the phone number you call from will be checked in the Envysion phone system. Please reach out to the Work Order Manager.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">You can message the work order manager to see if they can check your work but not guarantee.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Please do not leave the site while on hold.</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**Overview:**\n\n- Seeking a technician with experience in replacing IP cameras.\n- Tech is required to replace **(**Front door - Port 18**)** camera.\n- Troubleshoot any offline camera equipment.\n- Clean any dirty cameras.\n- **Tech needs to call to check in with the Envysion Helpdesk at (877) 258-9441 Opt. 8**\n\n**Tools Required:** *must haves*\n\n- **8' - 15'** Ladder: Tech will need to have both A frame and extension\n- IP cable tester\n- Toner\n- Drill / screw driver with anything needed to troubleshoot the camera\n- Crimping tool/ crimpers\n- RJ45 connectors (Can be expenses if used)\n- Spot monitor\n- Recommending tech have PPE for dust and debris.\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n***Pre-Site Requirements***\n\n1. Please do not schedule your visit on weekends and during meal rushes. Envysion Support Center hours are 6:00 AM - 8:00 PM Mountain Time week days and 8am-4:30pm on weekends.\n2. If you go on the weekend without permission, you may have to return if the issue is not resolved, and you will not get a return bonus\n3. Call the site to introduce yourself and let them know you are on your way.\n4. Phone numbers are listed on Google Maps\n5. If there is an issue with the time window please let us know by messaging the work order manager or calling the support number for emergency. Envysion Support (877) 258-9441 Option 8\n6. Check tracking if provided. If not then the replacement is on site already. If you go to the site and don't check the tracking then you will not receive the return bonus.\n\n***On-Site Tasks***\n\n1. **Tech needs to call to check in with the Envysion Helpdesk at (877) 258-9441 Option 8**\n2. Introduce yourself to the manager on duty and explain you are with Envysion Support, here to work on the CCTV system\n3. Replace the camera(s). **Equipment must be replaced even if the current equipment is working.**\n4. The technician should be prepared to both troubleshoot and re-terminate RJ45, test the cable to the camera with a the cable tester, and test the video output by using a spot monitor or by switching to a known good port.\n5. Please take pictures of cable test and/or spot monitor image if the camera is not working\n6. Before calling support please make sure you go through the PDF guides that are provided for troubleshooting our cameras if the camera is not working.\n7. If you have been onsite for over an hour and a half, you need to reach out to the helpdesk and update them with the current progress.\n8. During some visits, rarely, it is possible that additional troubleshooting may be requested for CCTV cameras (This may include re-angling, removing obstructions, or resolving video quality issues) or network connections, please be prepared to encounter this if necessary.\n9. If this is considered out of scope message work order manager for compensation.\n10. Check out with Envysion support. Envysion Support number (877) 258-9441 #8\n11. **Leave any old equipment with the site.**\n12. If a return visit is needed please do the return within 24 hours\n13. If checking out with support please be patient as sometimes there is a big volume of calls. Voicemail will not be considered as your check out\n\n***Required On-Site Deliverables***\n\n1. Upload any pictures that were taken as well upload any picture of expenses if needed.\n2. Check-out of work order via Field Nation and add any notes.\n\n**Dress code and behavior policy**\n\n- **Remember to be respectful of site employees and Envysion support**\n- **Do not approach site employees if there is no need to, please reach out to the manager on duty only**\n- **If there are any issues please find a manager or call Envysion support**\n- Dress **appropriately** for work being done on site\n\n**Escalation Process:**\n\nContact Work Order Manager via direct message for non-work related issues such as: ETA adjustments, needing to do a return trip, questions regarding pay\n\n- If immediate assistance is needed call the support line (877) 258-9441 Opt. 8\n\n**Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy**\n\n- Expenses\n- Payment for additional expenses for equipment, such as Fuses, BNC connectors, RJ45 connectors, patch cables, and silicone caulk will be paid only if a receipt is submitted in the Field Nation App and approved by the Work Order Manager.\n- Additional hours\n- This is a fixed rate work order to complete the scope of work listed in the service description. There is no hourly rate if the tech goes past the times that we have estimated for completion. Any additional work completed or extenuating circumstances will be taken into consideration and adjustment may be made at the work order managers discretion. The only exception to this is if a counter offer was accepted by the work order manager prior to the the work order being assigned.\n- Parking and toll road expenses will be paid only if a receipt is submitted in the Field Nation App and will then be approved by the Work Order Manager. Travel pay must be approved by the work order manager before the tech goes to the site.\n- If you do not have the required tools you will be asked to go get that item. Please make sure you have all the required items.**All bonuses will be forfeit if you do not bring the required equipment.**\n- If unable to commit to a return visit with the requires tools you will be dismissed without pay\n\n**Waiting on hold for more than 30 minutes**\n\n- Your patience is appreciated!\n- The phone could be busy but please call to check out. If you leave the site without a resolution and did not get released by support you will be asked to revisit the site without a bonus.\n- If on hold with Envysion support for greater than 30 minutes a $10 bonus will be added. To be approved, the phone number you call from will be checked in the Envysion phone system. Please reach out to the Work Order Manager.\n- You can message the work order manager to see if they can check your work but not guarantee.\n- Please do not leave the site while on hold.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-21T08:00","end":"2026-09-21T10:00","latestStart":"2026-09-21T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":120,"max":120},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":16},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $120 is below minimum threshold $400"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T23:00:00