{"job":{"id":19989450,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"IW Technologies","title":"Premium Brands- Network Equipment Issues","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Summary of Work</strong></p>\n<p>Tech needed to go on site to troubleshoot and repair the following networking issues:</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Description of Issue:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Assist with moving and extending network cables.</li>\n<li>Bring cabling and cabling tools.</li>\n<li>Tech should be prepared to be onsite 2-3 hours.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Tech Notes:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Call the Store Network Support Team at 740-951-5800 upon arrival and departure from the store. Do not perform any work without calling Store Network Support.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Check‑In / Check‑Out Requirement (MANDATORY)</strong></p>\n<p>You <strong>must check in and check out</strong> with<strong>both</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>IW Technologies</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Premium Brands (Store Network Team)</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Do NOT begin work without contacting the help desk.</strong></p>\n<p>Remain courteous and professional when working with all support teams.</p>\n<p><strong>Contact Numbers</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>IW Technologies:</strong> 847‑285‑4198</li>\n<li><strong>Store Network Team:</strong> 740‑951‑5800</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Required Tools (ALL REQUIRED)</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Laptop</li>\n<li>Console Cable</li>\n<li>Cisco Console Cables (Cisco switches/routers &amp; Fortigate)</li>\n<li>110 / 66 Punch Down Tool</li>\n<li>RJ‑45 Crimpers</li>\n<li>Cordless Drill w/ Misc. Bits</li>\n<li>Cable Certifier (Fluke or equivalent)</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">NOT a toner or multimeter</li>\n<li>Cable Toner / Speaker</li>\n<li>Basic Cabling Tool Kit</li>\n<li>150 ft Cat5e Cable + RJ‑45 Termination Ends</li>\n<li>Ladder (10–12 ft)</li>\n<li>P‑Touch Labeler</li>\n<li>Digital Camera or HD‑capable Cell Phone</li>\n<li>Valid ID <strong>matching your Field Nation profile name</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Ensure you have the <strong>correct drivers for Cisco console access</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>Pre‑Visit Instructions</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Review <strong>ALL attached documentation</strong></li>\n<li>Download / print required files before arrival</li>\n<li>Confirm ETA in <strong>Field Nation within 24 hours</strong> of appointment</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Onsite Tasks</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Check in using <strong>Field Nation App</strong></li>\n<li>Call <strong>IW Technologies</strong> to check in</li>\n<li>847‑285‑4198</li>\n<li>Call <strong>Store Network Team</strong></li>\n<li>740‑951‑5800</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Provide their <strong>internal ticket number</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li>Locate onsite contact and introduce yourself as an</li>\n<li><strong>IW Technologies Technician</strong></li>\n<li>Perform required tasks per documentation</li>\n<li>Validate connectivity/functionality with Support</li>\n<li>Clean up work area</li>\n<li>Call <strong>Store Network Team</strong> to confirm resolution or status</li>\n<li>Call <strong>IW Technologies to check out BEFORE leaving site</strong></li>\n<li>847‑285‑4198</li>\n<li>Submit work order for payment</li>\n</ol>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Approval within <strong>24 hours</strong>if no issues</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Special Instructions for Technician</strong></p>\n<p>(Insert any case‑specific notes here)</p>","markdown":"**Summary of Work**\n\nTech needed to go on site to troubleshoot and repair the following networking issues:\n\n**Description of Issue:**\n\n- Assist with moving and extending network cables.\n- Bring cabling and cabling tools.\n- Tech should be prepared to be onsite 2-3 hours.\n\n**Tech Notes:**\n\n- Call the Store Network Support Team at 740-951-5800 upon arrival and departure from the store. Do not perform any work without calling Store Network Support.\n\n**Check‑In / Check‑Out Requirement (MANDATORY)**\n\nYou **must check in and check out** with**both**:\n\n- **IW Technologies**\n- **Premium Brands (Store Network Team)**\n\n**Do NOT begin work without contacting the help desk.**\n\nRemain courteous and professional when working with all support teams.\n\n**Contact Numbers**\n\n- **IW Technologies:** 847‑285‑4198\n- **Store Network Team:** 740‑951‑5800\n\n**Required Tools (ALL REQUIRED)**\n\n- Laptop\n- Console Cable\n- Cisco Console Cables (Cisco switches/routers & Fortigate)\n- 110 / 66 Punch Down Tool\n- RJ‑45 Crimpers\n- Cordless Drill w/ Misc. Bits\n- Cable Certifier (Fluke or equivalent)\n- NOT a toner or multimeter\n- Cable Toner / Speaker\n- Basic Cabling Tool Kit\n- 150 ft Cat5e Cable + RJ‑45 Termination Ends\n- Ladder (10–12 ft)\n- P‑Touch Labeler\n- Digital Camera or HD‑capable Cell Phone\n- Valid ID **matching your Field Nation profile name**\n\nEnsure you have the **correct drivers for Cisco console access**.\n\n**Pre‑Visit Instructions**\n\n- Review **ALL attached documentation**\n- Download / print required files before arrival\n- Confirm ETA in **Field Nation within 24 hours** of appointment\n\n**Onsite Tasks**\n\n1. Check in using **Field Nation App**\n2. Call **IW Technologies** to check in\n3. 847‑285‑4198\n4. Call **Store Network Team**\n5. 740‑951‑5800\n\n- Provide their **internal ticket number**\n\n1. Locate onsite contact and introduce yourself as an\n2. **IW Technologies Technician**\n3. Perform required tasks per documentation\n4. Validate connectivity/functionality with Support\n5. Clean up work area\n6. Call **Store Network Team** to confirm resolution or status\n7. Call **IW Technologies to check out BEFORE leaving site**\n8. 847‑285‑4198\n9. Submit work order for payment\n\n- Approval within **24 hours**if no issues\n\n**Special Instructions for Technician**\n\n(Insert any case‑specific notes here)","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-19T15:00","end":"2026-09-19T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":90,"max":130},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":90},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":40}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":35},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $130 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789771520269}
{"job":{"id":"4507438215","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"05623631-TJM1057-EPIK Single Visit Install","description":"DESCRIPTION: SOW - EPIK Single Visit Install<br>***********************************************************************<br>Before Arrival<br>1.Call the LCON 30 minutes before arrival.<br>2.Review the EPIK install video if you are unfamiliar with EPIK:<br>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n7ZkeVrRRCo<br>3.Arrive with all required tools and materials listed below.<br>On Arrival<br>1.Check in on WorkMarket.<br>2.Locate the customer contact and confirm the install location.<br>3.Review the Special Instructions before starting work.<br>EPIK Install Requirements<br>1.Mount the Epik device in the approve install location and EPIK 66 block or connect harmonica to RJ 21X on Epik.<br>2.If EPIK device mounting location is not in a cool, clean, secure area reach out to Activation for an updated location. <br>3.Power on the EPIK device before starting the Wizard.<br>Do not log into the Wizard until the device is powered on.<br>4.If applicable connect the EPIK device to the customer network using the information provided in the Special Instructions.<br>5.Log into the EPIK Install Wizard:<br>https://wizard.epik.io<br>6.Follow the Wizard steps and complete the installation with the assigned Activations Representative. A member of the Activations team will reach out by text once assigned.<br>DO NOT CALL INTO THE QUEUE FOR WIZARD RELATED ISSUES<br>7.If not already stated in the TNs to be wired section of your ticket, confirm with site contact if there are fire alarm, security alarm, elevator or e911 lines on site. If so, notify activations of any port configuration changes that need to be made and complete testing with the fire, security or elevator monitoring companies.<br>8.For any lines that cannot be found, complete test calls on the number and notify activations of what end device, person or monitoring service answers the call. If it is ring no answer, run a new line to a biscuit jack and label it with the new Epik number.<br>9.If any of the TNs are voice or fax lines, confirm with the site contact if they need to keep the same numbers. If so, run a line to a biscuit jack and confirm dial tone at the jack. We will complete a revisit to complete the cross connection once the port order is ready.<br>Checkout Requirement<br>1. Provide a cut sheet to activations noting the old telephone number with the new number provided by Epik for each line.<br>2.Confirm Activations has released you.<br>3.Submit all WorkMarket deliverables.<br>4.Enter the checkout code in WorkMarket.<br>5.Check out on WorkMarket.<br><br>The install is not considered valid unless the checkout code is entered in WorkMarket.<br><br>Required Deliverables<br>Submit all required deliverables in WorkMarket before checkout:<br>1.Photo of completed EPIK install.<br>2.Photo of labeled 66 block / harmonica block.<br>3.List of existing TNs and the new number that replaced each TN, if applicable.<br>4.Customer signed sign-out sheet.<br>5.Any additional deliverables listed in Special Instructions.<br><br><br>Required Tools<br>•Laptop<br>•Smartphone with hotspot<br>•Tone generator and wand<br>•66/110 punch tool<br>•Butt set<br>•       Infrared Temperature Gun <br>•Electrician scissors<br>•Step ladder<br>•Flashlight/headlamp<br>•RJ11/RJ45 crimper<br>•Ethernet cable tester<br>•Impact drill / cordless drill<br>•Masonry bits<br>•Screwdrivers / driver bits<br>•Needle-nose pliers<br>•Label maker and label tape<br>•Cat3 or better cable<br>•Cat6 Ethernet cable<br>•Cross-connect wire<br>•Gel-crimp connectors<br>•Cable ties and mounting hardware<br>•RJ11/RJ45 plugs and keystone jacks<br>•Console cables: USB to DB9 PL2303 and USB to USB-mini<br>************************************************************************","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-02T07:00","end":"2026-10-02T10:00"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":195},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":13.2},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"hourly","counterRate":65,"baseAmount":195,"estHours":3,"travelExpense":30,"payStructure":null,"counterDate":{"start":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T18:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":60,"mode":"hours","reason":"arrival_window"}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-06T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ​Concord Police Department - NC ( Phase 2 ) (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-22T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"Remote Hands - Connect AT&T broadband circuit"},{"start":"2026-09-18T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-18T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Experienced L3 network tech needed to work with Maintech FE to swap out (2) Cisco 3850 switches with (2) new Cisco C9300 switches"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"}],"action":"COUNTER","ts":1789771876361}
{"job":{"id":19989770,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"GT Global Services","title":"Tech to troubleshoot network Issue| Remote support provided","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Overview:</strong></p><ul><li>Seeking a technician with experience in Satellite Euqipment, dish tv, Smart box, CMTS, Coax cabling</li><li>Estimated duration will be 3hours, additional hours will be approved</li></ul><p><strong>Dress Code:</strong></p><ul><li>Business Casual</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Technician's Scope of Work:</strong></p><p>Property Name: InTown Suites Extended Stay Raleigh NC(YRN)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Address:&nbsp;3215 Capital Blvd Raleigh, NC 27604-3337</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Site ID: C00743/YRN</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>POC: Jonathan Dill</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>POC’s phone and Email:&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(150, 96, 125);\">919-645-4700</span>&nbsp;|&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(150, 96, 125);\">Jonathan.Dill@intownsuites.com</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Case Number: CS0419385</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">The property is currently experiencing a network outage. A technician is required to trace and troubleshoot the network connections, verify the status of the equipment, and, if necessary, connect a laptop via console to the switches to restore connectivity.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Technician's Scope of Work:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">NOTE: Take pictures of before and after of your work per each rooms and upload it to WO and send it to&nbsp;</span><span style=\"color: rgb(150, 96, 125);\">support@worldvue.com</span>.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>1. Reach out to support at&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(150, 96, 125);\">419-879-3156</span>&nbsp;and provide case #CS0419385</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>2. Coordinate with the property POC to gain access to the equipment room. Work alongside the Advanced Support agent to bring the network online.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>3. Once equipment are all up and running, collaborate with the site POC to test the WiFi throughout the whole property</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>4. Verify that WiFi service is functioning properly.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>5. Address and resolve any additional issues that may arise.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Tools/Parts needed:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>- Networking tools kit</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Console cables</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>- CAT6 cable white</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>- Cable tester</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>- RJ45s</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>- Windows Laptop with WI-FI and LAN connectivity</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>- Ladder<strong><em>Required On-Site Deliverables</em></strong></p><ol><li>Pictures</li></ol><p><strong>Communication Directory:</strong></p><ul><li>If clarification is needed on work order, discuss with WO manager&nbsp;</li><li>Any issues or questions should be escalated to WO manager</li></ul><p><strong>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy</strong></p><ul><li>Any additional hours and expenses must be pre approved by WO manager</li><li>Any additional hours and expenses incurring without pre approval will be denied</li></ul>","markdown":"**Overview:**\n\n- Seeking a technician with experience in Satellite Euqipment, dish tv, Smart box, CMTS, Coax cabling\n- Estimated duration will be 3hours, additional hours will be approved\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n- Business Casual\n\n**Technician's Scope of Work:**\n\nProperty Name: InTown Suites Extended Stay Raleigh NC(YRN)\n\nAddress: 3215 Capital Blvd Raleigh, NC 27604-3337\n\nSite ID: C00743/YRN\n\nPOC: Jonathan Dill\n\nPOC’s phone and Email: 919-645-4700 | Jonathan.Dill@intownsuites.com\n\nCase Number: CS0419385\n\nThe property is currently experiencing a network outage. A technician is required to trace and troubleshoot the network connections, verify the status of the equipment, and, if necessary, connect a laptop via console to the switches to restore connectivity.\n\nTechnician's Scope of Work:\n\nNOTE: Take pictures of before and after of your work per each rooms and upload it to WO and send it to support@worldvue.com.\n\n1\\. Reach out to support at 419-879-3156 and provide case #CS0419385\n\n2\\. Coordinate with the property POC to gain access to the equipment room. Work alongside the Advanced Support agent to bring the network online.\n\n3\\. Once equipment are all up and running, collaborate with the site POC to test the WiFi throughout the whole property\n\n4\\. Verify that WiFi service is functioning properly.\n\n5\\. Address and resolve any additional issues that may arise.\n\nTools/Parts needed:\n\n\\- Networking tools kit\n\nConsole cables\n\n\\- CAT6 cable white\n\n\\- Cable tester\n\n\\- RJ45s\n\n\\- Windows Laptop with WI-FI and LAN connectivity\n\n\\- Ladder***Required On-Site Deliverables***\n\n1. Pictures\n\n**Communication Directory:**\n\n- If clarification is needed on work order, discuss with WO manager\n- Any issues or questions should be escalated to WO manager\n\n**Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy**\n\n- Any additional hours and expenses must be pre approved by WO manager\n- Any additional hours and expenses incurring without pre approval will be denied","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-19T10:00","end":"2026-09-19T12:00","latestStart":"2026-09-19T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":250,"max":375},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":250},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":125}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":9},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"📅 Requested schedule unavailable; a later date was considered.\nAlternative: Sep 23, 12:00 PM (Eastern)\n💸 Alternative-date minimum: $400 · listed maximum: $375\nRejected: pay does not meet the