ort the items and quantity needing replacement or addition.</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\"> 5</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\">Video and Audio Cables</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\"> </strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Inspect video and audio cables to ensure they are securely connected, without blemishes or </span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">scrapes on the cables. Also visually check that resolution on both (dual) monitors match.</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\"> </strong><em style=\"color: black;\">Video cables are culprit if the visual resolutions don't match.</em></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\"> 6</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\">Wi-Fi (Staff, Student, &amp; Guest)</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\"> </strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Check availability and accessibility of all 3 wi-fi networks on campus.</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\"> </strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Use your cellphone or laptop to connect to Guest wi-fi to sure it is functional. Ask staff if Staff and </span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">Student wi-fis are functional as well.</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\"> 7</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\">Firestick &amp; TV</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\"> </strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Reboot firestick and tv - unplug the firestick from tv and power for 2 minutes and plug it back to reboot. </span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">Troubleshoot firesticks that have problems.</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\"> </strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Cable management for TVs is required.</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\"> 8</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\">Desktop Printer</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\"> </strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Make sure printer is functional. Check for physical blemishes and/or missing parts.</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\"> picture of Printer config page</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\"> 9</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\">Photocopier</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\"> </strong><span style=\"color: black;\">Make sure copier is functional - able to print, scan, and scan-to-email. Check for physical blemishes and/or missing parts.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">picture of config page</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: black;\">10 </strong></p><p><span style=\"color: black;\">Check ALL staff workstations and make sure monitors are securely connected to docking stations and cabling adequately managed to avoid interference with staff work.</span></p><ul><li><strong>After accepting the work order there is no further negotiation regarding travel.&nbsp;All travel expenses must be negotiated and approved before accepting work order.&nbsp;This does not include tolls or parking.&nbsp;Those will be reimbursed with an uploaded receipt.</strong></li></ul>","markdown":"MUST call Abed once you arrive for directions 202.731.8588 - he will let you know what he needs\n\nIf you cannot reach Abed please call Chris 571-239-3717\n\nCall Celeste if you cannot get into the campus (214) 470-2626\n\nIf any issues with Networking/WiFi please call Myron 703.561.1672\n\nIf you cannot get InTouch with anyone above, call Wendy 240.527.3693 - do not sit around waiting\n\n**MAKE SURE EVERYTHING WORKS - detail report on any problem item/s**\n\n**MUST Call OR Text Wendy with any issues of time running late - not just enter this into the system**\n\n**MUST bring a laptop with you**\n\n**MUST enter in the notes if there are issues**\n\n**ALL questions are to go Abed or Wendy - staff cannot answer any questions.**\n\n**MUST get approval if going over 2 hours from Wendy - call or text do not enter into notes - you will not be paid if this is not approved**\n\n**MUST send a message saying this was read and you understand what you are doing - if you do not understand call Wendy 240.527.3693 - DO NOT WAIT INTIL YOU GET ONSITE TO SAY YOU DO NOT KNOW WHAT NEEDS TO BE DONE - READ THE SOW**\n\n**Campus Refresh List: Techs must be ready to troubleshoot items when onsite.**\n\n**Only need serial numbers for igels and old monitors**\n\nSOW:\n\n**1**\n\n**Projectors**\n\n Check functionality: Connectivity to classroom/faculty iGel. Ensure audio and video work great.\n\nVideo on the projector screen must fit and not pan from left to right or up and down.\n\n Open a new browser on the iGel and go YouTube.com. Use a YouTube video for audio and video test.\n\nAudio control knob is usually located on the wall by faculty desk in the classrooms\n\n **2**\n\n**Swap iGels with Dell Thin Client (Staff, faculty, Student)**\n\n **Swap iGels with Thin Clients, you will need to put the monitor together and swap the PCs. Go through installation with Abed, he MUST walk you through the process. Record serial number of iGel and add to notes. Remove Old Monitors and iGels and these can be recycled**\n\n **3**\n\n**Network Equipment Closet**\n\n Visually check Cisco Switches, Router, and Firewall for functionality. Check and record APC battery operating percentage.\n\n *(Report low percentage levels to the network team)*\n\nDocument and report all old/excess unusable IT equipment stored in the\n\nNetwork closet to IT to coordinate removal.\n\n**4**\n\n**Docks, Keyboards, Mice, Monitors**\n\n Inspect docking stations, keyboards, mice, and monitors for defects, blemishes, or physical damages.\n\nCable management is very essential - use Velcro ties for cable management,\n\n Techs must list/report the items and quantity needing replacement or addition.\n\n **5**\n\n**Video and Audio Cables**\n\n Inspect video and audio cables to ensure they are securely connected, without blemishes or\n\nscrapes on the cables. Also visually check that resolution on both (dual) monitors match.\n\n *Video cables are culprit if the visual resolutions don't match.*\n\n **6**\n\n**Wi-Fi (Staff, Student, & Guest)**\n\n Check availability and accessibility of all 3 wi-fi networks on campus.\n\n Use your cellphone or laptop to connect to Guest wi-fi to sure it is functional. Ask staff if Staff and\n\nStudent wi-fis are functional as well.\n\n **7**\n\n**Firestick & TV**\n\n Reboot firestick and tv - unplug the firestick from tv and power for 2 minutes and plug it back to reboot.\n\nTroubleshoot firesticks that have problems.\n\n Cable management for TVs is required.\n\n **8**\n\n**Desktop Printer**\n\n Make sure printer is functional. Check for physical blemishes and/or missing parts.\n\n **picture of Printer config page**\n\n **9**\n\n**Photocopier**\n\n Make sure copier is functional - able to print, scan, and scan-to-email. Check for physical blemishes and/or missing parts.\n\npicture of config page\n\n**10**\n\nCheck ALL staff workstations and make sure monitors are securely connected to docking stations and cabling adequately managed to avoid interference with staff work.\n\n- **After accepting the work order there is no further negotiation regarding travel. All travel expenses must be negotiated and approved before accepting work order. This does not include tolls or parking. Those will be reimbursed with an uploaded receipt.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00","end":"2026-09-23T17:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":240},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":60,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":9},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $240 (countered: $240) is below minimum threshold $400"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-23T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00: