{"job":{"id":19989907,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"InTech Together","title":"Dental Office Onboarding For Site Survey Discovery & RMM Installation","description":{"html":"<p><strong><em><u>Work Order Onboarding &amp; Discovery Assessment</u></em></strong></p><p><strong>Overview:</strong></p><p><strong><em><u>We are seeking an experienced IT field technician to perform an onsite IT onboarding assessment for a dental office that is either newly opened or preparing to open.</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em><u>The primary purpose of this visit is to:</u></em></strong></p><ol><li>Install our remote monitoring and management (RMM) tools on all applicable computers and servers.</li><li>Perform a complete IT infrastructure discovery and documentation process.</li><li>Collect equipment inventory, serial numbers, network information, and site photos/videos to support the upcoming onboarding.</li></ol><p>This visit is expected to take approximately 3 hours, though completion time may vary based on office size and equipment count.</p><p>The technician will work directly with the office's designated Point of Contact (POC) and must maintain professional communication throughout the engagement.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Required Skills</strong></p><ul><li>Network Equipment Identification</li><li>Windows Operating Systems</li><li>Basic Server Identification</li><li>Documentation &amp; Asset Inventory</li><li>Professional Customer Communication</li></ul><p><strong>Dress Code</strong></p><ul><li>Business Casual (Polo Preferred)</li><li>No smoking or vaping before or while onsite. (To avoid smelling like smoke)</li><li>Professional appearance and hygiene required</li></ul><p>Failure to maintain professional conduct may result in removal from the work orders engagement and non-payment.</p><p><strong>Required Tools</strong>Must Have</p><ul><li>Laptop</li><li>Smartphone capable of taking photos and videos</li><li>Phillips and Flathead Screwdrivers</li><li>USB Flash Drive (32GB+ recommended)</li></ul><p><strong><em><u>Scope of Work</u></em></strong></p><p><strong>Phase 1 – Site Check-In:</strong></p><ol><li>Contact the assigned <strong>Work Order Manager</strong> upon arrival. (will be listed within the \"<strong>Confidential information </strong>section)</li></ol><p><br></p><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Do not begin work until the work order manager has been contacted and updated on your arrival.</li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li>Meet the<strong> Office Manager </strong>once inside the office<strong> </strong>who will serve as the Point of Contact (POC) in the office for helping gather/confirm equipment locations and completing phases 2 and 3.</li><li>Request a brief walkthrough of the facility to identify all rooms and equipment locations.</li></ol><p><strong>Phase 2 – Practice Information Collection:</strong></p><ol><li>Practice Management Software: (Work with the office POC to gather)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Examples:(Open Dental, Eaglesoft, Dentrix)</li><li>Imaging Software</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Examples:( Dexis, Acteon AIS, Carestream, Vatech)</li><li>Determine Data Storage Information:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Where patient data is stored</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Server location</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Cloud services used</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Imaging storage location</li></ol><p><strong>Phase 3 – Device Inventory:</strong></p><p><strong><em><u>Visit every room and identify all technology (Can also knock out \"Phase 4\" at the same time)</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><em><u>Record (For each workstation:)</u></em></strong></p><ul><li>Room Name</li><li>Computer Name</li><li>Manufacturer</li><li>Model</li><li>Windows OS Version</li><li>Serial Number</li></ul><p>Examples of room names:</p><ul><li>Front Desk</li><li>Consult 1</li><li>Consult 2</li><li>Operatory 1</li><li>Operatory 2</li><li>Doctor Office</li><li>Lab</li><li>Imaging Room</li><li>Break Room</li></ul><p>Take a photo of each workstation and asset tag if available.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Phase 4 – RMM Deployment (Highest Priority):</strong>Install RMM Agent On: (<strong>This phase is the most important portion of the visit and MUST be completed before leaving the site</strong>)</p><ul><li>All workstations</li><li>Front desk computers</li><li>Doctor computers</li><li>Treatment room computers</li><li>Imaging computers</li><li>Servers</li><li>Any additional business-critical systems</li></ul><p>Required Information for each device to be gathered and documented within a shared Google Sheet: (Link to sheet will be provided within the \"<strong>Confidential information</strong>\" section)</p><p><br></p><ul><li>Device Name</li><li>User Currently Assigned/Used</li><li>Windows OS Version</li><li>Device Role/Location</li><li>Confirmation of Successful RMM Installation (The RMM's URL Deployment Link will be provided within the \"<strong>Confidential information</strong>\" section that can be copied and pasted into a web browser to download the.exe)</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Phase 5 – Infrastructure Discovery:﻿</strong></p><p><strong><em><u>Document the following: (Within the shared Google Sheet)</u></em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em><u>Server Information</u></em></strong></p><ul><li>Physical or Virtual Server</li><li>Server Name</li><li>Operating System</li><li>Manufacturer</li><li>Model</li><li>Serial Number</li></ul><p>Network Equipment</p><ul><li>Firewall</li><li>Router</li><li>ISP Equipment</li><li>Switches</li><li>Wireless Access Points</li><li>UPS/Battery Backups</li></ul><p>Collect:</p><ul><li>Manufacturer</li><li>Model</li><li>Serial Number</li><li>Photos</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Phase 6 – Site Documentation:</strong></p><p><strong><em><u>Capture:Photos</u></em></strong></p><ul><li>Server Room</li><li>Network Rack</li><li>Firewall</li><li>Switches</li><li>UPS Devices</li><li>ISP Equipment</li><li>Workstations</li><li>Imaging Equipment (Pano, Intraoral 2D xray and cameras)</li></ul><p>Video</p><p>Create a walkthrough video of the office covering:</p><ul><li>Front Desk</li><li>Operatories</li><li>Server Area</li><li>Imaging Area ( where the Pano machine is)</li><li>Network Equipment&nbsp;</li><li><br></li></ul>","markdown":"***Work Order Onboarding & Discovery Assessment***\n\n**Overview:**\n\n***We are seeking an experienced IT field technician to perform an onsite IT onboarding assessment for a dental office that is either newly opened or preparing to open.***\n\n***The primary purpose of this visit is to:***\n\n1. Install our remote monitoring and management (RMM) tools on all applicable computers and servers.\n2. Perform a complete IT infrastructure discovery and documentation process.\n3. Collect equipment inventory, serial numbers, network information, and site photos/videos to support the upcoming onboarding.\n\nThis visit is expected to take approximately 3 hours, though completion time may vary based on office size and equipment count.\n\nThe technician will work directly with the office's designated Point of Contact (POC) and must maintain professional communication throughout the engagement.\n\n**Required Skills**\n\n- Network Equipment Identification\n- Windows Operating Systems\n- Basic Server Identification\n- Documentation & Asset Inventory\n- Professional Customer Communication\n\n**Dress Code**\n\n- Business Casual (Polo Preferred)\n- No smoking or vaping before or while onsite. (To avoid smelling like smoke)\n- Professional appearance and hygiene required\n\nFailure to maintain professional conduct may result in removal from the work orders engagement and non-payment.\n\n**Required Tools**Must Have\n\n- Laptop\n- Smartphone capable of taking photos and videos\n- Phillips and Flathead Screwdrivers\n- USB Flash Drive (32GB+ recommended)\n\n***Scope of Work***\n\n**Phase 1 – Site Check-In:**\n\n1. Contact the assigned **Work Order Manager** upon arrival. (will be listed within the \"**Confidential information** section)\n\n- Do not begin work until the work order manager has been contacted and updated on your arrival.\n\n1. Meet the **Office Manager** once inside the office who will serve as the Point of Contact (POC) in the office for helping gather/confirm equipment locations and completing phases 2 and 3.\n2. Request a brief walkthrough of the facility to identify all rooms and equipment locations.\n\n**Phase 2 – Practice Information Collection:**\n\n1. Practice Management Software: (Work with the office POC to gather)\n2. Examples:(Open Dental, Eaglesoft, Dentrix)\n3. Imaging Software\n4. Examples:( Dexis, Acteon AIS, Carestream, Vatech)\n5. Determine Data Storage Information:\n6. Where patient data is stored\n7. Server location\n8. Cloud services used\n9. Imaging storage location\n\n**Phase 3 – Device Inventory:**\n\n***Visit every room and identify all technology (Can also knock out \"Phase 4\" at the same time)***\n\n***Record (For each workstation:)***\n\n- Room Name\n- Computer Name\n- Manufacturer\n- Model\n- Windows OS Version\n- Serial Number\n\nExamples of room names:\n\n- Front Desk\n- Consult 1\n- Consult 2\n- Operatory 1\n- Operatory 2\n- Doctor Office\n- Lab\n- Imaging Room\n- Break Room\n\nTake a photo of each workstation and asset tag if available.\n\n**Phase 4 – RMM Deployment (Highest Priority):**Install RMM Agent On: (**This phase is the most important portion of the visit and MUST be completed before leaving the site**)\n\n- All workstations\n- Front desk computers\n- Doctor computers\n- Treatment room computers\n- Imaging computers\n- Servers\n- Any additional business-critical systems\n\nRequired Information for each device to be gathered and documented within a shared Google Sheet: (Link to sheet will be provided within the \"**Confidential information**\" section)\n\n- Device Name\n- User Currently Assigned/Used\n- Windows OS Version\n- Device Role/Location\n- Confirmation of Successful RMM Installation (The RMM's URL Deployment Link will be provided within the \"**Confidential information**\" section that can be copied and pasted into a web browser to download the.exe)\n\n**Phase 5 – Infrastructure Discovery:﻿**\n\n***Document the following: (Within the shared Google Sheet)***\n\n***Server Information***\n\n- Physical or Virtual Server\n- Server Name\n- Operating System\n- Manufacturer\n- Model\n- Serial Number\n\nNetwork Equipment\n\n- Firewall\n- Router\n- ISP Equipment\n- Switches\n- Wireless Access Points\n- UPS/Battery Backups\n\nCollect:\n\n- Manufacturer\n- Model\n- Serial Number\n- Photos\n\n**Phase 6 – Site Documentation:**\n\n***Capture:Photos***\n\n- Server Room\n- Network Rack\n- Firewall\n- Switches\n- UPS Devices\n- ISP Equipment\n- Workstations\n- Imaging Equipment (Pano, Intraoral 2D xray and cameras)\n\nVideo\n\nCreate a walkthrough video of the office covering:\n\n- Front Desk\n- Operatories\n- Server Area\n- Imaging Area ( where the Pano machine is)\n- Network Equipment\n-","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-21T11:00","end":"2026-09-21T14:00","latestStart":"2026-09-21T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":200,"max":200},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":75},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $200 is below minimum threshold $400"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Busy"},{"start":"2026-09-22T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"gap"},{"start":"2026-09-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start"