{"job":{"id":19990752,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"ESP Global Services Inc.","title":"Cannot connect to domain","description":{"html":"<p>ESP Reference Ticket-&nbsp;CS0958900</p>\n<p>UA Reference Ticket-INC3203917</p>\n<p>Location- RDU/AIRPORT/BAGGAGE SERVICE OFFICE</p>\n<p>POC/Contact call back number:&nbsp;N/A</p>\n<p>Issue Description- Workstation WRDU001E (Asset tag:&nbsp;AB0580882-01) observed to be offline, user is reporting a domain error.</p>\n<p><strong>Please perform the below troubleshooting steps and document results for EACH step</strong>.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Verify Ethernet cable is securely connected; check port/link light</li>\n<li>Test with a known-good Ethernet cable and network port.</li>\n<li>Confirm other workstations on the same network are connected.</li>\n<li>Check <strong>Settings &gt; Network &amp; Internet &gt; Ethernet</strong> for connection status.</li>\n<li>Open <strong>Device Manager &gt; Network Adapters</strong> and verify the Ethernet adapter is enabled with no errors.</li>\n<li>Confirm <strong>date, time, and time zone</strong> are correct.</li>\n<li>Restart the workstation and retry domain sign-in.</li>\n<li>If possible, test with another authorized domain account.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>If the workstation has network connectivity but continues to display a <strong>domain/trust relationship error</strong>, escalate to <strong>Tier 2</strong> for reimage confirmation.</p>\n<p>Please see reimage instructions below.</p>\n<p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>-1 pen Drive: The technician is required to have 1 16GB pen drive.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>-USB Keyboard and mouse:&nbsp;</li>\n<li>-ISO Preparation: FN tech must be connected to internet on a pc/laptop and call us at 1 833 203 7372 to prepare the files prior going to the site (This may take 15-20 minutes and will be rebated upon WO completion at the cost of $30) -</li>\n</ol>\n<p>-Contact Tier 2 support once onsite and in front of the device to confirm the reimaging steps are correctly performed, and the image has been kickstarted and can be observed remotely.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>-Once the reimage has been kickstarted please notify the site to not utilize the device and leave it powered on until the next business day, please also attain a number of an agent/ supervisor who would be able to assist with configurations and confirming device functionality.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>-Confirm all the above the tasks are performed and check out of the work order, uploading required notes and deliverables before departure. <strong>NOTE: FE is NOT required to stay onsite for the duration of the image and will NOT be paid if these instructions are not followed</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Please ensure that relevant pictures are uploaded and thorough troubleshooting is performed and reflected with supporting detailed closure notes. FE must attain a signature from a United Manager or supervisor confirming that the issue has been resolved before departure.</strong></p>","markdown":"ESP Reference Ticket- CS0958900\n\nUA Reference Ticket-INC3203917\n\nLocation- RDU/AIRPORT/BAGGAGE SERVICE OFFICE\n\nPOC/Contact call back number: N/A\n\nIssue Description- Workstation WRDU001E (Asset tag: AB0580882-01) observed to be offline, user is reporting a domain error.\n\n**Please perform the below troubleshooting steps and document results for EACH step**.\n\n1. Verify Ethernet cable is securely connected; check port/link light\n2. Test with a known-good Ethernet cable and network port.\n3. Confirm other workstations on the same network are connected.\n4. Check **Settings > Network & Internet > Ethernet** for connection status.\n5. Open **Device Manager > Network Adapters** and verify the Ethernet adapter is enabled with no errors.\n6. Confirm **date, time, and time zone** are correct.\n7. Restart the workstation and retry domain sign-in.\n8. If possible, test with another authorized domain account.\n\nIf the workstation has network connectivity but continues to display a **domain/trust relationship error**, escalate to **Tier 2** for reimage confirmation.\n\nPlease see reimage instructions below.\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n1. -1 pen Drive: The technician is required to have 1 16GB pen drive.\n2. -USB Keyboard and mouse:\n3. -ISO Preparation: FN tech must be connected to internet on a pc/laptop and call us at 1 833 203 7372 to prepare the files prior going to the site (This may take 15-20 minutes and will be rebated upon WO completion at the cost of $30) -\n\n-Contact Tier 2 support once onsite and in front of the device to confirm the reimaging steps are correctly performed, and the image has been kickstarted and can be observed remotely.\n\n-Once the reimage has been kickstarted please notify the site to not utilize the device and leave it powered on until the next business day, please also attain a number of an agent/ supervisor who would be able to assist with configurations and confirming device functionality.\n\n-Confirm all the above the tasks are performed and check out of the work order, uploading required notes and deliverables before departure. **NOTE: FE is NOT required to stay onsite for the duration of the image and will NOT be paid if these instructions are not followed**\n\n**Please ensure that relevant pictures are uploaded and thorough troubleshooting is performed and reflected with supporting detailed closure notes. FE must attain a signature from a United Manager or supervisor confirming that the issue has been resolved before departure.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-19T12:48","end":"2026-09-19T14:48"},"payRange":{"min":65,"max":130},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":65,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":2},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $130 (countered: $130) is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T22:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Busy"},{"start":"2026-09-22T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"gap"},{"start":"2026-09-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-09-23T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ​Concord Police Department - NC ( Phase 2 ) (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T20:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-22T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"Remote Hands - Connect AT&T broadband circuit"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1789834167551}
{"job":{"id":19990790,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Park Place Technologies","title":"Remote Hands - PPT1010514 - Wissen - Durham","description":{"html":"<p>SERVICE OVERVIEW<br />\n<br />\n- Scope of Work: [Description of service details]<br />\nNeed to schedule one onsite smart hands tech to work with our remote deployment lead to assist with hardware deployment and testing on September 22nd, 8:00 AM – 5:00 PM (EDT).<br />\n<br />\nSpecial Instructions:<br />\n• Once onsite and the tech has talked to the local contact call the Technical Remote Contact<br />\n<br />\nWhen onsite complete the following:<br />\n• With the Local Contact’s help, locate and inventory all equipment that was shipped to the location.<br />\n• Patch cables, computers, printers, scanner, label rolls, etc...<br />\n• With the Local Contact’s help, identify the staging location and unpack and verify all equipment and parts are in expected condition.<br />\n• Staging area will need multiple active data jacks and electrical outlets.<br />\n• Verify that the MAC addresses on the front or side of the printer(s) matches the LAN/Wired or WLAN/Wireless MAC addresses of the manufacturer's labels. The Technical Contact will provide the tech with which MAC address should be identified for each printer. (for Zebra printers the manufacture’s label is on the bottom of the printer)<br />\n• DO NOT PLUG IN PRINTERS UNTIL APPROVED BY TECHINCAL CONTACT<br />\n• Provide the IP and MAC address information to the Technical Contact, as requested.<br />\n• Work with Technical Contact to connect and setup all PC's in the designated staging area.<br />\n• Note: Accu-tech PC’s MUST be moved into the Accu-Tech\\Computers OU to get the correct GPO for Accu-Tech users.<br />\n• Work with the Technical Once all PC's have completed the setup process and the Technical Contact has approved; you will begin to replace the existing IT equipment as instructed by the Technical Contact and in coordination with the Local contact.<br />\n• Note: The goal during replacement is to Contact to ensure the PC’s are in the correct OU.<br />\n• minimize business disruptions as much as possible.<br />\n• Technical Contact will coordinate with the Local Contact on the appropriate time to swap out the old equipment with the new equipment.<br />\n• Once the new equipment is in place the Tech and the Technical Contact will run tests to ensure that all equipment is fully functional for the local Operations team.<br />\n• After all equipment is successfully deployed and tested the Tech will gather all old equipment and coordinate with the Local Contact to place it in a safe security designated area. Equipment will be sent for recycling.<br />\n• A list of old equipment with Serial number and pictures should be provided to the Technical Contact.<br />\n• The Tech should gather any packing material from the deployment and ensure that it is properly disposed of before completed the job.<br />\n• The Tech should leave the work areas in the same or better cleanliness than when they arrived.<br />\n• Once the Tech has confirmed with the Technical Contact that all work is complete they may inform the Local Contact that the job is done and that they can contact the Technical Contact for any issues.<br />\n<br />\n- Resource Level: [Level 1 / Level 2 / Level 3] L1<br />\n<br />\n- Required Tools (in addition to standard toolkit): [List tools required or Parts ETA]<br />\ncell phone with voice/data and email access. MS Teams installed and working on cell phone. Cell phone charger or extra battery to ensure 8 hours of phone usage. Laptop recommended but not required.</p>","markdown":"SERVICE OVERVIEW  \n  \n\\- Scope of Work: \\[Description of service details\\]  \nNeed to schedule one onsite smart hands tech to work with our remote deployment lead to assist with hardware deployment and testing on September 22nd, 8:00 AM – 5:00 PM (EDT).  \n  \nSpecial Instructions:  \n• Once onsite and the tech has talked to the local contact call the Technical Remote Contact  \n  \nWhen onsite complete the following:  \n• With the Local Contact’s help, locate and inventory all equipment that was shipped to the location.  \n• Patch cables, computers, printers, scanner, label rolls, etc...  \n• With the Local Contact’s help, identify the staging location and unpack and verify all equipment and parts are in expected condition.  \n• Staging area will need multiple active data jacks and electrical outlets.  \n• Verify that the MAC addresses on the front or side of the printer(s) matches the LAN/Wired or WLAN/Wireless MAC addresses of the manufacturer's labels. The Technical Contact will provide the tech with which MAC address should be identified for each printer. (for Zebra printers the manufacture’s label is on the bottom of the printer)  \n• DO NOT PLUG IN PRINTERS UNTIL APPROVED BY TECHINCAL CONTACT  \n• Provide the IP and MAC address information to the Technical Contact, as requested.  \n• Work with Technical Contact to connect and setup all PC's in the designated staging area.  \n• Note: Accu-tech PC’s MUST be moved into the Accu-Tech\\\\Computers OU to get the correct GPO for Accu-Tech users.  \n• Work with the Technical Once all PC's have completed the setup process and the Technical Contact has approved; you will begin to replace the existing IT equipment as instructed by the Technical Contact and in coordination with the Local contact.  \n• Note: The goal during replacement is to Contact to ensure the PC’s are in the correct OU.  \n• minimize business disruptions as much as possible.  \n• Technical Contact will coordinate with the Local Contact on the appropriate time to swap out the old equipment with the new equipment.  \n• Once the new equipment is in place the Tech and the Technical Contact will run tests to ensure that all equipment is fully functional for the local Operations team.  \n• After all equipment is successfully deployed and tested the Tech will gather all old equipment and coordinate with the Local Contact to place it in a safe security designated area. Equipment will be sent for recycling.  \n• A list of old equipment with Serial number and pictures should be provided to the Technical Contact.  \n• The Tech should gather any packing material from the deployment and ensure that it is properly disposed of before completed the job.  \n• The Tech should leave the work areas in the same or better cleanliness than when they arrived.  \n• Once the Tech has confirmed with the Technical Contact that all work is complete they may inform the Local Contact that the job is done and that they can contact the Technical Contact for any issues.  \n  \n\\- Resource Level: \\[Level 1 / Level 2 / Level 3\\] L1  \n  \n\\- Required Tools (in addition to standard toolkit): \\[List tools required or Parts ETA\\]  \ncell phone with voice/data and email access. MS Teams installed and working on cell phone. Cell phone charger or extra battery to ensure 8 hours of phone usage. Laptop recommended but not required.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-22T08:00","end":"2026-09-22T10:00"},"payRange":{"min":110,"max":550},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":110},"additional":{"units":8,"amount":55}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":5},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":{"shouldCounterOffer":true,"payType":"blended","counterRate":60,"baseAmount":600,"estHours":2,"travelExpense":0,"payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":120},"additional":{"units":8,"amount":60}},"counterDate":{"start":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T17:00:00.000Z","durationMinutes":60,"mode":"hours","reason":"arrival_window"}},"reason":"COUNTER_DATES"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000