{"job":{"id":19991002,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Loopdrive LLC","title":"Smart Home - Door Lock Swap","description":{"html":"<p><strong>YOU REPRESENT DIAMOND PROPERTY SERVICES ON THIS JOB. Identify yourself to the resident and Smart Home Support as a contractor working for Diamond Property Services—not Field Nation or your own company.</strong></p>Smart Home - Door Lock Swap<p>Replace one existing smart-home door lock, have Smart Home Support pair it, and verify locking/unlocking.</p><p><strong>Additional devices: If other devices need service outside this scope, photograph and detail each item worked on in your closeout. You may request $10 per additional item in your final bill. Sensor pairing is included and does not qualify for the additional $10 allowance. Do not discuss billing with Smart Home Support.</strong></p>1. CALL THE SITE MANAGER WHEN THERE IS A PROBLEM<p><strong>For calls and texts, contact the site manager at (901) 675-6129.</strong></p><p>Call immediately if:</p><ul><li>You will be late, need to cancel, or cannot attend.</li><li>The resident does not answer, refuses access, or the site is not ready.</li><li>Parts are missing/incorrect or you cannot complete the work.</li><li>You encounter wiring questions, equipment damage, or another problem preventing completion.</li></ul><p><strong>If your call is unanswered, text the same number immediately. Include the property address, problem, and your ETA if running late.</strong></p><p>For access or site-readiness problems, call and, if unanswered, text while still at the property, before leaving, so we can try to reach the resident.</p><p>An FN message or call to Smart Home Support does not replace contacting the Site Manager. Schedule changes require Site Manager approval.</p>2. DEVICE REQUIREMENTS<p>Install and service devices according to the equipment manufacturer’s requirements. Photograph original connections before changing them and completed work afterward. Follow Smart Home Support instructions for resets and pairing preparation; do not independently pair devices.</p>3. PAIRING AND CHECKOUT<p><strong>Smart Home Support: 330-970-2020 | Hours: 9 AM–5 PM Eastern</strong></p><p>Call with the property address for pairing and checkout. If you do not reach support immediately, call the Site Manager immediately; if that call is unanswered, text the Site Manager immediately. Support must confirm pairing and online status. Report any unresolved issue before leaving. If your late arrival prevents pairing before support closes, you may be required to return during support's normal hours to complete pairing.</p>4. REQUIRED PHOTOS AND DEVICE REPORT<p>Upload:</p><ul><li>Timestamped arrival and departure photos showing the property/address.</li><li>Before/after photos of every device serviced, including original/completed connections where applicable.</li><li>Support call-log screenshot and available app evidence of paired devices.</li></ul><p><strong>Report every scoped device and every additional device worked on, one line per device:</strong></p><p><strong>Device/location | Work performed | Final result</strong></p><p>Example: Hall thermostat | Replaced and paired | Operation tested; online. Kitchen leak sensor | Paired existing sensor only | Online.</p><p>Distinguish replacement, new installation, pairing only, diagnosis, and battery replacement. List incomplete or unperformed work and the reason. Include arrival/departure times, support representative, and Site Manager instructions received.</p><p><strong>“Completed” or “all devices paired” alone is not an acceptable report.</strong></p>5. SERVICE AND PAYMENT TERMS<p>Only the assigned technician may attend. Treat the resident and support staff professionally.</p><p>Completion requires the listed work, operational verification, support checkout, and required documentation. Correct incomplete or inaccurate documentation before requesting approval.</p><p>For resident no-access, site not ready, power outage, or missing/incorrect parts preventing work from starting: $45 No Show / Site Not Ready Fee: This fee will ONLY be approved if you upload a photo of the home from this visit AND proof that you contacted the Site Manager before leaving the site. Both are required. Contact Smart Home Support alone does not satisfy the Site Manager contact requirement. Full completion pay does not apply when no work was attempted. A $10 late-arrival deduction applies when you arrive after the agreed appointment time.</p>","markdown":"**YOU REPRESENT DIAMOND PROPERTY SERVICES ON THIS JOB. Identify yourself to the resident and Smart Home Support as a contractor working for Diamond Property Services—not Field Nation or your own company.**\n\nSmart Home - Door Lock SwapReplace one existing smart-home door lock, have Smart Home Support pair it, and verify locking/unlocking.\n\n**Additional devices: If other devices need service outside this scope, photograph and detail each item worked on in your closeout. You may request $10 per additional item in your final bill. Sensor pairing is included and does not qualify for the additional $10 allowance. Do not discuss billing with Smart Home Support.**\n\n1. CALL THE SITE MANAGER WHEN THERE IS A PROBLEM**For calls and texts, contact the site manager at (901) 675-6129.**\n\nCall immediately if:\n\n- You will be late, need to cancel, or cannot attend.\n- The resident does not answer, refuses access, or the site is not ready.\n- Parts are missing/incorrect or you cannot complete the work.\n- You encounter wiring questions, equipment damage, or another problem preventing completion.\n\n**If your call is unanswered, text the same number immediately. Include the property address, problem, and your ETA if running late.**\n\nFor access or site-readiness problems, call and, if unanswered, text while still at the property, before leaving, so we can try to reach the resident.\n\nAn FN message or call to Smart Home Support does not replace contacting the Site Manager. Schedule changes require Site Manager approval.\n\n2. DEVICE REQUIREMENTSInstall and service devices according to the equipment manufacturer’s requirements. Photograph original connections before changing them and completed work afterward. Follow Smart Home Support instructions for resets and pairing preparation; do not independently pair devices.\n\n3. PAIRING AND CHECKOUT**Smart Home Support: 330-970-2020 | Hours: 9 AM–5 PM Eastern**\n\nCall with the property address for pairing and checkout. If you do not reach support immediately, call the Site Manager immediately; if that call is unanswered, text the Site Manager immediately. Support must confirm pairing and online status. Report any unresolved issue before leaving. If your late arrival prevents pairing before support closes, you may be required to return during support's normal hours to complete pairing.\n\n4. REQUIRED PHOTOS AND DEVICE REPORTUpload:\n\n- Timestamped arrival and departure photos showing the property/address.\n- Before/after photos of every device serviced, including original/completed connections where applicable.\n- Support call-log screenshot and available app evidence of paired devices.\n\n**Report every scoped device and every additional device worked on, one line per device:**\n\n**Device/location | Work performed | Final result**\n\nExample: Hall thermostat | Replaced and paired | Operation tested; online. Kitchen leak sensor | Paired existing sensor only | Online.\n\nDistinguish replacement, new installation, pairing only, diagnosis, and battery replacement. List incomplete or unperformed work and the reason. Include arrival/departure times, support representative, and Site Manager instructions received.\n\n**“Completed” or “all devices paired” alone is not an acceptable report.**\n\n5. SERVICE AND PAYMENT TERMSOnly the assigned technician may attend. Treat the resident and support staff professionally.\n\nCompletion requires the listed work, operational verification, support checkout, and required documentation. Correct incomplete or inaccurate documentation before requesting approval.\n\nFor resident no-access, site not ready, power outage, or missing/incorrect parts preventing work from starting: $45 No Show / Site Not Ready Fee: This fee will ONLY be approved if you upload a photo of the home from this visit AND proof that you contacted the Site Manager before leaving the site. Both are required. Contact Smart Home Support alone does not satisfy the Site Manager contact requirement. Full completion pay does not apply when no work was attempted. A $10 late-arrival deduction applies when you arrive after the agreed appointment time.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-22T09:00","end":"2026-09-22T10:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":100},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":37},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $100 is below minimum threshold $400"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-22T18:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"gap"},{"start":"2026-09-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-09-23T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Miniso"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-21T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-21T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 ​Concord Police Department - NC ( Phase 2 ) (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","s