{"job":{"id":20004852,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"ASR tech","title":"Perform Maintenance on an Automated Package Locker System (MUST HAVE ALL REQUIRED TOOLS)","description":{"html":"<p><strong><em>**PLEASE&nbsp;<u>READ</u>&nbsp;THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER BEFORE ACCEPTING*</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>*PLEASE&nbsp;<u>READ&nbsp;</u>PROBLEM DESCRIPTION/SCOPE OF WORK BEFORE ACCEPTING*</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>*PLEASE&nbsp;<u>READ&nbsp;</u>TOOL REQUIREMENT BEFORE ACCEPTING**</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>**PROBLEM DESCRIPTION/SCOPE OF WORK**</u></strong></p><p><strong><em><u>&nbsp;The following has been reported:</u></em></strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Parcel Pending Locker - -</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">HIGH || Service Call - - Once onsite, Text Brian at 949-281-3222. If no response in 15 min, call Field Service line 949-317-4169.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> </span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- No parts sent out</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> </span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- Requesting tech for 9/23 9:00 AM THIS IS A KEBA SYSTEM</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- Tools needed Laptop, USB-Keyboard, Ethernet port/adapter and spare ethernet cord, Security torx T25 screwdriver,two 9V batteries(or 18volt to 24 volt battery pack and two wires to connect the positive and the negative posts to the KEBA to open control door) and ladder to access top of lockers to open main control door</span></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- Need to: Restore System Down - Send picture of network test.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- Standard Tools Required Laptop, USB-Keyboard, Ethernet port/adapter and spare ethernet cord</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> </span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">- General Maintenance (Open All Box, Package Maintenance, Disabled Doors, Test Camera, Barcode scanner) </span></p><p><strong><em>Ensure the system is fully functional. General Linux, electrical, and mechanical knowledge is required, but technical support will guide you through most of the process. Professionalism and attention to detail are required for this client.&nbsp;&nbsp;Please be mindful of how you are representing ASR and yourself.&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>**TOOL REQUIREMENT**ALL TOOLS LISTED ARE REQUIRED**</u></strong></p><p><strong>Government issued Identification</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Standard Technicians tool kit</strong></li><li><strong>Precision screwdriver set</strong></li><li><strong>Rubber Mallet</strong></li><li><strong>4' ladder</strong></li><li><strong>5\" round reusable hard surface sliders (or similar for floor protection)</strong></li><li><strong>Laptop w/ HyperTerminal or Putty, must be able to connect to CAT5 Cable and runs Windows XP or higher</strong></li><li><strong>Laptop must have Team Viewer</strong></li><li><strong>Drill/Driver</strong></li><li><strong>Laptop Charger</strong></li><li><strong>Wired USB Keyboard</strong></li><li><strong>6ft Crossover patch cable</strong></li><li><strong>6ft Standard patch cable</strong></li><li><strong>22-16 AWG&nbsp;wire splicing connectors</strong></li><li><strong>Silicone caulking (for end of self-tapping screws)</strong></li><li><strong>Crimper/Stripper tool</strong></li><li><strong>Punch Down tool (used to terminate keystone jacks)</strong></li><li><strong>Smart Phone with ability to access e-mail and open a mobile web page, Camera, Text</strong></li><li><strong>Smart Phone Charger</strong></li><li><strong>Digital Camera or the Smart Phone Camera (Must upload all photos of equipment worked on)</strong></li><li><strong>Dry Cloth/Towel and non-abrasive cleaner (wipe down lockers before leaving site)</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Download, print, review, and bring the attached PDFs to site:&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>ServiceCallChecklist rev1_1.pdf</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>SCOPE OF WORK MAY include open all box test, redelivering all packages, check for jammed/disabled doors, etc.</strong></p><p><strong>Some issues may take longer than expected.&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Potential issues can include any or all of the following:</p><ul><li>Jammed Door</li><li>Controller Unit Replacement</li><li>Sub Board Replacement</li><li>Solenoid Replacement</li><li>Clear Box/Redeliver Packages</li><li>If parts are to be returned, please use the prepaid return label provided</li><li>IMPORTANT:Please Take Photos of the equipment and parts before packing and returning</li></ul><p><strong><em><u>Professionalism, attention to detail, and customer care are required for this client, Customer Service skills are a must!&nbsp;Any discussion of prior work performed by anyone is not allowed. This may be reported back to Parcel and ASR. It may be interpreted as unprofessional behavior.</u></em></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>ASR PROFESSIONALISM REQUIREMENTS</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Technician should NOT discuss any scheduling or payment issues with Parcel Pending support desk under any circumstances. Any scheduling or payment issues MUST be discussed with ASR.&nbsp;&nbsp;</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>If the customer reaches out directly to you, please refer them back to ASR.</u></strong></p><ul><li>Perform excellent customer service. Be friendly, communicate, and assure them they're in good hands.&nbsp;</li><li>Dress code is casual business attire with no logos.</li><li>Do not share any pricing information with client.&nbsp;</li><li>Do not leave personal business information or contact information with client.</li><li>Technician needs to ensure that each site is a DRUG-FREE WORKPLACE</li><li>The technician needs to ensure they do not smell or reek of odors or other substances.</li></ul><p><strong><u>ASR Services intends to help provide a safe and drug-free work environment for our clients.</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>The Company explicitly prohibits:</u></strong></p><p><strong><u>The use, possession, solicitation for, or sale of narcotics or other illegal drugs, alcohol, or prescription medication without a prescription on customer premises or while performing an assignment.</u></strong></p><p><strong><em><u>ASR Project Number: 887</u></em></strong></p><p><strong><u>STEP ONE:</u></strong></p><p><strong>CHECK-IN: With Parcel Pending, be mindful as you are in contact with the customer directly (your contact name and number is listed under the Problem Description)&nbsp;Ask if any Parts were shipped to site and who has the parts onsite. DO NOT PERFORM ANY WORK&nbsp;until you have contacted Parcel Pending.&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong>Please contact our customer when you have arrived onsite.</strong></p><p><strong>***Always Leave a message if your contact does not answer and then call their Field Service line&nbsp;</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************</del></span>***</p><p><strong><u>STEP TWO:</u></strong></p><p><strong>CHECK-IN:On Field Nation - Please do not check in on&nbsp;Field Nation until you have checked in with Parcel Pending.&nbsp;​Your check-in/out times MUST match what Parcel Pending provides us.</strong></p><p><strong><u>STEP THREE:</u></strong></p><p><strong>LOCATE: Leasing/Rental Office, General Contractors Office, Concierge, Front Desk etc. Once in contact, ask for parts, if they were shipped.&nbsp;You would have this information from your contact in step one.</strong></p><p><strong><u>STEP FOUR:</u></strong></p><p><strong>FOLLOW: Direction from Parcel Pending.&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><u>STEP FIVE:</u></strong></p><p><strong>REPORT: PROBLEMS/ISSUES&nbsp;BEFORE LEAVING SITE and&nbsp;<u>CHECK-OUT.</u>&nbsp;&nbsp;Please do NOT check out on Field Nation until you have checked out with Parcel Pending.&nbsp;​(Number and tech support name will be under the Problem Description</strong>)&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>Your check-in/out times MUST match what our customer provides us.</strong></p><p><strong><u>STEP SIX:</u></strong></p><p><strong>SUBMIT</strong>: W<strong>ork order for payment within 24 hours of scheduled date.&nbsp;</strong>Please provide&nbsp;<strong>detailed closing notes</strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>timeline&nbsp;</strong>when submitting this work order for payment.</p><p><strong><em>The name of the individual accepting this work must be the actual person who arrives on site and if we determine there was a substitution without prior notice, we will not pay for the work performed.&nbsp;&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong><em>Be sure to notify ASR by phone and message in work order prior to tech arriving onsite.&nbsp;</em></strong></p><p><strong>ACCEPTING THIS WORK ORDER MEANS THAT YOU WILL HAVE ALL OF THE REQUIRED TOOLS.&nbsp;ALSO, HAVE READ AND UNDERSTAND THE SCOPE OF WORK.&nbsp;&nbsp;PLEASE UPDATE YOUR ETA AS SOON AS YOU ARE ASSIGNED. YOU WILL BE HELD RESPONSIBLE FOR ARRIVING ON THE SCHEDULED DATE AND TIME. ANY VIOLATIONS WILL BE ESCALATED TO FIELD NATION.&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p><strong><em>Parcel Pending and Site may provide a report card based on professionalism and understanding of work being done.&nbsp;</em>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Tech should NOT discuss payment or scheduling discrepancies with Parcel Pending, Site Contact or anyone but ASR (NO exceptions)</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>***Please CALL Rodrigo R. 949-556-3604</strong>&nbsp;for any general questions/information.***</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>ONSITE DETAILS &amp; CONDUCT</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>If you are unable to make it to site, you must call/text Rodrigo </strong>(Phone number in Confidential Information)</li><li><strong>Work Order is subject to Penalty Fee at Buyers Discretion.&nbsp;</strong></li><li><strong>You will be representing ASR Services when communicating with the end user or Parcel Pending support.</strong></li><li><strong>All conversation on site should be kept to business related items and not personal matters.&nbsp;</strong></li><li><strong>Resolve the issues using the documentation provided with support from Technical Support.</strong></li><li><strong>Do not access the \"System Maintenance Screen\" unless instructed by Technical Support.</strong></li><li><strong><u>Upon completion of service:&nbsp;KEY NEEDS TO BE IN SECURE LOCATION</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>a: please return keys to MOD onsite. Will need first and last name of keyholder (this info is required for release from site and Work Order closure).</u></strong></li><li><strong><u>b: If no onsite personnel are onsite/available, ask Parcel Pending Support/ASR Support Team member with whom you are working for direction on where keys should be left.&nbsp;</u></strong></li><li><strong>If you are requested to do anything out side of the scope of work, including returning to site, or dealing with a DOA, you must call/text Rodrigo.&nbsp;</strong>(Phone number in Confidential Information)</li><li><strong>Tech must provide photos of any equipment that is worked on.</strong></li><li><strong>Tech must fill out the ServiceCallChecklist rev1_1.pdf COMPLETELY and have it signed by the property manager</strong></li><li><strong>Tech must note arrival and departure times on sign off sheet, document any site delays and requests that are made out of the scope of work in the closing notes.</strong></li><li><strong>During completion, tech must provide any photos, closing notes, open issues, service call checklist, sign off sheet, and name of person that released tech from site.</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong><u>RETURNING EQUIPMENT</u></strong></p><p><strong>If any equipment needs to be returned to Parcel Pending after completion please take a photo of equipment or parts before leaving site (damaged or undamaged) to ensure responsibility.&nbsp;A return label will be in the shipping pouch behind the original shipping label.</strong></p><p><strong>If a return label was not provided, please contact Parcel Pending immediately to obtain BEFORE leaving site, they will email a return label to you.</strong></p><p><strong>***A release code will be provided to you once tracking shows that parts are on the way back to our customer***</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>PAYMENT</u></strong></p><p>2 hours on site will be paid at a fixed rate of $85 with a potential of up to 2 additional hours paid in 15 min intervals @ $40/hr.</p><p><strong>Some issues may take long.&nbsp;Any time on site, after 2 hours, will need to be approved by Parcel Pending.</strong></p><p><strong>Your check in/out times on this work order must match what our customer provides.</strong></p><p>Site abort where technician does not go to site, but within 24 hrs $30.00</p><p>Site abort with technician onsite – determined by time spent at site.</p><p>Cancellation with more than 24 hrs notice will be paid $0.</p>","markdown":"***\\*\\*PLEASE READ THE ENTIRE WORK ORDER BEFORE ACCEPTING\\****\n\n***\\*PLEASE READ PROBLEM DESCRIPTION/SCOPE OF WORK BEFORE ACCEPTING\\****\n\n***\\*PLEASE READ TOOL REQUIREMENT BEFORE ACCEPTING\\*\\****\n\n**\\*\\*PROBLEM DESCRIPTION/SCOPE OF WORK\\*\\***\n\n ***The following has been reported:***\n\nParcel Pending Locker - -\n\nHIGH || Service Call - - Once onsite, Text Brian at 949-281-3222. If no response in 15 min, call Field Service line 949-317-4169.\n\n\\- No parts sent out\n\n\\- Requesting tech for 9/23 9:00 AM THIS IS A KEBA SYSTEM\n\n  \n\\\n\n\\- Tools needed Laptop, USB-Keyboard, Ethernet port/adapter and spare ethernet cord, Security torx T25 screwdriver,two 9V batteries(or 18volt to 24 volt battery pack and two wires to connect the positive and the negative posts to the KEBA to open control door) and ladder to access top of lockers to open main control door\n\n  \n\\\n\n\\- Need to: Restore System Down - Send picture of network test.\n\n  \n\\\n\n\\- Standard Tools Required Laptop, USB-Keyboard, Ethernet port/adapter and spare ethernet cord\n\n\\- General Maintenance (Open All Box, Package Maintenance, Disabled Doors, Test Camera, Barcode scanner)\n\n***Ensure the system is fully functional. General Linux, electrical, and mechanical knowledge is required, but technical support will guide you through most of the process. Professionalism and attention to detail are required for this client. Please be mindful of how you are representing ASR and yourself.***\n\n**\\*\\*TOOL REQUIREMENT\\*\\*ALL TOOLS LISTED ARE REQUIRED\\*\\***\n\n**Government issued Identification**\n\n- **Standard Technicians tool kit**\n- **Precision screwdriver set**\n- **Rubber Mallet**\n- **4' ladder**\n- **5\" round reusable hard surface sliders (or similar for floor protection)**\n- **Laptop w/ HyperTerminal or Putty, must be able to connect to CAT5 Cable and runs Windows XP or higher**\n- **Laptop must have Team Viewer**\n- **Drill/Driver**\n- **Laptop Charger**\n- **Wired USB Keyboard**\n- **6ft Crossover patch cable**\n- **6ft Standard patch cable**\n- **22-16 AWG wire splicing connectors**\n- **Silicone caulking (for end of self-tapping screws)**\n- **Crimper/Stripper tool**\n- **Punch Down tool (used to terminate keystone jacks)**\n- **Smart Phone with ability to access e-mail and open a mobile web page, Camera, Text**\n- **Smart Phone Charger**\n- **Digital Camera or the Smart Phone Camera (Must upload all photos of equipment worked on)**\n- **Dry Cloth/Towel and non-abrasive cleaner (wipe down lockers before leaving site)**\n\n**Download, print, review, and bring the attached PDFs to site:**\n\n- ServiceCallChecklist rev1\\_1.pdf\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK MAY include open all box test, redelivering all packages, check for jammed/disabled doors, etc.**\n\n**Some issues may take longer than expected.**\n\nPotential issues can include any or all of the following:\n\n- Jammed Door\n- Controller Unit Replacement\n- Sub Board Replacement\n- Solenoid Replacement\n- Clear Box/Redeliver Packages\n- If parts are to be returned, please use the prepaid return label provided\n- IMPORTANT:Please Take Photos of the equipment and parts before packing and returning\n\n***Professionalism, attention to detail, and customer care are required for this client, Customer Service skills are a must! Any discussion of prior work performed by anyone is not allowed. This may be reported back to Parcel and ASR. It may be interpreted as unprofessional behavior.***\n\n**ASR PROFESSIONALISM REQUIREMENTS**\n\n**Technician should NOT discuss any scheduling or payment issues with Parcel Pending support desk under any circumstances. Any scheduling or payment issues MUST be discussed with ASR.**\n\n**If the customer reaches out directly to you, please refer them back to ASR.**\n\n- Perform excellent customer service. Be friendly, communicate, and assure them they're in good hands.\n- Dress code is casual business attire with no logos.\n- Do not share any pricing information with client.\n- Do not leave personal business information or contact information with client.\n- Technician needs to ensure that each site is a DRUG-FREE WORKPLACE\n- The technician needs to ensure they do not smell or reek of odors or other substances.\n\n**ASR Services intends to help provide a safe and drug-free work environment for our clients.**\n\n**The Company explicitly prohibits:**\n\n**The use, possession, solicitation for, or sale of narcotics or other illegal drugs, alcohol, or prescription medication without a prescription on customer premises or while performing an assignment.**\n\n***ASR Project Number: 887***\n\n**STEP ONE:**\n\n**CHECK-IN: With Parcel Pending, be mindful as you are in contact with the customer directly (your contact name and number is listed under the Problem Description) Ask if any Parts were shipped to site and who has the parts onsite. DO NOT PERFORM ANY WORK until you have contacted Parcel Pending.**\n\n**Please contact our customer when you have arrived onsite.**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*Always Leave a message if your contact does not answer and then call their Field Service line** \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**STEP TWO:**\n\n**CHECK-IN:On Field Nation - Please do not check in on Field Nation until you have checked in with Parcel Pending. ​Your check-in/out times MUST match what Parcel Pending provides us.**\n\n**STEP THREE:**\n\n**LOCATE: Leasing/Rental Office, General Contractors Office, Concierge, Front Desk etc. Once in contact, ask for parts, if they were shipped. You would have this information from your contact in step one.**\n\n**STEP FOUR:**\n\n**FOLLOW: Direction from Parcel Pending.**\n\n**STEP FIVE:**\n\n**REPORT: PROBLEMS/ISSUES BEFORE LEAVING SITE and CHECK-OUT. Please do NOT check out on Field Nation until you have checked out with Parcel Pending. ​(Number and tech support name will be under the Problem Description**) **Your check-in/out times MUST match what our customer provides us.**\n\n**STEP SIX:**\n\n**SUBMIT**: W**ork order for payment within 24 hours of scheduled date.** Please provide **detailed closing notes** and **timeline** when submitting this work order for payment.\n\n***The name of the individual accepting this work must be the actual person who arrives on site and if we determine there was a substitution without prior notice, we will not pay for the work performed.***\n\n***Be sure to notify ASR by phone and message in work order prior to tech arriving onsite.***\n\n**ACCEPTING THIS WORK ORDER MEANS THAT YOU WILL HAVE ALL OF THE REQUIRED TOOLS. ALSO, HAVE READ AND UNDERSTAND THE SCOPE OF WORK. PLEASE UPDATE YOUR ETA AS SOON AS YOU ARE ASSIGNED. YOU WILL BE HELD RESPONSIBLE FOR ARRIVING ON THE SCHEDULED DATE AND TIME. ANY VIOLATIONS WILL BE ESCALATED TO FIELD NATION.**\n\n***Parcel Pending and Site may provide a report card based on professionalism and understanding of work being done.***\n\n**Tech should NOT discuss payment or scheduling discrepancies with Parcel Pending, Site Contact or anyone but ASR (NO exceptions)**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*Please CALL Rodrigo R. 949-556-3604** for any general questions/information.\\*\\*\\*\n\n**ONSITE DETAILS & CONDUCT**\n\n- **If you are unable to make it to site, you must call/text Rodrigo** (Phone number in Confidential Information)\n- **Work Order is subject to Penalty Fee at Buyers Discretion.**\n- **You will be representing ASR Services when communicating with the end user or Parcel Pending support.**\n- **All conversation on site should be kept to business related items and not personal matters.**\n- **Resolve the issues using the documentation provided with support from Technical Support.**\n- **Do not access the \"System Maintenance Screen\" unless instructed by Technical Support.**\n- **Upon completion of service: KEY NEEDS TO BE IN SECURE LOCATION**\n- **a: please return keys to MOD onsite. Will need first and last name of keyholder (this info is required for release from site and Work Order closure).**\n- **b: If no onsite personnel are onsite/available, ask Parcel Pending Support/ASR Support Team member with whom you are working for direction on where keys should be left.**\n- **If you are requested to do anything out side of the scope of work, including returning to site, or dealing with a DOA, you must call/text Rodrigo.** (Phone number in Confidential Information)\n- **Tech must provide photos of any equipment that is worked on.**\n- **Tech must fill out the ServiceCallChecklist rev1\\_1.pdf COMPLETELY and have it signed by the property manager**\n- **Tech must note arrival and departure times on sign off sheet, document any site delays and requests that are made out of the scope of work in the closing notes.**\n- **During completion, tech must provide any photos, closing notes, open issues, service call checklist, sign off sheet, and name of person that released tech from site.**\n\n**RETURNING EQUIPMENT**\n\n**If any equipment needs to be returned to Parcel Pending after completion please take a photo of equipment or parts before leaving site (damaged or undamaged) to ensure responsibility. A return label will be in the shipping pouch behind the original shipping label.**\n\n**If a return label was not provided, please contact Parcel Pending immediately to obtain BEFORE leaving site, they will email a return label to you.**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*A release code will be provided to you once tracking shows that parts are on the way back to our customer\\*\\*\\***\n\n**PAYMENT**\n\n2 hours on site will be paid at a fixed rate of $85 with a potential of up to 2 additional hours paid in 15 min intervals @ $40/hr.\n\n**Some issues may take long. Any time on site, after 2 hours, will need to be approved by Parcel Pending.**\n\n**Your check in/out times on this work order must match what our customer provides.**\n\nSite abort where technician does not go to site, but within 24 hrs $30.00\n\nSite abort with technician onsite – determined by time spent at site.\n\nCancellation with more than 24 hrs notice will be paid $0.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-23T09:00","end":"2026-09-23T11:00","latestStart":"2026-09-23T14:00"},"payRange":{"min":85,"max":125},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":85},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":40}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":13},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $125 is below minimum threshold $300"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T17:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-23T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","summary":