{"job":{"id":"3492585519","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"CallTek Inc","title":"A cable technician is required to visit the site to test the cable runs between the MDF/IDF rooms and the wall ports in all 149 guest rooms","description":"<p><strong>SNA ID: </strong>WO-000007881</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Please Note:&nbsp;</strong>&nbsp;</p><p>The job is posted for one hour, but this does not guarantee it will be completed within that time.&nbsp;</p><p>- Be prepared to stay on-site until the work is fully completed.&nbsp;</p><p>- Carefully review the scope of work in advance to ensure you have enough time to finish the task.&nbsp;</p><p>- Once the job is completed, a budget increase will be applied accordingly.&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p><em><u>***Do not begin the job unless you are actively connected to the Remote Support. Call Dispatch again for assistance. Work completed without their assistance will not be compensated.***</u></em></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>STATEMENT OF WORK:</strong></p><p><br></p><p>A cable technician is required to visit the site to test the cable runs between the MDF/IDF rooms and the wall ports in all 149 guest rooms.</p><p><br></p><p>To gain access to the guest rooms, contact the POC:</p><p><br></p><p>POC Name: Jenn Watson</p><p>POC Phone Number: 919-819-2361</p><p><br></p><p>### Switch Information</p><p><br></p><p>Switch Location: MDF</p><p>Switch Name: HLT-RDUCV-350-MDF-CS01</p><p>Switch MAC: 34:56:fe:ab:92:1c</p><p><br></p><p>Switch Name: HLT-RDUCV-350-MDF-AS01</p><p>Switch MAC: f8:9e:28:ee:e2:65</p><p><br></p><p>Switch Location: IDF</p><p>Switch Name: HLT-RDUCV-350-IDF1-AS02-1</p><p>Switch MAC: a8:46:9d:bf:37:15</p><p><br></p><p>Switch Name: HLT-RDUCV-350-IDF1-AS02-2</p><p>Switch MAC: f8:9e:28:ee:f4:11</p><p><br></p><p>Switch Name: HLT-RDUCV-350-IDF1-AS02-3</p><p>Switch MAC: f8:9e:28:ee:f6:1b</p><p><br></p><p>Switch Name: HLT-RDUCV-350-IDF1-AS02-4</p><p>Switch MAC: f8:9e:28:ef:03:3f</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>### Cable Run Troubleshooting</p><p><br></p><p>1. Test all existing wiring using a MicroScanner or equivalent device.</p><p>2. Identify and repair any faulty pairs.</p><p>3. Determine the appropriate solution and, if necessary, re-punch, re-terminate, and/or replace the patch cable or cable run.</p><p><br></p><p>Additional troubleshooting may be necessary to resolve any remaining connectivity or speed issues.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>### Documentation and Completion Requirements</p><p><br></p><p>After installation or repair, the job must be tested and delivered to the customer.</p><p>To maintain accurate documentation, the technician should take pictures of the closet being worked in before and after moving cables or performing troubleshooting.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>### Tech Must Bring the Following</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>* Laptop (latest Windows OS) with at least an integrated 1-Gigabit NIC, dual-band wireless, a USB port, and PuTTY installed</strong></p><p><strong>* Cell phone with a mobile data connection that can be used as a hotspot</strong></p><p><strong>* Cisco console cable, patch cables, and serial-to-USB adapter</strong></p><p><strong>* Diagnostic tools: cable tester/certifier (Fluke, Lantek, or Klein Tools), toner/probe kit, and digital multimeter</strong></p><p><strong>* Hand tools: screwdrivers (flat-head and Phillips, of various sizes), including a crimper and punch-down tool</strong></p><p><strong>* Extra RJ45 connectors and Ethernet patch cables</strong></p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-22T02:30","end":"2026-09-22T03:30"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":60},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":60,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":1.6},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 9/22/2026, 2:30:00 AM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T17