{"job":{"id":20003365,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Vimenture","title":"Control4 Music System Troubleshooting","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Overview:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Seeking a technician with experience in networking and residential/commercial AV systems. We need someone to troubleshoot a Control4 Music system that stopped working following a brief electrical outage.</li>\n<li>The site has already attempted to reboot both the network router and the <strong>Control4 Music system</strong>, but the issue remains unresolved. Technician will need to inspect the network and Control4 equipment, identify the cause of the failure, and restore functionality if possible.</li>\n<li>Job is estimated to take 1–2 hours.</li>\n<li>The technician assigned to this work order MUST be the technician performing the work on-site.</li>\n<li>The technician assigned to this work order MUST check in and out on-site using GPS, per our client's directive. If you cannot do this, please do not request this job.</li>\n<li>If any quotes are requested/required, these MUST be uploaded into Field Nation only and not shared with the site contact or our clients. Please include a breakdown of labor, materials, and any additional requested expenses.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Tools Required (must haves):</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Laptop</li>\n<li>Ethernet tester/toner</li>\n<li>Network troubleshooting tools</li>\n<li>Basic hand tools</li>\n<li>Ethernet cables/patch cables</li>\n<li>Any tools necessary to troubleshoot Control4/network equipment</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Pre-Site Requirements</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Review the work order and call the work order manager with any questions before proceeding.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>On-Site Tasks</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Check in to the work order using GPS.</li>\n<li>Introduce yourself to the onsite manager as being from Vimenture.</li>\n<li>Contact the client's IT Help Desk to check in and discuss the issue with <del>**** ** ****** ** *************</del></li>\n<li>Verify the Control4 Music system is powered on and inspect the equipment for any visible issues following the electrical outage.</li>\n<li>Verify power to the Control4 equipment and associated network equipment.</li>\n<li>Check the network connection to the Control4 system and verify that the necessary equipment is communicating.</li>\n<li>Check the network router, switches, and other related equipment for connectivity or configuration issues.</li>\n<li>Test network connectivity and internet access where applicable.</li>\n<li>Reboot applicable Control4/network equipment as needed and verify whether the system comes back online.</li>\n<li>Check Ethernet connections, patch cables, ports, and link/activity lights for possible faults.</li>\n<li>Troubleshoot the Control4 Music system to determine why it stopped functioning after the electrical outage.</li>\n<li>Restore the Control4 Music system to working condition if possible.</li>\n<li>If the issue cannot be resolved during the visit, document the findings and identify any equipment, cabling, configuration, or other issues requiring additional work.</li>\n<li>Put together a quote for any additional work or replacement equipment needed.</li>\n<li>Confirm the Control4 Music system and related network equipment are operating properly with the IT Help Desk prior to checking out of the site.</li>\n<li>Collect a signature from the onsite manager.</li>\n<li>Clean the work area fully before leaving the site.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Required On-Site Deliverables</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Provide detailed notes describing the troubleshooting performed, findings, and resolution.</li>\n<li>Include photos of the Control4 equipment, network connections, and any identified issues or faults.</li>\n<li>Document any equipment that appears damaged or failed following the electrical outage.</li>\n<li>Upload any required quote to Field Nation only.</li>\n<li>Check out of the work order in the Field Nation app using GPS.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Escalation Process:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Contact the work order manager if any of the following are true:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Clarification is needed on the work order or there are questions regarding the scope.</li>\n<li>The Control4 system cannot be restored within the approved time.</li>\n<li>Additional equipment, parts, labor, or services are required.</li>\n<li>Additional hours are needed beyond the approved time.</li>\n<li>A quote is required for additional work.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>If clarification is needed on the work order or there are any questions, please call <del>******* ** *************</del></p>\n<p><strong>Additional Hours and Expenses Approval Payment Policy:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Buyer will not pay travel expenses unless pre-approved. Travel expenses must be entered in Counter Offers. Any pre-approved travel expenses must be entered in the Field Nation app as \"Travel Expenses\" and not \"Additional Hours.\"</li>\n<li>Any hours worked beyond the pre-approved maximum hours on the published job description must be pre-approved by calling<del>*******</del>. If approved, the buyer will document the additional approved time in the messages of the Field Nation portal.</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**Overview:**\n\n- Seeking a technician with experience in networking and residential/commercial AV systems. We need someone to troubleshoot a Control4 Music system that stopped working following a brief electrical outage.\n- The site has already attempted to reboot both the network router and the **Control4 Music system**, but the issue remains unresolved. Technician will need to inspect the network and Control4 equipment, identify the cause of the failure, and restore functionality if possible.\n- Job is estimated to take 1–2 hours.\n- The technician assigned to this work order MUST be the technician performing the work on-site.\n- The technician assigned to this work order MUST check in and out on-site using GPS, per our client's directive. If you cannot do this, please do not request this job.\n- If any quotes are requested/required, these MUST be uploaded into Field Nation only and not shared with the site contact or our clients. Please include a breakdown of labor, materials, and any additional requested expenses.\n\n**Tools Required (must haves):**\n\n- Laptop\n- Ethernet tester/toner\n- Network troubleshooting tools\n- Basic hand tools\n- Ethernet cables/patch cables\n- Any tools necessary to troubleshoot Control4/network equipment\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n**Pre-Site Requirements**\n\n- Review the work order and call the work order manager with any questions before proceeding.\n\n**On-Site Tasks**\n\n- Check in to the work order using GPS.\n- Introduce yourself to the onsite manager as being from Vimenture.\n- Contact the client's IT Help Desk to check in and discuss the issue with \\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- Verify the Control4 Music system is powered on and inspect the equipment for any visible issues following the electrical outage.\n- Verify power to the Control4 equipment and associated network equipment.\n- Check the network connection to the Control4 system and verify that the necessary equipment is communicating.\n- Check the network router, switches, and other related equipment for connectivity or configuration issues.\n- Test network connectivity and internet access where applicable.\n- Reboot applicable Control4/network equipment as needed and verify whether the system comes back online.\n- Check Ethernet connections, patch cables, ports, and link/activity lights for possible faults.\n- Troubleshoot the Control4 Music system to determine why it stopped functioning after the electrical outage.\n- Restore the Control4 Music system to working condition if possible.\n- If the issue cannot be resolved during the visit, document the findings and identify any equipment, cabling, configuration, or other issues requiring additional work.\n- Put together a quote for any additional work or replacement equipment needed.\n- Confirm the Control4 Music system and related network equipment are operating properly with the IT Help Desk prior to checking out of the site.\n- Collect a signature from the onsite manager.\n- Clean the work area fully before leaving the site.\n\n**Required On-Site Deliverables**\n\n- Provide detailed notes describing the troubleshooting performed, findings, and resolution.\n- Include photos of the Control4 equipment, network connections, and any identified issues or faults.\n- Document any equipment that appears damaged or failed following the electrical outage.\n- Upload any required quote to Field Nation only.\n- Check out of the work order in the Field Nation app using GPS.\n\n**Escalation Process:**\n\n**Contact the work order manager if any of the following are true:**\n\n- Clarification is needed on the work order or there are questions regarding the scope.\n- The Control4 system cannot be restored within the approved time.\n- Additional equipment, parts, labor, or services are required.\n- Additional hours are needed beyond the approved time.\n- A quote is required for additional work.\n\nIf clarification is needed on the work order or there are any questions, please call \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Additional Hours and Expenses Approval Payment Policy:**\n\n- Buyer will not pay travel expenses unless pre-approved. Travel expenses must be entered in Counter Offers. Any pre-approved travel expenses must be entered in the Field Nation app as \"Travel Expenses\" and not \"Additional Hours.\"\n- Any hours worked beyond the pre-approved maximum hours on the published job description must be pre-approved by calling\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*. If approved, the buyer will document the additional approved time in the messages of the Field Nation portal.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"