{"job":{"id":19998025,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Pursuant Health","title":"Replace BP Cuff / Hose, Replace and Configure Kiosk PC and Antenna and PM Kiosk","description":{"html":"<ul><li>A Release Code must be obtained upon completion of the work order, prior to leaving the site. <strong>Failure to obtain Release Code</strong> will result in deduction and/or cancellation of the work order.</li><li>CAUTION: Do not plug any power tools or cleaning devices into the kiosk’s internal power strips. Doing so may result in blown fuses and system failure. Use only approved connections as directed.</li><li>CONNECT to WIFI - Poor connection may result in difficulties accessing work instructions and contacting support. If you are having connectivity issues please connect to the site&#39;s WIFI connection.</li><li>REMOVE MIRROR BOX (FM kiosks only) - Is a mirror box currently installed in kiosk? If so, remove and set aside for disposal. Instructions: https://bit.ly/KioskMirrorBox</li><li><strong>Replace the BP Cuff and Hose</strong><br /><ul><li>Please refer to the step-by-step guide in the link below:</li><li>https://bit.ly/MAVBPCuff</li></ul></li><li><strong>Remove old PC, networking hardware, and cellular antenna, then replace with newer model PC and new cellular antenna.</strong><br /><ul><li>Please refer to the step-by-step guide in the link below:</li><li>https://bit.ly/MAVOnLogic</li><li>When cable-managing, ensure that:<ul><li>Both antenna(s) are routed on the left wall of the kiosk.</li><li>All video cables are routed on the right wall of the kiosk.</li><li>The antenna(s) do not touch any of the video cables.</li></ul></li></ul></li><li><span>STOP BUTTON PHOTO (FM and PH kiosks only) - Verify the stop button is wired and secured correctly, then take a clear photo showing the wiring/mounting hardware. This photo will be needed during the checkout process to obtain your release code.</span></li></ul>","markdown":"- A Release Code must be obtained upon completion of the work order, prior to leaving the site. **Failure to obtain Release Code** will result in deduction and/or cancellation of the work order.\n- CAUTION: Do not plug any power tools or cleaning devices into the kiosk’s internal power strips. Doing so may result in blown fuses and system failure. Use only approved connections as directed.\n- CONNECT to WIFI - Poor connection may result in difficulties accessing work instructions and contacting support. If you are having connectivity issues please connect to the site's WIFI connection.\n- REMOVE MIRROR BOX (FM kiosks only) - Is a mirror box currently installed in kiosk? If so, remove and set aside for disposal. Instructions: <https://bit.ly/KioskMirrorBox>\n- **Replace the BP Cuff and Hose**  \n  \n  - Please refer to the step-by-step guide in the link below:\n  - <https://bit.ly/MAVBPCuff>\n- **Remove old PC, networking hardware, and cellular antenna, then replace with newer model PC and new cellular antenna.**  \n  \n  - Please refer to the step-by-step guide in the link below:\n  - <https://bit.ly/MAVOnLogic>\n  - When cable-managing, ensure that:\n      - Both antenna(s) are routed on the left wall of the kiosk.\n      - All video cables are routed on the right wall of the kiosk.\n      - The antenna(s) do not touch any of the video cables.\n- STOP BUTTON PHOTO (FM and PH kiosks only) - Verify the stop button is wired and secured correctly, then take a clear photo showing the wiring/mounting hardware. This photo will be needed during the checkout process to obtain your release code.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-25T14:00","end":"2026-09-25T17:00","latestStart":"2026-09-25T14:45"},"payRange":{"min":150,"max":150},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":39},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $150 is below minimum threshold $400"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-