{"job":{"id":19998886,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Simple Communications Technologies","title":"Telecom - POTS Line- TONE,TAG, TRACE (Fire, Burg, Elevators, Call Boxes)","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Onsite Contact: Mel Gower</strong></p><p>Core Network Services</p><p>IBM CIO Network Reliability Engineering</p><p>+1 919 543 1234 Office</p><p>+1 919 279 0987 mobile</p><p><strong>Technical Contact:</strong> </p><p><br></p><p><strong>To Provide more Details:</strong></p><ul><li>We will be looking to install a POTS replacement solution that can be from 1-8 lines per site. This solution is a enclosure style with a 66 block. It operates on cellular and a internet connection from the customers network.</li><li>This specific site has a range of line types. They have phone numbers but do not know what location these numbers go to.</li><li>Identify if any Lines will need to be roughed in or ran for internet or POTS from any other locations or areas to where we can install solution. (IDF, MDF, Maintenance Room.) See attached document for example images of system.</li><li>We will be looking for 3-4 line types and of those devices that have active POTS lines. Specifically Elevators, Fire Panels, Security, Fax and a few Escalators for this customer. If the lines are live, tagging them and list the number with label maker. Customer should have no more than 3-4 lines per site.</li><li>We have notes in the documentation attached on how to achieve the information we need. There will be a technical contact on call you need to check in with and will need to collaborate with from SimpleCom if you feel you need that help. But you will be required to check in and out with possible text message communications with our engineers once your onsite.</li><li>You will need to know how to send text messages, complete and screen shot cellular speed tests from your phone, required to bring a butt sett, fox and hound to trace telephone lines and a ladder if you need to look above ceiling tiles. Label Maker and if any of these things you do not have we could deduct 10% from the ticket.</li><li>We will need the formstack form link completed for each location about these lines while onsite NOT AFTER. This will be checked to confirm you have submitted it before you leave.</li><li>FOLLOW FORMSTACK &amp; FN TASK LIST. Documents Attached for Reference.</li><li>We have notified the site managers of the scheduled visit. Its important your at the site checked in at your specified time. (If you are late please call the SimpleCom contact on the ticket NOT the store.)</li><li>The locations of the phone lines may be in the same office or building as the customer but in certain locations they may be in other locations. Like a shopping mall will require collaboration with the manager to get you into the Mall Telco or building central Dmarc.</li><li>Some locations the landlord is using phone lines provided by our customer. But that doesn't mean they pay for that line. So its important you reference the phone line excel sheet to identify if this is a line owned by our customer. (attached under client documents.</li><li>Not every document listed below will be used. But is there for reference information or if the site contact asks.</li></ul><p><strong>This site survey includes the following: (Please see details SOW attached below.)</strong></p><ul><li>Tone &amp; Trace customers existing Telco Lines. (Find existing lines and if they are line.) Look for available 2x2 area with power, for new POTS enclosure and available WAN port for box from customers LAN.</li><li>This system will also have a cellular piece made into the box. Cell signal is also important to capture and identify in your mounting location. (Verizon or T-Mobile)</li></ul><p>(Types Could include)</p><p>1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Fire Alarms</p><p>2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Alarm (Security aka Burg)</p><p>3.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Elevator</p><p>4.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Fax</p><p>5.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Escalators</p><p>6.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Call Boxes</p><ul><li>Using a BUTT SET, attach clips to the 66-Block or trace wires from RJ31X on Fire or Burg and determine which phone numbers are active, what the phone numbers are and what devices they are connected to. (*Call your cell from your Buttsett, sometimes panel may need to be in test mode to make accurate calls.)</li><li>Label each of these lines with the phone number if not already labeled. Document for SimpleCom.</li><li>Determine the existing fire panel model and type including any security panels.</li><li>Perform a Cellular Site Survey to determine signal and throughput</li><li>Locate possible mounting and installation location of new enclosure and 66 block to provide new dial tone.</li><li>Look for existing internet connection from customers firewall. Fortinet or Meraki to connect a cable from to provide 2nd internet connection to the enclosure.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Required documentation includes: (See FN Task List)</strong></p><ul><li>Pictures of the Telco Room and 66-Block, Completed FormStack and all Field Nation Tasks Completed before payment is issued.</li><li>Pictures (screenshots) of the available throughput (www.SpeedTest.net) on Cellular carrier. (Verizon is Preferred.)</li><li>Pictures related to the proposed installation of new equipment and where this equipment will be mounted.</li><li>Any new lines that need to be ran and the distances.</li><li><strong>Technician MUST fill out the Formstack and all fields are required - this should provide all that is asked above</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>MUST FILL OUT THIS FORM:</strong>https://SimpleCom.formstack.com/forms/pots_site_survey_report_unitedstates</p><p><strong>Please see attached Work Order for more specific documentation.</strong></p>","markdown":"**Onsite Contact: Mel Gower**\n\nCore Network Services\n\nIBM CIO Network Reliability Engineering\n\n+1 919 543 1234 Office\n\n+1 919 279 0987 mobile\n\n**Technical Contact:**\n\n**To Provide more Details:**\n\n- We will be looking to install a POTS replacement solution that can be from 1-8 lines per site. This solution is a enclosure style with a 66 block. It operates on cellular and a internet connection from the customers network.\n- This specific site has a range of line types. They have phone numbers but do not know what location these numbers go to.\n- Identify if any Lines will need to be roughed in or ran for internet or POTS from any other locations or areas to where we can install solution. (IDF, MDF, Maintenance Room.) See attached document for example images of system.\n- We will be looking for 3-4 line types and of those devices that have active POTS lines. Specifically Elevators, Fire Panels, Security, Fax and a few Escalators for this customer. If the lines are live, tagging them and list the number with label maker. Customer should have no more than 3-4 lines per site.\n- We have notes in the documentation attached on how to achieve the information we need. There will be a technical contact on call you need to check in with and will need to collaborate with from SimpleCom if you feel you need that help. But you will be required to check in and out with possible text message communications with our engineers once your onsite.\n- You will need to know how to send text messages, complete and screen shot cellular speed tests from your phone, required to bring a butt sett, fox and hound to trace telephone lines and a ladder if you need to look above ceiling tiles. Label Maker and if any of these things you do not have we could deduct 10% from the ticket.\n- We will need the formstack form link completed for each location about these lines while onsite NOT AFTER. This will be checked to confirm you have submitted it before you leave.\n- FOLLOW FORMSTACK & FN TASK LIST. Documents Attached for Reference.\n- We have notified the site managers of the scheduled visit. Its important your at the site checked in at your specified time. (If you are late please call the SimpleCom contact on the ticket NOT the store.)\n- The locations of the phone lines may be in the same office or building as the customer but in certain locations they may be in other locations. Like a shopping mall will require collaboration with the manager to get you into the Mall Telco or building central Dmarc.\n- Some locations the landlord is using phone lines provided by our customer. But that doesn't mean they pay for that line. So its important you reference the phone line excel sheet to identify if this is a line owned by our customer. (attached under client documents.\n- Not every document listed below will be used. But is there for reference information or if the site contact asks.\n\n**This site survey includes the following: (Please see details SOW attached below.)**\n\n- Tone & Trace customers existing Telco Lines. (Find existing lines and if they are line.) Look for available 2x2 area with power, for new POTS enclosure and available WAN port for box from customers LAN.\n- This system will also have a cellular piece made into the box. Cell signal is also important to capture and identify in your mounting location. (Verizon or T-Mobile)\n\n(Types Could include)\n\n1\\. Fire Alarms\n\n2\\. Alarm (Security aka Burg)\n\n3\\. Elevator\n\n4\\. Fax\n\n5\\. Escalators\n\n6\\. Call Boxes\n\n- Using a BUTT SET, attach clips to the 66-Block or trace wires from RJ31X on Fire or Burg and determine which phone numbers are active, what the phone numbers are and what devices they are connected to. (\\*Call your cell from your Buttsett, sometimes panel may need to be in test mode to make accurate calls.)\n- Label each of these lines with the phone number if not already labeled. Document for SimpleCom.\n- Determine the existing fire panel model and type including any security panels.\n- Perform a Cellular Site Survey to determine signal and throughput\n- Locate possible mounting and installation location of new enclosure and 66 block to provide new dial tone.\n- Look for existing internet connection from customers firewall. Fortinet or Meraki to connect a cable from to provide 2nd internet connection to the enclosure.\n\n**Required documentation includes: (See FN Task List)**\n\n- Pictures of the Telco Room and 66-Block, Completed FormStack and all Field Nation Tasks Completed before payment is issued.\n- Pictures (screenshots) of the available throughput (www.SpeedTest.net) on Cellular carrier. (Verizon is Preferred.)\n- Pictures related to the proposed installation of new equipment and where this equipment will be mounted.\n- Any new lines that need to be ran and the distances.\n- **Technician MUST fill out the Formstack and all fields are required - this should provide all that is asked above**\n\n**MUST FILL OUT THIS FORM:**https://SimpleCom.formstack.com/forms/pots_site_survey_report_unitedstates\n\n**Please see attached Work Order for more specific documentation.**","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-24T09:00","end":"2026-09-24T13:00","latestStart":"2026-09-24T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":300},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":75,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":6},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $300 (countered: $300) is below minimum threshold $400"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Miniso"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z",