{"job":{"id":19990385,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TRCA","title":"Service Ticket #299448 - KMS Install - 10-7-26 @ 10:30 PM - Durham, NC","description":{"html":"<p>Our insurance requires all providers dispatched to our jobsites to have Worker’s compensation coverage. If you do not provide proof of this coverage, TRCA will provide this for your site visit, and the cost (listed as a penalty charge) will be applied to all work orders. Work orders will have 1% of labor only deducted from the total pay. Note: travel or materials cost do not apply, the deduction is for labor only. If you have a COI with workers compensation, please let the work order manager know, so we can get a copy of the COI and waive this deduction. The CoI must be received before the work order is placed on Work Done in order for the penalty to be removed.</p><p><br></p><p>****************************************************************</p><p>DISPATCH ETA: 10-07 -26 @ 10:30 PM </p><p>This site will have 11 - KMS monitors</p><p>This should only take 10-12 hours.</p><p><br></p><p>You must read all documentation before arriving on site.</p><p>You must follow the SOW and Sign Off document to the letter.</p><p>You must follow \"pictures needed document\".</p><p>Be sure to take before pictures as well as completion pictures which instructions for are outlined in the SOW.</p><p>Before pictures of each terminal before swap out, to prevent any he said/she said.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>****************************************************************</p><p><br></p><p>TECH MUST CHECK IN AND OUT WITH TRCA @ 940-323-2600</p><p>TECH MUST CALL MARIO CASAS AT <del>************</del> WHEN YOU ARRIVE AND AFTER FIRST TERMINAL INSTALL AND UPON COMPLETION.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>TRCA will call you the day before. You must answer your phone or call back ASAP to confirm that you are still good to go for the morning appointment.</p><p>TRCA will call you 1 to 2 hours prior of time scheduled to confirm again. You must answer you phone again to confirm. This is per our customer.</p><p>****************************************************************** </p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Cheesecake Factory is using a new terminal, the Toshiba 810F terminals. The supporting docs are written specifically for this terminal and show specifically where all of the peripherals will need to be connected and how the terminals are mounted to either the stand or brackets along with the proper cable management</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Project Description &amp; Scope of Work</p><p>Replace all existing PAR M7700 &amp; 6150 Front Desk terminals with Toshiba 810E terminals. </p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>MUST: AFTER EACH TERMINAL INSTALL, TECH MUST CONTACT MARIO CASAS AND SEND PICTURES TO TEST AND GET APPROVAL OF INSTALLATION AND CABLE MANAGEMENT.</p><p>IF IT IS NOT DONE PROPERLY AS PER THE ATTACHED INSTALL GUIDE, THE TECH WILL NEED TO FIX AND CONTACT MARIO AND SEND PICTURES AGAIN. THEN AND ONLY THEN CAN YOU MOVE TO THE NEXT TERMINAL.</p><p>DO NOT INSTALL THE NEXT TERMINAL UNTIL YOU HAVE APPROVAL OF HOW IT SHOULD BE INSTALLED AND TESTED BY MARIO CASAS.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Equipment &amp; Supplies</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Toshiba 810E Terminals (configured and labeled by name)</p><p>Silver Screws for Monitors on Channel</p><p>Long shaft Phillips Screwdriver for tilt brackets</p><p>Velcro (Do NOT use wire ties)</p><p>(9) 7ft Black Patch Cables</p><p>(2) 3ft Black Null Modem for Expo &amp; Runner; (1) GLC Pasta Monitor</p><p>7ft Black Null Modem for FQM</p><p>(6) 90 Degree Power Cord for Channel Power Supplies</p><p>“Extras Bag” This will contain a 10ft CATV &amp; 2 extra 7ft power cables – You will only use these items as needed</p><p>Printer Cable for 810E Runner, Expo &amp; FQM (COM port1) – 3ft RJ45 to DB25M</p><p><br></p><p>Power drill with Philips screwdriver bits will be quicker and work best to install stands</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Charged Camera Phone</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Equipment &amp; Supplies to be Provided by Technician</p><p>Power Drill with Philips screwdriver bits will be quicker and work best to remove/install brackets</p><p>Charged Camera Phone</p><p>Velcro</p><p>Gloves - as some of the terminals may be dirty.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;Scope of Work</p><p>Replace all existing KMS terminals on the Expo &amp; Cook’s line with Toshiba 810E terminals.</p><p>Note: Before disassembling any stations, ask the managers if they currently have issues with any equipment related to this exchange (specifically printers); have them test printing for you (or use their card to do so) so that you do not spend time troubleshooting (previously) broken printers at the end of install.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Arrive at 10:30 PM; check in with the Manager; locate equipment and compare against shipping manifest.</p><p>Replace KMS Monitors, power supplies &amp; CATV cables; organize power, printer and data cables with Velcro.</p><p>Test KMS Monitors &amp; attached peripherals.</p><p>Take front and back pictures of installed equipment.</p><p>Re-box the old equipment in Toshiba boxes and add shipping label; these will go to Homeboys Disposal.</p><p>Walkthrough with manager on duty to validate installation or discuss issues.</p><p>You will work with remote engineer contact Mario Casas with CBS at <del>************</del></p><p>Locate equipment and verify amount on-site; if the number doesn’t match, contact Mario.</p><p>Guests may still be in the restaurant when you arrive; if so, start un-boxing all the equipment in the back of the house in an area not being used by staff or a closed dining room at the management’s discretion.</p><p>There will be cleaners in the restaurant cleaning until morning. We have asked the managers to tell the cleaners to work around you and clean the cooks’ line last; ask managers to remind the cleaners again.</p><p>Start with the Expo line (Runner, Expo, and FQM) and work your way onto the cook’s line.</p><p>If a monitor is powered off, before removing, turn it back on so you know which monitor you are replacing (read the name on the screen, not the sticker, because it is not always correct). Turn off, unplug cables from monitor &amp; place to the side.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Items/Information to Retrieve from Closing Manager</p><p>Arrive on-site at time provided by your project manager; introduce yourself to the Manager on Duty (MOD) as the CBS Technician who will be performing the overnight KMS installation. Let them know you will need the below items before they leave for the night. Ask them to direct you to the shipment of equipment from CBS. Verify the amount against the order detail list; if anything is missing, contact your Project Manager, immediately. Once equipment inventory has been verified and the area you will be working in is closed down for the night (all food/stations are covered) you can begin installing.</p><p>• Manger MAG Card; This will be used for tested after install.</p><p>• Reimaging Thumb Drive; This will only be needed if any terminals do not load properly from PKI SETUP.</p><p>• FedEx Pickup Location; You will need to ask the managers where to put the boxes of old equipment after install.</p><p>• Shipping Tape; This will used to pack up the outgoing equipment, once the installation is complete.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>THIS IS A MUST PICTURES:</p><p>Example pictures show what the installation should look like when complete. There are additional pictures for the POS and KMS that show the testing of the devices and what the expectation is once those devices have been installed. As requested, the tech should be taking a picture of each station as that station is completed and sending those pictures immediately to Mario Casas for his review. This is to avoid any issues with asking for pictures after the tech has left the site and should also avoid any issues or questions about cable management with the terminals that are being installed.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Equipment Disposal</p><p>Box the 7700 &amp; 6150 PAR equipment, when possible, always pack 2 par terminals, power supplies and data cables ONLY in 1 Toshiba 810 box with protective covering.</p><p>Ask Manager for packaging tape. Seal and attach the provided UPS shipping label over the old label for Homeboy’s disposal. OST will contact UPS to schedule pick up.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Pictures:</p><p>NOTE: - Need before and after pictures of each terminal and cable management. THIS IS A MUST</p><p>Take Pictures (Pictures are VERY IMPORTANT and used throughout the year for troubleshoot &amp; remodels)</p><p>- At each location take a full front &amp; back view of monitors &amp; brackets plus cable organization.</p><p>- E-mail pictures or upload to pmt@trca.com before leaving site.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>Cheesecake Factory has asked us to relay to the techs doing the work is that they want clear pictures of work completed. The docs I have address what kind of pictures we need for each TLP completed. Cheesecake Factory is also asking that we submit pictures to them with 24 hours of completion of the TLP. We would greatly appreciate if you could assist us in getting these pictures submitted in a timely manner.</p>","markdown":"Our insurance requires all providers dispatched to our jobsites to have Worker’s compensation coverage. If you do not provide proof of this coverage, TRCA will provide this for your site visit, and the cost (listed as a penalty charge) will be applied to all work orders. Work orders will have 1% of labor only deducted from the total pay. Note: travel or materials cost do not apply, the deduction is for labor only. If you have a COI with workers compensation, please let the work order manager know, so we can get a copy of the COI and waive this deduction. The CoI must be received before the work order is placed on Work Done in order for the penalty to be removed.\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nDISPATCH ETA: 10-07 -26 @ 10:30 PM\n\nThis site will have 11 - KMS monitors\n\nThis should only take 10-12 hours.\n\nYou must read all documentation before arriving on site.\n\nYou must follow the SOW and Sign Off document to the letter.\n\nYou must follow \"pictures needed document\".\n\nBe sure to take before pictures as well as completion pictures which instructions for are outlined in the SOW.\n\nBefore pictures of each terminal before swap out, to prevent any he said/she said.\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nTECH MUST CHECK IN AND OUT WITH TRCA @ 940-323-2600\n\nTECH MUST CALL MARIO CASAS AT \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* WHEN YOU ARRIVE AND AFTER FIRST TERMINAL INSTALL AND UPON COMPLETION.\n\nTRCA will call you the day before. You must answer your phone or call back ASAP to confirm that you are still good to go for the morning appointment.\n\nTRCA will call you 1 to 2 hours prior of time scheduled to confirm again. You must answer you phone again to confirm. This is per our customer.\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nCheesecake Factory is using a new terminal, the Toshiba 810F terminals. The supporting docs are written specifically for this terminal and show specifically where all of the peripherals will need to be connected and how the terminals are mounted to either the stand or brackets along with the proper cable management\n\nProject Description & Scope of Work\n\nReplace all existing PAR M7700 & 6150 Front Desk terminals with Toshiba 810E terminals.\n\nMUST: AFTER EACH TERMINAL INSTALL, TECH MUST CONTACT MARIO CASAS AND SEND PICTURES TO TEST AND GET APPROVAL OF INSTALLATION AND CABLE MANAGEMENT.\n\nIF IT IS NOT DONE PROPERLY AS PER THE ATTACHED INSTALL GUIDE, THE TECH WILL NEED TO FIX AND CONTACT MARIO AND SEND PICTURES AGAIN. THEN AND ONLY THEN CAN YOU MOVE TO THE NEXT TERMINAL.\n\nDO NOT INSTALL THE NEXT TERMINAL UNTIL YOU HAVE APPROVAL OF HOW IT SHOULD BE INSTALLED AND TESTED BY MARIO CASAS.\n\nEquipment & Supplies\n\nToshiba 810E Terminals (configured and labeled by name)\n\nSilver Screws for Monitors on Channel\n\nLong shaft Phillips Screwdriver for tilt brackets\n\nVelcro (Do NOT use wire ties)\n\n(9) 7ft Black Patch Cables\n\n(2) 3ft Black Null Modem for Expo & Runner; (1) GLC Pasta Monitor\n\n7ft Black Null Modem for FQM\n\n(6) 90 Degree Power Cord for Channel Power Supplies\n\n“Extras Bag” This will contain a 10ft CATV & 2 extra 7ft power cables – You will only use these items as needed\n\nPrinter Cable for 810E Runner, Expo & FQM (COM port1) – 3ft RJ45 to DB25M\n\nPower drill with Philips screwdriver bits will be quicker and work best to install stands\n\nCharged Camera Phone\n\nEquipment & Supplies to be Provided by Technician\n\nPower Drill with Philips screwdriver bits will be quicker and work best to remove/install brackets\n\nCharged Camera Phone\n\nVelcro\n\nGloves - as some of the terminals may be dirty.\n\n Scope of Work\n\nReplace all existing KMS terminals on the Expo & Cook’s line with Toshiba 810E terminals.\n\nNote: Before disassembling any stations, ask the managers if they currently have issues with any equipment related to this exchange (specifically printers); have them test printing for you (or use their card to do so) so that you do not spend time troubleshooting (previously) broken printers at the end of install.\n\nArrive at 10:30 PM; check in with the Manager; locate equipment and compare against shipping manifest.\n\nReplace KMS Monitors, power supplies & CATV cables; organize power, printer and data cables with Velcro.\n\nTest KMS Monitors & attached peripherals.\n\nTake front and back pictures of installed equipment.\n\nRe-box the old equipment in Toshiba boxes and add shipping label; these will go to Homeboys Disposal.\n\nWalkthrough with manager on duty to validate installation or discuss issues.\n\nYou will work with remote engineer contact Mario Casas with CBS at \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\nLocate equipment and verify amount on-site; if the number doesn’t match, contact Mario.\n\nGuests may still be in the restaurant when you arrive; if so, start un-boxing all the equipment in the back of the house in an area not being used by staff or a closed dining room at the management’s discretion.\n\nThere will be cleaners in the restaurant cleaning until morning. We have asked the managers to tell the cleaners to work around you and clean the cooks’ line last; ask managers to remind the cleaners again.\n\nStart with the Expo line (Runner, Expo, and FQM) and work your way onto the cook’s line.\n\nIf a monitor is powered off, before removing, turn it back on so you know which monitor you are replacing (read the name on the screen, not the sticker, because it is not always correct). Turn off, unplug cables from monitor & place to the side.\n\nItems/Information to Retrieve from Closing Manager\n\nArrive on-site at time provided by your project manager; introduce yourself to the Manager on Duty (MOD) as the CBS Technician who will be performing the overnight KMS installation. Let them know you will need the below items before they leave for the night. Ask them to direct you to the shipment of equipment from CBS. Verify the amount against the order detail list; if anything is missing, contact your Project Manager, immediately. Once equipment inventory has been verified and the area you will be working in is closed down for the night (all food/stations are covered) you can begin installing.\n\n• Manger MAG Card; This will be used for tested after install.\n\n• Reimaging Thumb Drive; This will only be needed if any terminals do not load properly from PKI SETUP.\n\n• FedEx Pickup Location; You will need to ask the managers where to put the boxes of old equipment after install.\n\n• Shipping Tape; This will used to pack up the outgoing equipment, once the installation is complete.\n\nTHIS IS A MUST PICTURES:\n\nExample pictures show what the installation should look like when complete. There are additional pictures for the POS and KMS that show the testing of the devices and what the expectation is once those devices have been installed. As requested, the tech should be taking a picture of each station as that station is completed and sending those pictures immediately to Mario Casas for his review. This is to avoid any issues with asking for pictures after the tech has left the site and should also avoid any issues or questions about cable management with the terminals that are being installed.\n\nEquipment Disposal\n\nBox the 7700 & 6150 PAR equipment, when possible, always pack 2 par terminals, power supplies and data cables ONLY in 1 Toshiba 810 box with protective covering.\n\nAsk Manager for packaging tape. Seal and attach the provided UPS shipping label over the old label for Homeboy’s disposal. OST will contact UPS to schedule pick up.\n\nPictures:\n\nNOTE: - Need before and after pictures of each terminal and cable management. THIS IS A MUST\n\nTake Pictures (Pictures are VERY IMPORTANT and used throughout the year for troubleshoot & remodels)\n\n\\- At each location take a full front & back view of monitors & brackets plus cable organization.\n\n\\- E-mail pictures or upload to pmt@trca.com before leaving site.\n\nCheesecake Factory has asked us to relay to the techs doing the work is that they want clear pictures of work completed. The docs I have address what kind of pictures we need for each TLP completed. Cheesecake Factory is also asking that we submit pictures to them with 24 hours of completion of the TLP. We would greatly appreciate if you could assist us in getting these pictures submitted in a timely manner.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-07T22:30","end":"2026-10-07T34:30"},"payRange":{"min":57,"max":627},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":12,"distance":11},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No in-hours counter slot available\nRequested: Wed, Oct 7, 10:30 PM\nChecked: Wed, Oct 7, Thu, Oct 8, Fri, Oct 9 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-07T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.0