{"job":{"id":20005847,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"TechNet Partners","title":"Technician Needed with Tools to Test and Repair Guest Room Cable Runs – Raleigh, NC | 8495-092126 / TBD / 18899683","description":{"html":"<p>TechNet Contact - NationalSC@technetpartners.com</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Note: <strong>Do not exceed 15 minutes</strong> to complete all remaining tasks after the service is completed or remote assistance has ended</li>\n<li>Note: <strong>Each Visit corresponds to a single detailed summary</strong> explaining the activities conducted on site to validate the time spent before checking out.</li>\n<li>Note: Ensure that a note is added to this ticket to<strong>specify whether a follow-up visit is needed</strong> and its reason.</li>\n<li>Note: After installation or repair, <strong>the job must be tested and delivered to the customer</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Title</strong>: Technician Needed with Tools to Test and Repair Guest Room Cable Runs – Raleigh, NC | 8495-092126 / TBD / 18899683</p>\n<p><strong>Type of Work</strong>: Networking</p>\n<p><strong>Schedule</strong>: September 22, 2026 – ASAP (01:00EDT)</p>\n<p><strong>Site Name &amp; Address</strong>: Hilton Garden Inn Raleigh Crabtree, 3912 Arrow Drive, Raleigh, NC 27612, United States</p>\n<p><strong>WO / SA / Case</strong>: WO#: 8495-092126 / SA#: TBD / Case#: 18899683</p>\n<p><strong>Contact Details</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Site POC</strong>: Jenn Watson, (919) 819-2361, jenn.watson@hilton.com</li>\n<li><strong>Engineer</strong>: Support Team | TECHNET</li>\n<li><strong>Technician</strong>: TBD, TBD, TBD (Please Acknowledge)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Scope of Work</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Technician must call the Support Team before beginning any work on this work order.</li>\n<li>Test cable runs between MDF/IDF rooms and wall ports in all 149 guest rooms.</li>\n<li>Coordinate guest room access with Jenn Watson prior to testing.</li>\n<li>Use a MicroScanner or equivalent cable testing device on all existing cable runs.</li>\n<li>Identify and document any faulty cable pairs, damaged terminations, or connectivity issues.</li>\n<li>Repair faulty cable pairs where possible.</li>\n<li>Re-punch, re-terminate, replace patch cables, and/or repair cable runs as required.</li>\n<li>Perform additional troubleshooting to resolve remaining connectivity or speed issues.</li>\n<li>Verify switch connectivity and port status during testing.</li>\n<li>Test cabling associated with the following switches:</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">HLT-RDUCV-350-MDF-CS01 (MAC: 34:56:fe:ab:92:1c)</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">HLT-RDUCV-350-MDF-AS01 (MAC: f8:9e:28:ee:e2:65)</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">HLT-RDUCV-350-IDF1-AS02-1 (MAC: a8:46:9d:bf:37:15)</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">HLT-RDUCV-350-IDF1-AS02-2 (MAC: f8:9e:28:ee:f4:11)</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">HLT-RDUCV-350-IDF1-AS02-3 (MAC: f8:9e:28:ee:f6:1b)</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">HLT-RDUCV-350-IDF1-AS02-4 (MAC: f8:9e:28:ef:03:3f)</li>\n<li>Take clear photos of all closets/work areas before and after any cable moves or repairs.</li>\n<li>Email diagnostic findings and picture documentation to helpdesk@safetynetaccess.com.</li>\n<li>Use subject line format: \"Picture Documentation for WO8495-092126\".</li>\n<li>Document all repairs, cable labeling, testing results, and final status.</li>\n<li>Provide photos and completion notes after the job is done.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Asset &amp; Location</strong>: Guest Room Cable Runs, MDF &amp; IDF Network Infrastructure – Hilton Garden Inn Raleigh Crabtree</p>\n<p><strong>Tools Required</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Laptop (Windows) and power adapter</li>\n<li>Ethernet adapter</li>\n<li>Ethernet cable</li>\n<li>Mobile hotspot (cellphone data)</li>\n<li>Cellphone with camera</li>\n<li>Wire/Cable tester (capable of test Gigabit ethernet connections)</li>\n<li>Tone generator</li>\n<li>Console cable and USB adapter</li>\n<li>Label maker</li>\n<li>Crimper</li>\n<li>RJ45 plugs (cat5e and cat6)</li>\n<li>Keystone jacks (cat5e and cat6)</li>\n<li>Voltage tester</li>\n<li>Screwdrivers and security bits</li>\n<li>MicroScanner or equivalent cable tester/certifier</li>\n<li>Fluke, Lantek, Klein Tools tester, or equivalent</li>\n<li>Toner and probe kit</li>\n<li>Digital multimeter</li>\n<li>Punch-down tool</li>\n<li>Spare Ethernet patch cables</li>\n<li>Cisco console cable</li>\n<li><em>If testing fiber:</em> Laser to verify light continuity, fiber tester, and cleaning kit.</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"TechNet Contact - NationalSC@technetpartners.com\n\n- Note: **Do not exceed 15 minutes** to complete all remaining tasks after the service is completed or remote assistance has ended\n- Note: **Each Visit corresponds to a single detailed summary** explaining the activities conducted on site to validate the time spent before checking out.\n- Note: Ensure that a note is added to this ticket to**specify whether a follow-up visit is needed** and its reason.\n- Note: After installation or repair, **the job must be tested and delivered to the customer**.\n\n**Title**: Technician Needed with Tools to Test and Repair Guest Room Cable Runs – Raleigh, NC | 8495-092126 / TBD / 18899683\n\n**Type of Work**: Networking\n\n**Schedule**: September 22, 2026 – ASAP (01:00EDT)\n\n**Site Name & Address**: Hilton Garden Inn Raleigh Crabtree, 3912 Arrow Drive, Raleigh, NC 27612, United States\n\n**WO / SA / Case**: WO#: 8495-092126 / SA#: TBD / Case#: 18899683\n\n**Contact Details**:\n\n- **Site POC**: Jenn Watson, (919) 819-2361, jenn.watson@hilton.com\n- **Engineer**: Support Team | TECHNET\n- **Technician**: TBD, TBD, TBD (Please Acknowledge)\n\n**Scope of Work**:\n\n- Technician must call the Support Team before beginning any work on this work order.\n- Test cable runs between MDF/IDF rooms and wall ports in all 149 guest rooms.\n- Coordinate guest room access with Jenn Watson prior to testing.\n- Use a MicroScanner or equivalent cable testing device on all existing cable runs.\n- Identify and document any faulty cable pairs, damaged terminations, or connectivity issues.\n- Repair faulty cable pairs where possible.\n- Re-punch, re-terminate, replace patch cables, and/or repair cable runs as required.\n- Perform additional troubleshooting to resolve remaining connectivity or speed issues.\n- Verify switch connectivity and port status during testing.\n- Test cabling associated with the following switches:\n- HLT-RDUCV-350-MDF-CS01 (MAC: 34:56:fe:ab:92:1c)\n- HLT-RDUCV-350-MDF-AS01 (MAC: f8:9e:28:ee:e2:65)\n- HLT-RDUCV-350-IDF1-AS02-1 (MAC: a8:46:9d:bf:37:15)\n- HLT-RDUCV-350-IDF1-AS02-2 (MAC: f8:9e:28:ee:f4:11)\n- HLT-RDUCV-350-IDF1-AS02-3 (MAC: f8:9e:28:ee:f6:1b)\n- HLT-RDUCV-350-IDF1-AS02-4 (MAC: f8:9e:28:ef:03:3f)\n- Take clear photos of all closets/work areas before and after any cable moves or repairs.\n- Email diagnostic findings and picture documentation to helpdesk@safetynetaccess.com.\n- Use subject line format: \"Picture Documentation for WO8495-092126\".\n- Document all repairs, cable labeling, testing results, and final status.\n- Provide photos and completion notes after the job is done.\n\n**Asset & Location**: Guest Room Cable Runs, MDF & IDF Network Infrastructure – Hilton Garden Inn Raleigh Crabtree\n\n**Tools Required**:\n\n- Laptop (Windows) and power adapter\n- Ethernet adapter\n- Ethernet cable\n- Mobile hotspot (cellphone data)\n- Cellphone with camera\n- Wire/Cable tester (capable of test Gigabit ethernet connections)\n- Tone generator\n- Console cable and USB adapter\n- Label maker\n- Crimper\n- RJ45 plugs (cat5e and cat6)\n- Keystone jacks (cat5e and cat6)\n- Voltage tester\n- Screwdrivers and security bits\n- MicroScanner or equivalent cable tester/certifier\n- Fluke, Lantek, Klein Tools tester, or equivalent\n- Toner and probe kit\n- Digital multimeter\n- Punch-down tool\n- Spare Ethernet patch cables\n- Cisco console cable\n- *If testing fiber:* Laser to verify light continuity, fiber tester, and cleaning kit.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-22T13:00","end":"2026-09-22T15:00","latestStart":"2026-09-22T14:30"},"payRange":{"min":150,"max":300},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":150},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":75}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":5},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 9/22/2026, 1:00:00 PM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T17:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-22T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"gap"},{"start":"2026-09-23T02:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T03:00:00.000Z","summary":"Pay Bills"},{"start":"2026-09-23T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Miniso"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T1