{"job":{"id":19995462,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Tsunami USA LLC","title":"Troubleshoot Pole Mounted IP Camera in Oxford, NC","description":{"html":"<p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Overview:</strong></p><ul><li>Communication with TSUNAMI Support will be necessary to complete tickets as well as pictures in many cases.</li><li>The technician will need to be able to climb a ladder with the necessary tools and equipment.</li><li>TSUNAMI Support will take care of all shipping costs associated with replacement parts, etc.</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Dress Code:</strong></p><ul><li>Professional Attire</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Tools Required:</strong><em style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">&nbsp;</em></p><ul><li>16-25’ Extension ladder</li><li>&nbsp;Laptop with Ethernet Port</li><li>&nbsp;Hotspot for Internet</li><li>Multimeter</li><li>Hand tools</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Scope of Work:</strong></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">***(SEE TASKS section For Job Checklist)</strong></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><em>On-Site Tasks&nbsp;</em></strong></p><ul><li>Check-in to work order, contact TSUNAMI Support via phone, and introduce yourself to the onsite contact (when applicable). You represent TSUNAMI USA while onsite.</li><li>The TSUNAMI is a self-contained surveillance system that are typically installed 15 – 20 feet on a utility pole. Troubleshooting the TSUNAMI will consist of climbing the ladder, checking the breaker box for power, checking the exterior of the TSUNAMI for failures, then checking the interior for failures.</li><li>Tech is responsible for their own ladder.</li><li>TSUNAMI coordinates, badge, and nearest address will be located in the confidential section.</li><li>Service Technicians repair or replace modules, subassemblies and components of the TSUNAMI Surveillance System.</li><li>TSUNAMI Surveillance System in good operating condition as determined by the specifications.</li><li>TSUNAMI Support will provide all necessary parts needed for replacement.&nbsp;</li><li>Hardware to be maintained include but are not limited to IP cameras, routers, switches, hard drives, network video recorders, ptz cameras, LPR cameras, cables, and antennas.</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"><em>Required On-Site Deliverables&nbsp;</em></strong></p><ul><li>Check-out of work order</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Communication Directory:&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li>Tech must contact TSUNAMI Support for further instructions.</li><li>Support Line: 865-565-5000</li><li>Support Hours: 9 am - 5 pm</li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy</strong></p><ul><li>Any travel expenses must be applied as a counter-offer when requesting the work in order to get approved</li><li>Any additional hours must be requested and approved by WO Manager</li></ul>","markdown":"**Overview:**\n\n- Communication with TSUNAMI Support will be necessary to complete tickets as well as pictures in many cases.\n- The technician will need to be able to climb a ladder with the necessary tools and equipment.\n- TSUNAMI Support will take care of all shipping costs associated with replacement parts, etc.\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\n- Professional Attire\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- 16-25’ Extension ladder\n- Laptop with Ethernet Port\n- Hotspot for Internet\n- Multimeter\n- Hand tools\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\n**\\*\\*\\*(SEE TASKS section For Job Checklist)**\n\n***On-Site Tasks***\n\n- Check-in to work order, contact TSUNAMI Support via phone, and introduce yourself to the onsite contact (when applicable). You represent TSUNAMI USA while onsite.\n- The TSUNAMI is a self-contained surveillance system that are typically installed 15 – 20 feet on a utility pole. Troubleshooting the TSUNAMI will consist of climbing the ladder, checking the breaker box for power, checking the exterior of the TSUNAMI for failures, then checking the interior for failures.\n- Tech is responsible for their own ladder.\n- TSUNAMI coordinates, badge, and nearest address will be located in the confidential section.\n- Service Technicians repair or replace modules, subassemblies and components of the TSUNAMI Surveillance System.\n- TSUNAMI Surveillance System in good operating condition as determined by the specifications.\n- TSUNAMI Support will provide all necessary parts needed for replacement.\n- Hardware to be maintained include but are not limited to IP cameras, routers, switches, hard drives, network video recorders, ptz cameras, LPR cameras, cables, and antennas.\n\n***Required On-Site Deliverables***\n\n- Check-out of work order\n\n**Communication Directory:**\n\n- Tech must contact TSUNAMI Support for further instructions.\n- Support Line: 865-565-5000\n- Support Hours: 9 am - 5 pm\n\n**Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy**\n\n- Any travel expenses must be applied as a counter-offer when requesting the work in order to get approved\n- Any additional hours must be requested and approved by WO Manager","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-22T09:00","end":"2026-09-22T10:30","latestStart":"2026-09-22T15:00"},"payRange":{"min":90,"max":135},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":90,"estLaborHours":1.5,"distance":30},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"WO_IN_PAST","rejectDetails":"Requested start 9/22/2026, 9:00:00 AM is in the past"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T17:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-22T15:00