{"job":{"id":19994776,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"SHI - Corp Services","title":"**MUST HAVE REAL ID** Thin client (3) | Pin Pad (3) | Printer | Circuit Cutover - Removal | Install | Configuration","description":{"html":"<p>**MUST HAVE REAL ID, VALID INSURANCE &amp; REGISTRATION FOR BASE ACCESS**</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Scope Summary:</u></strong></p>\n<p>Perform inventory, remove old, install new, Configure and test the following:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Pin Pads</li>\n<li>Printer</li>\n<li>Thin Clients</li>\n<li>Circuit Cutover</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>**All work outlined below has been approved; any work out-of-scope will require authorization from the Work Order Manager.</strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>PRE-SITE INSTRUCTIONS</u></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>MUST Review INSTALL INSTRUCTIONS before going onsite (Attached)</li>\n<li>MUST print Checkout Form (Attached)&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Review this Work Order in its entirety</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Verify Inventory with inventory list attached to work order.&nbsp;Note – pin pads are shipped separately</p>\n<p><strong><u>PIN PADS:</u></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Verify Pin Pads</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Work order manager will give you list of pin pad serials and MACs</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Before installing - Make sure the cords in the box go with the pin pad in same box – the cords have the MAC addresses on them</li>\n<li>Remove old pin pad #1 and install NEW pin pad #1</li>\n<li>Activate Pin Pad #1 – text work order manager when online, wait for activation code&nbsp;</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Activation code will be received from support to work order manager.&nbsp;A pop up will show on the pin pad when ready to enter the code</li>\n<li>Install and Activate rest of Pin Pads: PP2, PP3, etc. text work order manager when ready for activation codes.&nbsp;</li>\n<li>Upload pictures of new Pin Pads (label pictures, PP1, PP2, ETC)</li>\n<li>Collect all old pin pads, upload a photo, and place them in the box.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong><u>PRINTER:</u></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Install the printer – replace old printer that has the fax line</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Notify work order manager when printer is plugged into network and fax line connected</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">For the initial set up questions – answer NO to all</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Enable health apps – NO</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Enable print from USB – NO</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Enable web updates – NO</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Enable Auto send – NO</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">DO NOT update any fax settings</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Upload picture of old printer + serial (label picture)</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Upload picture of new printer + serial (label picture)</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Support configures the printer remotely – work order manager will let you know when to send a test fax.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Test Fax number:&nbsp;470-300-796</li>\n</ol>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Thin Clients</u></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Install all thin clients.</li>\n<li>Identify each thin client (TC):</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Existing TC numbers can be found in the bottom corner of the desktop screen.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">New TC numbers are listed on the device box.</li>\n<li>Stage all thin clients at their designated workstations. Installation order does not matter.</li>\n<li>Take a photo of the old thin clients after they have been removed and stacked.</li>\n<li>Take a photo of each new thin client, ensuring the white asset tag is clearly visible.</li>\n<li>Have store associates log in as each thin client is installed using:</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Username: [Store Number]@nationalvision.com</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Password: Store email password</li>\n<li>Verify access to:</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Citrix</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">SDS</li>\n<li>Notify the Work Order Manager when all or most thin clients have been installed.</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Support will run the required printer scripts.</li>\n<li>Wait for approval from the Work Order Manager before beginning printer testing.</li>\n<li>Have associates perform test printing.</li>\n<li>Report any issues immediately to the Work Order Manager.</li>\n<li>Review the new scan process with store associates:</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">On the printer home screen, navigate to: Quicksets → papercapture-xxxx-load</li>\n</ol>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>PACK UP EQUIPMENT</u></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>All <strong>OLD equipment</strong> - pack in box, SEAL with tape and mark on box <strong>\"SHIP TO GEORGIA COMPUTERS\"</strong></li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Upload picture&nbsp;</li>\n<li>ANY NEW UN-USED/EXTRA EQUIPMENT – will be sent back to SHI “Knox”</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Upload picture of serial numbers</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Mark on checkout list which equipment needs to be sent back</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Place in SEPARATE BOX and give to manager</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Shipping label will be sent to manager</li>\n</ol>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>&nbsp;DELIVERABLES:</strong> (see examples on last page)</p>\n<p>LABEL EACH PICTURE WITH STORE NUMBER – DEVICE NUMBER - NEW OR OLD&nbsp;</p>\n<p>• Group old Pin Pads together and upload picture</p>\n<p>• Take picture of each NEW pin pad</p>\n<p>• Stack old TC to side and upload picture</p>\n<p>• Take picture of NEW TC showing bar code and monitor logged in&nbsp;</p>\n<p>• Take picture of old printer and serial</p>\n<p>• Take picture of new printer, serial, test fax</p>\n<p>• Take picture of boxed up OLD equipment</p>\n<p>• Take picture of NEW Un-used / EXTRA equipment being sent back to SHI “Knox”</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>NOTE:</strong> IF you need to join the “bridge” – here is the number.&nbsp;Your work order manager will let you know if you need to join call to troubleshoot with support.&nbsp;<del>** ************************</del></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Required Tools Needed:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Laptop</li>\n<li>Console cable</li>\n<li>Cable Toner</li>\n<li>Keystones</li>\n<li>Crimper</li>\n<li>Patch Cables</li>\n<li>Working Label Maker - with labels</li>\n<li>Cat6 Cable - approx. 200ft</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Escalation Process:</u></strong></p>\n<p>Please call the work order manager for any questions or issues while on-site</p>\n<p><strong><u>Dress Code:</u></strong></p>\n<p>Polo, Non-ripped Jeans, closed-toe shoes&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong><u>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Payment Policy:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Time onsite above estimate must be approved by work order manager BEFORE the time has lapsed</li>\n<li>Travel expense must be approved PRIOR to accepting job</li>\n<li>Material reimbursement will be approved at the cost below</li>\n<li>Failure to CORRECTLY complete the tasks listed in the work order - and/or leaving site without contacting WO Manager - will result in a minimum 25% deduction of payment.&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>Material Reimbursement:</u></strong></p>\n<p>Cat6 Cables .52 cents per foot</p>\n<p>Cat6 Patch cables 1-3ft $4.60 /ea</p>\n<p>Cat6 Patch cables 10ft + $8.00/ea</p>\n<p>Faceplate $3.50 / ea</p>\n<p>Keystones $5.00/ea</p>\n<p>Cable ends $2.50/ea</p>","markdown":"\\*\\*MUST HAVE REAL ID, VALID INSURANCE & REGISTRATION FOR BASE ACCESS\\*\\*\n\n**Scope Summary:**\n\nPerform inventory, remove old, install new, Configure and test the following:\n\n- Pin Pads\n- Printer\n- Thin Clients\n- Circuit Cutover\n\n**\\*\\*All work outlined below has been approved; any work out-of-scope will require authorization from the Work Order Manager.**\n\n**PRE-SITE INSTRUCTIONS**\n\n1. MUST Review INSTALL INSTRUCTIONS before going onsite (Attached)\n2. MUST print Checkout Form (Attached)\n3. Review this Work Order in its entirety\n\nVerify Inventory with inventory list attached to work order. Note – pin pads are shipped separately\n\n**PIN PADS:**\n\n1. Verify Pin Pads\n2. Work order manager will give you list of pin pad serials and MACs\n3. Before installing - Make sure the cords in the box go with the pin pad in same box – the cords have the MAC addresses on them\n4. Remove old pin pad #1 and install NEW pin pad #1\n5. Activate Pin Pad #1 – text work order manager when online, wait for activation code\n6. Activation code will be received from support to work order manager. A pop up will show on the pin pad when ready to enter the code\n7. Install and Activate rest of Pin Pads: PP2, PP3, etc. text work order manager when ready for activation codes.\n8. Upload pictures of new Pin Pads (label pictures, PP1, PP2, ETC)\n9. Collect all old pin pads, upload a photo, and place them in the box.\n\n**PRINTER:**\n\n1. Install the printer – replace old printer that has the fax line\n2. Notify work order manager when printer is plugged into network and fax line connected\n3. For the initial set up questions – answer NO to all\n4. Enable health apps – NO\n5. Enable print from USB – NO\n6. Enable web updates – NO\n7. Enable Auto send – NO\n8. DO NOT update any fax settings\n9. Upload picture of old printer + serial (label picture)\n10. Upload picture of new printer + serial (label picture)\n11. Support configures the printer remotely – work order manager will let you know when to send a test fax.\n12. Test Fax number: 470-300-796\n\n**Thin Clients**\n\n1. Install all thin clients.\n2. Identify each thin client (TC):\n3. Existing TC numbers can be found in the bottom corner of the desktop screen.\n4. New TC numbers are listed on the device box.\n5. Stage all thin clients at their designated workstations. Installation order does not matter.\n6. Take a photo of the old thin clients after they have been removed and stacked.\n7. Take a photo of each new thin client, ensuring the white asset tag is clearly visible.\n8. Have store associates log in as each thin client is installed using:\n9. Username: \\[Store Number\\]@nationalvision.com\n10. Password: Store email password\n11. Verify access to:\n12. Citrix\n13. SDS\n14. Notify the Work Order Manager when all or most thin clients have been installed.\n15. Support will run the required printer scripts.\n16. Wait for approval from the Work Order Manager before beginning printer testing.\n17. Have associates perform test printing.\n18. Report any issues immediately to the Work Order Manager.\n19. Review the new scan process with store associates:\n20. On the printer home screen, navigate to: Quicksets → papercapture-xxxx-load\n\n**PACK UP EQUIPMENT**\n\n1. All **OLD equipment** - pack in box, SEAL with tape and mark on box **\"SHIP TO GEORGIA COMPUTERS\"**\n2. Upload picture\n3. ANY NEW UN-USED/EXTRA EQUIPMENT – will be sent back to SHI “Knox”\n4. Upload picture of serial numbers\n5. Mark on checkout list which equipment needs to be sent back\n6. Place in SEPARATE BOX and give to manager\n7. Shipping label will be sent to manager\n\n **DELIVERABLES:** (see examples on last page)\n\nLABEL EACH PICTURE WITH STORE NUMBER – DEVICE NUMBER - NEW OR OLD\n\n• Group old Pin Pads together and upload picture\n\n• Take picture of each NEW pin pad\n\n• Stack old TC to side and upload picture\n\n• Take picture of NEW TC showing bar code and monitor logged in\n\n• Take picture of old printer and serial\n\n• Take picture of new printer, serial, test fax\n\n• Take picture of boxed up OLD equipment\n\n• Take picture of NEW Un-used / EXTRA equipment being sent back to SHI “Knox”\n\n**NOTE:** IF you need to join the “bridge” – here is the number. Your work order manager will let you know if you need to join call to troubleshoot with support. \\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**Required Tools Needed:**\n\n- Laptop\n- Console cable\n- Cable Toner\n- Keystones\n- Crimper\n- Patch Cables\n- Working Label Maker - with labels\n- Cat6 Cable - approx. 200ft\n\n**Escalation Process:**\n\nPlease call the work order manager for any questions or issues while on-site\n\n**Dress Code:**\n\nPolo, Non-ripped Jeans, closed-toe shoes\n\n**Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Payment Policy:**\n\n- Time onsite above estimate must be approved by work order manager BEFORE the time has lapsed\n- Travel expense must be approved PRIOR to accepting job\n- Material reimbursement will be approved at the cost below\n- Failure to CORRECTLY complete the tasks listed in the work order - and/or leaving site without contacting WO Manager - will result in a minimum 25% deduction of payment.\n\n**Material Reimbursement:**\n\nCat6 Cables .52 cents per foot\n\nCat6 Patch cables 1-3ft $4.60 /ea\n\nCat6 Patch cables 10ft + $8.00/ea\n\nFaceplate $3.50 / ea\n\nKeystones $5.00/ea\n\nCable ends $2.50/ea","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-01T08:00","end":"2026-10-01T10:00"},"payRange":{"min":120,"max":285},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":120},"additional":{"units":2.75,"amount":60}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":51},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $285 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Sw