{"job":{"id":19994179,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Netview Inc.","title":"Install 2 Outdoor AP's & 2 Omni Directional Antennas (2 Techs Required)","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>TECH IS NOT TO COMPLETE ANY WORK OTHER THAN WHAT IS NOTED ON THIS WORK ORDER WITHOUT GETTING APPROVAL FROM NETVIEW FIRST. THIS IS QUOTED AND ANY ADDITIONAL WORK WILL NOT BE PAID IF NOT APPROVED PRIOR TO COMPLETING THE WORK. SITE IS NOT TO ADD ON TO THE SCOPE OF WORK WITHOUT APPROVAL.</u></strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><em>TECH MUST NOTE CONTACT INFORMATION IN CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION ONCE ASSIGNED. TECH CANNOT LEAVE SITE WITHOUT REMOTE SUPPORT VERIFYING WORK IS COMPLETED.</em></strong></p><p><strong>TECH MUST NOTIFY NETVIEW IF THERE ARE DELAYS WHILE WAITING FOR REMOTE SUPPORT SO WE CAN ESCALATE AS SOON AS POSSIBLE TO THE CUSTOMER.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work: </u></strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">Install 2 Access Points and Starlink</strong></p><ul><li>Installation of the two outdoor wireless access points</li><li>Installation of the two omni-directional antennas</li><li>Network cabling required for both access points</li></ul><p><span style=\"color: black;\">Installation details:</span></p><ul><li>A small boom lift can be used both outside and inside the shop bay to run the cable for the AP located on the left rear corner.</li><li>An 8-foot ladder can be used to access the drop ceiling.</li><li>The approximate cable distance from the network rack to the AP on the right side is 80 feet.</li><li>The approximate cable distance to the AP on the left side is 175 feet.</li><li>Both cable runs appear to be straight.</li><li>Fire-rated caulk will be required to seal the cable penetrations; however, the existing cable penetration should already be available.</li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">For the installation, new network cabling will need to be run from the network switch to all three access points. </span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"color: black;\">The estimated cable length for each AP is approximately 250 feet.</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">Tech will need to bring approximately 1000' of Cat6 cable (should take more just in case).</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">Additional required materials and tools listed below.</span></li></ul><p><span style=\"color: rgb(36, 36, 36);\">﻿</span></p><p><strong><u>Additional Notes:</u></strong></p><p>Please ensure all devices are fully charged and in good working order.</p><p>The technician should be familiar with basic network troubleshooting procedures.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Required Tools and Materials (</u></strong><u>will be reimbursed for cables and connectors if used</u><strong><u>):</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong>(1) box of CAT6 Cable </strong></li><li><strong>RJ45's</strong></li><li><strong>Various Cat6 Patch Cables</strong> (3' and/or 6' patch cables)</li><li><strong>Standard Hand Tools</strong> (Screwdrivers, Drill, etc.)</li><li><strong>Standard Cabling Tools</strong></li><li><strong>Velcro for cable management</strong></li><li><strong>Laptop:</strong>&nbsp;With a functioning LAN port and Teams installed.</li><li><strong>Console Cable</strong></li><li><strong>Mobile Hotspot</strong></li><li><strong>Cable Tester</strong></li><li><strong>Ladder</strong>&nbsp;(8'-10' ladder)</li></ul>","markdown":"**TECH IS NOT TO COMPLETE ANY WORK OTHER THAN WHAT IS NOTED ON THIS WORK ORDER WITHOUT GETTING APPROVAL FROM NETVIEW FIRST. THIS IS QUOTED AND ANY ADDITIONAL WORK WILL NOT BE PAID IF NOT APPROVED PRIOR TO COMPLETING THE WORK. SITE IS NOT TO ADD ON TO THE SCOPE OF WORK WITHOUT APPROVAL.**\n\n***TECH MUST NOTE CONTACT INFORMATION IN CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION ONCE ASSIGNED. TECH CANNOT LEAVE SITE WITHOUT REMOTE SUPPORT VERIFYING WORK IS COMPLETED.***\n\n**TECH MUST NOTIFY NETVIEW IF THERE ARE DELAYS WHILE WAITING FOR REMOTE SUPPORT SO WE CAN ESCALATE AS SOON AS POSSIBLE TO THE CUSTOMER.**\n\n**Scope of Work:** **Install 2 Access Points and Starlink**\n\n- Installation of the two outdoor wireless access points\n- Installation of the two omni-directional antennas\n- Network cabling required for both access points\n\nInstallation details:\n\n- A small boom lift can be used both outside and inside the shop bay to run the cable for the AP located on the left rear corner.\n- An 8-foot ladder can be used to access the drop ceiling.\n- The approximate cable distance from the network rack to the AP on the right side is 80 feet.\n- The approximate cable distance to the AP on the left side is 175 feet.\n- Both cable runs appear to be straight.\n- Fire-rated caulk will be required to seal the cable penetrations; however, the existing cable penetration should already be available.\n- For the installation, new network cabling will need to be run from the network switch to all three access points.\n- The estimated cable length for each AP is approximately 250 feet.\n- Tech will need to bring approximately 1000' of Cat6 cable (should take more just in case).\n- Additional required materials and tools listed below.\n\n﻿\n\n**Additional Notes:**\n\nPlease ensure all devices are fully charged and in good working order.\n\nThe technician should be familiar with basic network troubleshooting procedures.\n\n**Required Tools and Materials (**will be reimbursed for cables and connectors if used**):**\n\n- **(1) box of CAT6 Cable**\n- **RJ45's**\n- **Various Cat6 Patch Cables** (3' and/or 6' patch cables)\n- **Standard Hand Tools** (Screwdrivers, Drill, etc.)\n- **Standard Cabling Tools**\n- **Velcro for cable management**\n- **Laptop:** With a functioning LAN port and Teams installed.\n- **Console Cable**\n- **Mobile Hotspot**\n- **Cable Tester**\n- **Ladder** (8'-10' ladder)","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-24T09:00","end":"2026-09-24T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":50,"max":100},"payType":"hourly","payStr