{"job":{"id":19994275,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Cipe Solutions","title":"Service Ticket #218916 - Audio | Amplifier Replacement and Audio Testing","description":{"html":"<p><strong>PLEASE READ THE FOLLOWING CAREFULLY. FAILURE TO COMPLY MAY RESULT IN WITHHELD PAYMENTS</strong></p><p>Call or chat <strong>Activations</strong> for check in as well as more detailed instruction.</p><ul><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">(888)747-9530, Ext. 888</strong></li><li><strong>techonsite.chat</strong></li></ul><br><p><strong>TICKET SUMMARY:</strong> JBL CSA140Z AUDIO AMPLIFIER REPLACEMENT, PREVIOUSLY INSTALLED SPEAKER CIRCUIT DIAGNOSTICS, POWER OUTPUT VERIFICATION &amp; RETURN LOGISTICS STAGING</p><p><br></p><strong>I. PROJECT SUMMARY</strong><p>An audio-experienced technician is required on-site to decommission a defective <strong>JBL CSA140Z Commercial Audio Amplifier</strong> and replace it with a brand-new JBL CSA140Z unit shipped directly to the location.</p><p><br></p><p>Prior to landing wires on the replacement JBL CSA140Z, the technician must conduct a layer-1 circuit audit on all previously installed speaker lines (measuring resistance $\\Omega$ and checking for shorts-to-ground) to ensure line integrity and prevent immediate output stage damage to the new unit. The technician will verify whether the speaker topology is wired for 70V/100V High-Z or 4$\\Omega$/8$\\Omega$ Low-Z operation and set the rear-panel output switch accordingly. Once installed, the technician must verify using a multimeter that the amplifier is outputting AC power correctly across the Euroblock speaker terminals under remote Support direction, perform live test playback, and stage the defective JBL CSA140Z on-site for return shipment.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>AMPLIFIER SAFETY &amp; OUTPUT SWITCH MANDATE:</strong> Always physically power <strong>OFF</strong> the amplifier and isolate utility power before adjusting rear DIP/output switches, splicing, testing, or landing any speaker cabling or Euroblock input/output leads.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>DEFECTIVE ASSET RETURN STAGING MANDATE:</strong> Carefully box up the defective JBL CSA140Z amplifier and its power cord into the shipping packaging from the replacement unit. Affix the return shipping label (if provided) or label the box clearly as <strong>\"DEFECTIVE JBL CSA140Z AMP - STAGED FOR RETURN SHIPMENT.\"</strong> Hand the package directly to the Manager on Duty (MOD) or stage it in the store's designated IT storage area. Do not remove hardware from the property unless explicitly instructed by Support.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>DUAL SIGN-OFF MANDATE:</strong> The technician must receive explicit operational and audio testing confirmation from remote <strong>Activations</strong> and obtain physical/digital sign-off from the on-site <strong>Manager on Duty (MOD)</strong> prior to departing the facility.</p><p><br></p><strong>II. REQUIRED TOOLS &amp; PARTS</strong><ul><li><strong>LAPTOP WITH PHYSICAL ETHERNET PORT &amp; MOBILE HOTSPOT!</strong> (<strong>Absolute Mandatory Requirement</strong> for web interface checks, audio source verification, gateway pings, and telemetry logging)</li><li><strong>Volt Meter / Multimeter &amp; Audio Wire Tester / Cable Toner</strong> (<strong>Mandatory</strong> for measuring speaker line impedance $\\Omega$, short-to-ground faults, and AC signal output voltage)</li><li><strong>Small Precision Screwdriver Set</strong> (<strong>Mandatory</strong> for securing wire leads into JBL Euroblock/Phoenix terminal connectors)</li><li><strong>Audio Interconnect Cabling &amp; Termination Supplies:</strong> Spare 16/2 or 18/2 speaker wire, wire nuts, B-connectors, RCA/3.5mm patch cables, wire strippers, and snips</li><li><strong>Rack/Shelf Mounting Hardware Pack</strong> (Technician stock of standard cage nuts, rack screws, or shelf mounting brackets)</li><li><strong>General Tool Kit w/ Power Drill, Bits, &amp; Drivers</strong></li><li><strong>Cable Management Supplies:</strong> High-quality <strong>Velcro ties</strong>, packaging tape, and permanent marker</li><li><strong>Mobile Smart-Phone</strong> (Required for live on-site check-in/check-out tracking via browser chat)</li></ul><p><br></p><strong>III. ON-SITE EXECUTION STEPS</strong><strong>PHASE 1: ARRIVAL &amp; STRATEGIC ALIGNMENT</strong><ol><li><strong>MANDATORY CHECK-IN:</strong> Visit <strong>CIPE.CHAT</strong> in your mobile device's browser with your Name and Service Ticket #. If you receive no response, contact Dispatch at <strong>(888) 747-9530, Ext. 888</strong>.</li><li><strong>MOD CONTACT:</strong> Meet with the Manager on Duty (MOD). Have them walk you to the main audio/IT rack and collect the newly shipped JBL CSA140Z replacement hardware box.</li><li><strong>SUPPORT ENGAGEMENT:</strong> Call <strong>Activations at (888) 747-9530, Ext. 411</strong>. Review the JBL CSA140Z replacement and speaker circuit testing scope with remote support before touching live equipment.</li></ol><p><br></p><strong>PHASE 2: SPEAKER CIRCUIT DIAGNOSTICS &amp; PRE-SWAP TESTING</strong><ol><li><strong>POWER ISOLATION:</strong> Power <strong>OFF</strong> the defective JBL CSA140Z amplifier and unplug the AC power cord. Unplug the Euroblock speaker output connector from the rear panel.</li><li><strong>SPEAKER LINE AUDIT (CRITICAL):</strong> Set your <strong>multimeter</strong> to measure resistance ($\\Omega$). Measure across positive (+)—negative (-) speaker leads on each previously installed zone:</li></ol><ul><li><strong>70V/100V High-Z Systems:</strong> Verify line resistance matches expected transformer primary load (typically $50\\Omega$ to several hundred $\\Omega$).</li><li><strong>4$\\Omega$/8$\\Omega$ Low-Z Systems:</strong> Verify direct line resistance measures within a safe $4\\Omega$ to $8\\Omega$ range.</li><li><strong>Ground-Fault Test:</strong> Measure resistance from each speaker lead to the rack frame/ground. Any reading below infinity ($\\infty$) indicates a ground fault that must be cleared before connecting the new amp.</li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><strong>DECOMMISSIONING:</strong> Unplug the input signal Euroblock/RCA connectors and unmount the defective JBL CSA140Z chassis from the rack or shelf.</li></ol><p><br></p><strong>PHASE 3: REPLACEMENT JBL CSA140Z INSTALLATION &amp; WIRING</strong><ol><li><strong>REAR OUTPUT SWITCH CONFIGURATION:</strong> Prior to applying power, set the rear-panel output switch on the new JBL CSA140Z to match the verified speaker topology (70V/100V High-Z or 4$\\Omega$/8$\\Omega$ Low-Z) as directed by Support.</li><li><strong>RACK / SHELF MOUNTING:</strong> Securely mount or position the new replacement JBL CSA140Z amplifier in the equipment rack.</li><li><strong>EUROBLOCK TERMINAL INTEGRATION:</strong> Land the input audio source leads and verified speaker lines into the Euroblock terminal connectors. Plug the connectors firmly into the rear panel of the new JBL CSA140Z, ensuring all terminal screws are tight with zero exposed copper strands crossing pins.</li></ol><p><br></p><strong>PHASE 4: POWER OUTPUT VERIFICATION &amp; AUDIO AUDIT</strong><ol><li><strong>POWER RESTORATION:</strong> Connect the AC power lead and power <strong>ON</strong> the replacement JBL CSA140Z. Verify the front master volume ring indicator lights up green. Stay on the line with Activations (Ext. 411).</li><li><strong>POWER OUTPUT VERIFICATION:</strong> With test audio playing from the media player, use your <strong>multimeter</strong> set to AC Voltage ($\\text{V AC}$) to measure signal output directly across the speaker output Euroblock terminals. Confirm with Support that the amplifier is outputting correct, stable AC power.</li><li><strong>AUDIO WALK TEST:</strong> Adjust input gain and master volume knobs to nominal levels. Walk all audio zones with the store manager and Support to confirm clear, balanced audio playback across all previously installed speakers with zero distortion, clipping, or thermal fault trips.</li></ol><p><br></p><strong>PHASE 5: DEFECTIVE ASSET STAGING &amp; WORKSPACE CLEANUP</strong><ol><li><strong>DEFECTIVE ASSET STAGING:</strong> Carefully box up the defective JBL CSA140Z amplifier and its power cord into the shipping box from the replacement unit. Affix the return shipping label (if present) or write <strong>\"DEFECTIVE JBL CSA140Z AMP - STAGED FOR RETURN SHIPMENT\"</strong> clearly on the outside. Hand the package directly to the MOD or stage it in the designated IT storage area. <strong>Do not remove hardware from the property.</strong></li><li><strong>CLEANUP:</strong> Neatly dress all audio patch cords and power cables along the rack frame using <strong>Velcro ties</strong>. Leave the server room floor and rack area spotless.</li></ol><p><br></p><strong>IV. REQUIRED PHOTO DELIVERABLES (TO BE ATTACHED TO TICKET)</strong><ul><li>[ ] <strong>Multimeter Speaker Line Impedance Reading:</strong> Clear photo displaying multimeter resistance ($\\Omega$) test readings taken on the speaker lines prior to landing wires.</li><li>[ ] <strong>Multimeter Output Power Verification:</strong> Photo showing multimeter probe leads measuring AC signal output voltage ($\\text{V AC}$) across the Euroblock speaker terminals while playing test audio.</li><li>[ ] <strong>New JBL CSA140Z Installed &amp; Active:</strong> Close-up photo showing the replacement JBL CSA140Z mounted, powered on, with clean Euroblock terminal wiring and active green power indicator.</li><li>[ ] <strong>Boxed Defective JBL CSA140Z Staged for Return:</strong> Photo showing the old defective amplifier packaged, labeled, and staged in the designated site area or handed to the MOD.</li><li>[ ] <strong>Optimized Network / Audio Rack:</strong> A wide-angle, comprehensive photo of the <strong>entire IT/audio rack cabinet with the door OPEN</strong>.</li><li>[ ] <strong>Immaculate Workspace:</strong> Photo proving the server room floor and rack area are swept completely clean.</li></ul><p><br></p><strong>V. FINAL SIGN-OFF &amp; TICKET CLOSEOUT</strong><ol><li><strong>DUAL CONFIRMATION MANDATE:</strong></li></ol><ul><li><strong>Activations:</strong> Confirm verbal sign-off from remote support (Ext. 411) that speaker line diagnostics are clear, JBL CSA140Z output power delivery is verified, gain levels are set, and audio testing is complete.</li><li><strong>MOD Acceptance:</strong> Walk the facility with the store manager to demonstrate clear audio playback, confirm return hardware staging, and obtain operational sign-off.</li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><strong>SIGN-OFF:</strong> Secure the MOD's signature on your physical or digital work order layout.</li><li><strong>MANDATORY CHECK-OUT:</strong> Visit <strong>CIPE.CHAT</strong> in your mobile browser to execute your final check-out tracking loop with Support (or call Dispatch at <strong>(888) 747-9530, Ext. 888</strong> if no response).</li><li><strong>TICKET LOGS:</strong> Update internal ticket notes detailing multimeter speaker impedance readings ($\\Omega$), amplifier AC output voltage readings ($\\text{V AC}$), serial numbers of both old and replacement JBL CSA140Z units, rear output mode selected (70V vs 8-ohm), and return staging confirmation before closing the work order.</li></ol><p>____________________________</p><p><strong><u>TERMS AND CONDITIONS</u></strong></p><ul><li>Cipe Activations team is empowered to Verbally approve labor overages</li><li><strong>Smoking and vaping are strictly Prohibited on premises!!</strong></li><li>All technicians must wear full-length pants as part of the dress code; shorts are strictly prohibited. Technicians are required to wear closed-toe shoes at all times. Slip-on or open-toe footwear is strictly prohibited.</li><li>Technicians are required to remove any debris, boxes or trash from work area prior to leaving.</li></ul><p><strong>Cancellation Fee:</strong> A flat <strong>$100 cancellation fee</strong> will apply in lieu of all hourly, fixed, or blended rates when scheduled work cannot be performed (and tech has already checked in) due to missing hardware, site refusal/turn-away, or the work being completed before technician arrival (provided the technician arrives within 15 minutes of the scheduled time).</p><ul><li>If the technician is unprepared for the agreed scope of work, lacks required equipment, or arrives more than 15 minutes late(for hard start), and the work cannot be completed due to these circumstances, both the <strong>$100 cancellation fee and all agreed service rates are waived</strong>.</li></ul><p><em>In order for work order to be considered complete and tech to receive prompt payment, all work order tasks must be completed and tech must be released by CIPE Support.</em></p>","markdown":"**PLEASE READ THE FOLLOWING CAREFULLY. FAILURE TO COMPLY MAY RESULT IN WITHHELD PAYMENTS**\n\nCall or chat **Activations** for check in as well as more detailed instruction.\n\n- **(888)747-9530, Ext. 888**\n- **techonsite.chat**\n\n  \n**TICKET SUMMARY:** JBL CSA140Z AUDIO AMPLIFIER REPLACEMENT, PREVIOUSLY INSTALLED SPEAKER CIRCUIT DIAGNOSTICS, POWER OUTPUT VERIFICATION & RETURN LOGISTICS STAGING\n\n**I. PROJECT SUMMARY**An audio-experienced technician is required on-site to decommission a defective **JBL CSA140Z Commercial Audio Amplifier** and replace it with a brand-new JBL CSA140Z unit shipped directly to the location.\n\nPrior to landing wires on the replacement JBL CSA140Z, the technician must conduct a layer-1 circuit audit on all previously installed speaker lines (measuring resistance $\\\\Omega$ and checking for shorts-to-ground) to ensure line integrity and prevent immediate output stage damage to the new unit. The technician will verify whether the speaker topology is wired for 70V/100V High-Z or 4$\\\\Omega$/8$\\\\Omega$ Low-Z operation and set the rear-panel output switch accordingly. Once installed, the technician must verify using a multimeter that the amplifier is outputting AC power correctly across the Euroblock speaker terminals under remote Support direction, perform live test playback, and stage the defective JBL CSA140Z on-site for return shipment.\n\n**AMPLIFIER SAFETY & OUTPUT SWITCH MANDATE:** Always physically power **OFF** the amplifier and isolate utility power before adjusting rear DIP/output switches, splicing, testing, or landing any speaker cabling or Euroblock input/output leads.\n\n**DEFECTIVE ASSET RETURN STAGING MANDATE:** Carefully box up the defective JBL CSA140Z amplifier and its power cord into the shipping packaging from the replacement unit. Affix the return shipping label (if provided) or label the box clearly as **\"DEFECTIVE JBL CSA140Z AMP - STAGED FOR RETURN SHIPMENT.\"** Hand the package directly to the Manager on Duty (MOD) or stage it in the store's designated IT storage area. Do not remove hardware from the property unless explicitly instructed by Support.\n\n**DUAL SIGN-OFF MANDATE:** The technician must receive explicit operational and audio testing confirmation from remote **Activations** and obtain physical/digital sign-off from the on-site **Manager on Duty (MOD)** prior to departing the facility.\n\n**II. REQUIRED TOOLS & PARTS**- **LAPTOP WITH PHYSICAL ETHERNET PORT & MOBILE HOTSPOT!** (**Absolute Mandatory Requirement** for web interface checks, audio source verification, gateway pings, and telemetry logging)\n- **Volt Meter / Multimeter & Audio Wire Tester / Cable Toner** (**Mandatory** for measuring speaker line impedance $\\\\Omega$, short-to-ground faults, and AC signal output voltage)\n- **Small Precision Screwdriver Set** (**Mandatory** for securing wire leads into JBL Euroblock/Phoenix terminal connectors)\n- **Audio Interconnect Cabling & Termination Supplies:** Spare 16/2 or 18/2 speaker wire, wire nuts, B-connectors, RCA/3.5mm patch cables, wire strippers, and snips\n- **Rack/Shelf Mounting Hardware Pack** (Technician stock of standard cage nuts, rack screws, or shelf mounting brackets)\n- **General Tool Kit w/ Power Drill, Bits, & Drivers**\n- **Cable Management Supplies:** High-quality **Velcro ties**, packaging tape, and permanent marker\n- **Mobile Smart-Phone** (Required for live on-site check-in/check-out tracking via browser chat)\n\n**III. ON-SITE EXECUTION STEPS****PHASE 1: ARRIVAL & STRATEGIC ALIGNMENT**1. **MANDATORY CHECK-IN:** Visit **CIPE.CHAT** in your mobile device's browser with your Name and Service Ticket #. If you receive no response, contact Dispatch at **(888) 747-9530, Ext. 888**.\n2. **MOD CONTACT:** Meet with the Manager on Duty (MOD). Have them walk you to the main audio/IT rack and collect the newly shipped JBL CSA140Z replacement hardware box.\n3. **SUPPORT ENGAGEMENT:** Call **Activations at (888) 747-9530, Ext. 411**. Review the JBL CSA140Z replacement and speaker circuit testing scope with remote support before touching live equipment.\n\n**PHASE 2: SPEAKER CIRCUIT DIAGNOSTICS & PRE-SWAP TESTING**1. **POWER ISOLATION:** Power **OFF** the defective JBL CSA140Z amplifier and unplug the AC power cord. Unplug the Euroblock speaker output connector from the rear panel.\n2. **SPEAKER LINE AUDIT (CRITICAL):** Set your **multimeter** to measure resistance ($\\\\Omega$). Measure across positive (+)—negative (-) speaker leads on each previously installed zone:\n\n- **70V/100V High-Z Systems:** Verify line resistance matches expected transformer primary load (typically $50\\\\Omega$ to several hundred $\\\\Omega$).\n- **4$\\\\Omega$/8$\\\\Omega$ Low-Z Systems:** Verify direct line resistance measures within a safe $4\\\\Omega$ to $8\\\\Omega$ range.\n- **Ground-Fault Test:** Measure resistance from each speaker lead to the rack frame/ground. Any reading below infinity ($\\\\infty$) indicates a ground fault that must be cleared before connecting the new amp.\n\n1. **DECOMMISSIONING:** Unplug the input signal Euroblock/RCA connectors and unmount the defective JBL CSA140Z chassis from the rack or shelf.\n\n**PHASE 3: REPLACEMENT JBL CSA140Z INSTALLATION & WIRING**1. **REAR OUTPUT SWITCH CONFIGURATION:** Prior to applying power, set the rear-panel output switch on the new JBL CSA140Z to match the verified speaker topology (70V/100V High-Z or 4$\\\\Omega$/8$\\\\Omega$ Low-Z) as directed by Support.\n2. **RACK / SHELF MOUNTING:** Securely mount or position the new replacement JBL CSA140Z amplifier in the equipment rack.\n3. **EUROBLOCK TERMINAL INTEGRATION:** Land the input audio source leads and verified speaker lines into the Euroblock terminal connectors. Plug the connectors firmly into the rear panel of the new JBL CSA140Z, ensuring all terminal screws are tight with zero exposed copper strands crossing pins.\n\n**PHASE 4: POWER OUTPUT VERIFICATION & AUDIO AUDIT**1. **POWER RESTORATION:** Connect the AC power lead and power **ON** the replacement JBL CSA140Z. Verify the front master volume ring indicator lights up green. Stay on the line with Activations (Ext. 411).\n2. **POWER OUTPUT VERIFICATION:** With test audio playing from the media player, use your **multimeter** set to AC Voltage ($\\\\text{V AC}$) to measure signal output directly across the speaker output Euroblock terminals. Confirm with Support that the amplifier is outputting correct, stable AC power.\n3. **AUDIO WALK TEST:** Adjust input gain and master volume knobs to nominal levels. Walk all audio zones with the store manager and Support to confirm clear, balanced audio playback across all previously installed speakers with zero distortion, clipping, or thermal fault trips.\n\n**PHASE 5: DEFECTIVE ASSET STAGING & WORKSPACE CLEANUP**1. **DEFECTIVE ASSET STAGING:** Carefully box up the defective JBL CSA140Z amplifier and its power cord into the shipping box from the replacement unit. Affix the return shipping label (if present) or write **\"DEFECTIVE JBL CSA140Z AMP - STAGED FOR RETURN SHIPMENT\"** clearly on the outside. Hand the package directly to the MOD or stage it in the designated IT storage area. **Do not remove hardware from the property.**\n2. **CLEANUP:** Neatly dress all audio patch cords and power cables along the rack frame using **Velcro ties**. Leave the server room floor and rack area spotless.\n\n**IV. REQUIRED PHOTO DELIVERABLES (TO BE ATTACHED TO TICKET)**- \\[ \\] **Multimeter Speaker Line Impedance Reading:** Clear photo displaying multimeter resistance ($\\\\Omega$) test readings taken on the speaker lines prior to landing wires.\n- \\[ \\] **Multimeter Output Power Verification:** Photo showing multimeter probe leads measuring AC signal output voltage ($\\\\text{V AC}$) across the Euroblock speaker terminals while playing test audio.\n- \\[ \\] **New JBL CSA140Z Installed & Active:** Close-up photo showing the replacement JBL CSA140Z mounted, powered on, with clean Euroblock terminal wiring and active green power indicator.\n- \\[ \\] **Boxed Defective JBL CSA140Z Staged for Return:** Photo showing the old defective amplifier packaged, labeled, and staged in the designated site area or handed to the MOD.\n- \\[ \\] **Optimized Network / Audio Rack:** A wide-angle, comprehensive photo of the **entire IT/audio rack cabinet with the door OPEN**.\n- \\[ \\] **Immaculate Workspace:** Photo proving the server room floor and rack area are swept completely clean.\n\n**V. FINAL SIGN-OFF & TICKET CLOSEOUT**1. **DUAL CONFIRMATION MANDATE:**\n\n- **Activations:** Confirm verbal sign-off from remote support (Ext. 411) that speaker line diagnostics are clear, JBL CSA140Z output power delivery is verified, gain levels are set, and audio testing is complete.\n- **MOD Acceptance:** Walk the facility with the store manager to demonstrate clear audio playback, confirm return hardware staging, and obtain operational sign-off.\n\n1. **SIGN-OFF:** Secure the MOD's signature on your physical or digital work order layout.\n2. **MANDATORY CHECK-OUT:** Visit **CIPE.CHAT** in your mobile browser to execute your final check-out tracking loop with Support (or call Dispatch at **(888) 747-9530, Ext. 888** if no response).\n3. **TICKET LOGS:** Update internal ticket notes detailing multimeter speaker impedance readings ($\\\\Omega$), amplifier AC output voltage readings ($\\\\text{V AC}$), serial numbers of both old and replacement JBL CSA140Z units, rear output mode selected (70V vs 8-ohm), and return staging confirmation before closing the work order.\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\n**TERMS AND CONDITIONS**\n\n- Cipe Activations team is empowered to Verbally approve labor overages\n- **Smoking and vaping are strictly Prohibited on premises!!**\n- All technicians must wear full-length pants as part of the dress code; shorts are strictly prohibited. Technicians are required to wear closed-toe shoes at all times. Slip-on or open-toe footwear is strictly prohibited.\n- Technicians are required to remove any debris, boxes or trash from work area prior to leaving.\n\n**Cancellation Fee:** A flat **$100 cancellation fee** will apply in lieu of all hourly, fixed, or blended rates when scheduled work cannot be performed (and tech has already checked in) due to missing hardware, site refusal/turn-away, or the work being completed before technician arrival (provided the technician arrives within 15 minutes of the scheduled time).\n\n- If the technician is unprepared for the agreed scope of work, lacks required equipment, or arrives more than 15 minutes late(for hard start), and the work cannot be completed due to these circumstances, both the **$100 cancellation fee and all agreed service rates are waived**.\n\n*In order for work order to be considered complete and tech to receive prompt payment, all work order tasks must be completed and tech must be released by CIPE Support.*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-23T09:00","end":"2026-09-23T11:00","latestStart":"2026-09-23T10:00"},"payRange":{"min":150,"max":300},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":150},"additional":{"units":2,"amount":75}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":14},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"SLOT_UNAVAILABLE","rejectDetails":"📅 No available schedule slot\nRequested: Wed, Sep 23, 9:00 AM\nChecked: Wed, Sep 23, Thu, Sep 24, Fri, Sep 25 · 9:00 AM–8:00 PM\nNo block long enough was found."},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T17:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-23T15:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"Gap"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Miniso"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"Remote Hands - Connect AT&T broadband circuit"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790099271401}
{"job":{"id":19994033,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Anatomage","title":"Anatomage Table - Monitor & Computer Replacement","description":{"html":"<p>Our product, the Anatomage Table, is a virtual dissection table comprised of two 46\" monitors connected to a computer with a touchscreen overlay.</p><p>Our customer at Enloe High School has been reporting some issues with their current monitor and computer setup. We're looking for someone to go onsite, remove the old display, computer, install the new display, install the new computer, and get their unit up and running again. A replacement is already onsite.</p><p>Please note that images will be needed to taken through out the WO to ensure no issues during installation. If there are uploading concerns due to service issues, please inform your WO manager.</p><p>Replacement will consist of</p><ol><li>Referencing the <strong>Samsung VM46 Replacement Guide</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Disconnect Touchscreen Boards</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Removing the top frame to access the displays</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Removing the defective monitor unit</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Reinstalling the new monitor</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>Take a photo of the display installed on the unit</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>Take a photo showing the displays are flush to each other.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Reconnect touchscreen boards</li><li>Install new computer</li><li>Testing the Display and computer to confirm it powers on with the remainder of the table</li><li>Reassembling the table for customer use</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Take a photo of the screens the table is put together and both displays are powering on</strong></li><li>Power on and confirm touch is functioning and TableEDU software can open</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If touch is uncalibrated, follow&nbsp;<strong>NVIDIA Surround Set Up Guide</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If TableEDU is not activated, contact your WO Manager</li><li>Additional Steps as needed</li><li>Repackaging defective monitor and computer in the same packaging (return label is included beind the shipping label)</li></ol><p>Monitor Specs:</p><ul><li>Model: Samsung VM46</li><li>Diagonal Size: 46\"</li><li>Weight: ~35lbs</li></ul><p>___</p><ul><li>Arrival Instructions: Check confidential</li></ul>","markdown":"Our product, the Anatomage Table, is a virtual dissection table comprised of two 46\" monitors connected to a computer with a touchscreen overlay.\n\nOur customer at Enloe High School has been reporting some issues with their current monitor and computer setup. We're looking for someone to go onsite, remove the old display, computer, install the new display, install the new computer, and get their unit up and running again. A replacement is already onsite.\n\nPlease note that images will be needed to taken through out the WO to ensure no issues during installation. If there are uploading concerns due to service issues, please inform your WO manager.\n\nReplacement will consist of\n\n1. Referencing the **Samsung VM46 Replacement Guide**\n2. Disconnect Touchscreen Boards\n3. Removing the top frame to access the displays\n4. Removing the defective monitor unit\n5. Reinstalling the new monitor\n6. **Take a photo of the display installed on the unit**\n7. **Take a photo showing the displays are flush to each other.**\n8. Reconnect touchscreen boards\n9. Install new computer\n10. Testing the Display and computer to confirm it powers on with the remainder of the table\n11. Reassembling the table for customer use\n12. **Take a photo of the screens the table is put together and both displays are powering on**\n13. Power on and confirm touch is functioning and TableEDU software can open\n14. If touch is uncalibrated, follow **NVIDIA Surround Set Up Guide**\n15. If TableEDU is not activated, contact your WO Manager\n16. Additional Steps as needed\n17. Repackaging defective monitor and computer in the same packaging (return label is included beind the shipping label)\n\nMonitor Specs:\n\n- Model: Samsung VM46\n- Diagonal Size: 46\"\n- Weight: ~35lbs\n\n\\_\\_\\_\n\n- Arrival Instructions: Check confidential","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-24T09:00","end":"2026-09-24T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":100,"max":150},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":100},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":10},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $150 is below minimum threshold $400"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Miniso"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-30T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974903-Method Townhomes-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-02T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974912-Red Wolf Crossing-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"Remote Hands - Connect AT&T broadband circuit"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790099294266}
{"job":{"id":"7641252788","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"TOGA TECHNOLOGY","title":"Office Depot - In-Home Printer Setup","description":"<p><strong>Service Description</strong></p><ul><li>The field Technician will set up and configure one (1) wired/wireless printer/scanner on an existing network. Connect up to two (2) devices (computer, phone, or tablet), demo basic printer features, print test page, test fax capabilities for printers with fax functionality (requires landline connectivity), neatly dress wires, and ensure all features are operating. Install consumable items in the printer, such as toner/ink cartridges or paper.</li><li><strong>If the job is not able to be completed, meaning there was NO WORK COMPLETED and you are at the customer's house, payment will be reduced to $40 for time and travel.</strong></li></ul><p><br></p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Service Procedure</strong></p><p><strong>The Field Technician will perform the following tasks:</strong></p><ul><li>Unbox the new printer (check the box and packaging for included accessories).</li><li>Unpack the toner or ink cartridges. Make sure to clear all packaging materials that are attached to these items. NOTE: If ink or toner is not included with the new product, the customer must supply it.</li><li>Install all toner or ink cartridges.</li><li>Install the printer paper provided by the customer in the default paper tray.</li><li>Follow the manufacturer's guidelines to power on the printer. (Verify the printer recognizes all installed supplies and accessories).</li><li>Follow any printer-specific guidelines for printer calibration (if applicable).</li><li>For a wired setup, connect to the network via Ethernet or USB cable (customer-supplied) if the wired network is available, or to the available Wi-Fi.</li><li>Have the customer log onto their computer/Device and attempt to auto-discover the new network printer in Windows, iOS, Android, Mac OS, or Chrome.</li><li>Download the latest installation software (for the serviced printer) and drivers from the manufacturer's website or install CD/DVD delivered inside the package by the manufacturer. Follow the default prompts to install the drivers and connect to the printer.</li><li>Verify the printer is connected by running a test print from up to two devices that have been connected.</li><li>Test all features of the printer to ensure they are working correctly (tray feeds, duplex, etc.).</li><li>Demonstrate basic printing/scanning functions.</li><li>Make the new printer the default printer.</li><li>Make sure the printer is set correctly in the preferred location, and all wiring is dressed.</li><li>Acquire customer signature indicating work has been completed to their satisfaction.</li><li>Clean up the service area and place packaging at the customer's designated area at the customer's location.</li><li>Service complete.&nbsp;</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>In-Scope</strong></p><ul><li>Support for Windows 8,10,11 Android, iOS, Mac OS, and Chrome</li><li>Set up one (1) wired/wireless printer/scanner on an existing network</li><li>Configure and test printer for Windows 8,10,11, Android, IOS, Mac OS or Chrome</li><li>Connect up to two (2) devices (computer, tablet or phone) or a combination (1) computer (1) device</li><li>Demonstrate basic printer features</li><li>Print test page</li><li>Ensure all basic features are operating properly</li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Out-of-Scope</strong></p><ul><li>Support for legacy versions of Windows XP, 7, and Vista,</li><li>Support for Linux</li><li>Network Printers</li><li>Industrial Printers i.e. EPSON Workforce enterprise Printers and their equivalence</li><li>Diagnosis or repair of a malfunctioning computer or network</li><li>Diagnosis or repair of a malfunctioning Printer&nbsp;</li><li>Advanced Functions, e.g., Fax, fax to email,</li><li>Setup or configuration of the wireless network</li><li>Providing or including printer supplies (toners, cartridges, paper, etc.) with a service call</li><li>How to print envelopes, photos, and labels from installed software</li><li>Removal of old devices or product packaging debris</li><li>If the company no longer supports the OS, i.e. HP</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>Customer Responsibilities</strong></p><ul><li>An adult (18+) must always be present at the installation site</li><li>Usernames and passwords</li><li>Network names and passwords</li><li>Make and model numbers</li><li>All needed cables or accessories</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>CODE OF CONDUCT:</strong></p><p>Your acceptance of our <strong>Agilant Solutions</strong> assignment (work order) is your agreement to comply with our code of conduct. Failure to comply can result in a reduction in payment or nonpayment, being placed on probation for a period, and the violation can include removal from the talent pool and/or being blocked from future dispatches. Contract Field Technicians (Service Pros) are expected to act in a polite, ethical, and professional manner at all times.</p><ul><li>All technicians must be dressed professionally in clean work pants (or jeans in good condition) and shirts with sleeves (and in good repair), socks, and closed-toe shoes.</li><li>Maintain good personal hygiene.</li><li>Avoid any non-assignment-related conversations with our Customers (e.g. opinion of product quality, personal issues, payment status, politics, etc.).</li><li>DO NOT solicit our Customers for any reason.&nbsp;If additional work is requested, call (844) 276-7263</li><li>The unauthorized use, possession, solicitation for, or sale of narcotics or other illegal drugs, alcohol, or prescription medication on Company or customer premises or while performing an assignment is strictly prohibited.</li><li>Being impaired or under the influence of legal or illegal drugs or alcohol on the Company or Customer premises.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><strong>By accepting this assignment, you agree:</strong></p><ul><li>You have the skills, knowledge, experience, and tools to successfully complete the scope of work.</li><li>You agree to <u>follow COVID-19 CDC safety guidelines</u> found at www.cdc.gov</li><li>To represent to the Customer, you are a Service Pro selected by<strong> Office Depot In-Home Support </strong>to complete the assignment</li><li>You will contact the<strong> Office Depot In-Home Support Team</strong> at (844) 276-7263 when en route and provide an approximate arrival time</li><li>You will contact&nbsp;<strong>Office Depot In-Home Support&nbsp;</strong>team at (844) 276-7263&nbsp;if additional work is requested, resolving issues during the initial appointment or requests by the customer to return to complete the original installation.</li><li>You will not share personal contact information such as email address, business card, website, or social media account with the customer</li><li>By accepting this job, you are acknowledging and agreeing to the flat rate that has been accepted. We do not operate on an hourly rate basis. Therefore, if the task extends beyond the estimated time, please contact us immediately</li><li>You will close out the assignment for payment no more than 24 hours after dispatch completion</li><li>If the job is not able to be completed, meaning there was NO WORK completed and you are at the customer's house, payment will be reduced to $40 for time and travel.</li></ul>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00","end":"2026-09-25T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":0,"max":60},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":4,"distance":2.3},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $60 is below minimum threshold $400"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z",