{"job":{"id":20006001,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Cipe Solutions","title":"Service Ticket #235829 - Wifi and Camera Recorder Down | Axis RMA 1227565","description":{"html":"<p><strong>PLEASE READ THE FOLLOWING CAREFULLY. FAILURE TO COMPLY MAY RESULT IN WITHHELD PAYMENTS</strong></p><p>Call or chat <strong>Activations</strong> for check in as well as more detailed instruction.</p><ul><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">(888)747-9530, Ext. 888</strong></li><li><strong>techonsite.chat</strong></li></ul><br><p><strong>TICKET SUMMARY:</strong> AXIS NVR WARRANTY HARDWARE REPLACEMENT, WIRELESS ACCESS POINT SWAP, CAMERA &amp; NETWORK PROVISIONING, RETURN LOGISTICS &amp; SITE DISPOSAL</p><p><br></p><strong>I. PROJECT SUMMARY</strong><p>A network and security technician is required on-site to decommission a defective <strong>Axis Network Video Recorder (NVR)</strong> under warranty and replace an existing, failed <strong>Wireless Access Point (AP)</strong>.</p><p><br></p><p>The technician will map all incoming IP camera network feeds and switch ports before unmounting the defective Axis NVR. The technician will install the replacement Axis NVR, mount the replacement Access Point (verifying 802.3af/at PoE power delivery), and coordinate directly with remote <strong>Activations</strong> to configure IP camera channels, push NVR recording profiles, adopt the AP into the network management controller, and verify corporate/guest Wi-Fi SSIDs.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>AXIS NVR RETURN LOGISTICS MANDATE:</strong> Upon successful camera stream verification, the technician must carefully package the defective Axis NVR (and its power supply) into the shipping box from the replacement unit. Affix the provided <strong>included return shipping label</strong> securely to the outside of the box, seal it tightly with packaging tape, and hand the package directly to the Manager on Duty (MOD) or stage it in the store's designated IT area for return carrier pickup. Record the return tracking number in the ticket notes prior to departure.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>FAILED ACCESS POINT SITE DISPOSAL MANDATE:</strong> Cleanly box or wrap the defective Access Point. Write <strong>\"DEFECTIVE ACCESS POINT - FOR SITE DISPOSAL\"</strong> in bold permanent marker on the box and stage it in the store's designated IT storage area. <strong>Do not remove the failed Access Point from the property.</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>DUAL SIGN-OFF MANDATE:</strong> The technician must receive explicit operational, video recording, and wireless network confirmation from remote <strong>Activations</strong> and obtain physical/digital sign-off from the on-site <strong>Manager on Duty (MOD)</strong> prior to departing the facility.</p><p><br></p><strong>II. REQUIRED TOOLS &amp; PARTS</strong><ul><li><strong>LAPTOP WITH PHYSICAL ETHERNET PORT &amp; MOBILE HOTSPOT!</strong> (<strong>Absolute Mandatory Requirement</strong> for Axis IP Utility / Axis Camera Station discovery, local web GUI diagnostics, ping sweeps, and AP network verification)</li><li><strong>6–8ft Step Ladder</strong> (Required for accessing ceiling- or high wall-mounted Access Point locations)</li><li><strong>Volt Meter / Multimeter &amp; Cable Tester / Wire Toner</strong> (<strong>Mandatory</strong> for verifying PoE voltage on the AP drop and checking RJ45 continuity on camera network lines)</li><li><strong>Cat5e/6 Cabling &amp; Termination Supplies:</strong> Pre-fabricated patch cords, RJ45 connectors, keystone jacks, modular crimpers, wire strippers, and snips</li><li><strong>Rack Mounting Hardware Pack:</strong> Technician stock of cage nuts, rack ears, and 10-32 rack screws</li><li><strong>General Tool Kit w/ Power Drill, Driver Bits &amp; Mounting Hardware:</strong> Drywall anchors, drop-ceiling grid clips, and wood/metal screws</li><li><strong>Cable Management Supplies:</strong> High-quality <strong>Velcro ties</strong>, packaging tape, Label Maker, and permanent marker</li><li><strong>Mobile Smart-Phone</strong> (Required for live on-site check-in/check-out tracking via browser chat)</li></ul><p><br></p><strong>III. ON-SITE EXECUTION STEPS</strong><strong>PHASE 1: ARRIVAL &amp; STRATEGIC ALIGNMENT</strong><ol><li><strong>MANDATORY CHECK-IN:</strong> Visit <strong>CIPE.CHAT</strong> in your mobile device's browser with your Name and Service Ticket #. If you receive no response, contact Dispatch at <strong>(888) 747-9530, Ext. 888</strong>.</li><li><strong>MOD CONTACT:</strong> Meet with the Manager on Duty (MOD). Have them walk you to the main IT network rack and the designated Access Point mounting location. Collect the shipped replacement hardware boxes (<strong>Axis NVR</strong> and <strong>Access Point</strong>) and confirm the return shipping label is present in the NVR box.</li><li><strong>SUPPORT ENGAGEMENT:</strong> Call <strong>Activations at (888) 747-9530, Ext. 411</strong>. Review the SOW, NVR IP profile, camera channel mapping, and AP adoption parameters before unplugging active equipment.</li></ol><p><br></p><strong>PHASE 2: LEGACY DECOMMISSIONING &amp; PORT MAPPING</strong><ol><li><strong>NVR CABLE MAPPING:</strong> Document and photograph all incoming camera switch drops and NVR network ports before disconnecting lines.</li><li><strong>DECOMMISSIONING:</strong> Gracefully power down the defective Axis NVR. Disconnect power and network patch cables, then unmount the unit from the rack frame.</li><li><strong>ACCESS POINT DECOMMISSIONING:</strong> Using your ladder, unmount the failed Access Point from the ceiling grid/wall and disconnect the Cat5e/6 PoE data cable. Test the drop using your cable tester/multimeter to verify PoE voltage.</li></ol><p><br></p><strong>PHASE 3: HARDWARE MOUNTING &amp; WIRING</strong><ol><li><strong>AXIS NVR RACK MOUNTING:</strong> Securely mount the replacement Axis NVR into the equipment rack using rack screws/ears. Land network and camera switch cables into their designated interface ports.</li><li><strong>ACCESS POINT MOUNTING:</strong> Install the replacement Access Point mounting bracket onto the ceiling grid or wall. Connect the verified PoE cable to the AP Ethernet port and twist-lock the chassis firmly into its bracket.</li></ol><p><br></p><strong>PHASE 4: ACTIVATIONS PROVISIONING &amp; SYSTEM TESTING</strong><ol><li><strong>NVR PROVISIONING &amp; CAMERA BINDING:</strong> Power on the Axis NVR. Stay on the line with Activations (Ext. 411) while Support provisions the NVR credentials, binds all IP cameras, and sets retention schedules.</li><li><strong>CAMERA FEED AUDIT:</strong> Connect your laptop to the network and run the Axis IP Utility / web client. Verify with Support and the MOD that every camera channel renders active, smooth video feeds with zero dropped frames.</li><li><strong>ACCESS POINT ADOPTION &amp; WIRELESS AUDIT:</strong> Confirm the new AP powers on (solid status LED). Allow Activations to adopt the AP into the network management platform and push SSIDs.</li><li><strong>WIRELESS WALK TEST:</strong> Connect your smartphone/laptop wirelessly to the newly broadcasted SSIDs. Walk the store perimeter with the MOD to confirm strong Wi-Fi signal coverage and active internet routing.</li></ol><p><br></p><strong>PHASE 5: LOGISTICS, DISPOSAL STAGING &amp; WORKSPACE CLEANUP</strong><ol><li><strong>AXIS NVR RETURN PACKAGING:</strong> Carefully box the defective warranty Axis NVR (and its power supply) into the replacement hardware box. Affix the <strong>included return shipping label</strong> securely to the outside, seal with packaging tape, and hand the box directly to the MOD or stage it in the IT storage room for carrier pickup.</li><li><strong>FAILED AP SITE DISPOSAL STAGING:</strong> Box up the failed Access Point. Write <strong>\"DEFECTIVE ACCESS POINT - FOR SITE DISPOSAL\"</strong> clearly on the box and stage it in the store's designated IT storage area. <strong>Do not remove it from the site.</strong></li><li><strong>CLEANUP:</strong> Neatly dress all network cables inside the rack using <strong>Velcro ties</strong>. Sweep up ceiling dust, drywall fragments, and wire snips, leaving the rack area completely spotless.</li></ol><p><br></p><strong>IV. REQUIRED PHOTO DELIVERABLES (TO BE ATTACHED TO TICKET)</strong><ul><li>[ ] <strong>New Axis NVR Installed &amp; Active:</strong> Close-up photo showing the replacement Axis NVR mounted, powered on, with active network/drive status LEDs.</li><li>[ ] <strong>New Access Point Mounted &amp; Active:</strong> Close-up photo showing the new Access Point cleanly mounted to the ceiling/wall with an active status LED.</li><li>[ ] <strong>Laptop CCTV &amp; Network Verification:</strong> Photo displaying your laptop screen showing active Axis camera feeds and passing wireless network speed/ping test.</li><li>[ ] <strong>Boxed Axis NVR w/ Return Label Attached:</strong> Clear photo showing the defective warranty NVR packaged, sealed, with the included return label clearly visible prior to carrier pickup.</li><li>[ ] <strong>Staged Defective Access Point:</strong> Photo showing the old failed Access Point boxed, labeled <strong>\"FOR SITE DISPOSAL,\"</strong> and staged in the designated site area.</li><li>[ ] <strong>Optimized Network Rack:</strong> A wide-angle, comprehensive photo of the <strong>entire IT network rack with the cabinet door OPEN</strong>, showing neat Velcro cable management.</li><li>[ ] <strong>Immaculate Workspace:</strong> Photo proving the server room floor and area beneath the AP installation are swept completely clean.</li></ul><p><br></p><strong>V. FINAL SIGN-OFF &amp; TICKET CLOSEOUT</strong><ol><li><strong>DUAL CONFIRMATION MANDATE:</strong></li></ol><ul><li><strong>Activations:</strong> Confirm verbal sign-off from remote support (Ext. 411) that Axis NVR camera channels are fully mapped and recording, AP network adoption is complete, and wireless SSIDs are operational.</li><li><strong>MOD Acceptance:</strong> Demonstrate active CCTV video feeds on the monitor and verified wireless connectivity to the store manager, confirm return logistics and disposal staging, and obtain operational sign-off.</li></ul><p><br></p><ol><li><strong>SIGN-OFF:</strong> Secure the MOD's signature on your physical or digital work order layout.</li><li><strong>MANDATORY CHECK-OUT:</strong> Visit <strong>CIPE.CHAT</strong> in your mobile browser to execute your final check-out tracking loop with Support (or call Dispatch at <strong>(888) 747-9530, Ext. 888</strong> if no response).</li><li><strong>TICKET LOGS:</strong> Update internal ticket notes detailing Serial Numbers and MAC Addresses for both old and new NVR and AP units, the <strong>NVR Return Shipping Tracking Number</strong>, and remote sign-off details before closing the work order.</li></ol><p>____________________________</p><p><strong><u>TERMS AND CONDITIONS</u></strong></p><ul><li>Cipe Activations team is empowered to Verbally approve labor overages</li><li><strong>Smoking and vaping are strictly Prohibited on premises!!</strong></li><li>All technicians must wear full-length pants as part of the dress code; shorts are strictly prohibited. Technicians are required to wear closed-toe shoes at all times. Slip-on or open-toe footwear is strictly prohibited.</li><li>Technicians are required to remove any debris, boxes or trash from work area prior to leaving.</li></ul><p><strong>Cancellation Fee:</strong> A flat <strong>$100 cancellation fee</strong> will apply in lieu of all hourly, fixed, or blended rates when scheduled work cannot be performed (and tech has already checked in) due to missing hardware, site refusal/turn-away, or the work being completed before technician arrival (provided the technician arrives within 15 minutes of the scheduled time).</p><ul><li>If the technician is unprepared for the agreed scope of work, lacks required equipment, or arrives more than 15 minutes late(for hard start), and the work cannot be completed due to these circumstances, both the <strong>$100 cancellation fee and all agreed service rates are waived</strong>.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><em>In order for work order to be considered complete and tech to receive prompt payment, all work order tasks must be completed and tech must be released by CIPE Support.</em></p>","markdown":"**PLEASE READ THE FOLLOWING CAREFULLY. FAILURE TO COMPLY MAY RESULT IN WITHHELD PAYMENTS**\n\nCall or chat **Activations** for check in as well as more detailed instruction.\n\n- **(888)747-9530, Ext. 888**\n- **techonsite.chat**\n\n  \n**TICKET SUMMARY:** AXIS NVR WARRANTY HARDWARE REPLACEMENT, WIRELESS ACCESS POINT SWAP, CAMERA & NETWORK PROVISIONING, RETURN LOGISTICS & SITE DISPOSAL\n\n**I. PROJECT SUMMARY**A network and security technician is required on-site to decommission a defective **Axis Network Video Recorder (NVR)** under warranty and replace an existing, failed **Wireless Access Point (AP)**.\n\nThe technician will map all incoming IP camera network feeds and switch ports before unmounting the defective Axis NVR. The technician will install the replacement Axis NVR, mount the replacement Access Point (verifying 802.3af/at PoE power delivery), and coordinate directly with remote **Activations** to configure IP camera channels, push NVR recording profiles, adopt the AP into the network management controller, and verify corporate/guest Wi-Fi SSIDs.\n\n**AXIS NVR RETURN LOGISTICS MANDATE:** Upon successful camera stream verification, the technician must carefully package the defective Axis NVR (and its power supply) into the shipping box from the replacement unit. Affix the provided **included return shipping label** securely to the outside of the box, seal it tightly with packaging tape, and hand the package directly to the Manager on Duty (MOD) or stage it in the store's designated IT area for return carrier pickup. Record the return tracking number in the ticket notes prior to departure.\n\n**FAILED ACCESS POINT SITE DISPOSAL MANDATE:** Cleanly box or wrap the defective Access Point. Write **\"DEFECTIVE ACCESS POINT - FOR SITE DISPOSAL\"** in bold permanent marker on the box and stage it in the store's designated IT storage area. **Do not remove the failed Access Point from the property.**\n\n**DUAL SIGN-OFF MANDATE:** The technician must receive explicit operational, video recording, and wireless network confirmation from remote **Activations** and obtain physical/digital sign-off from the on-site **Manager on Duty (MOD)** prior to departing the facility.\n\n**II. REQUIRED TOOLS & PARTS**- **LAPTOP WITH PHYSICAL ETHERNET PORT & MOBILE HOTSPOT!** (**Absolute Mandatory Requirement** for Axis IP Utility / Axis Camera Station discovery, local web GUI diagnostics, ping sweeps, and AP network verification)\n- **6–8ft Step Ladder** (Required for accessing ceiling- or high wall-mounted Access Point locations)\n- **Volt Meter / Multimeter & Cable Tester / Wire Toner** (**Mandatory** for verifying PoE voltage on the AP drop and checking RJ45 continuity on camera network lines)\n- **Cat5e/6 Cabling & Termination Supplies:** Pre-fabricated patch cords, RJ45 connectors, keystone jacks, modular crimpers, wire strippers, and snips\n- **Rack Mounting Hardware Pack:** Technician stock of cage nuts, rack ears, and 10-32 rack screws\n- **General Tool Kit w/ Power Drill, Driver Bits & Mounting Hardware:** Drywall anchors, drop-ceiling grid clips, and wood/metal screws\n- **Cable Management Supplies:** High-quality **Velcro ties**, packaging tape, Label Maker, and permanent marker\n- **Mobile Smart-Phone** (Required for live on-site check-in/check-out tracking via browser chat)\n\n**III. ON-SITE EXECUTION STEPS****PHASE 1: ARRIVAL & STRATEGIC ALIGNMENT**1. **MANDATORY CHECK-IN:** Visit **CIPE.CHAT** in your mobile device's browser with your Name and Service Ticket #. If you receive no response, contact Dispatch at **(888) 747-9530, Ext. 888**.\n2. **MOD CONTACT:** Meet with the Manager on Duty (MOD). Have them walk you to the main IT network rack and the designated Access Point mounting location. Collect the shipped replacement hardware boxes (**Axis NVR** and **Access Point**) and confirm the return shipping label is present in the NVR box.\n3. **SUPPORT ENGAGEMENT:** Call **Activations at (888) 747-9530, Ext. 411**. Review the SOW, NVR IP profile, camera channel mapping, and AP adoption parameters before unplugging active equipment.\n\n**PHASE 2: LEGACY DECOMMISSIONING & PORT MAPPING**1. **NVR CABLE MAPPING:** Document and photograph all incoming camera switch drops and NVR network ports before disconnecting lines.\n2. **DECOMMISSIONING:** Gracefully power down the defective Axis NVR. Disconnect power and network patch cables, then unmount the unit from the rack frame.\n3. **ACCESS POINT DECOMMISSIONING:** Using your ladder, unmount the failed Access Point from the ceiling grid/wall and disconnect the Cat5e/6 PoE data cable. Test the drop using your cable tester/multimeter to verify PoE voltage.\n\n**PHASE 3: HARDWARE MOUNTING & WIRING**1. **AXIS NVR RACK MOUNTING:** Securely mount the replacement Axis NVR into the equipment rack using rack screws/ears. Land network and camera switch cables into their designated interface ports.\n2. **ACCESS POINT MOUNTING:** Install the replacement Access Point mounting bracket onto the ceiling grid or wall. Connect the verified PoE cable to the AP Ethernet port and twist-lock the chassis firmly into its bracket.\n\n**PHASE 4: ACTIVATIONS PROVISIONING & SYSTEM TESTING**1. **NVR PROVISIONING & CAMERA BINDING:** Power on the Axis NVR. Stay on the line with Activations (Ext. 411) while Support provisions the NVR credentials, binds all IP cameras, and sets retention schedules.\n2. **CAMERA FEED AUDIT:** Connect your laptop to the network and run the Axis IP Utility / web client. Verify with Support and the MOD that every camera channel renders active, smooth video feeds with zero dropped frames.\n3. **ACCESS POINT ADOPTION & WIRELESS AUDIT:** Confirm the new AP powers on (solid status LED). Allow Activations to adopt the AP into the network management platform and push SSIDs.\n4. **WIRELESS WALK TEST:** Connect your smartphone/laptop wirelessly to the newly broadcasted SSIDs. Walk the store perimeter with the MOD to confirm strong Wi-Fi signal coverage and active internet routing.\n\n**PHASE 5: LOGISTICS, DISPOSAL STAGING & WORKSPACE CLEANUP**1. **AXIS NVR RETURN PACKAGING:** Carefully box the defective warranty Axis NVR (and its power supply) into the replacement hardware box. Affix the **included return shipping label** securely to the outside, seal with packaging tape, and hand the box directly to the MOD or stage it in the IT storage room for carrier pickup.\n2. **FAILED AP SITE DISPOSAL STAGING:** Box up the failed Access Point. Write **\"DEFECTIVE ACCESS POINT - FOR SITE DISPOSAL\"** clearly on the box and stage it in the store's designated IT storage area. **Do not remove it from the site.**\n3. **CLEANUP:** Neatly dress all network cables inside the rack using **Velcro ties**. Sweep up ceiling dust, drywall fragments, and wire snips, leaving the rack area completely spotless.\n\n**IV. REQUIRED PHOTO DELIVERABLES (TO BE ATTACHED TO TICKET)**- \\[ \\] **New Axis NVR Installed & Active:** Close-up photo showing the replacement Axis NVR mounted, powered on, with active network/drive status LEDs.\n- \\[ \\] **New Access Point Mounted & Active:** Close-up photo showing the new Access Point cleanly mounted to the ceiling/wall with an active status LED.\n- \\[ \\] **Laptop CCTV & Network Verification:** Photo displaying your laptop screen showing active Axis camera feeds and passing wireless network speed/ping test.\n- \\[ \\] **Boxed Axis NVR w/ Return Label Attached:** Clear photo showing the defective warranty NVR packaged, sealed, with the included return label clearly visible prior to carrier pickup.\n- \\[ \\] **Staged Defective Access Point:** Photo showing the old failed Access Point boxed, labeled **\"FOR SITE DISPOSAL,\"** and staged in the designated site area.\n- \\[ \\] **Optimized Network Rack:** A wide-angle, comprehensive photo of the **entire IT network rack with the cabinet door OPEN**, showing neat Velcro cable management.\n- \\[ \\] **Immaculate Workspace:** Photo proving the server room floor and area beneath the AP installation are swept completely clean.\n\n**V. FINAL SIGN-OFF & TICKET CLOSEOUT**1. **DUAL CONFIRMATION MANDATE:**\n\n- **Activations:** Confirm verbal sign-off from remote support (Ext. 411) that Axis NVR camera channels are fully mapped and recording, AP network adoption is complete, and wireless SSIDs are operational.\n- **MOD Acceptance:** Demonstrate active CCTV video feeds on the monitor and verified wireless connectivity to the store manager, confirm return logistics and disposal staging, and obtain operational sign-off.\n\n1. **SIGN-OFF:** Secure the MOD's signature on your physical or digital work order layout.\n2. **MANDATORY CHECK-OUT:** Visit **CIPE.CHAT** in your mobile browser to execute your final check-out tracking loop with Support (or call Dispatch at **(888) 747-9530, Ext. 888** if no response).\n3. **TICKET LOGS:** Update internal ticket notes detailing Serial Numbers and MAC Addresses for both old and new NVR and AP units, the **NVR Return Shipping Tracking Number**, and remote sign-off details before closing the work order.\n\n\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_\n\n**TERMS AND CONDITIONS**\n\n- Cipe Activations team is empowered to Verbally approve labor overages\n- **Smoking and vaping are strictly Prohibited on premises!!**\n- All technicians must wear full-length pants as part of the dress code; shorts are strictly prohibited. Technicians are required to wear closed-toe shoes at all times. Slip-on or open-toe footwear is strictly prohibited.\n- Technicians are required to remove any debris, boxes or trash from work area prior to leaving.\n\n**Cancellation Fee:** A flat **$100 cancellation fee** will apply in lieu of all hourly, fixed, or blended rates when scheduled work cannot be performed (and tech has already checked in) due to missing hardware, site refusal/turn-away, or the work being completed before technician arrival (provided the technician arrives within 15 minutes of the scheduled time).\n\n- If the technician is unprepared for the agreed scope of work, lacks required equipment, or arrives more than 15 minutes late(for hard start), and the work cannot be completed due to these circumstances, both the **$100 cancellation fee and all agreed service rates are waived**.\n\n*In order for work order to be considered complete and tech to receive prompt payment, all work order tasks must be completed and tech must be released by CIPE Support.*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":true,"time":{"start":"2026-09-24T20:00","end":"2026-09-24T22:00","latestStart":"2026-09-24T21:00"},"payRange":{"min":150,"max":200},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":2,"amount":150},"additional":{"units":1,"amount":50}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":13},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $200 is below minimum threshold $400"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T23:00:00.000Z","summary":"Miniso"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","summary":"Ortodont Dana"},{"start":"2026-09-25T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-25T22:00:00.000Z","summary":"Granite"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville