{"job":{"id":20004985,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Integrated Business Applications","title":"Troubleshoot 1x IP camera down & Remount 1x IP Camera","description":{"html":"<p><strong>Troubleshoot 1x IP camera down &amp; Remount 1x IP Camera</strong></p><p>Only an experienced&nbsp;<strong>IP Camera and Networking Technician</strong>&nbsp;is needed to troubleshoot&nbsp;One<strong>&nbsp;(1) offline IP camera (Cam 7) </strong>&amp; remount One <strong>(1) IP camera</strong>. Technician must be proficient in diagnosing issues involving&nbsp;<strong>PoE switches, network connections, access points, and CAT cabling</strong>.</p><p>Please&nbsp;<strong>do not request this work order</strong>&nbsp;if you are not equipped or skilled to perform IP camera diagnostics.</p><p><strong>Photos are required</strong>&nbsp;before and after troubleshooting, including:</p><ul><li>The manager’s camera view or NVR screen</li><li>Camera model and serial number labels</li><li>Any exposed cable runs or conduit conditions (installed, damaged, or missing)</li></ul><p>Thorough notes must be included for all findings and actions taken.</p><p><strong>Scope of Work:</strong></p><p>Upon arrival, the Technician must&nbsp;<strong>check in with the General Manager</strong>&nbsp;and inform them they are with&nbsp;<strong>IBA</strong>&nbsp;to troubleshoot the offline camera.</p><p>The Manager will identify the camera location and assist with access as needed.</p><p>The affected camera will be connected via&nbsp;<strong>CAT5 or CAT6 cabling</strong>&nbsp;to a&nbsp;<strong>PoE switch</strong>&nbsp;located in either the&nbsp;<strong>Main Building</strong>,&nbsp;<strong>Shop Building</strong>, or&nbsp;<strong>Pole-mounted cabinet</strong>.</p><p>Some outdoor cameras may require an extension ladder or lift for access.</p><p>If applicable, a&nbsp;<strong>40’ articulating boom lift will be available on-site</strong>&nbsp;for this task.</p><p>Technician must be&nbsp;<strong>trained and authorized to operate a boom lift</strong>&nbsp;— otherwise, this work order cannot be accepted.</p><p><strong>Troubleshooting Steps:</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Visually inspect</strong>&nbsp;camera, cabling, and mounting area for damage or loose connections.</li><li><strong>Test the PoE connection</strong>&nbsp;using an IP camera tester with built-in PoE.</li><li><strong>Check the network link</strong>&nbsp;between the camera and the PoE switch.</li><li>If the camera is offline,&nbsp;<strong>verify link lights</strong>&nbsp;and test the cable for continuity or damage.</li><li>If the camera has been reset to defaults,&nbsp;<strong>reconfigure network settings</strong>&nbsp;with assistance from remote support.</li><li><strong>Confirm camera visibility</strong>&nbsp;on the NVR or management software once restored.</li></ol><p><br></p><p>Contact&nbsp;<strong>Joshua Myers (918-813-1569)</strong>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<strong>Drew Dimatos (214-773-6902)</strong>&nbsp;for remote configuration support as needed.</p><p>Support may be provided through&nbsp;<strong>TeamViewer</strong>,&nbsp;<strong>AnyDesk</strong>, or&nbsp;<strong>Quick Assist</strong>&nbsp;as needed.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Documentation Requirements:</strong></p><ul><li>Before and after photos of the camera and manager’s screen</li><li>Photo of camera model/serial number label</li><li>Notes detailing the issue, diagnostic steps, and final outcome</li><li>Photos of any damaged or exposed cables/conduit</li></ul><p><strong>Required Equipment and Tools:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Tall Extension Ladder</strong>&nbsp;(up to 22’ if needed)</li><li><strong>Laptop and Hotspot</strong>&nbsp;(with&nbsp;<em>Advanced IP Scanner</em>&nbsp;installed)</li><li><strong>Monitor, Keyboard, and Mouse</strong>&nbsp;(for NVR access if necessary)</li><li><strong>IP Camera Tester with built-in PoE</strong>&nbsp;(NOT an analog tester)</li><li><strong>Cable Tester</strong></li><li>Standard networking tools and materials:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">RJ-45 connectors, CAT6 cable, termination/crimp tools</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Screwdrivers, drill, snips, labeler, pull string</li></ul><p>Technician is responsible for providing all required tools and materials to complete this troubleshooting work order.</p>","markdown":"**Troubleshoot 1x IP camera down & Remount 1x IP Camera**\n\nOnly an experienced **IP Camera and Networking Technician** is needed to troubleshoot One **(1) offline IP camera (Cam 7)** & remount One **(1) IP camera**. Technician must be proficient in diagnosing issues involving **PoE switches, network connections, access points, and CAT cabling**.\n\nPlease **do not request this work order** if you are not equipped or skilled to perform IP camera diagnostics.\n\n**Photos are required** before and after troubleshooting, including:\n\n- The manager’s camera view or NVR screen\n- Camera model and serial number labels\n- Any exposed cable runs or conduit conditions (installed, damaged, or missing)\n\nThorough notes must be included for all findings and actions taken.\n\n**Scope of Work:**\n\nUpon arrival, the Technician must **check in with the General Manager** and inform them they are with **IBA** to troubleshoot the offline camera.\n\nThe Manager will identify the camera location and assist with access as needed.\n\nThe affected camera will be connected via **CAT5 or CAT6 cabling** to a **PoE switch** located in either the **Main Building**, **Shop Building**, or **Pole-mounted cabinet**.\n\nSome outdoor cameras may require an extension ladder or lift for access.\n\nIf applicable, a **40’ articulating boom lift will be available on-site** for this task.\n\nTechnician must be **trained and authorized to operate a boom lift** — otherwise, this work order cannot be accepted.\n\n**Troubleshooting Steps:**\n\n1. **Visually inspect** camera, cabling, and mounting area for damage or loose connections.\n2. **Test the PoE connection** using an IP camera tester with built-in PoE.\n3. **Check the network link** between the camera and the PoE switch.\n4. If the camera is offline, **verify link lights** and test the cable for continuity or damage.\n5. If the camera has been reset to defaults, **reconfigure network settings** with assistance from remote support.\n6. **Confirm camera visibility** on the NVR or management software once restored.\n\nContact **Joshua Myers (918-813-1569)** or **Drew Dimatos (214-773-6902)** for remote configuration support as needed.\n\nSupport may be provided through **TeamViewer**, **AnyDesk**, or **Quick Assist** as needed.\n\n**Documentation Requirements:**\n\n- Before and after photos of the camera and manager’s screen\n- Photo of camera model/serial number label\n- Notes detailing the issue, diagnostic steps, and final outcome\n- Photos of any damaged or exposed cables/conduit\n\n**Required Equipment and Tools:**\n\n- **Tall Extension Ladder** (up to 22’ if needed)\n- **Laptop and Hotspot** (with *Advanced IP Scanner* installed)\n- **Monitor, Keyboard, and Mouse** (for NVR access if necessary)\n- **IP Camera Tester with built-in PoE** (NOT an analog tester)\n- **Cable Tester**\n- Standard networking tools and materials:\n- RJ-45 connectors, CAT6 cable, termination/crimp tools\n- Screwdrivers, drill, snips, labeler, pull string\n\nTechnician is responsible for providing all required tools and materials to complete this troubleshooting work order.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00","end":"2026-09-28T16:00"},"payRange":{"min":300,"max":300},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":3,"distance":43},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $300 is below minimum threshold $400"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Miniso Durham"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"Remote Hands - Connect AT&T broadband circuit"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790101002667}
{"job":{"id":20006222,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"CPT Network Solutions, Inc.","title":"Qbit Player Swap","description":{"html":"<p><strong><u>High Level Overview</u></strong></p><p>Technicians&nbsp;are&nbsp;to&nbsp;replace&nbsp;the existing Mood Media device with the Qbit audio play system.</p><p>This job is expected to take 30 minutes to one hour.</p><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Required Tools to Bring to Site:</u></strong></p><ol><li>Standard&nbsp;technician&nbsp;toolset</li><li>Label Maker</li><li>Screwdrivers</li><li>Phone</li><li>Spare Cat6 cables (3ft and 6ft)</li><li>Cable tester</li><li>Butt Set</li><li>Punch-Down Tool and Wire Strippers</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Scope of Work</u></strong></p><ol><li>Check-In&nbsp;and&nbsp;Coordination</li><li>Remove&nbsp;Mood Media device</li><li>Mount and connect Qbit device</li><li>Call QSIC to confirm connectivity</li><li>Test audio in store</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Deliverables</u></strong></p><ol><li>Picture&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;new&nbsp;QSIC&nbsp;player&nbsp;installed</li><li>Photos&nbsp;of&nbsp;Completed&nbsp;Install</li></ol>","markdown":"**High Level Overview**\n\nTechnicians are to replace the existing Mood Media device with the Qbit audio play system.\n\nThis job is expected to take 30 minutes to one hour.\n\n**Required Tools to Bring to Site:**\n\n1. Standard technician toolset\n2. Label Maker\n3. Screwdrivers\n4. Phone\n5. Spare Cat6 cables (3ft and 6ft)\n6. Cable tester\n7. Butt Set\n8. Punch-Down Tool and Wire Strippers\n\n**Scope of Work**\n\n1. Check-In and Coordination\n2. Remove Mood Media device\n3. Mount and connect Qbit device\n4. Call QSIC to confirm connectivity\n5. Test audio in store\n\n**Deliverables**\n\n1. Picture of the new QSIC player installed\n2. Photos of Completed Install","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-30T08:00","end":"2026-09-30T09:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":60},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":16},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $60 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T15:00:00.000Z","summary":"Remote Hands - Connect AT&T broadband circuit"},{"start":"2026-09-14T19:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"Device offline**See required tools**"}],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790101034192}
{"job":{"id":20006440,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Zayo Group","title":"Pick Up Equipment At UPS Prior to Arrival - install a VeloCloud, Wattbox, Cradlepoint, & NetGear switch | Est. Duration of Install: 2.5hrs","description":{"html":"<p><u>﻿</u><strong><u>OVERVIEW:</u></strong></p><ul><li>In need of a technician to pick-up equipment at a local UPS depot &amp; work with a remote team to install &amp; test a VeloCloud, Wattbox, Cradlepoint, new wireline circuit/modem, and NetGear switch</li><li>Estimated duration of install is 2.5hrs</li></ul><p><strong><u>Requirements/Expectation:</u></strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">Arrive at equipment pick-up location and call the <del>**********</del>&nbsp;team at the scheduled hard start time to check in</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">The equipment pick-up location can be found in the work order under the&nbsp;<strong><u>\"Pre-site Pickup\"</u></strong>&nbsp;section</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tech is picking up the equipment at a local <strong><u>UPS depot</u></strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\"><u>Ensure You Bring a Valid Government-Issued Photo ID (e.g. Driver's License)</u></strong></li><li>If gas/travel is required, it must be requested as a counter offer for review before the ticket is assigned. Any requests made after assignment may be denied</li><li><strong>MUST</strong>&nbsp;have the tools required listed in the “Service Description” section in the event they are needed. Note that materials used that remain onsite (e.g. cabling) can be reimbursed as an expense.</li><li>Exhibit professional behavior at all times (escalate to the Field Nation project manager listed in the work order with any issues)</li></ul><p><strong><u>Dress code:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Business casual, Close-toed shoes, pants no holes, no short tanks, no sleeveless shirts</li></ul><p><strong><u>Tools Required:</u></strong></p><ul><li>Laptop with charger&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li>Laptop with Ethernet &amp; internet capability</li><li>Console Cable</li><li>Smart phone with access to the internet</li><li>Smart phone with a camera</li><li>Smart phone fully charged and with a charger</li><li>Mobile hotspot</li><li>Ethernet patch cables: Quantity of three-five 3ft -6ft cat5e/cat6 patch cables (6ft patch cables would be best)</li><li>6” or 8' A Frame Ladder&nbsp;</li><li>100ft Cat5e/Cat6 Ethernet cabling&nbsp;</li><li>Standard network cabling tools&nbsp;</li><li>Cable punch down and termination tools</li><li>Cable stripper, cutter, &amp; crimper</li><li>Network cable tester</li><li>Network cable toner</li><li>Basic tools (screwdrivers, drill, tape measure, wrenches, etc)</li><li>Standard drill bit set</li><li>Tools for either rack mounting or wall mounting equipment</li><li>&nbsp;Fishtape</li><li>Push/Pull Rods</li><li>Label maker&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong><u>Pre-Site requirements:</u></strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>Review the work order information prior to the scheduled dispatch</li></ul><p><strong><u>On-Site Tasks:</u></strong></p><ol><li><strong>IMPORTANT</strong>:&nbsp;<strong>You are required to reference the </strong><strong style=\"color: rgb(238, 0, 0);\">‘Confidential Information’</strong><strong> section&nbsp;<em><u>IF</u></em>&nbsp;any additional details regarding this dispatch are posted</strong></li><li>When you arrive at the pick-up location, call&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************</del></span>&nbsp;to check in with the&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>****</del></span>&nbsp;Activations team</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Note:</strong>&nbsp;If you arrive at the install location before the scheduled Activation time listed in the&nbsp;<strong>custom field</strong>&nbsp;<strong>labeled</strong>&nbsp;'<strong><u>Activations Time',</u></strong>&nbsp;you may be able to start early if an Activation resource is available; otherwise, please wait until the scheduled Activations time</li><li><span style=\"color: black;\">Check in with the the manager on duty/local contact (MOD/LCON)</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">See customer field '<span style=\"color: rgb(16, 29, 113);\">Site Contact Name &amp; Number' for MOD/LCON information (may just list&nbsp;</span>MOD/LCON<span style=\"color: rgb(16, 29, 113);\">&nbsp;and not a specific person)</span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Note:</strong>&nbsp;The MOD/LCON may not be familiar with the SOW, so please check in with the manager on duty upon arrival at both the pick-up and install locations</li><li>Upon arrival at the install location, call&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>************</del></span>&nbsp;to connect with the&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>**********</del></span>Activations team and begin unboxing and setting up all equipment</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Important: Tech must work with the&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>****</del></span>&nbsp;team through the Install process which may include troubleshooting any of the networking equipment being installed</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If applicable, report a problem and/or message the <del>****</del> Dispatch team via Field Nation to request a time change if delays from a Public Storage install scheduled earlier that day cause you to arrive early or late</li><li>Connect Equipment Power to the Wattbox controller ports</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Broadband power to Wattbox Controller 1</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Cradlepoint power to Wattbox Controller 2</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">VeloCloud power to Wattbox Controller 3</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">NetGear power to Wattbox Controller 4</li><li>Identify the New&nbsp;<del>****</del><strong><del>******</del></strong>Broadband transport (if applicable) and the Cradlepoint LTE</li><li>Connect the Broadband transport to the GE1 port of the VeloCloud</li><li>Work with the&nbsp;<del>**********</del>team<strong>&nbsp;</strong>to test and confirm connectivity of the Broadband transport&nbsp;</li><li>Confirm with the<del>****</del> team how the modem needs labeled and label it accordingly</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Take a picture of the labelled modem</li><li>Swap out the existing Cradlepoint SIM card with the new&nbsp;<del>****</del><strong><del>******</del></strong>provided SIM</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>&nbsp;WARNING: ENSURE YOU INSTERT THE CORRECT SIZE SIM CARD. YOU MAY NOT BE ABLE TO REMOVE THE SMALLER SIM CARD IF INSTALLED IN ERROR AND WILL RESULT IN A CRADLEPOINT REPLACEMENT. DOUBLE CHECK WITH THE ACTIVATIONS REPRESENTATIVE TO ENSURE YOU ARE INSERTING THE CORRECT SIZE FOR THE RESPECTIVE CRADLEPOINT MODEL. SEE BELOW SIM INFORMATION FOR REFERENCE (Pictures of SIM cards also available in the attached guide)</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>CBA850=2FF-MINI SIZED SIM CARD</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>IBR600 SERIES=2FF-MINI SIZED SIM CARD</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>CBA850=2FF-MINI SIZED SIM CARD</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>L950=4FF-NANO SIZED SIM CARD</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>W1850=4FF-NANO SIZED SIM CARD</strong></li><li>Connect the Cradlepoint to the GE2 port of the VeloCloud</li><li>Work with&nbsp;<del>****</del><strong><del>******</del></strong>team&nbsp;to test and confirm connectivity of the Cradlepoint</li><li>Confirm with the<del>****</del>&nbsp;team how the Cradlepoint in production needs labeled and label it accordingly</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Take a picture of the labeled Cradlepoint that is in production</li><li>Label any Cradlepoint model that's an ARC 750 or an 850 that is<strong>NOT</strong> in production with the following and leave it onsite</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If the Cradlepoint that is<strong>NOT</strong> in production is broken, label it “Broken”</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">If the Cradlepoint that is<strong>NOT</strong> in production and is intact and working, label it ”Back up, not used”</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Take a picture of the labeled Cradlepoint that is <strong>NOT</strong> in production</li><li>Verify with the&nbsp;<del>****</del><strong><del>******</del></strong>team that the VeloCloud is online with both transports</li><li>Connect VeloCloud GE3 to NetGear switch port8</li><li>Connect VeloCloud GE4 to Wattbox Network Port</li><li>Move Customer existing LAN connections from old VeloCloud to new NetGear switch ports 1-7</li><li>Request verification from the&nbsp;<del>**********</del>team that you are approved to begin testing with local user</li><li>Ensure ALL systems are online by testing-The&nbsp;<del>**********</del>team&nbsp;representative will verify what systems to test</li></ol><p><strong><u>Required On-Site Deliverables:</u></strong></p><ol><li>Finishing up:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Take a picture showing the completed VeloCloud setup</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Email the picture to the&nbsp;<del>****</del>&nbsp;team (note that the&nbsp;<del>****</del>&nbsp;team may ask for more pictures during the installation to better assist with the installation)-<strong><del>****************</del></strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If applicable, hand the old Edge device to the manager on duty</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If applicable, take the old Modem that we disconnected putting it in one of the empty boxes and hand it over to the manager on duty onsite, record the name of that MOD. (This step is for sites with a successful modem replacement)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Upload pictures to work order</li></ol><p><strong><u>Escalations:</u></strong></p><p>For any questions regarding the SOW, arrival delays, or onsite concerns, please reach out to the appropriate Field Nation work order manager during the hours listed below:</p><p><strong>Contact Hours:</strong></p><p><strong><u>8:00 AM &ndash; 5:00 PM Eastern</u></strong></p><ul><li><del>***** ************</del></li><li><del>****** ************</del></li></ul><p><strong><u>2:00 PM &ndash; 11:00 PM Eastern</u></strong></p><ul><li><del>******** ******************</del></li></ul>","markdown":"﻿**OVERVIEW:**\n\n- In need of a technician to pick-up equipment at a local UPS depot & work with a remote team to install & test a VeloCloud, Wattbox, Cradlepoint, new wireline circuit/modem, and NetGear switch\n- Estimated duration of install is 2.5hrs\n\n**Requirements/Expectation:**\n\n- **Arrive at equipment pick-up location and call the \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* team at the scheduled hard start time to check in**\n- The equipment pick-up location can be found in the work order under the **\"Pre-site Pickup\"** section\n- Tech is picking up the equipment at a local **UPS depot**\n- **Ensure You Bring a Valid Government-Issued Photo ID (e.g. Driver's License)**\n- If gas/travel is required, it must be requested as a counter offer for review before the ticket is assigned. Any requests made after assignment may be denied\n- **MUST** have the tools required listed in the “Service Description” section in the event they are needed. Note that materials used that remain onsite (e.g. cabling) can be reimbursed as an expense.\n- Exhibit professional behavior at all times (escalate to the Field Nation project manager listed in the work order with any issues)\n\n**Dress code:**\n\n- Business casual, Close-toed shoes, pants no holes, no short tanks, no sleeveless shirts\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Laptop with charger\n- Laptop with Ethernet & internet capability\n- Console Cable\n- Smart phone with access to the internet\n- Smart phone with a camera\n- Smart phone fully charged and with a charger\n- Mobile hotspot\n- Ethernet patch cables: Quantity of three-five 3ft -6ft cat5e/cat6 patch cables (6ft patch cables would be best)\n- 6” or 8' A Frame Ladder\n- 100ft Cat5e/Cat6 Ethernet cabling\n- Standard network cabling tools\n- Cable punch down and termination tools\n- Cable stripper, cutter, & crimper\n- Network cable tester\n- Network cable toner\n- Basic tools (screwdrivers, drill, tape measure, wrenches, etc)\n- Standard drill bit set\n- Tools for either rack mounting or wall mounting equipment\n- Fishtape\n- Push/Pull Rods\n- Label maker\n\n**Pre-Site requirements:**\n\n- Review the work order information prior to the scheduled dispatch\n\n**On-Site Tasks:**\n\n1. **IMPORTANT**: **You are required to reference the** **‘Confidential Information’** **section *IF* any additional details regarding this dispatch are posted**\n2. When you arrive at the pick-up location, call \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* to check in with the \\*\\*\\*\\* Activations team\n3. **Note:** If you arrive at the install location before the scheduled Activation time listed in the **custom field** **labeled** '**Activations Time',** you may be able to start early if an Activation resource is available; otherwise, please wait until the scheduled Activations time\n4. Check in with the the manager on duty/local contact (MOD/LCON)\n5. See customer field 'Site Contact Name & Number' for MOD/LCON information (may just list MOD/LCON and not a specific person)\n6. **Note:** The MOD/LCON may not be familiar with the SOW, so please check in with the manager on duty upon arrival at both the pick-up and install locations\n7. Upon arrival at the install location, call \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* to connect with the \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*Activations team and begin unboxing and setting up all equipment\n8. Important: Tech must work with the \\*\\*\\*\\* team through the Install process which may include troubleshooting any of the networking equipment being installed\n9. If applicable, report a problem and/or message the \\*\\*\\*\\* Dispatch team via Field Nation to request a time change if delays from a Public Storage install scheduled earlier that day cause you to arrive early or late\n10. Connect Equipment Power to the Wattbox controller ports\n11. Broadband power to Wattbox Controller 1\n12. Cradlepoint power to Wattbox Controller 2\n13. VeloCloud power to Wattbox Controller 3\n14. NetGear power to Wattbox Controller 4\n15. Identify the New \\*\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***Broadband transport (if applicable) and the Cradlepoint LTE\n16. Connect the Broadband transport to the GE1 port of the VeloCloud\n17. Work with the \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*team to test and confirm connectivity of the Broadband transport\n18. Confirm with the\\*\\*\\*\\* team how the modem needs labeled and label it accordingly\n19. Take a picture of the labelled modem\n20. Swap out the existing Cradlepoint SIM card with the new \\*\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***provided SIM\n21. **WARNING: ENSURE YOU INSTERT THE CORRECT SIZE SIM CARD. YOU MAY NOT BE ABLE TO REMOVE THE SMALLER SIM CARD IF INSTALLED IN ERROR AND WILL RESULT IN A CRADLEPOINT REPLACEMENT. DOUBLE CHECK WITH THE ACTIVATIONS REPRESENTATIVE TO ENSURE YOU ARE INSERTING THE CORRECT SIZE FOR THE RESPECTIVE CRADLEPOINT MODEL. SEE BELOW SIM INFORMATION FOR REFERENCE (Pictures of SIM cards also available in the attached guide)**\n22. **CBA850=2FF-MINI SIZED SIM CARD**\n23. **IBR600 SERIES=2FF-MINI SIZED SIM CARD**\n24. **CBA850=2FF-MINI SIZED SIM CARD**\n25. **L950=4FF-NANO SIZED SIM CARD**\n26. **W1850=4FF-NANO SIZED SIM CARD**\n27. Connect the Cradlepoint to the GE2 port of the VeloCloud\n28. Work with \\*\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***team to test and confirm connectivity of the Cradlepoint\n29. Confirm with the\\*\\*\\*\\* team how the Cradlepoint in production needs labeled and label it accordingly\n30. Take a picture of the labeled Cradlepoint that is in production\n31. Label any Cradlepoint model that's an ARC 750 or an 850 that is**NOT** in production with the following and leave it onsite\n32. If the Cradlepoint that is**NOT** in production is broken, label it “Broken”\n33. If the Cradlepoint that is**NOT** in production and is intact and working, label it ”Back up, not used”\n34. Take a picture of the labeled Cradlepoint that is **NOT** in production\n35. Verify with the \\*\\*\\*\\***\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***team that the VeloCloud is online with both transports\n36. Connect VeloCloud GE3 to NetGear switch port8\n37. Connect VeloCloud GE4 to Wattbox Network Port\n38. Move Customer existing LAN connections from old VeloCloud to new NetGear switch ports 1-7\n39. Request verification from the \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*team that you are approved to begin testing with local user\n40. Ensure ALL systems are online by testing-The \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*team representative will verify what systems to test\n\n**Required On-Site Deliverables:**\n\n1. Finishing up:\n2. Take a picture showing the completed VeloCloud setup\n3. Email the picture to the \\*\\*\\*\\* team (note that the \\*\\*\\*\\* team may ask for more pictures during the installation to better assist with the installation)-**\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n4. If applicable, hand the old Edge device to the manager on duty\n5. If applicable, take the old Modem that we disconnected putting it in one of the empty boxes and hand it over to the manager on duty onsite, record the name of that MOD. (This step is for sites with a successful modem replacement)\n6. Upload pictures to work order\n\n**Escalations:**\n\nFor any questions regarding the SOW, arrival delays, or onsite concerns, please reach out to the appropriate Field Nation work order manager during the hours listed below:\n\n**Contact Hours:**\n\n**8:00 AM – 5:00 PM Eastern**\n\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**2:00 PM – 11:00 PM Eastern**\n\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-05T10:00","end":"2026-10-05T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":165},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":1,"amount":75},"additional":{"units":1.5,"amount":60}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":28},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $165 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[],"busyBlocks":[],"action":"SKIP","ts":1790101848789}
{"job":{"id":"5867308066","platform":"WorkMarket","company":"Granite Telecommunications","title":"Herc 9325 Raleigh NC WO","description":"<p>Property Name: Herc 9325, Raleigh, NC</p><p>Address: 1409 Capital Blvd. Raleigh, US-NC, US 27603</p><p>Local Contact Info: Chris Koliadko 919-754-5211 Email: Christopher.Koliadko@hercrentals.com</p><p>HERC IT Contact: Leif Bowman (503) 810-8776 Email : Leif.Bowman@Hercrentals.com</p><p>Scope of Work needed: DO NOT WORK ON ANY ITEMS NOT SPECIFIED IN SOW BELOW</p><p>PLEASE CONTACT THE FSA IN THE SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS IF ENCOUNTER ANY ISSUES AND BEFORE LEAVING SITE Issue: There is low hum feedback over the intercom system. This is likely caused by the Bogen UTI Tech requirements: Analog phone or Butt set, cable testing and termination tools, RJ11 cabling (30 – 50 ft)</p><p>1. Contact LCON Chris Koliadko when arriving onsite</p><p>2. Call and check in with Herc IT Leif Bowman</p><p>3. Locate the MDF and telecom boards. Bogen intercom system is on 1st floor, MDF is on 2nd floor above</p><p>4. There is currently a Cat5 spliced with a RJ11 head connecting from the ATA in the MDF to the UTI paging interface. Replace this line with a direct RJ11.</p><p>5. Once replaced. Check for remaining noise in the line and work with the LCON to test paging. If the issue persists, follow the guide provided, use analog phone or Butt set to reprogram the UTI</p><p>6. If issue still persist, Work with Herc IT Leif to troubleshoot further</p><p>7. Provide photos of replaced RJ45 line to Herc IT Leif</p><p>8. Call IT contact to check out</p><p>Special Instructions (if any) ** Identify if work is to be completed after hours or is certification needed</p><p>** MUST HAVE SAFETY GEAR: Boots, safety glasses, Bright colored/reflective safety vest </p><p>***PLEASE CONTACT LEIF BOWMAN 503-810-8776 BEFORE LEAVING SITE OR ENCOUNTER ANY ISSUES/PROBLEMS. DO NOT WORK ON ANYTHING THAT IS NOT INCLUDED IN THE SCOPE OF WORK ABOVE</p>","isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"st