{"job":{"id":20006722,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"SpotOn","title":"POS Site Survey and Cabling Verification","description":{"html":"<strong>Overview</strong><ul><li>Seeking a technician with experience in POS installations, networking, and site surveys.</li><li>Technician is required to perform a pre-installation site inspection for a SpotOn POS deployment.</li><li>Estimated duration will be 1 hour</li></ul><strong>Dress Code</strong><ul><li>Business casual attire.</li><li>Professional appearance required when interacting with restaurant management and staff.</li></ul><strong>Tools Required</strong><ul><li>Network cable toner and tester</li><li>Laptop</li><li>Label maker or cable labels</li><li>Camera or smartphone for site photos</li><li>Internet speed testing capability</li><li>Basic hand tools as needed</li></ul><strong>Pre-Site Requirements</strong><ol><li>Review the Site Inspection form and all project documentation.</li><li>Contact the site Point of Contact (POC) to confirm the inspection date and time.</li><li>Review hardware counts and deployment requirements.</li><li>Familiarize yourself with SpotOn network and connectivity requirements.</li></ol><strong>On-Site Tasks</strong><ol><li>Check in through the work order and introduce yourself to the site manager.</li><li>Review equipment counts with the POC.</li><li>Walk the site and identify proposed locations for all POS equipment.</li><li>Document and record each device location.</li><li>Create a diagram showing placement of terminals, printers, payment devices, KDS screens, and other hardware.</li><li>Tone and test cabling for future printer and KDS locations.</li><li>Perform a hardwired internet speed test.</li><li>Verify all POS devices can reside on the same wired network.</li><li>Label POS cabling and network ports.</li><li>Document any site readiness issues, including missing cabling, power, or construction concerns.</li><li><strong>Complete the site inspection form here: </strong>cognitoforms.com/SPOTON3/SiteInspectionResponsesFieldNation</li></ol><strong>Required On-Site Deliverables</strong><ol><li><strong>Completed Site Inspection form.</strong></li><li>Photos showing Ethernet and power availability for all stations, printers, and KDS locations.</li><li>Network speed test results.</li><li>Site diagram showing all equipment locations.</li><li>Documentation of any equipment additions/removals or site readiness concerns.</li><li>Technician and client/POC signatures.</li><li>If additional cabling is required, please provide a quote for labor and materials for cabling on this work order</li></ol><strong>Escalation Process</strong><ul><li>If equipment counts do not match project documentation, contact the project coordinator.</li><li>Escalate any network, cabling, power, or construction concerns before leaving the site.</li><li>Escalate any questions that prevent completion of the inspection to the SpotOn implementation team.</li></ul><strong>Additional Hours &amp; Expenses Approval Policy</strong><ul><li>Additional labor, travel, or material expenses must be approved before being incurred.</li><li>Do not perform work outside the defined scope without approval.</li><li>Notify the project coordinator immediately if additional work is identified.</li></ul>","markdown":"**Overview**- Seeking a technician with experience in POS installations, networking, and site surveys.\n- Technician is required to perform a pre-installation site inspection for a SpotOn POS deployment.\n- Estimated duration will be 1 hour\n\n**Dress Code**- Business casual attire.\n- Professional appearance required when interacting with restaurant management and staff.\n\n**Tools Required**- Network cable toner and tester\n- Laptop\n- Label maker or cable labels\n- Camera or smartphone for site photos\n- Internet speed testing capability\n- Basic hand tools as needed\n\n**Pre-Site Requirements**1. Review the Site Inspection form and all project documentation.\n2. Contact the site Point of Contact (POC) to confirm the inspection date and time.\n3. Review hardware counts and deployment requirements.\n4. Familiarize yourself with SpotOn network and connectivity requirements.\n\n**On-Site Tasks**1. Check in through the work order and introduce yourself to the site manager.\n2. Review equipment counts with the POC.\n3. Walk the site and identify proposed locations for all POS equipment.\n4. Document and record each device location.\n5. Create a diagram showing placement of terminals, printers, payment devices, KDS screens, and other hardware.\n6. Tone and test cabling for future printer and KDS locations.\n7. Perform a hardwired internet speed test.\n8. Verify all POS devices can reside on the same wired network.\n9. Label POS cabling and network ports.\n10. Document any site readiness issues, including missing cabling, power, or construction concerns.\n11. **Complete the site inspection form here:** cognitoforms.com/SPOTON3/SiteInspectionResponsesFieldNation\n\n**Required On-Site Deliverables**1. **Completed Site Inspection form.**\n2. Photos showing Ethernet and power availability for all stations, printers, and KDS locations.\n3. Network speed test results.\n4. Site diagram showing all equipment locations.\n5. Documentation of any equipment additions/removals or site readiness concerns.\n6. Technician and client/POC signatures.\n7. If additional cabling is required, please provide a quote for labor and materials for cabling on this work order\n\n**Escalation Process**- If equipment counts do not match project documentation, contact the project coordinator.\n- Escalate any network, cabling, power, or construction concerns before leaving the site.\n- Escalate any questions that prevent completion of the inspection to the SpotOn implementation team.\n\n**Additional Hours & Expenses Approval Policy**- Additional labor, travel, or material expenses must be approved before being incurred.\n- Do not perform work outside the defined scope without approval.\n- Notify the project coordinator immediately if additional work is identified.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-29T09:30","end":"2026-09-29T12:00"},"payRange":{"min":250,"max":250},"payType":"fixed","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":2.5,"distance":11},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $250 is below minimum threshold $400"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Miniso Durham"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T20:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974915-The Edition on Rosemary-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-22T19:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T23:30:00.000Z","summary":"Fast Food Restaurant #4945 — Refranchise Conversion — Oxford, NC"},{"start":"2026-09-22T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-22T15:0