ong>&nbsp;If you arrive at the install location before the scheduled Activation time listed in the&nbsp;<strong>custom field</strong>&nbsp;<strong>labeled</strong>&nbsp;'<strong><u>Activation Time',</u></strong>&nbsp;you may be able to start early if an Activation resource is available; otherwise, please wait until the scheduled Activations time</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Important: Tech must work with the&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>****</del></span>&nbsp;Activations team through the Install process which may include troubleshooting any of the networking equipment being installed</li><li>Upon arrival at the install location, call&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>******************</del></span>to connect with the <del>**** </del>Activations team and begin unboxing and setting up all equipment</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Install the VeloCloud, Wattbox, NetGear switch</li><li>Connect Equipment Power to the Wattbox controller ports</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Broadband power to Wattbox Controller 1</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Cradlepoint power to Wattbox Controller 2</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">VeloCloud power to Wattbox Controller 3</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">NetGear power to Wattbox Controller 4</li><li>Identify the New <del>****</del> Broadband transport (if applicable) and the Cradlepoint LTE</li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(64, 64, 64);\">C</span><span style=\"color: black;\">onnect the Broadband transport to the GE1 port of the VeloCloud</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(64, 64, 64);\">Work with the </span><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>****</del></span> team <span style=\"color: rgb(64, 64, 64);\">to test and confirm connectivity of the Broadband transport </span><span style=\"color: black;\">&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(64, 64, 64);\">Confirm with the <del>****</del> team how the modem needs labeled and label it accordingly </span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><span style=\"color: rgb(64, 64, 64);\">Take a picture of the labeled modem</span></li><li>Insert the correct size SIM Card in the Cradlepoint and power on the device</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong style=\"color: red;\">&nbsp;WARNING: ENSURE YOU INSTERT THE CORRECT SIZE SIM CARD. YOU MAY NOT BE ABLE TO REMOVE THE SMALLER SIM CARD IF INSTALLED IN ERROR AND WILL RESULT IN A CRADLEPOINT REPLACEMENT. DOUBLE CHECK WITH THE ACTIVATIONS REPRESENTATIVE TO ENSURE YOU ARE INSERTING THE CORRECT SIZE FOR THE RESPECTIVE CRADLEPOINT MODEL. SEE BELOW SIM INFORMATION FOR REFERENCE (Pictures of SIM cards also available in the attached guide)</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong style=\"color: red;\">CBA850=2FF-MINI SIZED SIM CARD</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong style=\"color: red;\">IBR600 SERIES=2FF-MINI SIZED SIM CARD</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong style=\"color: red;\">CBA850=2FF-MINI SIZED SIM CARD</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong style=\"color: red;\">L950=4FF-NANO SIZED SIM CARD</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong style=\"color: red;\">W1850=4FF-NANO SIZED SIM CARD</strong></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(64, 64, 64);\">Connect the Cradlepoint to the GE2 port of the VeloCloud</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(64, 64, 64);\">Work with </span><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>****</del></span> team <span style=\"color: rgb(64, 64, 64);\">to test and confirm connectivity of the Cradlepoint </span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(64, 64, 64);\">Confirm with the <del>****</del> team how the Cradlepoint needs labeled and label it accordingly </span></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">T<span style=\"color: rgb(64, 64, 64);\">ake a picture of the labeled Cradlepoint that is in production</span></li><li>Verify with the <span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>****</del></span> team that the VeloCloud is online with both transports</li><li>Connect VeloCloud GE3 to NetGear switch port8</li><li>Connect VeloCloud GE4 to Wattbox Network Port</li><li>Move Customer existing LAN connections from old VeloCloud to new NetGear switch ports 1-7</li><li>Request verification from the <span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>****</del></span> team that you are approved to begin testing with local user</li><li>Ensure ALL systems are online by testing-The <span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><del>****</del></span> team will verify what systems to test</li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Required On-Site Deliverables:</u></strong></p><ol><li>Finishing up:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Take a picture showing the completed VeloCloud setup</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Upload pictures to work order</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Email pictures to the <del>****</del> team - <strong><del>****************</del></strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>If applicable, hand the old Edge device to the manager on duty</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>If applicable, take the old Modem that we disconnected putting it in one of the empty boxes and hand it over to the manager on duty onsite, record the name of that MOD. (This step is for sites with a successful modem replacement)</strong></li></ol><p><br></p><p><strong><u>Escalations:</u></strong></p><p>For any questions regarding the SOW, arrival delays, or onsite concerns, please reach out to the appropriate Field Nation work order manager during the hours listed below:</p><p><strong>Contact Hours:</strong></p><p><strong><u>8:00 AM &ndash; 5:00 PM Eastern</u></strong></p><ul><li><del>***** ************</del></li><li><del>****** ************</del></li></ul><p><strong><u>2:00 PM &ndash; 11:00 PM Eastern</u></strong></p><ul><li><del>******** ******************</del></li></ul>","markdown":"﻿**OVERVIEW:**\n\n- In need of a technician to pick-up equipment & work with a remote team to install & test a VeloCloud, Wattbox, Cradlepoint, new wireline circuit/modem, and NetGear switch\n- Estimated duration of install is 2.5hrs\n\n**Requirements/Expectation:**\n\n- **Arrive at equipment pick-up location and call the****\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*** **Activations team at the scheduled hard start time**\n- The equipment pick-up location can be found in the work order under the **\"Pre-site Pickup\"** section\n- If gas/travel is required, it must be requested as a counter offer for review before the ticket is assigned. Any requests made after assignment may be denied\n- **MUST** have the tools required listed in the “Service Description” section in the event they are needed. Note that materials used that remain onsite (e.g. cabling) can be reimbursed as an expense.\n- Exhibit professional behavior at all times (escalate to the Field Nation project manager listed in the work order with any issues)\n\n**Dress code:**\n\n- Business casual Close-toed shoes, pants no holes, no short tanks, no sleeveless shirts\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Laptop with Ethernet connection\n- Laptop with console cable\n- Laptop with charger\n- Standard network cabling tools\n- Basic hand tools\n- 6-8' ladder\n- Cable tester\n- 3ft -6ft cat5e/cat6 patch cables quantity 3-5 cables (6ft patch cables would be best)\n- Smart phone with camera\n- Smartphone with access to the internet\n- Label maker\n- 100ft Cat5e/Cat6 Ethernet cabling\n\n**Pre-Site requirements:**\n\n- Review the work order information prior to the scheduled dispatch\n- Buyer will contact technician 1 business day prior to the scheduled dispatch to confirm date/time/location\n\n**On-Site Tasks:**.503.2553\n\n1. **IMPORTANT**: **You are required to reference the ‘****Confidential Information****’ section *IF* any additional details regarding this dispatch are posted**\n2. Check in with the the manager on duty/local contact (MOD/LCON)\n3. See customer field 'Site Contact Name & Number' for MOD/LCON information (may just list MOD/LCON and not a specific person)\n4. **Note:** The MOD/LCON may not be familiar with the SOW, so please check in with the manager on duty upon arrival at both the pick-up and install locations\n5. When you arrive at the pick-up location, call \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* to check in with the \\*\\*\\*\\* Activations team\n6. **Note:** If you arrive at the install location before the scheduled Activation time listed in the **custom field** **labeled** '**Activation Time',** you may be able to start early if an Activation resource is available; otherwise, please wait until the scheduled Activations time\n7. Important: Tech must work with the \\*\\*\\*\\* Activations team through the Install process which may include troubleshooting any of the networking equipment being installed\n8. Upon arrival at the install location, call \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*to connect with the \\*\\*\\*\\* Activations team and begin unboxing and setting up all equipment\n9. Install the VeloCloud, Wattbox, NetGear switch\n10. Connect Equipment Power to the Wattbox controller ports\n11. Broadband power to Wattbox Controller 1\n12. Cradlepoint power to Wattbox Controller 2\n13. VeloCloud power to Wattbox Controller 3\n14. NetGear power to Wattbox Controller 4\n15. Identify the New \\*\\*\\*\\* Broadband transport (if applicable) and the Cradlepoint LTE\n16. Connect the Broadband transport to the GE1 port of the VeloCloud\n17. Work with the \\*\\*\\*\\* team to test and confirm connectivity of the Broadband transport\n18. Confirm with the \\*\\*\\*\\* team how the modem needs labeled and label it accordingly\n19. Take a picture of the labeled modem\n20. Insert the correct size SIM Card in the Cradlepoint and power on the device\n21. **WARNING: ENSURE YOU INSTERT THE CORRECT SIZE SIM CARD. YOU MAY NOT BE ABLE TO REMOVE THE SMALLER SIM CARD IF INSTALLED IN ERROR AND WILL RESULT IN A CRADLEPOINT REPLACEMENT. DOUBLE CHECK WITH THE ACTIVATIONS REPRESENTATIVE TO ENSURE YOU ARE INSERTING THE CORRECT SIZE FOR THE RESPECTIVE CRADLEPOINT MODEL. SEE BELOW SIM INFORMATION FOR REFERENCE (Pictures of SIM cards also available in the attached guide)**\n22. **CBA850=2FF-MINI SIZED SIM CARD**\n23. **IBR600 SERIES=2FF-MINI SIZED SIM CARD**\n24. **CBA850=2FF-MINI SIZED SIM CARD**\n25. **L950=4FF-NANO SIZED SIM CARD**\n26. **W1850=4FF-NANO SIZED SIM CARD**\n27. Connect the Cradlepoint to the GE2 port of the VeloCloud\n28. Work with \\*\\*\\*\\* team to test and confirm connectivity of the Cradlepoint\n29. Confirm with the \\*\\*\\*\\* team how the Cradlepoint needs labeled and label it accordingly\n30. Take a picture of the labeled Cradlepoint that is in production\n31. Verify with the \\*\\*\\*\\* team that the VeloCloud is online with both transports\n32. Connect VeloCloud GE3 to NetGear switch port8\n33. Connect VeloCloud GE4 to Wattbox Network Port\n34. Move Customer existing LAN connections from old VeloCloud to new NetGear switch ports 1-7\n35. Request verification from the \\*\\*\\*\\* team that you are approved to begin testing with local user\n36. Ensure ALL systems are online by testing-The \\*\\*\\*\\* team will verify what systems to test\n\n**Required On-Site Deliverables:**\n\n1. Finishing up:\n2. Take a picture showing the completed VeloCloud setup\n3. Upload pictures to work order\n4. Email pictures to the \\*\\*\\*\\* team - **\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\***\n5. **If applicable, hand the old Edge device to the manager on duty**\n6. **If applicable, take the old Modem that we disconnected putting it in one of the empty boxes and hand it over to the manager on duty onsite, record the name of that MOD. (This step is for sites with a successful modem replacement)**\n\n**Escalations:**\n\nFor any questions regarding the SOW, arrival delays, or onsite concerns, please reach out to the appropriate Field Nation work order manager during the hours listed below:\n\n**Contact Hours:**\n\n**8:00 AM – 5:00 PM Eastern**\n\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\n**2:00 PM – 11:00 PM Eastern**\n\n- \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* \\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-10-05T10:00","end":"2026-10-05T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":165},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":1,"amount":75},"additional":{"units":1.5,"amount":60}},"hourlyRate":0,"estLaborHours":1,"distance":28},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $165 is below minimum threshold $450"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-05T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-06T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-06T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-07T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-07T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-08T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-10T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-10-09T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-09T20:30:00.000Z","summary":"Vika USCIS biometry"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02207602 + Swarovksi - Swarovski #63 + epik cutover / revisit (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T17:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 164043 - BK-6563 - ROUTER REBOOT - NO EQUIPMENT (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-23T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-23T16:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 02478029-851 - Free People-EPIK Survey (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-05T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-05T17:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 05974921-University Glen-EPIK Survey 