{"job":{"id":20007018,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"LITnetworking LLC","title":"CIRCUIT TEST AND ACTIVATION/ MUST HAVE LAPTOP-DIS151413","description":{"html":"PLEASE CALL METTEL SUPPORT UPON ARRIVAL 212-607-2121 Ticket 11306035<br/><br/>Please call Daniel C. 212-607-2121 when you arrive onsite. If not reachable, please call remote support toll free # 844-905-9779 for assistance. Provide Bruin ticket number 11306035 to MetTel Rep.<br/><br/>\"GAP is requesting to retest and cutover circuit to the Stores Router on for 10/07/2026 @7:30 am  local time. This must start at 7:30am local time in order to complete prior to store opening at 10am. <br/><br/>Please call in to the following ZOOM Link:<br/>https://gapinc.zoom.us/j/4448080300?pwd=aHpCZm5uckpWQkV3ZVF2VWJheEdkUT09 <br/> <br/>Dial In: Mobile call one-tap (US Toll):  +13462487799,4448080300# or +12532050468,4448080300# <br/>Direct# 916-625-7797 <br/><br/>engineer: Michael Allen<br/><br/>TECHNICAL LCON: GENEVIEVE AMATO<br/>LCOT: 800-333-7899 ext. 66494  option3<br/>EMAIL: HQ-SNI-DG@gap.com\"<br/><br/>.<br/><br/>Please review the following requirements and protocols for your upcoming assignment with Lit Networking:<br/><br/>To ensure the successful completion of this site visit, you must arrive with the following tools and materials: - A fully charged laptop with an Ethernet port and a cellphone with a hotspot device. - Cabling tools: Multimeter wire tester, butt set, punch down tool, crimpers, and wire cutters. - Hardware: RJ11 and RJ45 connectors, biscuit jacks, and 100 feet of Cat 5e/6 cable for potential device relocation. - Standard mounting kit: Drill, level, hammer, screwdrivers, screws, and anchors. - General supplies: Adjustable or open-end wrenches, a 4–6 ft ladder, and a 100 ft extension cord.<br/><br/>Work Order and Payment Procedures All work orders must be signed by the onsite Point of Contact and must clearly list your arrival and departure times. Please upload the signed Lit Networking work order directly to Field Nation. Please be advised that any forged signatures will be reported to Field Nation and will result in non-payment. Adhering to these documentation requirements is essential to avoid any delays in your payment processing. If you encounter any issues while onsite, please leave a detailed message through the Field Nation platform.","markdown":"PLEASE CALL METTEL SUPPORT UPON ARRIVAL 212-607-2121 Ticket 11306035  \n  \nPlease call Daniel C. 212-607-2121 when you arrive onsite. If not reachable, please call remote support toll free # 844-905-9779 for assistance. Provide Bruin ticket number 11306035 to MetTel Rep.  \n  \n\"GAP is requesting to retest and cutover circuit to the Stores Router on for 10/07/2026 @7:30 am local time. This must start at 7:30am local time in order to complete prior to store opening at 10am.   \n  \nPlease call in to the following ZOOM Link:  \n<https://gapinc.zoom.us/j/4448080300?pwd=aHpCZm5uckpWQkV3ZVF2VWJheEdkUT09>   \n   \nDial In: Mobile call one-tap (US Toll): +13462487799,4448080300# or +12532050468,4448080300#   \nDirect# 916-625-7797   \n  \nengineer: Michael Allen  \n  \nTECHNICAL LCON: GENEVIEVE AMATO  \nLCOT: 800-333-7899 ext. 66494 option3  \nEMAIL: HQ-SNI-DG@gap.com\"  \n  \n.  \n  \nPlease review the following requirements and protocols for your upcoming assignment with Lit Networking:  \n  \nTo ensure the successful completion of this site visit, you must arrive with the following tools and materials: - A fully charged laptop with an Ethernet port and a cellphone with a hotspot device. - Cabling tools: Multimeter wire tester, butt set, punch down tool, crimpers, and wire cutters. - Hardware: RJ11 and RJ45 connectors, biscuit jacks, and 100 feet of Cat 5e/6 cable for potential device relocation. - Standard mounting kit: Drill, level, hammer, screwdrivers, screws, and anchors. - General supplies: Adjustable or open-end wrenches, a 4–6 ft ladder, and a 100 ft extension cord.  \n  \nWork Order and Payment Procedure