{"job":{"id":20007602,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Splice Communications","title":"Remove and Install 1 Access Points | 91594 - Holly Springs, NC","description":{"html":"<p><strong>PLEASE REPRESENT YOURSELF AS A SPLICE TECHNICIAN WHEN SPEAKING WITH ONSITE CONTACTS OR WITH CUSTOMER TECHNICAL CONTACTS.</strong></p>\n<p><strong><u>SCOPE OF WORK SUMMARY:</u></strong></p>\n<p>Technician needed to perform onsite replacement of existing access points (APs) with new units, in coordination with the Lead Engineer and site contact. Work must follow provided site plans, installation guides, and safety procedures.</p>\n<p>APs to replace: 1</p>\n<p><strong>PLEASE CHECK THE \"Site Plan - AP Replacement\" ATTACHMENT</strong> - This will guide you through the deployment.<u>PLEASE BRING A PRINTED COPY FOR YOUR ONSITE VISIT. MAKE SURE YOU REVIEW IT BEFORE GOING AND CALL SERVICE MANAGER IF ANY QUESTIONS.</u></p>\n<p><strong><u>IMPORTANT NOTE – SITE WALL/FACILITY PROTECTION</u></strong></p>\n<p>Technicians must take extra care to avoid damaging or marking walls while performing work onsite.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>When using ladders, technicians must place towels, padding, or other protective material between the ladder and the wall surface whenever applicable.</li>\n<li>Please avoid leaning ladders directly against painted walls or finished surfaces without protection.</li>\n<li>Technicians should also be mindful of dirty/stained hands or gloves when working near walls and ceilings to avoid leaving marks or smudges.</li>\n<li>Any accidental damage or wall markings must be reported and fixed immediately.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Please ensure all work areas are left clean and in the same condition as found upon arrival.</p>\n<p><strong>WORKFLOW</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Check in with Club Local Contact (LCON) and assigned Lead Engineer upon arrival</li>\n<li>Set up a staging area to unpack new APs, verify equipment count, brackets, and report any discrepancies</li>\n<li>Review the site plan and installation instructions with the Lead Engineer prior to starting work</li>\n<li>Confirm understanding of proper AP removal and installation procedures (including reviewing provided guides/videos)</li>\n<li>Safely dismount existing APs without forcing or damaging mounting brackets</li>\n<li>Install new APs and brackets according to the site plan and instructions</li>\n<li>Cross-check each AP swap against the provided spreadsheet to ensure correct device replacement</li>\n<li>Report any inconsistencies or issues immediately to the Service Manager and Lead Engineer</li>\n<li>Coordinate with site management and Lead Engineer if any obstacles or restrictions are encountered (e.g., locked areas, events, access limitations)</li>\n<li>Follow all safety protocols and consult with the Lead Engineer in any high-risk situation</li>\n<li>Perform installation work strictly per plan; any deviations must be approved by the Lead Engineer</li>\n<li>Capture and submit clear photos of each existing AP before removal.</li>\n<li>Capture and submit clear photos of new AP after installation. Make sure that it is a mid range picture, showing the location where it has been mounted. PLEASE label the picture with the name of the AP that you are replacing.</li>\n<li>Capture and submit clear photos of old APs properly packaged for return.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>End of Day Activities:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Package old APs in the original boxes of the new units</li>\n<li>Place individual boxes into larger shipping boxes</li>\n<li>Seal boxes and apply provided shipping labels (provided by LCON)</li>\n<li>Clean and organize the staging/work area</li>\n<li>Await final release from the Lead Engineer before leaving the site</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>JOB DURATION AND REQUIRED EXPERIENCE:</u></strong></p>\n<p>Duration:&nbsp;# hour(s)</p>\n<p>&nbsp;Experience:</p>\n<p>Technician will need to be proficient with wireless access point (AP) installation, replacement, and mounting procedures, including safe removal of existing units and proper installation of new APs and brackets. Must be able to follow site plans, equipment spreadsheets, and installation guides with attention to detail, ensuring correct device matching and placement. Technician should have experience with structured cabling and basic networking concepts, including PoE connectivity and verification of network status.</p>\n<p>Technician must be comfortable working at heights using ladders and lifts, following all safety protocols and best practices. Experience navigating ceiling spaces and working in active environments is required. Technician should be able to coordinate effectively with remote engineers via bridge calls (Microsoft Teams, etc.), follow detailed instructions, and communicate any discrepancies or onsite challenges in real time.</p>\n<p><strong><u>REQUIRED TOOLS:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Basic networking tools (IP configuration, testing utilities)</li>\n<li>Standard hand tools (screwdrivers, pliers, snips, etc.)</li>\n<li>Mounting hardware tools (drill, bits, anchors as needed)</li>\n<li>Measuring tape</li>\n<li>Label maker</li>\n<li>Patch cables (various lengths)</li>\n<li>Cabling tools (crimpers, testers, toners, punch down tools)</li>\n<li>Smartphone for photos and communication</li>\n<li>Packing tape (for sealing boxes for return shipping)</li>\n<li>Mobile hotspot (if required for connectivity)</li>\n<li>Hex/Allen key set</li>\n<li>PPE (safety glasses, gloves, hard hat, safety vest, steel-toe boots as required)</li>\n<li>See the attached \"Site Plan - AP Replacement\" document to verify all tools required for this location.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>As stated in the terms related to this work order, as well as the tasks outlined below, all deliverables and tasks must be uploaded and completed as requested.&nbsp;Please contact your Service Manager PRIOR to departing your location if any questions or issues with a particular deliverable/task.&nbsp;All must be uploaded and marked as WORK DONE no later than 24 hours after departing site.&nbsp;There could be financial penalties if this is not adhered to.</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>IMPORTANT CONTACTS AND ESCALATION PATH:</u></strong></p>\n<p>CAN BE FOUND UNDER \"CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION\" OR IN THE \"CONTACTS\" FIELDS.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>TASKS/DELIVERABLES:</u></strong></p>\n<p>PLEASE FOLLOW THROUGH THE TASKS AND REQUESTED DELIVERABLES LISTED ON THE PORTAL.&nbsp;CONFIRM WITH YOUR SERVICE MANAGER IF A TASK MAY NOT BE APPLICABLE.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>DRESS CODE:</strong></p>\n<p>Business casual attire (unless doing any low voltage work involving attic spaces/etc.).&nbsp;This would include a clean shirt with no logos, button down or Polo, khakis or jeans with no holes, dress shoes and/or sneakers with no flashy design.</p>","markdown":"**PLEASE REPRESENT YOURSELF AS A SPLICE TECHNICIAN WHEN SPEAKING WITH ONSITE CONTACTS OR WITH CUSTOMER TECHNICAL CONTACTS.**\n\n**SCOPE OF WORK SUMMARY:**\n\nTechnician needed to perform onsite replacement of existing access points (APs) with new units, in coordination with the Lead Engineer and site contact. Work must follow provided site plans, installation guides, and safety procedures.\n\nAPs to replace: 1\n\n**PLEASE CHECK THE \"Site Plan - AP Replacement\" ATTACHMENT** - This will guide you through the deployment.PLEASE BRING A PRINTED COPY FOR YOUR ONSITE VISIT. MAKE SURE YOU REVIEW IT BEFORE GOING AND CALL SERVICE MANAGER IF ANY QUESTIONS.\n\n**IMPORTANT NOTE – SITE WALL/FACILITY PROTECTION**\n\nTechnicians must take extra care to avoid damaging or marking walls while performing work onsite.\n\n- When using ladders, technicians must place towels, padding, or other protective material between the ladder and the wall surface whenever applicable.\n- Please avoid leaning ladders directly against painted walls or finished surfaces without protection.\n- Technicians should also be mindful of dirty/stained hands or gloves when working near walls and ceilings to avoid leaving marks or smudges.\n- Any accidental damage or wall markings must be reported and fixed immediately.\n\nPlease ensure all work areas are left clean and in the same condition as found upon arrival.\n\n**WORKFLOW**:\n\n- Check in with Club Local Contact (LCON) and assigned Lead Engineer upon arrival\n- Set up a staging area to unpack new APs, verify equipment count, brackets, and report any discrepancies\n- Review the site plan and installation instructions with the Lead Engineer prior to starting work\n- Confirm understanding of proper AP removal and installation procedures (including reviewing provided guides/videos)\n- Safely dismount existing APs without forcing or damaging mounting brackets\n- Install new APs and brackets according to the site plan and instructions\n- Cross-check each AP swap against the provided spreadsheet to ensure correct device replacement\n- Report any inconsistencies or issues immediately to the Service Manager and Lead Engineer\n- Coordinate with site management and Lead Engineer if any obstacles or restrictions are encountered (e.g., locked areas, events, access limitations)\n- Follow all safety protocols and consult with the Lead Engineer in any high-risk situation\n- Perform installation work strictly per plan; any deviations must be approved by the Lead Engineer\n- Capture and submit clear photos of each existing AP before removal.\n- Capture and submit clear photos of new AP after installation. Make sure that it is a mid range picture, showing the location where it has been mounted. PLEASE label the picture with the name of the AP that you are replacing.\n- Capture and submit clear photos of old APs properly packaged for return.\n\n**End of Day Activities:**\n\n- Package old APs in the original boxes of the new units\n- Place individual boxes into larger shipping boxes\n- Seal boxes and apply provided shipping labels (provided by LCON)\n- Clean and organize the staging/work area\n- Await final release from the Lead Engineer before leaving the site\n\n**JOB DURATION AND REQUIRED EXPERIENCE:**\n\nDuration: # hour(s)\n\n Experience:\n\nTechnician will need to be proficient with wireless access point (AP) installation, replacement, and mounting procedures, including safe removal of existing units and proper installation of new APs and brackets. Must be able to follow site plans, equipment spreadsheets, and installation guides with attention to detail, ensuring correct device matching and placement. Technician should have experience with structured cabling and basic networking concepts, including PoE connectivity and verification of network status.\n\nTechnician must be comfortable working at heights using ladders and lifts, following all safety protocols and best practices. Experience navigating ceiling spaces and working in active environments is required. Technician should be able to coordinate effectively with remote engineers via bridge calls (Microsoft Teams, etc.), follow detailed instructions, and communicate any discrepancies or onsite challenges in real time.\n\n**REQUIRED TOOLS:**\n\n- Basic networking tools (IP configuration, testing utilities)\n- Standard hand tools (screwdrivers, pliers, snips, etc.)\n- Mounting hardware tools (drill, bits, anchors as needed)\n- Measuring tape\n- Label maker\n- Patch cables (various lengths)\n- Cabling tools (crimpers, testers, toners, punch down tools)\n- Smartphone for photos and communication\n- Packing tape (for sealing boxes for return shipping)\n- Mobile hotspot (if required for connectivity)\n- Hex/Allen key set\n- PPE (safety glasses, gloves, hard hat, safety vest, steel-toe boots as required)\n- See the attached \"Site Plan - AP Replacement\" document to verify all tools required for this location.\n\n**As stated in the terms related to this work order, as well as the tasks outlined below, all deliverables and tasks must be uploaded and completed as requested. Please contact your Service Manager PRIOR to departing your location if any questions or issues with a particular deliverable/task. All must be uploaded and marked as WORK DONE no later than 24 hours after departing site. There could be financial penalties if this is not adhered to.**\n\n**IMPORTANT CONTACTS AND ESCALATION PATH:**\n\nCAN BE FOUND UNDER \"CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION\" OR IN THE \"CONTACTS\" FIELDS.\n\n**TASKS/DELIVERABLES:**\n\nPLEASE FOLLOW THROUGH THE TASKS AND REQUESTED DELIVERABLES LISTED ON THE PORTAL. CONFIRM WITH YOUR SERVICE MANAGER IF A TASK MAY NOT BE APPLICABLE.\n\n**DRESS CODE:**\n\nBusiness casual attire (unless doing any low voltage work involving attic spaces/etc.). This would include a clean shirt with no logos, button down or Polo, khakis or jeans with no holes, dress shoes and/or sneakers with no flashy design.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-28T09:00","end":"2026-09-28T11:00"},"payRange":{"min":60,"max":120},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":60,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":16},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"PAYMENT_BELOW_MINIMUM","rejectDetails":"Total pay $120 (countered: $120) is below minimum threshold $400"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T21:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T21:00:00.000Z","summary":"Miniso Durham"},{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-15T17:00:00.0