{"job":{"id":20008587,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"KIOSK Information Systems","title":"IVS Zoomaroo - Four Season Town Centre | Kiosk Offline Troubleshooting & Testing","description":{"html":"<p>This WO is to help us get our customer back up and running.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Support Number:&nbsp;</strong>(303) 926-3154&nbsp;<strong>- Hours are Mon - Friday 7am - 5pm MST</strong></p>\n<p><strong>DO NOT CLOSE THE MAIN DOOR WITH THE KEY INSIDE THE LOCK</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Documentation:</strong></p>\n<p>*Please review the attached pictures and documents to help you be ready for this WO*</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>-Tools Required:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>__</strong>Box/Bag for up to 1000 coins</p>\n<p><strong>__&nbsp;</strong>Outlet Tester</p>\n<p><strong>__&nbsp;</strong>Basic<strong>&nbsp;</strong>Multimeter</p>\n<p>__Standard Tool Set</p>\n<p>__Nut Drivers or Ratchet &amp; Socket Set (3/8, 5/16, 11/32, 1/4)</p>\n<p>__Swivel sockets and/or flexible extension for sockets</p>\n<p>__Electronic Safe Wipes or Cloth</p>\n<p>__A to B USB Cable</p>\n<p>__VGA Cable</p>\n<p>__Compressed air/Canned Air</p>\n<p>__T-25 Security bit</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>Scope of work: Troubleshoot Kiosk Offline with KIS Support</strong></p>\n<p>*PLEASE take before &amp; after pictures*</p>\n<p><strong>DO NOT CLOSE THE MAIN DOOR WITH THE KEY INSIDE THE LOCK</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Kiosk serial #</strong> F0112593</p>\n<p><strong>Issue :</strong> Customer reported the kiosk is offline with potential power issues in main rental unit. Please follow steps below to troubleshoot unit offline</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Call KIS Support to check in. We will work with you to disable the alarm so it does not go off once power is restored</li>\n<li>Let KIS Support know if the blue LED lights are on or off on the kiosk</li>\n<li>If the blue lights are on, please check the UPS (If one is present) and reboot the PC behind the screen with KIS Support</li>\n</ol>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>IF THE UNIT HAS A UPS, PLEASE FOLLOW BELOW STEPS:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>UPS Location:</strong>&nbsp;inside the main rental unit, mounted on the floor or lower rear wall. (There is no UPS in the large endcap screen enclosure)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong><u>UPS Testing:</u></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Confirm status shown on UPS screen: battery health, %, errors if shown, etc.</li>\n<li>Disconnect all hardware from UPS and let charge for 10-15 minutes.</li>\n<li>Reconnect main components (PC, screen, etc.) and attempt power on.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong><u>If fails:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Let stand and charge for 10-15 minutes before connecting hardware.</li>\n<li>Reboot the unit</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><u>Instructions for KIS Agent:</u></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Make sure all hardware/devices are online</li>\n<li>Confirm inventory is online/available for rent</li>\n<li>Test<em>&nbsp;</em>both cash&nbsp;<em>&amp;</em>&nbsp;credit transactions (Do not need to fully process payment)</li>\n<li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If coin is not dispensed, test functionality with KIS Agent and possibly attempt coin dump</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>DO NOT CLOSE THE MAIN DOOR WITH THE KEY INSIDE THE LOCK</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;<strong>DOCK Troubleshooting (IF NECESSARY)</strong></p>\n<p>__We need to check to see which ones are blinking red and find out if its due to bad car or bad dock or issues with latches</p>\n<p>__if needed we can remove the car, so you can remove the dock using the T25 security bit</p>\n<p>__Inspect for any issues with the board, cabling, wiring, springs or hardware</p>\n<p>__Check with KIS Agent if you're unsure if something is damaged that you find as a potential issue</p>\n<p>__Usually screw that holds latch is loose or large spring is catching. (See attached drawing)</p>\n<p>__Kiosk Support will work with you to make sure it is operational</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong>DO NOT CLOSE THE MAIN DOOR WITH THE KEY INSIDE THE LOCK</strong></p>\n<p>MUST RETURN ALL PARTS TO KIOSK SUPPORT UNDER RMA NUMBER ON TITLE OF WORK ORDER. Do not leave any parts on site. If we do not see return tracking when you close WO we will not process for payment until we do.</p>\n<p>Company: Kiosk Information Systems Inc.</p>\n<p>346 S Arthur Ave.</p>\n<p>Louisville, CO 80027</p>\n<p>(303) 926-3154</p>","markdown":"This WO is to help us get our customer back up and running.\n\n**Support Number:** (303) 926-3154 **- Hours are Mon - Friday 7am - 5pm MST**\n\n**DO NOT CLOSE THE MAIN DOOR WITH THE KEY INSIDE THE LOCK**\n\n**Documentation:**\n\n\\*Please review the attached pictures and documents to help you be ready for this WO\\*\n\n**-Tools Required:**\n\n**\\_\\_**Box/Bag for up to 1000 coins\n\n**\\_\\_** Outlet Tester\n\n**\\_\\_** Basic Multimeter\n\n\\_\\_Standard Tool Set\n\n\\_\\_Nut Drivers or Ratchet & Socket Set (3/8, 5/16, 11/32, 1/4)\n\n\\_\\_Swivel sockets and/or flexible extension for sockets\n\n\\_\\_Electronic Safe Wipes or Cloth\n\n\\_\\_A to B USB Cable\n\n\\_\\_VGA Cable\n\n\\_\\_Compressed air/Canned Air\n\n\\_\\_T-25 Security bit\n\n**Scope of work: Troubleshoot Kiosk Offline with KIS Support**\n\n\\*PLEASE take before & after pictures\\*\n\n**DO NOT CLOSE THE MAIN DOOR WITH THE KEY INSIDE THE LOCK**\n\n**Kiosk serial #** F0112593\n\n**Issue :** Customer reported the kiosk is offline with potential power issues in main rental unit. Please follow steps below to troubleshoot unit offline\n\n1. Call KIS Support to check in. We will work with you to disable the alarm so it does not go off once power is restored\n2. Let KIS Support know if the blue LED lights are on or off on the kiosk\n3. If the blue lights are on, please check the UPS (If one is present) and reboot the PC behind the screen with KIS Support\n\n**IF THE UNIT HAS A UPS, PLEASE FOLLOW BELOW STEPS:**\n\n- **UPS Location:** inside the main rental unit, mounted on the floor or lower rear wall. (There is no UPS in the large endcap screen enclosure)\n\n**UPS Testing:**\n\n1. Confirm status shown on UPS screen: battery health, %, errors if shown, etc.\n2. Disconnect all hardware from UPS and let charge for 10-15 minutes.\n3. Reconnect main components (PC, screen, etc.) and attempt power on.\n\n**If fails:**\n\n- Let stand and charge for 10-15 minutes before connecting hardware.\n- Reboot the unit\n\n**Instructions for KIS Agent:**\n\n- Make sure all hardware/devices are online\n- Confirm inventory is online/available for rent\n- Test both cash *&* credit transactions (Do not need to fully process payment)\n- If coin is not dispensed, test functionality with KIS Agent and possibly attempt coin dump\n\n**DO NOT CLOSE THE MAIN DOOR WITH THE KEY INSIDE THE LOCK**\n\n **DOCK Troubleshooting (IF NECESSARY)**\n\n\\_\\_We need to check to see which ones are blinking red and find out if its due to bad car or bad dock or issues with latches\n\n\\_\\_if needed we can remove the car, so you can remove the dock using the T25 security bit\n\n\\_\\_Inspect for any issues with the board, cabling, wiring, springs or hardware\n\n\\_\\_Check with KIS Agent if you're unsure if something is damaged that you find as a potential issue\n\n\\_\\_Usually screw that holds latch is loose or large spring is catching. (See attached drawing)\n\n\\_\\_Kiosk Support will work with you to make sure it is operational\n\n**DO NOT CLOSE THE MAIN DOOR WITH THE KEY INSIDE THE LOCK**\n\nMUST RETURN ALL PARTS TO KIOSK SUPPORT UNDER RMA NUMBER ON TITLE OF WORK ORDER. Do not leave any parts on site. If we do not see return tracking when you close WO we will not process for payment until we do.\n\nCompany: Kiosk Information Systems Inc.\n\n346 S Arthur Ave.\n\nLouisville, CO 80027\n\n(303) 926-3154","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-23T10:00","end":"2026-09-23T11:30"},"payRange":{"min":75,"max":135},"payType":"blended","payStructure":{"type":"blended","base":{"units":1.5,"am