{"job":{"id":20012137,"platform":"FieldNation","company":"Unified Global Solutions","title":"Go Back to install Starlink, cordless phone and for cut over at Western Auto Associate Store*EXTENSION LADDER REQUIRED*","description":{"html":"<p><strong>VOIP / ATA Go-Back (Troubleshooting) – Technician Requirements</strong></p>\n<p>Unified Global Solutions is seeking a technician with Telecom and VoIP experience to resolve outstanding issues from a previous VOIP or VOIP-to-ATA installation.</p>\n<p><strong>Go-Back Scope / Anticipated Needs</strong></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><strong><em><u>SEND TECH TO INSTALL STARLINK, CORDLESS PHONE AND FOR CUTOVER. REQUIRES 18 INCH MASONRY BIT WITH DRILL, 20FT EXTENSION LADDER, 10-12 FT A-FRAME LADDER AND LITTLE GIANT LADDER FOR STAIRWAY.</u></em></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Any extra equipment left with the customer must be documented on the checklist (include what was left, who received it, and where it was placed).</li>\n</ul>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Punctuality &amp; Assignment Rules</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Arrive on time. The customer is expecting you at the scheduled date/time.</li>\n<li>Late arrival may result in removal from this assignment and any bundled work orders.</li>\n<li>If another technician will complete the work, you must obtain Project Manager approval and provide their contact information.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Required Tools &amp; Supplies</p>\n<p><strong>You must bring all items listed below. Failure to arrive fully prepared may result in removal from the site and non-payment.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Tools Required:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Windows laptop (Windows 10 or higher) with Gigabit RJ45 port</li>\n<li>Telephone butt set</li>\n<li>Cable toner and cable tester</li>\n<li>RJ45/RJ11 crimper</li>\n<li>110/66 punch-down tool</li>\n<li>Cable stripper and electrician scissors</li>\n<li>Telco banjo (or pair breakout tool)</li>\n<li>Multimeter</li>\n<li>Cable pulling rods and Fiche tape</li>\n<li>Drill, level, and stud finder</li>\n<li>6–8 ft ladder</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Supplies Required:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Minimum 500 ft of CAT5e cable</li>\n<li>6-pin RJ11 ends</li>\n<li>RJ45 jacks and keystone jacks</li>\n<li>Bridge clips</li>\n<li>Telephone splice connectors</li>\n<li>Patch cables and cable-making supplies</li>\n<li>Drywall screws/anchors and concrete screws</li>\n<li>Zip ties and Velcro wraps</li>\n<li>Wall plates and surface mount boxes</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Note:</strong> Bring any additional tools or supplies indicated during the site survey.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Dress Code</p>\n<p>Wear a clean, solid (non-logo) shirt with jeans or work pants.</p>\n<p><br /></p>\n<p>Pre-Visit Instructions</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Read and understand all instructions and attached documentation.</li>\n<li>Confirm your ETA in Field Nation within 24 hours of the appointment.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Onsite Tasks</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Check in on the Field Nation work order.</li>\n<li>Locate the onsite contact and introduce yourself as a Unified Global Solutions technician.</li>\n<li>Locate shipped parts and complete inventory.</li>\n<li>Inform support of any issues with the current system.</li>\n<li>Work with support to resolve outstanding issues and complete all tests.</li>\n<li>Clean up the work area.</li>\n<li>Remove old data/voice modem(s) if a new internet cutover is required.</li>\n<li>Give the onsite contact all removed equipment and any unused new equipment.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Close-Out Tasks</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Have support verify completion with the onsite contact.</li>\n<li>Review the checklist with support. You will be released only after all tasks are verified.</li>\n<li>Upload all required deliverables to the Field Nation work order.</li>\n<li>Check out on the Field Nation app.</li>\n<li>The provider is responsible for all time increases and expenses added to the work order.</li>\n</ul>","markdown":"**VOIP / ATA Go-Back (Troubleshooting) – Technician Requirements**\n\nUnified Global Solutions is seeking a technician with Telecom and VoIP experience to resolve outstanding issues from a previous VOIP or VOIP-to-ATA installation.\n\n**Go-Back Scope / Anticipated Needs**\n\n***SEND TECH TO INSTALL STARLINK, CORDLESS PHONE AND FOR CUTOVER. REQUIRES 18 INCH MASONRY BIT WITH DRILL, 20FT EXTENSION LADDER, 10-12 FT A-FRAME LADDER AND LITTLE GIANT LADDER FOR STAIRWAY.***\n\n**Additional Notes:**\n\n- Any extra equipment left with the customer must be documented on the checklist (include what was left, who received it, and where it was placed).\n\nPunctuality & Assignment Rules\n\n- Arrive on time. The customer is expecting you at the scheduled date/time.\n- Late arrival may result in removal from this assignment and any bundled work orders.\n- If another technician will complete the work, you must obtain Project Manager approval and provide their contact information.\n\nRequired Tools & Supplies\n\n**You must bring all items listed below. Failure to arrive fully prepared may result in removal from the site and non-payment.**\n\n**Tools Required:**\n\n- Windows laptop (Windows 10 or higher) with Gigabit RJ45 port\n- Telephone butt set\n- Cable toner and cable tester\n- RJ45/RJ11 crimper\n- 110/66 punch-down tool\n- Cable stripper and electrician scissors\n- Telco banjo (or pair breakout tool)\n- Multimeter\n- Cable pulling rods and Fiche tape\n- Drill, level, and stud finder\n- 6–8 ft ladder\n\n**Supplies Required:**\n\n- Minimum 500 ft of CAT5e cable\n- 6-pin RJ11 ends\n- RJ45 jacks and keystone jacks\n- Bridge clips\n- Telephone splice connectors\n- Patch cables and cable-making supplies\n- Drywall screws/anchors and concrete screws\n- Zip ties and Velcro wraps\n- Wall plates and surface mount boxes\n\n**Note:** Bring any additional tools or supplies indicated during the site survey.\n\nDress Code\n\nWear a clean, solid (non-logo) shirt with jeans or work pants.\n\nPre-Visit Instructions\n\n- Read and understand all instructions and attached documentation.\n- Confirm your ETA in Field Nation within 24 hours of the appointment.\n\nOnsite Tasks\n\n- Check in on the Field Nation work order.\n- Locate the onsite contact and introduce yourself as a Unified Global Solutions technician.\n- Locate shipped parts and complete inventory.\n- Inform support of any issues with the current system.\n- Work with support to resolve outstanding issues and complete all tests.\n- Clean up the work area.\n- Remove old data/voice modem(s) if a new internet cutover is required.\n- Give the onsite contact all removed equipment and any unused new equipment.\n\nClose-Out Tasks\n\n- Have support verify completion with the onsite contact.\n- Review the checklist with support. You will be released only after all tasks are verified.\n- Upload all required deliverables to the Field Nation work order.\n- Check out on the Field Nation app.\n- The provider is responsible for all time increases and expenses added to the work order.","actions":[]},"isRequestedWindow":false,"time":{"start":"2026-09-28T11:00","end":"2026-09-28T13:00"},"payRange":{"min":55,"max":110},"payType":"hourly","payStructure":null,"hourlyRate":55,"estLaborHours":2,"distance":41},"result":{"eligible":false,"counterOffer":null,"reason":"BLOCKED_KEYWORD","rejectDetails":"Blocked keyword \"starlink\" in title"},"availableBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-28T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-29T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-29T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-09-30T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-01T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-02T00:00:00.000Z"},{"start":"2026-10-02T13:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-10-03T00:00:00.000Z"}],"busyBlocks":[{"start":"2026-09-25T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-26T00:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 Budderfly - 162218 - MCD-11779 - MAX (WM)"},{"start":"2026-09-24T12:00:00.000Z","end":"2026-09-24T14:00:00.000Z","summary":"🔧 USK8 NC-Jacksonville Mall Miniso Retro (WM)"},{"start":"2026-10-15T14:00:00.